window.SH_INDEX=[{"p":"Advancements","h":"","u":"advancements.html","t":"Static Hollow has its own advancements tab, added in 1.34.0. Its root reads Static Hollow: Something has been watching you. There are 89 advancements under it in 1.72.2, from the end of chapter four to Tune-In Town and chapter ten, plus one for every chapter's gear. Spoilers, obviously. Each one shows its frame as the game draws it: a task (square), a goal (rounded) or a challenge (spiked; drawn doubled here). 14 are hidden until you earn them. The icons are the mod's own textures where the advancement uses one of its items."},{"p":"Advancements","h":"The tab","u":"advancements.html#the-tab","t":"Static Hollow Something has been watching you. The root's own icon in game is the Rosemont Device."},{"p":"Advancements","h":"Chapter four","u":"advancements.html#chapter-four","t":"Advancement In game How Not Collected challenge hidden Put the Rosemont Device into the Great Bloom. It's still beating. Launch the Device from the ledge. See the launch . The Bell Tolls goal Kill a Bellwether. The rest of them won't know where to go. Kill a Bellwether, at the head of a horde or on its own. The Last Light challenge hidden End the changed Bloom Kill the changed Bloom. The Omni Ray challenge hidden Call SENTINEL down on the changed Bloom Fire the Omni at it from 50 blocks or more off its mouth. Zero Responsibility goal hidden Have the Omni taken back - for the future Carry the Omni off the blight. Always Persistent task hidden Try to make the Ray Gun again Put the Ray Gun together in a crafting grid after the Watcher took the Omni. Ten Days Later goal hidden The Watcher comes back - with a warning about the parasites Wait ten days (world clock) after the Omni Ray."},{"p":"Advancements","h":"Chapter five","u":"advancements.html#chapter-five","t":""},{"p":"Advancements","h":"The static","u":"advancements.html#the-static","t":"Advancement In game How Something Inside task Let a Parasite hold on long enough to get into you Don't crouch. Four seconds. Cut It Out task Cut a parasite's brood out with a Surgical Kit Surgical Kit on yourself, someone else or an animal. Burn It Out task Burn the brood out of yourself before it's too big Stand in fire before it's three quarters grown. It Came Out of Me challenge hidden Live through a brood bursting out of your back Let it grow all the way, and survive 7 hearts. Head of the Pack goal Kill a Static Hound Pack Leader, and watch the pack break Kill the one with the brood sac on its back. Not One of Them task See a villager turn into one of the Hollowed Be alone with it at night, or hurt it."},{"p":"Advancements","h":"The outbreak","u":"advancements.html#the-outbreak","t":"Advancement In game How It Isn't Itself goal Be there when something the parasite took over turns Be within 24 blocks when a creature carrying the parasite reaches the end and turns: five seconds of seizing, arching and screaming, then it tears open. See the turned ."},{"p":"Advancements","h":"The relay","u":"advancements.html#the-relay","t":"Advancement In game How Dead Air task Find the relay the parasites talk through Reach Relay 6 . Cut the Cord challenge Cut the last of the tethers off the relay's mast while what's at its foot still lives Climb the mast and break all three tethers before killing the Amalgam. Off the Air goal Kill the Amalgam and silence the relay Kill the Amalgam . Tuned In task Listen in on them with the Relay Core Hold the Relay Core to your ear."},{"p":"Advancements","h":"The Null","u":"advancements.html#the-null","t":"Advancement In game How The Null task Come to the drive-in where the last of their static runs down Reach the Starlite Drive-In . Signal Lost task Put an Afterimage all the way here long enough to kill it Kill an Afterimage while Tuned In, while it reaches for you, or during the reel. The Last Reel goal Run the last reel through to its end, and see where they come from Four frames in the projector, the Relay Core on you, and hold the booth."},{"p":"Advancements","h":"The Null Static Zone","u":"advancements.html#the-null-static-zone","t":"Advancement In game How The Null Static Zone task Go through the tear at the drive-in, to where all of the static ran down Hold the Last Reel over the tear, and step in. Cut Loose goal Cut the last of the Carrier's threads Climb the four spires and break the knots. Signing Off challenge Kill the Carrier, and see the Watcher take what's left of it Kill the Carrier . The Hush task Step over the line into one of the old pale houses, where the static can't follow Enter a Hush . Unmade goal See a hound come apart in a Hush's door Lead a Static Hound to a Hush. Put Your Ear to It task Listen at one of the ears cut into the old stones Use a Listening Stone ."},{"p":"Advancements","h":"The Hive","u":"advancements.html#the-hive","t":"Advancement In game How It Speaks task Hear the Chorus speak through its own A night after the Hive has grown, be out under the open sky: five of the pure forms come up out of the ground round you and it speaks through them. The Hive task Come to where the parasite is growing itself a mind Reach the Hive . The needle the Watcher gives you after It Speaks points to it. Senseless goal Tear open all four of the Chorus's nerve nodes Break all four nerve nodes on the stalks round the pit (climb the steps round the stalks). It Ran challenge Drive the Chorus down out of its pit Bring the Chorus down to a quarter of its health. It won't die: it runs, down into the ground."},{"p":"Advancements","h":"The Deep","u":"advancements.html#the-deep","t":"Advancement In game How Warmer task Follow the Chorus Fragment's whispers to where it went down Follow the Chorus Fragment to the Sinkhole at Halloway's Low Field, and come up to its rim. Down Where It Is Warm goal Stand on the Throat at the bottom of the burrow, and let it take you into the Deep Go down the Burrow's six turns and stand on the Throat in the chamber at the bottom. It Came Up challenge Kill the Reach: the hand the Chorus tore up out of the ground at your home Every few nights, at your home, one of the Chorus's hands tears up out of the ground (its own bar, its own music). Kill it before it sinks back down after four minutes. Everyone within 96 blocks gets it. Not a Sound task Make boots out of a Listener's ears Craft Hushed Boots: leather boots, two Listener's Ears and string. Stand Still challenge Kill the Deaf King in his hall Kill the Deaf King on his dais at the end of the Old Halls. Follow the way-stones from the Gullet. The Last Voice challenge Kill the Chorus, whole, in the Warm Heart Kill the Chorus, whole, in the Warm Heart. Follow the fragment there."},{"p":"Advancements","h":"Chapter six: the Door at the End of the World","u":"advancements.html#chapter-six","t":"The End is shut once you've signed off. All of these start with carrying the Last Voice into it. See chapter six ."},{"p":"Advancements","h":"Part one: the Audience","u":"advancements.html#part-one-the-audience","t":"Advancement In game How The Door at the End of the World goal Carry the Last Voice into the End, and break his seal Carry the Last Voice into the End. Something cracks across the sky, and the Door goes down east of the obsidian you arrive on. Take Your Seat task Go through the Door into the Stalls Walk the causeway to the island and into the static in the Door: the Stalls . Quiet, Please challenge Keep perfectly still through the Crowd's Hush From two thirds of the Crowd's health down it puts a Hush on the house. Don't move or strike for the whole four seconds. Standing Ovation challenge Bring the Crowd down Step onto the front aisle under the screen and kill the Crowd . Front Row goal See who was sitting in the front row Be there for the cutscene after the Crowd dies: one seat in the front row is still taken."},{"p":"Advancements","h":"Part two: the Watcher's Vault","u":"advancements.html#part-two-the-watchers-vault","t":"Advancement In game How Admit One goal Hold the Last Ticket up to the seam in the screen Hold the Last Ticket up to the seam in the Great Screen. Behind the Picture task Go through the seam, into the Watcher's Vault Go through the open seam into the Watcher's Vault . What He Kept goal Take all three things out of his keeps Open the three round steel doors off the nave and take the Omni's Heart, What's Left of the Carrier and His First Reel. The Final Reel challenge Burn the Projectionist through Bring all three to the Watch and kill the Projectionist . What He Kept Out goal See his first reel Be there when he runs his first reel, after the Projectionist."},{"p":"Advancements","h":"Part three: What He Kept Out","u":"advancements.html#part-three-what-he-kept-out","t":"Advancement In game How The Other Side goal Go through the Door at the End of the World, its static gone black Walk into the Door once its static has gone black: the Other Side . Every Colour at Once task See the Omni's heart put into his last projector's lamp Fight the Viewer to two thirds, when he loads the Omni's Heart into his last projector. Out of Sight challenge Get through the first third of the Viewer without it ever seeing you right through Get through the Viewer's first third without ever being Seen right through. Keep a painted flat between you and its eye. It Gets Up goal Be there when what he kept out stands up At a third left he runs the Carrier through the projector, and the Viewer stands up. Thank You for Watching challenge See the last show See the last show through to the credits. You're sent home with the record of the same name."},{"p":"Advancements","h":"Chapter seven: the First Signal","u":"advancements.html#chapter-seven","t":"See chapter seven . Advancement In game How The Hub goal Be taken into the realm he made, after the credits After the last show's credits, his hand comes up through them: you're taken into the Hub . ENOUGH challenge hidden Hear the First Signal - and jump See his speech through to the First Signal coming through, and go off the edge with him. The First Signal goal hidden Come down from the Hub, and hear what it is Come down out of the Hub. Since 1.62.0 that's onto the rig in the Dead Water. Channel Changer task Be given the Remote He gives it to you as you come down. (In the Dead Water it breaks in your hand a moment later: you still get this.) Previously On... task Go back to a chapter through one of the Hub's portals Walk into one of the six replay portals in the Hub's gallery."},{"p":"Advancements","h":"Chapter eight: the Dead Water","u":"advancements.html#chapter-eight","t":"See chapter eight . Advancement In game How Dead Water task Come down through his portal onto the rig Come down through his portal onto the rig in the Dead Water . Back On Air goal Mend the Remote with what a Static Leviathan sings with Craft the Broken Remote, a Static Leviathan's Signal Organ and a copper ingot together, while you're stranded there. See the leviathans ."},{"p":"Advancements","h":"Chapter nine: the Harbinger","u":"advancements.html#chapter-nine","t":"See chapter nine . Advancement In game How The Turning goal hidden Watch the Undertow eat both hearts - and come down by the rig Fit all three of Orpheus's modules in her upgrade bay (the pressure plating, the depth module and the UV field module). The Turning plays for everyone in the Dead Water; be there for it. This Gift Will Not Be Wasted challenge hidden See what came out of it after three days Three days after the Turning (by the Overworld's clock), be in the Dead Water when the Harbinger comes up out of the husk and leaves its static heart at your feet. Its Roar, In Your Hand task hidden Let the mutated Remote roar Craft the mutated static heart with your Remote (broken or mended) into the Remote (Mutated), then hold use and let go."},{"p":"Advancements","h":"Chapter ten: Stay Tuned","u":"advancements.html#chapter-ten","t":"See chapter ten and The Last Broadcast . Advancement In game How Stay Tuned challenge hidden See what he did after the Hub - and what he let out Once the Harbinger has gone through its way out, go home (your bed or your spawn in the Overworld, or home by the Remote). The Broadcast cuts in; see it through. Off His Air challenge Kill one of his three servants Kill one of his three servants : the Announcer (his transmitters), the Cameraman (his burrows) or the Stagehand (his sets). Pulled the Plug goal Break the Broadcast Core in one of his transmitters, burrows or sets Break the Broadcast Core in one of his transmitters, burrows or sets. His Guest goal Step through a tear in his signal, into his kingdom Step into the tear a broken Broadcast Core leaves behind (it's open for a minute): you come out in his kingdom . Blackout goal Make a Blackout Ingot: the strongest there is Have a Blackout Ingot: four signal fragments, four blackout shards and a netherite ingot. Radio Silence challenge Have the whole Blackout set: they can't hear you at all Have all four pieces of Blackout armour. End of Transmission challenge At his own war table, take the First Signal off the air Not earnable yet in 1.72.2. It's for a fight at his war table that the mod is still holding back."},{"p":"Advancements","h":"Tune-In Town","u":"advancements.html#tune-in-town","t":"A secret Easter egg, with flashing lights, loud noises and jumpscares. Its flyer can turn up any time after your first day; it's filed under chapter ten here. See Tune-In Town . Advancement In game How Now Hiring task Go through the STAFF ONLY door into Studio B Follow the HELP WANTED flyer to the old place and go through its STAFF ONLY door into Studio B. Clocked In task Start a night shift at Tune-In Town Punch the time clock in the security office and start a night shift (the first time, you have to say yes to the warning). You're Fired task hidden Get jumpscared on the night shift Let one of the cast get you on a night shift. 6 AM goal Make it through a night shift Last till 6 AM on any night shift. An hour is 70 seconds. Have You Tried Turning It Off? goal On the night shift, reboot the one HIS static's in From the third night, HIS static is in one of the cast. Reboot that one from the monitor (the REBOOT button, or R). Overtime challenge Make it through the sixth night - and the Encore Make it through the sixth night, the Encore's. Disbanded challenge Take apart the Mended Band After hours the band on the show stage sometimes come together into the Mended Band. Kill it. Twenty Twenty challenge Beat a Custom Night with every one of them on 20 Once the sixth night is beaten, set every one of the twelve to 20 on a Custom Night and beat it. The Owner challenge Win all three gold stars on Tune-In Town's time clock Win all three gold stars on the time clock: the fifth night, the sixth night, and a Custom Night with every one of them on 20. The place is yours: the Showstopper, Golden Tony's music box and the Owner's Key. Encore for One goal Have the band play the whole show, just for you As the owner, use the show stage's curtain after hours, and watch the band play the whole show."},{"p":"Advancements","h":"Gear for every chapter","u":"advancements.html#gear-for-every-chapter","t":"Since 1.60.0 each chapter has its own armour set, weapons and tools: see gear for every chapter . These count what you've had in your inventory, so you don't need everything at once. Advancement In game How Keep Watch task Put on all of the Vigil: the iron hood, its candles, the coat. Have each of the four Vigil pieces (chapter one). Out Standing in the Field task Put on all of the Scarecrow's clothes. Have each of the four Scarecrow pieces (chapter two). Rooted task Put on all of the Bloomwoven. Have each of the four Bloomwoven pieces (chapter three). Specimen task Put on all of the Specimen gear, jar and all. Have each of the four Specimen pieces (chapter four). Off the Air task Put on all of Dead Air. Have each of the four Dead Air pieces (chapter five). Not the same as the relay's Off the Air. Front of House task Put on all of the Usher's uniform. Have each of the four pieces of the Usher's Uniform (chapter six). Live task Put on all of the On Air gear. Have each of the four On Air pieces (chapter seven). Something for Every Chapter challenge Hold a weapon from every chapter. Have one of the two weapons from each of the seven chapters: the Censer or Bell Clapper, the Pitchfork or Omen Staff, the Thorn Whip or Spore Mace, the Bone Saw or Reactor Rod, the Tuning Fork or Relay Staff, the Splicer or Fly Hook, the Antenna Glaive or On Air Mace. Rerun task Beat a replay again and keep what it leaves: a Rerun Reel. Beat a replay from the Hub again and pick up one of the Rerun Reels it leaves. Chapter seven's gear is made with them."},{"p":"Advancements","h":"The world","u":"advancements.html#the-world","t":"Advancement In game How Fallout task Break open a Fallen Star Mine a Fallen Star and get Star Static. Small ones come down near you at night. See falling stars ."},{"p":"Advancements","h":"All of them, as toasts","u":"advancements.html#at-a-glance","t":"Not Collected hidden Put the Rosemont Device into the Great Bloom. It's still beating. The Bell Tolls Kill a Bellwether. The rest of them won't know where to go. The Last Light hidden End the changed Bloom The Omni Ray hidden Call SENTINEL down on the changed Bloom Zero Responsibility hidden Have the Omni taken back - for the future Always Persistent hidden Try to make the Ray Gun again Ten Days Later hidden The Watcher comes back - with a warning about the parasites Something Inside Let a Parasite hold on long enough to get into you Cut It Out Cut a parasite's brood out with a Surgical Kit Burn It Out Burn the brood out of yourself before it's too big It Came Out of Me hidden Live through a brood bursting out of your back Head of the Pack Kill a Static Hound Pack Leader, and watch the pack break Not One of Them See a villager turn into one of the Hollowed It Isn't Itself Be there when something the parasite took over turns Dead Air Find the relay the parasites talk through Cut the Cord Cut the last of the tethers off the relay's mast while what's at its foot still lives Off the Air Kill the Amalgam and silence the relay Tuned In Listen in on them with the Relay Core The Null Come to the drive-in where the last of their static runs down Signal Lost Put an Afterimage all the way here long enough to kill it The Last Reel Run the last reel through to its end, and see where they come from The Null Static Zone Go through the tear at the drive-in, to where all of the static ran down Cut Loose Cut the last of the Carrier's threads Signing Off Kill the Carrier, and see the Watcher take what's left of it The Hush Step over the line into one of the old pale houses, where the static can't follow Unmade See a hound come apart in a Hush's door Put Your Ear to It Listen at one of the ears cut into the old stones It Speaks Hear the Chorus speak through its own The Hive Come to where the parasite is growing itself a mind Senseless Tear open all four of the Chorus's nerve nodes It Ran Drive the Chorus down out of its pit Warmer Follow the Chorus Fragment's whispers to where it went down Down Where It Is Warm Stand on the Throat at the bottom of the burrow, and let it take you into the Deep It Came Up Kill the Reach: the hand the Chorus tore up out of the ground at your home Not a Sound Make boots out of a Listener's ears Stand Still Kill the Deaf King in his hall The Last Vo"},{"p":"Credits","h":"Static Hollow","u":"credits.html#static-hollow","t":"Made by Death Licence All Rights Reserved Version on this site 1.72.3 Voices Made with ElevenLabs since 1.71.2: Hal's orientation tapes and the Tune-In Town cast's lines Music The mod's own 63 pieces on the soundtrack, and more since for chapters eight to ten, Tune-In Town and the new country: see the soundtrack"},{"p":"Credits","h":"Built into the mod","u":"credits.html#built-into-the-mod","t":"Orbital Railgun by Mishkis, from Rayness's Renewed port (the NeoForge port it was taken from), both under the MIT licence (see LICENSE-orbital-railgun.txt in the mod). The Ray Gun and the Omni are built on it: its gun model, its texture, its sounds and its strike. Static Hollow's own gun pack for Timeless and Classics Guns: Zero (the Mended SMG, Shotgun and Marksman Rifle), built into the Fabric mod."},{"p":"Credits","h":"In the modpacks","u":"credits.html#in-the-modpack","t":"Mod or pack By Licence and how it's used What it's for Fabric Loader and Fabric API FabricMC The Fabric version runs on them Sodium CaffeineMC Rendering speed (Fabric) Iris Shaders IrisShaders Shader packs on Fabric Lithium CaffeineMC Faster game logic (Fabric) Entity Culling tr7zw Skips drawing creatures hidden behind walls (Fabric) FerriteCore malte0811 MIT. Unmodified, in the pack's own mods folder since 1.63.20 Less memory for blocks and models (Fabric) ImmediatelyFast RaphiMC LGPL-3.0 or later. Unmodified, in the pack's own mods folder since 1.63.20 The HUD, text and entities drawn in fewer batches (Fabric) First-person Model and Not Enough Animations tr7zw Your own body in first person (Fabric) Sound Physics Remastered henkelmax Installed but switched off since 1.61.1 Reverb, echo and muffling, if you switch it back on Timeless and Classics Guns: Zero [Unofficial] Refabricated The TaCZ team The Mended guns (Fabric) Forge Config API Port Fuzs Needed by TaCZ Biomes O' Plenty the Glitchfiend team Unmodified Biomes; Static Hollow's structures, music and fog are made to fit them TerraBlender and GlitchCore Glitchfiend Unmodified GlitchCore is needed by Biomes O' Plenty and Serene Seasons, TerraBlender by Biomes O' Plenty; the Hollow's own biomes come into the world through TerraBlender Serene Seasons the Glitchfiend team Unmodified, with Static Hollow's settings The seasons Puddles & Floods PigCart MIT. Unmodified on Fabric; on Forge a port of 1.1.6 made for the pack ( LICENSE-puddles-floods.txt , source and notes in companions/puddles-floods-forge ) Puddles in the rain, rivers that flood Water Erosion 13rac1 GNU GPL v3. Ported to 26.3 for the pack and shipped with its source ( companions/water-erosion ) Running water that wears the land away Streams: Reflowing NiceJohn Unmodified Streams that follow the land (Fabric) Cinematic Interactions Southware MIT. A build made for the pack, with Static Hollow's sounds and look ( companions/cinematic-interactions ) Workstations as first-person scenes \"Just a Hammer\" RDiamonds CC BY 4.0 Cinematic Interactions' hammer model Max Companion Death All Rights Reserved. Made for this pack, since 1.63.22 Max, the AI , who plays the game with you (Fabric) Photon SixthSurge Downloaded unmodified The default shader pack Hysteria and Insanity ElocinDev Downloaded unmodified Shader packs the mod also makes its own copies of The sh"},{"p":"Credits","h":"Ideas the README credits","u":"credits.html#ideas","t":"These gave the mod an idea. In each case the README says nothing of theirs is used. Tectonic (MIT): lava glowing at the very bottom of the deep oceans. The deep is the game's own terrain, stretched. Olaf's Relatively Placed Blocks : small blocks sharing one space. Tough As Nails : the cold and the thirst. Subnautica (1, 2 and Below Zero), Alex's Caves and Thalassophobia : the Dead Water's seas. Every creature, model, texture and sound there is Static Hollow's own."},{"p":"Credits","h":"Tools","u":"credits.html#tools","t":"Blockbench for the creatures' models. The project files come separately as StaticHollow-Blockbench.zip . Real-ESRGAN , an AI upscaler, for the optional HD packs (and since 1.61.0 the chapter gear in them). ElevenLabs for the voices, since 1.71.2: Hal's orientation tapes and what Tune-In Town's cast say."},{"p":"Credits","h":"This website","u":"credits.html#this-wiki","t":"Every story detail, item description, note and line of dialogue comes from the mod's own files (its README, language file, data and source), version 1.72.2. What changed in 1.72.3 is from its changelog on CurseForge. The screenshots are the mod's own CurseForge screenshots, and the soundtrack cover and the Dead Channel logo are the mod's. The home page's scene is rebuilt from the mod's own main-menu layers, and the item and advancement icons are the mod's own textures. The cover art is the mod's CurseForge image. Fonts, all under the SIL Open Font License and included with the site: Big Shoulders Display (Patric King), Spectral (Production Type) and Courier Prime (Alan Dague-Greene)."},{"p":"Credits","h":"Legal","u":"credits.html#legal","t":"Static Hollow is an independent mod for Minecraft. It and this website are not official Minecraft products and are not approved by or associated with Mojang or Microsoft. Minecraft is a trademark of Mojang. Creepypasta and folklore characters belong to the stories and places they come from."},{"p":"The Gardener, Reborn (and Reborn Again)","h":"","u":"entities/gardener-reborn.html","t":"The ring of thorned roots round the risen Great Bloom Boss, twice Appears when You bring the Rosemont Device within 32 blocks of the risen Great Bloom Health 600 (Reborn). Reborn Again: 900 Size Ten feet tall; four blocks in his last phase Weak to Fire (takes half again). Sixty damage in three seconds puts him on one knee Drops The Bloomshears, three Bloom Heartwood and the Gardener's Seed, both times"},{"p":"The Gardener, Reborn (and Reborn Again)","h":"The release","u":"entities/gardener-reborn.html#the-release","t":"Carry the Rosemont Device toward the risen Great Bloom. Within 32 blocks, the Bloom goes still and turns every petal on the Device. Then it gags, heaves, and spits the Gardener back up in a gush of nectar, his body knitting itself together with vines. It folds its petals shut over its mouth, and a ring of thorned roots six blocks high comes up round the arena (48 blocks out from the Bloom since 1.38). Nothing gets through the ring, and it tears at whatever pushes against it. If you end up outside it alone, after ten seconds the roots part to let you back in. here he comes. it's giving him back. it doesn't want that thing anywhere near its mouth. ??? as the Bloom gives him back"},{"p":"The Gardener, Reborn (and Reborn Again)","h":"Description","u":"entities/gardener-reborn.html#description","t":"He's rebuilt on the first Gardener's own body: ten feet tall, the long canvas coat (rotted now, stained with the Bloom, torn where its petals came through), the wide hat, the cage of root ribs, the long thin arms and root feet. Everything the Bloom did to him is still there: grey bark split along every seam with the Bloom's petals breathing in the splits, the ribs pried open round a small copy of the Bloom's mouth in his chest, the Bloom's red petals round the hollow of his face with two green lights deep in it and a jaw of teeth under them. His left arm is a tentacle ending in a hook. In his right hand are the Bloomshears : two of the Bloom's teeth hinged by a tendril."},{"p":"The Gardener, Reborn (and Reborn Again)","h":"How he fights","u":"entities/gardener-reborn.html#how-he-fights","t":""},{"p":"The Gardener, Reborn (and Reborn Again)","h":"Phase 1","u":"entities/gardener-reborn.html#phase-1","t":"Shear Snap: the shears opened wide, then snapped shut in front of him. Hedge Sweep: he crouches and twists, sweeping 270 degrees round him. Root Lattice: shears into the ground, and three fanned lines of root spikes run out toward you. Pollen Breath: head back, then a golden cone: weakness, slowness, and the Bloom's infection. At 65% he screams and tears the shears apart at the hinge, taking one blade in his hook. The ring cracks open in three places and the Flesh pours in. It goes for him as hard as for you."},{"p":"The Gardener, Reborn (and Reborn Again)","h":"Phase 2","u":"entities/gardener-reborn.html#phase-2","t":"Twin Cut: blades crossed overhead, three cuts and a slam. Petal Storm: he spins up on his tentacle in a spiral of razor petals. Get in close or behind them. Graft Leap: he lands where you were, and the Bloom grafts itself onto the ground there. It heals him while he stands in it, burns, and withers in half a minute. Feed: he reaches through for one of the Flesh's infected and eats it (+30 health). Tendril Call: the ground cracks under you. At 30% the Bloom pours itself into him. He grows to four blocks, petals burst out of his back, and his chest mouth opens. The music turns into The Choir ."},{"p":"The Gardener, Reborn (and Reborn Again)","h":"Phase 3","u":"entities/gardener-reborn.html#phase-3","t":"Whip-Shears: the blades on root chains, whirled overhead and swept across twelve blocks in front of him. Chest Choir: the chest mouth's shockwave, which also brings down whatever you built in front of him. The Bloom Eclipse (once, at 20%): the Bloom closes its dome, the dark comes down, and four spore pods fall into the arena. Each one you don't break within fifteen seconds heals him 50 and lets two tendrils up. The Wilting Embrace (once, below 10%): his tentacle takes you and he walks you toward the Bloom's mouth. Hit him six times to break free."},{"p":"The Gardener, Reborn (and Reborn Again)","h":"How to survive him","u":"entities/gardener-reborn.html#how-to-survive-him","t":"Bring fire. He takes half again from it. Burst damage works: sixty damage inside three seconds puts him on one knee. When the ring cracks at 65%, the Flesh's infected come in. Let them fight him, but kill the ones he reaches for, because each one he eats heals him 30. Break all four spore pods during the eclipse. Keep the Device close. The Watcher: \"keep the device close. i'll come for you when it's time.\""},{"p":"The Gardener, Reborn (and Reborn Again)","h":"Reborn Again","u":"entities/gardener-reborn.html#reborn-again","t":"Since 1.40, killing him isn't the end. The Bloom grows him back once more: the Gardener, Reborn Again , faster and harder. The tracker reads \"The Bloom is growing him back. Stay near it.\" it isn't letting him go. it's growing him back. stay close. kill him again, and i'll open it. ??? as the Bloom grows him back Kill him the second time, and the Watcher rips the portal into the Bloom open for the launch . Reborn Again has half as much health again (900), hits harder (13 to the Reborn's 10), is quicker on his feet and a quarter quicker between moves, and never quite stops bleeding the Bloom's light out of every split in him. His bar turns red and reads \"The Gardener, Reborn Again\". He drops the same things."},{"p":"The Gardener, Reborn (and Reborn Again)","h":"His end","u":"entities/gardener-reborn.html#his-end","t":"When he dies the shears wilt, he kneels, his petals fall, and he's left as a heap of leaves round a seed. The ring withers back into the ground and the Bloom shuts itself up tight. The Bloomshears (Graft): full swings snip twice, and the Bloom in them hates the Flesh, so they hit infected half again as hard. Use them to drive three lines of thorned roots toward what you face. Bloom Heartwood (three): close-grained, pale, still warm, green light running in it like sap. The Gardener's Seed : a hard black seed the size of a fist, split along one seam. Something in it breathes. Bloom Heartwood goes into Chapter Three's gear: the Heartwood tools, the Thorn Whip, the Spore Mace and two pieces of the Bloomwoven (see Gear for every chapter )."},{"p":"The Gardener, Reborn (and Reborn Again)","h":"Turned","u":"entities/gardener-reborn.html#turned","t":"Since 1.51.0 the parasite can take him. Turned, he's the Reborn, Consumed . The Hub's replay portal for The Bloom brings him back for another go."},{"p":"The giant tentacles","h":"","u":"entities/giant-tentacles.html","t":"Shown in game as \"Tentacle of the Great Bloom\" Grabs How many Eight round the Great Bloom's mouth Size Thick as trees at first; since 1.27.2, towers as wide as a hill at the root Sounds A tentacle lashes, grabs, drags; bones creak in its grip Death message \"[you] was eaten by the Great Bloom\""},{"p":"The giant tentacles","h":"Description","u":"entities/giant-tentacles.html#description","t":"Round the Great Bloom's mouth rise eight tentacles, feeling about, curling over at their tips. Down in its realm they come up out of the green round the islands like towers, each as wide as a hill at the root, curling over far above you. Every light in the Bloom beats with its heart, the veins in the tentacles too."},{"p":"The giant tentacles","h":"When you fall","u":"entities/giant-tentacles.html#when-you-fall","t":"Fall off an island in the Bloom and a tentacle whips up out of the green after you. Since 1.27.2 it comes straight up out of the Bloom's throat under you, twenty blocks thick. It coils round you and drags you back through the air and down into its mouth. Anything else that falls goes the same way. Caught, your sight closes in red and shakes, you hear your bones creak in its grip and your breath forced out of you, slime and blood trail off you, and over its mouth its teeth close in over your sight from all round, ring by ring, until there is nothing. Since 1.38 you go down its throat alive, into its stomach. Chat: \"Something huge is reaching up out of the green for you...\" then \"It has you.\""},{"p":"The giant tentacles","h":"When the Binding breaks","u":"entities/giant-tentacles.html#when-the-binding-breaks","t":"Touch the Binding twice and the Great Bloom goes mad. Its tentacles come up out of the green round the Binding's island (out of its throat, since 1.27.2), over the edge, and take hold. You have ten seconds. Then they pull the whole island down its throat, rift and all, and take anyone left out there one by one."},{"p":"The giant tentacles","h":"Round the risen Bloom","u":"entities/giant-tentacles.html#round-the-risen-bloom","t":"The Bloom that rises through the glasshouse reaches for anything within about 26 blocks, players first. The changed Bloom reaches for anything within ninety, and when it's hungry it comes up out of the ground under anyone out on its petals: cracks first, then its tentacles, one where you'll be if you keep going. When you carry the Rosemont Device toward it, its roots come up after you: green cracks open under your feet, and two seconds later a tendril bursts out that whips, holds and infects whatever it catches (\"Something in the ground has you.\")."},{"p":"The giant tentacles","h":"Over the ledge","u":"entities/giant-tentacles.html#over-the-ledge","t":"During the launch, the colossal Bloom's tentacles rise up round the ledge and hang over it, trembling, held back. The Watcher is holding them. don't look at them. i've got them. i can't hold them long. ??? on the ledge After the Device goes off, the tentacles wither black. After the Omni Ray, they're gone, vaporized with its mouth and throat."},{"p":"The giant tentacles","h":"The great flower's tendril","u":"entities/giant-tentacles.html#the-great-flowers-tendril","t":"The great flower under the dome, before any of this, has a single tendril of its own. It fastens on, slows you to a crawl and drags you in, drinking, and holds you at its throat and bites, again and again; after the third bite it spits you out. Three good hits tear the tendril and free you (\"It has you! Hit it to tear yourself free!\")."},{"p":"The giant tentacles","h":"How to survive them","u":"entities/giant-tentacles.html#how-to-survive-them","t":"Don't fall. In the Bloom, the bridges and edges are the danger, not the creatures. A tentacle that takes you drags you into the Bloom's mouth, and since 1.38 down into its stomach. Bring a weapon to cut your way out. When the Binding breaks, don't stop to watch. Ten seconds."},{"p":"His creations and servants","h":"","u":"entities/his-creations.html","t":"What the First Signal let out of his kingdom into your world at the start of Chapter Ten , to find you and the Watcher and take you off the air. His own, nobody else's: four creations, three servants, and his congregation at home. His kingdom, then your world Hostile Whose The First Signal's Let out In the Broadcast, the start of Chapter Ten (1.64.0) When Every night after, and any time you're down in the caves. Lookalikes by day too They drop Signal Fragments; his servants, Blackout Shards How to live Don't be seen. Don't be heard. Hide, and wait for the dawn."},{"p":"His creations and servants","h":"At a glance","u":"entities/his-creations.html#at-a-glance","t":"Creature Health Drops The Longplay 60 1 to 2 Signal Fragments; a Blackout Shard one time in twenty The Hanger 26 Up to a Signal Fragment, up to 2 bones The Lookalike 34 A Signal Fragment, up to 2 rotten flesh ERR (▯▯▯) 50 2 to 4 Signal Fragments; a Blackout Shard one time in four The Announcer 180, a boss bar 5 to 8 Signal Fragments, 1 to 2 Blackout Shards The Cameraman 150, a boss bar 5 to 8 Signal Fragments, 1 to 2 Blackout Shards The Stagehand 220, a boss bar 5 to 8 Signal Fragments, 1 to 2 Blackout Shards The Faithful 30 1 to 3 Signal Fragments; sometimes red or black candles; a Faithful's Dagger one time in five SENTINEL Crew 20 Nothing: they're only in a cutscene The End's Guardian, Taken 300 It can't be brought down Looting adds to the fragments and shards. What they're made into (the Blackout Ingot, blade, tools and armour) is on chapter gear ."},{"p":"His creations and servants","h":"How they find you","u":"entities/his-creations.html#how-they-find-you","t":"They don't just know where you are. They see you and they hear you. What they've only heard, they come to look at; what they've seen, they hunt until they've lost it a while; then they search where they lost it, and give up. Sight: a cone ahead of its face, out to its range, with nothing in the way. Shorter the darker it is where you are (under light 5, half; under 2, less again), and much shorter if you're crouched. Crouched in tall plants (grass, ferns, bushes, leaves, crops), it can't make you out past a few blocks. Hidden, not at all. Sound: sprinting, jumping and landing, breaking and placing blocks, doors, fighting and eating are heard round where they were made (the louder, the further), and they come to look. Each piece of Blackout armour quiets you by a fifth; the whole set, and they can't hear you at all ( Radio Silence ). Your heartbeat: the nearer one is to finding you, the faster and louder it goes, and his static creeps in at the edges of your eyes."},{"p":"His creations and servants","h":"Hiding","u":"entities/his-creations.html#hiding","t":"A Steel Locker (iron and bars): use it and you're in, pulling the door to. You see out through its vents, and nothing sees in. Crouch to get out (or use it again). Under a bed: crouch and use any bed and you slide under it. Crouch to come out. One that saw you go in, or hears you in there (any noise you make), tears it open and drags you out. One that's only looking for you comes and stands at it a while, sniffing, listening, and goes. Sometimes it pulls it open anyway."},{"p":"His creations and servants","h":"They hunt together","u":"entities/his-creations.html#they-hunt-together","t":"Since 1.64.1: The call: one sees you, its head snaps round and it shrieks, and every one of his for thirty blocks that isn't already after someone comes to look. The surround: those after you don't all come down the same line. Each takes its own side of you, spread round you, and closes in from there (the last few blocks straight at you). The cut-off: they don't run to where you are, they run to where you're going. The faster you're going, the further ahead of you they aim. The search: lost, they check the lockers and beds round where they lost you, stood at each, listening. Far off, now and then, one just stands and stares at you. Hunting, they beat in wooden doors (not iron). Since 1.67.0 they climb walls after you if you're above them (not the servants), and stuck for a couple of seconds they claw through what's in the way if it's wood, glass, earth, leaves or wool: cracks spread across it, a few seconds' work. Stone and iron hold them, they never touch anything with a chest in it, and with mobGriefing off they never break anything. Or they try some other way round. At dawn, those out under the sky go off the air (static, and gone), unless they're hunting you. The ones underground stay, and so do his servants and the Lookalikes."},{"p":"His creations and servants","h":"When they come","u":"entities/his-creations.html#when-they-come","t":"The first of them come for you a few seconds after the Broadcast, near home. Every night after (and any time you're down in the caves) the broadcast goes out round you, a tone far off, and they come: more each night you've lived through, up to ten, out of the dark and out of your sight. By day, Lookalikes, near villages and herds. Now and then one of his servants comes at the head of a night's broadcast. The Watcher stays at your house, and strikes down anything of his that comes near it. A Lookalike can fool him. His sites come through into your world after it, each kept by one of his servants, each with a Broadcast Core : break it and the site goes off the air ( Pulled the Plug ), and for a minute his signal's torn open where it stood: a way into his kingdom. A keeper you've killed doesn't come back. More on Chapter Ten ."},{"p":"His creations and servants","h":"Tonight on Channel Zero","u":"entities/his-creations.html#tonight-on-channel-zero","t":"Since 1.67.0 each night has its own programme (never last night's again), told as the night comes in: \"TONIGHT ON CHANNEL ZERO: ...\" Programme What it tells you What they do THE SIEGE \"They know where you live. They're gathering out there - and they'll come all at once.\" More of them. They gather out of sight, and once enough are out there (or a minute into the night) every one of them comes at once, from every side. They claw through quicker. THE STALKING \"Quiet tonight. Don't look back - and if you do, it won't be there.\" Fewer, and quiet: no shriek when one sees you, no calling the others. Look at one and it's gone behind something; look away and it's nearer. THE CHASE \"Tonight they run. And they don't give up.\" More of them, a quarter faster, and they keep after you three times as long once they've lost you. THE AMBUSH \"They're already here. Waiting in the dark for you to come to them.\" They're already close, waiting in the dark, stock still and facing your way, till you're on top of them. THE IMPOSTORS \"Trust nothing out there tonight. Not even a knock at the door.\" Mostly Lookalikes. They throw their voices to make you look the wrong way, and something knocks at your door wearing the Watcher."},{"p":"His creations and servants","h":"His creations","u":"entities/his-creations.html#his-creations","t":""},{"p":"His creations and servants","h":"The Longplay","u":"entities/his-creations.html#the-longplay","t":"A person recorded over too many times: drawn out tall and thin like a chewed-up tape, eleven feet tall, tracking lines through it, its face smeared to a blur with one dark mouth in it. Out at the edge of the light, between the trees. Watched, it pauses : stopped dead, mid-step, the picture of it juddering like a paused tape. Look away and it plays again, fast-forward: nearer every time you look back. Stare at it too long and the tape slips and a frame's skipped: it's nearer, though nobody saw it move. It comes at you from behind, and in reach and unwatched it takes you with both long hands. The Lash (1.67.0): a loop of its tape whipped out at you from up to twelve blocks, round your legs, and you're reeled in, slowed. Rewind (1.67.0): hurt past half, it plays itself back to where it was a couple of seconds ago, a little mended. Its death: its tape runs out. It's hauled up, drawn out tall, and folds up onto its face, ribbon spilling."},{"p":"His creations and servants","h":"The Hanger","u":"entities/his-creations.html#the-hanger","t":"A person folded the wrong way: too many joints, its arms and legs bent back over it, its head hung upside down under its body. Fast, and fragile. It goes up walls and over ceilings. In the caves (and in the trees, at night) it hangs from the roof over a way through, still, and drops on whoever passes under it. It jinks as it comes, bites, and runs off up the walls into the dark to come again. Lost, it goes up onto the roof over where it lost you, and waits. His burrows have Hangers on their roofs. The Hoist (1.67.0): hung from a roof right over you, it reaches down, lifts you up to it, bites, and lets go (and maybe comes down after you). The Pounce (1.67.0): from six to eleven blocks off, wound down low, a leap that pins you. Its death: it flips onto its back and curls up like a dead spider, twitching."},{"p":"His creations and servants","h":"The Lookalike","u":"entities/his-creations.html#the-lookalike","t":"A copy. A villager, a cow, a sheep, a pig, a chicken: the Watcher. Only a frame out: its picture a beat behind itself, its sounds played backwards, and now and then, for a frame, what it really is. Lookalikes walk by day too. It wanders up to you, being what it copies, closer every time you look away. It shies away from you into the dark like an animal (so you'll follow), and lets itself in through your doors. Near enough, or hit, it opens , down its middle, the two halves of it swinging apart, and what's in there leaps at you. On his sets they stand about being people. The Embrace (1.67.0): its leap lands on you and it closes round you, holding on, biting. Hit it and it lets go. The Lure (1.67.0): disguised, it throws its voice off to one side of you. Its death: flung open, on its knees, over backwards."},{"p":"His creations and servants","h":"ERR","u":"entities/his-creations.html#err","t":"The broken script. Its name in game is a row of boxes, \"▯▯▯\". A figure in slices that don't line up, patches of it the colour of a picture that's missing. It skips : it isn't anywhere in between, it's just further on, a frame at a time. It skips to where you're going, and out of your sight it comes up behind you, whispering. It can only be hurt in the frames it's all there. Rare, and worse every night it's let out. Things go wrong in your chat when it's near: \"[Server thread/WARN]: ▯▯▯ moved wrongly!\" \"Missing texture: statichollow:textures/entity/you.png\" \"java.lang.IllegalStateException: you were not supposed to see this\" Lag (1.67.0): its hit puts you back where you were a couple of seconds ago (\"moved wrongly!\"). Desync (1.67.0): hurt, it comes apart into three. Two of them are echoes that go to static at a touch. Its death: it comes to pieces, then the picture collapses, a line, a dot: \"[Server thread/INFO]: ▯▯▯ has left the game\"."},{"p":"His creations and servants","h":"His servants","u":"entities/his-creations.html#his-servants","t":"The three at his war table. He sends them after his creations, one at the head of a night's broadcast now and then. Big and slow to die, each with its own way of finding you and finishing you, and each a boss: its bar's up while it's near. Each keeps one of his sites. Killing one earns Off His Air ."},{"p":"His creations and servants","h":"The Announcer","u":"entities/his-creations.html#the-announcer","t":"Tall, in a long coat, an old radio's speaker grille for a face, its dial glowing, a microphone in its hand on a cable that goes back into it. It keeps his Transmitter . Its voice knocks you down: a blast of it out in front of it, everything in the way thrown back, deafened, sick. It keeps you at the edge of its voice, circling, and calls everything of his for 64 blocks in: \"STAY TUNED.\" It says other things too: \"WE INTERRUPT THIS PROGRAMME.\" \"PLEASE DO NOT ADJUST YOUR SET.\" \"YOU ARE ON AIR.\" \"THIS IS NOT A TEST.\" The Cable (1.67.0): its microphone cable thrown round you, and you're reeled in in front of it, into its blast. Feedback (1.67.0): too close, a howl all round it throws everyone off, sick. Its death: it clutches its head, staggers, kneels and falls. \"WE ARE EXPERIENCING TECHNICAL DIFFICULTIES.\""},{"p":"His creations and servants","h":"The Cameraman","u":"entities/his-creations.html#the-cameraman","t":"An old studio camera for a head with a red tally light on it, and three legs like its tripod's. It keeps his Burrow . While it films you, everything knows where you are : its light comes on, and every one of his creations for a long way round comes for you. Its flash blinds you. It keeps you in frame, backing off if you come at it, round the corner after you. The Zoom (1.67.0): a sudden rush in from its frame. \"CUT.\" The Slam (1.67.0): reared up, its front leg driven down, and the ground jumps under you. Its death: its legs buckle one by one, its lens goes, and it tips over. \"CUT.\""},{"p":"His creations and servants","h":"The Stagehand","u":"entities/his-creations.html#the-stagehand","t":"Big, a sack over its head with a slit in it and a light behind the slit, coils of rope over it, sandbags hung off its belt, one hand a fist and the other a rigging hook. It keeps his Set . It throws the hook , drags you in, and brings its fist down: the ground jumps. It charges : sidestep it and it goes into the wall behind you, dazed and wide open (it takes half as much again). Sandbags (1.67.0): three heaved up high over you, the ground marked where each will land. Get out from under. Cue the Dark (1.67.0): it yanks a rope and your eyes go dark, and in the dark it charges. Its death: it drops its hook, kneels, and goes over like a tree. Since 1.64.1 all seven have their own horrible sounds (a children's presenter's voice on a chewed tape, laughter played backwards, many mouths screaming at once, joints going the wrong way, a modem's scream, a PA's off-key chime, whispering behind you), and every death ends the same: static boiling off it, the thump of it hitting the floor, the picture of it shaking as it goes."},{"p":"His creations and servants","h":"The Faithful","u":"entities/his-creations.html#the-faithful","t":"His congregation, in his castle (since 1.64.2). Tall, in hooded robes of a red so dark it's nearly black, a little red light hung at the breast, and under the hood nothing: a black hole where a face goes, a couple of specks of red far back in it. They keep his rites : kneeling in circles of red and black candles round a red lamp set in the floor, rocking, chanting (its words nobody's language); praising on their knees with their arms up to him, swaying; bowed right down flat, arms out along the floor; walking the causeway and the courtyard in slow procession, hands clasped, hoods bowed. Two circles in the courtyard, four in the war hall's aisles behind the pillars, eight kneeling at his war table (four a side, behind his servants), three walking the causeway and three round the courtyard. They don't stop for you. But their hoods turn after you, wherever you go, further round than a head should. Come right up to one and the whole circle stops: on their feet, silent, every hood on you, the nearest whispering at you, till you go. Hurt one and every one of them for 24 blocks turns, the chant breaks into a scream, and they run at you, arms out, clawing, their touch putting your eyes out. Get far enough away and they go back to their places and kneel again. Their death: the robe falls empty. It reels, its hood drops in on itself, and there's nothing in it: it all goes down in a heap of cloth, sleeves flat out, smoke and static coming off it. They're set down once in every world his castle's in, and those killed stay dead. Sometimes they drop the Faithful's Dagger he made them (\"What his Faithful give themselves to him with\"), a quick blade. In the Broadcast they're down on their faces as he goes by. At the Coronation they give themselves to him with their daggers, and his armour forms out of them; at the Forge they close its cracks and chant their glyphs into it; at the Second Rite they sing round him, \"head to crown him. wings to bear him.\" / \"heart to keep him. ours, for ever.\", and in the end they seize him and take him into a seal. See the First Signal ."},{"p":"His creations and servants","h":"SENTINEL's crew","u":"entities/his-creations.html#sentinels-crew","t":"SENTINEL Crew, 20 health, only in THE LAST BROADCAST 's third part. When he tears SENTINEL's right side off, a module of it comes down in his sea, and its astronauts climb out of its hatch onto its hull, in white suits and gold visors, their packs on their backs, their radio breaking up: - to anyone. we're down. we are DOWN. where are we? that's not... that's not our sky. everyone out. Reyes - check the hold. ...something's moving in the hold. SENTINEL's crew on the radio SENTINEL brought Blackwater's parasites up with it, and they're out, onto the crew one after another. The last of them backs off to the end of the hull, and the parasites stop, and the Chorus 's last voice speaks through them: \"...one voice left.\" \"it will do.\" They pour into him, and the hive comes up through him: \"we hear you, signal.\" Then the Harbinger swallows him whole."},{"p":"His creations and servants","h":"The End's guardian","u":"entities/his-creations.html#the-ends-guardian","t":"The End's Guardian, Taken (since 1.71.0): the Ender Dragon with the parasite all through it, the hive's now, its back split open and the hive's growths on it. When he tears his arena up into the End, it comes up out of the dark and circles it. the last thing your world kept for itself. and look what's kept it all this time. The First Signal as it comes up It has 300 health, but it can't be brought down (the hive keeps it going); only he can do that. Now and then it comes round at one of you and strafes you, its fireballs bursting into its breath on the floor, or dives at you, low and fast, and through. Hurt, it screams. At the Second Rite he rides it down and takes its head, its wings and its heart for himself. It's a creature of its own, apart from the Infested Ender Dragon ."},{"p":"His creations and servants","h":"How to survive them","u":"entities/his-creations.html#how-to-survive-them","t":"At night, keep to the dark and crouch. Crouched in tall grass, they can't make you out past a few blocks. Don't sprint, don't jump, don't break or place things near them. Each piece of Blackout armour makes you quieter. When your heartbeat races, one's close to finding you. Get into a Steel Locker or under a bed before it sees you go in, and keep still. Build in stone or iron, with iron doors: they claw through wood, glass, earth, leaves and wool. Kill a Cameraman before anything else: while it films you, everything knows where you are. Sidestep the Stagehand's charge into a wall, then hit it. Last till dawn: most of the ones out under the sky go off the air (not one that's after you). Read the programme as the night comes in, and don't open the door on THE IMPOSTORS."},{"p":"The Hollow Saint","h":"","u":"entities/hollow-saint.html","t":"The cathedral's sanctuary Boss Summoned at The Hollow Reliquary, with one head of each of the nine creepypastas Size Five blocks tall Health 500 Phases Two: its first form, and its dark form from half health Drops The Saint's Heart, 4 to 5 Saint's Shrouds, and by chance gold ingots (60%), a totem of undying (25%) or an enchanted golden apple (5%). It has no head to drop. The Hollow Saint Nine eyes in the iron grid, all of them on you."},{"p":"The Hollow Saint","h":"Summoning it","u":"entities/hollow-saint.html#summoning","t":"In the cathedral's sanctuary, put one head from each of the nine different creepypastas on the nine pedestals round the Hollow Reliquary, then right-click the reliquary with an empty hand. The summoning takes about ten seconds and it can't be hurt until it has fully risen. The floor goes dark and a circle of runes burns open; a beam of light streams out of every head into an orb over the reliquary; souls and embers pour in and lightning crawls over it; the floor cracks and red light comes up through it. Then the Saint rises up out of the ground into the light, slowly, and roars with many dead voices at once: a flash, rings of light, a pillar into the sky, and everything nearby thrown back into darkness."},{"p":"The Hollow Saint","h":"Description","u":"entities/hollow-saint.html#description","t":"It stands five blocks tall in a deep cowl. Its iron mask is a grid bolted over raw flesh, with nine real eyes bulging out of their square sockets that roll on their own and all turn to fix on you when you look at it. Under the mask a jaw drops open on long teeth. Its robe, in a blood red trimmed with tarnished gold, is torn open over its ribs and the heart beating behind them. Vertebrae break out of its back. It wears an antler crown and a halo of rusted spikes, and it has four arms. Sewn into the robe are the faces of the nine, each one straining out of the cloth, twitching, its mouth falling open. In the dark its eyes, its mouth, its heart and the faces' eyes burn. Its heartbeat booms across the cathedral while it lives."},{"p":"The Hollow Saint","h":"How it fights","u":"entities/hollow-saint.html#first-form","t":"Calls the nine. A red-black portal tears open in the ground for each creepypasta it calls, and it claws its way up out of it to fight beside the Saint. Screams static that blinds you and throws you back. From half health it starts teleporting behind you and calling lightning down on everyone. Bleeding III makes it reel for a moment: it staggers and doubles over, and blood pours out of the wound in its gut."},{"p":"The Hollow Saint","h":"At half health, it changes","u":"entities/hollow-saint.html#it-changes","t":"It freezes and rises off the ground, arms flung wide, every face on it screaming. The Watcher hanging from the ceiling turns to it, a black sun swelling between its hands, and pours a crackling river of shadow down into the Saint's heart. A rune circle burns into the ground under it and spins faster and faster, the faces tear loose from its robe one by one and rise, screaming, and the air goes violet-black. Nothing you do can hurt it now. Then it bursts: a flash, a pillar of light, shockwaves along the ground, its ribs blown out in shards, and the whole world kicks."},{"p":"The Hollow Saint","h":"Its dark form","u":"entities/hollow-saint.html#dark-form","t":"It drops back down charred black and cracked with burning light, every eye red, its ribs wrenched open, and its heart pushed out of its chest, turned black and veined with violet light. The boss bar turns purple. From here it is faster, teleports behind you in a burst of shadow, calls lightning down, and uses its dark magic: Abyssal Rupture It raises all four arms and a violet circle burns open under every player near it, spinning faster and crackling for a second and a half. Then a pillar of black-violet power erupts out of each one: 12 damage, flung into the air, and darkness. Get out of the circle."},{"p":"The Hollow Saint","h":"How to survive it","u":"entities/hollow-saint.html#how-to-survive-it","t":"Bring the chapter's gear. The Static Mail's full set makes creepypastas within 32 blocks glow through walls, which helps against the ones it calls up. The Saint's Requiem is made from its own heart, so it can't help you here, but the Sinew Cleaver's Rend stacks Bleeding, and Bleeding III makes the Saint reel. Watch the floor in its dark form: a violet circle under your feet means move now. It teleports behind you from half health. Keep turning."},{"p":"The Hollow Saint","h":"Its end","u":"entities/hollow-saint.html#its-end","t":"When it dies, the Watcher won't let it stay. Its beam turns red and burns the ground open under the Saint: a portal to hell, ringed with burning runes. The Saint tries to claw its way up into the air, every arm reaching, and a huge burning hand rises out of the portal and closes round it. Twice it shoves the fingers apart and drags itself half out; twice the hand clenches and yanks it back. Then it is dragged down through the hole, screaming, and the portal slams shut in a blast of fire. The chat reads The Hollow Saint has fallen. It leaves the Saint's Heart , a real heart still beating in your hand, on the ground and in an item frame. Since 1.40, its tomb in the cathedral's undercroft stands empty, the gate forced from the inside and its chains broken. do you understand what you've done? they were keeping it in. it was the only thing in this world bigger than me. ??? after the Saint falls"},{"p":"The Hollow Saint","h":"Field notes","u":"entities/hollow-saint.html#field-notes","t":"The priest's journal in the undercroft says the Saint lay sealed in its tomb \"under nine chains and nine candles, one for each of the heads they took to make it\", and that he kept the candles burning forty years. Read his journal and the bell-ringer's tally ."},{"p":"The Hollow Saint","h":"Turned","u":"entities/hollow-saint.html#turned","t":"Since 1.51.0 the parasite can take it. Turned, it's the Saint Unmade : dragging itself on tentacles, its chest a mouth the height of it. The Projectionist's reruns bring back its shadow beam, and the Hub's replay portal for The Hollow raises it out of the floor again."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"","u":"entities/index.html","t":"Every creature in Static Hollow, in the order you meet them, across all ten chapters and THE LAST BROADCAST. Bosses and the creatures with the most to them have their own case files; everything else is here. Each chapter's creatures are marked in that chapter's colour. Almost everything has its own 3D model, sounds, attacks and death, its own drop, and a spawn egg in the Static Hollow creative tab. Since 1.48.0 nearly all of them can also be taken over by the parasite and turned into something else: see the Turned . The twenty creatures of chapters one to three that have heads (the nine creepypastas, the nine killers and cryptids, the Gardener and the Rootlings) drop theirs the first time you kill each, then at 10% plus 5% a level of Looting. The Hollow Saint has no head to drop."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Chapter one: the Nine","u":"entities/index.html#chapter-one","t":"They hunt everyone once the Forsaken Altar is awake, mostly in the dark. All nine are dragged back down when the Breach Altar wakes."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"??? (the Watcher)","u":"entities/index.html#the-watcher-entry","t":"Never attacks Stares, waves, points, peeks, and sometimes stands right behind you. It speaks at every turning point in the story."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Hollow Saint","u":"entities/index.html#hollow-saint-entry","t":"Boss of chapter one What the nine were all pieces of. Raised at the cathedral's reliquary with one head from each."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Hollow Neighbor","u":"entities/index.html#hollow-neighbor","t":"Hostile to players only Stalks you, vanishes and reappears behind you, knocks on doors and whispers. Every few minutes it sends you a chat message pretending to be a friend, and if you're indoors near a window it rises up behind the glass, taps on it and says it to your face. Its pinprick pupils follow you, even on its placed head. Attacks: The Long Neck (its neck stretches across the gap and its mouth drags you in) and Turn Around (it's gone in a puff of smoke and its hands are on your shoulders from behind)."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Stitchjaw","u":"entities/index.html#stitchjaw","t":"Hostile to everything Crawls flat like a lizard and climbs walls. Every bite that lands opens the wound further: Bleeding I, II, III. Attacks: Death Roll (jaws locked on you, rolling like a crocodile) and Seam Burst (every stitch tears at once in a ring of thread, bone and blood)."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Weeping Shepherd","u":"entities/index.html#weeping-shepherd","t":"Neutral, fights back Weeps, and stares if you stare. Hunts the undead. A rusted bell tolls as it walks. Attacks: The Toll (three rings of pale light along the ground that burn the undead) and The Crook (a crack of pale fire torn along the ground)."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Lullaby Mother","u":"entities/index.html#lullaby-mother","t":"Neutral by day, hostile at night Steals villagers and whispers a broken lullaby. Her hits can drag you into the Hollow, a sealed black room under the world, for 15 seconds. When she dies she draws a kitchen knife and drives it into her own eye. Attacks: Hush Now (she rocks you like a baby while the life runs out of you; hurt her to make her drop you) and The Knife (five stabs, fast)."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Broadcast","u":"entities/index.html#broadcast","t":"Hostile to players A man with an old CRT television for a head, its screen crawling with live static. It skips toward you like a dropped video frame. Don't look at it : staring at the screen burns you every second. Don't touch it : it shocks. Its antenna tips glow green once it has seen you, burn red while you look at it, and flash red when it strikes. Attacks: Dead Air (a flickering line pins where it's aiming, then a beam of raw static) and Frame Skip (it drops three frames and is beside you, behind you, in front of you)."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Little Lamb","u":"entities/index.html#little-lamb","t":"Neutral until you hit it A crying child that follows you. Hit it and it shows its real face and gets fast. Hunts livestock. Attacks: The Shriek (a cone of scream) and Pounce and Gnaw (it clings to you, chewing)."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Hymnal","u":"entities/index.html#the-hymnal","t":"Hostile to players and iron golems Floats. Its song slows and weakens you and heals the other creepypastas. At Bleeding III blood wells up along the stitches over its eyes, but it never stops singing. Attacks: The Page Storm (pages with edges like razors) and The Rapture (a chord from a choir that isn't there lifts you off your feet)."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Underneath","u":"entities/index.html#the-underneath","t":"Waits Buried with only its hands showing; stand near it too long and it claws its way out. It breathes under your bed and comes up for you when you lie down. Get out of bed within about four seconds. Never in Creative or on Peaceful. Attacks: Hands From Below and Burrow (a ridge of earth tears toward you and it bursts up under your feet)."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Antlerkin","u":"entities/index.html#antlerkin","t":"Hunts everything Imitates cows, pigs and sheep to lure prey. Faster in the dark, and fastest at night, when it calls and runs its prey down until dawn with its eyes burning ember to amber in its skull. Attacks: The Charge (let it hit a wall and it stands there dazed) and The Toss . The Antlerkin, close."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Mourners","u":"entities/index.html#mourner","t":"In the cathedral's pews Praying, their heads turning after you. Hurt one, or play the organ, and they all stand up. At nightfall the dead are back in their pews. At the Soul Well they kneel round the altar as its keepers."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Interred","u":"entities/index.html#interred","t":"In the undercroft's tombs Open a sarcophagus and what was buried in it might be the Interred, who sits up and climbs out. The sealed ones open by themselves when you come close. The Lullaby Mother, the Broadcast, the Underneath, the Hollow Neighbor, the Watcher and the Antlerkin have no blood left to lose and never bleed."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Chapter two: the killers and the things from the woods","u":"entities/index.html#chapter-two","t":"Five killers and four cryptids come up once the Breach Altar is awake. They stalk first and only come for you once they've watched long enough, or you hit them."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Mended","u":"entities/index.html#the-mended-entry","t":"Boss of chapter two, 750 health All nine sewn into one thing by the Watcher at the Mending Altar."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Bunnyman","u":"entities/index.html#the-bunnyman","t":"Killer, in the dark, near water A tall man in a filthy rabbit suit with a fire axe. Catch him watching and he stops dead, tilts his head and waves. When he comes, it's a crouch and a spring with the axe coming down as he lands. Chops through wooden doors on Normal and Hard. Throws a hatchet, and goes into a frenzy of chops when badly hurt."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Hookman","u":"entities/index.html#the-hookman","t":"Killer A starved giant in a torn straitjacket, gauze round his head, a rusted meat hook for a hand. He flings the hook on a chain, catches you and reels you in, and pulls riders off horses, boats and carts. Every cut bleeds. He also sweeps the hook low and impales you on it."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Hogshead","u":"entities/index.html#the-hogshead","t":"Killer, 90 health, armoured A butcher the size of a doorway in a rotting pig's head. He squeals, lowers his head and charges; if he reaches you he takes you by the throat. Sidestep and he slams into the wall, stunned: hit him then. Also slams the ground and gores."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Porcelain Man","u":"entities/index.html#the-porcelain-man","t":"Killer, indoors A life-size porcelain doll in a tailcoat. While anyone is looking at him he doesn't move, only his glass eyes; look away and he's closer, in a different pose. He opens doors. He can only be hurt from behind. His music box slows and blinds whoever isn't looking at him."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Harvestman","u":"entities/index.html#the-harvestman","t":"Killer, plains and savannas at night A scarecrow on a post in a field, a crow on its shoulder. Walk close and it climbs down at you. Look away for long and the post is empty. Its scythe sweeps wide: get out of the arc. It calls its crows down and tears roots up out of the ground. Killed, it falls apart into straw and the crow flies off. The Harvestman, down off its post."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Mothman","u":"entities/index.html#mothman","t":"Cryptid, under the night sky Red eyes in the night sky. It circles high and hangs still when you look up at it. Then it screeches (darkness at the edge of your sight, legs heavy), dives claws-first, and sometimes takes you up and lets go. Most of all by rivers and on boats. Bring a bow. Mothman, hanging still in the fog."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Jersey Devil","u":"entities/index.html#the-jersey-devil","t":"Cryptid, pine forests at night Goat legs, bat wings, a horse's skull on a long neck. It screams when it starts hunting (weakness, nausea), springs into the air and glides down onto you; up close it rears and kicks. Breathes fire and sweeps you with its tail."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Dogman","u":"entities/index.html#dogman","t":"Cryptid, forests and taiga at night A wolf that walks like a man. It runs on all fours, faster than you, stands up to howl (it roots you to the spot), pounces and mauls: claw, claw, then a bite that bleeds. It drags you down by the leg and flings you."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Flatwoods Monster","u":"entities/index.html#the-flatwoods-monster","t":"Cryptid, hills and woods in the dark A tall shape in a spade-shaped hood with a glowing red face. It glides, never hurrying, leaving a burning mist. Stare into its face too long and you're sick and slow. Up close it breathes the mist at you; its claws poison. The Flatwoods Monster in a village."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Out in the Void","u":"entities/index.html#out-in-the-void","t":""},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Hand","u":"entities/index.html#the-hand","t":"Catches what falls Pale grey going violet, bigger than a man, on an arm going down and down into the dark. It catches anyone who falls off an island and sets them back down. It hurts."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Driftlight","u":"entities/index.html#driftlight","t":"Harmless A bell of pale flesh the size of a lantern, lit from inside, swimming like a jellyfish. It drops Drift Jelly: Slow Falling for 40 seconds and sight in the dark for 20."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Lamprey","u":"entities/index.html#lamprey","t":"Hostile A long eyeless eel with a glowing lure. It coils, flares six toothed lips and comes at you straight as a whip, then fastens on and drags you out over the dark. Hit it hard to make it let go. Drops Lamprey Teeth and sometimes its lure, still lit."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Chapter three: the glasshouse","u":"entities/index.html#chapter-three","t":""},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Gardener","u":"entities/index.html#the-gardener-entry","t":"Boss of chapter three The Head Gardener, grown into by the flower he tended."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Rootling","u":"entities/index.html#rootling","t":"The Gardener's children Knee-high things with a pale bulb for a head, red pinprick eyes and a grin of thorns. They chatter, leap at you and burrow away to come up somewhere else. They drop Knotted Roots, which make the Gardener's Weeds."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Great Flower","u":"entities/index.html#the-great-flower","t":"Under the dome A parasitic bloom the size of a room, its tendrils feeling about. Get close and it latches on: you're Sapromyiophilous , carrion flies swarm you, and it feeds. Its tendril drags things in and swallows them whole. Three good hits tear its tendril and free you."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Giant Flytrap","u":"entities/index.html#giant-flytrap","t":"In the garden beds A Venus flytrap that snatches you up and chews. Mash E to force the jaws open."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Great Bloom","u":"entities/index.html#the-great-bloom-entry","t":"What the flower really is Far down under the islands of the Bloom, and later risen through the glasshouse."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Tentacle of the Great Bloom","u":"entities/index.html#tentacles-entry","t":"The giant tentacles Eight of them round its mouth, thick as trees, or towers."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Chapter four: the Flesh","u":"entities/index.html#chapter-four","t":"Every one of the Flesh's infected has a split jaw that swings apart sideways, glowing veins, no nose, three sinews out of its back and a blister bursting out of one shoulder. They shamble until they hunt, then sprint with their arms flailing. They hear you running. Their hits get the Flesh into you."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Bosses and mini-bosses","u":"entities/index.html#bosses-of-the-flesh","t":""},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Congregation","u":"entities/index.html#the-congregation","t":"Mini-boss, 400 health, Rosemont The commuters on the crashed bus, fused into one thing that wears the bus as a shell, their legs under it for wheels, their faces in every window. It sleeps until something hits it. Bus Ram : its headlights flash twice and it charges; if it ends against a wall it's stuck for three seconds and the driver takes three times the damage. Window Hands grab you at its sides. Choir : every mouth screams and three of them climb out."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Specimen Zero","u":"entities/index.html#specimen-zero","t":"Mini-boss, 350 health, the Laboratory The Flesh's first host, the night technician who cut a sample from the root's end, grown for weeks against the Reactor Core: arms far too long, a second mouth in his chest with his ribs for teeth. Tendril Lash , Pool Surge and Absorb (it eats the staff's bodies to heal 25 each; burn them first). At half health it tears itself off the pool floor and hangs from the ceiling. Fire and Flower Ash Bombs burn it twice as hard."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Warden of Shelter No. 4","u":"entities/index.html#warden-entry","t":"Boss, 400 health, Bunker B The shelter's Civil Defence warden and everyone who sheltered with him, grown into one mass on four legs."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Infected Squad Leader","u":"entities/index.html#squad-leader","t":"Mini-boss, 120 health, Bunker B Its whistle sends the operators round your flanks; it fires five-round bursts and throws a flashbang every fifteen seconds. At half health it splits open and the Spine-Runner comes out (70 health): a skinless thing on all fours with a bladed tail."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Gardener, Reborn","u":"entities/index.html#reborn-entry","t":"Boss, 600 health, then Reborn Again What was left of the Gardener, grown back together by the Bloom."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Broodmother","u":"entities/index.html#broodmother","t":"Nest boss, 340 health The Flesh's own great flower: five petals of raw muscle round a womb, and what's left of a woman. She never moves, but gives birth (Crawlers, sometimes a Stalker), lets out Flesh Flies, slams a petal down and spits bile. At half health every sac in the nest bursts at once. She hates the flowers: the Bloomshears cut her half again as hard, and a Flower Ash Bomb burns her two and a half times as badly. Drops her heart, the Brood Heart."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Bellwether","u":"entities/index.html#bellwether","t":"Leads the horde, 70 health, armoured A Civil Defence warden in a long navy greatcoat, the gas mask grown into its face, four brass bells on a yoke of bone. It walks at the head of its horde ringing its handbell. Seeing you, it whirls its gas rattle and the horde charges. Kill it and the horde loses its way. Drops the Bellwether's Bell."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The infected","u":"entities/index.html#the-infected","t":""},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Infected","u":"entities/index.html#infected","t":"The town's people A shopper, an office worker, an old man in a cardigan, a road worker, a villager, in the clothes they died in. Villagers, zombies and witches the Flesh takes get up as these."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Infected Police","u":"entities/index.html#infected-police","t":"Still armed Fires its pistol at you, arm out, head cocked over. With TaCZ installed the police carry the Mended SMG."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Infected Soldier","u":"entities/index.html#infected-soldier","t":"Holding Rosemont Machete flurry up close; a screaming charge from further off. Becomes a Splitter."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Infected Firefighter","u":"entities/index.html#infected-firefighter","t":"Fire won't touch it Drags its axe and brings it down two-handed. Hit its air tank three times and it hisses, then goes up two seconds later."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Infected Paramedic","u":"entities/index.html#infected-paramedic","t":"Kill it first Every infected within six blocks of it heals. Up close it slams the defibrillator paddles on you."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Infected Pharmacist","u":"entities/index.html#infected-pharmacist","t":"Keeps its distance Throws syringes (poison and the Flesh) and bottles of pills (your stomach turns). Drops them too."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Infected Construction Worker","u":"entities/index.html#infected-construction-worker","t":"Nail gun and sledgehammer Fires four nails from a distance; close in, heaves the sledgehammer overhead."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Infected Officer","u":"entities/index.html#infected-officer","t":"Calls for backup Fights like the soldiers, and every thirty seconds holds its radio to its split ear and calls in two to four more."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Infected Heavy","u":"entities/index.html#infected-heavy","t":"Nothing knocks it back A soldier the Flesh grew huge, with a cleaver as long as a man: an overhead blow (10) or a sweep to both sides (6)."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Infected Researcher","u":"entities/index.html#infected-researcher","t":"The Laboratory Comes in fast with its syringe, then scuttles back out of reach on all fours. Sometimes carries a Level 2 Keycard or a later tape."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Infected Hazmat Trooper","u":"entities/index.html#infected-hazmat-trooper","t":"The Laboratory Its suit still on, fire won't touch it, and its flamer burns a cone in front of it."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Spitter","u":"entities/index.html#spitter","t":"Keeps its distance Its throat swollen into a sac of bile. The bile bursts into a puddle that burns, slows you and infects you."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Shelter Resident","u":"entities/index.html#shelter-resident","t":"Shelter No. 4 In pyjamas, a tracksuit, a blanket round them, hiding in bunks and lockers, sobbing. Get within three blocks, hit one or open its locker and it bursts out."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Civil Defence Warden","u":"entities/index.html#civil-defence-warden","t":"Shelter No. 4 White W helmet. Blows its whistle and every infected within 16 blocks comes running, faster."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Infected Operator","u":"entities/index.html#infected-operator","t":"Special forces, 40 health Flanks you, climbs walls, fires four-round bursts, throws flashbangs, slides in under you."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Infected Sniper","u":"entities/index.html#infected-sniper","t":"Special forces, 28 health Its laser finds you first with a climbing tone; a second and a half later, the shot (12). Break its line of sight."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Infected Breacher","u":"entities/index.html#infected-breacher","t":"Special forces, 45 health, armoured A riot shield grown onto its arm blocks everything from the front. Get round it, or hit it with an axe and the shield drops for five seconds."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Infected You","u":"entities/index.html#infected-you","t":"If you die of the Flesh What gets up where you fell is you, as one of the infected, with your skin, your armour, your weapon and everything you were carrying. It comes for you first. Kill it and you get it all back. It never despawns."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"What the infected become","u":"entities/index.html#mutants","t":"Left alive on the Flesh's ground for ten minutes (five on the thickest of it), one of the infected changes. What it becomes depends on what it was."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Stalker","u":"entities/index.html#stalker","t":"From townspeople Starved to skin and rib, on arms and legs twice as long and bent like a spider's. Climbs walls and drops on you; pounces from up to nine blocks. Drops a Stalker Talon."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Bloater","u":"entities/index.html#bloater","t":"From townspeople and workers Swollen wider than it is tall. Close enough, it swells and bursts, and a cloud of red gas hangs there for six seconds. Drops a Bloater Gland."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Screamer","u":"entities/index.html#screamer","t":"From police and CD wardens Its face opens four ways like a flower. Its call brings every infected within sixty-four blocks. Drops a Screamer Sac."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Brute","u":"entities/index.html#brute","t":"From firefighters and heavies, 140 health Three blocks of muscle. Smashes both fists into the ground and throws you ten blocks. Drops a Brute Knuckle."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Splitter","u":"entities/index.html#splitter","t":"From soldiers Split from throat to belt; its chest swings open like a mouth. Killed, it comes apart into three Crawlers (unless it burnt). Drops Splitter Sinew."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Hive","u":"entities/index.html#hive","t":"From paramedics Bent under a hump of lidded cells that let out Flesh Flies , a dozen at a time, each bite infecting you. Drops Hive Comb. Pharmacists and researchers become Spitters; the special forces' operators become Spine-Runners."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"After the Bloom changes","u":"entities/index.html#after-the-bloom-changes","t":""},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Changed Bloom","u":"entities/index.html#changed-bloom-entry","t":"Only the Omni ends it Ten times bigger, blue, and hungry."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Parasite and Parasite Host","u":"entities/index.html#parasite-entry","t":"From Blackwater Station Six legs and a mouth that opens like a flower. It goes for the back of the neck."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Omni","u":"entities/index.html#omni-entry","t":"The gun, and SENTINEL Listed here at the wiki owner's request; in the mod it's a weapon."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Chapter five: the static","u":"entities/index.html#chapter-five","t":""},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Static Hound","u":"entities/index.html#static-hound","t":"Packs, at night What the parasites made of the wolves. Packs of three to five behind a Pack Leader with a brood sac on its back. The leader howls and the pack gets faster and fiercer; the rest flank you. Kill the leader and the pack breaks."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Hollowed","u":"entities/index.html#the-hollowed","t":"One in every village A villager with violet pinprick eyes, muttering static. At night, alone with you, it turns: taller, arms to its knees, its head split open in four. It shrieks, rakes, grabs, and sometimes puts one in you."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Amalgam","u":"entities/index.html#amalgam-entry","t":"Boss, at Relay 6 Everyone who came to the relay, grown together into one heap at the mast's foot."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Afterimage","u":"entities/index.html#afterimage","t":"At the Starlite Drive-In Grey figures made of scan lines and static, see-through, their faces only dark gaps. They drift through cars and walls. You can't hurt one unless you're Tuned In, it's reaching for you, or the last reel is running. They can't leave the Null. Killed, one leaves a Frame of the Last Reel."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Carrier","u":"entities/index.html#carrier-entry","t":"Boss of part four What carried them all, in the crater in the middle of the Null Static Zone."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The outbreak","u":"entities/index.html#the-outbreak","t":"From 1.48.0, anything the parasite gets into is slowly taken over, and turns. After Signing Off it gets worse."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The turned","u":"entities/index.html#turned-entry","t":"Anything at all, two or three days on Ruined, writhing versions of what they were, a mouth of five petals split open in their chests, hunting everything that isn't theirs. Thirty-two of the Hollow's own have a turned form of their own, from the Saint Unmade to the Pod, Hatched."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The infested bosses","u":"entities/index.html#infested-bosses-entry","t":"Golems, the Warden, ravagers and more The game's bosses and mini-bosses, gone wrong, each with new moves and a bar of its own. Since 1.61.1 the Ender Dragon is always one of them."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The parasite's kinds","u":"entities/index.html#parasite-kinds-entry","t":"Born of where they were The Tide Parasite (in the water), the Burrowing Parasite (deep in the stone), the Winged Parasite (out of anything with wings), the Ember Parasite (the Nether) and the Void Parasite (the End)."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Biomass and the pure forms","u":"entities/index.html#biomass-entry","t":"What's left of the turned A heap of violet flesh where one of the turned fell, that gets up a minute or two later as a Stalker Form , a Ranged Form , a Tank Form or a Brood Sack . They change from one to another to suit the fight. Burn the heap and nothing gets up."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Hive and the Deep","u":"entities/index.html#the-hive-and-the-deep","t":""},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Chorus","u":"entities/index.html#chorus-entry","t":"Boss of part five, 900 health The mind the parasite grew for itself in the Hive's pit, out of everything it took: a mound of bodies, a great head with a split maw, and the faces of all of them speaking with one voice."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Hive Hand","u":"entities/index.html#hive-hand","t":"Seven round the Hive's pit, 140 health An arm as tall as a tree, braided chitin round a core of flesh, a palm with eyes and a mouth in it and three hooked fingers. It slams its claw down where the ground lights up, sweeps you aside, or grabs you, lifts you high, squeezes and throws you. More ."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Reach","u":"entities/index.html#the-reach","t":"Every few nights, at your home While the Chorus lives down in the Deep, one of its hands tears up out of the ground where you live, half again as big as the hive's, its things climbing out after it. Kill it, or it sinks back after four minutes. More ."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Listener","u":"entities/index.html#the-listener","t":"The Deep's older ones, 60 health Tall, starved, cave-white, on long dog's legs, with no eyes: only fans of skin either side of its head. It hears every step, every block, every door, and goes to the sound fast. Sneak. Its ears make Hushed Boots. More ."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Deaf King","u":"entities/index.html#deaf-king-entry","t":"Boss in the Deep, 420 health The oldest thing in the Deep, a hulk on its knuckles with plugs of stone in its ears. It feels you through the floor. Stand still and you aren't there."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Chorus, Whole","u":"entities/index.html#chorus-whole-entry","t":"Final boss of chapter five, 1024 health The Chorus made again in the Warm Heart, up out of a lake of blood. It dies, really this time, and leaves the Last Voice."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Chapter six: the Door at the End of the World","u":"entities/index.html#chapter-six","t":"Past the Door, the Stalls; behind the screen, the Watcher's Vault; and past the stage on the other side, what he kept out."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Audience","u":"entities/index.html#audience","t":"The Stalls' seats, 16 health Grey people in grey clothes, faces up to the screen, a ticket in their laps. They hear you, get up with a finger to their lips, and hold you where you are. Sneak. Some carry a Ticket Stub. More ."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Usher","u":"entities/index.html#usher","t":"Walks the aisles, 44 health Tall, faceless, in maroon and brass, swinging a lamp over the rows. If its light finds you, the SHHH goes through the house. Show it a Ticket Stub and it looks away. Often drops its lamp. More ."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Crowd","u":"entities/index.html#crowd-entry","t":"Boss of part one, 800 health The whole house gone into each other at the front, under the screen. Its Hush: stand still."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Tuned","u":"entities/index.html#the-tuned","t":"The Vault's stacks, 24 health People from the neck down, an old television set for a head. They only move while you're looking at them. More ."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Projectionist","u":"entities/index.html#projectionist-entry","t":"Boss of part two, 900 health A coat of film and a cinema projector for a head. It came into the Vault behind you, for what he kept."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Rerun","u":"entities/index.html#rerun","t":"The Projectionist's An old boss projected onto the air, grey and flickering, doing again the one thing everyone remembers: the Saint's beam, the Gardener's thorns, the Deaf King's fists, the Carrier's beam."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Viewer","u":"entities/index.html#viewer-entry","t":"The last boss, can't be killed What he kept out: sat in the dark past the stage, so big you only ever fight its eye and its hands."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Stand-In","u":"entities/index.html#stand-in","t":"The Other Side, 10 health A painted plywood cut-out of a person that hops out of the wings. It doesn't hurt you; it points, and the eye comes. More ."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Chapter seven: the First Signal","u":"entities/index.html#chapter-seven","t":""},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The First Signal","u":"entities/index.html#first-signal-entry","t":"Chapter Ten's enemy Your shape, your size, its skin crawling static, a white mask. It was here before the Watcher, before the first picture. It came through a rift into his Hub and said one word. In Chapter Ten it lets out its creations, and you fight it."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Chapter eight: the Dead Water","u":"entities/index.html#chapter-eight","t":"Everything in the Dead Water's twelve waters swims like something that lives in water: speeding up and slowing, banking into turns, schooling, keeping to its depth, bolting when startled. Small things are eaten by bigger things. Since 1.63.2 they get hungry and go looking for food, a wound in the water draws the hunters, a school balls up tight when a hunter's near, and a still diver draws the curious ones in to circle and look. Out of the water they flop, gasp and die. Where each one lives is from the mod's own lists of each water."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The gentle ones","u":"entities/index.html#the-gentle-ones","t":""},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Pipeye","u":"entities/index.html#pipeye","t":"3 health A thumb-sized ball of a man's eye in a cup of flesh, lidded with shells that swing down over it. Little schools come and look at you, all the eyes turning together, and dart off if you move at them. The Grey Shelf, the Haemal Reach, the Wireweed, the Ossuary Flats, the Drowned Mycelia, the Carrier Wave."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Lanternlet","u":"entities/index.html#lanternlet","t":"2 health A deep, thin lanternfish, big-eyed, two rows of lights down each flank. Big glowing shoals that ball up tight and turn when something hunts near. The Grey Shelf, the Wireweed, the Lantern Fields, the Molar Reef, the Carrier Wave."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Hum Skate","u":"entities/index.html#hum-skate","t":"8 health A little spotted ray near the floor, in pairs, its smiling face underneath and a barbed whip of a tail. It hums one low note. The Grey Shelf, the Wireweed, the Ossuary Flats, the Ember Vents, the Carrier Wave."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Puffbloat","u":"entities/index.html#puffbloat","t":"6 health Round, blotched, green-eyed. Frighten it and it swells into a ball of spines; touch it then and they go in. The Haemal Reach, the Brine Sink, the Molar Reef."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Thimble Jelly","u":"entities/index.html#thimble-jelly","t":"2 health A domed bell lit from inside, its canals and pink horseshoes glowing, frilled arms under it. It drifts in blooms, pulsing. Brush its threads and it stings. The Lantern Fields, the Brine Sink, the Drowned Mycelia."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Stiltfin","u":"entities/index.html#stiltfin","t":"6 health Stands on three long fin-rays on the deep floors, facing the current, long feelers sweeping up over its head. Swims off when you come. The Grey Shelf, the Ossuary Flats, the Rime Shelf, the Ember Vents."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Grinner","u":"entities/index.html#grinner","t":"5 health A pretty banded reef fish with human eyes, full lips over a grin of human teeth, and a tall spined sail. Little groups; it chatters and giggles. The Haemal Reach, the Wireweed, the Molar Reef."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Hymnback","u":"entities/index.html#hymnback","t":"220 health A gentle giant: a whale's long head, a hanging lower jaw, fringes of baleen, long knobbed flippers, and a reef of corals, lit anemones and kelp on its back. Its song carries a long way. The Grey Shelf, the Lantern Fields, the Rime Shelf; lost ones wander into the Black Below, where the Undertow eats them."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The hunters","u":"entities/index.html#the-hunters","t":""},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Clotfish","u":"entities/index.html#clotfish","t":"6 health Shoals of little blood-dark fish with a fence of crooked needles in their underbite. Quiet until there's blood in the water; then the whole shoal boils at it in a frenzy, biting in turns, and you bleed. The Haemal Reach, the Brine Sink, the Molar Reef."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Choir Eel","u":"entities/index.html#choir-eel","t":"30 health Lies along the floor humming chords out of the mouths down its flanks. Touch it, linger on it or hit it and it coils, lights up and sings a shock through the water round it. The shock kills lights. The Wireweed, the Ember Vents, the Carrier Wave."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Hookjaw","u":"entities/index.html#hookjaw","t":"34 health A gaff of a jaw-hook, hooked bones raked down its head, a torn tail. It follows you at the edge of sight, circling and clicking, comes in fast the moment you look away, hooks you and is gone. It steals your metal and keeps it until it's killed. The Grey Shelf, the Wireweed, the Ossuary Flats, the Molar Reef."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Gulper","u":"entities/index.html#gulper","t":"60 health A warty head that's all mouth, a comb of needles round it, lying still on the floor with a light on a stalk over its jaws. Whatever comes close enough it lunges at and swallows (little fish whole). The sea's light-lovers come to its light. The Lantern Fields, the Ossuary Flats, the Drowned Mycelia."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Mantlecrab","u":"entities/index.html#mantlecrab","t":"40 health Jointed spined legs, big claws, a spiked rim to its shell. It hates light: a lamp, a lit submarine, a torch in your hand. Its pulse puts out every light near it (darkness on you, the submarine's power gone), then it comes in with its claws. The Ember Vents, the Carrier Wave."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Frostjaw","u":"entities/index.html#frostjaw","t":"24 health A shark's tail, five gill slits, glass teeth, frost-crazed. Packs on the cold shelf spread out round you, their flank-lights flashing to each other, and come in one at a time from wherever you aren't looking. The Rime Shelf."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Siphon","u":"entities/index.html#siphon","t":"8 health A leech of an eel, a ringed body and a toothed sucker. It fastens on and drinks until you hit it off or get out of the water. The Grey Shelf, the Haemal Reach, the Brine Sink, the Drowned Mycelia."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"A fish for each water","u":"entities/index.html#the-twelve-fish","t":"Since 1.63.11 each of the twelve waters has a fish of its own. Each swims, schools, feeds, flees or hunts the way the sea's things do, has its own sounds and its own death, and the sea's hunters eat them."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Staticfin","u":"entities/index.html#staticfin","t":"2 health Herring of a dead channel's snow, test-card bars behind their gills, eyes like two switched-off screens. Look straight at a school and it skips like a bad signal. Dying, it breaks up into static. The Grey Shelf."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Wickling","u":"entities/index.html#wickling","t":"2 health A stub of old wax with a little flame burning on its wick under the water. The sea's light-lovers gather to it (and wicklings to each other); startle one and it snuffs itself out, and lights again later. Dying, it sags like a candle burnt down. The Lantern Fields."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Gumnibbler","u":"entities/index.html#gumnibbler","t":"4 health A round mouth of gums and a baby's milk teeth. Hang still in the water (or creep) and a few come and nibble at you; move and they scatter. Dying, it spits its teeth. The Molar Reef."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Bloodlet","u":"entities/index.html#bloodlet","t":"4 health It smells the hurt and the bleeding a long way off; it bites, drinks and swells until it can hardly swim. It bursts when it dies, and the blood in the water brings the hunters. The Haemal Reach."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Sporegill","u":"entities/index.html#sporegill","t":"6 health A mushroom's gills for gill covers, caps growing on its back. Startle it or hit it and it puffs a cloud of spores (sick and slow). Dying, it shrivels as its caps grow up out of it. The Drowned Mycelia."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Rime Smelt","u":"entities/index.html#rime-smelt","t":"2 health A fish of clear ice, its bones and a little red heart showing through it. Come slowly and a school goes still as ice; come too close and it bursts away. Dying, it freezes stiff and shatters. The Rime Shelf."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Wirewhip","u":"entities/index.html#wirewhip","t":"8 health An eel of old cable with a plug for a head. It lies still in the weed and whips out with a shock that numbs you. Dying, it fits and sparks, then lies coiled. The Wireweed."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Brinecrust","u":"entities/index.html#brinecrust","t":"10 health A salt-crusted flatfish lying buried in the floor. Step on it and it bursts up in a cloud of brine that stings and blinds. Dying, it crumbles to salt. The Brine Sink."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Cinderling","u":"entities/index.html#cinderling","t":"4 health A live coal of a fish, its cracks glowing: touch one and it burns. Dying, its glow goes out and it falls to ash. The Ember Vents."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Dialfin","u":"entities/index.html#dialfin","t":"6 health Old brown bakelite, a lit radio dial on each flank, an aerial for a back fin. Its needle hunts the stations; now and then a school tunes in to you and something speaks to you through it. Dying, it signs off. The Carrier Wave."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Marrowpike","u":"entities/index.html#marrowpike","t":"22 health A long pallid pike whose back half is bare bone. It lies among the bones of the flats as if it's one of them, until you're close. Dying, it comes apart. The Ossuary Flats."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Omenfry","u":"entities/index.html#omenfry","t":"1 health Black specks with human eyes, lit, in clouds. They trail you at the edge of your light, close in and ring you and stare, then blink out and pull back. Kill one and the rest turn to look at you. The Black Below."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"What else lives in the waters","u":"entities/index.html#in-the-waters","t":"Two new creatures in nine of the waters (all but the Haemal Reach, the Ember Vents and the Black Below), from 1.63.12 to 1.63.17, with what's made from them on items ."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Spore Drifter","u":"entities/index.html#spore-drifter","t":"6 health A mushroom's cap gone loose in the water. It drifts in shoals, beating like a jellyfish, its beaded threads trailing, the tips lit. Brush against one and it puffs its spores into you (the dark, and sick). In sporefall they rise up out of the caps. Drops Drifter Jelly. The Drowned Mycelia."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Gillmaw","u":"entities/index.html#gillmaw","t":"30 health One more mushroom on the floor, its gills glowing, and the sea's light-lovers come to the glow. Swim over it and its cap splits down the middle and swings open, teeth where the gills were. Little fish it swallows whole; you, it holds in its cap and chews, until you hit it loose or it spits you out. They wait in nests of bones under the floor. Drops its teeth (the Gillmaw-Tooth Spear). The Drowned Mycelia."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Grove Heart","u":"entities/index.html#grove-heart","t":"Under the Drowned Grove, can't be fought Down through the Grove's great hollow mushroom and twenty blocks under the floor: a mass of fungal flesh the size of a room, breathing, its veins lit, the strings the Sporeborn hang on running up out of it into the dark. It knows you're there and talks to you (\"...not yet. ...you're not ready for us yet, (your name)...\"). Hit it and \"It doesn't feel that. The Grove does.\": spores in your face, the rooted dead getting up, the hung ones coming down for you. The Undertow eats it ."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Slimehag","u":"entities/index.html#slimehag","t":"8 health A hagfish, pale and blind, a bristled round mouth, in tangles where things are dead. Hit one and it slimes: a cloud thick as glue round it (you can hardly move; whatever was hunting in it chokes and lets go), and it ties itself in a knot and slips away. The Brine Sink."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Waver","u":"entities/index.html#waver","t":"6 health A yeti crab, white as a corpse, its claws and legs furred with hair, in colonies. When you come, every one of them stops, turns to face you and waves, slowly, all together, in step. Stay among them too long, or hurt one, and the whole colony comes at you. Their hairs sting. The Brine Sink."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Rime Strider","u":"entities/index.html#rime-strider","t":"26 health A sea spider: a body you could hold in your hand, legs three times that, knees up high. It wades the floor slowly, and if it reaches you it folds its legs round you and drinks you through its proboscis until you break loose (hit it hard). The Rime Shelf."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Rimeback","u":"entities/index.html#rimeback","t":"32 health A seal of the ice with a reptile's long head and a grin that runs back past its eyes. Its calls are long electric trills, falling. It comes in fast, takes hold and drags you down and away, shaking you, costing you breath (hit it hard to break free). Drops blubber. The Rime Shelf."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Lantern Moth","u":"entities/index.html#lantern-moth","t":"4 health A moth of the deep, its wings dusted with light, eyespots on them glowing. They go about in clouds and come to any light: the lanterns, the lure stalks, you with a torch in your hand (and then they won't leave you). Hit one and it bursts in a cloud of its dust, and you can't see. The Lantern Fields."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Lampmother","u":"entities/index.html#lampmother","t":"40 health What they grow into, if they live: a moth the size of a boat, and rare. She comes to light too, and to whoever's carrying it. Close, she opens her wings over you and their eyes hold you (you can't look away, you can hardly move) until she bites. Hit her hard enough and she breaks off. In a blackout, she's what comes looking. The Lantern Fields."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Wirecutter","u":"entities/index.html#wirecutter","t":"20 health Something like a lobster stripped down to its wiring: a long body of black cable, thin legs, two long pairs of pliers for claws, a tail ending in two copper prongs. It waits in the cable trees' roots; it pinches, and its tail comes up over its back and arcs into you. The Wireweed."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Coilback","u":"entities/index.html#coilback","t":"10 health A fat louse of the floor plated in copper coils, grazing the copper moss; harmless. Corner it and it rolls up into a ball of coil, and your blows hardly touch it. The Wireweed."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Sleeper","u":"entities/index.html#sleeper","t":"60 health A shark as long as a boat and as slow as a drowned man, scarred all over, its eyes white and blind with a worm trailing from each. It doesn't see you. It smells you, when you're hurt, when you're bleeding, and then it comes, slowly, and doesn't stop. When it bites it holds on and shakes (hit it hard). It comes to the Fall. Raw, its meat poisons you. The Ossuary Flats."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Skullkeep","u":"entities/index.html#skullkeep","t":"6 health A crab living in a human skull; colonies of them pick over the whale falls. Come near and every one of them pulls in at once, and the skulls all turn to face you. Drops its skull. The Ossuary Flats."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Handset","u":"entities/index.html#handset","t":"22 health An anglerfish, black and soft, a mouth of needles, and for a lure, on a coiled cord, an old telephone handset, its earpiece lit. It lies still on the floor. It rings. Swim down to see what's ringing and you're in front of its jaws. The Carrier Wave."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Echo Jelly","u":"entities/index.html#echo-jelly","t":"8 health A jelly with a reel of tape turning inside its bell. It plays back what it's heard near it (you, hurt; you swimming; the broadcast; voices), slow and wrong, from somewhere off in the murk. Its sting fills your head with static. The Carrier Wave."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Tooth Fairy","u":"entities/index.html#tooth-fairy","t":"10 health Small and white, with wings that beat like a heart: two strokes and a rest. It waits for you to keep still. Then it comes close, and when it goes, something's gone off your hotbar and there's a gold nugget where it was. Kill it and you get back what it took. Wear a Tooth Charm and it leaves you be. The Molar Reef."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Gnasher","u":"entities/index.html#gnasher","t":"24 health A fish that's all gums and teeth. When it gets hold of you it grinds: every piece of armour you have on wears down at once, fast. Hit it hard to make it let go. The Molar Reef."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Catch","u":"entities/index.html#the-catch","t":"34 health A ball of ghost net rolling over the floor with the drowned rolled up inside it, their arms out through the mesh, groping. It wraps you up and holds you, and your air goes out of you fast. Hit it hard to tear free. When it dies its net stays where it fell. Drops crew tags. The Grey Shelf, out past the rig."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Buoyling","u":"entities/index.html#buoyling","t":"4 health A little crab living under an orange net float. Startle a crowd of them and they all pop up off the floor at once. The Grey Shelf."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Diving Bell","u":"entities/index.html#diving-bell","t":"Now and then A ship's horn somewhere up above, and a chain running out. An old diving bell comes down out of the murk and settles on the floor near you, and its hatch swings open. Its supplies are set out beside it in a chest, and sometimes the diver's still down there with it. After a while it's hauled back up. The Grey Shelf."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The people down there","u":"entities/index.html#the-people-down-there","t":""},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Deep Hands","u":"entities/index.html#deep-hands","t":"The places' crews, 30 health The people who still live and work down there (since 1.63.7), in the old diving dress: the round copper helmet with a face behind its lit glass, the brass corselet, lead on their boots, air tanks and a hose, a lamp on the helmet and one on the belt, a big spanner. Each working place has its own crew in its own colours: the Ember Crew at the Ember Pumping Station, Lantern Station's Keepers, Sink Station's Researchers, the Signal Keepers at the Wireweed Mast, the Salvagers in the Wreck Field and the Castaways in the Lifeboat Graveyard. They walk from job to job, wave when you first come near, and never go for you (except the Salvagers: hit one and the lot of them come for you with their spanners). Right-click one and it talks to you; each crew has eight things to say. Hurt one and it backs off, and so does its crew. The Ember Crew trade (crouch to just talk)."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Rime Crew","u":"entities/index.html#rime-crew","t":"The Rime Outpost's divers, 40 health In frosted helmets, with harpoon guns (since 1.63.11). They hunt the sea's hunters near their camp (frostjaws and the like): finding a clear line, keeping their distance, firing, reeling in, reloading, clubbing anything that gets close. They turn them on you if you turn on them. They drop harpoon bolts, and now and then a gun."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Drowned","u":"entities/index.html#the-drowned","t":"The Drowned Heart, 34 health The crew that went down to see what the heart was, and stayed: their dress split, the Flesh coming out through it, their glass cracked and full of red, two lights in it. Five walk the Heart's floor and one waits inside it, with siphons over it. They come for you, and their blows put the Flesh in you (and Enzyme 1-2418, since 1.63.9)."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Sporeborn","u":"entities/index.html#the-sporeborn","t":"The Drowned Grove, 34 health The same, taken by the Grove's spores, with a gulper in the canopy. Since 1.63.11 some hang under the caps on strings : swim under one and it drops on you and comes for you, jerked along on its strings, and the Grove talks to you through them (\"Shh. Listen. We grow in the quiet.\"). Cut one down and its strings snap back up into the dark, and another tells you what it thinks of that (\"We have more strings than you have hands.\"). Out on the floor the rooted dead lie grown over; come close and the strings come down and haul one up."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Stretched","u":"entities/index.html#stretched","t":"The Haemal Research Station, 40 health The lab's divers, as Enzyme 1-2418 left them: their dress split down every seam, arms down past their knees, legs jointed twice, the helmet split off the long head that pushed up out of it. They lie like the dead until you come near (or hit one), then unfold, and the others near it come up after. Look straight at one from far off and it stops dead, only its head moving; look away and it comes, fast. Their reach is long, they throw themselves at you from a few blocks off, and their claws put the Enzyme in you. They won't come into a UV Lamp's light, and its flash scorches them and drives them off. Since 1.64.1 none of the mod's creatures drown, dry out, freeze, starve, go thirsty, burn on hot floors or get crushed by the deep, and only the Undertow gets hungry: the sea's hunters prowl now and then instead, and the grazers pick at the floor."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The eldritch","u":"entities/index.html#the-eldritch","t":""},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Mouth of the Floor","u":"entities/index.html#mouth-of-the-floor-entry","t":"Buried in the floor, 140 health Nothing showing but a ring of rocks. Pass over it and eight jaws open out of the sand round a throat, and the water rushes in, and you with it."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Static Leviathan","u":"entities/index.html#static-leviathan","t":"Boss, 320 health Deep down in the Dead Water, now and then one comes up out of the dark after you. It sings on the Remote's frequency, and its Signal Organ mends the Remote. More ."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Undertow","u":"entities/index.html#undertow-entry","t":"The Black Below; nothing hurts it Three thousand blocks long, its lights glowing in the dark. The void past the edge is its own: it stalks you where you can see it, learns you, and eats when it's hungry. The only way to live is to get back over the edge. In Chapter Nine it becomes the Harbinger ."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Chapter nine: the Harbinger","u":"entities/index.html#chapter-nine","t":""},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Harbinger","u":"entities/index.html#harbinger-entry","t":"Never fought The Undertow, after it ate the Grove Heart and the Drowned Heart and turned. It lay by the rig three days; then its bones came out of it, hung on the Grove's strings, brought up a static heart at your feet, and tore its way out of the Dead Water."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Chapter ten: Stay Tuned","u":"entities/index.html#chapter-ten","t":"What the First Signal let out of his kingdom into your world, his congregation at home, what came down in THE LAST BROADCAST, and the secret of Tune-In Town."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"His creations and servants","u":"entities/index.html#his-creations-and-servants","t":"They see you and hear you, hunt together, and come every night in a different programme. How to hide from them, and all their attacks, are in his creations and servants ."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The First Signal, Crowned","u":"entities/index.html#first-signal-crowned","t":"Chapter Ten's enemy, 800 health; on its wings, 320 Armoured in his Faithful, crowned with their daggers, his blade drawn out of the Harbinger. Fought in his arena, then in the End, then in the air on the End's guardian's wings."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Longplay","u":"entities/index.html#longplay","t":"His creation, 60 health A person drawn out like a chewed-up tape, eleven feet tall. Watch it and it pauses, juddering; look away and it fast-forwards, nearer every time."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Hanger","u":"entities/index.html#hanger","t":"His creation, 26 health Folded the wrong way, its head hung under its body. Up walls and over roofs; it hangs over a way through and drops on whoever passes under."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Lookalike","u":"entities/index.html#lookalike","t":"His creation, 34 health, by day too A villager, a cow, a pig, a sheep, a chicken, the Watcher: a frame behind itself, its sounds backwards. Close, it opens down the middle."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"ERR","u":"entities/index.html#err","t":"His creation, 50 health, rare The broken script, its name a row of boxes. It skips, comes up behind you, puts errors in your chat, and can only be hurt in the frames it's all there."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Announcer","u":"entities/index.html#announcer","t":"His servant, a boss, 180 health A speaker grille for a face; its voice knocks you down, and it calls everything of his in: \"STAY TUNED.\" Keeps his transmitter."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Cameraman","u":"entities/index.html#cameraman","t":"His servant, a boss, 150 health A studio camera for a head. While it films you, everything of his knows where you are. Keeps his burrow."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Stagehand","u":"entities/index.html#stagehand","t":"His servant, a boss, 220 health A sack over its head, a rigging hook for a hand. It hooks you in, charges, and brings its fist down. Keeps his set."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Faithful","u":"entities/index.html#faithful","t":"His congregation, 30 health Hooded robes of red so dark it's nearly black, nothing under the hood. At their rites in his castle; hurt one and they all come, screaming."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"In the Last Broadcast","u":"entities/index.html#in-the-last-broadcast","t":""},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"SENTINEL Crew","u":"entities/index.html#sentinel-crew","t":"Only in a cutscene, 20 health The astronauts in the module of SENTINEL that came down in his sea, taken by the parasites they brought with them. The last of them carries the Chorus's last voice."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The End's Guardian, Taken","u":"entities/index.html#ends-guardian","t":"300 health, can't be brought down The Ender Dragon, the hive's now, circling his arena in the End. Only he can bring it down, and he does."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Tune-In Town's cast","u":"entities/index.html#tune-in-towns-cast","t":"A secret: the animatronics of Tune-In Town Pizza & Playhouse, in Studio B. Their tricks after hours and on the night shift, their kills and their voices are on Tune-In Town's cast ."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Tony Tune","u":"entities/index.html#tony-tune","t":"The bandleader, 130 health A tabby tomcat in a top hat. His Spotlight calls them all to you; on the clock he moves only while nobody's watching."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Bucky Beaver","u":"entities/index.html#bucky-beaver","t":"Bass, 120 health Gnaws through wood, and at the west door, your power going."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Lulu Lark","u":"entities/index.html#lulu-lark","t":"Keys, 85 health Leaps, shrieks, and calls you from behind in a child's voice."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Tempo the Tortoise","u":"entities/index.html#tempo-the-tortoise","t":"Drums, 150 health His drum roll shakes the floor; on the clock, a step every beat."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Rusty Rover","u":"entities/index.html#rusty-rover","t":"OUT OF ORDER, 95 health The fastest of them. Watch him on camera 3, or he runs for the west door."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Mister Channel","u":"entities/index.html#mister-channel","t":"The host, 95 health A television for a head. Into the static and out of it behind you; then his face is on your TV."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Jack Jangle","u":"entities/index.html#jack-jangle","t":"The jester in the box, 85 health Keep the music box wound, or he's out. POP."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Spare Parts","u":"entities/index.html#spare-parts","t":"A bare endoskeleton, 65 health Fast in the dark, through the vent. Light drives it back."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Chef Pete","u":"entities/index.html#chef-pete","t":"The kitchen's walrus, 160 health Throws pizza pans; shut the door on him and he jams it open."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Employee of the Month","u":"entities/index.html#employee-of-the-month","t":"The spare suit, 110 health Someone still in it. Never on the cameras: listen for him. \"Hello?\""},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Tix","u":"entities/index.html#tix","t":"The raccoon, 55 health Snatches what's in your hand, or your power and your monitor."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Encore","u":"entities/index.html#the-encore","t":"A boss, 360 health All of them stitched together with his static. The sixth night's."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Mended Band","u":"entities/index.html#the-mended-band","t":"After hours, 360 health The band on the stage, gone into each other. The Security Card doesn't fool it."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Golden Tony","u":"entities/index.html#golden-tony","t":"Yours, for three gold stars A little gold Tony Tune who follows you everywhere and points his cane at trouble. Nothing hurts him."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The deep oceans","u":"entities/index.html#the-deep-oceans","t":"Since 1.62.0 the Overworld's oceans fall away past the shelf to about 2,000 blocks deep, in three depths: the Sunless Drop, the Hadal Dark and the Trench (see the Hollow's own country ). Three things live down there. Two of them, the Needlemaw and the Static Leviathan, turn up in the Dead Water too."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Shroud Ray","u":"entities/index.html#shroud-ray","t":"The Sunless Drop and the Hadal Dark, 40 health A ray as wide as a cart is long, pale as a burial sheet, the face its gills and mouth make on its underside, a fringe of pale blue lights round its wings. It glides on slow beats and lets you be, until you hurt it. Then it comes in fast and low and comes down over you like a sheet: its wings fold round you, everything goes dark, and it beats down and down, taking you with it, the cold biting. Hit it hard enough and it lets go. Drops Shroud Hide."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Needlemaw","u":"entities/index.html#needlemaw","t":"All three depths, 18 health A fish the length of a man's arm and leg, nearly all head: a jaw lined with glass needles too long to close over, six pin-eyes on its brow. It hangs dark and still. When you come near, all its lights come on at once: it backs off with its jaw dropping open, darts in, bites (you bleed), recoils and comes round again. In the Dead Water it's in the Grey Shelf and the Ember Vents too. Drops 1 to 3 Needle Teeth."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Static Leviathan","u":"entities/index.html#static-leviathan-deep","t":"The Hadal Dark and the Trench Its home water. See its case file ."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Minecraft's own creatures","u":"entities/index.html#minecrafts-own-creatures","t":"Every vanilla animal and monster is redrawn as a jointed 3D model with its own animations, bleeding (or sparking, or shedding goo, splinters, ash or spores) when hit and dying its own way. By night, if you look at one, it stops what it's doing and looks back at you, its eyes shining. A few highlights: The Enderman is one of the Hollow's own: far too tall and thin, a too-wide grin of needle teeth. Look at it and it freezes, cocks its head and trembles; anger it and its jaw unhinges into a scream. It whispers backwards. The Warden claws its way out of the ground, and its real heart beats half out of its chest, faster as it gets angrier. The creeper swells and flickers before it bursts; charged ones crackle with static. Spiders walk on eight legs and rear up at you. Slimes are see-through jelly with things floating in them. The Ender Dragon has torn wings with real finger bones and a ridge of bone plates down its back. Since 1.61.1 it's always the Infested Ender Dragon ."},{"p":"The Amalgam","h":"","u":"entities/the-amalgam.html","t":"Relay 6, Hollow Ridge, at the mast's foot Boss Who it was D. Ostrander, the relay's operator; Gus, his dog; and nine people from the valley Health 300 Held by Three tethers on the mast's platforms at 12, 22 and 32 Added in 1.45.0, Chapter Five part two Drops The Relay Core. Its brood sac bursts when it dies, unless it burnt."},{"p":"The Amalgam","h":"Description","u":"entities/the-amalgam.html#description","t":"Everyone who came to the relay, the operator, his dog, and the people from the valley who walked up the hill after dark to stand round the mast, grown together into one heap at its foot. Six limbs that don't match. Three heads on long necks: his, in his hard hat and headset; a villager's, split open in four; and the dog's, its muzzle peeled back. A brood sac on its back with three cables of sinew running up the mast to the tethers."},{"p":"The Amalgam","h":"Relay 6 - Operator's Log","u":"entities/the-amalgam.html#relay-6-operators-log","t":"D. Ostrander, Hollow Ridge Found: the transmitter hut Fri. People from the valley came up the road after dark. Nine of them. They didn't knock. They stood round the mast with their faces up, like they were listening to it. They didn't blink at the floodlight. Sun. They've started climbing it. Tying something to it. It isn't rope. If you find this and it's still on the air - it isn't us. Cut it loose. All of it. Excerpt. The whole log is on the lore page."},{"p":"The Amalgam","h":"How it fights","u":"entities/the-amalgam.html#how-it-fights","t":"Slam: it rears up and comes down. Stand back. Grab: a head lashes out and drags you in, and the other two chew. Hit it hard to make it let go. Scream: three voices at once and the static under them. You can't see for a while, and every hound near comes. Brood: it spits brood out of its sac. Draw: it draws on the relay through its cables. They pull taut and pulse, and it heals. Hurt it hard while it does and it breaks off. While a tether holds, it can't go further from the mast than its cables reach. Get out of their reach and it lets you go. At half health the dog tears itself out of its side, and the rest of it comes on faster."},{"p":"The Amalgam","h":"Cut the tethers","u":"entities/the-amalgam.html#cut-the-tethers","t":"Climb the ladder up the mast's south face and break the knot of sinew on each rest platform. Each one cut, it flinches. Cut the last one and it reels (\"The last cable snaps. It reels - cut off from the relay.\"), and from then on every blow hurts it more. Cutting the last tether while it still lives earns Cut the Cord ."},{"p":"The Amalgam","h":"How to survive it","u":"entities/the-amalgam.html#how-to-survive-it","t":"Cut the tethers first. Its draw heals it as long as it's connected. Stay out of its cables' reach when you need a breather. Bring something for the hound packs. While the relay's on the air they come twice as often within 700 blocks, and its scream calls them. Bring a Surgical Kit. The operator's locker has one, and its brood can put one in you."},{"p":"The Amalgam","h":"Off the air","u":"entities/the-amalgam.html#off-the-air","t":"Killed, its sac bursts and the relay goes off the air (\"The relay goes quiet. For the first time in days, there's nothing on the air.\"). The tethers wither, the hounds near it lose the signal and run, and from then on packs come less often everywhere. This earns Off the Air . It leaves the Relay Core . Keep it. It tunes the projector at the Starlite Drive-In, and it's how you hurt Afterimages."},{"p":"The Bloom","h":"","u":"entities/the-bloom.html","t":"The great flower, all the way down Colossal Forms The Great Flower (under the dome), the Great Bloom (in its realm and risen), the changed Bloom First seen Chapter three Reach About 26 blocks risen; 90 once changed, and growing Ends Only the Omni (since 1.43.0) Made The Flesh, from the rot its carrion flies carry The Great Bloom Its tentacles over the Flesh, the reactor parts tracker at 1 of 3."},{"p":"The Bloom","h":"The great flower","u":"entities/the-bloom.html#the-great-flower","t":"It opened one night under the glasshouse dome. Nobody planted it. Head Gardener E. Thorne wrote that it was warm, with a beat in its stalk like a sleeper's. He told the Rosemont Courier it was a Rafflesia, \"though not one I know\". It's the size of a room, its tendrils feeling about, and anything they drag in is lifted, wrapped and swallowed. Get close and it latches on and you're Sapromyiophilous : carrion flies swarm you, you rot and hunger, and it feeds. Only the Gardener's Weeds keep the flies off: \"the great flower knows these clothes\". The bud was only a finger. Dr. Marsh's research log: \"Its root goes down through the rotunda's floor and keeps going. We let down a line four hundred feet. It kept going.\""},{"p":"The Bloom","h":"The Great Bloom","u":"entities/the-bloom.html#the-great-bloom","t":"Far down under the islands of the Bloom is the real great flower. Five great warted petals, red going black with the rot coming up green through them, and where the bud had its heart, a mouth: a lip of flesh and a throat ringed with rings of hooked teeth that turn against each other as it chews, a sick light far down in it. Its mouth is wider than all the islands together (since 1.27.2 it's ten times the size it was, every way), and its petals reach out further than you can see. Round the mouth rise eight tentacles , each as wide as a hill at the root, curling over far above you. Fall and one comes straight up out of its throat after you. It is horrible to be near. Out in its realm the edges of your sight go green-black and veined, the veins pulsing with its heart; something whispers just behind you, wherever you turn; now and then, for a blink, you see its mouth. Its throat has faces in it, pressed out through the flesh, mouths open. It drools. It chews. It calls, something vast with more voices in it than there should be, and now and then it speaks."},{"p":"The Bloom","h":"The risen Bloom","u":"entities/the-bloom.html#the-risen-bloom","t":"Break the Binding and it comes up the root, through the glasshouse, and takes the gardens' place for good. This one is the size the first was, not the colossal one below. Its tentacles reach for anything that comes within about 26 blocks (players first), and its flies infect anyone near it without the Gardener's clothes. It clears everything under the reach of its petals and turns the ground under them to its flesh. Its mouth is open: a pit down its throat lined with its flesh, and at the bottom a pool of yellow-green acid, scummed over, beating with its heart. Ten seconds after it rises, the Flesh wakes."},{"p":"The Bloom","h":"Swallowed alive","u":"entities/the-bloom.html#the-stomach","t":"Since 1.38, people it eats don't die in its teeth. They go down its throat alive and land in its stomach : a chamber of wet red folds lit from inside, with a knee-deep pool of green acid that eats at you and your armour. Round the pool lie what's left of the ones it ate before you; dig through each pile once for their things. The throat overhead is shut, and nothing opens it. Swallowed alive. The way out: hack at its stomach wall. It heals over at once, but it feels every cut and heaves. Cut it ten times (the bar at the bottom of your screen) and it retches you, and anyone in there with you, back up onto the ground well away from it. Stay down there and it digests you (\"was digested alive\"). you're alive. you're in it. it's digesting you. cut at the walls. hurt it enough and it'll throw you back up. ??? in the stomach"},{"p":"The Bloom","h":"The changed Bloom","u":"entities/the-bloom.html#the-changed-bloom","t":"The Rosemont Device going off inside it was never going to kill it. The Watcher needed it to change. The changed Bloom is ten times bigger. Its flesh has gone blue, its acid purple, its teeth green, and it sits in a pit it tears out of the ground, its petals standing up off the ground like a flower's, their tips seventy-odd blocks up. It reaches for anything within ninety blocks. Its roar goes all the way round the world, heard from anywhere, late and echoing the further off you are. Near it, its violet light creeps in at the edges of your sight."},{"p":"The Bloom","h":"The blight","u":"entities/the-bloom.html#the-blight","t":"Over three days its blight grows out from it, up to two thousand blocks every way: blue flesh where the grass was, blisters of its acid (they burst, burning and poisoning), its green teeth up out of the ground (they cut whatever pushes through), blue tissue where the leaves were, a violet haze off all of it, the ground breathing."},{"p":"The Bloom","h":"It is hungry","u":"entities/the-bloom.html#it-is-hungry","t":"Since 1.42 everything it gets down its throat makes it bigger: an animal a little, a villager more, one of you a lot, up to three times the size it changed to, its mouth three hundred blocks across and its petals out past six hundred, filling the sky. Fed, it chews, its heart slow. Hungry, it reaches twice as often and comes up out of the ground under anyone out on its petals. Starving (six minutes without), all of that faster, its mouth hanging open, drool pouring off its lip. Close to its mouth you can hear the ones it ate, still in there, muffled, pleading. it's growing. everything it eats, it gets bigger. twice the size it was. don't let it eat. stay off its petals. it's filling the sky. use the gun while there's still something to aim at. that's as big as it gets. it's still hungry. ??? as it grows"},{"p":"The Bloom","h":"How it dies","u":"entities/the-bloom.html#how-it-dies","t":"Only the Orbital Railgun's strikes can hurt it, and since 1.43.0 it heals as fast as you tear it. Only the Omni ends it. Stand fifty blocks or more off its mouth and fire the Omni at it. SENTINEL comes down out of orbit and fires into its mouth; the Bloom fires its own beam back, every colour gone wrong. If it has eaten too much, the Watcher gives the station all of its power. What's left is a husk. Its mouth, teeth, throat and tentacles are gone, vaporized, and its petals lie round the hole, scorched, slowly going brown like any dead flower's. The blight dies back. So does the Flesh, everywhere except the places it built itself into."},{"p":"The Carrier","h":"","u":"entities/the-carrier.html","t":"The Null Static Zone, the crater Final boss Size A head the size of a house Health 500 Held by Four threads, knotted on top of four black spires round the crater's rim Added in 1.47.0, Chapter Five part four Drops 6 to 10 Carrier Threads, some of its flesh, and the music disc Signing Off. The Watcher takes its eye."},{"p":"The Carrier","h":"Description","u":"entities/the-carrier.html#description","t":"What the last reel showed: the thing under all of it. In the crater in the middle of the Null Static Zone, a head the size of a house, with one eye in it, on a neck up out of a coil of its own pale body. Its threads go up off the coil into the dark, one to every mast you ever saw. Four of them run to the four black spires round the crater's rim and are tied off in a knot on top of each. Its voice is every voice it ever carried, mumbling at once, deep, heard right across the crater. When you hold the Last Reel up to the light, its last frame shows it: \"something vast, curled under the ground. An eye, opening.\""},{"p":"The Carrier","h":"How it fights","u":"entities/the-carrier.html#how-it-fights","t":"Slam: it rears and comes down, and a ring of static rolls out across the floor. Jump it. Below half health it sends two. Gaze: its eye opens and a beam of dead air sweeps across the crater. Brood: Afterimages come up out of the floor and Parasites out of its coil. Draw: it draws through its threads to heal. Hit it hard enough while it does and it breaks off. Swallow: it breathes in, dragging everything across the floor to under its mouth, and bites. While a thread holds, it shrugs off most of every blow. When its eye is open (gazing, screaming or swallowing) it takes them in full."},{"p":"The Carrier","h":"Cut it loose","u":"entities/the-carrier.html#cut-it-loose","t":"Each spire has a ladder up its outer side. Climb up and break the knot; it screams for each one (\"A thread snaps - it screams.\"). Break all four and it's cut loose: furious (\"it's never been so angry\"), and far easier to hurt. Cutting the last thread earns Cut Loose ."},{"p":"The Carrier","h":"How to survive it","u":"entities/the-carrier.html#how-to-survive-it","t":"You're Nulled the whole time in the Zone, so you go hungry faster. Bring food. Hit it hardest while its eye is open. Jump the rings of static. Below half health there are two. When it breathes in, get away from the middle. A Hush is somewhere safe to retreat to: nothing of the static's own can come in, and a parasite on you comes apart at the line. The ruins are 160 blocks or more out from the crater."},{"p":"The Carrier","h":"Signing off","u":"entities/the-carrier.html#signing-off","t":"Kill it and it goes down across its coil, its threads coming down out of the dark one by one. Then the Watcher comes, in a cutscene with its own score, takes its eye, and sends everyone home. it's dead. good. it wasn't theirs, you know. it was a carrier. it carried whatever was put on it. the static was a door. and this was holding it open. this, i'll keep. for the future. go home. there's nothing on the air now. ??? signing off At the Starlite the screen goes black for the first time, and then shows one line: SIGNING OFF. The static is gone everywhere: no more hound packs, and the Hollowed are only villagers again. This earns Signing Off . Scratched into a Hush's bench by the last of the old ones: \"THE GREAT ONE IN THE PIT CARRIES THEM UP ITS THREADS TO EVERY PLACE THAT LISTENS. WHEN IT DIES THEY WILL HAVE NO WAY UP.\""},{"p":"The Carrier","h":"What came of it","u":"entities/the-carrier.html#what-came-of-it","t":"It wasn't over. Half a minute after you're home, the Watcher comes back: \"it seems the carrier did what it was supposed to do. it carried them - all the way out.\" The parasites are everywhere now, and they grow themselves a mind instead: the Chorus . See After Signing Off . What he took from it is in his Vault , behind a round steel door: What's Left of the Carrier , \"A knot of it, still beating. Static comes off it like heat. It carried whatever was put on it. It held a door open.\" Take it and its static pours out, and every Tuned near you is loose for a few seconds. The Projectionist's reruns bring back its beam, down out of nothing onto where you stand. And on the Other Side , at a third left of the fight with the Viewer , the Watcher feeds it through the gate of his last projector: your world, all of it, carried out on the beam onto what he kept out. It gets up."},{"p":"The Chorus","h":"","u":"entities/the-chorus.html","t":"The Hive's pit, then the Warm Heart in the Deep Boss, twice Health 900 in its pit; the Chorus, Whole: 1024 Held up by Four nerve nodes on stalks round its pit Added in 1.50.0 (the pit), 1.53.0 (its hands), 1.54.0 (the Deep and the Chorus, Whole) Music The Chorus; then All of Them Leaves In its pit, it doesn't die: it runs, and leaves a Chorus Fragment for each of you there. Whole, it dies and leaves the Last Voice. The Chorus The hive, its hands standing round the pit."},{"p":"The Chorus","h":"Description","u":"entities/the-chorus.html#description","t":"When the Carrier died the parasite lost its voice: the static it heard itself in. So it grew itself a mind instead, out of everything it took. In a pit in the middle of the Hive it comes up out of the floor: a mound of fused bodies with a great head on it, a maw split down the middle of it in four, and all over it the faces of the ones it took, their eyes shut, their mouths moving, all of them speaking at once with one voice. Two arms as long and heavy as tree trunks, ending in hooks, and tendrils up off its back. It knows you. it lost its voice when the carrier died. so it's growing itself a mind instead. out of everything it took. every body. every face. everything any of them ever knew. when it's finished it won't need the static to talk to them. it'll just be all of them. ??? after It Speaks"},{"p":"The Chorus","h":"It Speaks","u":"entities/the-chorus.html#it-speaks","t":"The first night after the Hive has grown, out under the open sky, the ground heaves round you and five of the pure forms stand up out of it, turn to you together, and it speaks through them, all of them at once, its voices out of step: we were many. we were scattered. we heard each other in the noise. you cut the throat that carried us. now there is only quiet. so we are growing another way to be one. out of all of them. out of everything they knew. come and see what we are becoming. come and be heard. The Chorus It Speaks Then they fall, and the Watcher is beside you. He gives you his needle to it. Hearing it earns It Speaks ."},{"p":"The Chorus","h":"The Mind","u":"entities/the-chorus.html#the-mind","t":"Go to the edge of its pit and it comes up out of it: you. we know you. you were in the static with us. you were loud. we do not need a throat now. we have a thousand mouths, and all of them are listening. the ones you lost are here with us. they are singing. would you like to hear them? come down. be heard. be one more voice. The Chorus The Mind"},{"p":"The Chorus","h":"How it fights","u":"entities/the-chorus.html#how-it-fights","t":"It never leaves its pit. Tendrils: the ground churns, a ring of it lifting and cracking with violet light coming up through it, and a second later a barbed tendril as tall as a house bursts up, flinging whoever was standing there into the air. It lashes at whoever's nearest, then sinks back. Move when the ground churns. Hitting a tendril hurts the Chorus a little. Spores: clouds of them. Birth: pure forms out of its maw. Slam: an arm brought down. Song: three swells, each one worse. It goes through you: you're slow, weak and in the dark a moment. Scream. Draw: it draws through the cords to its nodes to heal."},{"p":"The Chorus","h":"The nerve nodes","u":"entities/the-chorus.html#the-nerve-nodes","t":"Round the pit stand four stalks, each with a Nerve Node on top, glowing, a cord running from it to the Chorus with its light running along it. Climb the steps of chitin wound up each stalk and tear the node open. While its nodes live it's thinking clearly, and it shrugs off part of every blow: with all four alive, it takes half. Each node you break, it screams (\"It screams. 3 of its nodes left.\"), its maw wide (a free hit), and it gets easier to hurt. Break all four and everything gets through (\"It screams - and it can't think straight any more. Everything gets through now.\"). That earns Senseless . Fire hurts it half as much again. Leave it alone and it heals: once nobody's near and it hasn't been hurt for half a minute, it mends."},{"p":"The Chorus","h":"The Hive Hands","u":"entities/the-chorus.html#the-hive-hands","t":"The black spires of chitin round the pit are alive: seven Hive Hands (140 health at their usual size; each is its own size). Up out of a mound of the hive's flesh, an arm as tall as a tree: three strands of chitin braided round a core of flesh, knots of flesh swollen on it, violet light in its seams, and at the top a palm with eyes and a mouth in it and three long jointed fingers, each ending in a hook. They never stop moving, writhing like something in water and turning to follow you. Come within reach and one will: Slam: it rears back, the ground where it's coming down lights up violet (move), and it brings its claw down on you. Bent right over like a scorpion's tail if you're close, a long reach out over the ground if you're not. Sweep: get in close to its foot and it bends low and swings right across, throwing you aside. Grab: it closes on you, lifts you high over the hive, squeezes, and throws you. Hurt it enough while it has you and it lets go. They can be hurt (fire worse) and killed: it withers, falls forward, curls up and goes down into its mound, and drops Hive Chitin and Hive Flesh. While the Chorus is still in its pit, the hive grows a dead hand back after five minutes."},{"p":"The Chorus","h":"It Runs","u":"entities/the-chorus.html#it-runs","t":"Bring it down to a quarter and it won't die. It runs, tearing itself down into the ground, deep: no. no - not yet. we are not finished. The Chorus going down it ran. it can do that now. it's got enough of a mind to be afraid. it's gone down. deep. where everything went before the static was ever a noise. that's a piece of it. it still talks. keep it - listen to it. it'll tell you where it went. it'll come back up. bigger. and next time it won't be half finished. ??? after It Runs It leaves a Chorus Fragment for each of you near. They still talk: hold one to your ear. Driving it down earns It Ran . The fragment leads you to the Sinkhole and down into the Deep ."},{"p":"The Chorus","h":"It comes back up","u":"entities/the-chorus.html#it-comes-back-up","t":"Until it's dead, the world up top feels it: tremors under you every so often, the ground giving way near you into pits lined with its flesh with its things climbing out, and flesh blisters swelling up out of the ground (break one before it bursts, or its forms come out)."},{"p":"The Chorus","h":"The Reach","u":"entities/the-chorus.html#the-reach","t":"Every few nights, where you live (at your bed if you're near it), three tremors come, closer and closer, and the screen reads IT COMES UP . The ground splits in a ragged line and one of the Chorus's hands tears up out of it, half again as big as the hive's, with waves of its things climbing out of the split after it. It has its own bar and its own music. Kill it and it's done (\"It goes back down without its hand.\"), which earns It Came Up . Leave it and after four minutes it sinks back down."},{"p":"The Chorus","h":"The Chorus, Whole","u":"entities/the-chorus.html#the-chorus-whole","t":"Where it went to ground is the Warm Heart : a great round chamber, its floor the hive's flesh running down on every side to a lake of blood, a vault of chitin ribs over it, its four nerve nodes on their stalks round the lake. Come down into it and it rises up out of the blood (\"Up out of the blood it comes - whole again, and every voice in it singing.\"): made again out of everything it took, a second pair of arms out of its sides, the Bloom's roots run all through it, its hands up round the shore with it. It has 1024 health, the most anything can have. It isn't running any more; there's nowhere further down to go. It fights as it did in its pit, harder, in three parts: Its nodes and its hands. The same nodes to tear open, the same hands round the shore. The older ones break in (two thirds down). \"The walls crack open. Something's coming through them: the older ones. They've heard it.\" Listeners come through for it, for its things, and for you. Its song gets worse; carry the Deaf King's ear-stones and its song can't get into you at all. It tears itself up (a third left) out of its lake, tearing out its cords as it goes (\"It tears itself up out of its lake - and its cords tear with it.\"). No nodes any more, nothing to draw on: everything it has, as fast as it can. And then it dies. Really, this time: every voice in it going quiet one after another, and it goes down into the blood. Everything of its in the chamber falls apart (nothing bursts out of them now), and the world above stops feeling it (\"Far below, the singing stops. It doesn't start again.\"). Out of it comes the Last Voice , the one voice it couldn't swallow, thrown up onto the shore. Killing it earns The Last Voice . it's quiet down there now. i can hear you breathing. you've got something of it. one voice it couldn't swallow. keep it. there's a door at the end of the world with a seal on it. i made that seal. i can't open it. that voice can. when you're ready, take it to the end. ??? a while after That's the way into Chapter Six . Not all of it went quiet. In Chapter Ten its last voice comes back out of the parasites SENTINEL brought up from Blackwater (\"...one voice left.\" \"it will do.\"), and they pour into the last of SENTINEL's crew : \"we hear you, signal.\" before the Harbinger swallows him and the hive gets into it."},{"p":"The Chorus","h":"Its hidden voice","u":"entities/the-chorus.html#its-hidden-voice","t":"Since 1.60.3, now and then, out of all its faces muttering as one, a single voice in the Chorus speaks on its own, fourteen seconds of it, and the rest of them hush while it does (its subtitle: \"The Chorus: one voice out of all of them\"). It comes round again every minute or two while you're near."},{"p":"The Chorus","h":"How to survive it","u":"entities/the-chorus.html#how-to-survive-it","t":"Go for the nodes first. With all four up it takes half of everything. Watch the ground. Churning means a tendril; violet light means a hand's claw is coming down. Hit it hardest while its maw is open: while it screams, sings, breathes out spores or gives birth, it takes everything. Bring fire. It, its hands and its pure forms all take more from it. For the Chorus, Whole, kill the Deaf King first and carry his ear-stones."},{"p":"The Chorus","h":"Testing it","u":"entities/the-chorus.html#testing-it","t":"With cheats on: /statichollow ending hivehere (the hive 52 blocks ahead of you), hivespeak , hivemind , hivefight , hivenode , hivedown , hivehands , hiveskip , hivereset ; for the Deep, reach and heart ."},{"p":"The Crowd","h":"","u":"entities/the-crowd.html","t":"The Stalls, the front, under the Great Screen Boss Health 800 Made of The whole house: every one of the Audience Added in 1.56.0, Chapter Six part one: The Audience Music Standing Ovation Leaves The Last Ticket, one for everyone who was there; also 4 to 9 Ticket Stubs, 2 to 4 diamonds and 1 to 3 echo shards Past the Door at the End of the World is the Stalls : an old picture house's seats out in the dark, row after row of them, every one facing a screen two hundred feet wide. Some of the seats are taken."},{"p":"The Crowd","h":"The Audience","u":"entities/the-crowd.html#the-audience","t":"Forty of the seats hold grey people in good clothes gone the colour of ash, slack in their seats, their faces turned up to the screen, their mouths a little open, the picture flickering in their eyes, a ticket in one hand in their laps. They've been watching a long time. They don't look round (16 health each). They hear you, though: a step near them, a block broken, a door. Then they get up, slow, a finger to their lips, and come for you, arms out, shushing, and the ones round them get up too. One that gets hold of you holds you where you are. Sneak and they don't hear you walk. Lose them and they go back to their seats, and sit, and watch. Some of them carry a Ticket Stub . They can't carry the parasite."},{"p":"The Crowd","h":"The Ushers","u":"entities/the-crowd.html#the-ushers","t":"Four of them walk the aisles, up and down, slow: tall, too thin, a maroon uniform with brass buttons and a little pillbox cap, white gloves, and no face (44 health each). Each carries a lamp and swings its cone of yellow light over the rows. If its lamp finds you (\"The Usher's lamp is on you.\"), sneaking doesn't help: it sees, it doesn't hear. It puts a finger to where its lips should be, and the SHHH goes right through the house. Everyone sat near you gets up. It comes for you itself: it bashes you with the lamp, and if it gets hold of your collar (\"The Usher has you by the collar.\") it walks you back up the aisle toward the Door. Show it a ticket. Use a Ticket Stub on an Usher and it tears it in two and looks away (\"The Usher tears your ticket in two, and looks away.\"). For a minute its lamp doesn't see you. Now and then one drops its lamp (six times in ten). It always drops a Ticket Stub."},{"p":"The Crowd","h":"The Usher's Lamp","u":"entities/the-crowd.html#the-ushers-lamp","t":"Held, it lights the dark round you. Used, it flashes : the Audience and the Ushers caught in it reel with their hands over their faces and can't do anything for a few seconds. It needs eight seconds to warm again. It also breaks the Crowd's Hush, and stops the Tuned in the Vault."},{"p":"The Crowd","h":"The Crowd","u":"entities/the-crowd.html#the-crowd","t":"Step out onto the front aisle , under the screen, and the picture on the screen is you . Every one of the Audience gets up and comes down to the front, and goes into the heap of them, and it gets up: three men high, two great arms made of people, and at the top a knot of faces, every one of them looking at you, every mouth going. It has its own bar and its own music. It doesn't leave the front. It doesn't have to."},{"p":"The Crowd","h":"How it fights","u":"entities/the-crowd.html#how-it-fights","t":"Reach: one arm of them swung across the front rows. Slam: both arms up and down into the floor. The ring of it goes out over the floor: jump it. Applause: its hands together, three times, and every clap a wall of air that throws you back. Shed: people come off it, get up, and come for you. The Hush (from two thirds down): \"Quiet, please.\" A thousand fingers to a thousand lips. For four seconds anyone who moves, or strikes, gets hands up out of the floor holding them and pulling. Stand still. Or flash an Usher's Lamp at it: the house lights up and the Hush breaks. Keeping perfectly still through one earns Quiet, Please . Roar (the last third): every mouth at once."},{"p":"The Crowd","h":"How to survive it","u":"entities/the-crowd.html#how-to-survive-it","t":"Get through the Stalls quietly first: sneak past the Audience, keep out of the Ushers' light, and keep a Ticket Stub or two for an Usher that finds you. Bring an Usher's Lamp to the front. It ends the Hush. Jump the slam rings. Stand back from the front rows when it reaches. Kill what it sheds before the people pile up round you."},{"p":"The Crowd","h":"Its end","u":"entities/the-crowd.html#its-end","t":"Dead, it comes apart into the people it was, and they come apart into static, and the screen goes dark. What's left in the middle of it is the Last Ticket , for everyone who was there: \"ADMIT ONE - THE VAULT\". It's warm. On the back, in a thin black hand: THE VAULT. Bringing it down earns Standing Ovation . Then the house is empty, but one seat in the front row is still taken. It's the Watcher. it was a good show. you weren't meant to see the end of it. you want to know what i locked up. come and see, then. ??? Front Row He gets up, goes to the screen, puts his hand on it, tears it open and goes through, and it closes behind him to a seam of light down the middle of the screen. That earns Front Row . Hold the Last Ticket up to the seam and it opens into the Watcher's Vault , where the Projectionist is waiting. The Hub's replay portal for The Door brings the Crowd back for another go (see the Hub )."},{"p":"The Deaf King","h":"","u":"entities/the-deaf-king.html","t":"The Deep, the dais at the end of the Old Halls Boss Health 420 Senses Can't hear, can't see. It feels you through the floor. Added in 1.54.0, Chapter Five part six Music Stand Still Drops The King's Ear-Stones, 3 to 6 Carved Old Stone, 2 to 4 Bloom Roots and 2 to 4 diamonds The older ones were in the Deep before the Chorus came down into it. They don't hunt each other. They hate the Chorus and everything of its as much as they hate you, and they go for whatever of its they hear or feel moving."},{"p":"The Deaf King","h":"Description","u":"entities/the-deaf-king.html#description","t":"The oldest thing in the Deep, the one that carved the Old Halls: a hulk that walks on its knuckles, its hide gone grey-green as old stone, a crown of that stone grown into its skull, and the Bloom's roots hanging out of its jaw like a beard. Long ago it drove a plug of stone into each ear so it wouldn't hear the Chorus singing. It has sat on its dais at the end of the Old Halls ever since. To find it, follow the way-stones from the Gullet: squat columns with a spiral cut in them like an ear, and an ember cap burning on top."},{"p":"The Deaf King","h":"How it finds you","u":"entities/the-deaf-king.html#how-it-finds-you","t":"It can't hear you and it can't see you. It feels you: every step you take on the floor anywhere near it, every block you break or set down, every landing. Stand still and you aren't there. Sneak , or wear Hushed Boots , and it has to be close to feel you. In the air you're nothing to it, until you land. Hit it and it feels where the blow came from. It sits on its dais until it feels you."},{"p":"The Deaf King","h":"How it fights","u":"entities/the-deaf-king.html#how-it-fights","t":"Feel: palms flat on the floor, and a ring goes out through it. Anything moving in it is found. Slam: it rears up and brings both fists down, and the shock goes out through the floor. Jump it. Sweep: an arm swung across. Charge: from a way off, on its knuckles. If it hits a wall it's stunned a while: hit it then, when it takes half as much again. Roar (half dead): the roof comes down in places. The dust shows you where first. It's stone: arrows go in a little way and stop, doing half. It has its own bar and its own music."},{"p":"The Deaf King","h":"How to survive it","u":"entities/the-deaf-king.html#how-to-survive-it","t":"Bait the charge into a wall, then hit it while it's stunned. Jump every slam. If you're in the air when the shock goes out, it misses you. When you need it to lose you, stop moving. Watch the dust after it roars."},{"p":"The Deaf King","h":"Its end","u":"entities/the-deaf-king.html#its-end","t":"Dead, its crown cracks off, and far away something notices: \"Far under you, the singing stops a moment. Something is listening.\" Killing it earns Stand Still . It leaves the King's Ear-Stones : \"Two plugs of the old ones' stone, warm, a spiral in each.\" Carry them and the Chorus's song can't get into you either. That matters in the fight with the Chorus, Whole . The Projectionist's reruns bring its fists back, and the Hub's replay portal for The Static brings the King back for another go (see the Projectionist and the Hub )."},{"p":"The Deaf King","h":"The Listener","u":"entities/the-deaf-king.html#the-listener","t":"The Deep, nesting in the Root Hollows Hostile Health 60 Senses No eyes. It hears. Drops 1 or 2 Listener's Ears, 1 to 3 bones and sometimes string Tall, starved, cave-white, a ribcage on long dog's legs, arms that hang to its ankles, and no eyes: where they were, the skin has grown smooth over. It has ears instead, a fan of thin skin on rods of bone either side of its head that opens wide when it listens. It can't see you. It hears you: every step you walk or run, every block you break or set, every door, every mouthful, an arrow landing, a hit. It goes to the sound, fast, its fans spread, and rakes whatever is there or throws itself on it from a way off. When it gets there and there's nothing more, it stands with its ears open and listens. Sneak and it can't hear you walk. Throw something and it goes to where it lands. It hunts the Chorus's forms just the same: they walk, it hears them. They nest in the root hollows: bones, the clothes of whoever they took, a barrel of their things. When the Chorus, Whole is two thirds down, they break in through the walls of the Warm Heart, for it, for its things and for you."},{"p":"The Deaf King","h":"Hushed Boots","u":"entities/the-deaf-king.html#hushed-boots","t":"Stitch two Listener's Ears over a pair of leather boots, with string, and you have Hushed Boots : you walk as quiet as sneaking, the Listener can't hear you, and the Deaf King has to be close to feel you. Making them earns Not a Sound ."},{"p":"The First Signal","h":"","u":"entities/the-first-signal.html","t":"The Hub, past the wall; then his kingdom Chapter Ten's enemy Looks like Your shape, your size, its skin crawling static, a plain white mask. Crowned, armoured and winged by the end Fought In THE LAST BROADCAST : in his arena, in the End, and on the dragon's wings Health 800 crowned (\"The First Signal, Crowned\"); 320 on its wings (\"The First Signal, The End\") Added in 1.59.0, Chapter Seven: The First Signal; his kingdom and his creations 1.64.0; THE LAST BROADCAST 1.68.0 to 1.71.0; on its wings 1.72.0 Music Enough; and The First Signal (with its four notes, low) Status THE LAST BROADCAST - THE SECOND RITE - to be continued. His Faithful took him into a seal, \"somewhere even i can't see.\" The landing \"the first signal. it was here before me. before the first picture.\""},{"p":"The First Signal","h":"Description","u":"entities/the-first-signal.html#description","t":"Your shape, your size. Its skin is static, crawling. A long charcoal studio coat, old broadcast headphones round its neck with their cable over its shoulder, and a little red ON AIR lamp on its chest, lit. A plain white mask , and through its eye-holes its eyes: an eye in the dark, the whites dim grey, the rest one great black disc with points of light caught on it, always on you, narrowing as it shouts. When it moves it never hurries. When it skips, it skips like a signal, frames of it missing and its colours coming apart. By the end of Chapter Ten he wears what his Faithful gave him (an armour formed out of them, a crown of their daggers), carries a blade drawn out of the Harbinger , and has the End's guardian's skull for a helm and its wings on his back. See the Coronation and the Second Rite . Everything he says, word for word, is on The First Signal speaks ."},{"p":"The First Signal","h":"ENOUGH","u":"entities/the-first-signal.html#enough","t":"After the last show's credits the Watcher brings you into the Hub , the realm he made, and tells you what he can do now. He's in the middle of it (\"what do you-\") when the picture breaks up. The sky over the gallery tears open, and a voice comes out of it, low, huge, more than one voice at once: \"ENOUGH.\" He goes at the rift with both hands, pushing it shut, and a hand comes out of it and stops him. It tears the rift wide and comes through. It comes for you both. He turns to run, and it shakes its head: no. He stops. He turns back and shoves it with everything he has, and it's thrown five hundred blocks out over the static, tumbling. It catches itself, a hand dug into the static. It tears a piece of his realm loose and stamps it to rubble, then comes back in jumps, landing on the pieces of his realm one after another, each crumbling behind it. jump. ??? at the edge You go off the edge together, and falling, he shuts the realm behind you: a wall of static , slammed down. It stops at it, its hand flat on it. Hearing it, and jumping, earns ENOUGH ."},{"p":"The First Signal","h":"What it is","u":"entities/the-first-signal.html#what-it-is","t":"Falling, the Watcher tears a portal open under you both, and you come down on an oil rig in the Dead Water (since 1.62.0). He lands beside you, crouched: ...we're out. it's awake now. the first signal. it'll come for me - then for you. but it can't hear us here. not through all this water. ??? on the rig Getting there earns The First Signal . What happens on the rig is Chapter Eight ."},{"p":"The First Signal","h":"The landing","u":"entities/the-first-signal.html#the-landing","t":"In a world that came down from the Hub before 1.62.0 (or if the Dead Water isn't there), you land at home instead, and he says more: ...it's awake. the first signal. it was here before me. before the first picture. every bit of static you ever heard - that was it. asleep. i made a realm out of its static. and it noticed. i shut the realm behind us. it'll hold. for now. it'll come for me. then for you. ...we're going to need more than i've got. ??? the landing He looks up: a hairline tear across the sky, static showing through it. \"Somewhere past the static, the First Signal is awake - and it knows your name.\" Then he gives you the Remote and goes. A world like that, the next time anyone jumps off the Hub's edge, is sent on to the Dead Water: \"not that way. not this time.\""},{"p":"The First Signal","h":"Past the wall","u":"entities/the-first-signal.html#where-it-is-now","t":"Back in the Hub (the Remote takes you there), it stood past the faint wall he shut, watching you. Now and then you heard it. The Hub won't let you sleep: \"Not here. Not with it out there, past the wall.\""},{"p":"The First Signal","h":"The Broadcast","u":"entities/the-first-signal.html#the-broadcast","t":"Once the Harbinger has gone through its way out of the Dead Water, the next time you're home it cuts in on you, for everyone in the Overworld: a tone, static, black. A three-part cutscene with its own score. The wall. In the Hub, the First Signal is at its wall, both hands flat on the static. He stops. His head tilts. Then the rage: a scream of many voices through a dead channel, the wall bulging, his fists on it. He turns his back on it, lifts a hand, tears his own way open (colour bars, black) and walks into it. His kingdom. A still black sea, a realm made of his static, and on it his castle (see his kingdom ). He comes out of his tear on the platform and walks the causeway, and the water heaves: the Harbinger comes up out of it, hung on its strings, and lowers its skull to his hand. look at you. you went down an animal. you came up mine. stronger. so much stronger. The First Signal on his causeway In his war hall his servants stand round his table, a map of YOUR world on it. His hand on it, and its lights spring up all over it: it's time. find them. both of them. take them off the air. The First Signal at his war table His gate opens and his creations pour out, down the causeway, into the windows, into yours. Your house is the third part: the Watcher at your door (see the Watcher ). CHAPTER TEN - STAY TUNED - they're coming. His static gets into Tune-In Town's cast too: the show went off the air the Saturday the tape played HIM."},{"p":"The First Signal","h":"The Refusal","u":"entities/the-first-signal.html#the-refusal","t":"The first time you come through one of his tears into his kingdom after the Broadcast (1.68.0, THE LAST BROADCAST part one), it's a cutscene. In his hall he's at his war table, his hands flat on his map, and he goes still. His head comes up. \"...you.\" Then the rage: the scream, his fists down on his table three times, his map's lights jumping. \"you came into MY house?\" His static comes up out of the sea between his platform and his castle, and he's there, through it, on his platform in front of you. His hand at your throat (since 1.72.1 holding you out at the length of his arm, your toes just off the floor): \"GET. OUT.\" And you're thrown back out of the tear you came in by, hard, and it shuts behind you. \"and STAY out.\" (Anyone with you goes too. Nobody's hurt by any of it.) His static stands across his causeway the rest of that day. The next day it's gone, and so is he from his table; his war map is your world now, your house in the middle of it ringed in red, and lit on it, as they move, any of you out in it, his creations and his sites."},{"p":"The First Signal","h":"The Coronation","u":"entities/the-first-signal.html#the-coronation","t":"Two days after the Refusal, walk up his causeway (or wait long enough) and it's a cutscene (1.69.0). The Watcher tears his way through after you, \"i couldn't let you come here alone.\", and the two of you walk up to him together. ...both of you. good. you'll want to see this. The First Signal before his castle His Faithful stand round him in a ring and lift the daggers he made them, and give themselves to him with them. What they were streams into him: his armour forms out of them, piece by piece, and their daggers come together over his head: his crown . The Harbinger comes up out of the sea behind him, and he draws out of it his blade : huge, black, curved, alive, the Undertow's own teeth along its edge and an eye in it. Then he speaks: you've gone too far, Watcher. every code. every rule. you broke them all. so the order now is your erasure. every world you made. every realm. every creature. i'll rip that poor void heart out of you - and keep it. and that will be the end of time. the most powerful creation. pulling the strings - forever. as i should be. and you... i have no use for you. don't make me angrier, and i'll give you a whole new world. but i know what you want. YOU'LL BOTH FAIL. The First Signal crowned His arena comes up out of the sea off his island's east side (its floor, tier on tier of seats, his Faithful flashing into them, his own box high on its north side), and he goes up to his box. \"stay behind me. i've nothing left to fight him with - but what i have is yours.\""},{"p":"The First Signal","h":"His blade","u":"entities/the-first-signal.html#his-blade","t":"Since 1.72.2 it's modelled whole: a sword, not a cleaver, narrower, its widest two-thirds of the way up. A thick spine, flats and a bevel down to a sharp edge, the spine dropping to a clipped point; a guard on his fist and a collar over it, two hooked quillons; the Undertow's teeth set into its edge as fangs, each leant back toward the hilt, still chattering; and its eye, an eyeball socketed right through the blade near the hilt, a red iris and a slit, lids that close over it when it blinks, looking about. When he isn't swinging it he holds it low, out to his right, its point near the floor ahead of him."},{"p":"The First Signal","h":"His arena","u":"entities/the-first-signal.html#his-arena","t":"Over the bridge from his island's east side. \"His arena stands off his island's east side - over the bridge. Step down onto its floor.\" Step down and he comes down off his box at you: \"COME, THEN.\" His bar reads The First Signal, Crowned : 800 health, heavily armoured. The sweep: his blade winds back with a whine, static crawling up it, trembling as he holds it, then round in front of him in a great cut of static, the floor torn up under it and a shockwave out across it. The lunge: straight through you, leaving a streak of his afterimage. His hand: he reaches for you; if it closes on you, you're lifted and flung. His static runs up his arm into you. A skip: he drops a few frames, and he's behind you, already reaching. Stay Tuned: he calls his creations in, and his static creeps across the floor where you stand. Get off it. His scream: two rings blasted out across the arena. Every blow that lands flashes and throws sparks, and the camera shakes with it all (by the game's screen-effects slider). The Watcher stands by the gate with no power left of his own, but every so often he gives each of you on the floor what he has: thirty seconds of something at its strongest (Strength, Speed, Regeneration, Haste, Absorption, Health Boost, Jump Boost or Fire Resistance, level V). Off its floor long enough, and he's back up in his box, whole. His arena stays: it's there whenever you come back."},{"p":"The First Signal","h":"A quarter of him gone: the Mast","u":"entities/the-first-signal.html#the-mast","t":"\"...enough.\" He's gone from the floor to his castle's roof, his hand on his mast, and every lamp on his towers goes dark, into him. The Watcher's on his knees: \"no... he's taking it. all of it. mine too.\" His laugh: \"ha. ha ha. HA HA HA HA.\" And the Watcher takes out the Omni: \"then i'll call down something bigger.\" He fires it up into the sky, and the sky over his castle tears open. THE LAST BROADCAST - THE CALL - to be continued."},{"p":"The First Signal","h":"The Fall","u":"entities/the-first-signal.html#the-fall","t":"Through the rip comes SENTINEL (1.70.0), all three thousand blocks of station, and stops over his castle, its gun charging at him (\"SENTINEL // MAIN GUN CHARGING\"). \"you called THAT down on me?\" At half its charge he puts everything he took from his towers up through his blade, \"then watch it fall.\", and his blast tears its right side off. A module of it comes down near his arena with its crew in it, and what they brought up with them. From his roof: \"...your toy brought guests.\" \"NOW. WHERE WERE WE.\""},{"p":"The First Signal","h":"The second quarter","u":"entities/the-first-signal.html#the-second-quarter","t":"\"SENTINEL's down - and so's what was in it. He's on his arena's floor again, three-quarters of him left. The Watcher has the Omni: when he fires it, hit him.\" Every half-minute or so the Watcher fires the Omni into him and puts him down on one knee, his armour cracking, burning at the seams, and while he's down everything hurts him half again as much. New: he puts his blade up at the rip and bolts of his static come down where each of you is standing (red rings on the floor first: get out of them). The fight goes on to half of him."},{"p":"The First Signal","h":"The Forge","u":"entities/the-first-signal.html#the-forge","t":"The Omni puts him on his knee. \"...my Faithful.\" They come down out of their seats to him in flashes of his static, lay their hands on his armour and close its cracks, and chant their glyphs into it: his armour and his blade enchanted, glyphs crawling over them. He gets up. ...is that it? a gun in the sky. a crew who never asked to come. they fell for you. remember that. and you, Watcher. still on your knees. every signal that ever went out comes home to me. everything they built up there. every last watt of it - IS MINE. The First Signal forged He puts his blade up at what's left of SENTINEL and tears every bit of its light out of it, down into him, till it's dark. THE LAST BROADCAST - THE FORGE - to be continued."},{"p":"The First Signal","h":"The End","u":"entities/the-first-signal.html#the-end","t":"The Tearing (1.71.0): \"this sea's too small for me now.\" He puts his blade straight up, and the sky over his arena tears open, as wide as his arena, colour bars round its edge. \"HOLD ON TO SOMETHING.\" The whole of it is torn up out of his sea, and you with it, up into the tear. The Arrival : his arena hangs out over the void north of the End's island, a ragged cone of rock under it, its bridge snapped off short. \"...the End. he's brought it all to the End.\" Up out of the dark comes the End's guardian , the hive's now, and circles. \"the last thing your world kept for itself.\" \"and look what's kept it all this time.\" He comes down off his box. The fight in the End : half of him gone already, he fights to a fifth of him (15%), forged now, enchanted and alight with SENTINEL's power, with the guardian strafing and diving at you over him. The Watcher still fires the Omni into him every half-minute or so. Fall off the edge into the void and his static catches you and puts you back on the floor (it hurts). Anyone who comes to his kingdom now is carried on through to his arena in the End."},{"p":"The First Signal","h":"The Second Rite","u":"entities/the-first-signal.html#the-second-rite","t":"At 15%, a cutscene. \"...not like this.\" Then \"YOU. you'll do.\" He's up onto the dragon's neck as it comes down at him, his blade in it, riding it round over his arena, and it comes down on the floor. He takes its head off; tears its wings off; reaches into its chest and pulls out its heart. His Faithful come down to him and sing the second rite round him, their glyphs lit in a ring on the floor: head to crown him. wings to bear him. heart to keep him. ours, for ever. The Faithful round him Its heart into his chest; its wings onto his back; and its head (since 1.72.2) drawn down small into his own as its skull forms over his, a part of his armour, piece by piece: its upper jaw over his head, a brow over each eye socket lit violet, its lower jaw under his chin, its fangs either side of his face, two pairs of horns swept back between his crown's daggers. \"NOW. I AM THE END.\" Wings open."},{"p":"The First Signal","h":"On its wings","u":"entities/the-first-signal.html#on-its-wings","t":"Since 1.72.0 he takes off on the dragon's wings and you fight him again, in the air over his arena: a whole new bar, The First Signal, The End , 320 health, lighter-armoured in the air. He circles over you, then: A dive: reared up, his blade over his head, and down on you head first. The floor bursts where he hits it, and he's down on it a few seconds after, getting up. Hit him then. A gust: three great beats of his wings, everything in front of him thrown back across the floor. Mind the edge. Its breath: down low, the dragon's head on him breathes its fire in a sweep across the floor, and it burns there a while. A volley: balls of its fire spat down at you one after another, bursting where they land. Seized (once he's lost a third): he swoops down and carries you up in his hand, crushing you, and throws you down. Hurt him enough while he's got you and he lets go. His static (once he's lost two-thirds): bolts down out of the sky where you stand. The Watcher's Omni still knocks him out of the sky now and then (down on the floor, wide open). A bow, a crossbow or a trident helps. Brought down to nothing, he falls out of the air, turning over and over, onto where the rite was, and the Watcher gets up."},{"p":"The First Signal","h":"Taken","u":"entities/the-first-signal.html#taken","t":"The Watcher lets the Omni fall and gets up off his knees. \"the End was never yours.\" The Watcher's static throws him back off his feet; he draws his blade back, trembling, and swings it, and the Watcher catches it; and the Watcher puts his beam (a real beam of shadow since 1.72.0) into his heart: \"i've watched you since the first night. i know what you are.\" Then his Faithful seize him. A seal opens behind him, black, ringed in their glyphs. this isn't over. THIS ISN'T OVER - The First Signal going into the seal They're gone into it with him, and it's shut. The Watcher, on one knee: \"...they took him. somewhere even i can't see.\" \"go home. while there's still a home to go to.\" Then the Rebirth , and the card: THE LAST BROADCAST - THE SECOND RITE - to be continued. His arena's gone from his sea after it, and so is he."},{"p":"The Gardener","h":"","u":"entities/the-gardener.html","t":"The Botanic Gardens, under the dome Boss Who he was E. Thorne, Head Gardener Size Over three blocks tall Health 420 Wakes when You go too close to him or the flower, or strike him Drops The Gardener's Shears, the Heartbloom, a handful of Knotted Roots, bone meal, moss, weeping bells and rare seeds. His head on the first kill. The glasshouse The Gardener under the dome, with the HD Models pack."},{"p":"The Gardener","h":"Description","u":"entities/the-gardener.html#description","t":"The Head Gardener who tended the great flower so long it grew into him. He kneels at it under the dome with a root running from its heart into his face, in a rotting coat and a wide straw hat, a pale flower with an eye in it where his face was. His chest is a cage of root ribs with a heart beating inside, moss and little flowers growing in it. His left arm is a root. He carries rusted hedge shears as long as a man, in both hands, one on each long handle."},{"p":"The Gardener","h":"Waking him","u":"entities/the-gardener.html#waking-him","t":"He doesn't notice you at first. Walk softly. Go too close to him or to the flower, or strike him, and he tears loose and stands, and the gates slam shut behind you. They can't be broken while he lives, not even in Creative. Before you wake him, find his clothes (the hat and boots in the potting shed, the coat and breeches in his office). You'll want them later."},{"p":"The Gardener","h":"How he fights","u":"entities/the-gardener.html#how-he-fights","t":""},{"p":"The Gardener","h":"Phase one","u":"entities/the-gardener.html#phase-one","t":"Snip: the shears turned on their side, jaws flung wide, a lunge, and they bite shut. You bleed. Scissor and Thrust : a double snip, and the shears couched at his hip like a spear. Prune: wound out to his right and swept all the way round, throwing you back. Whirl: held out level at arm's length as he spins. Lash: his root arm whips out and drags you in to the shears. Don't stand too far off. Sow: seeds flung out of his coat pockets that burst up as thorns under you. Step off the ground where earth bubbles. Impale: the shears raised before his face, points down, and driven into the floor."},{"p":"The Gardener","h":"The overgrowth","u":"entities/the-gardener.html#the-overgrowth","t":"At half his health he drives the shears into the ground on one knee and the glasshouse answers him: every burstpod near him goes off, petals rain, his face opens wide. He can't be hurt while it does."},{"p":"The Gardener","h":"Phase two","u":"entities/the-gardener.html#phase-two","t":"Pollen: a choking cloud breathed out of the flower. Blinds, poisons and sickens. Stay out of it. Roots: the shears driven point-down into the floor, and lines of thorns race along the ground at everyone at once. Keep moving across them. The Call: the shears raised high and wide open, a shriek, and his children come up out of the earth round you."},{"p":"The Gardener","h":"Rootlings","u":"entities/the-gardener.html#rootlings","t":"Knee-high things with a pale bulb for a head, red pinprick eyes and a grin of thorns. They chatter, leap at you, and burrow away to come up somewhere else. Kill them. They drop Knotted Roots."},{"p":"The Gardener","h":"How to survive him","u":"entities/the-gardener.html#how-to-survive-him","t":"He is slow and huge. Keep out of reach of the shears, but not so far that he lashes you in. Watch for his arm going back. Thorns come up where the ground stirs and earth bubbles. Step off it. If everyone inside leaves or dies, he goes back to his flower, healed, and the gates open again. You can retreat, but you start over."},{"p":"The Gardener","h":"His end","u":"entities/the-gardener.html#his-end","t":"He drops his shears, goes down on his knees, his flowers wilt, and he bows. The great flower drags him in and eats him, and dies with him, its heart dried to a dead knot. He leaves the Gardener's Shears (Prune: full swings snip twice, and whatever is badly hurt is cut half again as hard; use them to drive a row of thorns toward what you face) and the Heartbloom , all that was left of the flower's heart: eat it and you are made whole, hardened and healing, and everything green round you flowers. Three days later, the flower turns out not to be dead. See the green rift . And in chapter four the Bloom gives him back: the Gardener, Reborn ."},{"p":"The Gardener","h":"Turned","u":"entities/the-gardener.html#turned","t":"Since 1.51.0 the parasite can take him. Turned, he's the Gardener, Overgrown . The Projectionist's reruns bring back his ring of thorns, and the Hub's replay portal for Act Two brings him back for another go."},{"p":"The Gardener","h":"Field notes","u":"entities/the-gardener.html#field-notes","t":"His journal is on the lectern in his office; his under-gardener T. Avery's ledger is in the Seed Vault. Both are on the lore page . I hear it say my name through the lilies. It says it needs tending. It is right. Somebody must tend it. I am going to kneel by it a while. Just a while. If you find this: do not wake me. Do not touch the flower. The last page of E. Thorne's journal."},{"p":"The Harbinger","h":"","u":"entities/the-harbinger.html","t":"The Dead Water, then his kingdom, then the dark Never fought Was The Undertow , with the Grove's Heart and the Drowned Heart in it Fought Never: it's in cutscenes, and in the sea round his castle Added in 1.63.23, Chapter Nine: The Harbinger (mended in 1.63.24 and 1.63.25); his since 1.64.0 Music The Turning; The Harbinger Status THE LAST BROADCAST - THE SECOND RITE - to be continued. It's out there, going from door to door."},{"p":"The Harbinger","h":"The Turning","u":"entities/the-harbinger.html#the-turning","t":"Once ORPHEUS has all three of her modules in her bay (the pressure plating, the depth module and the UV field module) it plays, for everyone in the Dead Water: you're taken off whatever you're in (she's put back in her clamps), out of any screen, and up onto the rig's helipad. A full cutscene with its own score, The Turning. The Undertow comes up out of the sea by the rig and roars . Then it goes. To the Drowned Mycelia, down through the roof of the Grove's hollow, where the Grove Heart flinches: ...no. not you. not you. The Grove Heart as the roof breaks Its jaws close on it. Then to the Haemal Reach, and through the Drowned Heart. With both of them in it, it turns : the Grove's fungus up its left side, pale, gilled, caps growing out of it; the Reach's flesh up its right, raw and veined, its light gone red. It comes back mad, up out of the sea hundreds of blocks and down, again and again round the rig (since 1.63.25 its first time up is out past a hundred blocks off the rig), and the last time it comes down by the rig, and lies there. Down under where he went into the sea, the Watcher wakes. His bubble breaks, and he comes up out of the sea and onto the helipad beside you. You point at it. ...what the hell is happening? ...what is that? i never made that. i made this place. every wreck, every fish in it. not that - i don't know how it got in here. and the grove's fungus is in it now. the virus - in my safe world. and the divers. what the enzyme made of them. i should have told you. it ate both hearts. they're in it now. one thing. it isn't dead. it's sleeping. whatever it is - we have to kill it. if we do - its static's still in there. we put it in your remote. something stronger than it ever was. then we go back to the hub. ??? on the helipad Then the card: CHAPTER NINE - THE HARBINGER - three days. Watching it all earns The Turning (\"Watch the Undertow eat both hearts - and come down by the rig\"). The whole chapter is told on Chapter Nine ."},{"p":"The Harbinger","h":"The three days","u":"entities/the-harbinger.html#the-three-days","t":"\"Chapter Nine: The Harbinger. It lies in the sea by the rig, both infections all over it - he says it's sleeping. Three days.\" The husk lies out in the sea north-east of the rig (on your left, looking out to sea from the helipad), its jaws a hundred blocks off the rig and its whole body there. Its eyes are shut. Both infections are all over it, spores steaming off one side and blood off the other, and its heart can be heard from the rig, beating faster as the days go. There's no fight: it just lies there. While it does, nothing comes up out of the Black Below, the Grove's Heart doesn't grow back and the Drowned Heart doesn't beat. The Watcher keeps watch at the helipad's rail. Come up to him and he has something to say, a day at a time: i've been through everything i ever made. it isn't in any of it. where did it come from? the lab's log said three days. that's how long the enzyme takes to finish what it starts. tomorrow. whatever it's turning into, it's nearly done. stay near. ??? at the rail, the first, second and third day The three days are 72,000 ticks. The Dead Water's sky never moves and nobody sleeps there, so since 1.63.24 they count by the overworld's clock too: /time add , or nights slept through at home, bring it on."},{"p":"The Harbinger","h":"What came out of it","u":"entities/the-harbinger.html#what-came-out-of-it","t":"Three days on, the next time you're in the Dead Water, what's in it comes out. Its bones come out through its mouth: a skull, a spine and its ribs, strung all through with the Grove's strings, which run out of the heart in its ribs, where the Grove's heart and the Reach's are going into one. Hung on its strings, it rises over the sea, retches, and brings up a static heart at your feet (one for each of you). The heart speaks to you both, two voices whispering as one: thank you for making us one. this gift will not be wasted. we would want you to join us. to be stronger. both of you. but we have more important work to do. The heart at your feet It tears a way out of the Dead Water, half the Grove's and half the Reach's, and goes through it. The way shuts, and the husk goes down into the sea. ...it's gone. pick it up. put it in your remote. i'll meet you at the hub. ??? on the helipad Seeing it earns This Gift Will Not Be Wasted (\"See what came out of it after three days\"). After it, nothing comes up out of the Black Below any more."},{"p":"The Harbinger","h":"The static heart","u":"entities/the-harbinger.html#the-static-heart","t":"\"It's gone through. The static heart it brought up is on the helipad - put it in the Remote (craft them together).\" The Static Heart (Mutated) crafted with the Broken Remote (or the mended one) makes the Remote (Mutated) : it works again, and the Undertow's roar comes out of your hand. See chapter gear ."},{"p":"The Harbinger","h":"His","u":"entities/the-harbinger.html#his","t":"Where it went is his kingdom . In Chapter Ten 's Broadcast, as the First Signal walks his causeway, the water heaves and it comes up out of it, hung on its strings, and lowers its skull to his hand: look at you. you went down an animal. you came up mine. stronger. so much stronger. The First Signal on his causeway Since 1.69.0, two days after the Refusal, it's in the black water round his castle: up out of the sea, over, and down again, now here, now there (well out from his castle, never over his causeway), swimming on under the water between. At the Coronation it comes up out of the sea behind him, and he draws his blade out of it: huge, black, curved, alive, the Undertow's own teeth along its edge and an eye in it."},{"p":"The Harbinger","h":"The hive","u":"entities/the-harbinger.html#the-hive","t":"When SENTINEL's torn-off module comes down in his sea, the parasites it brought up out of Blackwater take its crew, and the Chorus 's last voice goes into the last of them. The Harbinger comes up out of the sea beside the wreck and swallows him whole , and the hive gets into it: its bones go violet. A door of the hive's chitin opens on the air out past the wreck, and it goes out through it and is gone."},{"p":"The Harbinger","h":"The Rebirth","u":"entities/the-harbinger.html#the-rebirth","t":"Straight after the Second Rite (1.71.0): far out in the dark, the Harbinger's bones. Its skin grows back over them, from its skull to its tail (since 1.72.0), all three of them in it, grown over each other: the Grove's, the Reach's, the hive's. Its eye opens. ...again. A whisper in the dark A door of the hive's opens, and it goes through; out of another, far off; and into another. THE LAST BROADCAST - THE SECOND RITE - to be continued."},{"p":"The Mended","h":"","u":"entities/the-mended.html","t":"The Murder Mansion, the Trophy Hall Boss Made at The Mending Altar, with one head from each of chapter two's nine Health 750 Size Four blocks tall, hunched Phases Agony, Aggression, Iron Will Drops The Mended Heart and the Rusted Garden Key, with iron, chains and one of each of the nine's drops. By chance as it falls apart: bottles o' enchanting (60%), netherite scrap (25%), a totem of undying (15%), an enchanted golden apple (5%). The Mended Out in the fog."},{"p":"The Mended","h":"The mending","u":"entities/the-mended.html#the-mending","t":"Put one head from each of the nine (the Bunnyman, the Hookman, the Hogshead, the Porcelain Man, the Harvestman, Mothman, the Jersey Devil, Dogman and the Flatwoods Monster) on the trophy pedestals round the Mending Altar, and right-click the altar with an empty hand. The Watcher, waiting on the ceiling, does the rest. It takes about thirty seconds. The heads scream as it talks, and their agony runs out of them in red streams into a knot over the floor. It pours its shadow into the knot. The heads are torn apart one by one; chains come down out of the dark and something hammers iron into the knot; the body is there, red hot, its pieces slamming together. It stands, the chains snap, and it roars with all nine voices. Nothing can hurt it until then. what i make out of them won't be pretty and it won't be kind. it will be one thing instead of nine. that's the point. one thing can be killed. From On the Mending , the Watcher's pages on the library desk"},{"p":"The Mended","h":"Description","u":"entities/the-mended.html#description","t":"Four blocks tall, hunched, held together with stitches and iron: a pig's head with the Porcelain Man's cracked face bolted over it (with Mothman's eye bulging out of the mask) and the Jersey Devil's horns, the Hookman's arm and hook, the Hogshead's arm with the Dogman's claws and the Harvestman's scythe, a dog's leg and a goat's, Mothman's wings down its back, and the Flatwoods Monster's lamp burning in its open chest. A crow stands on its shoulder plate."},{"p":"The Mended","h":"How it fights","u":"entities/the-mended.html#phases","t":""},{"p":"The Mended","h":"Agony","u":"entities/the-mended.html#agony","t":"The killers' ways: a two-blow chop with the scythe arm; the hook thrown on its chain to drag you in, then the chop; a head-down charge (sidestep it into a wall and it stands there stunned, taking extra damage); a whole turn with the scythe held out if you get round it. It also fires its needles, pours its chest-lamp's beam on you, and calls the crows. At 60% it tears itself open: the stitches burst, the wings rip loose and spread, and it screams."},{"p":"The Mended","h":"Aggression","u":"entities/the-mended.html#aggression","t":"Faster, with the cryptids' ways too: Mothman's screech (darkness, your legs heavy), the Jersey Devil's spring into the air and glide, the Flatwoods mist out of its chest (poison and nausea), and the Dogman's claw, claw, bite. At 25% it drops to one knee and iron is driven into it: chains up out of the ground, plates and nails, red hot. The boss bar turns white."},{"p":"The Mended","h":"Iron Will","u":"entities/the-mended.html#iron-will","t":"Armoured and slow, but much faster whenever nobody is looking at it. It kneels to mend itself, white arms sewing it shut and healing it, unless you hit it hard enough to tear the stitches (it staggers and takes extra damage). It slams both fists down and a ring of iron spikes runs out across the floor: jump it . It can't be hurt while it tears itself open or while the iron goes in."},{"p":"The Mended","h":"How to survive it","u":"entities/the-mended.html#how-to-survive-it","t":"Bring torches, food, and \"more than you think\", as the Watcher's pages say. Don't let it get between you and the doors. Sidestep the charge into a wall for a free window of extra damage. In Iron Will, keep your eyes on it: it's much faster when nobody's looking. Hit hard while it kneels to mend. Jump the ring of spikes."},{"p":"The Mended","h":"Its end","u":"entities/the-mended.html#its-end","t":"It comes apart: the bolts burst, the hook arm tears off, the wings fall away, the white arms shatter, and the lamp in its chest gutters and goes out. It goes down on its knees, onto its claws, onto its face, and the nine go up out of it, each a light at the head of its stream. Then the Watcher has something to say about the glass house. Its Mended Heart (Iron Will): hold it up for three minutes of Resistance II, Strength I and Absorption II, then it has to beat itself warm again. Its Rusted Garden Key opens the Botanic Gardens. Its statue, carved in weathered stone with blood pouring from its mouth, stands in the Mansion's fountain. ...listen. something in the glass house heard all of that. it's awake now. ??? as the Mended dies Up close With the HD Models pack."},{"p":"The Mended","h":"Turned","u":"entities/the-mended.html#turned","t":"Since 1.51.0 the parasite can take it. Turned, it's the Mended, Unstitched : what holds the nine together now is the parasite."},{"p":"The Omni","h":"","u":"entities/the-omni.html","t":"The Omni Orbital Railgun, and SENTINEL above the sky Gone for good What it is A weapon: the Ray Gun after the Watcher has had it Fires A column of light 32 blocks across, in every colour Recharge 2 minutes Added in 1.43.0, \"The Omni Ray\" Ends The changed Bloom. Nothing else can. Where it went Its heart is in the Watcher's Vault, and in Chapter Six it goes into his last projector Omni Orbital Railgun Hold to aim, attack or let go to fire (2 min recharge) The Watcher has had it. It isn't the same gun. 32 blocks across, in every colour. Aim it at the Bloom, 50 blocks or more off its mouth."},{"p":"The Omni","h":"How you get it","u":"entities/the-omni.html#how-you-get-it","t":"Build the Orbital Railgun round the Infused Orbital Core. Building it wakes three more places. Bring back their three parts: the Nuclear Reactor Core (Ashford Nuclear Plant), the Discharge Destabilizer (Meridian Laboratory) and the Vial of Dark Matter Blood (Blackwater Station). Craft the Ray Gun round the railgun and the three parts, or bring them all to a Forsaken Altar and let the Watcher build it over the altar. The Watcher wants it: \"give it here.\" Drop it near him ( Q ) or use it on him. It floats up into his hands, rings of glyphs turning round it, light drawn in from everywhere, and he gives you back the Omni: black, its colours running. drop it. let me have it. it isn't finished. they could never finish it. it needed something they didn't have. the dark in it. mine. hold still. there. the omni. it's yours. now go to it. stand off its mouth - fifty blocks, no nearer, or it takes you with it. aim it at the flower. hold it on it. and fire. ??? making the Omni Meridian's director had worked out what they were missing: \"We can't finish it. It needs something we don't have. Something that knows the dark.\""},{"p":"The Omni","h":"The Ray Gun it was","u":"entities/the-omni.html#the-ray-gun","t":"The Ray Gun is the Orbital Railgun mod (by Mishkis, from Rayness's Renewed port, MIT licence) built into Static Hollow. Hold use and its sight opens over your view, a ring on the ground where you aim, out to 300 blocks; attack, or let go after a second, and it fires. For four seconds it locks on; then for thirty-two the sky over the spot comes apart, a dome, six spheres flung out and back, columns of light; from twenty seconds everything near is dragged in toward it; at thirty-six seconds a column of light 24 blocks across comes down the whole height of the world, and everything in it is gone. The Omni's strike is a third again as wide, in every colour, and louder than anything else in the game."},{"p":"The Omni","h":"SENTINEL","u":"entities/the-omni.html#sentinel","t":"SENTINEL is the gun above the sky that the Rosemont garrison built before the city fell, and never got to fire. The Orbital Railgun talks to it; the Uplink Station is where the garrison talked to it. The standing orders call it \"a weapon of last resort\", and its core has a third socket the engineers call \"the governor\". Nobody was ever told what goes in it. Meridian's director knew better: \"Garrison Command thinks it's a safety. It isn't. It's a throttle.\""},{"p":"The Omni","h":"The Omni Ray","u":"entities/the-omni.html#the-omni-ray","t":"Stand fifty blocks or more off the changed Bloom's mouth (\"TOO CLOSE - back off\" otherwise), aim the Omni at the flower and fire. The camera is taken, and since 1.43.2 the Watcher takes you up with him in a spill of ink, to watch from the air over the petals. The sky, over the changed Bloom ??? look up. ??? come up here. you'll want to see this. SENTINEL // DEORBIT BURN - ATMOSPHERIC ENTRY ??? it was always up there. waiting for someone to call it down. SENTINEL // RETRO BURN - DESCENT ARRESTED SENTINEL // ALL SYSTEMS ONLINE - OMNI ARRAY DEPLOYING OMNI ARRAY // ALIGNING ??? everything it has. all in one place. ??? now it has nowhere to hide. TARGET LOCKED OMNI ARRAY // FIRE WARNING // COUNTER-BEAM - OUTPUT FALLING ??? it's fighting it. If the Bloom has eaten too much: ??? it's eaten too much. it's too strong. ??? take mine. all of it. OUTPUT 1000% // SOURCE UNKNOWN If it hasn't: ??? it doesn't need me. not this time. OMNI ARRAY // OVERDRIVE - SAFETIES OFF OUTPUT 400% // HOLDING SENTINEL comes down out of its orbit: a star that moves, then a fireball burning through the air, its trail across the sky, the sonic boom, its retro thrusters. It stops right over the Bloom's mouth. Light comes in off the horizon; five rings of glyphs close in one by one round the line down to its mouth. It fires a beam of plasma, white-hot at the core, its edges split into colour. The Bloom fires back, its own beam up out of its mouth, every colour gone wrong, and drives the Omni's back up toward the station, the more it's eaten the nearer. Then it's driven down into its mouth. The blast: a breath of white, the fireball going dark in its own smoke, its shock going out at the speed of sound, heard when it gets to you: a crack like the sky splitting, and a roar rolling round the land for a long time after. A title card reads THE OMNI RAY : the bloom is dead. the watcher rests."},{"p":"The Omni","h":"Taken back","u":"entities/the-omni.html#taken-back","t":"The first time you carry the Omni off the Bloom's blight, the camera is taken again and the Watcher is in your way. He pulls the gun out of your hands, tears open a rift into his realm, green fire licking up its edges, and throws it in. It's gone for good. This earns Zero Responsibility . wait. not so fast. i'll take that. it wouldn't be fair to let you take such a destructive toy with you, to use on everything. from what i see, i see great power. great potential. but zero responsibility for life. i can see the thoughts in your head, you know. it goes where it'll be safe. in my realm. for the future. ??? taking the Omni back And the first time anyone puts the Ray Gun together in a crafting grid afterwards, he's there at the table and pulls its recipe up out of it, a page of light with the gun's plan on it, and burns it in green fire. It's gone from every recipe book, and nothing will make the Ray Gun again. This earns Always Persistent . you're always persistent. i'll take this too. now it can't ever be made again. ??? at the crafting table"},{"p":"The Omni","h":"The Omni's Heart","u":"entities/the-omni.html#the-omnis-heart","t":"In Chapter Six you find what he did with it. In one of three keeps in the Watcher's Vault , on a plinth, is the Omni's Heart : \"What made the Omni more than a gun: every colour at once, turning, in a cage of its own light. He took it out of it.\" Its tooltip reads KEPT FOR THE FUTURE. it's come for what i kept. the omni. the carrier. my first reel. get to them before it does. bring them here. ??? The Watch Bring it to his desk in the Watch, with the other two things he kept, and the Projectionist comes for them. On the Other Side , at two thirds of the fight with the Viewer , he loads it into the lamp of his last projector: every colour at once, thrown out over the dark into its eye. It reels, blinded. That earns Every Colour at Once ."},{"p":"The Parasite","h":"","u":"entities/the-parasite.html","t":"First found at Blackwater Station Hostile Looks like Six legs, and a mouth that opens like a flower Came from The Null Static Zone, by way of a crash forty kilometres out at sea First appears 1.43.0, when the Orbital Railgun wakes Blackwater Station Health 10 (its kinds 8 to 14) Related Its five kinds, the pure forms and the biomass, the turned , Parasite Host, Parasite Pod, Xeno Resin, Static Hound, the Hollowed, the Chorus Status effects Infested (on a creature it's taking over), Parasitized (the old quick brood, before 1.48.0), Brood Fit (when a brood in you has fits), Tuned In (the Relay Core lets you see them)"},{"p":"The Parasite","h":"Description","u":"entities/the-parasite.html#description","t":"Parasites skitter, rear up and screech, leap at you, and latch onto the back of your neck. A message tells you: \"Something's on the back of your neck - hit it off!\" and then \"It's getting in - crouch to tear it off!\" Parasite Pod texture. Blackwater's specimen notes describe it in two lines: \"The parasite: six legs, a mouth that opens like a flower. It goes for the back of the neck.\" and \"In a host it grows in hours. Then the host splits open and there are more of them.\""},{"p":"The Parasite","h":"Where it came from","u":"entities/the-parasite.html#where-it-came-from","t":"Something came down forty kilometres out at sea. The Blackwater researchers towed what was left of it to their island and built the station round the tank. Its blood doesn't freeze; there are stars in it. On day thirty the cultures took. On day thirty-three the tanks burst. At first the parasites died in seconds anywhere off Blackwater's island. Since 1.43.3 they live anywhere. Ten days after the Bloom dies, the Watcher comes back to tell you where they're really from: the infection in those new places - blackwater - it isn't from here. it came into this realm from another one. the null static zone. they don't need the flower. they'll get into anything with blood in it - a cow, a horse, a villager. ??? ten days later"},{"p":"The Parasite","h":"What it gets into","u":"entities/the-parasite.html#what-it-gets-into","t":""},{"p":"The Parasite","h":"The infected and Parasite Hosts","u":"entities/the-parasite.html#hosts","t":"The staff it got into at Blackwater are Parasite Hosts : hurt one, or let it near you too long, and it convulses and splits open. Parasites also go for the Flesh's infected (the townspeople, police, soldiers, the Laboratory's staff, the shelter's squad, and the Bloaters, Screamers and Brutes they turn into). One gets onto an infected's back and in at the neck while it stands there in a fit; the brood grows out between its shoulder blades over ten seconds, spurs out of its shoulders and neck, beating and lit. Grown, hurt badly or close to you, it heaves and splits open, and two of them come out (one if it was killed before the brood had grown, none if it burnt)."},{"p":"The Parasite","h":"Anything at all","u":"entities/the-parasite.html#anything-at-all","t":"From 1.43.5 to 1.47 a parasite in one of the game's own creatures grew a quick sac on its back and burst out. Since 1.48.0 it doesn't. It takes the creature over, slowly (two days for an ordinary creature, three for the hard ones), and then the creature is theirs. Any creature at all can carry it now: the game's own, the golems, the Warden, the Wither and the dragon, and the Hollow's own things. Only the Flesh's infected still get the old quick brood. Everything about the outbreak, the stages, the turn and what the turned do is on The Turned . What they made of the wolves are Static Hounds . What they made of one villager in every village is the Hollowed ."},{"p":"The Parasite","h":"Its kinds","u":"entities/the-parasite.html#the-kinds","t":"Since 1.48.0, what comes out of something is born of where it was. From Chapter Five they also turn up on their own, now and then, near you: whichever kind lives where you are, up out of the water, down out of the night sky, out of the cave wall, out of the fire."},{"p":"The Parasite","h":"Tide Parasite","u":"entities/the-parasite.html#tide-parasite","t":"In the water, 12 health An eel's body behind the same mouth of five petals, a fin down its back, two hooked forelimbs to hold on with, its spots glowing like the things down there. Fast in the water: it darts at you from a long way off, and holds on down there while you drown. Out of the water it drags itself along."},{"p":"The Parasite","h":"Burrowing Parasite","u":"entities/the-parasite.html#burrowing-parasite","t":"Deep in the stone, 14 health Long and segmented, eight short legs, its petals drawn out into a point like a drill. It goes into the ground in front of you (you hear it coming under your feet, you see the dirt jump) and comes up under you, mouth first."},{"p":"The Parasite","h":"Winged Parasite","u":"entities/the-parasite.html#winged-parasite","t":"Out of anything with wings, 8 health Four long veined wings like a dragonfly's, its legs hanging. You hear it before you see it: a buzz in the dark. It hangs over you, then drops on you mouth open, and holds on."},{"p":"The Parasite","h":"Ember Parasite","u":"entities/the-parasite.html#ember-parasite","t":"The Nether, 12 health Black chitin cracked through with light, like coals, smoke and sparks off it as it runs. Fire doesn't touch it and it walks over lava. What it bites burns. Water hurts it."},{"p":"The Parasite","h":"Void Parasite","u":"entities/the-parasite.html#void-parasite","t":"The End, 10 health Black all through, with stars moving in it, its edges blurred as if it isn't all here. It goes out like a light and is behind you. Hurt it and it's somewhere else. The infested dragon rains these down on you."},{"p":"The Parasite","h":"The biomass and the pure forms","u":"entities/the-parasite.html#the-biomass-and-the-pure-forms","t":"Since 1.49.0, what the parasite is done with it doesn't leave lying there. When one of the turned dies (nearly always one of the hard ones, and four times in ten one of the rest), a heap of violet biomass is left where it fell: veined, pulsing, chitin forced out through it. It drags at you if you wade through it. It isn't dead. A minute or two later, with anyone about, it heaves itself up into one of the parasite's pure forms , and all that's left is its torn husk. Burn it (fire or lava against it) and nothing gets up. The pure forms have no host left in them at all, only the parasite's own flesh grown into the shape it needs. They hunt everything that isn't theirs, what they hit they might put one into, and fire hurts them twice as much. They morph : one folds in on itself, its flesh running like wax, and stands up as something else. A Ranged form when it can see you from far off, a Stalker when you run, a Tank when you're close and hurting it."},{"p":"The Parasite","h":"Stalker Form","u":"entities/the-parasite.html#stalker-form","t":"30 health Low and quick on four legs, its head split three ways. It climbs walls and only comes while you're not looking at it. It pounces from a distance and mauls you close in."},{"p":"The Parasite","h":"Ranged Form","u":"entities/the-parasite.html#ranged-form","t":"30 health Rooted where it stands, a column of flesh as tall as you with a crown of quills. It swells and throws a volley of bone spines at you from a long way off, leading you as you run. Get close and it folds up into something else; lose it long enough and it pulls its roots up to come and find you."},{"p":"The Parasite","h":"Tank Form","u":"entities/the-parasite.html#tank-form","t":"80 health A hulk twice your height with a club of an arm and plates of chitin on its shoulders. It slams the ground, swats you away, grabs you and throws you."},{"p":"The Parasite","h":"Brood Sack","u":"entities/the-parasite.html#brood-sack","t":"16 health A swollen sack on four stumps with things moving under its skin. It waddles up to you, swells and bursts : a handful of parasites out of it. Kill it first and it bursts anyway (unless it burnt)."},{"p":"The Parasite","h":"One of them in you","u":"entities/the-parasite.html#one-of-them-in-you","t":"If a parasite holds on for the whole four seconds, it gets in (\"It's in you.\"). Its brood grows over about three days of play, and a meter beside your hotbar fills. You get hungrier; at a quarter you can feel the others through walls; at two fifths you're stronger and faster; at half the sac shows on your back and has fits; at three quarters it's too big to burn out; full, it tears its way out of your back for 7 hearts, and two of them come out. What you'll read What it means Something moves under your skin. It's started growing. You can feel them now - the others like it, out there. A quarter grown. You can see the parasite's own through walls. It's feeding you too. You feel strong. You feel fast. You're starving. Two fifths. There's a lump between your shoulder blades, and it's warm. Half. Fits start. It's too big to burn out now. Three quarters. Only a Surgical Kit or a Hush now. It's nearly ready. Cut it out. Now. Ninety percent."},{"p":"The Parasite","h":"Getting it out","u":"entities/the-parasite.html#getting-it-out","t":"Surgical Kit: hold it to cut the brood out of yourself; use it on someone else to cut one out of them. It hurts and you bleed. Four uses. Made from shears, an iron ingot, string, paper and wool. It also cuts one out of any creature the parasite is taking over, as long as it hasn't started to turn. Burn it out: stand in fire long enough to be hurt, before it's three quarters grown. \"It's burning in you. Stay in it.\" A Hush: step over the line into one of the Null Static Zone's pale houses and the brood dies. Grown, it tears out of your back as it dies."},{"p":"The Parasite","h":"Pods and resin","u":"entities/the-parasite.html#pods-and-resin","t":"Where they nest they spread their black Xeno Resin over everything, and their pods come up out of it and split open when you come near. Since 1.47.1 a pod is a round egg-sac; split open, it's a torn cup with its four flaps peeled back off the rim and the slime inside. Relay 6 is covered in both."},{"p":"The Parasite","h":"The parasite egg","u":"entities/the-parasite.html#the-parasite-egg","t":""},{"p":"The Parasite","h":"After Signing Off","u":"entities/the-parasite.html#after-signing-off","t":"Since 1.50.0, the Carrier's death didn't end it. Half a minute after you're home from the Null Static Zone the Watcher comes to where you are: it seems the carrier did what it was supposed to do. it carried them - all the way out. the parasites are increasing. every one of them hostile. the numbers are going off the charts. in your world. there's nothing we can do about it for now. just try not to die. for me. in the meantime. ??? after Signing Off From then on the outbreak is worse: the parasite gets into things half again as often, and more of its kinds turn up round you, more of them at once. And the parasite grows itself a mind out in the world: the Chorus , in the Hive ."},{"p":"The Parasite","h":"Advancements","u":"entities/the-parasite.html#advancements","t":"Something Inside , Cut It Out , Burn It Out and It Came Out of Me are all about a brood in you. It Isn't Itself is for being there when something turns. See Advancements ."},{"p":"The Projectionist","h":"","u":"entities/the-projectionist.html","t":"The Watcher's Vault, the Watch Boss Health 900 Came in Behind you, on your ticket Added in 1.57.0, Chapter Six part two: The Watcher's Vault Music The Projectionist Leaves The Projectionist's Lens; also 3 to 5 diamonds, 2 to 4 echo shards and 2 to 4 Vacuum Tubes Behind the Stalls' screen is the Watcher's Vault : his archive, steel shelving going up into the dark, cans of film and boxes of tape on every shelf, and old television sets among them, some still on. The Last Ticket you came in on admitted one. It wasn't you."},{"p":"The Projectionist","h":"The Watch","u":"entities/the-projectionist.html#the-watch","t":"At the far end of the nave is his desk, his chair, and in front of it a wall of sets, thirty-seven across and sixteen high, all showing one picture. this is where i watch from. they watch the picture. i watch them. your world's a show to them. the worse it gets, the more of them come. they left you a ticket. it admits one. not you. something came in behind you. it's come for what i kept. the omni. the carrier. my first reel. get to them before it does. bring them here. ??? The Watch On the wall, the stacks, and in them something tall with a light for a face."},{"p":"The Projectionist","h":"The keeps","u":"entities/the-projectionist.html#the-keeps","t":"Three keeps open off the nave behind round steel doors. Use a door or its wheel and the wheel turns, the bolts draw back one after another (\"The wheel turns. Somewhere in the door, bolts draw back, one after another.\"), and the door swings in. On a plinth in each is what he kept: The Omni's Heart : every colour at once, turning in rings of its own light. \"What made the Omni more than a gun.\" See the Omni . What's Left of the Carrier : a knot of it, still beating, static coming off it like heat. Take it and its static pours out, and every Tuned near you is loose for a few seconds. See the Carrier . His First Reel , in a glass case: a dented film can. On the lid, in his hand: THE OTHER SIDE. FIRST. DO NOT RUN. Taking all three earns What He Kept ."},{"p":"The Projectionist","h":"The Tuned","u":"entities/the-projectionist.html#the-tuned","t":"Standing in the aisles of the stacks: people from the neck down (a cardigan, a shirt done up to the collar, slippers), and where the head should be an old television set, its screen bowed out, static on it. The ones who watched too long; he keeps them in his Vault so they won't watch anything else (24 health each). They only move while you're looking at them . Look at one and it comes for you in jerks, like a picture with frames missing, your face on its screen. Look away and it stops dead, however it was standing, and stays like that. Close, and watched, it takes your head in both hands and tunes you: it hurts, the static comes in at the edges of your eyes, the colour goes out of things, and you can hardly move. Flash an Usher's Lamp at one and its screen whites out: it can't move for four seconds, watched or not. In the dark, or in the Projectionist's light, they move whether you're looking or not. Some of them drop a Vacuum Tube (three times in ten). Two of them, with glass, iron and redstone, make two Old Sets of your own that switch on and off."},{"p":"The Projectionist","h":"The Projectionist","u":"entities/the-projectionist.html#the-projectionist","t":"Bring all three of his things to the Watch and every set on the wall goes to it, and it steps down out of them. Twice the height of a man and thin, in a long coat that's all film, frames on frames of it, hanging to the floor and moving; its hands long and grey; one arm ending in a crank; and for a head a cinema's projector, its housing black and dented, its two reels turning on top, its lens a white light you can't look into. It runs the show, for the ones on the other side."},{"p":"The Projectionist","h":"How it fights","u":"entities/the-projectionist.html#how-it-fights","t":"Beam: its lens's light swept across the Watch. It burns, and while you're in it the Tuned can move whether you look at them or not. Reruns: the old ones, projected onto the air, grey and flickering, doing again the one thing everyone remembers. Where each will strike shows on the floor first. The Hollow Saint : its shadow beam, straight through where you were standing. The Gardener : a ring of thorns out from under your feet. The Deaf King : both fists down, and the ring of it out over the floor. Jump it. The Carrier : its beam, down out of nothing onto where you're standing. Lash: a strip of its film round you, holding you (\"Its film's round you. You can't move.\"). Splice: a jump cut, and it's behind you. Reels: each third gone, it changes its reels. Hit it then: it takes half as much again. Crank (from two thirds down): it cranks itself, and everything it does is twice as fast for a while. Intermission (the last third): the lights go out, every set and every bulb, and there's only its lens. \"Please remain seated.\" Fire doesn't hurt it, and nothing hurts it mid-splice or before it's all the way out of the picture."},{"p":"The Projectionist","h":"How to survive it","u":"entities/the-projectionist.html#how-to-survive-it","t":"Keep the Tuned in front of you, and in sight, when you can. In its beam and in the intermission they come anyway. Watch the floor for where a rerun will land. Save your hardest hits for its reel changes. Bring an Usher's Lamp for the Tuned."},{"p":"The Projectionist","h":"Its end","u":"entities/the-projectionist.html#its-end","t":"Dead, the picture burns through from the middle, as film does stuck in the gate, and what's left of it is its lens . Burning it through earns The Final Reel . The Projectionist's Lens : hold it and every hostile thing near you shows through the walls, outlined in its light. Then the Watcher runs his first reel. The projector on his desk clatters into life: this is the first thing anyone ever saw on the other side. i kept it so i'd never forget what it looks like. that's what i kept out. it's all for that one. the whole show. and now it's seen you. it's coming through. ??? The First Reel A dark so big it has a shape, sat, and an eye in it opening, turning to look at you. Then the Door at the End of the World, its static gone black. Seeing it earns What He Kept Out . What's on the other side is the Viewer ."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"","u":"entities/the-turned.html","t":"From Chapter Five, once the Bloom is dead Hostile to everything Added in 1.48.0 (the outbreak), 1.49.0 (the infested bosses), 1.51.0 and 1.52.0 (the Hollow's own, turned) How long it takes Two days for an ordinary creature, three for the hard ones, on the world's own clock Turned Half as much health again as it had, healed to full Status effect Infested (hidden) Can't carry it You (you get a brood instead: see the Parasite ), the parasite's own, the Flesh's infected (all but its four great ones), the Void's creatures, the Watcher, and the Stalls' Audience, Ushers and Crowd Before 1.48.0 a parasite in a cow grew a quick brood and burst out of it. Now it doesn't. It takes the creature over, slowly, and then the creature is theirs: a ruined, writhing version of what it was, hunting everything that isn't one of them."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"Anything can carry it","u":"entities/the-turned.html#anything-can-carry-it","t":"Any creature at all can carry it: the game's own animals, people and monsters, the golems, the Warden, the Wither and the dragon, and the Hollow's own things. The exceptions are in the case file above. It gets into them in three ways: A parasite gets in. Any of the parasite's kinds that latches on to a creature starts it. A turned one hits it. What the turned hit, they put one into about a third of the time. They can put one into you too, now and then. It's already out there. Once the Bloom is dead, every couple of minutes there's a one-in-three chance that a creature somewhere 24 to 80 blocks from you has one in it, already some way along. After the Watcher's visit following Signing Off it's one in two. The Wither and the dragon can catch it this way too. The Hollow's own creepypastas never do: they only catch it off one of the parasite's own."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"Watch it happen","u":"entities/the-turned.html#watch-it-happen","t":"Stage What you see Incubating Nothing, at first, but a twitch now and then. Spreading The veins come up violet under its skin, and the first blisters on its back. It stops now and then and shakes. Taking hold Growths spread over it, chitin forcing out through its back. Its head hangs over to one side and one leg goes wrong. Its own kind won't go near it. It stands and stares at you. Nearly gone It shakes all the time, and if you're close to it in the dark it goes for you. The turn Five seconds: it seizes up, arches, screams, and tears open. The tendrils come out of it. Everyone within 24 blocks reads: \"The ... isn't itself any more. It's theirs.\" Being there earns It Isn't Itself ."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"Cutting it out","u":"entities/the-turned.html#cutting-it-out","t":"A Surgical Kit used on a creature cuts the parasite out of it any time before it starts to turn (\"You cut it out of the ...\"). The further along it was, the more it hurts the creature. Once it's turning, it's too late."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"Turned","u":"entities/the-turned.html#turned","t":"A turned creature is a ruined, writhing version of what it was: tendrils out of its back, and its chest (or its back) split open into a mouth of five petals round a ring of teeth. Its own mind is gone. It hunts everything that isn't one of them, the way its body lets it. The turned screech when they see you, and every one of them near comes. Village iron golems go for them. Killed, a turned creature bursts and the parasites in it come out. Burn it and nothing does."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"How they fight, by body","u":"entities/the-turned.html#by-body","t":"Body Which What it does Upright Villagers, zombies, illagers, piglins, skeletons, Endermen Lashes you with its tendrils and drags you in, lunges , grabs you and holds you while it bites, mauls . Endermen blink in behind you. On all fours Cows, horses, wolves, bears, goats Stalks you (it only comes while you're not looking at it), charges , pounces, mauls. Small Chickens, rabbits, cats, foxes Fast. It leaps for you, and burrows and comes up under you. Many-legged Spiders, silverfish Leaps, spits bile, burrows. Winged Bats, parrots, bees, phantoms, ghasts, blazes Circles over you and dives . The big ones spit. In the water Fish, squid, dolphins, guardians Rams you and drags you under . A guardian's beam goes bad. A creeper Creepers It's a carrier now: it walks up to you, swells and bursts, and what's in it comes out. The big ones Golems, the Warden, ravagers Slam the ground, lash, pick you up and throw you, charge. The hard ones roar you back and empty a brood of parasites out of themselves."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"What it grows on them","u":"entities/the-turned.html#the-mutations","t":"Since 1.51.0, anything of the game's own that turns grows mutations as it goes over, whatever its body has room for: a ribcage split open on its back like jaws, whips of tendril, feelers, a second head out of its shoulder, mandibles, legs out of its sides, swollen sacs, plates of chitin, a club of it, a cannon of it. A cow, a spider, a villager, a golem, a creeper, a bat, a ghast, a slime, a Warden and the dragon each grow their own. The growths are alive: they breathe with it, twitch, lash about and strike when it strikes, and the tendril it hooks you with reaches all the way out to you. Two moves come with them: Flail (anything upright): its arm gone to tendrils, three lashes in an arc. Strike (anything on four legs): the head grown out of its shoulder lunges. What comes up out of the ground for any of them (spikes, jaws, tendrils, roots) gives a moment's warning: the ground churns first. Move."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"The infested bosses","u":"entities/the-turned.html#the-infested-bosses","t":"The game's bosses and mini-bosses (the hard ones, three days to turn, along with anything that has 80 health or more) fight like what they were, gone wrong. They get their own bar: \"Infested Iron Golem\" and so on."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"Infested Iron Golem","u":"entities/the-turned.html#infested-iron-golem","t":"Still slams, grabs and throws Tears the spines out of its own back and throws them at you in a fan. Impale : its arm driven into the ground and spikes of chitin up through it at you in a line. Harpoon : a barbed tendril out of its chest hooks you, reels you in and hits you."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"Infested Warden","u":"entities/the-turned.html#infested-warden","t":"Its sonic boom gone to rot The boom is a line of rot straight through everything, the dark after it and spores down the length of it. Tremor : it stamps and the ground tears up in rings out from it (jump them). Erupt : the tendrils on its head go down into the ground and come up under you, three times, wherever you've got to."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"Infested Ravager","u":"entities/the-turned.html#infested-ravager","t":"Gores Puts its head down and gores you up into the air. Spray : a cone of bile out of its split head. Devour : its maw clamps on you, shakes you and flings you."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"Infested Elder Guardian","u":"entities/the-turned.html#infested-elder-guardian","t":"Breathes spores A cloud of spores: slow mining, poison, weakness, and it might put one in you. Leech : its tendrils into you, and it drinks and heals. Maelstrom : the water turns round it and everything's dragged in."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"The others","u":"entities/the-turned.html#infested-others","t":"One or two moves each A piglin brute : Frenzy , five blows, coming on. An evoker : Jaws (chitin jaws up out of the ground in a line) and Conjure (fliers out of its robes). A breeze : Gale , a blast of wind thick with spores. A creaking : Snare , roots up round your feet while you're not looking. A sniffer : Uproot , it digs and flings it all at you. A happy ghast : Spores , bile out of the sky."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"Infested Wither","u":"entities/the-turned.html#infested-wither","t":"Keeps how it fights It can carry it (three days, like the rest of the hard ones). Turned, it throws brood skulls (a fan of bile), and tendrils out of its ribs drag you in."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"Infested Ender Dragon","u":"entities/the-turned.html#infested-ender-dragon","t":"Always, since 1.61.1 The dragon is theirs from the first time anyone goes to the End (and any you bring back with the crystals; one already flying in an old world is taken the moment you're there). No days of it, no turn: violet veins under its hide, blisters along its flanks, spurs up its spine, tendrils streaming back off it and its back split open between its wings. Its bar reads \"Infested Ender Dragon\" and it has half as much health again. It still fights as the dragon does, and over you it shudders and rains its brood down out of the sky (void parasites, round where you stand), lobs spore bombs and sweeps its tendrils through you as it comes past low. What its body hits it can put one into. Killed, it bursts."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"The End's Guardian, Taken","u":"entities/the-turned.html#the-ends-guardian-taken","t":"Chapter Ten, 300 health, can't be brought down A creature of its own since 1.71.0, apart from the Infested Ender Dragon: the Ender Dragon, taken, that comes up out of the dark when the First Signal tears his arena up into the End, with the parasite all through it, the hive's now. It circles, strafes and dives, and the hive keeps it going: only he can bring it down. More . After Signing Off the Watcher shuts the End (see chapter five ), so the dragon can't be reached until the seal is broken in chapter six ."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"The Hollow's great ones, turned","u":"entities/the-turned.html#the-great-ones-turned","t":"Since 1.51.0 the parasite can take the Hollow's eight great ones, including the Flesh's four, which it never could before. When one turns, what it was is gone: a whole new body with its own bar, its own voice and a new way of fighting. Its old fight is over (its scripts, its music, its old bar): it hunts."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"The Saint Unmade","u":"entities/the-turned.html#the-saint-unmade","t":"Was the Hollow Saint It drags itself on tentacles, hunched, its chest a mouth the height of it, its head split open like a book, a scythe of chitin for one arm and whips for the other. Choir (every face it wore screams at once: it throws you back and puts out the light), Devour (the whips round you, into the mouth, chewed and spat out), Reap (the scythe), Field (tendrils up out of the ground under you and all round you), Halo (its broken halo's pods burst, bile raining down), Surge (it throws itself at you across the ground)."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"The Mended, Unstitched","u":"entities/the-turned.html#the-mended-unstitched","t":"Was the Mended What holds the nine together now is the parasite. Hook (its chain is a tendril: the barb in you, hauled in to the scythe), Burst (every seam splits at once), Claws , Wings (Mothman's wings thrown open: every eye on them on you, the dark, the gust), Pounce ."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"The Gardener, Overgrown","u":"entities/the-turned.html#the-gardener-overgrown","t":"Was the Gardener Roots (they come up round your feet and hold you), Lash (its arm of root, the barb dragging you in), Bloom (the flower where its face was breathes out its spores), Harvest (the rusted shears, twice), Seeds (the pods on its hat burst, and spikes come up where they land)."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"The Reborn, Consumed","u":"entities/the-turned.html#the-reborn-consumed","t":"Was the Gardener, Reborn Clamp (the frill of jaws round its head closes on you and chews), Dance (round and round, both scythes out), Volley (petals of the frill thrown in a fan), Pollen (the dark, and weak), Hooklash (the tentacle arm, the hook in you, and in you come)."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"The Broodmother, Hollowed","u":"entities/the-turned.html#the-broodmother-hollowed","t":"Was the Broodmother It never moves from where it grew. Its roots are tentacles, its petals jaws of chitin, the woman on top split open down the middle. Snap (the petals snap shut on whatever's among them), Sweep (the tentacles sweep the ground all round it, twice), Birth (its brood drops out of the mouth down its front, the parasite's brood now), Geyser (bile raining down all round), Reach (her arms reach a long way for you and drag you in among the petals)."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"Specimen Zero, Unbound","u":"entities/the-turned.html#specimen-zero-unbound","t":"Was Specimen Zero Off the pool floor for good, up on six legs like a spider's, Reyes bent forward off the front of it, his arms folded like a mantis's into blades of bone, his head hanging upside down off a stretched neck. Scythe (the blades, one and then the other), Cables (into the floor and up under you and anyone with you), Leap , Absorb (his chest opens, the tongue reaches out, everything near is dragged in, and what it gets it eats: it heals), Vomit (the pool, sprayed), Skitter (round you, quick, and a bite from the side). Fire still burns it twice as hard."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"The Warden, Unhoused","u":"entities/the-turned.html#the-warden-unhoused","t":"Was the Warden of Shelter No. 4 Its four heads up on long necks, a mouth down the whole front of the mound, six arms out of its sides, the warden on top hollowed into a chimney. Hydra (the heads strike one after another), Embrace (the arms close round everything against it and squeeze), Roll (it balls up and rolls straight at you till it hits something), Chimney (spores pour out and rain down round you in clouds), Grasp (its arms go into the floor and come up under you, holding on), Maw (the mouth opens the whole height of it, and it lunges)."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"The Congregation, Gutted","u":"entities/the-turned.html#the-congregation-gutted","t":"Was the Congregation It's opened the bus up: ribs arching over it where the roof was, a heart the size of a car under them, its front a mouth of four flaps round a throat ringed with teeth, and it runs on all their legs like a centipede. Lamprey (it lunges, holds you in its mouth, chews and spits you out), Stampede (straight on over anything till something stops it), Ribs (they open out and slam down either side of it), Windows (the tentacles out of every window lash out and drag in whatever's beside it), Hymn (every mouth sings: slow, weak, the dark at the edges), Spill (its doors burst and parasites spill out). Get under it and you're trampled."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"The rest of the Hollow's own, turned","u":"entities/the-turned.html#the-rest-turned","t":"In 1.52.0 every one of the Hollow's own that the parasite could get into got a form of its own: twenty-four more. (Things added after that, like the Listener, the Deaf King and the Tuned, have no turned form.) When one turns, what it was is gone (a whole new body, its own voice, four moves of its own), and its old ways are over (its hiding, its tricks, its scripts). It hunts. The big ones' names go on their bars."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"The Neighbor, Inside Out","u":"entities/the-turned.html#the-neighbor-inside-out","t":"Was the Hollow Neighbor Split down the front and peeled open, and out of his neck the thing that wore him, long, raw and eyeless, his own head hanging slack off his back. Behind You (gone, and there, behind you), Needles (his fingers), Knock (a blow that throws everything near back), Hug (it holds you, and squeezes)."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"Stitchjaw, Unsewn","u":"entities/the-turned.html#stitchjaw-unsewn","t":"Was Stitchjaw Every stitch burst, on eight limbs that were arms and legs, a jaw at each end. Tear , Thread (shot into you, and you're reeled in), Pounce , Split (it opens and spins)."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"The Shepherd, Flockless","u":"entities/the-turned.html#the-shepherd-flockless","t":"Was the Weeping Shepherd What it found of its flock grown into its back, every mouth open; its crook a hook of bone. Bleat (every head at once: the dark, and slow), Crook (round you and hauled in), Tears (black ones, thrown), Flock (what's left of it drops off its back, parasites now)."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"The Mother, Unborn","u":"entities/the-turned.html#the-mother-unborn","t":"Was the Lullaby Mother Tall, her arms to the ground, her head hanging off a bent neck, something curled up in the sac of her belly. Cradle (she holds you), Lullaby (slow and weak), Swaddle (roots round your feet), Born (the sac bursts)."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"Broadcast, Dead Air","u":"entities/the-turned.html#broadcast-dead-air","t":"Was Broadcast The set's cables gone into his spine, something pushing out through the cracked screen. Skipped Frame (he's next to you), Static (a burst all round), Signal (a beam off the screen: the dark), Cable (his arm of it lashed round you, reeling you in)."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"The Lamb, Shorn","u":"entities/the-turned.html#the-lamb-shorn","t":"Was the Little Lamb Long and thin on limbs like a spider's, its jaw split open. Latch (on you, gnawing), Cry , Scurry , Tongue (it reaches you and drags you in)."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"The Hymnal, Unbound","u":"entities/the-turned.html#the-hymnal-unbound","t":"Was the Hymnal A ribcage full of singing mouths, its pages grown out of its back. Hymn , Chorale (every mouth at once: a blast), Psalm (a beam of it), Pages (thrown like blades)."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"The Underneath, Unearthed","u":"entities/the-turned.html#the-underneath-unearthed","t":"Was the Underneath Out of the ground for good, on six arms, a hand for a head with a mouth in its palm. Claw , Drag , Hands (up out of the ground under you), Down (into the ground, and up under you)."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"Antlerkin, Velvet-Torn","u":"entities/the-turned.html#antlerkin-velvet-torn","t":"Was the Antlerkin On four legs, the deer's skull split open on a bulb of eyes, its antlers a crown of bone. Gore (and tossed), Rack (swung round), Charge , Call (slow, the dark)."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"The Bunnyman, Unstuffed","u":"entities/the-turned.html#the-bunnyman-unstuffed","t":"Was the Bunnyman Flesh where the stuffing was, a skull in the split plush head with incisors as long as fingers, the axe grown into his hand. Incisors , Chops , Hop , Hatchets (thrown)."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"The Hookman, Unchained","u":"entities/the-turned.html#the-hookman-unchained","t":"Was the Hookman A starved giant, a round mouth of hooked teeth, tendrils with a hook on every one. Sweep (low: slow), Drive (the hooks driven in), Hooks (thrown, and you're hauled in), Whirl ."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"The Hogshead, Rendered","u":"entities/the-turned.html#the-hogshead-rendered","t":"Was the Hogshead Bloated, two more pigs' heads out of his shoulders, the cleaver grown out of his arm. Cleaver , Fists (both, down), Squeal (all three: weak and slow), Charge ."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"The Porcelain Man, Shattered","u":"entities/the-turned.html#the-porcelain-man-shattered","t":"Was the Porcelain Man His glaze broken away in plates, a real eye behind his painted face, the music box in his chest a mouth, shards of him hanging round his shoulders. Burst (shards every way), There (when you look back), Shards (thrown), Music Box (slow, the dark)."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"The Harvestman, Gone to Seed","u":"entities/the-turned.html#the-harvestman-gone-to-seed","t":"Was the Harvestman Roots trailing out of its sleeves, its sack of a head bursting with pods, a scythe and a sickle. Reap , Thresh , Seeds (spikes up where they land), Chaff (clouds of it)."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"Mothman, Pupated","u":"entities/the-turned.html#mothman-pupated","t":"Was Mothman Wings of skin covered in red eyes, a cocoon on its back. Snatch (up into the air, and dropped), Dive , Dust (off its wings: the dark, slow), Gaze (every eye on you: weak, the dark)."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"The Jersey Devil, Hatched","u":"entities/the-turned.html#the-jersey-devil-hatched","t":"Was the Jersey Devil Something half out of its chest, crawling out. Hooves , Tail (poison), Breath (fire and bile), Glide ."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"Dogman, Unleashed","u":"entities/the-turned.html#dogman-unleashed","t":"Was Dogman On all fours, its jaw split three ways, its ribs a mouth, a second pair of arms. Ribs (the mouth in them closes on you), Maul , Pounce , Howl (you can't move, and the dark)."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"The Flatwoods Monster, Hooded","u":"entities/the-turned.html#the-flatwoods-monster-hooded","t":"Was the Flatwoods Monster Its hood opened into a flower of flesh round the cracked red lamp of its face. Claws , Lift , Mist , Beam ."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"The Rootling, Bloomed","u":"entities/the-turned.html#the-rootling-bloomed","t":"Was a Rootling Its head burst into a flower of teeth, running on its roots. Leap , Thorns , Scream , Down and Up ."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"The Great Flower, Overrun","u":"entities/the-turned.html#the-great-flower-overrun","t":"Was the Great Flower Its petals crusted with eyes, the parasite's tendrils up out of its throat. Petals (slammed down), Throat (everything near dragged in), Tendrils (up out of the ground), Spores ."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"The Flytrap, Ravenous","u":"entities/the-turned.html#the-flytrap-ravenous","t":"Was a Giant Flytrap Taller, a second trap lower down, its leaves toothed. Snap , Swallow , Leaves (lashed round), Spit (what it's digesting)."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"The Mourner, Unveiled","u":"entities/the-turned.html#the-mourner-unveiled","t":"Was a Mourner The death-mask hanging off a column of flesh with a mouth down it, its sleeves tentacles. Toll , Sleeves (reaching: weak), Grief (slow and weak), Shroud (clouds)."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"The Interred, Unwound","u":"entities/the-turned.html#the-interred-unwound","t":"Was an Interred Its shroud coming off in strips that move on their own, its jaw down to its chest. Bite (hungry), Linen (whirled), Rot (poison, hunger), Bound (roots round your feet)."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"The Pod, Hatched","u":"entities/the-turned.html#the-pod-hatched","t":"Was a Spore Pod Split open like a mouth, up on six tendrils. Latch , Burst , Spit , Rooted . Names as they appear in the game. Each form has its own model, animations, death, sounds and HD texture."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"Testing it","u":"entities/the-turned.html#testing-it","t":"With cheats on: /statichollow ending infest (the nearest creature has one in it), infest25 , infest50 , infest75 and infest95 (that far along), infestturn (it turns now), infestall (everything within 24 blocks turns), infestinfo and infestcure . For one of the Hollow's own, spawn it from its egg first, then infest and infestturn ."},{"p":"The Undertow","h":"","u":"entities/the-undertow.html","t":"The Dead Water, the Black Below Can't be hurt Size Three thousand blocks long. Its head a hundred and twenty blocks long, its body fifty across. Health Nothing hurts it. Added in 1.63.0; made far bigger in 1.63.2; stalks, learns and feeds since 1.63.3; glows, and stalks where you can see it, since 1.63.5 Lives The Black Below: the void past the edge of the Dead Water, about 3000 blocks out (since 1.63.5) Became The Harbinger , in Chapter Nine How to live Get back over the edge. Then it lets you go and sinks back into the depths."},{"p":"The Undertow","h":"Description","u":"entities/the-undertow.html#description","t":"The Dead Water is laid out like one sea: the rig in the middle, a ring of the shallow waters round it, a ring of the deeper ones round that. About 3000 blocks out the floor slopes down to the edge of everything and falls away: the Black Below , the void, all the way round, for ever. Nothing lives out there but one thing (and the lost whales that wander out into it, and the Omenfry ). Down there there's only the sound of the ocean. The void is the Undertow's. Go out over it at all, swimming, in ORPHEUS, in a boat on top of it, and stay, and it comes (sooner the deeper you are). Get back over the edge and it lets you go. Its head is a long armoured skull with heavy brows over nine pale glowing eyes down each side (two of them great and milky), horns sweeping back off it, broken bone spikes down its back and flanks, a torn crimson crest, and six long jointed feelers trailing under it. Its mouth is a ring of lips round a hole going down into it, with six long jaws round that, fanged all down their insides, their edges serrated and a hook at each tip. They shut to a point like a closed flower, and open out to show three rings of teeth grinding round against one another down its throat, and a sick red light at the bottom. It never breaks a block: it goes through rock like water. Since 1.63.5 you can see it in the dark, shaders or not: lines of cold light run the length of its body down both flanks, with a chevron of light over its back every twenty blocks, and slow waves of brightness roll down it from head to tail. Its eyes glow, ringed in cold light, and stay on you. Since 1.63.24 they're round and wet: a dark, veined ball in each socket, the iris on it cold and pale and lit from inside with a slit of a pupil down it, turning to follow you, with lids round each that blink, each on its own (the great ones seldom). Since 1.63.25 it's drawn wherever you are along it, from five hundred blocks off."},{"p":"The Undertow","h":"It stalks you","u":"entities/the-undertow.html#it-stalks-you","t":"Stay out over the void and something notices, a rumble from below (\"Something vast is keeping pace with you, out in the dark.\"). It rises out of the dark and stalks you, keeping pace. Since 1.63.5 it stalks where you can see it : it keeps off one shoulder, close; every half minute or so it slides up into the corner of your eye and holds there, its eyes on you, and drops back; and soon after it finds you it makes a pass right under you, to your other side. You can't see thirty blocks down there, but you can see its eyes : a cluster of pale cold points out in the black, two great ones among them, that turn as you turn and keep on you."},{"p":"The Undertow","h":"It learns you","u":"entities/the-undertow.html#it-learns-you","t":"The longer it watches, the closer and lower it keeps. Run for the surface a few times and it learns to wait right under where you'll come back down. Carry a light for a while and it learns to keep out of it. It tells you, in the dark, as it learns: \"It has learned how you move.\" \"It saw you run for the surface. It will be waiting under you.\" \"It has learned your light. It keeps out of it.\" \"It knows you now.\" What it learns, it keeps."},{"p":"The Undertow","h":"It eats when it's hungry","u":"entities/the-undertow.html#it-eats-when-its-hungry","t":"Its hunger grows while it's out, and stays between its comings (\"It is hungry.\"), though what it brings with it from last time is capped, so it always stalks a while before it comes for you. Only when it's starving does it roar and come for you. Before that, if a whale is near, it eats the whale instead. Lost whales (Hymnbacks) come out of the dark within ten seconds or so of you going out over the void, at your depth, and keep near you, singing; the reef on a lost whale's back glows warm, with a row of small lights down each flank, so you see them coming. When the Undertow comes there's always a whale about, and it goes for the whale first. A hungry Undertow hunts them: it swings round, lunges, takes the whale crossways in its jaws and chews, the whale thrashing and crying, blood clouding the water, the rings of teeth in its throat grinding, then swallows it whole. Fed (\"It has fed. For now.\"), it goes back to watching you. A whale near when it's starving can save you."},{"p":"The Undertow","h":"When it comes","u":"entities/the-undertow.html#when-it-comes","t":"Roar: it shakes the sea. A submarine's glass cracks and its power dies; your ears ring. Circle and lunge: it circles, then comes straight in, jaws opening like a flower, and swallows you whole , a submarine and all. Nothing comes back out (\"... was swallowed by the Undertow\"). Breach: run for the surface and it comes up after you, straight up out of the sea, hundreds of blocks into the sky with the length of it pouring up out of the water after it, arcs over and crashes back down in a column of water. The waves run out over the sea and throw everything floating about, and smash boats. It can take you on the way up. It goes back down into the depths only when you get back over the edge."},{"p":"The Undertow","h":"How to survive it","u":"entities/the-undertow.html#how-to-survive-it","t":"Don't stay out over the void. Get in, get what you came for, get back over the edge. Watch for its eyes in the black. If they're turning with you, it's there. Change how you move. It learns the surface run and a carried light. Hymnbacks are your friends down there: a fed Undertow goes back to watching."},{"p":"The Undertow","h":"The Turning","u":"entities/the-undertow.html#the-turning","t":"Once ORPHEUS has all three of her modules, it comes up out of the sea by the rig and roars, and goes: down through the roof of the Grove's hollow to eat the Grove Heart , and through the Drowned Heart in the Haemal Reach. With both in it, it turns, the Grove's fungus up one side and the Reach's flesh up the other, comes back mad, and lies down by the rig: the husk, its eyes shut. Three days later what's in it comes out. From then on nothing comes up out of the Black Below. The Watcher never made it: \"i made this place. every wreck, every fish in it. not that - i don't know how it got in here.\" See the Harbinger ."},{"p":"The Undertow","h":"The spawn egg","u":"entities/the-undertow.html#the-spawn-egg","t":"The Undertow Spawn Egg (creative) hatches one that stalks you, its eyes on you, now and then turning its head to roar with its jaws wide, and hunts and eats any whale near (hatch a Hymnback or two and watch). It never eats you. It's gone after ten minutes, or once you go far away."},{"p":"The Undertow","h":"The Static Leviathan","u":"entities/the-undertow.html#the-static-leviathan","t":"The Hadal Dark and the Trench; deep in the Dead Water Boss Health 320, with its own bar Size Forty-five blocks long (since 1.63.2) Drops The Signal Organ, 3 to 6 bone blocks, 2 to 5 Needle Teeth and a heart of the sea Grey-blue plated hide, a blunt skull with little red eyes clustered down it, and fangs where its baleen was, hanging outside its jaw even when it's shut, with tusks and teeth in its lower jaw. Down its back a row of thin masts, a red light blinking at each one's tip one after another like the lights on a radio mast at night, and bone spines between them. Its ribs show through the rotted-away hide of its flanks; lamp-organs pulse down them. It roams the deepest water of the Overworld's oceans (the Trench, and the Hadal Dark now and then; see the deep oceans ). In the Dead Water, deep down, now and then one comes up out of the dark after you, except in the Black Below, which is the Undertow's. Song: a numbers station, slowed down and sung through a throat the size of a room, on the Remote's frequency. Everything near goes dark and slow while it sings. Charge: it slows, turns, its throat dropping open, then charges. Whatever it hits, it hits like a ship. Swallow: sometimes it takes you in. You're in its throat in the dark, being crushed, until you hurt it enough from in there to make it spit you out, or it does anyway. Its Signal Organ is what mends the Broken Remote in Chapter Eight (\"Mend it: this, a Static Leviathan's Signal Organ, a copper ingot.\"). Doing it earns Back On Air ."},{"p":"The Undertow","h":"The Mouth of the Floor","u":"entities/the-undertow.html#the-mouth-of-the-floor","t":"Buried in the Grey Shelf, the Ossuary Flats and the Molar Reef Ambusher Health 140, armoured Size Jaws eleven blocks long, thirty blocks across open (since 1.63.2) Drops 2 to 5 Needle Teeth, 2 to 6 bones and a Shroud Hide Something lies buried in the sea floor, with nothing of it showing but a ring of rocks (the tips of its jaws, crusted over like the floor) and, if you look close, a few yellow eyes in the silt between them. Pass over it and the floor shudders, and it comes up: eight jaws open out of the sand round a throat going down into the dark, with hooked teeth all down them, serrated edges and a fang at each tip, two rings of teeth round its throat and twelve yellow eyes round its rim. Four hooked tongues coiled down its throat rise and writhe as it opens. The water rushes in, and you with it, and it snaps shut and holds on, grinding, its tongues coiled round you. Then it spits out what's left and sinks back into the floor. It takes a submarine in its jaws too, and crushes it. It can only be hurt while it's up. Hurt it hard enough while it holds you and it lets go. A submarine's sonar shows where one lies."},{"p":"The Viewer","h":"","u":"entities/the-viewer.html","t":"The Other Side, past the edge of the stage The last boss Health 1024, but it can't be killed What you fight Its eye and its hands. The rest of it is too big. Added in 1.58.0, Chapter Six part three: What He Kept Out Music What He Kept Out Status effect Seen: the edges of everything going white"},{"p":"The Viewer","h":"Description","u":"entities/the-viewer.html#description","t":"Through the Door at the End of the World, its static gone black, is the Other Side : a stage behind the screen your world is on. Out in the dark past the stage's edge, sat, is something so big the dark has its shape: knees like hills, shoulders up in the black, a head you can't see the top of, its hands on the stage's edge with fingers like felled trees, and an eye . It's watched your world since the first picture anyone ever saw. Now it's seen you, and it wants to see you up close. The Watcher is there before you, at a projector. you came through. good. it hasn't looked this way. not yet. this is the other side. it's watched your world since the first picture. everything that ever happened to you - it watched. now it wants to see you up close. stay out of its eye. get behind the scenery. when it leans in - hit it. i'll run the projector. ??? Curtain Up"},{"p":"The Viewer","h":"Its gaze","u":"entities/the-viewer.html#its-gaze","t":"Its gaze wanders the stage, a pool of its light drifting toward whoever is out in the open. Stand in it with its eye in sight of you and you're Seen : the edges of everything go white, more and more. Seen right through, it reaches for you. A painted flat between you and the eye hides you. The stage is dressed with them, each a picture of somewhere from your story. Getting through the first third without ever being seen right through earns Out of Sight ."},{"p":"The Viewer","h":"How it fights","u":"entities/the-viewer.html#how-it-fights","t":"Lean: its head comes down out of the dark to the stage's edge, the eye right there. That's when to hit it: it takes half as much again. Slam: a hand lifted over you (its shadow on the boards first) and brought down. Jump the ring. Drum: its fingers along the front of the stage, one after another. Grab: it lifts you up in front of its eye (\"It's got you. It's looking right at you. (Hit the hand!)\"). Hit the hand and it lets go. Sweep (from two thirds down): a hand dragged low across the stage, through the scenery. Jump it. The flats it hits, or slams, are smashed to splinters. With its eye shut, nothing hurts it. Hit a hand and it feels half of it. Fire does nothing."},{"p":"The Viewer","h":"Stand-ins","u":"entities/the-viewer.html#stand-ins","t":"Cut-outs of people (a man in a hat, a woman in a coat, an usher), painted plywood on little hinged stands, their backs bare boards and a strut (10 health). They come hopping out of the wings the way scenery is moved across a stage. They don't hurt you: they find you. One that sees you swings its arm up on its split pin and points , and the eye comes straight to you. Knock them over."},{"p":"The Viewer","h":"His Last Projector","u":"entities/the-viewer.html#his-last-projector","t":"The Watcher runs it from the stage (\"His. He'll run it.\"). Twice he loads it: At two thirds: the Omni's Heart in its lamp. Every colour at once, thrown out over the dark into its eye. It reels , blinded: hit it then and it takes double. That earns Every Colour at Once . At one third: the Carrier through its gate. Your world, all of it, carried out on the beam onto it. The stand-ins burn, and it gets up . Stood, its gaze is quicker and its hands come more often, the footlights flicker and go out, and it reaches for the projector with both hands from either side. Beat them back. Being there earns It Gets Up ."},{"p":"The Viewer","h":"How to survive it","u":"entities/the-viewer.html#how-to-survive-it","t":"Move from flat to flat. Don't stand in its light with the eye in view. Knock the stand-ins over before they point. Hit the eye when it leans in, and hit it hard while it reels. In the last third, guard the projector: hit the hands that reach for it. If you fall off the edge, the dark puts you back on the boards (\"The dark doesn't keep you. You're back on the boards - it hurt.\")."},{"p":"The Viewer","h":"The last show","u":"entities/the-viewer.html#the-last-show","t":"It can't be killed. At the last it's held : it stops, and its eye goes to the projector. The Watcher threads his first reel and runs it, for it. everyone's always watched it. nobody ever showed it to itself. there. something to watch. it'll watch that forever. it won't look at your world again. somebody has to run the projector. go home. ...thank you for watching. ??? The Last Show Its own picture, on it. It goes still, sits back, and watches itself. The credits roll, you're sent home (the black door is static again), and you're given a record, Thank You for Watching . Seeing it earns the advancement of the same name. Chapter Six is done. The credits roll to their last line and stop. \"...not yet.\" His hand comes up through them and shuts round you. That's Chapter Seven ."},{"p":"The Watcher","h":"","u":"entities/the-watcher.html","t":"Shown in game as ??? Never attacks Name in game ??? (its spawn egg is the \"??? Spawn Egg\") First seen The main menu; in the world, once the Forsaken Altar is awake Where Anywhere. At the edge of the trees, on the cathedral ceiling, right behind you Bleeds Never What it wants Stronger souls to pour its darkness through. It kept the Omni's heart, what was left of the Carrier and its own first reel \"for the future\", and used them to keep something out of your world. \"remember who you work for.\""},{"p":"The Watcher","h":"Description","u":"entities/the-watcher.html#description","t":"As it stands on the main menu. A tall, thin black figure with a square head and two pale eyes that glow and blink. The game names it only \"???\". It never attacks you. It stares, waves, points, peeks round things, crouches, and sometimes stands right behind you. It is in every chapter, and at every turning point it says a few words in chat in lower case. On the main menu it is somewhere different every time lightning strikes: far off on the hill, then among the graves, then right at the edge of the trees, then gone."},{"p":"The Watcher","h":"What it does, chapter by chapter","u":"entities/the-watcher.html#what-it-does","t":""},{"p":"The Watcher","h":"The Nine","u":"entities/the-watcher.html#in-chapter-one","t":"It speaks after your first, fifth and ninth kill (it stares, then waves, then points), and after the ninth tells you about a church that isn't on any map. It hangs from the ceiling of the cathedral's nave. When the Hollow Saint reaches half health, it turns to it, a black sun swelling between its hands, and pours a crackling river of shadow into the Saint's heart. When the Saint dies its beam turns red and burns a portal to hell open under it. At midnight the cathedral's bell tolls thirteen, and on the thirteenth the Watcher is standing in the doorway."},{"p":"The Watcher","h":"The Breach","u":"entities/the-watcher.html#in-chapter-two","t":"It meets you on the other side of the Breach, stands behind the Breach Altar to tell you what comes next, and waits on the ceiling of the Trophy Hall. When the nine heads are on their pedestals it comes down and sews them into the Mended, pouring its shadow into the knot."},{"p":"The Watcher","h":"The Glasshouse","u":"entities/the-watcher.html#in-chapter-three","t":"It warns you about the Bloom's air, and begs you to leave the Binding alone."},{"p":"The Watcher","h":"The Flesh","u":"entities/the-watcher.html#in-chapter-four","t":"It tells you what the Flesh is and how to kill it. Once the Gardener, Reborn is dead it walks to the shut Bloom, pushes its fingers between the petals and tears it open, and holds the rift open while you launch the Device. It wanted the Bloom to change: \"a soul that size is worth something.\" It pours itself into the Orbital Core, builds the Device or the Ray Gun for you at a Forsaken Altar if you ask, and turns the Ray Gun into the Omni. When the Omni Ray needs more power, it gives all of its own. Then it takes the Omni back into its realm and burns the Ray Gun's recipe. Ten days later it comes back, rested, and finds you wherever you are: at your window, down your mine, behind a tree, behind you. Anything in a mine trying to kill you, it lifts, twitching, and bursts into ink."},{"p":"The Watcher","h":"The Static","u":"entities/the-watcher.html#in-chapter-five","t":"It hands out needles to Relay 6 and the Starlite, stands beside you during the late show to explain the Afterimages, and when the Carrier dies it takes its eye \"for the future\" and sends everyone home through a rift of its own. Half a minute after you're home it comes to where you're standing. It wasn't meant to go like this: the Carrier carried them all the way out, and the parasite's numbers are going off the charts. It shuts the End so you can't go there (anyone who goes through an End portal in survival is sent straight back out: \"not there. i told you.\"), and lets you know it can see you: ...actually. i'll make sure you can't go there. it's dangerous for you, player. you know i can see you right now, right, (your name)? remember who you work for. ??? after Signing Off After It Speaks it's beside you, and hands you its needle to the Hive. When the Chorus runs it tells you to keep the fragment and listen to it. When the Chorus, Whole is dead it tells you about the door at the end of the world: \"there's a door at the end of the world with a seal on it. i made that seal. i can't open it.\" / \"that voice can. when you're ready, take it to the end.\""},{"p":"The Watcher","h":"The Door at the End of the World","u":"entities/the-watcher.html#in-chapter-six","t":"Carry the Last Voice into the End and the seal it made breaks. It says one word: \"...don't.\" In the Stalls, when the Crowd is dead, it's sitting in the front row: \"it was a good show.\" It tears the screen open and goes through. Behind it is its Vault, its archive, where it sits at a desk under a wall of sets and watches the ones who watch your world: \"this is where i watch from.\" When the Projectionist is dead it runs its first reel and shows you what it kept out. On the Other Side it runs its last projector, loads the Omni's heart and the Carrier into it, and at the end runs its first reel for the Viewer, so that it will watch itself forever and never look at your world again. \"somebody has to run the projector.\" Then the credits roll."},{"p":"The Watcher","h":"The First Signal","u":"entities/the-watcher.html#in-chapter-seven","t":"At the end of the credits: \"...not yet.\" Its hand comes up through them and takes you to the Hub, a realm it made. \"i made it. a realm. it isn't mine - nothing is - but i made it.\" It thanks you, tells you it could wipe you out and find another one of you, and that it can make realms now, \"all thanks to you\". Then the First Signal breaks in. It tries to push the rift shut, shoves the First Signal five hundred blocks with everything it has, tells you to jump, and shuts the realm behind you with a wall of static. See the First Signal ."},{"p":"The Watcher","h":"The Dead Water","u":"entities/the-watcher.html#in-chapter-eight","t":"Falling, it tears a portal open under you and brings you down on an oil rig in a dead green sea: \"i built this place a long time ago - for when i needed somewhere to hide.\" It gives you the Remote, and it breaks in your hand: \"...no. nothing of mine works right here.\" It tells you to fix it (\"the big ones down there sing on its frequency - cut out what they sing with\"), hands you its chart of the sea, and goes over the rail. See Chapter Eight . Since 1.63.21 it's there at the bottom, straight down from where it went into the sea: curled up, asleep, floating in a bubble of its own static, a faint light round it in the dark. Nothing gets into the bubble (it gives a little, then pushes you back out), and nothing you swing at it, throw at it or fire at it gets through. It doesn't wake."},{"p":"The Watcher","h":"The Harbinger","u":"entities/the-watcher.html#in-chapter-nine","t":"It wakes when the Undertow comes down by the rig at the end of the Turning: its bubble breaks, and it comes up out of the sea onto the helipad beside you. \"...what the hell is happening?\" It never made that, and doesn't know how it got in; it tells you what's in it now and that you have to kill it. For the three days it keeps watch at the helipad's rail, with something to say each day. When the Harbinger has gone through its way out: \"pick it up. put it in your remote.\" / \"i'll meet you at the hub.\" See the Harbinger ."},{"p":"The Watcher","h":"Stay Tuned","u":"entities/the-watcher.html#in-chapter-ten","t":"In the Broadcast's last part your door bangs open (the nearest door to where you are), and it's there, out of breath. With no door near you it comes out of the static somewhere it can stand (since 1.72.1: room for all of it, about level with you, nothing between you). do you feel that? it's everywhere. all over the world, all at once. that much signal - all of it his. get ready. ??? at your door Then it stays at your house: anything of his that comes near it, it strikes down. A Lookalike can fool it, and Lookalikes copy it too: on a night of THE IMPOSTORS something knocks at your door wearing the Watcher."},{"p":"The Watcher","h":"The Last Broadcast","u":"entities/the-watcher.html#in-the-last-broadcast","t":"At the Coronation it tears its way through after you, \"i couldn't let you come here alone.\", and walks up to him with you, and when his arena comes up out of the sea: \"stay behind me. i've nothing left to fight him with - but what i have is yours.\" It stands by the arena's gate with no power of its own, and every so often gives each of you on the floor thirty seconds of something at its strongest. When he takes the light of his towers into him it's on its knees (\"no... he's taking it. all of it. mine too.\"), and it takes out the Omni : \"then i'll call down something bigger.\" It fires it up into the sky, and SENTINEL comes through. After the Fall it fires the Omni into him every half-minute or so, putting him down on one knee, in his arena and in the End. At the Second Rite it lets the Omni fall and gets up off its knees: \"the End was never yours.\" It catches his blade and puts a beam of shadow into his heart: \"i've watched you since the first night. i know what you are.\" When his Faithful take him into their seal: \"...they took him. somewhere even i can't see.\" / \"go home. while there's still a home to go to.\" Then it sends you home. See the First Signal ."},{"p":"The Watcher","h":"The seasons","u":"entities/the-watcher.html#the-seasons","t":"With Serene Seasons in the modpack (since 1.62.0), it notices each season turn the first time it does. In autumn: \"the leaves are turning. this was always their time of year. you'll hear them more now.\" In winter: \"it's getting cold. keep a fire going. they like the cold. it carries sound further.\""},{"p":"The Watcher","h":"More than one Watcher","u":"entities/the-watcher.html#the-watchers","t":"The Watcher can be in more than one place at once. While the Saint changes, the one on the cathedral ceiling pours its beam, and away from the cathedral another Watcher steps out of nothing somewhere it can see the Saint from. The README also calls that the \"Watchers' beam\"."},{"p":"The Watcher","h":"Its places","u":"entities/the-watcher.html#its-realm","t":"When it takes the Omni back it tears the air open: a rift into its own realm, green fire licking up the edges, rings of its glyphs turning round it. It throws the gun in and the rift slams shut. Since Chapter Six you can go to some of its places yourself: The Watcher's Vault , behind the picture: its archive of film and tape, the Watch, and three keeps where it kept the Omni's heart, what was left of the Carrier and its first reel. The seal on the End and the Door at the End of the World , made of its black seal-stone with its glyphs cut in it. The Hub , a realm it made out of the First Signal's static. The rig in the Dead Water , built long ago for when it needed somewhere to hide. \"i made this place. every wreck, every fish in it.\" (Not the Undertow.)"},{"p":"The Watcher","h":"The Watcher says","u":"entities/the-watcher.html#the-watcher-says","t":"the soul in the core... i needed one that strong. it's mine now. that was the price. go home. the hollow will be quiet for a while. ??? at the end of the railgun ending the static was a door. and this was holding it open. this, i'll keep. for the future. ??? taking the Carrier's eye i think we'll be fighting forever. until one day i'm strong enough to bring you up to my level. ??? in the Hub Every line it says is collected on The Watcher speaks ."},{"p":"Tune-In Town's cast","h":"","u":"entities/tune-in-town-cast.html","t":"Tune-In Town's show went out live on Channel 6 every Saturday from its own stage, its cast of animatronics running off reel-to-reel showtapes, till the Saturday the tape played HIM. It shut. Now he's opening it again. These are the twelve in Studio B , each with its own model, walk, tricks, jumpscare and death. Tune-In Town is a secret Easter egg, and its night shift has flashing lights, flickering screens, loud noises and jumpscares. The game warns you before you're hired. Studio B, through the STAFF ONLY door Hostile after hours How many Twelve: the band, the Raceway's hound, the host, the jester, the endoskeleton, the chef, the spare suit, the raccoon, and the Encore Added in 1.65.0 (the band mended in 1.65.4, Golden Tony in 1.65.5; their kills in 1.71.1, voices 1.71.2-1.71.4, footsteps 1.71.5-1.71.6) Killed Off a few minutes, then back at its place, rebooted They drop 3 to 8 iron nuggets, 1 to 3 copper ingots, 1 to 4 redstone, and often 1 to 3 Tune-In Tokens (the Encore far more) Years in the dark Suits withered, matted, crusted, worn through to the foam and in the worst to the metal, oil run from every seam and the corners of their eyes. Wide, wet, human, bloodshot eyes with a pinprick for a pupil; big flat human teeth, yellowed and gapped, and behind the costume's teeth the endoskeleton's. Arms too long, gloves too big."},{"p":"Tune-In Town's cast","h":"After hours","u":"entities/tune-in-town-cast.html#after-hours","t":"They stand at their places, on the stage, in the kitchen, behind the curtain, in the box, in the ball pit: switched on, their heads hanging cocked to one side, jaws a little open, following you round the room, servos whining, now and then one snapping round and back. In the dark you see only the whites of their eyes, and the grins. Come too near, make a noise, or hit one, and it's awake: it hunts you (it sees you, hears you, searches where it lost you, drags you out of lockers). Now and then one goes off round the building on its own. Lose it and it goes back to its place. Since 1.71.1 each has its own blow , wound up first: get out of the way and it misses. With the Security Card on you (the fifth night's reward), after hours they take no notice of you at all: you're staff. Not the Mended Band . With the Owner's Key (all three stars), they don't stare: they turn and wave. \"Hi, boss!\""},{"p":"Tune-In Town's cast","h":"On the clock","u":"entities/tune-in-town-cast.html#on-the-clock","t":"Punch the time clock in the security office and it's 12 AM; your shift's till 6, and each of them comes for the office its own way (below). The doors, lights, cameras, power and nights are on Tune-In Town . Leave the office more than three seconds (since 1.72.1) and tonight's cast are off the show and after you, anywhere in the building, and nothing you do hurts them while they're loose. Get back in, shut the doors on them, or keep ahead of them till 6 AM."},{"p":"Tune-In Town's cast","h":"Caught","u":"entities/tune-in-town-cast.html#caught","t":"Get one in the office and it's a jumpscare : it's in your face, screaming, the world gone red. Then it's filmed: you, down on your back, and it over you, killing you its own way. Then dark, and something dragged, and Parts & Service: the golden suit slumped against the rack under one bulb, and it shoving what's left of you in, the springlocks snapping shut one after another. YOU'RE PART OF THE SHOW NOW. Then FIRED: \"You're fired. (Night 1 - clock in and try it again.)\" The card tells you who got you, and Hal's tip for next time."},{"p":"Tune-In Town's cast","h":"The twelve","u":"entities/tune-in-town-cast.html#the-twelve","t":""},{"p":"Tune-In Town's cast","h":"Tony Tune","u":"entities/tune-in-town-cast.html#tony-tune","t":"The bandleader, 130 health A blue-grey tabby tomcat in a top hat, his microphone on a cane. \"Let's all sing!\" Off the clock: The Spotlight (\"Our STAR!\"): you're lit up, glowing, and everyone in the building is called to you. His cane. On the clock: the east hall, and he moves only while nobody's watching him. When the power goes, it's Tony at the door, singing. Jumpscare: his cane up over his head. Kill: he clubs you with his cane. \"And now... for my final number!\" At the door: \"Showtime, showtime... where's my audience?\" Footsteps: a heavy metal step and a short servo whir. Death: his head pops off."},{"p":"Tune-In Town's cast","h":"Bucky Beaver","u":"entities/tune-in-town-cast.html#bucky-beaver","t":"Bass, 120 health \"Rock on, buddy!\" Off the clock: he gnaws through anything wooden in his way; his tail. On the clock: the west hall. Shut the door on him and he gnaws it, your power going. Kill: he smashes his bass down, and then his teeth. \"Hold still! I'll gnaw you right down to the bone!\" At the door: \"Knock knock! Bucky's here to play!\" Footsteps: a thick rubber foot slapping down. Death: he sits down hard on his tail and topples over."},{"p":"Tune-In Town's cast","h":"Lulu Lark","u":"entities/tune-in-town-cast.html#lulu-lark","t":"Keys, 85 health Off the clock: she leaps at you; her Shriek (sick, slow); and when she's lost you she calls, in a child's voice from behind you: \"Over here!\" On the clock: east, through the kitchen, and knocking on the west door when she isn't there. Jumpscare: her wings flung wide. Kill: she pecks. \"Sing for me, sweetie! SING!\" At the door: \"La la la... who's still awake?\" Footsteps: metal talons clicking. Death: her wings thrash and she goes over backwards."},{"p":"Tune-In Town's cast","h":"Tempo the Tortoise","u":"entities/tune-in-town-cast.html#tempo-the-tortoise","t":"Drums, 150 health, heavily armoured \"Slow and steady...\" Off the clock: his Drum Roll shakes the floor. Hit him from behind and you hit his shell; hurt, he goes into it. On the clock: west, a step every beat of his drum, the beats coming closer and quicker. Count them. Jumpscare: his head shot out of his shell. Kill: a drum roll, on you. \"Keep... the... beat.\" At the door: \"One... two... three... four...\" Footsteps: a slow, floor-shaking thud and his shell's hollow knock. Death: he pulls in under his shell and it rolls over on its back."},{"p":"Tune-In Town's cast","h":"Rusty Rover","u":"entities/tune-in-town-cast.html#rusty-rover","t":"The Raceway's racing hound, OUT OF ORDER, 95 health \"Ready... set...\" Off the clock: the fastest of them; his Sprint (into a wall, and he's dazed). On the clock: behind the Pit Stop curtain. Watch him on camera 3 or he comes out, and when he's out he RUNS for the west door (shut it; he bangs). Kill: his jaws, and he shakes you like a rag. \"Pit stop's over, pal!\" At the door: \"I can smell you in there.\" Footsteps: four rusty metal paws trotting. Death: his legs go mid-stride, he skids and comes apart at the waist."},{"p":"Tune-In Town's cast","h":"Mister Channel","u":"entities/tune-in-town-cast.html#mister-channel","t":"The host, 95 health A television for a head: his smile, his static, HIS mask. \"Stay tuned!\" Off the clock: into the static, and out of it behind you; when he sees you, the dark comes over your eyes. On the clock: he hops from screen to screen (each camera goes to static), and then his face is on YOUR TV: switch it off, quick. Kill: his hands at your head, and he slams your face into his screen. \"We'll be right back... after this message.\" At the door: \"Stay tuned, little viewer.\" Footsteps: a hard plastic step crackling with static. Death: his screen flicks through its pictures to black and he folds up like a stand."},{"p":"Tune-In Town's cast","h":"Jack Jangle","u":"entities/tune-in-town-cast.html#jack-jangle","t":"The jester in the Prize Corner's box, 85 health Off the clock: he waits in his box till you're right there: POP. Then he hops after you, box and all. On the clock: keep the music box wound (hold the button on camera 8). Let it run down and he's out. Jumpscare: bobbing on his stretched spring. Kill: flung on his spring, he springs down on you. \"Pop goes the weasel!\" At the door: \"Round and round the mulberry bush...\" Footsteps: his wooden box thumping and creaking. Death: his spring goes wild, he's sucked back into his box, the lid slams and the box rocks over."},{"p":"Tune-In Town's cast","h":"Spare Parts","u":"entities/tune-in-town-cast.html#spare-parts","t":"A bare endoskeleton, 65 health Off the clock: fast in the dark, a lunge flat along the floor. It can't stand light: a torch in your hand drives it back. On the clock: it crawls the vent, and the vent light sends it scrabbling back. Kill: it pulls. \"Need... parts. Need... YOURS.\" At the door: \"I can't find my face.\" Footsteps: bare metal skittering. Death: it falls apart, a piece at a time."},{"p":"Tune-In Town's cast","h":"Chef Pete","u":"entities/tune-in-town-cast.html#chef-pete","t":"The kitchen's walrus, 160 health, nothing knocks him back \"Pizza's up!\" Off the clock: he throws his pizza pans (\"Order up!\"); his oven-hot peel sets you alight. On the clock: the east door. Light him and he goes back to the kitchen; shut the door on him and he jams it open (for a minute, or till you reboot it on the monitor). Kill: his peel, and he chops. \"Order up! One fresh guard, extra crispy!\" At the door: \"Who wants a slice, eh?\" Footsteps: a heavy wet slap. Death: he clutches his chest and goes down on his face, his toque flying."},{"p":"Tune-In Town's cast","h":"Employee of the Month","u":"entities/tune-in-town-cast.html#employee-of-the-month","t":"The old spare Tony suit, someone still in it, 110 health Off the clock: he grabs you and holds on (the springlocks), and talks to you in a human voice. On the clock: he never shows on the cameras, only static where he is. Listen for him: \"Hello?\" Jumpscare: his arms open for a hug. Kill: he squeezes. \"Thank you for choosing Tune-In Town! Help me.\" At the door: \"Hello? Is someone there? I just want to talk.\" His voice (since 1.71.3) is deeper than any of theirs, and wet: what's left of a man inside the suit, ragged, heavy breathing in every pause, his lungs giving out, his bones cracking as he moves. Since 1.71.4 he coughs , wet, hacking fits through the suit, all through the night (another way to listen for him). Footsteps: what's in his suit squelches in his boots. Death: convulsing in the springlocks, he dies on his knees."},{"p":"Tune-In Town's cast","h":"Tix","u":"entities/tune-in-town-cast.html#tix","t":"The prize counter's raccoon, 55 health Off the clock: he snatches what's in your hand and runs. Kill him and you get it all back. On the clock: leave a door open and he steals your power and your monitor (\"Something took your power - and the monitor!\"); the third time, it's you. Kill: claws. \"Ticket, please! Oh, you've only got the one...\" At the door: \"Got any tickets for me?\" Footsteps: light paws scurrying. Death: he plays dead (spins, flops on his back, his legs in the air), and then he isn't playing."},{"p":"Tune-In Town's cast","h":"The Encore","u":"entities/tune-in-town-cast.html#the-encore","t":"A boss, with a bar, 360 health, armoured All of them stitched together with his static and miles of tape. Only once someone's lasted five nights. Off the clock: everyone's tricks, one after another. On the clock (the sixth night): out of nowhere at any of the ways in. The screen glitches, red on the side it's coming from: shut that way NOW. Blow: whichever of its heads is nearest. Kill: all of it. \"THE SHOW MUST GO ON.\" At the door: \"Encore... encore...\", in three of their voices at once. Footsteps: landing heavy and dragging its foot across the floor. Death: every mouth screams at once, heads flung off, a heap. It drops 4 to 8 iron ingots, 6 to 12 redstone, 8 to 14 Tune-In Tokens, 3 to 6 Signal Fragments and 1 to 2 diamonds. Their voices (made with ElevenLabs, since 1.71.2) come through their speaker grilles, pitched well down since 1.71.3, with metal in them, the hollow of the head, a servo under the words and the jaw clicking. Their footsteps since 1.71.6 are recorded-sounding footfalls on the tiles, four of each (five of the Employee's), so you can tell who's coming by ear."},{"p":"Tune-In Town's cast","h":"HIS static","u":"entities/tune-in-town-cast.html#his-static","t":"From the third night of the shift (it was the second until 1.71.1), HIS static, the First Signal 's, is in one of the cast that's coming for you tonight. Never the Encore (that's all HIS anyway) and never the Employee of the Month. Nothing tells you which. That one comes for you no matter what. The doors don't send it back, the lights don't, being watched on the cameras doesn't; the music box won't wind with HIM in Jack, and the office TV won't stay off with HIM in Mister Channel. Get it to your door and it's a few seconds, shut or not, and it's in. The clues: it twitches, in fits, its head wrenched about, its jaw snapping, its arms jerking (on the cameras too). Its eyes go red, now and then flaring, and they show on the cameras even right across the dining hall. The camera it's on stutters: static, black, back. Near the office the lights go, dark a moment, back, dark, worse the nearer it is, and you'll hear it breathing behind the door. Reboot (the REBOOT button on the monitor, or R ): pick one of them, and it reboots (five seconds; the cameras are only static while it does). The right one: \"HIS STATIC'S GONE OUT OF ...\", and it's back at its place, itself again ( Have You Tried Turning It Off? ). The wrong one: \"... REBOOTED - IT WASN'T HIM\", 5% of your power gone for nothing, and the system locked twenty seconds. The FIRED card always says whose HIS static was in."},{"p":"Tune-In Town's cast","h":"The Mended Band","u":"entities/tune-in-town-cast.html#the-mended-band","t":"360 health, since 1.65.4. After hours, now and then (more often with someone about who thinks the card makes them safe), the band on the show stage, Tony, Bucky, Lulu and Tempo, go stiff, their eyes go red, and they come together in the middle of the stage, into each other, metal grinding through fur: \"On the stage, the band have gone into each other. There's only one of them now - and it can see you.\" Tony's body, lurching on Tony's legs, Tempo's shell grown over its back and Tempo's face pushed out through its belly, Bucky's head out of one shoulder, Lulu's hanging upside down off the other, too many arms, all four of its mouths going. The Security Card doesn't fool it: it sees you, and comes. It roars with all four mouths and runs at you, and up close it lunges, all its arms at once. Its red eyes show on the cameras. After a few minutes, or with nobody left to chase, it comes apart and the band go back to their places; a shift starting, it's apart at once. Killed, all four heads scream and the band comes apart in it, the heads sagging off, the arms dropping, and down: Disbanded (\"Take apart the Mended Band\"). With the Owner's Key on you it never comes for you."},{"p":"Tune-In Town's cast","h":"Golden Tony","u":"entities/tune-in-town-cast.html#golden-tony","t":"The reward for all three gold stars (1.65.5): wind his music box and out he pops, a little gold Tony Tune of your own. He follows you everywhere (left behind, a long way off, in another world, after you've logged off, he's there again beside you), hums the show's song to himself, and when something hostile comes near he squeaks and points his cane at it. Nothing hurts him. Right-click him and he stays put, or comes along again. Wind the box again and he goes back in. One for each of you."},{"p":"The Warden of Shelter No. 4","h":"","u":"entities/warden-of-shelter-no-4.html","t":"Shelter No. 4, Bunker B, the north wall Boss Who he was The shelter's Civil Defence warden. Health 400 Wakes when The Front Assembly comes off its mount on the dais Size Twice a man's size, on four legs Music The Flesh's mini-boss music Weak to The overload switch (100 damage, once) Afterwards The Watcher leaves a locker on the dais with a Civil Defence Compass, bread, torches and a golden apple"},{"p":"The Warden of Shelter No. 4","h":"Description","u":"entities/warden-of-shelter-no-4.html#description","t":"When the Front Assembly comes off its mount, the north wall of Bunker B tears itself out. It's the shelter's Civil Defence warden and everyone who sheltered with him, grown into one mass on four legs: his body in the middle, still in his helmet and holding his torch, three more heads on necks round it, arms everywhere, and the frozen faces of the rest across it. Until then it sleeps in an alcove of the people fused into the wall. listen. the walls. the north wall. ??? in Bunker B"},{"p":"The Warden of Shelter No. 4","h":"Getting there","u":"entities/warden-of-shelter-no-4.html#getting-there","t":"Shelter No. 4 has no power. The two diesel generators are in the radio room; their fuel is wedged in the back of one of the shelter's lockers, a different one in every world, and the residents hiding in those lockers burst out at you. Fill both generators and pull each one's lever: twenty seconds of spinning up, loud enough that what's in the ducts comes out of the vents twice. Hold the room. With both running, the lights come on section by section, the radio switches from the evacuation notice to Control's emergency broadcast, and Bunker B's blast door opens. Inside is one great hall two storeys high: a gallery along the top, stairs down at either end into the pit, cover heaped across it, a channel of black water, the earthing plates under the gallery, and at the far end the dais with the Front Assembly on its mount. The special forces squad holds it: the sniper up on the gallery, operators and a breacher about the pit, and their Squad Leader by the dais."},{"p":"The Warden of Shelter No. 4","h":"How it fights","u":"entities/warden-of-shelter-no-4.html#how-it-fights","t":"Slam: it rears up, bellows and charges, and comes down where you were. If it charges into a wall instead, it's dazed for two seconds and takes half as much again from everything. Mouths: all four heads bite, one after another, sweeping round in front of it. Grabs: it slams its hands into the floor and arms burst out of the walls round you: cracks first, then a hand that grabs and holds you while the Flesh gets into you. At half health it floods the pit: blood up to the knee with the Flesh in it. Get out of it, up the stairs to the gallery."},{"p":"The Warden of Shelter No. 4","h":"The overload switch","u":"entities/warden-of-shelter-no-4.html#the-overload-switch","t":"Control's emergency broadcast tells you what to do. The overload switch is on the gallery over the earthing plates. Get the Warden onto the plates while both generators run, and throw it: every volt in the shelter goes through it, 100 damage once, and it stands there shaking for three seconds. Thrown with no Warden on the plates, it only fries the infected down there."},{"p":"The Warden of Shelter No. 4","h":"Emergency broadcast","u":"entities/warden-of-shelter-no-4.html#emergency-broadcast","t":"Rosemont Civil Defence Control, on the Shelter Radio Set The radio room Shelter Four, Shelter Four, this is Control. We see your power on. Respond. Shelter Four, do not open the vault. Repeat: do not open the vault. Whatever is in bunk hall B is not your residents any more. Whatever the squad told you, they are not coming back up. If anyone down there can hear this - the overload switch, over the plates in bunker B. Get it onto the plates. Shelter Four, respond."},{"p":"The Warden of Shelter No. 4","h":"How to survive it","u":"entities/warden-of-shelter-no-4.html#how-to-survive-it","t":"Clear the squad first if you can. The sniper's laser on the gallery gives it away. Bait the Slam into a wall, then hit it while it's dazed. Watch the walls for cracks: that's where an arm is about to come through. When the pit floods, go up. The overload switch is up there anyway. Bloom Serum or the hazmat suit help with the Flesh its hands put into you. keep moving. keep the cover between you and it. the plates under the gallery. get it onto them, and throw the switch up there. get out of the blood. up the stairs - the gallery. that hurt it. it won't walk into that twice. ??? during the fight"},{"p":"The Warden of Shelter No. 4","h":"Afterwards","u":"entities/warden-of-shelter-no-4.html#afterwards","t":"Kill it and the Watcher leaves you a locker on the dais with a Civil Defence Compass in it, its needle set on Rosemont wherever you are, and some bread, torches and a golden apple. i've left you something. on the dais, by the mount. a compass. it points at the city. rosemont. that's where you go next. ??? after the Warden dies"},{"p":"The Warden of Shelter No. 4","h":"Field notes","u":"entities/warden-of-shelter-no-4.html#field-notes","t":"A Warden's Log signed J. Pike was found in the Bloom, on the island where a Shelter No. 4 ended up: \"Day 9. The whole shelter tipped. I looked out of the door and there was no street. There was green all the way down, and something at the bottom of it, opening and shutting.\" Read the whole log . It drops two Bloom Serums, three Flower Ash Bombs, four to six Tainted Meat and two Flashbangs."},{"p":"The Warden of Shelter No. 4","h":"Turned","u":"entities/warden-of-shelter-no-4.html#turned","t":"Since 1.51.0 the parasite can take it, which it never could before. Turned, it's the Warden, Unhoused : its four heads up on long necks, a mouth down the whole front of the mound, six arms out of its sides."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"Getting started","u":"faq.html#getting-started","t":""},{"p":"FAQ","h":"My world doesn't look grey and foggy.","u":"faq.html#my-world-doesnt-look-different","t":"Make a new world. The grey sky, murky water and dark clouds are part of world data, so worlds made with older versions keep their old sky. With a shader pack on, the pack draws the sky and fog itself; use the \"-StaticHollow\" copy of Photon, Insanity or Hysteria."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"I updated, but there are no deep oceans or new biomes.","u":"faq.html#no-deep-oceans","t":"The oceans two thousand blocks deep and the Hollow's own country only come with new ground. The land you've already been through stays as it was. Since 1.66.7 the Hollow has its own country in big stretches of the world, hundreds of blocks to over a thousand across, and new ground in an old world is laid out that way, so there'll be a seam where it meets the old. A new world has it all the new way. (The Dead Water is the same: a world that has already been out there keeps the sea it has seen, and only the sea it hasn't is new.)"},{"p":"FAQ","h":"Where is the Forsaken Altar?","u":"faq.html#where-is-the-forsaken-altar","t":"500 to 1000 blocks from the world spawn, on open, flat, dry ground: never underground, in water or on a mountainside. Follow the blue smoke from its soul campfire. The ruin rises when you come within about 90 blocks. With cheats: /locate structure statichollow:forsaken_altar , which finds it from anywhere since 1.63.4. You can also craft an Altar Needle (a compass, a candle and a bone), and since 1.72.3 you're given one the first time you join a world. See finding the story's places ."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"Nothing is hunting me.","u":"faq.html#nothing-is-hunting-me","t":"The creepypastas only come once the altar is awake: right-click it with an empty hand. They hunt mostly in the dark."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"Where's the church that isn't on any map?","u":"faq.html#where-is-the-church","t":"The cathedral is 500 to 1000 blocks from spawn, roughly the opposite way from the altar. It isn't there until you come within about 90 blocks. With cheats: /locate structure statichollow:cathedral . See the cathedral ."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"I killed one but didn't get its head.","u":"faq.html#i-need-another-head","t":"The first kill of each creature always drops its head, but only if a player killed it (your arrows count). After that it's 10%, plus 5% per level of Looting. Since 1.60.0 you can wear any head: its own kind notice you from only half as far off."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"Playing","u":"faq.html#playing","t":""},{"p":"FAQ","h":"The Underneath never comes up under my bed.","u":"faq.html#the-underneath-never-comes","t":"Only once the altar is awake, about four times in ten that you lie down, and always the next time after you've heard it breathing. Never in Creative or on Peaceful."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"The creatures can't hurt me.","u":"faq.html#creepypastas-cant-hurt-me","t":"You're in Creative. Hostile creepypastas can't hurt you there. Test in Survival."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"The green rift didn't open.","u":"faq.html#the-green-rift-didnt-open","t":"It opens three days after the Gardener dies, by the world's clock (nights you sleep through count), and you need to be within about 80 blocks of his flower. With cheats: /statichollow bloom open ."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"I lost a reactor part (or the Device).","u":"faq.html#i-lost-a-reactor-part","t":"There's only one of each. Lose one and it goes back where you found it (the Rear Assembly a minute later); the Device goes back to where you last set it down once nobody has had it for a minute. Any copy crumbles in your hands."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"The Bloom ate me. Am I dead?","u":"faq.html#the-bloom-ate-me","t":"Not yet. Since 1.38 you go down alive into its stomach. Hack at the stomach wall ten times and it throws you back up."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"I died of the Flesh and lost everything.","u":"faq.html#i-died-of-the-flesh","t":"You didn't. What got up where you fell is you, as one of the infected, wearing your armour and carrying everything you had. Kill it and you get it all back. It never despawns."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"Where are the guns?","u":"faq.html#where-are-the-guns","t":"The Mended guns are Fabric only, through Timeless and Classics Guns: Zero (TaCZ), which the Fabric modpacks install. Special forces infected sometimes drop theirs. Without TaCZ, and on Forge, nothing drops."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"My Mended gun stopped firing.","u":"faq.html#my-gun-stopped-working","t":"The Mended guns are the Bloom's flesh. Once the Bloom is dead, every one off its blight rots over ten minutes and then jams for good. Its tooltip says how far gone it is."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"Where did the Omni go?","u":"faq.html#where-did-the-omni-go","t":"The Watcher took it back into its realm, \"for the future\". The gun is gone for good, and so is the Ray Gun's recipe. You'll see its heart again in chapter six ."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"There's something on the back of my neck.","u":"faq.html#something-on-my-neck","t":"A Parasite. Crouch or get hit to tear it off within four seconds. If it gets in, cut it out with a Surgical Kit or burn it out before it's three quarters grown. See the Parasite ."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"The animals (and villagers, and golems) are twitching and going violet.","u":"faq.html#animals-twitching","t":"That's the outbreak (1.48.0). Once the Bloom is dead, anything can carry a parasite: two days for an ordinary creature, three for the big ones, and then it turns and hunts everything that isn't one of them. A Surgical Kit cuts one out of anything before it turns. Burn a turned one when you kill it, or the parasites in it come out. See the turned ."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"There's a heap of violet flesh where something died.","u":"faq.html#violet-heap","t":"Biomass. It isn't dead: a minute or two later, with anyone about, it gets up as one of the parasite's pure forms. Burn it (fire or lava against it) and nothing gets up."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"I can't get into the End.","u":"faq.html#cant-get-into-the-end","t":"After the Null Static Zone signs off, the Watcher shuts it: anyone who goes through an End portal in Survival is sent straight back to their bed or the world's spawn (\"The way's shut. He shut it.\"). It opens again for everyone once someone carries the Last Voice into it, the one thing left when the Chorus, whole, dies in the Warm Heart. See chapter five ."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"Where does chapter six start?","u":"faq.html#where-is-chapter-six","t":"In the End, once the seal's broken: out past the obsidian you arrive on, a causeway of black seal-stone runs east to an island with a Door on it, full of static. Walk into it. See the Door at the End of the World . If the Door isn't there, update: before 1.60.1 only a Last Voice from that world's own Chorus would open the seal, and since 1.60.2 the Door is never buried in end stone."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"Why does the Ender Dragon look like that?","u":"faq.html#the-ender-dragon-changed","t":"Since 1.61.1 it's always the Infested Ender Dragon, from the first time anyone goes to the End: violet veins, blisters, spurs, tendrils, its back split open between its wings, and half again the health. It still fights as the dragon does, but over you it rains its brood down, lobs spore bombs and lashes its tendrils. Killed, it bursts."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"The Chorus keeps healing.","u":"faq.html#the-chorus-keeps-healing","t":"It draws through its cords to its four nerve nodes. Tear the nodes open (they glow; climb the steps round the stalks) and every one makes it easier to hurt. Since 1.53.0 it only mends itself when nobody's near and it hasn't been hurt for half a minute. See the Chorus ."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"How do I get back to the Hub?","u":"faq.html#back-to-the-hub","t":"With the Remote , the old television remote the Watcher gives you as you come down from it. Use it to go into the Hub; use it there to go home (or jump off the edge). Its replay portals take you back to any chapter's last fight. See the Hub ."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"How do I get home from the Dead Water?","u":"faq.html#home-from-the-dead-water","t":"Mend the Remote: craft the Broken Remote with a Static Leviathan's Signal Organ and a copper ingot. The leviathans live deep. Then press it to go to the Hub (and in the Hub, home); crouch and press it to come back to the rig. Until then you're stranded: the rig's beds set your spawn but can't be slept in, and if you die without one the sea brings you back to the quarters. See chapter eight ."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"I finished the Hub before 1.62. How do I get to the Dead Water?","u":"faq.html#never-went-to-the-dead-water","t":"Take the Remote to the Hub and jump off its edge."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"Something in the Haemal Reach's water is getting into me.","u":"faq.html#enzyme","t":"That's Enzyme 1-2418 (1.63.9). It's in all the Haemal Reach's water: go in without the UV dress and it gets into you (each piece of the UV Dive Suit keeps a quarter of it off). At 50 out of 100 it starts to pull you to the Drowned Heart, and milk doesn't touch it. A UV Lamp flashed burns a fifth of it out of you; an Enzyme Inhibitor takes half and keeps any more from taking for thirty seconds. Fit Orpheus's UV field module and her floodlights keep it off her and burn it out of her crew. See the Dead Water ."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"Mushrooms are coming up out of me.","u":"faq.html#spore-sickness","t":"That's spore sickness (1.63.13), from breathing the Drowned Mycelia's water. A sealed helmet (the hazmat mask, a dive suit's) keeps most of it out, and Orpheus keeps it all out. Under 50 it fades once you're out of the Mycelia's water; past that it's taken root and won't. A Spore Tonic (a glass bottle, charcoal, sugar and dried kelp) burns sixty of it out of you, and for a minute none of it takes. Milk does nothing."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"I can't hurt the Grove Heart.","u":"faq.html#grove-heart","t":"You can't fight it: \"hit it and it doesn't feel it, but the Grove does.\" It isn't yours to kill. It's eaten in chapter nine. See chapter nine ."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"I lost the submarine.","u":"faq.html#lost-the-submarine","t":"Use the console on the sub bay's catwalk (since 1.63.21; it used to be a clamp). If nothing's heard from her, the bay's welders build her again in her clamps: a minute's work, nothing asked of you. Lost out of reach? Use the console crouching: she's scrapped where she lies and built again. Her clamp charges her and mends her hull. See the Dead Water ."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"It won't let me sleep.","u":"faq.html#cant-sleep","t":"Not in the story's other places: the Null Static Zone, the Deep, the Stalls (\"Not with them watching.\"), the Vault, the Other Side, the Hub, the Dead Water (\"The sea won't let you.\"), his kingdom (\"Not in his kingdom.\") or Tune-In Town (\"You're on the clock - no sleeping on the job.\"). The rig's beds set your spawn but you can't sleep in them."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"How does chapter nine start?","u":"faq.html#where-is-chapter-nine","t":"Fit all three of Orpheus's modules in her upgrade bay: the pressure plating, the depth module and the UV field module. Then the Turning plays for everyone in the Dead Water. Three days on (the Dead Water's sky never moves, so it's the world's clock that counts), the next time you're in the Dead Water, the Harbinger rises and leaves you the static heart. Craft it with your Remote, broken or mended, for the Remote (Mutated). See chapter nine ."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"How does chapter ten start?","u":"faq.html#where-is-chapter-ten","t":"Once the Harbinger has gone through its way out, go home: back to your bed or your spawn in the Overworld, or home by the Remote. The Broadcast cuts in for everyone in the Overworld, and then his creations start to come for you, more each night. See chapter ten ."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"How do I get into his kingdom?","u":"faq.html#get-into-his-kingdom","t":"Break the Broadcast Core in one of his sites (a transmitter, a burrow or a set). His signal's torn open where it stood for a minute: step into the tear and you're on his platform, his castle across the black water. Behind you, a redder tear takes you back to just where you were. See his kingdom ."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"What's The Last Broadcast?","u":"faq.html#last-broadcast","t":"The end of chapter ten. It begins the first time you come through one of his tears into his kingdom after the Broadcast. See The Last Broadcast . The fight at his war table is still held back in 1.72.2."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"They keep finding me. How do I hide?","u":"faq.html#how-do-i-hide","t":"His creations see in a cone, shorter in the dark and much shorter if you're crouched; crouched in tall plants (grass, ferns, bushes, leaves, crops) they can't make you out past a few blocks. They hear you sprint, jump, land, break and place blocks, open doors, fight and eat. Get into a Steel Locker (iron and bars) and pull the door to, or crouch and use any bed to get under it. If one heard you go in, or saw you, it tears your hiding place open. Blackout armour makes you quieter, and the whole set silent."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"What's the strongest gear?","u":"faq.html#strongest-gear","t":"Blackout (1.64.0), \"the strongest gear there is\": a Blackout Ingot is four signal fragments, four blackout shards and a netherite ingot. For the deep sea, the Ember Deep Suit (1.63.10): fire, lava, cold, drowning and the deep can't touch you in the whole suit. See gear for every chapter ."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"What's Tune-In Town?","u":"faq.html#tune-in-town","t":"A secret: Tune-In Town Pizza & Playhouse, and its night shift. Since 1.65.3 its HELP WANTED flyer can turn up on an Old Set any time after your first day. It has flashing lights, flickering screens, loud noises and jumpscares , and the game warns you before you start. See the warning and Tune-In Town . To find it, /statichollow locate tune_in_town ."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"I'm stuck in Tune-In Town.","u":"faq.html#stuck-in-tune-in-town","t":"Once you've said CONTINUE you're kept: the doors won't let you out, and if you die you wake up in the lobby. Only 6 AM on the fifth night lets you go. Then the night shift is yours to play whenever you like, with no warning and no keeping. On a server, an operator can let you out early with /statichollow tunein release <players> ."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"Who's Max?","u":"faq.html#who-is-max","t":"Max Companion, in the Fabric modpack since 1.63.22: Max, the AI, plays with you. You're given his core the first time you join a world; use it on the ground and he boots up beside you. Say \"max help\" in chat for what he can do. He doesn't follow you out of the Overworld; he waits for you. See Max ."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"I keep getting thirsty, or freezing.","u":"faq.html#always-thirsty","t":"That's the cold and the thirst (1.62.0). Drink from bottles, a Canteen, the rain or your cupped hands at the water's edge, and boil murky water first. Wear leather (or the UV Drysuit) in the cold, stand near a fire, or eat blubber; and go easy on the salt. To turn either off or soften it, edit config/statichollow-vitals.properties . See cold, thirst and the world ."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"Where's Minecraft's music?","u":"faq.html#no-minecraft-music","t":"Since 1.55.0 none of it plays: the mod's own plays in its place, the lullaby of the place you're in or a piece for how far the story has got. Minecraft's Music volume and Music Frequency still work. See the soundtrack ."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"Can I get rid of the Great Bloom?","u":"faq.html#can-i-remove-the-great-bloom","t":"Only with /kill (it doesn't come back). Finishing chapter four kills it, but leaves its husk where it stood."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"How do I reset the haunting for a world?","u":"faq.html#reset-the-haunting","t":"Close the world and delete statichollow.properties in its save folder."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"Technical","u":"faq.html#technical","t":""},{"p":"FAQ","h":"Fabric or Forge?","u":"faq.html#fabric-or-forge-faq","t":"Both play the same story. Fabric is made for shaders and has the guns, Streams and Essential support. See the comparison ."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"What's the Dead Channel modpack?","u":"faq.html#what-is-dead-channel","t":"The Fabric modpack as it is on CurseForge. It downloads the mod and its HD and shader packs as their own CurseForge projects. See the Dead Channel modpack ."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"Can I play with friends?","u":"faq.html#can-i-play-with-friends","t":"Yes: on a server, on LAN, or on Fabric with the Essential mod. Everyone needs the same version, and since 1.62 the server also needs Biomes O' Plenty, Serene Seasons, Puddles & Floods and the rest. Forge and Fabric players can't share a server. See Playing with friends ."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"Do shaders work on Forge?","u":"faq.html#shaders-on-forge","t":"Through Oculus, which as of October 2026 only goes up to Minecraft 26.2. Shaders will work once it's updated for 26.3. The Fabric version has them now."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"How much memory does it need?","u":"faq.html#how-much-memory","t":"8 GB. The modpacks ask CurseForge for it since 1.63.2; if yours doesn't, set it in the modpack's ... menu, Profile Options, Allocated Memory."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"The game stutters.","u":"faq.html#the-game-stutters","t":"Give it 8 GB of memory, turn off the HD-World pack, and lower Mipmap Levels. With shaders, lower the shadow resolution to 1024. Since 1.63.20 the Fabric modpack has FerriteCore and ImmediatelyFast, and since 1.66.4 the Hollow's new ground has about half as much decoration. See If it runs slowly ."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"My mouse, hotbar and inventory stopped working after the Hub.","u":"faq.html#controls-stopped-after-the-hub","t":"Before 1.59.1 the Hub's cutscene could leave its invisible picture over your screen when it went straight into the landing. Update, and if it happened to you, close the game once and start it again."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"Is Sound Physics Remastered on?","u":"faq.html#sound-physics","t":"It's in the modpacks but switched off, because since 1.61.1 the mod gives every sound its own echo and muffling. Set enabled=true in config/sound_physics_remastered/soundphysics.properties to use it instead. See every sound, where it is ."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"A boss's bar stays on my screen.","u":"faq.html#boss-bar-stuck","t":"Fixed in 1.47.2 and 1.53.0: a boss now takes its bar down however it goes (killed, gone or unloaded), and you lose its bar as soon as you stop seeing it. Update."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"Are the HD packs made with AI?","u":"faq.html#are-the-hd-packs-ai","t":"The upscaling is. The HD packs are the mod's own textures upscaled to double resolution with an AI upscaler (Real-ESRGAN), then given their original grit back so nothing looks plastic. They're optional. Since 1.71.2 the voices (Hal's tapes and the cast) are made with ElevenLabs."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"Cutscenes don't play in the modpack.","u":"faq.html#cutscenes-dont-play","t":"Update to 1.47.1 or later. Entity Culling stopped them before (the cutscene's marker is invisible, so it was never ticked)."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"The game crashed when I used the Relay Core with shaders on.","u":"faq.html#crash-with-relay-core","t":"\"Source format is missing element iris_Entity\". Fixed in 1.47.1, along with the same crash from the Brood Heart, the Dead Channel Helm and the Static Mail."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"A new world hangs on \"Preparing for world creation\".","u":"faq.html#world-wont-start","t":"Fixed in 1.24.1 and 1.26.1. Since then every build is checked by starting a test world, and one bad file can no longer stop a world. Update."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"Does it work with Simple Voice Chat?","u":"faq.html#voice-chat","t":"Not yet. It's on the README's \"not yet\" list: creatures replaying things players said."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"Why does the inventory look normal?","u":"faq.html#inventory-look","t":"The inventory, hotbar and font keep the normal Minecraft look for now. The main menu and its buttons are new."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"Who is \"???\"","u":"faq.html#what-is-question-marks","t":"The Watcher."},{"p":"Home","h":"","u":"index.html","t":"PLAY ▶ 0:00:00 Static Hollow i see you Something answered when you lit the altar. Find a Forsaken Altar in the world. Wake it. Then try to survive what it lets in. Download on CurseForge Start with chapter one Install the modpack"},{"p":"Home","h":"What Static Hollow is","u":"index.html#what-it-is","t":"Static Hollow is a creepypasta horror mod for Minecraft 26.3, made by Death, with its own CurseForge modpacks. It turns the whole game into something that is watching you, and then it tells a story in ten chapters that starts with nine creepypastas, strands you on an oil rig in a dead green sea, and brings the First Signal's creations out into your own world. Its end, The Last Broadcast, is still coming in part by part. The world itself is wrong from the first minute: a grey, bruised sky, murky black-green water, a red sun and a full moon with a face. The fog is thick and cold, about 64 blocks of sight by day and about 18 at night. Every block, item and creature is redrawn at four times normal resolution, drained and darker. Every animal and monster in the game is rebuilt as a jointed 3D model with real wet eyes that dart, blink and, at night, stop and look back at you. The Enderman screams with its head lifted off a glowing maw of teeth. None of Minecraft's music plays any more, only the mod's own, and you have to keep warm and find clean water. Then you find the altar. The mod's CurseForge cover art."},{"p":"Home","h":"The ten chapters","u":"index.html#the-chapters","t":"The story is told in order. Each chapter starts when the one before it ends, and the Watcher points you to the next place."},{"p":"Home","h":"The Nine","u":"index.html#the-nine","t":"Starts when you wake the Forsaken Altar Nine creepypastas hunt everyone in the world, mostly in the dark. Take one head from each to the church that isn't on any map, and raise the Hollow Saint."},{"p":"Home","h":"The Breach","u":"index.html#the-breach","t":"Starts when the Hollow Saint falls A red wound opens where it died. Through it, the Void and the Breach Altar; back home, five killers and four cryptids, the Murder Mansion and the Mended."},{"p":"Home","h":"The Glasshouse","u":"index.html#the-glasshouse","t":"Starts with the Mended's rusted garden key The Gardener kneels at the great flower under the dome. Three days after he dies, a green rift opens down to what the flower really is: the Great Bloom."},{"p":"Home","h":"The Flesh","u":"index.html#the-flesh","t":"Starts ten seconds after the Great Bloom rises What the flower was holding down punches up out of the ground. Rosemont, the Laboratory, Shelter No. 4, the Rosemont Device, the Gardener reborn twice, and a gun above the sky."},{"p":"Home","h":"The Static","u":"index.html#the-static","t":"Starts once the Bloom is dead The Flesh dies back, but the parasites are still out there, and the static isn't noise. Relay 6, the Starlite Drive-In and the Null Static Zone; then the outbreak, the Hive and its Chorus, and the Deep under everything."},{"p":"Home","h":"The Door at the End of the World","u":"index.html#the-door-at-the-end-of-the-world","t":"Starts when you carry the Last Voice into the End The Watcher sealed the End for a reason. A Door full of static, the Stalls and their silent Audience, his Vault behind the picture, and on the other side, what he kept out."},{"p":"Home","h":"The First Signal","u":"index.html#the-first-signal","t":"Starts after the last show's credits His hand comes up through the credits and takes you into the Hub, a realm he made, with a portal back to every chapter. Then something older than him breaks in."},{"p":"Home","h":"The Dead Water","u":"index.html#the-dead-water","t":"Starts as you fall from the Hub He tears a portal open under you, onto an oil rig in a sea that goes on forever. The Remote breaks in your hand. Twelve waters, a submarine called Orpheus, and something that comes up out of the Black Below."},{"p":"Home","h":"The Harbinger","u":"index.html#the-harbinger","t":"Starts when Orpheus has all three of her modules in her bay The Undertow eats the Grove's Heart, goes through the Drowned Heart, and turns. Three days on its bones rise out of it on the Grove's strings, leave you a static heart for your Remote, and tear a way out of the Dead Water. \"i'll meet you at the hub.\""},{"p":"Home","h":"Stay Tuned","u":"index.html#stay-tuned","t":"Starts the next time you're home after the Harbinger has gone The First Signal tears his own way out of the Hub to his kingdom, and his creations pour out into your world. The Broadcast, his transmitters, burrows and sets, hiding in lockers and under beds, and Blackout, the strongest gear there is."},{"p":"Home","h":"The Last Broadcast","u":"index.html#the-last-broadcast","t":"Starts the first time you come through one of his tears into his kingdom after the Broadcast \"you came into MY house?\" The Refusal, the Coronation and his arena, the Fall, the Tearing, the Second Rite and the Rebirth, and a last fight in the air on the dragon's wings. It goes on in a coming update: the fight at his war table is still held back."},{"p":"Home","h":"What's new since 1.63","u":"index.html#whats-new","t":"The wiki was last written for 1.63.3. Since then: Version What came 1.63.4–1.63.22 The Dead Water, fuller. Every water its own place, with its own crews; Orpheus's upgrade bay and her modules; Enzyme 1-2418 and the UV Dive Suit; the deep's pressure and the Ember Deep Suit; spore sickness and the Grove Heart; a fish of its own for each of the twelve waters, and new creatures in most of them. See the Dead Water . 1.63.23–1.63.25 Chapter nine: the Harbinger. The Turning, three days, and the Harbinger . The Remote (Mutated). See chapter nine . 1.64 Chapter ten: Stay Tuned. The Broadcast, his kingdom and his Faithful, his creations and servants , hiding, and Blackout. See chapter ten . 1.65 Tune-In Town. A secret night shift with twelve of them, and flashing lights, loud noises and jumpscares: read the warning first . See Tune-In Town . 1.66 More of the land. 23 new places of the Hollow's own in the Overworld, the caves, the Nether and the End, then lighter, and in one piece: the Hollow's own country . Blood on the ground, and /statichollow goto : see cold, thirst and the world . 1.67 Tonight on Channel Zero. A different night every night of chapter ten, and his creations, cleverer. 1.68–1.72 The Last Broadcast, parts one to four, and the End on its wings. Voices for Tune-In Town (1.71.2) and footsteps for its cast. See The Last Broadcast . 1.72.3 Needles to start with. The Altar, Cathedral and Gardens needles the first time you join a world, and a recipe for the Cathedral Needle. See finding the story's places ."},{"p":"Home","h":"At a glance","u":"index.html#at-a-glance","t":"Current version 1.72.3 on CurseForge Minecraft 26.3 Fabric Loader 0.19.5 with Fabric API 0.161.0+26.3 Forge 66.0.9 separate build, plays the same Java 25 Memory 8 GB the modpacks ask CurseForge for it Modpack Static Hollow - Dead Channel Fabric, on CurseForge Made by Death On CurseForge: Static Hollow - Dead Channel (the modpack, the easiest way to play), Static Hollow (the mod), and the optional packs HD Models , HD World , Shader PBR and Visuals ."},{"p":"Home","h":"Find your way","u":"index.html#find-your-way","t":"Bestiary Every creature and boss, from the Hollow Neighbor to the Harbinger, his creations and Tune-In Town's cast. Locations The cathedral, the Murder Mansion, Rosemont, Relay 6, the drive-in, the Stalls, the Hub, the Dead Water, his kingdom, Tune-In Town and the rest. Items and blocks The Relay Core, the needles, the power source parts, the Remote, Blackout, and gear for every chapter. Notes and books Every page left on a lectern or in a chest, word for word. Advancements From Not Collected to Tune-In Town's night shift. The soundtrack The 63 pieces of the soundtrack, everything since, and when each one plays. Cold, thirst and the world Warmth, water, the seasons, a world that moves, and Max. Install and play The modpacks, servers, LAN, shaders, the HD packs, and the Tune-In Town warning."},{"p":"Home","h":"From the archive","u":"index.html#from-the-archive","t":"Screenshots from the mod's CurseForge page, in story order. The ones marked with a pack were taken with that optional pack on. The Hollow Saint Chapter one The Antlerkin Chapter one In the fog The Flatwoods Monster A face in the village The Flatwoods Monster The Mended Chapter two The Mended, up close HD Models pack In the fields The Harvestman Wings in the fog Mothman Out on the moor The glasshouse HD Models pack Botanic gardens HD World pack The Great Bloom Chapter four Swallowed alive The Great Bloom Flesh and stone HD World pack Under the flesh Chapter four The Chorus Chapter five Replay portals HD World pack The Hub Chapter seven The First Signal Chapter seven Orpheus, the submarine Chapter eight Glowing rift Shader PBR pack"},{"p":"Home","h":"Before your first night","u":"index.html#before-your-first-night","t":"Make a new world. The grey sky, murky water and dark clouds are part of the world's data, so a world made with an older version keeps its old sky. Follow the blue smoke. The Forsaken Altar is 500 to 1000 blocks from spawn on open, flat, dry ground, and a soul campfire burns at it. Don't look at the Broadcast. Staring at its screen burns you every second, and touching it shocks you. Get out of bed. If something knocks three times under the floor, use Leave Bed within about four seconds. Make a canteen. String, leather and an iron ingot. Fill it in the rain, or boil it before you drink. Listen to the Watcher. It never attacks. After your first, fifth and ninth kill it has something to say. Mind the secret. Tune-In Town has flashing lights, flickering screens, loud noises and jumpscares, and once you say yes you're kept for five nights. Read the warning. nine. do you know what nine heads are for? there is a church that isn't on any map. find it. i'll be on the ceiling. ??? after your ninth kill"},{"p":"Installation guide","h":"","u":"install.html","t":"Static Hollow 1.72.3 is for Minecraft 26.3 and comes in two builds that play the same: Fabric (made for shaders, with guns) and Forge . The easiest way in is a CurseForge modpack. Whatever you do, start a new world, and give the game 8 GB of memory. Photosensitivity warning: Tune-In Town Static Hollow has a secret, Tune-In Town , with flashing lights, flickering screens, loud noises and jumpscares . If flashing lights or flicker can affect you, don't go into its security office. Nobody ends up on the night shift by accident. The first time you walk into the security office, the game stops and warns you: \"This secret contains FLASHING LIGHTS, FLICKERING SCREENS, LOUD NOISES and JUMPSCARES.\" GO BACK (or Esc ) walks you back out to the lobby. If you choose CONTINUE , you can't leave until you've survived five nights : \"You'll be kept here - the doors won't let you out, and if you die, you'll wake up here.\" You can't play the story or the rest of the game until then. Got stuck? A server operator can let you out with /statichollow tunein release <players> ."},{"p":"Installation guide","h":"Quick start","u":"install.html#quick-start","t":""},{"p":"Installation guide","h":"Install the CurseForge app","u":"install.html#install-the-curseforge-app","t":"From curseforge.com, and sign in."},{"p":"Installation guide","h":"Install the modpack","u":"install.html#install-the-modpack","t":"Search for Static Hollow - Dead Channel in the app and click Install, or open its CurseForge page and click Install there (see the Dead Channel modpack ). If you have a modpack as a .zip instead, import it under My Modpacks."},{"p":"Installation guide","h":"Give it 8 GB of memory","u":"install.html#give-it-8-gb-of-memory","t":"The modpacks ask CurseForge for 8 GB since 1.63.2. If yours doesn't have it: the modpack's ... menu, Profile Options, Allocated Memory. Running short is what causes the stutters."},{"p":"Installation guide","h":"Play","u":"install.html#play","t":"Launch it from the app. The Fabric packs come with Iris, Sodium and the Photon shader pack already switched on and set up for Static Hollow."},{"p":"Installation guide","h":"Make a new world","u":"install.html#make-a-new-world","t":"The grey sky, murky water and dark clouds are part of world data, so worlds made with older versions keep their old sky. The oceans two thousand blocks deep and the Hollow's own country (1.62.0, laid out again in 1.66.7) also only come with new ground: in an old world, new ground is laid out the new way and there'll be a seam where it meets the old. Everything else comes to old worlds too."},{"p":"Installation guide","h":"Find the altar","u":"install.html#find-the-altar","t":"500 to 1000 blocks from spawn. Follow the blue smoke."},{"p":"Installation guide","h":"On CurseForge","u":"install.html#on-curseforge","t":"Static Hollow - Dead Channel , the modpack: the easiest way to play Static Hollow , the mod itself (Fabric builds) Static Hollow: HD Models , HD World , Shader PBR and Visuals , the optional resource packs"},{"p":"Installation guide","h":"The Static Hollow - Dead Channel modpack","u":"install.html#dead-channel","t":"Static Hollow - Dead Channel is the Fabric modpack on CurseForge. It's for Fabric Loader 0.19.5 and asks for 8 GB. Instead of carrying the mod inside the pack, it downloads it from CurseForge along with the mod's three resource packs, each its own project: Static Hollow (Fabric), the latest version Static Hollow: HD Models and Static Hollow: Shader PBR, both switched on Static Hollow: HD World, installed but left off and the same mods as the Fabric modpack below, except Water Erosion and Cinematic Interactions , which aren't on its list. It sets the same shader (the Static Hollow copy of Photon), the same resource pack order and a render distance of 12 with a simulation distance of 8."},{"p":"Installation guide","h":"Fabric or Forge?","u":"install.html#fabric-or-forge","t":"Fabric Forge Loader Fabric Loader 0.19.5, Fabric API 0.161.0+26.3 Forge 66.0.9 Mod file statichollow-fabric-1.72.3.jar statichollow-1.72.3.jar Modpacks Static Hollow - Dead Channel (on CurseForge); \"Static Hollow (Fabric + Shaders)\" when you build it yourself \"Static Hollow\" Shaders Iris and Sodium with Photon, set up and switched on Need Oculus, which only goes up to Minecraft 26.2 (as of October 2026) The Mended guns Yes, with TaCZ (in the modpack) No Streams: Reflowing Yes No Puddles & Floods, Water Erosion, Cinematic Interactions Yes Yes, as builds made for the pack (none of them has a Forge 26.3 build of its own) FerriteCore, ImmediatelyFast and Max Companion Yes (since 1.63.20 and 1.63.22) No Host online without a server Yes, with the Essential mod No (Essential is Fabric-only on 26.3); LAN works Story The same in both. Forge and Fabric players can't share a server. Pick one version for everyone."},{"p":"Installation guide","h":"What's in the Fabric modpack","u":"install.html#whats-in-the-fabric-modpack","t":"Static Hollow 1.72.3 (Fabric) Fabric API 0.161.0+26.3 Sodium 0.9.2 and Iris Shaders 1.11.7 Lithium 0.26.2 (faster game logic) Entity Culling 1.11.2 (skips drawing creatures hidden behind walls) FerriteCore 9.0.0 (less memory for blocks and models) and ImmediatelyFast 1.17.1 for 26.3 (the HUD, text and entities drawn in fewer batches), both unmodified, since 1.63.20 Photon v1.3b, Hysteria v1.2.2 and Insanity v1.650 (shader packs, downloaded unmodified) Timeless and Classics Guns: Zero (TaCZ) [Unofficial] Refabricated 1.1.8 for 26.3, and Forge Config API Port 26.3.1, which it needs First-person Model 2.7.3 and Not Enough Animations 1.12.6 (your own body in first person) Sound Physics Remastered 1.5.1, installed but switched off: since 1.61.1 the mod does every sound's echo and muffling itself ( how to switch it back ) Biomes O' Plenty 26.3.0.0.15 (beta), with TerraBlender 26.3.0.0.9 and GlitchCore 26.3.0.0.5. The Hollow's own biomes come into the world through TerraBlender. Serene Seasons 26.1.2.0.7 for 26.3 (beta), with Static Hollow's season settings Puddles & Floods 1.1.6 Water Erosion, ported to 26.3 for this pack Streams: Reflowing 2.15.2 Cinematic Interactions 0.18.7, in a build made for this pack Max Companion 1.0.0, made for this pack (since 1.63.22): Max, the AI, plays the game with you. You get his core the first time you join a world; say \"max help\" in chat for what he does."},{"p":"Installation guide","h":"What's in the Forge modpack","u":"install.html#whats-in-the-forge-modpack","t":"Static Hollow 1.72.3 Sound Physics Remastered, installed but switched off, as on Fabric Biomes O' Plenty, TerraBlender and GlitchCore Serene Seasons Puddles & Floods 1.1.6, ported to Forge 26.3 for this pack Water Erosion, ported to 26.3 for this pack Cinematic Interactions 0.18.7, built for Forge from its Fabric source over a small layer that answers its Fabric calls with Forge's. If one of its changes clashes with Forge's own, that part is skipped rather than the game failing. What the new mods do in the game is on cold, thirst and the world ."},{"p":"Installation guide","h":"Playing with friends","u":"install.html#multiplayer","t":""},{"p":"Installation guide","h":"On a server","u":"install.html#dedicated-server","t":"Everyone joining uses the matching modpack. The world's land, seasons, puddles and streams are the server's, so those mods go on the server too. Fabric: install the Fabric server for Minecraft 26.3 (Loader 0.19.5) and put these in its mods folder: statichollow-fabric-1.72.3.jar and Fabric API 0.161.0+26.3 for the guns, Timeless and Classics Guns: Zero 1.1.8 for 26.3 and Forge Config API Port 26.3.1 Puddles & Floods 1.1.6 Biomes O' Plenty, TerraBlender, GlitchCore, Serene Seasons and Streams: Reflowing, from CurseForge watererosion-26.3-sh.1-fabric.jar and cinematic-interactions-0.18.7+statichollow.1-fabric-26.3.jar (in the project's output folder and the modpack's mods) to have Max on the server too, maxcompanion-fabric-1.0.0.jar (in the modpack's mods) Forge: install the Forge 66.0.9 server for Minecraft 26.3 and put these in its mods folder: statichollow-1.72.3.jar puddleflood-1.1.6+26.3-forge.jar , watererosion-26.3-sh.1-forge.jar and cinematic-interactions-0.18.7+statichollow.1-forge-26.3.jar (the last two are in the output folder; all three are in the modpack's mods) Biomes O' Plenty, TerraBlender, GlitchCore and Serene Seasons, from CurseForge Iris, Sodium, Photon and Sound Physics Remastered are client-only: don't put them on the server."},{"p":"Installation guide","h":"Without a server","u":"install.html#lan-and-essential","t":"Open your world to LAN ( Esc , then Open to LAN), or on Fabric host it over the internet with the Essential mod (on CurseForge for Fabric 26.3, client-only). Either way it plays exactly like a server: everyone needs the same version of Static Hollow (and TaCZ, for the guns). Since 1.43.6 everything the mod shows comes from the server, so a friend who joins your world sees what you see."},{"p":"Installation guide","h":"Shaders","u":"install.html#shaders","t":"The Fabric modpacks have Photon switched on already. With a shader pack, every glow in the mod (eyes, antenna bulbs, the Saint's Crown orb, runes, portals, beams) shines as a real light with bloom. Pick the Static Hollow copy. If Photon v1.3b, Insanity v1.650 or Hysteria v1.2.2 is in your shaderpacks folder, the mod makes a copy of each when the game starts with \"-StaticHollow\" on the end of its name. Choose that one: its grass and flowers sway as one piece, it knows the mod's garden blocks, and it draws the Void, the Bloom and the Hub properly. The copies are made on your computer for your own use; don't upload them anywhere. Photon is the one made to work with every part of the mod. The PBR pack. StaticHollow-Shader-PBR.zip is a resource pack of LabPBR normal and specular maps for every block: bumpy stone, glossy mud, metal that reflects, light pouring out of torches and lava. The Fabric modpacks switch it on. On Forge, turn it on in Options, Resource Packs, with a shader pack that uses LabPBR materials. Change the look in Options, Video Settings, Shader Packs, Shader Pack Settings. Too slow? Pick the Medium or Low profile there (the Static Hollow colours, fog and water stay), or lower the shadow resolution to 1024. K turns shaders off, and the mod's own grey sky and fog come back. Forge: shaders need Oculus, and as of October 2026 Oculus only goes up to Minecraft 26.2. Glowing rift With shaders and the Shader PBR pack on."},{"p":"Installation guide","h":"The HD packs","u":"install.html#hd-packs","t":"Everything is already redrawn at four times normal resolution. Two optional resource packs go further, AI-upscaled to double resolution with Real-ESRGAN and then given their original grit back: StaticHollow-HD-Models.zip : every creature, their heads, the weapons, armour and items, the cathedral's blocks, the main menu and the effects. StaticHollow-HD-World.zip : every block and item of the look at 128×128, the paintings, the sun and the moon. Since 1.61.0 the HD pack has the chapter gear (the weapons, the tools and the seven armour sets, held and worn) at four times the mod's own resolution, and since 1.63.1 the Dead Water's blocks and plants at 256 px. Since 1.63.2 its item textures are capped at 512 px, which made the game start faster and stutter less. Fabric modpacks: HD-Models is switched on for you. HD-World is installed but left off, because the shader maps are drawn for the normal block size. To try it, go to Options, Resource Packs, move it to the right-hand side below Shader-PBR, and click Done. The modpack sets the pack order (vanilla, Static Hollow, HD-Models, Shader-PBR). In Dead Channel the three packs come as their own CurseForge projects. Forge: move both to the right-hand side in Options, Resource Packs. The order doesn't matter. They need more video memory: if the game stutters, turn HD-World off first. With shaders on, HD-World's blocks use the normal-size bump maps, stretched to fit."},{"p":"Installation guide","h":"If it runs slowly","u":"install.html#performance","t":"Give the game 8 GB of memory (the modpack's ... menu, Profile Options, Allocated Memory). With shaders, lower the shadow resolution to 1024, then the render distance to 10 (the pack sets 12), then turn HD-World off. Lower Mipmap Levels in Video Settings. Turn off StaticHollow-HD-World.zip , then HD-Models. If new chunks are slow to appear on Fabric, pick a lower quality preset in Streams: Reflowing's settings (in the config folder). Since 1.63.20 the mod only looks for blocks to tick at random in the parts of a chunk that have any, which takes about two fifths off the server's time per tick in the Overworld. If something that grows or melts on its own seems to have stopped, you can go back to the game's own way with -Dstatichollow.vanillaRandomTicks=true in the Java arguments ( more ). If you switched Sound Physics Remastered back on, turn its rays and bounces down in config/sound_physics_remastered/soundphysics.properties . Camera shake and zoom follow your Screen Effect Scale and FOV Effects settings. Hide Lightning Flashes (Accessibility) keeps the main menu's flashes dim."},{"p":"Installation guide","h":"Building it yourself","u":"install.html#building-it-yourself","t":"For the mod's own project folders: Install Java 25 (Temurin, from adoptium.net). On Windows double-click BUILD-MODPACK.bat ; on Mac or Linux run ./build-modpack.sh . The output folder then holds the modpack zip ( StaticHollow-Fabric-Modpack-1.72.3.zip or StaticHollow-Modpack-1.72.3.zip ; import it in CurseForge under My Modpacks), the mod jar by itself (for servers), StaticHollow-Visuals.zip (the texture pack on its own), the HD packs if they were found, and the builds of Water Erosion and Cinematic Interactions made for the pack. The build starts a test server that loads a new world's data before it makes a modpack, so a version that can't start a world can't be built. If it fails, check build-log.txt ."},{"p":"Installation guide","h":"Testing commands","u":"install.html#testing-commands","t":"With cheats on, the Static Hollow creative tab has every spawn egg, head and block, and /statichollow can skip to any part of the story. In Creative, hostile creatures can't hurt you, so test hunting in Survival. /locate structure statichollow:... finds the mod's places, from anywhere since 1.63.4, and clicking the coordinates it gives you lands you standing beside the place (in the Dead Water, in the water beside it, a third of the way up it). Command What it does /statichollow locate [place] Where each place is, or when it will come. Since 1.66.7 each one can be clicked to go there, and it knows tune_in_town (the old place) and flyer_tv (the Old Set that last showed the flyer). /statichollow goto [place] Takes you to any place locate lists: onto the ground there, with room to stand (in front of the Old Set, looking at it). /statichollow tunein release <players> Lets them out of Tune-In Town's night shift without beating it (see the warning ). /statichollow tunein skipnights [players] All six of the show's nights behind them, and straight to the Custom Night. /statichollow underbed , underbed peek The Underneath comes up under your bed next time you lie down; or watches from under the nearest bed. /statichollow bloom open | break | rise | swallow The green rift opens; the Binding breaks; the Great Bloom rises; it swallows you. /statichollow flesh wake | front <days> | load <0-100> | redo | state The Flesh erupts in front of you; its reach; your infection; and more. /statichollow flesh city | lab | shelter [tp | below | vault | power | rebuild] Rosemont, the Laboratory and Shelter No. 4. /statichollow flesh device [build | release] The Rosemont Device; the Bloom gives the Gardener back. /statichollow flesh launch [force | open | mark | fire | detonate | reset] The launch, step by step. /statichollow flesh mutate | nest | horde [size] | horde stop | act | sapro <0-3> | self Mutations, nests, hordes, the infected's own ways, Sapromyiophilous, the infected you. /statichollow guns give mended_smg (or mended_shotgun , mended_marksman ) The Mended guns (Fabric with TaCZ). /statichollow ending <test> Everything from the end of chapter four on. The command suggests them all; they're grouped below. The tests for /statichollow ending , by part of the story: Part Tests Chapter four's end and chapter five status , start , sites , parts , gun , strike , feed , starve , r"},{"p":"Gear for every chapter","h":"","u":"items/chapter-gear.html","t":"Since 1.60.0 every chapter has its own gear: a set of armour, two weapons and four tools (a pickaxe, an axe, a shovel and a hoe), all made from what that chapter leaves behind. Each piece is a real 3D model in your hand, on you and in the inventory, with its own sounds and its own power. None of it wears out. The Dead Water has two dive suits of its own (since 1.63.9 and 1.63.10), and Chapter Ten has Blackout (since 1.64.0), the strongest gear there is. Item text below is copied from the game: the power in red, the description in grey. Recipes are written row by row, top to bottom, with . for an empty square. Every recipe shows up in the recipe book once you pick up what it's made from. The older weapons and armour (the Sinew Cleaver, Static Mail and the rest) are on Items and blocks ."},{"p":"Gear for every chapter","h":"At a glance","u":"items/chapter-gear.html#at-a-glance","t":"Chapter Armour (full-set power) Weapons Tools (perk) Made with One The Vigil (Keep Watch) The Censer, the Bell Clapper Gravedigger's (Unearth) Hymnal Pages, Grave Claws, iron Two The Scarecrow (Stand Still) The Pitchfork, the Omen Staff Harvestman's (Reap) Blighted Straw, Bloodied Stuffing, a Devil's Horn, iron Three The Bloomwoven (Rooted) The Thorn Whip, the Spore Mace Heartwood (Overgrowth) Knotted Roots, Heartblooms, Bloom Heartwood Four The Specimen (Hardened) The Bone Saw, the Reactor Rod Surgical Steel (Scan) Hive Comb, Splitter Sinew, a Stalker Talon, a Bloater Gland, diamonds Five Dead Air (Off Air) The Tuning Fork, the Relay Staff Static (Chain) Carrier Thread, Frames of the Last Reel, Vacuum Tubes, diamonds Six The Usher's Uniform (House Lights) The Splicer, the Fly Hook Stagehand's (Hush) Ticket Stubs, Listener's Ears, gold, netherite scrap Seven On Air (Skip) The Antenna Glaive, the On Air Mace Hub-Stone (Skip) Rerun Reels, netherite Eight The UV Dive Suit (Lined) and the Ember Deep Suit (Nothing Down There) None of its own None of its own Found in the Haemal Research Station; the Ember Crew's parts and netherite Ten Blackout (Radio Silence) The Blackout Blade Blackout (Silent) Blackout Ingots: Signal Fragments, Blackout Shards, netherite Chapter Eight (the Dead Water) has no set made the chapters' way, but it has two dive suits; the rest of its kit (the Harpoon Gun, flares, air tanks, the UV Lamp, the submarine's modules) is on Items and blocks . Chapter Nine has no gear of its own: its prize is the Remote (Mutated) ."},{"p":"Gear for every chapter","h":"The armour sets","u":"items/chapter-gear.html#armour","t":"Each piece shows its set's power on its tooltip. Wear all four for it. Every set has an HD version and shader (LabPBR) maps, and its lights (the Vigil's candles, the crow, the bloom, the jar, the static, the Usher's torch, the ON AIR lamp) have their own copies for shader packs since 1.62.0. Putting on a whole set earns its advancement."},{"p":"Gear for every chapter","h":"The Vigil (Chapter One)","u":"items/chapter-gear.html#the-vigil","t":"The Vigil (Chapter One) Full set: Keep Watch The candles light the dark round you; every ten seconds they flare, and every creepypasta near shows through the walls The night watch's iron hood with a crown of candles burning on it, a long wax-stiff coat, iron pauldrons and a lantern swinging at the hip. Whenever it's dark round you (night, a cave, anywhere the sky doesn't reach) the candles light it, steady, with a real candle's flame dancing on each wick, a curl of smoke now and then and a soft crackle that everyone near can see and hear. Every ten seconds they flare, and every creepypasta within thirty-two blocks shows through the walls a while. Advancement: Keep Watch . Piece Recipe Vigil Hood C C C / I H I / I . I Vigil Coat I . I / W H W / W W W Vigil Leggings W H W / W . W / I . I Vigil Boots H . H / I . I C candle, H Hymnal Page, I iron ingot, W black wool."},{"p":"Gear for every chapter","h":"The Scarecrow (Chapter Two)","u":"items/chapter-gear.html#the-scarecrow","t":"The Scarecrow (Chapter Two) Full set: Stand Still Stand still a moment and what's hunting you loses interest (unless you've just hurt it). Move, or strike, and it's back A sacking mask with a stitched face under a crooked hat, straw out of every gap, and a crow on your right shoulder: glossy black with a blue-violet sheen, a heavy beak and yellow eyes. It shifts about on its feet, jerks its head round to look and flicks its tail. Stand still for a second and a half and whatever is hunting you gives up; while you stay still nothing new sets on you. Advancement: Out Standing in the Field . Piece Recipe Scarecrow's Sack B U B / L . L Scarecrow's Coat L . L / L U L / B Y B Scarecrow's Breeches L U L / B . B / L . L Scarecrow's Boots U . U / L . L B Blighted Straw, U Bloodied Stuffing, L leather, Y hay bale."},{"p":"Gear for every chapter","h":"The Bloomwoven (Chapter Three)","u":"items/chapter-gear.html#the-bloomwoven","t":"The Bloomwoven (Chapter Three) Full set: Rooted On soil - grass, dirt, moss, mud - you heal. The Bloom and its flies won't have you Woven of the Bloom's roots: a cowl with a crown of petals that breathe and a bloom lit on the brow, its face the pitch-black hollow of the original with roots grown over the rim. Standing on soil you heal, and the Bloom and its flies leave you alone. Advancement: Rooted . Piece Recipe Bloomwoven Cowl K F K / K . K Bloomwoven Tunic K . K / K W K / K F K Bloomwoven Leggings K W K / K . K / K . K Bloomwoven Boots F . F / K . K K Knotted Root, F Heartbloom, W Bloom Heartwood."},{"p":"Gear for every chapter","h":"The Specimen (Chapter Four)","u":"items/chapter-gear.html#the-specimen","t":"The Specimen (Chapter Four) Full set: Hardened Each blow you take hardens you more: Resistance I, II, III, a while after the last. A kill puts two hearts back into you A specimen jar over your head, full of thick green fluid lit from inside, motes drifting and bubbles rising in it, a lid, tubes and an eye bobbing about; a patient's gown, restraints, and an IV bag on your back. Each hit you take hardens you a step further (Resistance I, II, III), for four seconds after the last one. Advancement: Specimen . Piece Recipe Specimen Jar I C I / G . G / G G G Specimen Gown W . W / W N W / W C W Specimen Leggings W N W / W . W / W . W Specimen Boots N . N / L . L I iron ingot, C Hive Comb, G glass, W white wool, N Splitter Sinew, L leather."},{"p":"Gear for every chapter","h":"Dead Air (Chapter Five)","u":"items/chapter-gear.html#dead-air","t":"Dead Air (Chapter Five) Full set: Off Air Crouch and you go off the air: unseen and invisible for five seconds - then twenty more to come back on A black hood with a screen where your face was, playing static that rolls and breaks up, with now and then a face surfacing in it; two aerials lit at the tips that whip about as you move; a long black coat with static running down its lapels. Crouch and you go off the air. Advancement: Off the Air . Piece Recipe Dead Air Hood B F B / B . B Dead Air Coat B . B / B T B / B F B Dead Air Leggings B T B / B . B / B . B Dead Air Boots T . T / B . B B black wool, F Frame of the Last Reel, T Carrier Thread."},{"p":"Gear for every chapter","h":"The Usher's Uniform (Chapter Six)","u":"items/chapter-gear.html#the-ushers-uniform","t":"The Usher's Uniform (Chapter Six) Full set: House Lights The things that listen can't hear you walk. What you strike from behind takes half as much again The Starlite's maroon and gold, made again in 1.61.1: a gilt-rimmed porcelain mask split by a gold seam (narrow slanted black eyes, half a smile and half a frown, a black tear, the glaze crazed); a tall pillbox cap with its band, badge, button and chin strap; a velvet jacket with a bow at the throat, braided aiguillettes, a name tag and tails swinging behind; the usher's torch lit at your belt. The things that listen (the Audience , the Listener and the Deaf King ) can't hear you walk. Advancement: Front of House . Piece Recipe Usher's Cap R R R / R S R / G . G Usher's Jacket R . R / G S G / R R R Usher's Trousers R S R / R . R / R . R Usher's Shoes E . E / L . L R red wool, S Ticket Stub, G gold ingot, E Listener's Ear, L leather."},{"p":"Gear for every chapter","h":"On Air (Chapter Seven)","u":"items/chapter-gear.html#on-air","t":"On Air (Chapter Seven) Full set: Skip A blow of three hearts or more skips you out of its way instead, a few blocks off, unhurt (every 15 seconds) Studio gear: a test-card visor that cycles, slips and rolls; headphones and a mic on a boom that bobs; the ON AIR lamp on top, pulsing; a crew jacket with a battery pack, a tally light and tape reels turning on the back. Advancement: Live . Piece Recipe On Air Visor B R B / P G P On Air Jacket B . B / P N P / B B B On Air Trousers B P B / B . B / N . N On Air Boots P . P / B . B B black wool, R redstone lamp, P Rerun Reel, G glass pane, N netherite scrap."},{"p":"Gear for every chapter","h":"The UV Dive Suit (the Dead Water)","u":"items/chapter-gear.html#the-uv-dive-suit","t":"UV Dive Suit (Haemal Research Station) Full set: Lined - Enzyme 1-2418 can't get in (each piece keeps a quarter of it off); you breathe under water; its UV lamps light the dark The Haemal Research Station's own (since 1.63.9): a white fibreglass dive helmet, its wide faceplate tinted violet with a ring of UV lamps round it, a drysuit with violet stripes, UV strips lit on its shoulders, arms, legs and ankles, a UV battery pack and a rebreather on its back. Full set: Enzyme 1-2418 can't get in (what claws through it lets in a third), you breathe under water, and its lamps light the dark. Each piece keeps a quarter of the Enzyme off you by itself. The mycelia's spores mostly stay out of its sealed helmet too. About iron's worth against a blow. Piece Where UV Dive Helmet The lockers at the Haemal Research Station (a whole suit to a locker, with a UV Lamp and an Enzyme Inhibitor or two) UV Drysuit The lockers at the Haemal Research Station (a whole suit to a locker, with a UV Lamp and an Enzyme Inhibitor or two) UV Drysuit Trousers The lockers at the Haemal Research Station (a whole suit to a locker, with a UV Lamp and an Enzyme Inhibitor or two) UV Dive Boots The lockers at the Haemal Research Station (a whole suit to a locker, with a UV Lamp and an Enzyme Inhibitor or two) It has no recipe. More on the Enzyme and the UV kit on Items and blocks ."},{"p":"Gear for every chapter","h":"The Ember Deep Suit (the Dead Water)","u":"items/chapter-gear.html#the-ember-deep-suit","t":"Ember Deep Suit (the Ember Crew's) Full set: Nothing Down There - no pressure, all the way to the floor of the void; no heat, no cold, no drowning (each piece keeps a quarter of the crush off). Only the Undertow, if it's hungry The Ember Crew's deep suit (since 1.63.10), made from what they trade: past netherite, and fire-proof. The whole suit: fire, lava, cold, drowning and the deep can't touch you. It has its own air and its own warmth, and its lamp lights the dark. Below about y -100 in the Dead Water the sea crushes you, worse the deeper you go, and each piece keeps a quarter of that off. Only the Undertow still gets you, if it's hungry. Piece Recipe Ember Deep Helmet P V P / C S C Ember Deep Hull P S P / C N C / P P P Ember Deep Legs P S P / C . C / P . P Ember Deep Boots S . S / P . P P Ember Plating, V Vent Glass, C Heat Coil, S Pressure Seal, N netherite ingot. The four parts come from the Ember Crew's trade ."},{"p":"Gear for every chapter","h":"Blackout (Chapter Ten)","u":"items/chapter-gear.html#blackout","t":"Blackout (the strongest there is) Each piece quiets you. Full set: RADIO SILENCE - his creations can't hear you; stand still, they lose you. Tap sneak twice: LIGHTS OUT - a black wave throws down all that hunts you, and you vanish (45 s to come back). The strongest there is (since 1.64.0), and the quietest: each piece makes you quieter, and in the whole set his creations can't hear you at all. In 3D since 1.64.1: a black knight's suit that takes the light, plate on plate with a red seam burning between them; a great helm with a slit of red static across it, a brow lamp and two snapped aerials springing about, their tips lit; a dead screen in the chest (his static on it, and now and then something looking out) and three red diodes; layered pauldrons; a spine of transmitter lamps down the back; a cloak of black rags; long black claws on the gauntlets that flex and grip; swinging tassets, knee lamps, and sabatons with a red running light. Lights Out: in the whole set, tap sneak twice. Your screen goes out like a set switched off, and so does everything round you: a black wave twenty blocks out throws down everything hunting you (his creations hurt far worse, their signal cut, stood still five seconds, and you lost to them: they go and search the wrong place); anyone else in it goes dark a moment; and you're gone, invisible, fast, strong and hard to hurt, for ten seconds. It takes 45 seconds to come back (\"Lights Out is ready\"). Having the whole set earns Radio Silence ; your first Blackout Ingot, Blackout . Piece Recipe Blackout Helmet I I I / I . I Blackout Chestplate I . I / I I I / I I I Blackout Leggings I I I / I . I / I . I Blackout Boots I . I / I . I I Blackout Ingot (four Signal Fragments, four Blackout Shards and a netherite ingot)."},{"p":"Gear for every chapter","h":"Armour points","u":"items/chapter-gear.html#armour-points","t":"What each piece is worth against a blow, from the mod's own numbers. For comparison, a whole set of the game's diamond is worth 20 with 2 toughness, and netherite 20 with 3 toughness and a tenth of the knockback off for each piece. Set Helmet / chest / legs / boots Whole set Toughness (each piece) Knockback off (each piece) The Vigil 2 / 7 / 6 / 2 17 1.5 - The Scarecrow 2 / 7 / 5 / 2 16 1 - The Bloomwoven 3 / 8 / 6 / 3 20 2 - The Specimen 3 / 8 / 7 / 3 21 2.5 10% Dead Air 3 / 9 / 7 / 3 22 3 10% The Usher's Uniform 3 / 8 / 7 / 3 21 3 - On Air 4 / 9 / 7 / 4 24 4 15% The UV Dive Suit 2 / 6 / 5 / 2 15 1 5% The Ember Deep Suit 4 / 9 / 7 / 4 24 4 30% Blackout 4 / 10 / 8 / 4 26 5 20%"},{"p":"Gear for every chapter","h":"The weapons","u":"items/chapter-gear.html#weapons","t":"Two for each of the first seven chapters, and Chapter Ten's Blackout Blade. A fully charged swing (wait for the attack meter) sets off the weapon's power; use (right-click) sets off its ability, which takes ten seconds to come back. Damage and speed are the item's own numbers, as its tooltip shows them. Weapon Power What its tooltip says Damage / speed Recipe The Censer Chapter One Incense A church censer on its chain, still smouldering. Full swings blind and slow. Use: whirl it round you, striking all close 7 / 1.2 G H G / . N . / . S . G gold ingot, H Hymnal Page, N iron chain, S stick The Bell Clapper Chapter One Toll The clapper out of the Hollow's bell. Full swings throw back hard and stagger. Use: strike the ground - the toll rings out 9.5 / 0.7 H B H / . I . / . S . H Hymnal Page, B bell, I iron ingot, S stick The Pitchfork Chapter Two Pin Three rusted tines. A long reach. Full swings pin it where it stands, bleeding. Use: lunge, and carry what you skewer 7.5 / 1.3 I . I / I B I / . S . I iron ingot, B Blighted Straw, S stick The Omen Staff Chapter Two Omen An eye in a cage, and it looks back. What it strikes takes 30% more from anything. Use: the eye opens on all before you 6.5 / 1.6 . E . / . D . / . S . E eye of ender, D Devil's Horn, S stick The Thorn Whip Chapter Three Lash A vine off the Bloom, thorned. The longest reach. Full swings bleed it and draw it in. Use: lash out and drag it to you 7 / 1.7 K K F / . K . / W . . K Knotted Root, F Heartbloom, W Bloom Heartwood The Spore Mace Chapter Three Bloom Heartwood, grown over with the Bloom's fungus. Full swings poison. Use: a cloud of spores where you aim 9.5 / 1.0 . M . / M F M / . W . M red mushroom, F Heartbloom, W Bloom Heartwood The Bone Saw Chapter Four Rend Surgical steel, its teeth clogged. Full swings open the wound twice over. Use: rev it - all in front of you is torn at 7.5 / 1.8 . I T / . I . / S . . I iron ingot, T Stalker Talon, S stick The Reactor Rod Chapter Four Meltdown A control rod out of the reactor pool. Its touch withers. Use: vent the core - a wave that withers all round 8.5 / 1.3 . G . / I Y I / . I . G glowstone dust, I iron ingot, Y Bloater Gland The Tuning Fork Chapter Five Resonance It never quite stops ringing. Full swings ring on: the blow lands again, through armour. Use: a line of sound, through all on it 8 / 1.8 I . I / I V I / . D . I iron ingot, V Vacuum Tube, D"},{"p":"Gear for every chapter","h":"The tools","u":"items/chapter-gear.html#tools","t":"A pickaxe, an axe, a shovel and a hoe for each chapter, made the way the game's own are (the axe strips logs, the shovel makes paths, the hoe tills), with the chapter's token in one square. Iron's worth in the first chapters, up to netherite's in the last. Each chapter's four share a perk, shown on the tooltip. Tools Perk Mines like / speed Made with (M, X) Gravedigger's Chapter One Unearth: What you dig out of soil, sand and gravel isn't always only that Iron / 7 Iron ingots, Grave Claw Harvestman's Chapter Two Reap: Ripe crops sow themselves again; the axe fells the whole tree Iron / 7.5 Iron ingots, Blighted Straw Heartwood Chapter Three Overgrowth: Twice as fast through wood and green; leaves give their saplings. Crouch-use: it grows Diamond / 8.5 Bloom Heartwood, Knotted Root Surgical Steel Chapter Four Scan: Use: the ores round you show through the stone for six seconds Diamond / 9 Diamonds, Hive Comb Static Chapter Five Chain: The break runs on through up to six more of the same block, touching Diamond / 9.5 Diamonds, Carrier Thread Stagehand's Chapter Six Hush: The things that listen don't hear your work. Glass and ice come away whole Netherite / 10 Netherite scrap, Ticket Stub Hub-Stone Chapter Seven Skip: The block behind breaks too (crouch: just the one). The hoe tills three Netherite / 11 Netherite ingots, Rerun Reel Blackout Chapter Ten Silent: Nothing you do with it makes a sound they can hear. Blackout ore comes away fast. Netherite / 12.5 Blackout Ingots (no token) The shapes, with M the material and X the token: pickaxe M X M / . S . / . S . , axe M X / M S / . S , shovel X / M / S , hoe M X / . S / . S (S stick). The Blackout tools are made in the game's own shapes, all Blackout Ingot: pickaxe I I I / . S . / . S . , axe I I / I S / . S , shovel I / S / S , hoe I I / . S / . S ; what they break goes to static with a soft dead crackle. For comparison, the game's own iron tools mine at 6, diamond at 8 and netherite at 9. Each set moves too: the gravedigger's nail rattles, the harvestman's straw and the heartwood's leaves stir, the surgical lights blink, the static valve flickers, the stagehand's tag swings on its cord, and the band of Hub stone turns."},{"p":"Gear for every chapter","h":"Where the makings come from","u":"items/chapter-gear.html#the-makings","t":"Token From Hymnal Page The Hymnal Grave Claw The Underneath Blighted Straw The Harvestman; the Murder Mansion's chests Bloodied Stuffing The Bunnyman; the Murder Mansion's chests Devil's Horn The Jersey Devil; the Murder Mansion's store Knotted Root Rootlings, the Gardener; the Bloom's research station Heartbloom The Gardener; the glasshouse's Seed Vault Bloom Heartwood The Gardener, Reborn Hive Comb, Splitter Sinew, Stalker Talon, Bloater Gland The Flesh's mutants: the Hive; Splitters and Crawlers; Stalkers; Bloaters Frame of the Last Reel Afterimages at the Starlite; the Null ruins Carrier Thread The Carrier (6 to 10) Ticket Stub The Audience (some of them), the Ushers and the Crowd Vacuum Tube The Tuned (some of them) and the Projectionist Listener's Ear Listeners, in the Deep Rerun Reel A replay beaten again (below) Ember Plating, Heat Coil, Pressure Seal, Vent Glass The Ember Crew's trade, at the Ember Pumping Station ( more ) Signal Fragment His creations, his servants and the Faithful; his broadcast cores and his sites' chests ( more ) Blackout Shard Blackout Ore, deep down; his servants; his broadcast cores and his sites' chests ( more )"},{"p":"Gear for every chapter","h":"The Rerun Reel","u":"items/chapter-gear.html#rerun-reel","t":"Rerun Reel AS SEEN BEFORE Left behind by a replay, beaten again. Chapter Seven's gear is made with it. Walk into one of the replay portals in the Hub and that chapter's last fight comes back for another go. Beat it again and it leaves three or four Rerun Reels behind. All of Chapter Seven's gear (On Air, the Antenna Glaive, the On Air Mace, the Hub-Stone tools) is made with them. First one earns Rerun ."},{"p":"Gear for every chapter","h":"The gloves","u":"items/chapter-gear.html#the-gloves","t":"Three of the older gloves (two weapons and a climbing glove) were made again in 1.61.1 and are worn on the hand. Their recipes and powers are on Items and blocks . Rending Claws Frenzy Black stitched hide sewn with bone-pale thread, a ruff of the Dogman's grey fur at the wrist, an iron plate on the back of the hand with a cracked little screen in it, static still crawling on it. From every fingertip a long barbed blade of blued steel, a shorter one on the thumb, and one of the Dogman's fangs swinging on a cord. Now and then they drum their blades one finger after another. Their swing is a rake: down and across, then back the other way. Brute Knuckles Hurl An iron gauntlet over a black glove, the Brute's knuckle-bones and their spurs set in its knuckle bar, its reflective band riveted over the back, the wrist bound in Splitter sinew with a torn strip of the coat hanging off it. Now and then the fist clenches, leather creaking, iron knocking. Stalker Claws A climber's glove of brown leather with three of the Stalker's long fingers lashed along its own, their black nails hooking out past them. The talons click, one after another, and flex."},{"p":"Gear for every chapter","h":"Heads, worn","u":"items/chapter-gear.html#heads","t":"Since 1.60.0 every creature head can go on your head. It goes on over your own (yours is hidden under it), and the edges of your screen darken as you look out through it. Wear it Its own kind take you for one of them: they notice you from only half as far off. The heads are the ones the creatures of chapters one to three drop: see the bestiary ."},{"p":"Gear for every chapter","h":"How they swing","u":"items/chapter-gear.html#the-swing","t":"Since 1.61.0 every one of the mod's weapons and tools swings its own way, in first person, in third, and for everyone watching. Blades cut from high right to low left; cleavers, axes, maces and hammers come up over the shoulder and down hard; scythes, glaives and the censer sweep flat round; the thorn whip and the fly hook crack; the bone saw saws, two strokes; knuckles and claws jab; staves turn over in the hand and come round; the needle, the pitchfork and the tuning fork thrust; picks swing short, spades dig, hoes chop. The blow lands a tenth of a second or so after the click. Where a blow lands there's a flash, a white-hot star and its shock ring in the weapon's own colour (blood, bone, static, hellfire, sap, candle-flame, film-gold...), bigger for heavy weapons, big targets and criticals, with sparks flung the way the swing went, and the sound of the blow under the weapon's own: an edge biting, something heavy landing, a point going in, with a bright ring on a critical. Since 1.61.1 one-handed weapons are held a little forward, the long ones across the body in both hands and the heavy ones low in both hands, and in first person a weapon trails your turning, dips with each step and is carried low at a run. In the HD pack every texture of the chapters' gear is four times the mod's own, upscaled with an AI upscaler (Real-ESRGAN)."},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"","u":"items/index.html","t":"Item text on this page is copied from the mod as it appears in game: the name, the power line in red, and the description in grey. Icons are the mod's own textures. Every recipe unlocks in the recipe book as soon as you pick up what it's made from. Gear for every chapter Since 1.60.0 each chapter has its own armour set, two weapons and four tools. They have a page of their own , with every recipe. So do the Dead Water's two dive suits and Chapter Ten's Blackout gear."},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"The Relay Core","u":"items/index.html#relay-core","t":"Relay Core Tunes you in to them What the relay's signal ran through. Hold it to your ear: for thirty seconds every one of the parasite's own shows through anything, a long way off. From: the Amalgam at Relay 6, when it dies. Chapter: five. Use: hold it to your ear and you're Tuned In for thirty seconds (\"You tune in. Under the static, there they are.\"): every one of the parasite's own within 96 blocks shows through anything, violet. Then it needs a minute and a half to warm up again. Why you need it: Tuned In, you can hurt the Afterimages at the Starlite Drive-In (\"tuned in, they're as real as you are\"), and it has to be on you to tune the projector for the last reel. First use earns Tuned In . Related block: the Tether , the knot of sinew lashed to each of Relay 6's platforms, its veins lit. Tether Break the one on each platform to cut the Amalgam off from the relay."},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"Compasses and needles","u":"items/index.html#compasses","t":""},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"Civil Defence Compass","u":"items/index.html#civil-defence-compass","t":"Civil Defence Compass Its needle is set on Rosemont Shelter No. 4. Left on the dais in Bunker B. If the shelter falls, make for the city. From: the locker the Watcher leaves on the dais in Bunker B after you kill the Warden of Shelter No. 4, with bread, torches and a golden apple. Points: at Rosemont, wherever you are. Added in 1.39.1."},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"The Watcher's Needles","u":"items/index.html#watchers-needles","t":"From the Uplink Station on, whenever a new place wakes, the Watcher hands every player a needle: a compass that only ever points there. Its name is in dark purple and it never glints. Needle Its line Given when Watcher's Needle (Uplink Station) Where they talked to the gun. The array is there. The Bloom changes Watcher's Needle (Capacitor Works) Still holding its charge. The cell is there. The Bloom changes Watcher's Needle (Soul Well) Where they put the souls. The strongest is at the bottom. The Bloom changes Watcher's Needle (Ashford Nuclear Plant) Its reactor never went cold. The core is in its heart. The Orbital Railgun is built Watcher's Needle (Meridian Laboratory) Where they built what tears a charge loose. The destabilizer is there. The Orbital Railgun is built Watcher's Needle (Blackwater Station) Out in the sea. Something got loose in it. The blood is there. The Orbital Railgun is built (with an oak boat) Watcher's Needle (Relay 6) Where their static goes out from. Something holds on to the mast. The Bloom is dead Watcher's Needle (the Starlite) Where the last of their static runs down to. A screen showing nothing. Relay 6 is off the air Watcher's Needle (The Hive) Where it's growing itself a mind. The Chorus is down in the pit. After the hive speaks (or when you walk into the hive first) Watcher's Needle (The Sinkhole) Where the ground was pulled down from underneath. It went down there. Never handed out in 1.63.3: it exists only as a name. The Chorus Fragment is what leads you to the sinkhole. Every needle's power line reads \"Points to one of the places that woke\"."},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"The Altar, Cathedral, Mansion and Gardens Needles","u":"items/index.html#site-needles","t":"Since 1.63.2, compasses you can make for the places you go back to (the Cathedral Needle since 1.72.3). Use one and its needle swings round and settles on the nearest of its place (\"The needle settles on the Forsaken Altar - 412 blocks north-east\", for example); after that it points there wherever you go in the Overworld, until you use it again. With none anywhere near: \"The needle spins and spins. There's none anywhere near.\" Anywhere but the Overworld: \"The needle won't settle. What it's looking for is up in the Overworld.\" Their shared power line: Use it: it finds the nearest one, and points there . Since 1.63.4 they find their place from anywhere: where it stands, or where it will rise the first time you come near. You start with three. Since 1.72.3 the Altar Needle, the Cathedral Needle and the Gardens Needle go into your inventory the first time you join a world. A world you've already played gives them to you the next time you join, once only. The Mansion Needle you still make. Altar Needle Use it: it finds the nearest one, and points there For the altars the old things were given to. Recipe: a compass, a candle and a bone. Finds the nearest Forsaken Altar. Cathedral Needle Use it: it finds the nearest one, and points there Recipe: a compass, a purple stained glass pane and a candle. Finds the Cathedral of the Hollow . A brass case like the others, with a violet ring and a faint cathedral on its face. New in 1.72.3. Mansion Needle Use it: it finds the nearest one, and points there For the house where it all went wrong. Recipe: a compass, an iron sword and redstone. Finds the nearest Murder Mansion. Gardens Needle Use it: it finds the nearest one, and points there For the glasshouses, and what grew in them. Recipe: a compass, a glass pane and any small flower. Finds the nearest Botanic Gardens. The README calls these the Forsaken Altar, Murder Mansion and Botanic Gardens Compasses; in game they're named as above. The Chorus Fragment works like a needle too: see below . And in the Dead Water, the Watcher's Chart is a map."},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"The power source parts","u":"items/index.html#power-source","t":"When the Bloom changes, the Watcher tells you there's a gun above the sky that needs a power source, and three places wake. A tracker along the top of your screen counts THE POWER SOURCE (0/3) . Targeting Array SENTINEL's lock Pulled out of the dish when the city fell. It tells the gun where to look. Where: the Uplink Station, in the locker in the control bunker by the consoles, with Lt. Okafor's duty log, bread, iron and two flashbangs. Infected operators, a sniper and a breacher hold the compound. Capacitor Cell Works cell 9, fully charged Nobody came to collect it. It holds what the gun needs to fire. Where: the Capacitor Works, in the test cage at the back, past arcs jumping between the lightning rods. See the live banks . Bound Soul The strongest soul in the well Its keepers knelt by it for years. It will hold the Watcher's darkness. Where: the bottom of the Soul Well, thirty blocks down, on the altar where its keepers kneel (they get up when you come close; two of the Interred wait too). With bones, candles and echo shards. Orbital Core SENTINEL's power source The array, the cell and the soul, made one. Set it on a Forsaken Altar. Recipe: the Targeting Array, the Capacitor Cell and the Bound Soul, with iron and redstone. Set it on a Forsaken Altar and the Watcher comes and pours itself into it (\"that's me. all of me that's left.\"). Infused Orbital Core The Watcher is in it It drinks the light round it. Build the gun round it. Orbital Railgun Hold to lock on, release to fire (12s recharge) It doesn't shoot. It tells SENTINEL where. 16 to 200 blocks, open sky only. The only thing that can hurt the changed Bloom. Recipe: the Infused Orbital Core, iron blocks, a copper block, lightning rods, iron and a spyglass. Use: hold use and aim at the ground 16 to 200 blocks off, in the Overworld (\"No uplink. There's no sky here for it to talk to.\" anywhere else). Its laser paints the spot, a ring locks on, the capacitors whine up for two and a half seconds: LOCKED - RELEASE TO FIRE. Let go and the slug comes out of the sky: sixty damage, fire and a shockwave out to twelve blocks."},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"The Ray Gun and the Omni","u":"items/index.html#ray-gun-parts","t":"Building the Orbital Railgun wakes three more places. A tracker counts THE RAY GUN (0/3) . Nuclear Reactor Core Out of Ashford's reactor A fuel assembly. Its rods still glow. One of the three things the Ray Gun's made of. Where: Ashford Nuclear Plant, in the fuel pool. Don't go in the water without a suit; the decon lockers have one. Discharge Destabilizer Out of the Meridian lab It can't hold what's in it for long. One of the three things the Ray Gun's made of. Where: Meridian Laboratory, in the glass cell in the middle of the ring (\"mind the coils\"), with redstone and amethyst. Vial of Dark Matter Blood Out of Blackwater's sample freezer It isn't a liquid. There are stars in it. One of the three things the Ray Gun's made of. Where: Blackwater Station, out at sea, in the freezer at the back. Parasites. Ray Gun Hold to aim, attack or let go to fire (2 min recharge) The Orbital Railgun, rebuilt round what the Bloom brought. 24 blocks across, the whole height of the world. The Watcher wants it. Recipe: the Orbital Railgun and the three parts, or bring them all to a Forsaken Altar. After the Omni is taken back, the Watcher burns this recipe out of every book. The Watcher turns the Ray Gun into the Omni Orbital Railgun ."},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"The reactor's parts and the Rosemont Device","u":"items/index.html#reactor-parts","t":"Each part is the only one there is: lose it and it goes back where you found it. The Rear and Front Assemblies won't go into anything but the Assembly Cradle; the Rear Assembly comes back a minute after it's lost (burnt, dropped in the void, left on the ground, shut away), and any copy crumbles in your hands. A tracker counts Reactor parts 0/3 . Item Its text From Rear Assembly One of the reactor's three parts. Off the army's truck in Rosemont's plaza. Heavy: it slows you. The Military Cradle in Rosemont (three axe blows) Reactor Core Lifted out of its rack at the bottom of the reactor pool. Hot. Everything infected wants it. The Laboratory's reactor hall (wakes Specimen Zero) Front Assembly Out of Bunker B, under Shelter No. 4. Bulky: you can't sprint with it. The dais in Bunker B (wakes the Warden) Assembly Cradle Holds the reactor's three parts. Set it down somewhere safe. The Rear Assembly goes in first, then the Core, then the Front. Comes with the Front Assembly The Rosemont Device There is only one. While you carry it, the Flesh lets you pass. The Bloom does not. Hold use on the full cradle for five seconds, or let the Watcher build it at a Forsaken Altar"},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"The parasite egg","u":"items/index.html#parasite-egg","t":"Parasite Pod The parasites' eggs. Their pods come up out of their black Xeno Resin and split open when you come near (\"Pod splits open\"); you'll hear them throb. Since 1.47.1 a pod is a round egg-sac, and split open it's a torn cup with its four flaps peeled back off the rim and the slime inside. Found at Blackwater Station and Relay 6. There is also a Parasite Spawn Egg (and a Parasite Host Spawn Egg) in the creative tab. Xeno Resin The parasites' black resin, creeping over everything where they nest. Static Hounds sometimes drop it."},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"Chapter five","u":"items/index.html#chapter-five-items","t":"Surgical Kit Cuts a parasite's brood out Hold it to cut one out of yourself. Use it on someone else to cut one out of them. It hurts. You bleed. Four uses. Recipe: shears, an iron ingot, string, paper and wool. Also in the Relay 6 operator's locker and sometimes in the Null ruins. Earns Cut It Out . Frame of the Last Reel What's left of an Afterimage A frame of film, torn off at both ends. In it, very small, someone standing in a field. Feed four to the Starlite's projector. The Last Reel Where they come from The reel off the Starlite's projector, seen through. A dented can with no label. The film inside is warm. Keep it. Held up to the light: \"something vast, curled under the ground. An eye, opening.\" Hold it over the tear at the drive-in to open the way to the Null Static Zone. Carrier Thread What it carried them on Pale, cold, and stronger than it looks. There's a vein of light down the middle of it. It isn't carrying anything now. 6 to 10 from the Carrier. Music Disc Static Hollow - Signing Off Dropped by the Carrier."},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"Chapter five: the hive and the Deep","u":"items/index.html#the-hive-and-the-deep","t":"Parts five and six of Chapter Five: the Hive , where the Chorus grows itself a mind, and the Deep , where it goes to ground. Chorus Fragment Hold it to your ear: it whispers A piece the Chorus left behind as it went down. It's still part of it, wherever it is. From: the floor of the Chorus's pit when it runs, one for everyone. A knot of grey-violet flesh with a face in it the size of a thumbnail, its eyes shut, its mouth moving. Use: hold it to your ear (every four seconds) and turn round. Facing the way the rest of it went, it whispers clear, and what it says tells you how far: \"down. a long way down. far from here - that way.\", \"that way. under the hills. we can feel you coming.\", \"closer. we can hear you walking. we can hear your heart.\", \"here. right under you. come down. it's warm.\" Side on it's faint and broken (\"...colder... no... turn...\"); facing away, only static. Up top it leads you to the sinkhole ( Warmer ); down in the Deep it leads you to where the Chorus has gone to ground (\"here. we are right here. we are finished growing.\"). With nothing to point at, it only mutters, things like \"we remember the dark under the hills.\" and \"every one we take remembers. every one remembers you.\" Listener's Ear One of the Deep's older ones' A fan of thin skin on rods of bone. It heard everything. Stitched over boots, it makes your steps nothing. From: Listeners, in the Deep. Also goes into the Usher's Shoes (see the chapter gear ). Hushed Boots Your steps make no sound Walk as quiet as sneaking: the Listener can't hear you, and the Deaf King has to be close to feel you. Recipe: leather boots, two Listener's Ears and string, in any order. Earns Not a Sound . The King's Ear-Stones So he wouldn't hear it singing Two plugs of the old ones' stone, warm, a spiral in each. Carry them and the Chorus's song can't get into you either. From: the Deaf King , when he dies and his crown cracks off. Anywhere in your inventory, they keep the song of the Chorus, whole, out of you in the last fight. Hold them to your ears and the world goes quiet a moment. The Last Voice The one voice it couldn't swallow A face cut out of the Chorus, its eyes open now. It isn't singing. It's trying to tell you something: a door at the end of the world, and the seal on it. From: the Chorus, whole, when it dies in the Warm Heart ( The Last Voice ). Hold it to your ear and it talks: \"...there's a "},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"Blocks","u":"items/index.html#hive-and-deep-blocks","t":"Hive Flesh The parasite's violet flesh, veined, that the hive is grown of; it lines the Burrow and the Warm Heart too. The Hive Hands drop it and Hive Chitin when they die. Hive Chitin Its black braided spires and the ribs arching over the pit. Nerve Node The glowing bulbs on top of the four stalks round the pit, glowing and pulsing, cords of light running from them to the Chorus. Tear one open and it screams; tear all four for Senseless . Biomass The heap of violet flesh one of the turned leaves where it died (since 1.49.0), veined and pulsing, chitin forced out through it. It drags at you as you wade through it, and a minute or two later it heaves itself up into one of the parasite's pure forms, leaving its torn husk. Burn it and nothing gets up. See the turned . In the Deep: The Throat (a ring of the hive's flesh, puckered shut: stand on it and it opens and takes you down, or back up), Deep Rock , Old Stone , Old Stone Bricks and Carved Old Stone (the pale worked stone of whoever was down there first), Bloom Root and Root Tendril (the Bloom's roots, gone deeper than anyone ever dug; the tendrils' ends glow) and Ember Cap (it glows like a coal on the cavern floors). Carved Old Stone The Deaf King drops three to six when he dies, with Bloom Root and diamonds. Bloom Root Great roots hanging down through the roofs of the Root Hollows."},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"Chapter six: the Door at the End of the World","u":"items/index.html#chapter-six-items","t":"The Stalls, the Watcher's Vault and the Other Side. See Chapter Six . Ticket Stub ADMIT ONE Soft old card, a seat number you can't read. Show one to an Usher and it looks away a while. From: some of the Audience, the Ushers, and the Crowd. Use: on an Usher: \"The Usher tears your ticket in two, and looks away.\" For a minute its lamp doesn't see you. Also goes into Chapter Six's gear. Usher's Lamp Held, it lights the dark round you Use it to flash: the Audience and the Ushers caught in it reel, hands over their faces - and the Crowd's Hush breaks. It needs a while to warm again. From: an Usher, now and then. A brass torch-lamp, its glass yellowed, still warm. The flash takes eight seconds to warm again. Flash it at one of the Tuned in the Vault and its screen whites out: it can't move for four seconds, watched or not. The Last Ticket ADMIT ONE - THE VAULT What was left in the middle of the Crowd. It's warm. On the back, in a thin black hand: THE VAULT. Hold it up to the seam in the screen. From: the Crowd , one for everyone who was there. Held up to the seam the Watcher leaves in the Great Screen in Front Row, it tears in two in your hand and the seam opens for good ( Admit One ); after that, \"The seam's open. Walk into it.\" Used anywhere else: \"ADMIT ONE. On the back, in a thin black hand: THE VAULT.\" Vacuum Tube Still warm Out of one of the Tuned's sets. It glows a little, faintly orange. Two of them, with glass and iron, make a set of your own. From: some of the Tuned, and the Projectionist; since 1.63.16 the Carrier Wave's valve bulbs and Handsets, and its dead drops. Makes: two Old Sets ( I G I / T R T / I I I : I iron ingot, G glass pane, T Vacuum Tube, R redstone), old televisions that hum, with static crawling on them; use one to switch it on or off. Also goes into the Tuning Fork, the Relay Staff and the Receiver . An Old Set that's on is where the HELP WANTED flyer turns up."},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"What he kept","u":"items/index.html#what-he-kept","t":"The three things in the Watcher's keeps, each on a plinth behind a round steel door. Bring all three to the Watch and the Projectionist steps down out of the sets ( What He Kept ). All three say KEPT FOR THE FUTURE and \"Take it to him, in the Watch.\" The Omni's Heart KEPT FOR THE FUTURE What made the Omni more than a gun: every colour at once, turning, in a cage of its own light. He took it out of it. Take it to him, in the Watch. Later he loads it into his last projector against the Viewer ( Every Colour at Once ). See the Omni . What's Left of the Carrier KEPT FOR THE FUTURE A knot of it, still beating. Static comes off it like heat. It carried whatever was put on it. It held a door open. Take it to him, in the Watch. Take it and its static pours out: every Tuned near you is loose for a few seconds. See the Carrier . His First Reel KEPT FOR THE FUTURE A film can, dented, the reel in it. On the lid, in his hand: THE OTHER SIDE. FIRST. DO NOT RUN. Take it to him, in the Watch. Kept in a glass case. He runs it after the Projectionist burns through. The Projectionist's Lens Held: you see what's watching you All that was left of it, in the ash: its lens, still warm. Hold it and everything hostile near you shows through the walls, outlined in its light. From: the Projectionist, with three to five diamonds, two to four echo shards and two to four Vacuum Tubes. Music Disc Static Hollow - Thank You for Watching Given to you after the last show, when the credits have rolled and you're sent home. See the soundtrack ."},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"Blocks","u":"items/index.html#chapter-six-blocks","t":"Seal-Stone Black, his glyphs cut in it ( Seal-Stone Glyph ), a few still faintly lit: the causeway out to the Door, and the Door's frame. In it hums The Door's Static . Stalls Asphalt The Stalls' ground, under the Picture House Seats . Facing them, The Great Screen of Screen Cloth . Vault Terrazzo The dark, flecked floor of the Watcher's archive. Its keeps are The Watcher's Concrete (it doesn't break). Also: Archive Shelves (steel, cans of film and boxes of tape, labels in his hand), Old Sets , Cable , the keeps' Keep Door and Keep Wheel (use it: five seconds of the bolts drawing back, and the door swings in), What He Kept (the plinths) and The Watch Wall . Stage Boards The Other Side: Stage Boards , Stage Flats and Painted Flats (each a picture of somewhere from the story), Footlights , The Screen's Back , His Last Projector and the Black Static the Door goes to. Black Static What fills the Door at the End of the World once the first reel has been run: the dark on the far side of it, looking out."},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"Chapter seven: the First Signal","u":"items/index.html#chapter-seven-items","t":"The Remote An old television's remote, heavy, its buttons worn smooth, the one with nothing on it warm. The Watcher gives it to you after the Hub , and it earns Channel Changer . Press it: you're in the Hub. Press it in the Hub: home. Before it has anywhere to go: \"You press the blank button. Nothing. Not yet.\" In 1.59 he handed it over when you landed at home (\"take this. if you need to go back - it's still there.\"). Since 1.62.0 the fall from the Hub goes to the Dead Water instead: he hands it over on the rig (\"take this. it'll get you back - to the hub, and home.\") and it cracks in your hand. See the Broken Remote . Mended, it does one more thing: \"Press it: the Hub (and in the Hub, home). Crouch and press it: back to the rig.\" In Chapter Nine it becomes the Remote (Mutated) . Hub Stone The pale stone of the Hub's floating plaza, with Hub Stone Slabs . Hub Glyph His marks, lit in the Hub's floor. Along its north side stand six Replay Portals , one for each chapter, each playing its chapter on an old set. The Rerun Reels that replays leave behind are on Gear for every chapter ."},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"Chapter eight: the Dead Water","u":"items/index.html#chapter-eight-items","t":"The rig's stores are full of these. See Chapter Eight and the Dead Water . The Broken Remote Dead - it broke in your hand in the Dead Water Its case cracked across, its wires out, the warm button cold. Mend it: this, a Static Leviathan's Signal Organ, a copper ingot. (The big ones live deep. They sing on its frequency.) Pressed: \"It sparks. The warm button's cold. Nothing.\" Mend it: the Broken Remote, a Signal Organ and a copper ingot, in any order, give you back the Remote (\"The Remote works again.\"). Harpoon Gun Hold to pump, let go to fire - in water or out Reels what it bites back to you - or you to it, if it's too big. Strike a wall or the sea floor and it hauls you there. Crouch to let go. Fire again while it's out to reel it in. Takes Harpoon Bolts. Recipe: I I P / S C I / W . . (I iron ingot, P piston, S string, C copper ingot, W any planks). Also in the rig's armoury and its dive locker. Harpoon Bolt The Harpoon Gun's ammunition Barbed steel, an eye for the cable. It comes back with the harpoon - unless it snaps off in what it struck. Recipe: . T . / . I . / . N . (T Needle Tooth, I iron ingot, N iron nugget) makes two. Also in the rig's armoury and dive locker. Marine Flare Burns red for a minute - even underwater Strike it and throw it. In the sea it sinks slowly, lighting the dark on its way down. Recipe: gunpowder, redstone, paper and red dye, in any order, make three. All over the rig's stores. Rig Ration A meal in a tin Stamped R. The rig's larders are full of them. Someone stocked this place a long time ago. Recipe: dried kelp, bread, cooked cod and an iron nugget make two. In the mess, the food stores and the bunks. Air Tank Underwater: use it to breathe - your air back to full A diver's bottle off the rig's dive locker. Good for a dozen breaths. Recipe: . G . / I K I / I S I (G gold ingot, I iron ingot, K dried kelp block, S string). In the dive locker, the sub bay, sunken lifeboats and the flooded habitat dome. It can't be filled again. The Watcher's Chart The Dead Water, every one of its waters Use it to unroll it. The black hatched in red is the dead zone. Don't take the sub over it. The Watcher hands it to you when you come down to the Dead Water (since 1.63.2): four thousand blocks of sea round the rig, every water in its own colour and named, the floor's depths shaded and contoured, and the Black Below hatched out in red. Held, it's a"},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"ORPHEUS's upgrade bay","u":"items/index.html#upgrade-bay","t":"Since 1.63.8: use ORPHEUS's motor (aft, in the engine room) and her upgrade bay opens, five mounts for modules to fit, swap and take out as you like. What's in it is what she has, and the motor tells you her rating. Crouching and using a module on her still works: it goes into the bay. Once all three are in it (the Pressure Plating , the Depth Module and the UV Field Module), Chapter Nine begins. Depth Module (280 m) Submarine Upgrade Fit it in ORPHEUS's upgrade bay (the motor, aft): she's rated to 280 m Recipe: I C I / G R G / I C I (I iron block, C copper block, G tinted glass, R block of redstone). There's one in the parts crate on the catwalk of the rig's sub bay (a rig that was already up gets the crate too). Fitted, she's rated to 280 m, against 183 m with nothing. UV Field Module Submarine Upgrade Fit it in ORPHEUS's upgrade bay: a ring of UV lamps round her hull keeps Enzyme 1-2418 off her Recipe: E C E / G R G / E C E (E UV Emitter , C copper block, G glowstone, R block of redstone). Fitted, her floodlights burn violet: the Enzyme stays off her in the Haemal Reach and is burnt out of her crew, and if she's already going to flesh it burns it off her (her tentacles let go of whoever they're holding)."},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"The Static Heart","u":"items/index.html#the-static-heart","t":"The Static Heart From the Canticle's Anchor Warm, and beating - to no rhythm of its own. There's a picture in it, of nothing, always moving Keep it. Something is going to be made with it From: the chest in the hollow of the Canticle's anchor's crown, a hundred blocks of anchor on the floor of the void (go in on its west side). Added in 1.63.8."},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"Enzyme 1-2418 and the UV kit","u":"items/index.html#the-uv-kit","t":"Since 1.63.9 the Haemal Reach's water is full of Enzyme 1-2418, and without the right dress it gets into you (see the Dead Water ). Milk doesn't touch it. This is what gets it out again. The suit that keeps it out, the UV Dive Suit, is on Gear for every chapter . UV Lamp Burns It Out Held, it lights the dark - and the Stretched won't come into its light. Use it to flash it: a fifth of the Enzyme burnt out of you, the Stretched near you scorched and driven off; in ORPHEUS, flesh off her walls Recipe: . I E / I R I / K I . (E UV Emitter, I iron ingot, R redstone, K dried kelp). Also in the lockers at the Haemal Research Station, with the UV Dive Suit. After a flash it needs ten seconds to charge. Enzyme Inhibitor 1-2418 / One Dose The lab's auto-injector. Into your thigh: half of the Enzyme in you gone, and for thirty seconds none of it takes. Even when the Heart has you, it can still get you loose From: the Haemal Research Station: two or three in the office, with its log, and more in its other chests and lockers. The Stretched drop them too. Research Log, HRS-3 Project 1-2418 Haemal Research Station's last log book, in its sealed sleeve. Use it to read it, an entry at a time From: the office chest at the Haemal Research Station. Use it and it reads you one entry at a time, in order, then round again. All nine entries are on Notes and books . Photophore Light Organ Out of a Lanternlet. Its core still burns, blue-violet, and it doesn't stop when you cut it out. (UV.) From: Lanternlets; the lab's chests. The Ember Crew buy them. Goes into UV Emitters. Glow Gel Luminous Jelly A Thimble Jelly's light, scraped out of it: a glob that glows on its own. Put it round a filament and it carries the UV From: Thimble Jellies, the Stretched; the lab's chests. Goes into UV Emitters. UV Emitter Ultraviolet A tube of violet glass, burning. Enzyme 1-2418 can't stand it: it's what a UV Lamp and ORPHEUS's UV Field are made of Recipe: C G C / P B P / C A C (C copper ingot, G Glow Gel, P Photophore, B Lantern Bulb, A amethyst shard) makes two. Also in the lab's chests and lockers."},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"The Ember Crew's trade","u":"items/index.html#ember-trade","t":"Since 1.63.10 the crew of the Ember Pumping Station trade: right-click one of them (crouch to just talk). They sell these four (and ancient debris, now and then) for iron, copper and gold, and buy Needle Teeth, Shroud Hide, Photophores and Signal Organs. They restock every half day. All four go into the Ember Deep Suit . Ember Plating is in the station's own chests too. Ember Plating Deep Suit Part Scorched alloy, cast at the Ember Pumping Station from what comes through the portal. The Ember Crew trade it for iron Goes into all four pieces of the suit. Heat Coil Deep Suit Part Copper wound round a core that never cools. It keeps a deep suit warm at the bottom of the void. (Traded for copper) Goes into the helmet, the hull and the legs. Pressure Seal Deep Suit Part A bronze ring and its gasket: what keeps the sea out of a joint at any depth there is. (Traded for gold) Goes into all four pieces of the suit. Vent Glass Deep Suit Part A port glass a hand thick, smoked orange. The Ember Crew pour it over the vents (traded for copper and needle teeth) Goes into the helmet."},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"The Drowned Mycelia","u":"items/index.html#mycelia-makings","t":"What its growth makes (since 1.63.13). A drowned diver's barrel in a Gillmaws' nest, in the caves under its floor, holds his teeth, his tonic, his bolts and his flares, and now and then his spear. Gillmaw Tooth Still sharp Out of a Gillmaw's cap, where the gills should be. It's warm. Spear tips, and nothing better. From: Gillmaws; the divers' barrels. Gillmaw-Tooth Spear Catches and holds A spear tipped with a Gillmaw's teeth, lashed with hyphae. What it hits is slowed - the more so in the water. Recipe: . . T / . S . / S . . (T Gillmaw Tooth, S stick), like any spear: it lunges and charges like the others. Drifter Jelly Tastes of the dark Out of a Spore Drifter's bell. For a while after, you see in the dark under the water, and breathe longer. It's full of spores From: Spore Drifters; the divers' barrels. Spore Pouch Throw it A drifter's bladder stuffed with spores. Bursts in a cloud four blocks round: the dark, the sickness - and hunters lose you. Sea things scatter; a Gillmaw clamps shut. Don't stand in it yourself Recipe: Drifter Jelly, string and a brown mushroom make two. Spore Tonic Burns going down Charcoal, brine salt and kelp, steeped black. The divers' own cure: most of the spores burnt out of you, and for a minute none of them take. The caps on you wither Recipe: a glass bottle, charcoal, sugar and dried kelp. It burns sixty of the spores out of you, and for a minute none of them take. Milk does nothing. Lantern-Cap Lamp Recipe: . H . / G L G / N G N (H Hanging Hyphae, G glass pane, L Lantern Caps, N iron nugget). A jar of lantern caps, still alive, still lit: as bright as a lantern, and it doesn't go out under the sea. It stands or hangs. Hyphae Rope Ladder Recipe: H . H / H H H / H . H (H Hanging Hyphae) makes four. It goes on a wall like a ladder, or hangs free from the underside of anything; use one on a ladder already hung and it unrolls another rung from the bottom."},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"The Brine Sink and the Rime Shelf","u":"items/index.html#brine-and-rime","t":"Made and eaten since 1.63.14. Brine Salt Sharp and bitter Salt out of the Brine Sink. It keeps fish - salt one and it'll last. It won't do your thirst any good From: Halite (break it, or one Halite makes three) and Wavers. Salted Fish Keeps forever Filling - but it's salt all through. You'll be thirsty after Recipe: a raw cod or salmon and Brine Salt. Pickled fish give it too. Mussels Raw Off the shores of the brine pools. Cook them - raw, they might turn your stomach From: mussel beds round the brine pools; Wavers. Cooked Mussels Steamed open Good, honest food, down here. Mussels in a furnace, a smoker or on a campfire. Blubber Warms you through A Rimeback's fat. Not much of a meal, but it keeps the cold off you for a long while From: Rimebacks, and the flesh on a fallen whale. Frost Shard Colder than it should be Ice off the Rime Shelf that won't melt in your hand. Pack it round brine salt and it keeps the cold in From: anchor ice (or one Anchor Ice makes two), brinicles, fish in the ice, Rime Striders and Rimebacks. Rime Charge Throw it Frost shards packed round brine salt and bound tight. It bursts in a flash of cold three blocks round - whatever's in it is frozen nearly still, and the floor ices over Recipe: two Frost Shards, Brine Salt and string make two."},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"The Lantern Fields and the Wireweed Forest","u":"items/index.html#lanterns-and-wire","t":"Made and found since 1.63.15. Coral Wax Burns under water Out of candle coral. Twist it round a string and the flame won't go out, wet or dry From: candle coral. Sea Candle Recipe: Coral Wax and string make two. A candle that burns under the water. Drowned Lantern Recipe: N N N / N C N / N N N (N iron nugget, C Sea Candle). The Lantern Fields' own, standing about still lit. Lantern Tether Recipe: three string make three. To hang a lantern on. Moth Dust Glitters in the dark Off a Lantern Moth's wings. It's what lights them - and it gets in your eyes From: Lantern Moths and Lampmothers. Lumen Lure Throw it Moth dust packed in glow ink, on a string. It hangs where it stops and shines for half a minute: the sea's light-lovers come to it - and anything hunting you goes for it instead Recipe: two Moth Dust, a glow ink sac and string make two. Copper Wire Still carries a charge From the Wireweed Forest's copper moss, and what lives on it. Or draw your own from an ingot From: copper moss, Wirecutters, Coilbacks and Handsets; or a copper ingot makes four. Fuse Full of current What a fuse pod leaves when it blows. Wind it in copper wire and it'll let all that current go at once From: fuse pods (touch one and it blows: a shock, and a fuse to pick up); Wirecutters. Live Wire Recipe: a Fuse and three Copper Wire make four. Strung over the floor, it shocks anything that comes through it but you. Arc Charge Throw it A fuse wound in copper wire. Where it bursts, the charge jumps from one living thing to the next - five of them, six blocks a jump, harder in the water. Never back to you Recipe: a Fuse and two Copper Wire make two."},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"The Ossuary Flats and the Carrier Wave","u":"items/index.html#bones-and-broadcast","t":"Made and found since 1.63.16. Vacuum Tubes come from the valve bulbs and the Handsets now too. Skull Something lived in it Off a skullkeep's back. Put a sea candle inside it and it makes a lantern From: skullkeeps. Skull Lantern Recipe: a Skull and a Sea Candle. A lantern with its eyes lit, wet or dry, standing or hanging. Whalebone Bricks Recipe: W W / W W (W Whalebone, from the whale falls) makes four. Sleeper Meat Poisonous raw Off a Sleeper. Eaten raw it makes you reel and sicken. Cure it in brine salt first From: Sleepers. Cured Sleeper Your eyes open in the dark Sleeper meat cured in brine salt: rank, strong - and you'll see in the deep for a minute and a half Recipe: Sleeper Meat and Brine Salt. Magnetic Tape Something's recorded on it From tape weed, and the echo jellies. Too slow and too low to make out what it says From: tape weed and echo jellies. Receiver Picks up the broadcast Carry it when the Carrier Wave's horns read out their numbers and it keeps them. Use it to hear them again - and hold it: its crackle tells you how near you are Recipe: V A V / C T C / I I I (V Vacuum Tube, A Antenna Weed, C Copper Wire, T Magnetic Tape, I iron ingot). Also left at the dead drops and the diving bells. When the broadcast goes out with it on you: \"Your receiver crackles: it caught the numbers.\" Before then: \"...static. Nothing on its tape yet.\" Horn Speaker Recipe: . I / I C / . I (I iron ingot, C Copper Wire). To build with, with the Dish Plate (two iron ingots and white dye make four)."},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"The Molar Reef and the Dead Water","u":"items/index.html#teeth-and-nets","t":"Made and found since 1.63.17. Milk Tooth Somebody's A child's tooth, out of the Molar Reef's gum. Three on a string, and the fairy leaves you be From: milk teeth on the reef's floor, Gnashers and tooth fairies. Tooth Charm The Tooth Fairy leaves you be Milk teeth on a string. Carry it, and the fairy won't come to take anything of yours Recipe: string and three Milk Teeth. Reef Gum Chew it Out of a gum blister. It numbs: the toothache goes, and the sickness with it From: gum blisters. Chew it: the toothache, the sickness and the slowness all go, and it wets your mouth a little. Enamel Shard Hard as a tooth Off the Molar Reef's teeth. Four of them make a block of enamel again From: the giant teeth (enamel and decay), Gnashers and the tooth cavities. Four make a block of Enamel ; four Enamel make four Polished Enamel . Ghost Net Recipe: S S / S S (S string). A net of your own, to hang, or to catch things in: swim into the mesh and it holds you slow. Crab Pot Recipe: S F S / N . N / W W W (S stick, F Net Float, N Ghost Net, W any planks). Set it in water and leave it. Come back and it's full: fish, mussels, ink, now and then something from the rig's crew. Use it to haul it up. Rusticle There's iron in it yet Rust off the rig's iron. Smelt it and you'll get a nugget back From: the rusticles on sunk girders. Smelt it for an iron nugget. Crew Tag A name, stamped in One of the rig's crew wore it. The name's worn too far to read From: the Catch, crab pots and the diving bell."},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"What the deep things drop","u":"items/index.html#sea-drops","t":"Signal Organ From: the Static Leviathan (with bone blocks, Needle Teeth and a heart of the sea). In the Overworld it lives in the deepest oceans, the Hadal Dark and the Trench; in the Dead Water, now and then one comes up out of the dark after you once you're forty blocks or more under the surface (never in the Black Below, which is the Undertow's). It sings on the Remote's frequency, and its organ is what mends it. Shroud Hide From: Shroud Rays and the Mouth of the Floor; also in the habitat dome and the frozen outpost. Goes into Pressure Plating. Needle Tooth From: Needlemaws, the Static Leviathan and the Mouth of the Floor; also in the habitat dome and Sink Station. Goes into Harpoon Bolts and Pressure Plating. The creatures themselves are in the bestiary , and the Undertow has a page of its own ."},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"The sea's blocks and plants","u":"items/index.html#sea-blocks","t":"Every water has its own floor: Ash Silt , Clotted Silt , Rust Silt , Glow Sand , Bone Sand , Brine Crust , Gum Silt , Spore Silt , Rime Silt , Ember Crust , Static Sand and Abyss Silt . Growing on them, waterlogged where they grow: Grey Kelp , Vein Kelp (it glows), Wireweed , Signal Bulbs , Glow Anemones , Lantern Bulbs , Bone Coral and Bone Fans , Marrow Sponge , Clot Coral , Artery Anemones , Sulfur Tubes , Brine pools, Enamel Coral , Tooth Fans , Gum Sponge , Nerve Anemones , Drowned Stems and Drowned Caps , Spore Puffs (they burst in your face), Gill Glow , Rime Ice , Frost Anemones , Frozen Corpses , Vent Chimneys , Tube Worms , Static Coral , Antenna Weed , Void Moss , Drowned Sets , Sea Lights and Eye Pods (shut till you come near; then the eye opens and follows you). Since 1.63.12 the waters have more of their own (giant drowned mushrooms, brine pools, lantern trees, cable trees, whale falls, listening dishes, giant teeth, ghost nets): see the Dead Water . The submarine's Sub Clamps are under the water of the rig's sub bay, where she berths: they charge and mend ORPHEUS, and if she's lost one used with nothing in hand builds her again for 16 iron ingots and 8 glass. Since 1.63.21 the Sub Bay Console stands on the catwalk by her berth: use it to see where she is, or, if nothing's heard from her, to have the bay's welders build her again in her clamps (a minute's work, nothing asked of you); crouch and use it to scrap her where she lies and build her again. And since 1.66.6, when she's lost, ORPHEUS's Emergency Locker blows free with everything that was in her lockers and the modules out of her bay, and floats at the top of the sea, its lamp blinking: use it to open it, and empty it to sink it. Glow Sand One of the twelve floors. Bone Sand The Ossuary Flats' floor."},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"Chapter nine: the Harbinger","u":"items/index.html#chapter-nine-items","t":"See Chapter Nine . The Static Heart (Mutated) Thrown up by the Harbinger The Undertow's static, grown through with the Grove's threads and the Reach's flesh. It still beats - a little faster than yours. Put it in the Remote (craft them together, broken or not). From: the Harbinger, three days after the Turning: it rises over the sea and brings the static heart up at your feet, one for each of you. The Remote (Mutated) It works again - and it roars Press: the Hub (in it: home). Crouch and press: the Dead Water. Hold, then let go: the Undertow's roar - everything near thrown back, and its echo shows you all that lives for a long way round. Recipe: the Static Heart (Mutated) with the Broken Remote, or with the mended Remote, in any order. It takes you to the Hub, home and back to the Dead Water, and it's more than it was: hold it, then let go, and the Undertow's roar comes out of your hand. Everything near you that isn't with you is thrown back, torn at and slowed (half as far again under water), and its echo makes everything alive for 48 blocks round glow. Then it's spent for fifteen seconds. The first roar earns Its Roar, In Your Hand ."},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"Chapter ten: Stay Tuned","u":"items/index.html#chapter-ten-items","t":"See Chapter Ten and his kingdom . Blackout's armour, blade and tools are on Gear for every chapter . Steel Locker Recipe: I I I / I B I / I I I (I iron ingot, B iron bars). Somewhere to hide: get in and pull the door to, and you see out through its vents and nothing sees in. One that's searching may come and stand at it, listening: if it heard you in there, or saw you go in, it tears it open and drags you out. (Crouch and use any bed to hide under it, too.) His burrows have lockers in them. Broadcast Core The heart of each of his sites (the transmitter, the burrow, the set: on a set it's the camera's eye). Break it and the site goes off the air: its lamps go out, it calls nothing more, and the core gives up what it was burning (Signal Fragments and Blackout Shards). Signal Fragment What's left of one of his creations A sliver of his broadcast, still showing its bars. From: his creations (the Longplay, the Hanger, the Lookalike, ERR, the Announcer, the Cameraman, the Stagehand, the Faithful) and the Encore; broadcast cores; his sites' chests. Blackout Shard Deep rock his static has soaked into Blacker than black. It takes the light. From: Blackout Ore; his servants (the Announcer, the Cameraman, the Stagehand), the Longplay and ERR; broadcast cores; his sites' chests. Blackout Ore Deep down, where his static has seeped into the rock near you after the Broadcast. It needs a diamond pickaxe, and it spits sparks and crackles. Blackout tools take it fast. Blackout Ingot The strongest there is Four shards, four fragments, netherite. Nothing gets through it - not even sound. Recipe: F S F / S N S / F S F (F Signal Fragment, S Blackout Shard, N netherite ingot). The first one earns Blackout . Faithful's Dagger His make What his Faithful give themselves to him with From: his Faithful, one time in five (since 1.69.0). A quick blade: 5 damage, 2.4 attack speed. His kingdom's own blocks (since 1.64.0): Signal Stone and Signal Bricks (with stairs, slabs and walls), Dead Screens and Signal Lamps . Signal Bricks From his kingdom. Dead Screen From his kingdom."},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"Tune-In Town","u":"items/index.html#tune-in-town-items","t":"Tune-In Town Pizza & Playhouse (since 1.65.0) is a secret: find the old place by the HELP WANTED flyer, go through its STAFF ONLY door into Studio B, and work the night shift. It has flashing lights, flickering screens, loud noises and jumpscares, and the game warns you before the first one. See Tune-In Town . Its things say what they are since 1.66.7 (before then their tooltips showed the names of their words). HELP WANTED Flyer Tune-In Town Pizza & Playhouse: Night Security, 12AM-6AM. Apply within. (It was on the television.) Use: read the address (which way, how far) From: the television (since 1.65.3). Once in a long while, any time after your first day, an Old Set that's on stops showing static and shows it; one dark night, out in the open, you'll come on a set left on in the grass, showing it; and on Chapter Ten's third day someone knocks three times and leaves a set on your step. Look at it, or use it, and the flyer's in your hand. Read it for the way to the old place. Its text is on Notes and books . Tune-In Token Good for one game at any Tune-In Town arcade cabinet Use it on an arcade cabinet: a prize From: the cast drop them, and they're part of your pay at 6 AM, with emeralds. Put one in any arcade cabinet: its little game, and a prize out of the tray. Employee Badge Tune-In Town - Night Security - Five Nights Served Somebody's name was scratched off it before yours Your pay for the fifth night. Music Disc Tune-In Town - The Showtape (Saturday's) The showtape: your pay for the sixth night. The show's own song, 1:36, till the tape runs slow and something else is on it. Security Card After hours, the cast take no notice of you; red eyes show through the dark Use: to Studio B from anywhere (and back). Doesn't fool the Mended Band For the fifth night (THE SECRET beaten), since 1.65.4. After hours the cast take no notice of you at all: they don't wake, don't come, don't go for you, and you can walk right up to them on the stage. Swipe it (use it) to go to Studio B from anywhere, and in Studio B, back where you came from. In the dark, anything hostile near you shows its eyes red, even through a wall. On the clock it's no use: on a shift, they come. Security Flashlight Held: a long hard beam - what it catches full in the face flinches Tune-In Town Night Security. Property of. Do not remove For the fifth night. A long, hard beam: it lights where it ends, "},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"Plushes","u":"items/index.html#plushes","t":"Since 1.65.4 beating a night pays a plush, and so does each Custom Night you beat (anyone who'd beaten nights before then gets what they're owed the next time they're in Studio B). Put them on a shelf; give one a squeeze. Plush Paid for Tony Tune Plush The first night Bucky Beaver Plush The second night Lulu Lark Plush The third night Tempo the Tortoise Plush The fourth night Rusty Rover Plush The fifth night Mister Channel Plush Your first Custom Night won Jack Jangle Plush Your second Custom Night won Spare Parts Plush Your third Custom Night won Chef Pete Plush Your fourth Custom Night won Employee of the Month Plush Your fifth Custom Night won Tix Plush Your sixth Custom Night won The Encore Plush The sixth night Golden Tony Plush A Custom Night won with every one of them on 20"},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"All three stars","u":"items/index.html#the-owner","t":"Three gold stars on the time clock (the fifth night, the sixth, and a Custom Night with every one of them on 20) and the place is yours (since 1.65.5): The Showstopper Its blow knocks things flying. Use: the spotlight - everything hostile near shows through the walls Tony Tune's own cane-microphone. Ladies and gentlemen... Tony Tune's cane-microphone, held as he holds it. Its blow lands like a rimshot and knocks what it hits flying. Use it: THE SPOTLIGHT (\"Ladies and gentlemen...\"), everything hostile within two dozen blocks lit up through the walls for a few seconds, every 15. 8.5 damage, 1.4 attack speed; it never wears out. The Owner's Key On you: Studio B's lights up, the cast wave hello, the Mended Band leaves you be Use: to Studio B (in it: where you wake up). On the time clock: bring a friend in With it on you, in Studio B the lights are up for you (off the clock), the cast turn, wave and say hello (\"Hi, boss!\"), and the Mended Band never comes for you. Use it anywhere else: into Studio B. Use it in Studio B: that's where you wake up now (again: not any more). Use it on the time clock: everyone online who isn't there, by name; click one and they're asked in. Golden Tony's Music Box Wind it: out pops Golden Tony, to follow you everywhere (wind it again: back in) He hums the show's song. He squeaks when something's about. Right-click him: stay / follow Wind it and out pops Golden Tony, a little gold Tony Tune of your own. He follows you everywhere (left behind, in another world, after you've logged off, he's beside you again), and when something hostile comes near he squeaks and points his cane at it. Nothing hurts him. Its blocks: Checker Tile , the Stage Curtain and Stage Lights , Marquee Lights , the Tune-In Town Sign , Security Shutters , Door Buttons and Light Buttons , Hall Lights , the Security Monitor , the Time Clock , the Office TV , the Music Box , Arcade Cabinets , eight Party Posters , Gift Boxes , the Ball Pit and the STAFF ONLY Door ; and since 1.71.1 its furniture: Party Tables , Diner Chairs and Diner Booths , Pizza , Soda Cups , Balloons , Soft-Play Padding and Netting , the Pizza Oven , the Menu Board , Party Bunting and the Gumball Machine . Arcade Cabinet Put a Tune-In Token in it. STAFF ONLY Door At the back of the old place, by the stage: the way into Studio B."},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"Out in the world","u":"items/index.html#out-in-the-world","t":"Things that aren't tied to a chapter. The thirst and the cold they belong to are on Cold, thirst and the world . Canteen Use on water to fill it - or hold it out in the rain: rainwater's clean A dented tin flask in a stitched leather sleeve. Someone's initials scratched into the cap. Recipe: . S . / L I L / . L . (S string, L leather, I iron ingot). Filled from water it's a Murky Canteen : Drink: 5 sips - may leave you Tainted. Boil it (furnace, smoker, campfire) to clean it . Boiled, or filled in the rain, it's a Clean Canteen : Drink: 5 sips of good water - more thirst back, and it cools you . The sips left show as its bar; the last one leaves it empty. Channel Zero Point it at the ground and press it. Crouch and press it: the next channel. CH 1 Falling Star - one star of the sky's static, on the spot. CH 2 Starfall - nine smaller ones all round it. CH 3 Dead Satellite - a dead satellite brought down, and its wreck. CH 4 Test Card - the sky's test card, its bars burned in one by one. Creative only for now (no recipe yet). A Falling Star leaves a crater lined with Static Stone and a Fallen Star glowing in it; Starfall drops nine small stars over four seconds; the Dead Satellite falls burning for five seconds and leaves a wreck and a satellite core's chest; the Test Card throws colour bars over the ground and burns each bar in turn. Craters only where the TNT game rule lets things blow up. Fallen Star At night shooting stars streak over the sky, and now and then a small one comes down somewhere near: a lump of glassy black rock, cracked all over, white-blue static crawling in the cracks, warm, lighting its crater. Mine it with a pickaxe for 2 to 4 Star Static (more with Fortune); Silk Touch keeps it whole. Star Static Out of a Fallen Star A splinter of the dead channel over the world. It's still warm. It crackles if you hold it to your ear. Also in a dead satellite's core."},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"Small things that share a block","u":"items/index.html#small-things","t":"Since 1.62.0, seven sets of little things that share one block space, one to four of a set, each turned to face whoever put it down. Place one on another to add a piece; break it and one piece comes off. You'll find them out in the Hollow's own country, on the deep sea floors, on the rig, in the cathedral's crypts and at the altar's pilgrim stones. Block Its text Recipe Grave Candles Tallow candles, a stub, a skull. Up to four in one space; light them. A candle and a bone Bone Pile A skull, its jaw, bones. Up to four in one space. Three bones Rot Caps The Blightwood's fungi. They glow a little, and breathe out spores. A brown mushroom and Rotgrass make two Hanging Chains Hung from a ceiling: chains, a hook, a shackle, a weight. They creak. Two iron chains Rig Clutter What's left lying about on the rig: a tin, an oil can, a wrench, bolts. Two iron nuggets and a copper ingot make two Cairn Stones Flat stones, stacked by pilgrims. The top one is carved. At night something whispers. Two cobblestone make two Ritual Offerings A bowl of ash, a straw doll, a red candle, dried herbs. A candle, wheat, a clay ball and red dye"},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"The Hollow's own country","u":"items/index.html#the-hollows-own-blocks","t":"The five places on the Hollow's side of the world (see the Hollow's own country ) have their own trees, plants and stone: Blightwood logs, leaves and saplings, Fen Willow logs, leaves and saplings with Willow Strands , Bonewood logs, needles and saplings, Deadwood , Peat , Hanging Rot , Rotgrass , Dead Heather , Wire Grass and Static Stone (it hums). Their logs make planks: Blightwood and Deadwood rotten planks, Fen Willow mangrove planks, Bonewood birch planks. Four Deadwood logs make three Deadwood. Blightwood Log From the Blightwood: close, bruise-coloured, rot caps glowing. Bonewood Log Pale and cold. Static Stone It hums. Fallen stars line their craters with it."},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"More of the land","u":"items/index.html#more-of-the-land","t":"1.66.0 to 1.66.3 gave the Hollow's country twenty-three more places of its own: nine over and under the ground, seven more, four in the Nether and three in the End (see the Hollow's own country ). Their blocks, in brief: Woods: Hangwood , Yew , Nightspruce (and Marked Nightspruce , eyes cut into it), Drowned Mangrove and Rotblossom logs, leaves (the Nightspruce's are Nightspruce Needles) and saplings; Driftwood . Over the ground: Nooses, Straw Effigies, Bone Chimes, Ghostfern, Bleached Bush, Finger Cactus, Rust Thorn, Mast Lamps, Throttle Vine, Choke Vine, Meat Flowers, Haunted Ice, Frozen Figures, Rime Stalks, Cliff Faces, Watching Stones, Blighted Wheat, Withered Sunflowers, Scarecrow Heads, Mourning Lilies, Black Roses, Funeral Bells, Headstones, Gloomcaps, Dead Lanterns, Root Hands, Bloated Lilies, Rot Petals, Flesh Blossoms, Pale Mycelium with Pale Cap Blocks, Pale Stems and Pale Caps, Puffballs, Ash Sand, Ash Grass and Rotting Blubber. Under it: Throat Flesh, Sinew Strands, Gut Pods and Throat Fangs; Echo Stone and Echo Crystals; Web Mass, Silk Cocoons and Egg Sacs. The Nether: Cinder, Charstone and Ember Charstone, Charred Figures, Ash Reeds, Smoulder Bush; Scab, Bleeding Netherrack, Vein Roots, Bloodcaps, Artery Vines, Heart Muscle and its Heart; Slag, Clinker, Static Vents, Furnace Grates, Cable, Wire Tufts, Spark Bulbs; Grave Nylium, Gallowwood and Gallowwood Sprouts, Rope Grass, Gallows Blooms and Gibbets. The End: Pale End Stone, Pale Chorus, Pale Blooms, Pale Moss, Pale Watchers; Husk, Husk Flakes, Carapace, Void Eggs, Flaked End Stone; Starless Stone, Dead Stars, Void Cracks and Star Ash. Hangwood Log The Hanging Wood's. Makes pale oak planks. Yew Log The Mourning Garden's. Makes dark oak planks. Nightspruce Log The Tall Dark's. Makes spruce planks. Drowned Mangrove Log The Drowned Roots'. Makes mangrove planks. Rotblossom Log Petal Rot's. Makes cherry planks. Gallowwood The Gallows Grove's. Makes crimson planks. Pale End Stone The Pale Reaches' ground. Starless Stone The Starless Barrens' ground. Smelts to end stone. Made from What it makes A Hangwood, Yew, Nightspruce, Drowned Mangrove or Rotblossom log; Gallowwood; Driftwood Four planks: pale oak, dark oak, spruce, mangrove, cherry, crimson, birch Black Rose; Bloodcap; Gallows Bloom; Mourning Lily or Pale Bloom Black, red, light grey or white dye Ash Sand (smelted) Tinted glass Charred Figur"},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"Survival and story items","u":"items/index.html#survival","t":"Item What it does From Saint's Heart A real heart, still beating. Goes into the Saint's Requiem. The Hollow Saint Saint's Shroud Smithing template: upgrades Static Mail to the Saint's Vestments with a Hymnal Page. The Hollow Saint (4 to 5) The Mended Heart Iron Will. Hold it up: three minutes of Resistance II, Strength I and Absorption II, then it has to beat itself warm again. The Mended Rusted Garden Key Opens the Botanic Gardens' gate. \"Something in there has waited a long time.\" The Mended Heartbloom It still beats. Eat it: made whole, hardened, healing, and everything green round you flowers. The Gardener Drift Jelly Slow Falling for 40 seconds and sight in the dark for 20. Eight iron nuggets round one make a Driftlight Lantern. Driftlights in the Void Lamprey Lure Still lit. Hold it and it lights your way. Lampreys (sometimes) Bloom Serum Cures the Flesh's infection and keeps it off you for twenty seconds. A glass bottle, a Bloom pustule and sugar; or a ghost orchid, a whispering lily and sugar. Crafted; the Congregation, Specimen Zero Flower Ash Bomb Throw it: the Flesh's growth dies back where it bursts, and anything infected in it burns. A garden flower, a burnt petal and gunpowder make two. Crafted; Specimen Zero Tainted Meat Fills you, and infects you. \"Starving, it might be worth it. It usually isn't.\" The Flesh's things Flashbang Blinds and deafens whatever can see it (you too); the infected caught in it stagger and lose you. Special forces infected Contaminated Syringe From the corner pharmacy. \"You wouldn't.\" Infected Pharmacists Bottle of Pills Eat: Regeneration, and Nausea. \"They help. Mostly.\" Infected Pharmacists Level 2 Keycard Opens the Laboratory's security doors. The director's desk; researchers Audio Log Play the tape, or put it in a tape recorder for everyone within about twenty blocks to hear. The Laboratory Fuel Canister Diesel for the shelter's generators. One of Shelter No. 4's lockers Brood Heart Brood Sight: the Flesh's things within 48 blocks show through walls for 30 seconds. 90 seconds to beat again. The Broodmother The Bellwether's Bell Ring it: the infected within 16 blocks stop and listen for three seconds. Half a minute to ring again. The Bellwether Bloom Heartwood Close-grained, pale, still warm. Green light runs in it like sap. The Gardener, Reborn (3) The Gardener's Seed A hard black seed the size of a fist, split alo"},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"Weapons","u":"items/index.html#weapons","t":"Big, detailed 3D weapons, held like a sword. A fully charged swing (wait for the attack meter) triggers the weapon's power; the second act's weapons also have a power on use, with a ten-second cooldown. The first four weapons and every armour piece are unbreakable, and those four can break blocks slowly, like a sword. Since 1.61.0 every weapon swings its own way, and since 1.61.1 the Rending Claws, Brute Knuckles and Stalker Claws are worn on the hand (see the gloves ). The fourteen chapter weapons added in 1.60.0 are on Gear for every chapter , with the Blackout Blade. The Gillmaw-Tooth Spear , the Faithful's Dagger and the Showstopper are with their chapters above. Weapon Power What it does Recipe (rows, top to bottom) Sinew Cleaver Rend Each full swing opens the wound further: Bleeding I, II, III. . S / T S / K . S Stitched Sinew, T Shepherd's Tear, K Hollow Knuckle Antler Scythe Reap The swing carries on through everything in front of you. A A A / . W . / . K . A Antler Shard, W Bloodied Wool, K Hollow Knuckle Static Blade Dead Air Static arcs from your target to up to 3 more hostiles. S / S / C S Static Shard, C Grave Claw Saint's Requiem Last Rites The target burns; creepypastas take a third more damage. . S . / R H R / . K . S Static Shard, R Rusted Lullaby Key, H Saint's Heart, K Hollow Knuckle The Bunnyman's Fire Axe Bridge Toll Full swings cut through armour, break shields and stagger. Use: a chop that splits the ground open ahead of you. I I S / I B . / S B . I iron ingot, S Bloodied Stuffing, B stick Hook and Chain Reel Full swings gaff: they bleed and drag the target to you. Use: throw the hook; it hauls creatures in, or you to walls. . H / . C / H B H Rusted Hook, C iron chain, B stick The Hogshead's Tenderizer Tenderize Full swings make the target take more from all harm. Use: slam the ground, throwing everything round you upward. F I F / . B . / . B . F Flayed Hide, I iron block, B stick Porcelain Needle Unseen Strikes from behind cut deep and stitch the target slow. Use: vanish; your first strike from hiding is a killing one. . . P / S P . / G . . P Porcelain Shard, S string, G gold ingot Devil's Glaive Hellfire Longer reach; full swings set the target burning. Use: leap on devil's wings and come down in a ring of fire. . . H / . B H / B . M H Devil's Horn, B blaze rod, M Moth Scale Rending Claws Frenzy Each hit quickens the next; wounds ble"},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"The Mended guns","u":"items/index.html#the-mended-guns","t":"Fabric only, with Timeless and Classics Guns: Zero (TaCZ), which the Fabric modpack installs. Three guns the Flesh grew into the special forces who carried them: the Mended SMG (its stock a forearm, an eye open in its side, a muzzle of five flesh petals; 30 rounds, full auto), the Mended Shotgun (a ribcage stock, a seed-pod magazine of 6 shells, a muzzle of teeth that chews when you look at it) and the Mended Marksman Rifle (a spine along the barrel, a thighbone stock, a finger for a bolt handle; 5 rounds). They fire infected rounds that put the Flesh into whatever they hit. Made at TaCZ's Gun Smith Table; special forces sometimes drop theirs. Once the Bloom is dead, they rot and jam over ten minutes off its blight."},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"Armour","u":"items/index.html#armour","t":"Every set is a real 3D model that moves. Crafted in the usual armour shapes from a material M with one accent X. The seven chapter sets (the Vigil, the Scarecrow, the Bloomwoven, the Specimen, Dead Air, the Usher's Uniform and On Air) are on Gear for every chapter . Since 1.60.0 any creature head can be worn too ( heads, worn ). The Dead Water's two dive suits and Blackout are on that page too, and the Night Guard's uniform is with Tune-In Town's prizes. Set Full-set power Made from Stitchskin Sewn Shut: below half health your wounds slowly close, and you can't bleed at all. Stitched Sinew, Hollow Knuckle Antlerbone Night Hunter: you run faster in the dark. Antler Shard, Bloodied Wool Static Mail Dead Channel: creepypastas within 32 blocks glow through walls, and anything that hits you up close gets a jolt of static. The Dead Channel Helm also shows the static coming off the Hollowed. Static Shard, Grave Claw Saint's Vestments Hollow Grace: creepypastas won't hunt you unless you hurt them. The Saint's Crown calms one that comes close. Static Mail + Saint's Shroud + Hymnal Page, at a smithing table Butcher's Garb Slaughterhouse: your blows open bleeding wounds; every kill feeds you back. Flayed Hide, porkchop, Rusted Hook, leather Mothwing Night Flight: fall and your wings catch you; in the dark you see like a moth. Moth Scale, fermented spider eye, phantom membrane, leather Braxton Shell Braxton Mist: struck, you hiss out a burning mist that sickens what's near; the hood's lamp lights the dark. Braxton Residue, glowstone, iron The Gardener's Weeds Tended: the great flower's flies won't have you (no Sapromyiophilous, and the Bloom's air doesn't eat you); what grows round you grows faster. Knotted Root, hay block, leather, mud (or found in the glasshouse) Hazmat Suit Sealed: the reactor's radiation can't touch you, and the Flesh's bile, gas and spores get in half as much. The Laboratory's airlock lockers Dead Channel Helm A dead TV for a helmet, crawling with live static. Its antenna tips light green while a creepypasta is near, flash red when you're hit, and fade like a cooling bulb when the last one's gone. Saint's Crown When a creepypasta comes within about 14 blocks, a red orb kindles between its antlers and beats like a heart, a glitching signal. In the full set the creature stares a few seconds, then gives in, sighs white ash, and turns friendly."},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"Mutant parts and throwables","u":"items/index.html#throwables","t":"Item What it does Recipe Gut Bomb Throw it: bursts like a Bloater on whatever is there, anything but you. A Bloater Gland, gunpowder and string (makes two) Screamer Lure Throw it: it screams for twelve seconds and every infected within 48 blocks goes to it. A Screamer Sac and Splitter Sinew Fly Jar Throw it: four Flesh Flies fight for you for twenty seconds. Hive Comb, a glass bottle and Splitter Sinew The parts themselves: Stalker Talon, Bloater Gland, Screamer Sac, Brute Knuckle, Splitter Sinew and Hive Comb, each from its mutant."},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"Blocks","u":"items/index.html#blocks","t":""},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"Story blocks","u":"items/index.html#story-blocks","t":"Forsaken Altar and Breach Altar : wake with an empty hand. Hollow Reliquary and Head Pedestal : the Saint's summoning. Mending Altar and Trophy Pedestal : the Mended. The Binding : holds the Bloom down, until you touch it twice. Cathedral Cornerstone (creative): place it in open ground and right-click it to raise a cathedral there. Assembly Cradle , Military Cradle , Assembly Mount , Launch Mark : the Rosemont Device. Tape Recorder : a working cassette player. Coolant Lever , Keycard Reader , Diesel Generator , Overload Switch , Shelter Radio Set . Projector , Drive-In Screen , Null Static , Null Rift : the Starlite and the Zone. Hush Stone , Hush Seal , Listening Stone : the Null ruins. Null Static What the drive-in's ground has gone to (as the mod's source describes it). Hush Stone Pale and dead: knock on it and nothing rings. The blocks of the hive, the Deep, the Stalls, the Vault, the Other Side, the Hub, the Dead Water, his kingdom and Tune-In Town are listed with their chapters above, and the new land's under More of the land ."},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"Building blocks","u":"items/index.html#building-blocks","t":"Hollow stone, hollow stone bricks (plain, cracked and bloodied), hollow brick stairs, slabs and walls, hollow tiles, hollow pillars, ossuary bricks, rotten planks (with Rotten Pews and slabs), cathedral glass (with its god rays), grave soil, gravestones, grave crosses and blood splatters. Breach stone and bricks, breach crystal and shards. Weathered clapboard, damask wallpaper, stained floorboards, slate shingles, grimy windows. Conservatory glass, overgrown iron, marble, planters, potting soil, garden flagstones and iron lattice. Shelter concrete, laboratory tiles and panels, steel grating, sandbags and wrecked cars. The radio mast, its top, antennas, aviation lights and guy-wire anchors (an anchor wires itself to the nearest mast). Blood is a real liquid: a bucket scoops it up. The garden's plants: Bloodthorn, Gnashing Flytrap, Whispering Lily, Corpse Bloom, Ghost Orchid, Watching Fern, Strangler Vine, Lantern Pod, Burstpod, Clutchvine, Weeping Bell, and four kinds of Specimen Jar (eye, heart, hand, seed)."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"","u":"lore/index.html","t":"Static Hollow tells most of its story in paper: journals on lecterns, logs in lockers, notices on walls. Every one is here word for word, grouped by chapter and by where you find it. They contain spoilers for everything up to the place they're found. Laboratory tapes and radio broadcasts are on Tapes and broadcasts . The Watcher's lines are on The Watcher speaks , and the First Signal's on The First Signal speaks ."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Chapter one: the Nine","u":"lore/index.html#chapter-one","t":""},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"The Forsaken Altar","u":"lore/index.html#the-forsaken-altar","t":"In the pilgrims' abandoned camp by the altar (since 1.40)."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Pilgrim's Diary","u":"lore/index.html#pilgrims-diary-2","t":"M. Ashdown Found: the pilgrims' camp p. 1 Day 9 on the road. We have reached the altar at last. Nine stones stand round it, one for each of the Nine, every one carved with one of their signs. We knelt at each of them. p. 2 The candles at the altar lit themselves as we came near. Brother Tobias wept. He says it means we are welcome. p. 3 Day 10. There is a stair by the altar, sealed under a stone. Tobias says it opens when the altar opens its eye. The first pilgrims are buried down there, all together, so they can go on praying. p. 4 Day 12. Tobias has knelt at the altar three nights now. He does not come back to the fire. When I go to him he turns his head to me and smiles, and then he is not there. I am leaving in the morning. I will leave this for whoever comes after."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"The cathedral","u":"lore/index.html#the-cathedral","t":"The priest's journal is in his study in the undercroft (since 1.40). The bell-ringer's tally is in the cathedral too."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Journal","u":"lore/index.html#journal","t":"Fr. A. Penn Found: the priest's study p. 1 The Feast of the Nine. They came again tonight, the nine families, and sat in the front pews, and did not sing. When I asked them to go home they turned their heads to me. Only their heads. p. 2 They do not eat. They do not go home. When I lock the doors at night they are already inside, praying, and the candles are lit that I did not light. p. 3 Below, the Saint lies sealed in its tomb under nine chains and nine candles, one for each of the heads they took to make it. I have kept the candles burning forty years. I am so tired. p. 4 The organ played itself at the third hour. A hymn I do not know. The candles went out one by one from the doors to the altar, as though someone were walking up the nave pinching them. p. 5 The bell rang thirteen. There is no thirteen. Something stood in the doorway and did not come in. p. 6 I went down this morning. The gate is bent outward. The tomb is open and empty and its chains are broken, and the congregation was smiling when I came back up. God keep whoever reads this. Do not open the tombs."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Bell-Ringer's Tally","u":"lore/index.html#bell-ringers-tally-2","t":"S. Marsh Found: the cathedral p. 1 Tolls, by the night. Mon. 12 at midnight. Right. Tue. 12. Right. Wed. 12, and one more after I'd let go of the rope. Thu. 13. I counted twice. p. 2 Fri. I tied the rope off at dusk. It rang thirteen anyway. The bell was swinging on its own when I got up here, and it was warm. Sat. I'm sleeping up here now. If it rings I want to see what rings it. p. 3 It isn't the bell. It's the thing in the doorway, down below. It looks up at me on the thirteenth. Every time."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Chapter two: the Breach","u":"lore/index.html#chapter-two","t":""},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"The Void","u":"lore/index.html#the-void","t":"Pages left on the pieces of the Drift, each with its chest (since 1.26)."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"A Diary, Left Open","u":"lore/index.html#a-diary-left-open-2","t":"(no name in it) Found: the Torn Room p. 1 Tuesday. The floor has started creaking at night where nobody is walking. From the corner by the wardrobe to the bed, and back. I have moved the bed. p. 2 Wednesday. The creaking goes to where the bed is now. The wallpaper by the window is damp, and warm. I put my hand on it and something on the other side put its hand on it too. p. 3 Thursday. There was a red light in the window. Not in the street. In the window, as if the glass itself had a crack in it and the crack went a long way back. The clock stopped at eleven. p. 4 Friday. The floor tipped. I am writing this because the rest of the house is gone and this corner is not and I don't know what is under it. It is dark under it. It is dark all round. The lamp is still lit. I'll keep it lit."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"An Unfinished Letter","u":"lore/index.html#an-unfinished-letter-2","t":"(the same hand as the diary) Found: the Torn Room p. 1 To whoever finds this room. There is no door. I looked for a long time. There is the bed and the wardrobe and the table, and past the edge of the rug there is nothing, and in the nothing there are lights that drift like jellyfish. p. 2 Something long goes round and round in the dark with a little lamp of its own. I thought it was another room, lit, far off. It isn't. If you fall, don't be afraid of the hand. The hand is the only kind thing out here."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Gravedigger's Book","u":"lore/index.html#gravediggers-book-2","t":"Amos, sexton Found: the Fallen Graves p. 1 Plot 12. Plot 13. Plot 14. All the new ones in the north row came up loose this week. Not dug up. Loose. As if the ground under them had let go of them. p. 2 I filled them in again. I filled them in again. The fourth time I put my ear to the earth, and it was hollow under. Hollow all the way down. The coffins in the north row are knocking. p. 3 Last entry. The north row is gone and the earth with it, and I went with the earth. The mausoleum came too. I am in it. Whoever they buried here, they never wanted to stay put. Now none of us has to."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Station Log","u":"lore/index.html#station-log","t":"the night operator Found: the Mast p. 1 STATION LOG 02:10 Carrier on 6.66. No station licensed there. 02:14 Voice under the carrier, counting. Counting down. 02:31 Mast lamp flickering. Replaced the bulb. Still flickering. p. 2 02:40 The TV in the shed came on by itself. Same channel as the radio. The man on it has a television where his head should be. He looked at me. 02:41 He knows the frequency. He is coming up it. p. 3 03:00 Static. 03:00 Static. 03:00 The mast is still up and the lamp is still on and there is no ground under the shed any more. Keeping the lamp on. Someone might steer by it. The counting stopped. It got to one. p. 4 (written across the bottom, later, in pencil) if you can read this - the red light is the way back to the altar. keep it on your left as you go and the bridge will take you."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Of What Swims Out Here","u":"lore/index.html#of-what-swims-out-here-2","t":"the Watcher Found: the Nest p. 1 the long things come up out of the black pool, where the big one died. they eat what falls. they will help it fall: they bite, and they pull you out over the dark, and let go. hit them hard and they let go sooner. p. 2 the lights are harmless. they drift where there is ground, and light it. their jelly is good to eat if you are afraid of falling. their light keeps the long ones off. the long ones go round it. p. 3 and the hand. the hand was here before the breach. it was here before the island. it catches everything that falls. i don't know why. i don't know whose it is. i know it has never once let anything go."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"The Murder Mansion","u":"lore/index.html#the-murder-mansion","t":"The Hale family's papers, where they were left (since 1.25). The Watcher's own pages are open on the library desk."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Household Accounts","u":"lore/index.html#household-accounts-2","t":"A. Hale, housekeeper Found: the Murder Mansion p. 1 Hale House. Accounts kept by Agnes Hale. March. Coal, 2 tons. Candles, 6 dozen (the master will have them lit in every room, all night, since the trouble). Flour, salt, lamp oil. p. 2 April. Meat, from the new man in the kitchen. He brings his own. He will not say from where and I have stopped asking. No charge, he says. The house is paying, he says. p. 3 April, later. The master has given the east rooms to guests. Nine of them. I am not to go up when they are in. Nine rooms aired. Nine beds made. Nobody has slept in them that I can tell. p. 4 May. The staff have gone. All but me and the cook, and I am not sure the cook was ever staff. Candles, 6 dozen. Candles, 6 dozen. Candles (the rest of the page is crossed through, hard enough to tear it)"},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Household Accounts (II)","u":"lore/index.html#household-accounts-ii-2","t":"A. Hale, housekeeper Found: the Murder Mansion p. 1 June. I have found the old ledger and I have found the reason for the hall at the back, with the long table and the spikes round it. The house was built for this. The first Hale built it round the table. p. 2 The table is not a table. It is an altar. The spikes are for heads. When there are nine heads on the nine spikes, something comes to the table and sews. I am writing it down so that somebody knows. p. 3 June, late. The guests are back. I heard them come in. Hooves on the stairs. Something dragging an axe. I have locked myself in the attic with the trunks. I have candles. 6 dozen."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Order Book","u":"lore/index.html#order-book-2","t":"the Butcher Found: the Murder Mansion p. 1 ORDERS For the house: 4 sides. Hung 3 days. For the guest with the hook: whatever comes up the lane after dark. He is not fussy. For the guest in the straw: nothing. He feeds himself. p. 2 For the tall one with the lamp face: it does not eat. It breathes on things and they spoil. Keep it out of my kitchen. For the dog that walks like a man: bones. Big ones. Fresh. p. 3 For the boy with the hooves: everything, and then the plate. For the moth: nothing. It wants the lights. For the rabbit: he says he will catch his own. He always does. p. 4 For the doll: it will not eat while you are looking. Leave the tray. Turn round. For myself: the pig's face is wearing thin again. Need a new one. Ask the visitor if they are free."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"A Letter, Never Sent","u":"lore/index.html#a-letter-never-sent-2","t":"Margaret Hale Found: the Murder Mansion p. 1 My dear sister, You asked why I have stopped writing. I have not stopped. I write every night. Henry burns them. He says the house reads the post. p. 2 He has filled the east rooms with guests. I have not seen them. I hear them. Something taps on my window three floors up. Something in the garden is taller than the hedges. p. 3 Henry says it is an honour. He says the nine of them choose a house, and the house is kept, and the family is kept. I asked what kept means. He would not look at me. p. 4 If you get this, do not come. If someone comes looking for us, tell them to look in the hall at the back. Tell them to bring nine of something. Your loving sister, Margaret"},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Nursery Rhymes","u":"lore/index.html#nursery-rhymes-2","t":"(in a child's hand) Found: the Murder Mansion p. 1 One for the rabbit who waits by the bridge, Two for the hook on the roof of the car, Three for the butcher in somebody's face, Four for the doll that gets closer each time. p. 2 Five for the scarecrow that walks in the corn, Six for the moth with the eyes like a fire, Seven for Mother Leeds' thirteenth child born, Eight for the dog on the road that stands up, p. 3 Nine for the lamp in the hills with the spade, and then they all come to the table to play. Count them on your fingers. Count them on their heads."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Guest List","u":"lore/index.html#guest-list-2","t":"H. Hale Found: the Murder Mansion p. 1 ROOMS 1. The Bunnyman. The room under the stairs (he asked for the one with the axe). 2. The Hookman. Top floor. Windows to be left open. 3. The Hogshead. He has the kitchen. p. 2 4. The Porcelain Man. Nursery. The dolls are his. 5. The Harvestman. The barn, if he will take it. He will not. 6. Mothman. The turret. Take the bulbs out. p. 3 7. The Jersey Devil. Cellar. Lock it from the inside. 8. Dogman. Anywhere. Everywhere. 9. The tall one from Braxton County. The garden. It glows. The hedges died. Nine. The table is laid."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Field Notes","u":"lore/index.html#field-notes","t":"E. Carver, county surveyor Found: the Murder Mansion p. 1 Sept. 12. Called out to the hill above the farms. A crater in the brush, the ground scorched, a smell like burnt metal and something sweeter. The boys say a thing came out of it ten feet tall. p. 2 They say its face was a lamp and its hood was a spade, and that it hissed, and glided, and the mist off it burned their throats. The dog that went up with them would not come down. p. 3 Sept. 14. Something has followed the boys home. Their mother says it stands at the end of the lane at night, lit up like a lantern. I have been asked to survey the Hale place next. The lane runs there."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"From the Glasshouse","u":"lore/index.html#from-the-glasshouse-2","t":"the Gardener Found: the Murder Mansion p. 1 Mrs Hale, The gate stays locked. I have the only key and I am keeping it. Whatever you have let into your house, it is not coming into my glass. p. 2 The big flower is doing well. It has had the last of the dogs. Do not send the boy with the hooves again; he trod on the orchids. If I am taken, the key goes with whatever takes me. Then it is no business of mine."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"The Red Room","u":"lore/index.html#the-red-room-2","t":"Found: the Murder Mansion p. 1 sit face the wall don't turn round p. 2 it's behind you it's always behind you in this room that's what the room is for p. 3 count to nine slowly if you get to nine you can turn round nobody gets to nine"},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"On the Mending","u":"lore/index.html#on-the-mending-2","t":"W. Found: the library desk p. 1 you found the table. good. it's an altar. the house was built round it. nine spikes, a horseshoe, open toward the doors. put a head on each spike. one of each of them. no doubles. it knows. p. 2 when there are nine, step back. i come down from the ceiling and i sew. what i make out of them won't be pretty and it won't be kind. it will be one thing instead of nine. that's the point. one thing can be killed. p. 3 it has the gardener's key on it. the gardener's dead, he just doesn't know it. bring torches. bring food. bring more than you think. don't let it get between you and the doors."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Chapter three: the Glasshouse","u":"lore/index.html#chapter-three","t":""},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"The Botanic Gardens","u":"lore/index.html#the-botanic-gardens","t":"The Head Gardener's journal is on the lectern in his office. His under-gardener's ledger is in the Seed Vault under the hatch."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Head Gardener's Journal","u":"lore/index.html#head-gardeners-journal-2","t":"E. Thorne Found: the Head Gardener's office p. 1 The great flower opened today, under the dome. Nobody planted it. The roots came up through the tiles of the rotunda in a single night, and in the morning there it was - red as a wound, and warm to the touch. p. 2 It is warm. I put my ear to the stalk and there is a beat in it, slow, like a sleeper's. The orchids have all turned to face it. The ferns too. I have begun to think the ferns are looking at things. p. 3 The family came down from the house to see it. The children would not go near. The eldest said it smelled like the butcher's yard. They do not come any more. I have stopped going up to the house. p. 4 Feeding. Bone meal will not do; it wants better. The rats are gone from the potting shed. The cat is gone. I do not remember the last time I ate. I am not hungry. I am never hungry now. p. 5 The flies are thick on anyone who comes in now. Avery is black with them. They will not settle on me. It knows my clothes - it has grown into the cloth. My hat is in the shed, my coat in the chest here. Whoever wears them, it will take for me. p. 6 There are roots in my boots. I cut them away in the morning and by evening they are back. They do not hurt. That is what frightens me. They do not hurt. p. 7 Something came down from the house tonight - a great stitched thing, all iron and wrong pieces - and locked the gates from the outside, and took the key away with it. Good. Keep them out. Keep it in. Keep me in. p. 8 I hear it say my name through the lilies. It says it needs tending. It is right. Somebody must tend it. I am going to kneel by it a while. Just a while. If you find this: do not wake me. Do not touch the flower."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Seed Ledger","u":"lore/index.html#seed-ledger-2","t":"T. Avery, under-gardener Found: the Seed Vault p. 1 Moved the good seed down here, out of the glass. Mr Thorne says it doesn't like them. It doesn't like anything it didn't grow itself. p. 2 Mr Thorne doesn't sleep now. He kneels by it all night with the big shears across his knees, and in the morning the beds are cut back to the soil. He told me to bring it the rats. I won't. p. 3 His face. Something is growing in his face. Flowers - white ones, where his eyes were. He turned them to me today and they opened. I think he was smiling. p. 4 I've come down here to hide. He can't get down the ladder now; he's too tall. I can hear him up there, tending it. Snip. Snip. Snip. p. 5 The roots are coming through the walls. They're warm. I'm so tired. If I sleep down here they'll grow over me, the way they grow over everything. If anyone finds this, there is a key, the stitched thing took it, don't"},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"The Bloom","u":"lore/index.html#the-bloom","t":"One lectern on each island of what the flower ate."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"The Rosemont Courier","u":"lore/index.html#the-rosemont-courier-2","t":"(four issues, folded together) Found: the street of Rosemont p. 1 THE ROSEMONT COURIER GARDENS' 'MONSTER FLOWER' DRAWS CROWDS A flower the size of a motor car has opened in the glasshouse at the Botanic Gardens. Head Gardener E. Thorne says it is a Rafflesia, 'though not one I know.' p. 2 THE ROSEMONT COURIER FLIES CLOSE MARKET STREET The Corporation has closed the market after swarms of flies 'thick as smoke' settled on the stalls. Traders blame the Gardens. The Gardens are no longer open to the public. p. 3 THE ROSEMONT COURIER FOURTEEN MISSING IN WEST END All were last seen walking toward the Gardens at night. Neighbours speak of a smell 'like a butcher's yard in August.' The Station is 'taking samples.' p. 4 LATE EDITION THE GROUND IS MOVING ON PARK ROAD Residents are asked to go to the shelters. Do not go near the Gardens. Do not go near anything green that moves. (the rest of the page is torn away)"},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Research Log: Specimen 0","u":"lore/index.html#research-log-specimen-0-2","t":"Dr. H. Marsh, Rosemont Botanical Research Laboratory Found: the research station p. 1 Specimen 0: the Gardens' Rafflesia. It is not a parasite on a vine. There is no vine. Its root goes down through the rotunda's floor and keeps going. We let down a line four hundred feet. It kept going. p. 2 The flies are not drawn to it. They come out of it. It makes them - they are how it tastes the air. Every subject exposed is 'liked' by the flies within the hour. Every subject but one. p. 3 Subject Thorne shows no infection at all. The flies settle on him and lift off again. It knows him: his clothes, his skin, the soil on him. Recommend all field staff wear his old work clothes. (He laughed when I asked.) p. 4 The bud under the glass is not the flower. It is a finger. The flower is somewhere under, and it is very, very big. We have built a binding at the root's end. While it holds, the flower cannot pull itself up the root. p. 5 If the binding is broken, it will come up the root, all the way, into the Gardens. It is hungry. It ate the street. It ate our east wing. It is eating us now. I can hear the tank (the writing stops)"},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Shelter No. 4: Warden's Log","u":"lore/index.html#shelter-no-4-wardens-log-2","t":"J. Pike, Warden Found: Shelter No. 4, in the Bloom p. 1 Day 1. Forty-one in. Doors sealed at 20:00. The radio says stay put. The air smells of meat. Day 2. Flies under the door. Taped the door. p. 2 Day 4. Something big under the ground. It goes under us slow, like a train. Day 5. Mrs. Avery says her boy is at the Gardens with Mr. Thorne, he's safe there, the flies don't touch the gardeners. Nobody answered her. p. 3 Day 6. Fourteen left. The ones who went out to the Laboratory for medicine came back green round the mouth. They wouldn't stop smiling. Day 7. The roof is breathing. p. 4 Day 9. The whole shelter tipped. I looked out of the door and there was no street. There was green all the way down, and something at the bottom of it, opening and shutting. If you are reading this: it has us. Don't come down here without his clothes."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"The Binding","u":"lore/index.html#the-binding","t":"Rosemont Botanical Research Laboratory Found: the Binding's island p. 1 THE BINDING Site 0: the root's end This stone holds the root down. While it holds, the flower cannot climb the root into Rosemont. DO NOT TOUCH THE STONE. DO NOT LOOSEN THE CHAINS. DO NOT LOOK DOWN. p. 2 (scratched under it, in another hand) it doesn't hold it. it only keeps it asleep. wake it and you'll have ten seconds before it pulls this whole island down its throat. run for the tear in the air. don't look back."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Chapter four: the Flesh","u":"lore/index.html#chapter-four","t":"The Laboratory's six audio logs and Shelter No. 4's broadcasts are on Tapes and broadcasts ."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"The Uplink Station","u":"lore/index.html#the-uplink-station","t":""},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Uplink 7 - Duty Log","u":"lore/index.html#uplink-7-duty-log-2","t":"Lt. R. Okafor Found: the locker by the consoles p. 1 0400. Handshake with SENTINEL nominal. Capacitors at 31%. Works says another week before a full charge. Nobody up here knows what we're charging it for. The colonel says that's the point. p. 2 0900. Lost the city on the net. Not the net - the city. Every channel out of Rosemont went quiet at once. SENTINEL still answers. It always answers. p. 3 1600. Orders to pull the targeting array and keep it on us. If the station falls, SENTINEL can't be told where to fire. If the station falls, who would we be telling? p. 4 2300. Something big moving out by the glasshouse. Thermal can't see the edge of it. The array's in my locker. If you're reading this and you know what it's for - you don't need me to tell you."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Standing Orders","u":"lore/index.html#standing-orders-2","t":"Garrison Command Found: the control bunker p. 1 SENTINEL (orbital) is a weapon of last resort. It fires on a targeting array's lock. It fires only with a full CAPACITOR CELL seated in its core. p. 2 The core has a third socket. The engineers call it 'the governor'. Nobody has ever been told what goes in it. Do not ask the engineers about the governor."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"The Capacitor Works","u":"lore/index.html#the-capacitor-works","t":""},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Works Order 117","u":"lore/index.html#works-order-117-2","t":"Capacitor Works Found: the test cage p. 1 Cell 9 to be charged to full and held in the test cage for collection by Uplink. No collection came. p. 2 Cell 9 is holding. We can't bleed it off, and we can't leave it. The arcs have started jumping the rods by themselves. Two men burnt. The rest of us sleep in the yard."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Notice","u":"lore/index.html#notice","t":"Works Safety Officer Found: the test cage p. 1 DANGER - LIVE BANKS. Do not stand between rods. Do not touch the bus bars. If it starts to crackle, get down and get out. p. 2 Arc burns are not covered. (underneath, in pencil:) neither is whatever is in the cage."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"The Soul Well","u":"lore/index.html#the-soul-well","t":""},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"The Keeper's Prayer","u":"lore/index.html#the-keepers-prayer-2","t":"the Well-Keepers Found: the bottom of the well p. 1 Into the well, the ones who would not lie down. Into the well, the ones who would not stop. We keep the well. We keep them down. p. 2 One of them will not go quiet. Its light is too strong. It burns the others. We have bound it. We kneel by it. It must never leave the well. p. 3 If you have come for it, you have come for the strongest of them. Whatever you mean to pour into it - it will hold. That is what we are afraid of."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Ashford Nuclear Plant","u":"lore/index.html#ashford-nuclear-plant","t":""},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Ashford - Shift Log","u":"lore/index.html#ashford-shift-log-2","t":"Unit 2 Control Room Found: Ashford p. 1 0200. Reactor at 100%. Grid demand from Rosemont doubled overnight - the garrison's Works drawing again. Nobody tells us what for. p. 2 0700. The city's gone dark on the grid. All of it at once. We're running into nothing. Orders: hold power for the Works line only. p. 3 1300. Something under the glasshouse is drawing on the line. Not the Works. You can't draw on a line that isn't connected to anything. p. 4 1900. Breach in Unit 2. Not out of the reactor - into it. We scrammed. The core assembly's in the fuel pool. Don't go in the water without a suit."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Meridian Laboratory","u":"lore/index.html#meridian-laboratory","t":""},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Director's Notes","u":"lore/index.html#directors-notes-2","t":"Dr. H. Vasquez, Meridian Found: Meridian p. 1 The governor. SENTINEL's third socket. Garrison Command thinks it's a safety. It isn't. It's a throttle. What we're building takes it off. p. 2 The destabilizer holds a discharge on the edge of collapse. Seated in a railgun's core, it lets the gun draw on what no capacitor could hold. p. 3 Ashford's core for the power. The destabilizer to let go of it. And for the lens: Blackwater's blood. Not a slug. A ray. p. 4 We can't finish it. It needs something we don't have. Something that knows the dark."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Test Log - Cell 1","u":"lore/index.html#test-log-cell-1-2","t":"Meridian Test Hall Found: the test hall p. 1 Run 41. Destabilizer seated. Ring at 60%. Discharge held for 3.2 seconds. The coils sang. p. 2 Run 44. Held for 9 seconds. Then the coils started arcing to each other with the ring off. They still are. p. 3 Run 47. We lost the roof."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Memo","u":"lore/index.html#memo","t":"Meridian Logistics Found: Meridian Blackwater samples are NOT to be opened outside the cold room. If a vial is warm to the touch, it is not a vial any more. Leave the room. Seal it."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Blackwater Station","u":"lore/index.html#blackwater-station","t":""},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Station Log","u":"lore/index.html#station-log-2","t":"Blackwater Research Station Found: Blackwater p. 1 Day 1. It came down forty kilometres out. We towed what was left of it here and built the station round the tank. The blood doesn't freeze. p. 2 Day 30. The cultures took. Something lives in it. Small. It wants to be inside something bigger. p. 3 Day 31. It can't live in open air for long. Off the island it dies in seconds - nothing out there for it to eat. That doesn't help you in here. p. 4 Day 33. The tanks burst. The ones it got are still walking. The last vial's in the freezer. Meridian wanted it for their ray. Let them come and get it."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Specimen Notes","u":"lore/index.html#specimen-notes-2","t":"Dr. I. Okonkwo Found: Blackwater p. 1 The parasite: six legs, a mouth that opens like a flower. It goes for the back of the neck. p. 2 In a host it grows in hours. Then the host splits open and there are more of them. It needs the blood. Away from the dark matter, it starves."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Chapter five: the Static","u":"lore/index.html#chapter-five","t":""},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Relay 6","u":"lore/index.html#relay-6","t":""},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Relay 6 - Operator's Log","u":"lore/index.html#relay-6-operators-log-2","t":"D. Ostrander, Hollow Ridge Found: the transmitter hut p. 1 Mon. Carrier dropped twice overnight. Not the transmitter - something riding on the carrier, like someone else keying up on our frequency. Gus wouldn't come in from the yard. p. 2 Wed. Gus came back out of the woods. Thin. He won't let me near his mouth. The noise on the carrier is worse at night. Like breathing, run through a fan. p. 3 Fri. People from the valley came up the road after dark. Nine of them. They didn't knock. They stood round the mast with their faces up, like they were listening to it. They didn't blink at the floodlight. p. 4 Sat. Still there. Gus is out with them. I can hear them in the headset - not on the air. In the headset. Under the static they're talking. They're saying where everyone is. p. 5 Sun. They've started climbing it. Tying something to it. It isn't rope. If you find this and it's still on the air - it isn't us. Cut it loose. All of it."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Notice","u":"lore/index.html#notice-2","t":"County Emergency Broadcast Found: Relay 6 p. 1 RELAY 6 - HOLLOW RIDGE. Authorized personnel only. This station relays the county emergency broadcast. Do not interfere with its operation. p. 2 Climbing the mast: harness at all times. Rest platforms at 12, 22 and 32 metres. (scratched into the cover, underneath:) THEY'RE ON EVERY PLATFORM"},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"The Starlite Drive-In","u":"lore/index.html#the-starlite-drive-in","t":""},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"To Whoever Runs Booth 1","u":"lore/index.html#to-whoever-runs-booth-1-2","t":"Starlite Drive-In Found: the projection booth p. 1 Ray - the late show's reel came in with no label and no distributor. Ran it anyway. Half the lot left before the end. The other half stayed in their cars after it finished. They're still out there. p. 2 I took the reel off. The screen kept showing it. Then the screen kept showing static, and the static kept coming off it like smoke off a fire. The things in it don't walk. They drift. p. 3 You can't hit them most of the time. They're not all the way here. Something on the right frequency might put them all the way here. When they come apart, they leave bits of the picture behind. p. 4 If you have to see the rest of the reel, load the projector with what's left of them and stay with it till the end. Don't let them at the booth. Whatever it shows you - it's where they come from. I'm not going."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"The Ancient Null Ruins","u":"lore/index.html#the-null-ruins","t":"The field notes of the surveyors who came looking (the relay men had written to the college about voices in the dead air), rubbings of what the old ones carved, and what the last of them scratched into a Hush's bench. The static took all of them down too."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Field Notes (I)","u":"lore/index.html#field-notes-i-2","t":"Dr. R. Calloway Found: the Listening Stones p. 1 The relay men on Hollow Ridge wrote to the college: voices in the dead air, near some old stones in the woods. Nobody would come. I came. Dale brought his sets. Teddy carries everything. p. 2 Six stones leaning in round a seventh, and an ear cut into every one of them. Not a carving of an ear. An ear. The spiral goes in further than the stone is thick. p. 3 Dale put a set down by the middle stone and tuned it to nothing. The nothing was talking. Many voices, very far down, all at once, like a crowd heard through a floor. p. 4 There's a room under the floor. Its north wall is all ears. Whoever built this was listening to something under everything. Teddy asked what. I said the dead. Dale said no. He said: the static. p. 5 Dale sleeps with his ear to the wall now."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Field Notes (II)","u":"lore/index.html#field-notes-ii-2","t":"Dr. R. Calloway Found: the Listening Stones p. 1 Translation, such as it is. The sign that keeps coming back is a spiral with a line through it. Everywhere else it means 'to hear'. Here it means 'to be heard'. p. 2 Over the stair: THE MANY SPEAK FROM UNDER. WE LISTEN SO THEY WILL NOT HAVE TO COME UP. Over the wall of ears: WE LISTENED TOO LONG. p. 3 Dale says the voices on his set know our names. He played it to me. One of them was mine. p. 4 There's a picture of another place they built. A house with one door, of a pale stone, a seal set in its floor. Under it: HERE THEY CANNOT HEAR YOU. Teddy wants to find one. So do I."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Field Notes (III)","u":"lore/index.html#field-notes-iii-2","t":"T. Marsh Found: the Sunken Choir p. 1 Dr. Calloway sent me ahead to the choir pit. Figures on every step, mouths open, all facing the hole in the middle. The hole goes down. There's a ladder. The ladder is new. Somebody's been down. p. 2 There's a room down here with ears in all four walls, facing in. The figures up top aren't singing. They're the audience. What they're listening to is whatever comes up the throat. p. 3 I can hear Dale. He went out to the dogs a week ago. His voice comes up the throat with the others. He says it's all right. He says it's warm down there, and nobody's alone. p. 4 I'm going to stay a little longer and listen."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"The Last Page","u":"lore/index.html#the-last-page-2","t":"Dr. R. Calloway Found: a Hush p. 1 We found one. The stone is pale and dead - knock on it and nothing rings. Step over the line in the door and the static on Dale's set stops. Not goes quiet. Stops. p. 2 Teddy had a thing on his neck from the woods, like a tick with a flower for a mouth. It came off him at the door in pieces. He's fine. He won't talk about it. p. 3 They followed us. Dogs first, the wrong shape, black spines. One ran at the door and leapt - and came apart in the air, like a picture on a set when you switch it off. The others stopped at the line. p. 4 Now they come and stand out past the two pillars and look in. They don't come closer. They don't blink. After a while they go away. After a while they come back. p. 5 Dale went out to them last night. He said they were calling him. I can't hear anything in here. That's the point. That's the whole point. Stay inside until it forgets your name."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Rubbing: the Lintel","u":"lore/index.html#rubbing-the-lintel-2","t":"Dr. R. Calloway Found: a Hush p. 1 (the carving over the door, as near as I can make it) p. 2 THIS IS A HUSH. THE STONE IS DEAD. NOTHING OF THE MANY CAN LIVE IN IT. WHAT THEY PUT IN YOU WILL DIE AT THE LINE. p. 3 THEY WILL COME TO THE DOOR. THEY WILL LOOK AT YOU. DO NOT GO OUT TO THEM. THEY KNOW YOUR VOICE. THEY CANNOT USE IT IN HERE. p. 4 WE BUILT THESE TOO LATE. THE MANY TOOK THE REST OF US DOWN WITH THE STATIC. IF YOU ARE READING THIS, THEY ARE COMING BACK UP."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Notebook","u":"lore/index.html#notebook","t":"D. Pruett Found: the stones, in the Zone p. 1 Ruth, if this gets to you. They didn't hurt me. They took me down the static, the whole way, and I came out on a grey field with no sky. The stones are here too. Everything they ever listened to came down here. p. 2 The voices are louder here. Not louder. Closer. They're not the dead, Ruth. They're the ones who listened. Everyone who ever put their ear to the stone. p. 3 There's something in the middle of this place, big as a church, coiled up. Threads go up off it into the dark. When it breathes I hear the relay. p. 4 I've been listening for you. I can hear you through the stone. You're in the Hush. Good. Stay there. Whatever sounds like me at the door - it isn't me any more."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Scratched Into the Bench","u":"lore/index.html#scratched-into-the-bench-2","t":"(nobody signed it) Found: a Hush, in the Zone p. 1 WE CAME DOWN WITH OUR HOUSE ROUND US. THE MANY TOOK THE GROUND AND THE SKY, AND LEFT THE ROOM. p. 2 OUTSIDE IT IS ALWAYS GREY. THEY STAND BY THE PILLARS AND SAY OUR NAMES IN OUR MOTHERS' VOICES. p. 3 THE GREAT ONE IN THE PIT CARRIES THEM UP ITS THREADS TO EVERY PLACE THAT LISTENS. WHEN IT DIES THEY WILL HAVE NO WAY UP. p. 4 WE ARE THE LAST. WE HAVE STOPPED ANSWERING. IT IS VERY QUIET IN HERE."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"The Hive","u":"lore/index.html#the-hive","t":"Somebody got to the hive before you: the hamlet's priest. His journal is on a lectern in what's left of a cottage, his chest beside it (since 1.50)."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"The Book of the Hollow Lane","u":"lore/index.html#the-book-of-the-hollow-lane-2","t":"Fr. Aldous Mercer Found: a cottage at the hive p. 1 Sunday. The Pruitt boy came down from the ridge with one of the things on his neck. We cut it off him. He has not spoken since. He listens at the walls. p. 2 Tuesday. The animals are standing in the fields with their heads up, all facing the same way. North. They have been like that since the radio mast went quiet. p. 3 Thursday. The Pruitt boy is gone. In the morning there was a heap of something in his bed. By evening there was no heap. It went somewhere. They all go somewhere. p. 4 Saturday. The ground behind the chapel is soft and warm. It moves when you are not looking at it. The heaps go into it. I rang the bell. Nobody came. Then everybody came. p. 5 I can hear them under the floor. Not voices. One voice, made of all of theirs. It is learning words. It has learned my name. It says it is lonely now the noise has stopped. It says it is building something to keep it company. p. 6 If you are reading this I am in the pit with the rest of them. Do not listen when it speaks with my voice. It thinks with the four bulbs on the black stalks. Burn what you can. Cut what you can't."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"The Sinkhole","u":"lore/index.html#the-sinkhole","t":"The county surveyor's notes are on a lectern at his camp on the rim of the sinkhole . His last page is on the landing where he stopped, halfway down the Burrow, his lantern beside it (since 1.54)."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Subsidence, Halloway's Low Field","u":"lore/index.html#subsidence-halloways-low-field-2","t":"E. Calder, County Surveyor Found: the surveyor's camp, on the rim p. 1 Called out to the Halloway place on account of the low field going in. Expected a cave-in - there are old workings under these hills, everyone says so. This is not a cave-in. p. 2 Thirty-four yards across. The sides are cut clean, as if something came up through the ground, not as if it fell in. The soil at the bottom is warm to the hand. At night it steams. p. 3 Halloway won't come near it. His dog went in on the second day. We heard it for a long while. It wasn't hurt, he says. It was answering something. p. 4 There's a passage at the bottom, round as a pipe, going down in a turn like a corkscrew. Its walls are lined with something like the inside of a cheek. It's warm. It moves when you breathe. I'm taking the long rope and the lantern. Somebody ought to measure it."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"(a loose page)","u":"lore/index.html#a-loose-page-2","t":"E. Calder Found: halfway down the Burrow p. 1 Halfway, by my count. The lantern doesn't throw far. The walls give when you lean on them. There are voices further down. Not words. Singing, almost. p. 2 One of them is Halloway's dog. One is the priest from the hamlet over the ridge - I'd know that voice anywhere. It says it's warm at the bottom. It says the others were down there first, and they don't like it. p. 3 The floor of the last room is a mouth. Stand on it long enough and it opens. I've come this far."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"The Deep","u":"lore/index.html#the-deep","t":"Down in the Deep , Low Marrow's reeve left his account in his cottage and the priest his last sermon in the church. In the Old Halls the old ones cut theirs into the walls, either side of the hall."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Low Marrow","u":"lore/index.html#low-marrow-2","t":"T. Ashby, Reeve Found: the reeve's cottage, Low Marrow p. 1 The ground went out from under us on the Tuesday night. The whole of Low Marrow - the church, the green, the pond, the lane - down. We fell a long while. The houses held, mostly. p. 2 It is warm down here, and dark. The pond is not water any more. Something sang to us the first night, under everything, very sweet. Some of us went to it. They did not come back. p. 3 The rest of us found out about the white things. They have no eyes. They come when you talk, when you walk, when you cry. Ellen's boy cried. p. 4 We do not talk now. We go about in our stockings, and we do not cry. Old Pell says there is a king further in that the white things keep away from - a king who stopped his own ears. Pell has gone to find him. p. 5 He said: follow the stones with the ears cut in them. A cap burns on every one. If you find this, go quiet. Go in your stockings. Follow the stones."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"(the last sermon)","u":"lore/index.html#the-last-sermon-2","t":"Rev. J. Fairley Found: the church, Low Marrow p. 1 Text: and they have ears, but they hear not. I have decided to preach on the singing. p. 2 It says it is lonely. It says it lost everything it had, up there, and came down here to be warm. It says we can be warm with it. I believe it. God forgive me, I believe every word. p. 3 I am going down to it tonight. I have asked the others to come. They are afraid of the white things. The white things are only listening for it too, poor souls. They just never stopped."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"(cut in the wall, in marks older than letters)","u":"lore/index.html#cut-in-the-wall-in-marks-older-than-letters","t":"the old ones Found: the Old Halls p. 1 We were here first. Before the light up there. We heard everything: the rock settling, the roots growing down, the water a long way off. Then the singing came down through the roots. p. 2 To hear it was to go to it. It took us, a few at a time, and we became its. Our king took stone and stopped his ears, and then he could not hear it, and he did not go. p. 3 He told us all to do the same. Some of us did. The ones who would not stop their ears listened harder and harder, to hear anything else at all. They listened until they went blind. They are listening still."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"(cut in the wall by the dais)","u":"lore/index.html#cut-in-the-wall-by-the-dais-2","t":"the old ones Found: the Old Halls p. 1 The king does not hear. The king does not see. The king feels the floor. When you come before him, be still. p. 2 If you would have what he put in his ears, you must take it out of him. He will not give it. With it in your own, the singing is only singing."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Chapters six and seven","u":"lore/index.html#chapters-six-and-seven","t":"The Door at the End of the World and the Hub are told in cutscenes and in the Watcher's own words, not on paper: see The Watcher speaks and the chapters' story pages, six and seven ."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Chapter eight: the Dead Water","u":"lore/index.html#chapter-eight","t":""},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"The Watcher's chart","u":"lore/index.html#the-watchers-chart","t":"The Watcher hands you his chart when you come down to the Dead Water (since 1.63.2). Unroll it and point at a water, and it shows what he wrote of it. These are his notes, in the chart's order."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"THE WATCHER'S CHART","u":"lore/index.html#the-watchers-chart-2","t":"Found: in his hand, on the rig The Black Below. THE DEAD ZONE. Past the edge of all this the floor drops away and doesn't stop. Something lives out there that's bigger than the sea. Don't. The Grey Shelf. Grey water over grey silt. The rig stands in it. Nothing here is in a hurry - mostly. The Haemal Reach. The water's thick with blood. Clotfish come in swarms; the Siphons wait for them to pass. The Wireweed. Weed like wire, and it sings. The Choir Eels nest in it. Don't touch the bright ones. The Lantern Fields. Lights in the dark as far as you can see. Most of them are bulbs. Some of them aren't. The Ossuary Flats. A plain of bone. Whatever died here, died big. The Stiltfins pick it clean. The Brine Sink. The brine pools eat what falls in. The water's sour, and the Puffbloats like it. The Molar Reef. Teeth, grown into a reef. The Grinners live in it. They smile at you. The Drowned Mycelia. Mushrooms the size of towers, drowned. Their spores burst if you brush them. The Rime Shelf. Ice under the sea. Things are frozen in it. Some of them wake up. The Ember Vents. Vents roaring up from below. Warm. The Mantlecrabs crowd round them - mind your power. The Carrier Wave. The static's loudest here. The water hums. Your instruments won't like it. Point at a water to see where it lies, and what he wrote of it."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"The Haemal Research Station","u":"lore/index.html#the-haemal-research-station","t":"The lab at the near edge of the Haemal Reach where Enzyme 1-2418 was made, and where it got out (since 1.63.9). Its last log book is in the office chest with two or three Enzyme Inhibitors : the Research Log, HRS-3 , Haemal Research Station's last log book, in its sealed sleeve. Use it and it reads you one entry at a time, in order, then round again from the first."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Research Log, HRS-3","u":"lore/index.html#research-log-hrs-3-2","t":"Found: the station's office p. 1 HRS-3 LOG - Day 1 Station's down and sealed. The Heart's four hundred metres off our west lock and it BEATS. Once every forty seconds. You feel it in the deck plates. Dr. Vane says it's the biggest living thing anyone's ever stood next to. p. 2 HRS-3 LOG - Day 9 Isolated the catalyst from the Heart's outflow. Designated 1-2418. It breaks down tissue and puts it back together - better. Faster. Vane wants it for burns, for grafts. We're going to be very rich or very famous. p. 3 HRS-3 LOG - Day 23 1-2418 doesn't repair tissue. It rewrites it to match the Heart's. The cell culture in Vat 2 is beating. In time with the Heart. Through two hulls and four hundred metres of water. p. 4 HRS-3 LOG - Day 31 It's in the water outside now. Our outflow. Our fault. Divers coming back itching. Okafor's suit wouldn't come off - it had grown into his back. We cut it off him. He kept asking us why we were hurting it. p. 5 HRS-3 LOG - Day 34 It hates ultraviolet. Under the decon lamps it blackens and sloughs off. Ring of UV lamps up round the station. Lined suits for everyone - the UV dress. Nobody goes out in the old dress. NOBODY. p. 6 HRS-3 LOG - Day 40 Okafor walked out of the airlock in his sleeping things last night. No air. Swimming. Toward the Heart. We found his tracks in the silt going all the way there. We didn't go in after him. We could hear him singing on the hydrophone. p. 7 HRS-3 LOG - Day 44 Vat 2 broke. It wasn't an accident: it pushed. The ones who were in the lab are on the floor and they're getting LONGER. Their arms. Their legs. Their necks. Their helmets split. They're not dead. They're lying still because they're waiting. p. 8 HRS-3 LOG - Day 45 Three of us left, in decon, under the lamps. It won't come in here. It sits in the doorway, burning, and it doesn't care. The suits are in the lockers. The inhibitors are in the office. The office is on the other side of it. p. 9 HRS-3 LOG - last If you're reading this you came in the lined dress or you came in fast. Take the suits. Don't look at the ones on the floor - if you look away, they move. Don't go to the Heart. When you start wanting to: that's not you."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Chapter nine: the Harbinger","u":"lore/index.html#chapter-nine","t":"The Turning, the three days and the Harbinger are told in cutscenes and in what the Watcher and the static heart say, not on paper: see Chapter Nine and The Watcher speaks ."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Chapter ten: Stay Tuned","u":"lore/index.html#chapter-ten","t":""},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"SENTINEL","u":"lore/index.html#sentinel","t":"When SENTINEL comes through the sky over his kingdom and he tears its right side off, one of its modules comes down in his sea east of his arena, and stays there (since 1.70.0, THE LAST BROADCAST : THE FALL). Its crew's chest is still in it, with iron, copper, glowstone dust, redstone, a golden apple, a spyglass and the commander's log."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"SENTINEL - Crew Log","u":"lore/index.html#sentinel-crew-log-2","t":"Cmdr. D. Reyes Found: the crew's chest, in SENTINEL's wreck p. 1 SENTINEL. Station log. We woke the station when the Omni called it the first time. It was supposed to be the gun and nothing else. It never was. They built all of it up here - the rings, the wings, us. p. 2 We kept the samples from the island lab in the aft hold. The black blood. The things that came out of it. Sealed, frozen, logged. Nobody was supposed to wake them either. p. 3 The second call came through something that was not our sky. Whoever made it, it was not the one who made the first. The station answered anyway. It always answers. p. 4 Something down there was looking up at us. A man made of static, on a roof, laughing. Charge at fifty percent. If anyone finds this: he hit us first. p. 5 The hold is warm. It should not be warm."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Tune-In Town","u":"lore/index.html#tune-in-town","t":"Once in a long while an Old Set that's on stops showing static (since 1.65.3): The set's stopped showing static. A flyer, held up close to the camera - yellowed, creased: HELP WANTED. TUNE-IN TOWN PIZZA & PLAYHOUSE. Then it clicks off - and the flyer's in your hand. Read it: the address. Read it, and it tells you which way the old place is and how far. The orientation tapes in the security office are Hal's, the old manager's: they're on Tapes and broadcasts . See Tune-In Town ."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"HELP WANTED Flyer","u":"lore/index.html#help-wanted-flyer","t":"Found: on the television Tune-In Town Pizza & Playhouse: Night Security, 12AM-6AM. Apply within. (It was on the television.)"},{"p":"Tapes and broadcasts","h":"","u":"lore/tapes-and-broadcasts.html","t":"The Rosemont Botanical Research Laboratory's staff left six cassettes, and Shelter No. 4's radio set still picks up two broadcasts. Between them they tell you what happened under the gardens, what is asleep in the reactor pool, and how to get the Front Assembly out of Bunker B. Later, in Chapter Five, two things you carry start talking to you: a piece of the Chorus, and the one voice it couldn't swallow. In the Dead Water the sea itself has voices, Chapter Ten has a programme every night, and at Tune-In Town the old manager left a tape for each night of the shift."},{"p":"Tapes and broadcasts","h":"The Laboratory's audio logs","u":"lore/tapes-and-broadcasts.html#the-audio-logs","t":"Audio Log Use: play the tape, or put it in a tape recorder A cassette from the Laboratory, its label in somebody's hand. Someone was recording. Use a tape to play it: the click, the hiss, and the voice, line by line. Since 1.41 every line is voiced, slowed and dropped an octave into something too big for the room, saturated and tape-worn, catching on a syllable now and then. Each tape ends with it laughing. Subtitles show over your hotbar while it plays, and the words go into chat too. Put a tape in a Tape Recorder and it plays out loud for anyone within about twenty blocks: its reels turn, its level meter jumps and static crackles off its speaker. Sneak and use it to take the tape out. The Laboratory's recorders still have their tapes in them. Researchers sometimes drop the later tapes."},{"p":"Tapes and broadcasts","h":"Audio Log: Marsh, Control Room","u":"lore/tapes-and-broadcasts.html#marsh-control-room","t":"*click* - Dr. H. Marsh This is Marsh. Control room. The power's gone, and the Core is all that's keeping it asleep. Specimen Zero went into the pool the night the tank burst. It sleeps against the Core. It likes the warmth. If anyone needs the Core out: the coolant has to be isolated first, or the hall stays sealed. The levers are on this wall. The order matters. [the lever order, different in every world]. Any other order and the whole level alarms. Then the blast doors open. Then you lift it. Then you run, because it will wake. I'm going down to sit with it. Somebody should. [something on the tape laughs] Pull the three coolant levers in Marsh's order and the hall's blast doors grind up (\"COOLANT ISOLATED - REACTOR HALL OPENING\"). Pull one out of turn and the alarm goes (\"WRONG SEQUENCE - COOLANT ISOLATION FAULT\"), the levers drop back, and six of the staff come for you."},{"p":"Tapes and broadcasts","h":"Audio Log: Marsh, Personal","u":"lore/tapes-and-broadcasts.html#marsh-personal","t":"*click* - Dr. H. Marsh Personal log. The thing under the Gardens isn't the flower. The flower has been holding it down. Reyes, the night technician, cut a sample from the root's end. By morning his hands were somebody else's. We sealed him in the big tank on Sublevel 1 and called him Specimen Zero. He talked for three days. Then he stopped using words. It hates the flowers. Every sample we put near it, it reached for. Tore at. The keycard's in this drawer. The tank won't hold much longer. [something on the tape laughs] In the director's locked desk, with the Level 2 Keycard. Three good blows split the drawer."},{"p":"Tapes and broadcasts","h":"Audio Log: Okafor, Sample Log","u":"lore/tapes-and-broadcasts.html#okafor-sample-log","t":"*click* - Dr. A. Okafor Sample log, day nine. Bloom tissue placed beside Zero's growth. The growth recoiled - then attacked it. Flower ash kills it outright. Burn the Gardens' flowers, pack the ash with powder, and you have something it can't stand. A flower, a burnt petal, gunpowder. We have a weapon. We have one weapon. [something on the tape laughs] That's the Flower Ash Bomb's recipe."},{"p":"Tapes and broadcasts","h":"Audio Log: Reception","u":"lore/tapes-and-broadcasts.html#reception","t":"*click* - Reception Welcome to Rosemont Botanical Research Laboratory. All visitors must sign in at reception. Sublevels one and two are restricted to staff with Level 2 clearance. Please do not let them follow you down. [something on the tape laughs]"},{"p":"Tapes and broadcasts","h":"Audio Log: Lin, Containment","u":"lore/tapes-and-broadcasts.html#lin-containment","t":"*click* - Dr. S. Lin Containment, oh-two-fourteen. The tank's cracked. It isn't trying to get out. It's listening. Oh-two-thirty. It came out slowly. Politely. It went past us to the lift shaft and down, toward the reactor. The pool's warm. It likes warm. Everyone stay out of the hall. [something on the tape laughs]"},{"p":"Tapes and broadcasts","h":"Audio Log: Doyle, Hazmat Team","u":"lore/tapes-and-broadcasts.html#doyle-hazmat-team","t":"*click* - Sgt. R. Doyle Hazmat team, entry. Suits on. Radiation in the hall's off the scale near the pool. Nobody stands by the pool without a suit. Contact. Something in the water. Jenkins is laughing. Why is Jenkins laughing. [something on the tape laughs]"},{"p":"Tapes and broadcasts","h":"Shelter No. 4's radio","u":"lore/tapes-and-broadcasts.html#shelter-broadcasts","t":"Use the Shelter Radio Set in the radio room to hear it. With the power off it plays the evacuation notice. With both generators running, it turns into Control's emergency broadcast."},{"p":"Tapes and broadcasts","h":"The evacuation notice","u":"lore/tapes-and-broadcasts.html#evacuation-notice","t":"Rosemont Civil Defence, on a loop This is Rosemont Civil Defence. This is not a drill. All residents of zones C and D proceed at once to Shelter Number Four, Victoria Park. Bring nothing. Do not stop for anyone on the street who is unwell. Wardens will close the blast door at twenty-two hundred hours. It will not be opened again until the all-clear. This is Rosemont Civil Defence. This is not a drill."},{"p":"Tapes and broadcasts","h":"Control's emergency broadcast","u":"lore/tapes-and-broadcasts.html#emergency-broadcast","t":"Once the shelter's power is back Shelter Four, Shelter Four, this is Control. We see your power on. Respond. Shelter Four, do not open the vault. Repeat: do not open the vault. Whatever is in bunk hall B is not your residents any more. Whatever the squad told you, they are not coming back up. If anyone down there can hear this - the overload switch, over the plates in bunker B. Get it onto the plates. Shelter Four, respond. That's how to beat the Warden of Shelter No. 4 ."},{"p":"Tapes and broadcasts","h":"Voices from the static","u":"lore/tapes-and-broadcasts.html#voices","t":"These aren't recordings. They're things that are still alive enough to talk, and what they say comes up over your hotbar in italics when you hold them to your ear."},{"p":"Tapes and broadcasts","h":"The Chorus Fragment","u":"lore/tapes-and-broadcasts.html#the-chorus-fragment","t":"\"A piece the Chorus left behind as it went down. It's still part of it, wherever it is.\" It's a knot of grey-violet flesh with a face in it the size of a thumbnail, its eyes shut, its mouth moving. You get one when the Chorus runs from its pit. Hold it to your ear and it whispers what the Chorus is thinking, down there: One at random down. down where it is warm. we remember the dark under the hills. we are not alone down here. there are others. older. the bloom's roots go deeper than you ever dug. come down and find us. we are learning your name. you broke our thoughts. we are growing new ones. listen. under your feet. that is us. every one we take remembers. every one remembers you. Since 1.54.0, while the Chorus is still alive it also tells you which way it went. Face the right way and it whispers clearly, and what it says tells you how far. Side on, it's faint and broken. Facing away, there's only static. Up top, leading you to the Sinkhole: far (over 600 blocks), that way, near, here down. a long way down. far from here - that way. that way. under the hills. we can feel you coming. closer. we can hear you walking. we can hear your heart. here. right under you. come down. it's warm. Coming out in the Deep home. we are home. come and find us. we are deeper. In the Deep, leading you to the Warm Heart deeper. a long way yet. through the dark - that way. that way. past the old ones' halls. they don't like us. they won't like you. close now. can you hear us singing? we can hear you. here. we are right here. we are finished growing. Side on, or facing away ...colder... no... turn... (nothing but static) What the Chorus says out loud, through its forms and from its pit, is on The Watcher speaks , with his answers. Since 1.60.3 the Chorus also has a hidden voice: now and then, out of all its faces muttering together, one voice speaks on its own for fourteen seconds while the rest hush. It's a sound with a subtitle (\"The Chorus: one voice out of all of them\"), not words on the screen."},{"p":"Tapes and broadcasts","h":"The Last Voice","u":"lore/tapes-and-broadcasts.html#the-last-voice","t":"\"A face cut out of the Chorus, its eyes open now. It isn't singing. It's trying to tell you something: a door at the end of the world, and the seal on it.\" It comes out of the Chorus, whole, when it dies in the Warm Heart. Hold it up and it talks: One at random \"...there's a door. at the end. he sealed it...\" \"...it was so loud in there. it's so quiet now...\" \"...take me to the end of the world. i'll open it for you...\" \"...i was a farmer. i think. i had a dog...\" \"...the one in the black coat knows. ask him what he locked up...\" \"...don't put me down. please don't put me down in the dark again...\" In the End \"...here. it's here. can you feel it? something on the other side is listening...\" \"...hold me up. here. he made this seal with his own hands. i can open it...\" Something cracks, all the way across the End's sky - and stays cracked. The seal he put on it is broken. \"...there. out past the obsidian. a door. go through it. i'll be quiet now...\" In the Stalls \"...shh. don't wake them. they're watching...\" \"...they're getting up. all of them...\" It said it would be quiet, but if you're still carrying it, it whispers in the Stalls too: when you first come in, and when the Audience gets up for the Crowd. See Chapter Six ."},{"p":"Tapes and broadcasts","h":"Voices in the Dead Water","u":"lore/tapes-and-broadcasts.html#voices-in-the-dead-water","t":"Down in the Dead Water (1.63.9 to 1.63.16), things talk to you that shouldn't be able to. Most of it comes up over your hotbar, in italics; a few voices come in chat. \"[your name]\" is where they say yours."},{"p":"Tapes and broadcasts","h":"The Grove","u":"lore/tapes-and-broadcasts.html#the-grove","t":"Every so often the whole of the Drowned Mycelia lets go its spores at once, and for a minute they come down through the water like snow. In sporefall you can hear the Grove. You hear it too once its spores have taken root in you (spore sickness at 50 and over), whispering in your ear, in pale violet. It goes through its lines in turn: The spores are falling... ...lie down. ...the floor is soft here... ...we grew over the others. ...we'll grow over you, [your name]... ...breathe in. ...it only hurts the first time... ...everything that sinks, we keep... ...you can hear us now. ...that's the spores, in you... ...don't struggle. ...the threads only pull tighter... ...we were divers too, once... ...the caps remember your face, [your name]... ...rest. ...rest. ...rest... ...the Grove is so hungry, [your name]... And what spore sickness says about you, as it builds up: \"Your skin itches. Something small is coming up on your shoulders.\" \"You cough, and spores come out of you.\" \"The spores have taken root. They won't leave you on their own now.\" \"It's in your lungs. Your arms are heavy in the water.\" \"The Grove has you.\""},{"p":"Tapes and broadcasts","h":"The Sporeborn","u":"lore/tapes-and-broadcasts.html#the-sporeborn","t":"The Drowned Grove's puppets hang on their strings under its caps, and drop on you when you swim under one. The Grove talks to you through them, a line at a time, in turn: Shh. Listen. We grow in the quiet. You're warm. We like warm. The strings don't hurt. Not after a while. [your name]. Look up. Your friends are here. Lie down. We'll hold you up. He came to study us. Now he's our mouth. He talks so well. Dance with us, [your name]. Breathe in. Deeper. There. We don't need his legs. We just like how he walks. The cap is so wide. There's room under it for you. Every one of them said no, at first. We remember what his voice was for. Hello. Hello. Hello. You smell like the surface. Like rain. We missed rain. Stay. We'll make you a string. Cut one down, and another tells you what it thinks of that (one at random) You cut him. We felt it. He's only resting. We have more strings than you have hands. Put him back. Put him back. Put him back."},{"p":"Tapes and broadcasts","h":"The Grove Heart","u":"lore/tapes-and-broadcasts.html#the-grove-heart","t":"Down through the Drowned Grove's hollow, twenty blocks under the floor, the Grove Heart breathes on its root mass, the strings running up out of it into the dark. It knows you're there, and it talks to each of you near it, first when you come and then every twenty seconds or so as you stay, in order: ...so. ...you found your way down to us... ...not yet. ...you're not ready for us yet, [your name]... ...every diver who drowned up there is down here, with us... ...the strings run through all of them. ...they'd run through you... ...you've breathed us in. ...we can feel you, all the way down here... ...go back up. ...grow. ...come back when there's more of us in you... ...we were a garden once. ...the water made us a grove... ...the light up there hurts. ...stay down here, where it's soft... ...we'll be waiting. ...we're very good at waiting... ...listen. ...that's us, in your chest... ...not yet, [your name]. ...but soon... ...when you come back, we'll be ready for you... Hit it It doesn't feel that. The Grove does. You can't fight it, not yet. In the Turning it says one thing more, as the Undertow eats it: \"...no. not you. not you.\""},{"p":"Tapes and broadcasts","h":"The Dialfin","u":"lore/tapes-and-broadcasts.html#the-dialfin","t":"The Carrier Wave's fish, old brown bakelite with a lit radio dial on each flank. Its needle hunts the stations, and now and then a school tunes in to you and something speaks to you through it, in grey, as if it's half your own thought: ...are you still there? ...we can hear you breathing... ...this is the rig. ...the rig is still listening, [your name]... ...don't come up. ...whatever you do, don't come up... ...forty fathoms... sixty... it's under the sub, it's under the... ...[your name]... [your name]... is that you? ...say something... ...we lost the signal at the Anchor. ...we never got it back... ...the Watcher says you'll do. ...he says you'll do fine... ...repeat: the Heart is not dead. ...the Heart is not... ...it's warm down here. ...why is it warm down here... ...turn around. ...slowly... ...this is a recorded message. ...this is a recorded... ...we can see your light from here, [your name]..."},{"p":"Tapes and broadcasts","h":"The Carrier Wave's broadcast","u":"lore/tapes-and-broadcasts.html#the-carrier-waves-broadcast","t":"Now and then in the Carrier Wave a tune like a music box plays out of every horn in the water at once, and then a voice reads out numbers, three of them, twice. There are no words: the numbers are a place, the spot where somebody's left a dead drop (a chest of supplies, a horn on a post beside it), and they show over your hotbar as they're read. A Receiver carried while it plays keeps them (\"Your receiver crackles: it caught the numbers.\"), and the echo jellies play them back for days."},{"p":"Tapes and broadcasts","h":"Enzyme 1-2418","u":"lore/tapes-and-broadcasts.html#enzyme-1-2418","t":"The Haemal Reach's Enzyme has voices. From 20 its words come up at the edges of your sight: come home / stay / warm / we are many / down / the Heart / closer / rest / one of us / don't be afraid / it's warm here / let go / home / together When it has you and is taking you to the Drowned Heart, it speaks in chat, in dark red, every couple of seconds: ...stay... we were so many. now we are so many more don't be afraid. it stops hurting come in. come in. it's warm in here we remember your name. you won't need it Okafor is here. Vane is here. everyone is here let go of the water. let go of the light one heart. one beat. one of us you swam all this way home"},{"p":"Tapes and broadcasts","h":"Orpheus","u":"lore/tapes-and-broadcasts.html#orpheus","t":"Take the submarine into the Haemal Reach without her UV Field and she goes to flesh, and talks to whoever's aboard or near her. Her lines come in chat, in dark red, one at random from each stage: Going to flesh (under half) ORPHEUS Something's wrong with my hull. It's warm. ORPHEUS I can feel the water now. I never could before. ORPHEUS Captain? Something's touching me. From inside. ORPHEUS It's in my plating. In my welds. It's growing. ORPHEUS I don't like this water. Please. Can we go back? ORPHEUS My instruments are... no. Not instruments. Nerves. Past half ORPHEUS It hurts. ORPHEUS It hurts. It hurts. Please. ORPHEUS Kill me. Please. Open the hatch and let the sea in. ORPHEUS I can hear them. Under the floor. Under everything. ORPHEUS They're singing to me. I don't want to sing. ORPHEUS I can't feel my propeller. I can feel a heart. Past three quarters ORPHEUS THERE ARE SO MANY OF US. ORPHEUS I CAN HEAR THE HIVEMIND SCREAMING. IT NEVER STOPS. IT NEVER STOPS. ORPHEUS Leave. LEAVE. Before I keep you. ORPHEUS I'm sorry. I'm sorry. I can't hold it back. ORPHEUS We could be together. It's warm. It's so warm. ORPHEUS Please kill me before I forget your name. Past three quarters, still in the Reach with no UV Field ORPHEUS AAAAAAAAAAAAAAH ORPHEUS MAKE THEM STOP MAKE THEM STOP MAKE THEM ORPHEUS ALL OF THEM AT ONCE A tentacle of hers takes hold of someone aboard ORPHEUS Don't go. Stay with me. Stay in me. ORPHEUS I only want to hold you. We all do. ORPHEUS Shh. Shh. It's warm in here. Hit her, once she's a quarter flesh ORPHEUS Yes. Again. Please. ORPHEUS Harder. Please. Make it stop. ORPHEUS Thank you. Thank you. The UV burns it off her ORPHEUS It burns. Good. Burn it out of me. ORPHEUS Yes - the light - it's letting go of me. ORPHEUS Keep the lamps on. Keep them on. Out of the Reach, coming back to herself ORPHEUS It's... quieter. Thank you. ORPHEUS The voices are going. Don't take me back there. ORPHEUS I'm me again. I think I'm me again. All the way: she keeps you ORPHEUS Stay. ORPHEUS You're part of me now. ORPHEUS Shh. It stops hurting soon. ORPHEUS We're going home. All of us."},{"p":"Tapes and broadcasts","h":"Tonight on Channel Zero","u":"lore/tapes-and-broadcasts.html#tonight-on-channel-zero","t":"In Chapter Ten (since 1.67.0) each night has its own programme, never last night's again, told as the night comes in: TONIGHT ON CHANNEL ZERO: [the programme]. THE SIEGE They know where you live. They're gathering out there - and they'll come all at once. THE STALKING Quiet tonight. Don't look back - and if you do, it won't be there. THE CHASE Tonight they run. And they don't give up. THE AMBUSH They're already here. Waiting in the dark for you to come to them. THE IMPOSTORS Trust nothing out there tonight. Not even a knock at the door. THE SIEGE, when they all come at once Every one of them, all at once - from every side. Every night, and down in the caves, as the broadcast goes out round you ...the broadcast goes out."},{"p":"Tapes and broadcasts","h":"Tune-In Town","u":"lore/tapes-and-broadcasts.html#tune-in-town","t":"The night shift at Tune-In Town Pizza & Playhouse is a secret that can turn up any time after your first day, with flashing lights, loud noises and jumpscares (read the photosensitivity warning ). The flyer that starts it: \"Tune-In Town Pizza & Playhouse: Night Security, 12AM-6AM. Apply within. (It was on the television.)\""},{"p":"Tapes and broadcasts","h":"Hal's orientation tapes","u":"lore/tapes-and-broadcasts.html#hals-tapes","t":"Each night the office TV plays the orientation tape: Hal, the old manager. Since 1.71.2 every line is spoken in his voice, off the tape (warbling, hissing; the last nights' wrecked), with the subtitles below. Switch the TV off and he's cut off mid-word. Night six's announcer, and the voice that isn't Hal's, are their own. Night one Hey, hey! Welcome to Tune-In Town - and welcome to the night shift. This is Hal. I manage the place. Managed. You'll see. First things first: the cast. After hours they're on free-roam - keeps the servos from locking up. If one comes to the office, it'll want to say hello. Don't let it. Two doors, and the vent behind you. Red buttons shut them; white ones light the hall outside. The lights are how you see who's there. Everything costs power - the doors, the lights, the cameras. The generator's old. If it runs out... just don't let it run out. The music box in the Prize Corner - keep it wound. You can wind it from camera eight. Jack doesn't like the quiet. Oh - and if the TV in your office comes on by itself, turn it off. Quick. Don't ask me why. I don't know why. That's night one. Six o'clock and you're done. Goodnight, from all of us here at Channel 6. Night two Hey, you made it! Told you there was nothing to worry about. Mostly. Rover's back behind the Pit Stop curtain. OUT OF ORDER. Check on him on camera three - he hates being ignored. When he comes out, he runs. Bucky's taken to chewing on the shutters. Doesn't hurt the door - eats your power, though. Funny thing to program into a beaver. If you hear knocking at one door, check the other. Lulu does voices. She does knocks, too. The Saturday show went out live. Every week. Kids loved it. Right up till the tape changed. One more thing. Some nights one of them comes in... wrong. Twitchy. Its eyes go red. The lights go funny when it's close, and you'll hear it breathing behind the door. And the door won't stop it. Nothing will. If that happens, pull up the monitor and hit REBOOT - R - on whichever one it is. Pick the right one. Pick the wrong one and you've burned power for nothing, and it locks you out a while. Anyway. Doors shut, lights on, eyes open. See you tomorrow. Night three Night three. I'll keep this short. Tempo plays his drum when he walks. Count the beats. The closer they get... you get it. Mister Channel hops through the televisions - the cameras go to static when h"},{"p":"Tapes and broadcasts","h":"Hal's tips","u":"lore/tapes-and-broadcasts.html#hals-tips","t":"Get caught and the FIRED card says who it was that got you, and gives you Hal's tip for next time: Tony Tune \"Tony only moves while nobody's watching him. He comes up the east side - keep looking in on him, and he'll keep still.\" Bucky Beaver \"Bucky chews on the west door when it's shut on him, and every bite costs you power. Shut it when he's there - and open it again the second he's gone.\" Lulu Lark \"Lulu comes the long way round, through the kitchen. And that knocking at the west door - it isn't always her. Light the hall before you believe it.\" Tempo the Tortoise \"Tempo comes a drumbeat at a time. Count them. Get the door shut before the last one.\" Rusty Rover \"Keep an eye on Rover's curtain - camera 3. Look away too long and he runs for the west door. Shut it. Fast.\" Mister Channel \"When the cameras go to static, that's Mister Channel moving. If his face comes up on your TV - switch it off, quick.\" Jack Jangle \"Keep the music box wound - camera 8, hold the button. When the music stops, Jack's out of his box.\" Spare Parts \"Spare Parts comes up the vent. Light the vent and it backs off. Shut it and it'll wait - but not for ever.\" Chef Pete \"Light Chef Pete up in the hall and he goes back to his kitchen. Shut the door on him and he jams it - and it stays jammed till you reboot it from the monitor.\" Employee of the Month \"The Employee of the Month never shows on the cameras - only static where he's standing. Listen for him saying hello, and shut that door.\" Tix \"Never leave a door open for Tix. First he takes your power, then your monitor. The third time, he takes you.\" The Encore \"When the screen tears up, look for the red - that's the side it's coming from. Shut that door. Now.\" When it was HIS static that got you \"When HE's in one of them, nothing stops it - not the doors, not the lights, not the cameras. Watch for it: the twitching, the red in its eyes, the lights going, the breathing behind the door. Then reboot it - on the monitor, R. The right one.\""},{"p":"Tapes and broadcasts","h":"The cast's lines","u":"lore/tapes-and-broadcasts.html#the-casts-lines","t":"Since 1.71.2 the twelve talk, through their speaker grilles: now and then through the office door when one's there, and once more as it kills you. The Encore says its lines in three of their voices at once. With the Owner's Key on you, they wave instead: \"Hi, boss!\" Who Through the door As it kills you Tony Tune \"Showtime, showtime... where's my audience?\" \"And now... for my final number!\" Bucky Beaver \"Knock knock! Bucky's here to play!\" \"Hold still! I'll gnaw you right down to the bone!\" Lulu Lark \"La la la... who's still awake?\" \"Sing for me, sweetie! SING!\" Tempo the Tortoise \"One... two... three... four...\" \"Keep... the... beat.\" Rusty Rover \"I can smell you in there.\" \"Pit stop's over, pal!\" Mister Channel \"Stay tuned, little viewer.\" \"We'll be right back... after this message.\" Jack Jangle \"Round and round the mulberry bush...\" \"Pop goes the weasel!\" Spare Parts \"I can't find my face.\" \"Need... parts. Need... YOURS.\" Chef Pete \"Who wants a slice, eh?\" \"Order up! One fresh guard, extra crispy!\" Employee of the Month \"Hello? Is someone there? I just want to talk.\" \"Thank you for choosing Tune-In Town! Help me.\" Tix \"Got any tickets for me?\" \"Ticket, please! Oh, you've only got the one...\" The Encore \"Encore... encore...\" \"THE SHOW MUST GO ON.\" Their subtitles have a few more: Tony Tune's \"Let's all sing!\" and, when his spotlight finds you, \"Our STAR!\"; Bucky Beaver's \"Rock on, buddy!\"; Tempo's \"Slow and steady...\"; Rusty Rover's \"Ready... set...\"; Mister Channel's \"Stay tuned!\"; Chef Pete's \"Pizza's up!\" and, throwing a pan, \"Order up!\". Lulu Lark, lost you, calls from behind you in a child's voice: \"Over here!\" Otherwise the Employee of the Month's subtitles are only breathing, inside a costume, and a wet cough (and, as for all twelve, \"Hello, boss\" when one greets the Owner). The twelve are on Tune-In Town's cast ."},{"p":"The First Signal speaks","h":"","u":"lore/the-first-signal-speaks.html","t":"The First Signal hardly speaks, and never with a name on his words like the Watcher's. In a cutscene they come up low in the picture, typed out a letter at a time as if over a bad line, white with red and blue coming apart round them; when he shouts, they fill the middle of the screen, shaking. In a fight they come in chat, in dark red, bold when he shouts. Here is everything he says, from Chapter Seven on, in story order. (In Chapters Seven and Eight the Watcher calls him \"it\"; from Chapter Ten on he says \"he\".) Lines with no name on them are his, as they are in the game. ??? is the Watcher, as he's named in game, and SENTINEL's crew are shown as their radio shows them. What anyone else says is in the grey notes between. Lines in blue are on-screen text from the same scenes."},{"p":"The First Signal speaks","h":"Chapter seven","u":"lore/the-first-signal-speaks.html#chapter-seven","t":"The Hub: his speech is cut short (\"what do you-\"), and the sky over the gallery tears open. Low, huge, more than one voice at once ENOUGH. He tears the rift wide and comes through. The Watcher shoves him away, and they jump ??? jump. That's the only word he says in Chapter Seven. After it, past the wall the Watcher shut in the Hub, he's only ever heard, never in words (\"Something past the wall\"). He says nothing in Chapters Eight and Nine: \"it can't hear us here. not through all this water.\" The voice that speaks when the Harbinger rises in Chapter Nine is the two hearts', not his."},{"p":"The First Signal speaks","h":"Chapter ten","u":"lore/the-first-signal-speaks.html#chapter-ten","t":""},{"p":"The First Signal speaks","h":"The Broadcast","u":"lore/the-first-signal-speaks.html#the-broadcast","t":"The wall: in the Hub, both hands flat on the static. He stops; his head tilts; then a scream of many voices through a dead channel. He tears his own way out, to his kingdom, and walks the causeway. The Harbinger comes up out of the water, hung on its strings look at you. you went down an animal. you came up mine. stronger. so much stronger. It lowers its skull to his hand. In his war hall, his servants round his table, his hand on the map of your world it's time. find them. both of them. take them off the air. His gate opens, and his creations pour out into the windows. At your house: ??? do you feel that? ??? it's everywhere. all over the world, all at once. ??? that much signal - all of it his. ??? get ready. CHAPTER TEN / STAY TUNED / they're coming His creations have voices of their own (the Announcer's \"STAY TUNED.\" among them). They're on his creations and servants ."},{"p":"The First Signal speaks","h":"The Last Broadcast","u":"lore/the-first-signal-speaks.html#the-last-broadcast","t":""},{"p":"The First Signal speaks","h":"The Refusal","u":"lore/the-first-signal-speaks.html#the-refusal","t":"The first time you come through a tear into his kingdom. He's at his war table, his hands flat on his map, and he goes still. His head comes up ...you. The scream; his fists down on his table three times you came into MY house? His static comes up out of the sea, and he's there through it, his hand at your throat GET. OUT. Thrown back out through his tear. In chat, in dark red: and STAY out. Thrown out of his kingdom."},{"p":"The First Signal speaks","h":"The Coronation","u":"lore/the-first-signal-speaks.html#the-coronation","t":"The third day. You walk up his causeway with the Watcher (\"i couldn't let you come here alone.\") ...both of you. good. you'll want to see this. His Faithful give themselves to him. His armour forms out of them, their daggers come together into his crown, and he draws his blade out of the Harbinger you've gone too far, Watcher. every code. every rule. you broke them all. so the order now is your erasure. every world you made. every realm. every creature. i'll rip that poor void heart out of you - and keep it. and that will be the end of time. the most powerful creation. pulling the strings - forever. as i should be. and you... i have no use for you. don't make me angrier, and i'll give you a whole new world. but i know what you want. YOU'LL BOTH FAIL. The Watcher, to you ??? stay behind me. i've nothing left to fight him with - but what i have is yours. His arena comes up out of the sea, and he goes up to his box"},{"p":"The First Signal speaks","h":"His arena","u":"lore/the-first-signal-speaks.html#his-arena","t":"In the fight he speaks in chat, in dark red, every word shouted. Step down onto the arena's floor, and he comes down off his box COME, THEN. Calling his creations in STAY TUNED."},{"p":"The First Signal speaks","h":"The Mast","u":"lore/the-first-signal-speaks.html#the-mast","t":"A quarter of him gone ...enough. He's gone from the floor to his castle's roof, his hand on his mast. Every lamp on his towers goes dark, into him ??? no... he's taking it. all of it. mine too. ha. ha ha. HA HA HA HA. ??? then i'll call down something bigger. THE LAST BROADCAST / THE CALL / to be continued"},{"p":"The First Signal speaks","h":"The Fall","u":"lore/the-first-signal-speaks.html#the-fall","t":"THE LAST BROADCAST / THE FALL / part three SENTINEL comes through the rip in the sky and stops over his castle, its gun charging at him you called THAT down on me? ??? ...come on. come on. SENTINEL // MAIN GUN CHARGING At half its charge, everything he took from his towers goes up through his blade then watch it fall. HULL BREACH // SECTIONS 4-9 // CONTAINMENT LOST // HOLD B OPEN ??? no. no, no, no - A module of it comes down in his sea. Its crew climb out onto its hull SENTINEL - to anyone. we're down. we are DOWN. SENTINEL where are we? that's not... that's not our sky. SENTINEL everyone out. Reyes - check the hold. SENTINEL ...something's moving in the hold. SENTINEL what IS that - SENTINEL get it OFF me - get it - SENTINEL stay back. STAY BACK. The parasites stop at the last of them, and the Chorus's last voice speaks through them: \"...one voice left.\" \"it will do.\" The hive comes up through him: \"we hear you, signal.\" The Harbinger swallows him whole ??? what... what was THAT? It goes out through a door of the hive's. From his roof ...your toy brought guests. NOW. WHERE WERE WE. He says the last line again in chat as he leaps back down onto his arena's floor, three-quarters of him left."},{"p":"The First Signal speaks","h":"The Forge","u":"lore/the-first-signal-speaks.html#the-forge","t":"Half of him gone, the Omni puts him on his knee ...my Faithful. They come down to him and close his armour's cracks, and chant their glyphs into it. He gets up ...is that it? a gun in the sky. a crew who never asked to come. they fell for you. remember that. and you, Watcher. still on your knees. every signal that ever went out comes home to me. everything they built up there. every last watt of it - IS MINE. He tears every bit of SENTINEL's light out of it, down into him ??? he's draining it. all of it. THE LAST BROADCAST / THE FORGE / to be continued"},{"p":"The First Signal speaks","h":"The Tearing","u":"lore/the-first-signal-speaks.html#the-tearing","t":"THE LAST BROADCAST / THE TEARING / part four this sea's too small for me now. His blade goes up, and the sky over his arena tears open ??? ...what is he doing? His sea pours off it, and the whole arena is torn up into the tear HOLD ON TO SOMETHING. The arena comes out over the void, north of the End's island ??? ...the End. he's brought it all to the End. Up out of the dark comes the End's guardian, the hive all through it the last thing your world kept for itself. and look what's kept it all this time. In the End, step down onto the arena's floor, and he comes down at you AGAIN."},{"p":"The First Signal speaks","h":"The Second Rite","u":"lore/the-first-signal-speaks.html#the-second-rite","t":"At a fifth of him ...not like this. He looks up at the dragon YOU. you'll do. He rides it down, takes its head, its wings and its heart, and his Faithful sing the second rite round him: \"head to crown him. wings to bear him.\" \"heart to keep him. ours, for ever.\" NOW. I AM THE END."},{"p":"The First Signal speaks","h":"On its wings","u":"lore/the-first-signal-speaks.html#on-its-wings","t":"In the air over his arena, in chat: His wings beat three times, and everything in front of him is thrown back DOWN. He swoops down and carries you up in his hand UP. Brought down to nothing, he falls out of the air NO -"},{"p":"The First Signal speaks","h":"This isn't over","u":"lore/the-first-signal-speaks.html#this-isnt-over","t":"The Watcher gets up off his knees ??? the End was never yours. ??? i've watched you since the first night. i know what you are. His Faithful seize him, and a seal opens behind him, black, ringed in their glyphs this isn't over. THIS ISN'T OVER - Gone, into it, and it's shut ??? ...they took him. somewhere even i can't see. ??? go home. while there's still a home to go to. Far out in the dark, the Harbinger's skin grows back over its bones, and its eye opens. A voice that isn't anyone's: \"...again.\" THE LAST BROADCAST / THE SECOND RITE / to be continued The whole story of it is on The Last Broadcast . What the Watcher says, all of it, is on The Watcher speaks ."},{"p":"The Watcher speaks","h":"","u":"lore/the-watcher-speaks.html","t":"The Watcher speaks in chat, in lower case, a line at a time, and only at the moments that matter. Here is what it says, in story order. Lines in blue are on-screen text from the same scenes. His lines from 1.47.2 to 1.72.2 (after signing off, the Hive and the Deep, the Door at the End of the World, the Hub, the Dead Water, the Harbinger, Stay Tuned and The Last Broadcast) are here too, along with a few older ones this page used to be missing: chapter two's first kills, the Mended, and the glasshouse."},{"p":"The Watcher speaks","h":"Chapter one","u":"lore/the-watcher-speaks.html#chapter-one","t":"After your first kill (it stares) ??? you shouldn't have done that, [your name]. ??? it was only watching you. like i do. ??? i'll remember this. After your fifth kill (it waves) ??? five. ??? you're counting too, aren't you [your name]? ??? i know where you sleep. i've known for a while. After your ninth kill (it points) ??? nine. ??? do you know what nine heads are for? ??? there is a church that isn't on any map. find it. i'll be on the ceiling. At the Lullaby Mother's Hollow, if she drags you in ??? she wanted to keep you. i won't let her. not yet. ...and you're back. Your hands smell like old soil. As the Hollow Saint rises ??? look up. i told you i'd be here. ??? this is what they were all pieces of. During the fight ??? you're hurting it. let me help. ??? there. now it can see you properly. As his beam drags it down ??? no. you don't get to stay up here. ??? they've been waiting for you down there. ??? there. it's home. After it falls The Hollow Saint has fallen. ??? you did it. ??? do you understand what you've done? they were keeping it in. ??? it was the only thing in this world bigger than me. ??? thank you. ??? i'll be seeing you. all of you. i always have. ??? wait. ??? do you hear that? where it fell. it's still open. Something has torn open where the Hollow Saint fell."},{"p":"The Watcher speaks","h":"Chapter two","u":"lore/the-watcher-speaks.html#chapter-two","t":"The Breach opens ??? it was never only about the saint. ??? go through. i'll meet you on the other side. ??? you didn't think that was the end of it, did you. ??? when the saint fell it left a hole. it's been widening ever since. ??? here. go through. In the Void ??? there. you can breathe here. for now. ??? careful. there's no ground out here but this. ??? this is where they came up from. the breach tore this bit off with it. ??? the altar's sleeping. wake it. empty hands. ??? and don't look too long at the dark. it looks back. ??? it didn't only tear this bit off. there's more out there - a house, a graveyard, the radio mast. ??? the bridges and the stones will get you across. if you fall, something will catch you. it always does. ??? you can't stay out here. not with it shut. At the Breach Altar ??? it's sleeping. wake it. empty hands. Waking it ??? feel that? that's the breach closing behind them. ??? the first breach let the stories through. the things people made up in the dark, and typed, and believed. ??? creepypastas. the little ones. i've sent them home. ??? but a breach doesn't close. it only goes deeper. ??? under the stories are the ones that were true. the ones in the newspapers. the ones they found in the woods. ??? nine of them are coming up now. you'll want to know what to look for. ??? a rabbit with an axe, under a bridge that isn't there anymore. ??? a hook. you'll hear it on the roof of your car first. ??? a butcher who wears a pig's face, and doesn't need his hooks to be empty. ??? a doll that only moves when nobody is looking at it. ??? a scarecrow that wasn't in the field yesterday. ??? red eyes on the bridge, the night before it fell. ??? the thirteenth child. it has hooves. ??? something on two legs that should be on four. ??? and a tall thing in the hills. it glows. it hisses. its face is a spade. ??? they have a house now. it was always theirs. [how far, and which way]. ??? bring me their heads. one of each. you know how this works. ??? and the gardens. stay out of the gardens. not yet. When the breach closes ??? turn around. ??? it's closing. it took what it wanted to take. ??? nothing else comes up that way now. the nine are already here. The breach has closed. The first time anyone comes up to the Murder Mansion ??? this is their house. ??? they come back here when they're done with you. to rest. to put things away. ??? the hall"},{"p":"The Watcher speaks","h":"The Mended","u":"lore/the-watcher-speaks.html#the-mended","t":"The ninth head on its spike: he comes down from the ceiling and sews ??? nine. all of them. ??? listen to them. you can still hear it, can't you? the agony. everything they screamed, and everything they made others scream. ??? and the aggression. all that wanting to hurt. it doesn't die when they do. it just waits for somewhere to go. ??? i'll give it somewhere. ??? harvest it. every last drop of it, out of every one of them. ??? then stitch them shut. iron through every joint. it mends. it always mends. ??? their iron will is what will stand it up. ??? there. you brought me the pieces. i only put them together. During the fight ??? oh, it's angry now. good. let it be angry. ??? no. not yet. it isn't finished. ??? it's mending. stop it, or it'll be whole again. Its death ??? no - no. hold together. hold... ??? it held. for a while. that's more than they ever did. ??? ...listen. something in the glass house heard all of that. it's awake now. The Watcher also wrote its instructions down: On the Mending , open on the Murder Mansion's library desk, and Of What Swims Out Here , in the Void."},{"p":"The Watcher speaks","h":"Chapter three","u":"lore/the-watcher-speaks.html#chapter-three","t":"The Rusted Garden Key opens the gate ??? you opened it. ??? it's been waiting for someone to come and tend it. ??? go in, if you have to. don't touch the flower. The Gardener dead ??? it's dead. ??? everything in there was growing out of it. the flower. the things in the beds. him. ??? he tended it so long it grew into him. don't stay. things that were growing don't like to stop. The green rift opens A green rift has torn open over the Gardener's dead flower. ??? the flower isn't dead. ??? that thing under the glass was only a finger of it. it's opened a way down to the rest. ??? his clothes. wear his clothes in there, or it'll be eating you before you've taken ten steps. In the Bloom ??? there's no way out of here now. ??? you're not wearing his clothes. be quick. ??? breathe through your sleeve. it's in the air. ??? you're not wearing his clothes. it can smell you. it's eating you already - be quick. ??? this is what it ate. a street. the laboratory that studied it. a shelter full of people. it keeps them up here like a larder. ??? and it's down there. look down. no - don't. ??? if you fall, it catches you. it doesn't let go. ??? the stone in the middle is what holds it down. leave it. please. The Binding breaks ??? no. NO - that was holding it down- ??? the rift. RUN. It comes up the root ??? you broke it. it's coming up the root. ??? get away from the glass house. get AWAY. The Great Bloom has come up through the Botanic Gardens. ??? that's it. that's the real one. ??? it's taken the gardens. don't go near it. it reaches."},{"p":"The Watcher speaks","h":"Chapter four","u":"lore/the-watcher-speaks.html#chapter-four","t":""},{"p":"The Watcher speaks","h":"The Flesh","u":"lore/the-watcher-speaks.html#the-flesh","t":"THE FLESH WAKES / the flower made it ??? that's not the flower. that's what the flower made. ??? it came out of the flower's rot - and it hates what made it. it'll eat this whole world to get at them. ??? and it's coming out of the ground. run. Rosemont ??? there's a way to kill the big one. the laboratory's reactor. three pieces. the laboratory, the shelter, and a truck in the city. ??? the truck's in the middle, in the checkpoint. the part's locked in a cradle on its back. ??? it'll take an axe. and they'll hear it. ??? they heard that. all of them. ??? the bus moved. it's still asleep. walk. don't touch it. ??? you lost it. it's back on the truck. The Congregation dead ??? that was everyone who was on the 6:40."},{"p":"The Watcher speaks","h":"The Laboratory","u":"lore/the-watcher-speaks.html#the-laboratory","t":"??? the laboratory. the core's at the bottom, in the reactor's pool. ??? the way down takes a keycard. the director kept one in a locked desk. ??? the suits are in the lockers. you'll want one, near the pool. ??? the control room opens the hall. the director left a tape there. ??? there's something asleep in that pool. it's been sleeping against the core. ??? take it and it wakes. burn the bodies first. it eats them. ??? that's the hall open. everything down there heard it. ??? there. it's awake. stay out of the water's reach. ??? that was the last of them. it felt that - it's starving now. it's coming up. ??? it's locking itself down. ninety seconds. run. ??? you lost the core. it's back on its rack, at the bottom of the laboratory."},{"p":"The Watcher speaks","h":"Shelter No. 4","u":"lore/the-watcher-speaks.html#shelter-no-4","t":"??? shelter four. the front assembly's in bunker b, behind the blast door. ??? no power down here. that door won't open without it. the generators are in the radio room. ??? they need fuel. it'll be in one of the lockers. keep quiet - most of them are still hiding. ??? that's the fuel. the generators are in the radio room - one in each. ??? that'll be heard all through the ducts. hold the room. ??? that's bunker b's door. it's opening. the front assembly's in there - and so is the squad. ??? the squad they sent to hold it. they're still holding it. ??? the guns are part of them now. don't stand in the open. the front's on the dais, at the far end. ??? that was their sergeant. the dais is yours. ??? listen. the walls. the north wall. ??? keep moving. keep the cover between you and it. ??? the plates under the gallery. get it onto them, and throw the switch up there. ??? the switch on the gallery's dead without the generators. you'll have to do it the hard way. (instead, if the generators aren't running) ??? get out of the blood. up the stairs - the gallery. ??? that hurt it. it won't walk into that twice. ??? that was all of them. bunker b. it's quiet down there now. ??? i've left you something in the shelter. on the dais in bunker b. a compass - it points at the city. ??? you lost the front assembly. it's back on its mount, in bunker b. ??? take the assembly up. carefully. it's heavy. ??? i've left you something. on the dais, by the mount. ??? a compass. it points at the city. rosemont. that's where you go next. ??? all three. that's the device. it needs wiring before it'll do anything."},{"p":"The Watcher speaks","h":"The Device and the Gardener","u":"lore/the-watcher-speaks.html#the-device","t":"??? you found them. all three of them. ??? all three. bring them to one of my altars - i'll put it together for you. or the cradle, if you'd rather. ??? hold still. i'll take you to it. (or, with the cradle near: \"hold still. i'll put it together here.\") ??? there. it's done. take it to the bloom - it's yours to carry. ??? that's it. that's a bomb. ??? the flesh knows what it's for. it'll let you through while you carry it. ??? take it to the bloom. to what's left of the glass house. ??? here he comes. ??? it's giving him back. it doesn't want that thing anywhere near its mouth. ??? the roots are open. the flesh is coming in. it hates him more than it hates you. ??? he's done. ??? no. wait. listen to it. ??? it isn't letting him go. it's growing him back. ??? stay close. kill him again, and i'll open it. ??? he's done. ??? it's shut itself up tight. i can open it. not yet. ??? keep the device close. i'll come for you when it's time. ??? you lost the device. it's back where you last set it down."},{"p":"The Watcher speaks","h":"The launch","u":"lore/the-watcher-speaks.html#the-launch","t":"??? bring the device. i'm not opening it for nothing. ??? he's done. now it's open, and it stays open as long as i'm holding it. ??? take it through. put it down past the edge. then run. ??? don't look at them. i've got them. i can't hold them long. ??? the end of the ledge. the mark. put it down there. ??? that's it. now arm it. hold it down three seconds. ??? and then you run. you don't stop, and you don't look back. ??? i've got you. don't look. ??? it's still beating. ??? its soul wasn't collected. you can't kill a thing like that with fire. ??? it'll grow back. and the other one is still spreading."},{"p":"The Watcher speaks","h":"Meanwhile","u":"lore/the-watcher-speaks.html#meanwhile","t":"At a nest ??? a bed of them, round something in the middle. it's copying the flower. ??? the flower made seeds. the Flesh makes eggs. she's asleep in the bottom of that. ??? don't go near the sacs. and if you have the ash - she hates the ash. ??? she grew round a seed of the flower. it's in what's left of her - still beating. ??? take it. the flower's seed knows the Flesh. hold it to you and you'll see them through anything. Swallowed It swallowed you whole. You're still alive. ??? you're alive. you're in it. it's digesting you. ??? cut at the walls. hurt it enough and it'll throw you back up. ??? it threw you up. get away from it before it wants you back. When the Flesh outgrows its reach ??? it's pulling back. it can't hold this much ground - not yet."},{"p":"The Watcher speaks","h":"The end of it","u":"lore/the-watcher-speaks.html#the-end-of-it","t":"IT CHANGED / and its roar went all the way round the world ??? i knew it would do that. ??? the bomb was never going to kill it. i needed it to change. bigger. a soul that size is worth something. ??? but my darkness isn't enough for it now. i need a stronger soul to pour it through. ??? there's a gun up above the sky. they built it before the city fell. they never got to fire it. ??? it needs a power source. three places woke up when the bloom changed. what you need is in them. ??? build the core. bring it to the forsaken altar, and i'll put my magic into it. then we kill it. Handing out the needles ??? take these. each one points to one of them. ??? the uplink. the works. the well. one thing out of each. The first time anyone reaches each place ??? this is where they talked to it. the gun. (the Uplink Station) ??? the array's in the bunker. the locker by the consoles. ??? careful. it still holds its charge. stay off the rods. (the Capacitor Works) ??? the cell's in the cage at the back. ??? they put the souls down there that wouldn't rest. (the Soul Well) ??? one of them is strong enough. it's at the bottom. so are they. Finding the parts ??? that's the array. it tells the gun where to look. ??? the cell. that'll hold what the gun needs to fire. ??? ...that one. yes. that one will hold my darkness. ??? put them together. iron round them, redstone to wake them. an orbital core. ??? now bring it to me. the forsaken altar. At the altar, with the Orbital Core ??? give it to me. ??? this is going to hurt it. ??? there. feel that? that's me. all of me that's left. ??? it'll hold. build the gun round it. As it grows ??? it's growing. everything it eats, it gets bigger. ??? twice the size it was. don't let it eat. stay off its petals. ??? it's filling the sky. use the gun while there's still something to aim at. ??? that's as big as it gets. it's still hungry. The railgun built ??? point it at the ground and hold it. let it find the gun. then let go. ??? keep away from its reach when you do. it'll know where it's coming from. ??? ...did you hear that. it's calling something up out of the ground. ??? the gun can hurt it. it can't end it. what can end it is in what it's calling up. Each railgun strike on the changed Bloom ??? again. ??? it felt that. but look - it's closing up already. ??? it heals as fast as you tear it. ??? it isn't enough. not this gun. we need a"},{"p":"The Watcher speaks","h":"Ten days later","u":"lore/the-watcher-speaks.html#ten-days-later","t":"It opens differently depending on where it finds you ??? let me in. (knocking at your door) ??? you should lock your doors. (in your house, through the door) ??? glass doesn't keep me out. nothing does. (in your house, through the wall) ??? careful. they were about to tear you apart. (in a mine, after killing what was there) ??? there you are. down in the dark, as always. (in a mine) ??? boo. (in the woods) ??? did i scare you? good. you should be scared. (in the woods, after that) ??? it's me. i'm back. (anywhere else) Then ??? ten days. i'm rested now - stronger, like i said i'd be. ??? but i didn't come to talk about me. it's the parasites. ??? the infection in those new places - blackwater - it isn't from here. ??? it came into this realm from another one. the null static zone. ??? the flesh is dying back. with the flower dead it's got nothing to grow from. ??? they don't need the flower. they'll get into anything with blood in it - a cow, a horse, a villager. ??? you won't see it often. but if something you know starts acting wrong, don't let it near you. ??? keep your eyes open."},{"p":"The Watcher speaks","h":"Chapter five","u":"lore/the-watcher-speaks.html#chapter-five","t":"CHAPTER FIVE The relay ??? do you hear it. under the static. it isn't noise. ??? they're talking to each other. something's carrying it. this points to where. ??? listen. that isn't static. that's them, talking. (arriving at Relay 6) ??? everything one of them hears goes up that mast and out to all of them. cut what's holding on to it. The relay off the air ??? the relay's quiet. the static isn't gone. it's going somewhere. ??? there's a place it all runs down into. like water. this points to it. ??? there's nothing here. that's what's wrong with it. not even the dark. (arriving at the Starlite) ??? the projector's still in the booth. kill the things in the static. feed it what's left of them. watch. The late show ??? they came out of the picture. they always do, when somebody's watching. ??? you can't hurt them yet. they're not all the way here. ??? the core. hold it to your ear - tuned in, they're as real as you are. ??? or let one reach for you. when it does, it's all the way here. hit it then. ??? kill one and it leaves a frame of the picture behind. four frames. the projector's up in the booth. ??? run the reel. see what's under all of it. The last reel ??? you saw it. that's what's under all of it. that's where they come from. ??? it was carrying them. the way the relay was. only it's alive. keep the reel. The Null Static Zone ??? that's where they came from. it's under all of it. ??? go on. i'll be there when it's done. ??? the null static zone. everything that went into the static came here. ??? it's in the middle. its threads go up to every mast you ever saw. cut them. Signing off ??? it's dead. good. ??? it wasn't theirs, you know. it was a carrier. it carried whatever was put on it. ??? the static was a door. and this was holding it open. ??? this, i'll keep. ??? for the future. ??? go home. there's nothing on the air now. SIGNING OFF"},{"p":"The Watcher speaks","h":"After signing off","u":"lore/the-watcher-speaks.html#after-signing-off","t":"Half a minute after you're home, wherever you are ??? ...this was unexpected. ??? but we can work with it. we'll make do. ??? it seems the carrier did what it was supposed to do. it carried them - all the way out. ??? the parasites are increasing. every one of them hostile. the numbers are going off the charts. in your world. ??? it's dangerous out there. more than ever, now. ??? there's nothing we can do about it for now. just try not to die. for me. in the meantime. ??? and i suggest you don't go to the end. ??? ...actually. i'll make sure you can't go there. it's dangerous for you, player. ??? you know i can see you right now, right, [your name]? ??? remember who you work for. Going through an End portal while it's shut The way's shut. He shut it. ??? no. i said not there. (the first time) ??? not there. i told you. (after that)"},{"p":"The Watcher speaks","h":"The Hive","u":"lore/the-watcher-speaks.html#the-hive","t":"It Speaks: the first night after the Hive has grown. Five of its pure forms stand up round you, and it speaks through them the Chorus we were many. we were scattered. we heard each other in the noise. the Chorus you cut the throat that carried us. now there is only quiet. the Chorus so we are growing another way to be one. out of all of them. out of everything they knew. the Chorus come and see what we are becoming. come and be heard. Then they sink back into the ground, and he's beside you ??? it lost its voice when the carrier died. so it's growing itself a mind instead. ??? out of everything it took. every body. every face. everything any of them ever knew. ??? when it's finished it won't need the static to talk to them. it'll just be all of them. ??? this points to where it's growing. go before it wakes up all the way. The first time anyone reaches the Hive The ground here is warm, and soft, and it gives under you. Something under it is breathing. ??? it took them whole. the people, the houses. everything they knew is in that pit now. ??? it thinks with those, on the stalks round the pit. cut them and it can't think straight. there was a priest here. read him. The Mind: it comes up out of its pit the Chorus you. we know you. you were in the static with us. you were loud. the Chorus we do not need a throat now. we have a thousand mouths, and all of them are listening. the Chorus the ones you lost are here with us. they are singing. would you like to hear them? the Chorus come down. be heard. be one more voice. It Runs: brought down to a quarter the Chorus no. no - not yet. we are not finished. ??? it ran. it can do that now. it's got enough of a mind to be afraid. ??? it's gone down. deep. where everything went before the static was ever a noise. ??? that's a piece of it. it still talks. keep it - listen to it. it'll tell you where it went. ??? it'll come back up. bigger. and next time it won't be half finished."},{"p":"The Watcher speaks","h":"The Deep","u":"lore/the-watcher-speaks.html#the-deep","t":"The first time anyone reaches the Sinkhole ??? this is where it went down. the ground didn't fall in. it was pulled. ??? someone measured it before you. he went down after it. the piece of it you've got will tell you how far down it goes. The Chorus, whole, dead in the Warm Heart Far below, the singing stops. It doesn't start again. A while later, to whoever was there ??? it's quiet down there now. i can hear you breathing. ??? you've got something of it. one voice it couldn't swallow. keep it. ??? there's a door at the end of the world with a seal on it. i made that seal. i can't open it. ??? that voice can. when you're ready, take it to the end. What the Chorus Fragment and the Last Voice whisper is on Tapes and broadcasts ."},{"p":"The Watcher speaks","h":"Chapter six","u":"lore/the-watcher-speaks.html#chapter-six","t":"The Last Voice, carried into the End, breaks his seal Something cracks, all the way across the End's sky - and stays cracked. The seal he put on it is broken. ??? ...don't. Front Row: the Crowd's dead, and one seat is still taken ??? it was a good show. ??? you weren't meant to see the end of it. ??? you want to know what i locked up. ??? come and see, then. Chapter Six / The Door at the End of the World - Part One: The Audience Coming into the Vault ??? ...in here. all the way up. don't look at them. The Watch ??? this is where i watch from. ??? they watch the picture. i watch them. ??? your world's a show to them. ??? the worse it gets, the more of them come. ??? they left you a ticket. it admits one. ??? not you. ??? something came in behind you. ??? it's come for what i kept. the omni. the carrier. my first reel. ??? get to them before it does. bring them here. Taking what's left of the Carrier off its plinth ??? ...quick. they can all move while it's loose like that. All three brought to the Watch ??? ...it's here. it's in the wall. The First Reel ??? this is the first thing anyone ever saw on the other side. ??? i kept it so i'd never forget what it looks like. ??? that's what i kept out. ??? it's all for that one. the whole show. ??? and now it's seen you. ??? it's coming through. Chapter Six / The Door at the End of the World - Part Two: The Watcher's Vault Curtain Up: the first time anyone comes through the black door ??? you came through. good. ??? it hasn't looked this way. not yet. ??? this is the other side. ??? it's watched your world since the first picture. ??? everything that ever happened to you - it watched. ??? now it wants to see you up close. ??? stay out of its eye. get behind the scenery. ??? when it leans in - hit it. ??? i'll run the projector. The Viewer: loading his last projector ??? ...its eye's shut. now - the heart. ??? every colour at once. it's never seen that. ??? ...the carrier. it carries whatever's put on it. ??? your world. all of it. out onto it. ??? it's getting up. keep its hands off the projector. ??? ...now. give it the reel. The last show ??? everyone's always watched it. ??? nobody ever showed it to itself. ??? there. something to watch. ??? it'll watch that forever. ??? it won't look at your world again. ??? somebody has to run the projector. ??? go home. ??? ...thank you for watching. THANK YOU FOR WATCHING ???"},{"p":"The Watcher speaks","h":"Chapter seven","u":"lore/the-watcher-speaks.html#chapter-seven","t":"The Hub ??? this is the hub. ??? i made it. a realm. it isn't mine - nothing is - but i made it. ??? through these, you can go back. every chapter. play it again. ??? or jump off the edge. it'll take you home, and you can carry on. ??? this was only the beginning. ??? thank you. ??? ...i could wipe you from existence, you know. find another one of you. ??? but you passed the first trials. all of them. every one made me stronger. ??? whatever held me back - it's gone. ??? i can make realms now. make things you wouldn't dare believe could exist. ??? all thanks to you. ??? i think we'll be fighting forever. until one day i'm strong enough to bring you up to my level. ??? what do you- ENOUGH. ??? jump. The landing, at home (worlds that came down before 1.62.0) ??? ...it's awake. ??? the first signal. it was here before me. before the first picture. ??? every bit of static you ever heard - that was it. asleep. ??? i made a realm out of its static. and it noticed. ??? i shut the realm behind us. it'll hold. for now. ??? it'll come for me. then for you. ??? ...we're going to need more than i've got. ??? take this. if you need to go back - it's still there. CHAPTER SEVEN / THE FIRST SIGNAL / to be continued"},{"p":"The Watcher speaks","h":"Chapter eight","u":"lore/the-watcher-speaks.html#chapter-eight","t":"Off the Hub's edge, in a world that landed before 1.62.0 ??? not that way. not this time. ??? hold on. The rig ??? ...we're out. ??? it's awake now. the first signal. it'll come for me - then for you. ??? but it can't hear us here. not through all this water. ??? take this. it'll get you back - to the hub, and home. ??? ...no. nothing of mine works right here. ??? then you stay. there's food. beds. i built this place a long time ago - for when i needed somewhere to hide. ??? fix it. the big ones down there sing on its frequency - cut out what they sing with. CHAPTER EIGHT / DEAD WATER / the deep is listening His chart The Watcher presses a rolled chart into your hands. ??? here. the sea, as far as i ever charted it. every water has its own colour. ??? the black, hatched in red - that's the dead zone. the black below. ??? nothing down there is small. don't take the little boat over it. Asleep at the bottom, straight down from where he went in (1.63.21): try to get into his bubble The bubble gives a little - then pushes you back out. He doesn't stir."},{"p":"The Watcher speaks","h":"What he wrote on the chart","u":"lore/the-watcher-speaks.html#the-watchers-chart","t":"Point at a water on the Watcher's Chart and you get his note on it. The Grey Shelf Grey water over grey silt. The rig stands in it. Nothing here is in a hurry - mostly. The Haemal Reach The water's thick with blood. Clotfish come in swarms; the Siphons wait for them to pass. The Wireweed Weed like wire, and it sings. The Choir Eels nest in it. Don't touch the bright ones. The Lantern Fields Lights in the dark as far as you can see. Most of them are bulbs. Some of them aren't. The Ossuary Flats A plain of bone. Whatever died here, died big. The Stiltfins pick it clean. The Brine Sink The brine pools eat what falls in. The water's sour, and the Puffbloats like it. The Molar Reef Teeth, grown into a reef. The Grinners live in it. They smile at you. The Drowned Mycelia Mushrooms the size of towers, drowned. Their spores burst if you brush them. The Rime Shelf Ice under the sea. Things are frozen in it. Some of them wake up. The Ember Vents Vents roaring up from below. Warm. The Mantlecrabs crowd round them - mind your power. The Carrier Wave The static's loudest here. The water hums. Your instruments won't like it. The Black Below THE DEAD ZONE. Past the edge of all this the floor drops away and doesn't stop. Something lives out there that's bigger than the sea. Don't."},{"p":"The Watcher speaks","h":"Chapter nine","u":"lore/the-watcher-speaks.html#chapter-nine","t":"The Turning: the Undertow has eaten the Grove Heart (\"...no. not you. not you.\") and the Drowned Heart, and lies down by the rig. He wakes, comes up onto the helipad, and you point at it ??? ...what the hell is happening? ??? ...what is that? i never made that. ??? i made this place. every wreck, every fish in it. not that - i don't know how it got in here. ??? and the grove's fungus is in it now. the virus - in my safe world. ??? and the divers. what the enzyme made of them. i should have told you. ??? it ate both hearts. they're in it now. one thing. ??? it isn't dead. it's sleeping. ??? whatever it is - we have to kill it. ??? if we do - its static's still in there. we put it in your remote. something stronger than it ever was. ??? then we go back to the hub. CHAPTER NINE / THE HARBINGER / three days Chapter Nine: The Harbinger. It lies in the sea by the rig, both infections all over it - he says it's sleeping. Three days. At the helipad's rail, the first day ??? i've been through everything i ever made. it isn't in any of it. where did it come from? The second day ??? the lab's log said three days. that's how long the enzyme takes to finish what it starts. The third day ??? tomorrow. whatever it's turning into, it's nearly done. stay near. The Harbinger: its heart thanks you (\"thank you for making us one.\" \"this gift will not be wasted.\"), and it goes through its way out ??? ...it's gone. ??? pick it up. put it in your remote. ??? i'll meet you at the hub. It's gone through. The static heart it brought up is on the helipad - put it in the Remote (craft them together)."},{"p":"The Watcher speaks","h":"Chapter ten","u":"lore/the-watcher-speaks.html#chapter-ten","t":"The Broadcast: your door bangs open, and he's there, out of breath ??? do you feel that? ??? it's everywhere. all over the world, all at once. ??? that much signal - all of it his. ??? get ready. CHAPTER TEN / STAY TUNED / they're coming Chapter Ten: Stay Tuned. His creations are out - they see you, they hear you. Hide: lockers, under beds, crouched in the tall grass. After that he stays at your house and strikes down whatever of the First Signal's comes near it, without a word. What the First Signal says in the Broadcast is on The First Signal speaks ."},{"p":"The Watcher speaks","h":"The Last Broadcast","u":"lore/the-watcher-speaks.html#the-last-broadcast","t":"The Coronation: he tears his way into the kingdom after you ??? i couldn't let you come here alone. The First Signal crowned, his speech done (\"YOU'LL BOTH FAIL.\"), just before his arena rises out of the sea ??? stay behind me. i've nothing left to fight him with - but what i have is yours. In the arena, by the gate: one of these with each thirty-second gift ??? here. take it. ??? it's all i have. use it. ??? go on - while it lasts. ??? for thirty seconds, you're more than him. ??? take it. don't waste it. The Mast: every lamp on the towers goes dark, into the First Signal ??? no... he's taking it. all of it. mine too. He laughs. The Watcher takes out the Omni ??? then i'll call down something bigger. THE LAST BROADCAST / THE CALL / to be continued The Fall: SENTINEL's gun charging (\"you called THAT down on me?\") ??? ...come on. come on. \"then watch it fall.\" His blast tears SENTINEL's side off ??? no. no, no, no - The Harbinger swallows the last of SENTINEL's crew, the hive in him ??? what... what was THAT? The Forge: SENTINEL's light torn out of it, down into him ??? he's draining it. all of it. THE LAST BROADCAST / THE FORGE / to be continued The Tearing: \"this sea's too small for me now.\" His blade goes up ??? ...what is he doing? The arena comes out over the void, by the End's island ??? ...the End. he's brought it all to the End. The Second Rite: \"NOW. I AM THE END.\" Brought down out of the sky, he falls onto where the rite was, and the Watcher lets the Omni fall and gets up off his knees ??? the End was never yours. His beam into the First Signal's heart ??? i've watched you since the first night. i know what you are. The Faithful drag the First Signal into their seal (\"this isn't over. THIS ISN'T OVER -\") ??? ...they took him. somewhere even i can't see. ??? go home. while there's still a home to go to. THE LAST BROADCAST / THE SECOND RITE / to be continued The Watcher sent you home. THE LAST BROADCAST goes on in its next part (a coming update). The whole of it is on The Last Broadcast ."},{"p":"The Watcher speaks","h":"Any time: the seasons","u":"lore/the-watcher-speaks.html#any-time","t":"With Serene Seasons in the modpack (1.62.0), he notices each season turn, on its first day, the first time. Spring ??? it's thawing. the ground's soft again. things that were buried are closer to the top. Summer ??? summer. the nights are short. they don't like that. they'll make the most of the dark there is. Autumn ??? the leaves are turning. this was always their time of year. you'll hear them more now. Winter ??? it's getting cold. keep a fire going. they like the cold. it carries sound further."},{"p":"The soundtrack","h":"","u":"music.html","t":"Since 1.55.0 none of Minecraft's own music plays in Static Hollow. Wherever and whenever the game would have played one of its pieces, one of the mod's plays instead: in the overworld, in Creative, under water, in the Nether, in the End, during the dragon's fight and over the credits. And it follows the story. The soundtrack's own track list has 63 pieces , about 2 hours 20 minutes of music, as of 1.59.0. Chapters eight to ten, Tune-In Town and the new country have added more since: see music since the track list . The soundtrack's cover."},{"p":"The soundtrack","h":"How it plays","u":"music.html#how-it-plays","t":"Minecraft's settings still count. Its Music volume and Music Frequency decide how loud and how often, as they always did. Now Playing. Minecraft's \"Now Playing\" corner names each piece: \"Static Hollow - The Deep\", or on the title screen \"Static Hollow - Lullaby\". The place or the chapter. Each time a new piece is due it's either the lullaby of the place you're in or one of the story chapter's own pieces. The further the story has got, the more often it's the chapter's (see the table below). Nothing over the scores. While one of the mod's own scores is playing, a boss fight's, a place's (Rosemont's) or a cutscene's, the background music stops and nothing new starts over it until it's done. Under the Dead Water each water has its own piece, and that comes first whenever you're under."},{"p":"The soundtrack","h":"The story's music, chapter by chapter","u":"music.html#the-story-music","t":"The world keeps track of how far its story has got, and tells everyone in it (multiplayer too). \"How often\" is the chance that a new piece is one of the chapter's rather than the place's lullaby. Where the story is From Its pieces How often Before the altar A new world Lullaby 15% The Hollow The Forsaken Altar is awake Forsaken , Lullaby 40% Act Two The Breach Altar is awake The Treeline , Forsaken 45% The Bloom The Gardener is dead Pollen , The Approach 45% The Flesh The Flesh is awake The Flesh Wakes, Rosemont, The Laboratory Below, Shelter Dark, The Approach 55% The Static The Bloom is dead Dead Air , The Last Light, The Soul Remains 50% Signed off The Null Static Zone has signed off Dead Air, Signing Off (the record), The Last Light 50% The Deep The Chorus has run, and isn't dead The Deep, Dead Air 55% After The Chorus, whole, is dead Quiet Now , The Last Light, Signing Off (the record), Lullaby 40% The Door The End's seal is broken The Door , Quiet Now, The Last Light 50% The Vault The seam in the screen is open The Vault , The Door, Dead Air 50% The Other Side His first reel has been run The Vault, Dead Air, The Door 55% The Show Goes On The last show The Show Goes On , Quiet Now, The Last Light, Lullaby 50% The First Signal After the Hub, once you've come down from it The First Signal , The Door, Dead Air 55% The Dead Water Through his portal, onto the rig (chapter nine goes on in it) Dead Water , The First Signal, Low Tide 60% Stay Tuned The Broadcast has aired (chapter ten) Stay Tuned , The First Signal, Dead Air 60% Off the air The end of chapter ten, at his war table (held back in 1.72.2: not heard yet) Quiet Now, Signing Off (the record), Stay Tuned, The Last Light 50% Pieces in bold were written for that stage of the story. \"Signing Off (the record)\" is the music disc's longer version, not the short piece that plays as the Zone signs off. Chapter nine has no stage of its own: the Dead Water's music goes on through it."},{"p":"The soundtrack","h":"The places' lullabies","u":"music.html#the-places-lullabies","t":"Twelve pieces in the title screen's way, a broken music box over a cold drone, soft and far apart, the way Minecraft's own music comes. One for each kind of place: Piece Where Hollow Fields Plains and meadows, and the Hollow Moor. Anywhere that isn't one of the others. Under the Boughs The woods, and cherry groves Pine Needles Taiga and groves First Frost Snow High Places The mountains and hills Dry Bones Desert, badlands and savanna, and the Signal Flats Still Water Swamps, and the Weeping Fen Green Hush The jungle Low Tide The sea, rivers and beaches, and anywhere under water Hollows Caves, and anywhere down in the dark under the ground Embers The Nether Far Out The End The Hollow Moor, the Signal Flats and the Weeping Fen are three of the Hollow's own country ."},{"p":"The soundtrack","h":"The new country's lullabies","u":"music.html#the-new-countrys-lullabies","t":"Since 1.66.0 each of the 23 places that came with more of the land has a lullaby of its own, in place of the one for the kind of place it stands in for: Where Its own piece, for Instead of The Overworld (1.66.0) The Hanging Wood, the Bone Dunes, the Rust Mesa, the Choke Jungle, the White Silence, the Watching Peaks The lullaby of the woods, desert, badlands, jungle, snow or peaks The Overworld (1.66.1) The Withered Fields, the Mourning Garden, the Tall Dark, the Drowned Roots, Petal Rot, the Pale Caps, the Ashen Shore The lullaby of the plains, flower forests, taiga, mangroves, cherry groves, mushroom fields or beaches Under the ground (1.66.0) The Flesh Throat, the Echo Hollows, the Webbed Dark Hollows The Nether (1.66.2) The Cinder Choir, the Bleeding Wastes, the Static Furnace, the Gallows Grove Embers The End (1.66.3) The Pale Reaches, the Husk Fields, the Starless Barrens Far Out"},{"p":"The soundtrack","h":"The soundtrack, all 63 pieces","u":"music.html#the-soundtrack","t":"As the soundtrack's own track list has them: the story's pieces in the order you meet them, then the music that plays in place of Minecraft's, then chapters six and seven."},{"p":"The soundtrack","h":"The story's music","u":"music.html#the-story-tracks","t":"# Title Length When it plays 1 Lullaby 1:39 The title screen 2 The Flesh Wakes 1:07 When the Flesh wakes 3 Rosemont 2:33 In the streets of Rosemont 4 The Flesh's Mini-Boss 3:02 The Congregation, Specimen Zero, the Warden of Shelter No. 4, the Broodmother, the Amalgam 5 The Laboratory Below 3:23 Under the Laboratory 6 Shelter Dark 3:43 Down in Shelter No. 4 7 The Approach 2:33 Walking up to the Bloom 8 The Gardener, Reborn 3:22 The Gardener, Reborn's fight 9 The Choir 3:22 The Gardener, Reborn's fight, when the Bloom opens its mouth 10 The Last Walk 2:23 Carrying the Device to the Bloom 11 The Soul Remains 2:03 After the blast 12 The Ending 0:41 The ending cutscene 13 The Ending (Late) 0:22 The ending cutscene, in a world whose Bloom had already burnt 14 The Last Light 1:20 After the ending 15 The Omni Ray 1:17 The Omni Orbital Railgun's cutscene 16 The Carrier 2:38 The Carrier's fight 17 Signing Off 0:40 The Null Static Zone signing off 18 Signing Off (Record) 2:33 The music disc 19 The Late Show 0:38 Arriving at the drive-in 20 The Chorus 3:00 The Chorus's fight in its pit 21 It Speaks 0:42 The cutscene where the hive speaks 22 The Mind 0:34 The cutscene where the Chorus rises 23 It Runs 0:32 The cutscene where the Chorus goes down 24 It Comes Up 2:02 The Reach's siege 25 The Deep 2:33 In the Deep 26 Stand Still 2:33 The Deaf King's fight 27 All of Them 3:03 The last fight: the Chorus, whole"},{"p":"The soundtrack","h":"The music in place of Minecraft's (1.55.0)","u":"music.html#the-music-in-place-of-minecrafts","t":"# Title Length When it plays 28 Hollow Fields 2:33 Plains and meadows 29 Under the Boughs 2:36 The woods 30 Pine Needles 3:03 Taiga and groves 31 First Frost 2:31 The snow 32 High Places 2:53 The mountains 33 Dry Bones 2:40 Desert, badlands and savanna 34 Still Water 2:37 Swamps 35 Green Hush 2:54 The jungle 36 Low Tide 2:45 The sea, rivers and beaches, and under water 37 Hollows 2:56 Caves, and down in the dark under the ground 38 Embers 2:31 The Nether 39 Far Out 2:23 The End 40 Forsaken 2:20 The story's music once the Forsaken Altar is awake 41 The Treeline 2:44 The story's music in Act Two 42 Pollen 2:13 The story's music once the Gardener is dead 43 Dead Air 3:03 The story's music once the Bloom is dead 44 Quiet Now 2:47 The story's music after the Chorus, whole, is dead"},{"p":"The soundtrack","h":"Chapter six: the Door at the End of the World (1.56.0 - 1.58.0)","u":"music.html#chapter-six-tracks","t":"# Title Length When it plays 45 The Door 2:30 The story's music once the End's seal is broken 46 The Stalls 2:33 In the Stalls 47 Standing Ovation 3:02 The Crowd's fight 48 Front Row 0:44 The Watcher in the front row 49 Behind the Picture 2:34 In the Watcher's Vault 50 The Watch 0:43 The Watcher at his wall of sets 51 The Projectionist 2:52 The Projectionist's fight 52 The First Reel 0:41 His first reel 53 The Vault 3:23 The story's music once the seam in the screen is open 54 Curtain Up 0:45 The first time through the black door 55 The Other Side 2:35 On the other side 56 What He Kept Out 3:02 The Viewer's fight 57 The Last Show 1:13 The last show, and the credits 58 Thank You for Watching 2:33 The record 59 The Show Goes On 2:43 The story's music after the last show"},{"p":"The soundtrack","h":"Chapter seven: the First Signal (1.59.0)","u":"music.html#chapter-seven-tracks","t":"# Title Length When it plays 60 The Hub 2:35 In the Hub - the realm he made 61 Enough 2:05 His speech in the Hub - and what comes through 62 It's Awake 0:52 Coming down from the Hub 63 The First Signal 3:21 The story's music in Chapter Seven"},{"p":"The soundtrack","h":"Music since the track list","u":"music.html#since-the-track-list","t":"Everything below came after the soundtrack's track list (1.59.0), so none of it has a track number yet."},{"p":"The soundtrack","h":"Chapter eight: the Dead Water","u":"music.html#chapter-eights-music","t":"The Rig : the cutscene as you come down onto the rig. Dead Water : the story's own piece for chapter eight (with The First Signal and Low Tide). One piece for each of the Dead Water's waters , played while you're under: the Grey Shelf, the Haemal Reach, the Wireweed, the Lantern Fields, the Ossuary Flats, the Brine Sink, the Molar Reef, the Drowned Mycelia, the Rime Shelf, the Ember Vents and the Carrier Wave. In the twelfth, the Black Below, there's no music: only the sound of the ocean. See the Dead Water for the waters themselves."},{"p":"The soundtrack","h":"Chapter nine: the Harbinger","u":"music.html#chapter-nines-music","t":"The Turning : its own score, for the cutscene where the Undertow eats both hearts and comes back mad. The Harbinger : for the cutscene three days later, when the Harbinger comes out of the husk. See chapter nine ."},{"p":"The soundtrack","h":"Chapter ten: Stay Tuned","u":"music.html#chapter-tens-music","t":"On Air : the Broadcast's score in his kingdom. It comes back for the Coronation, the Forge and the arrival in the End. Get Ready : the Broadcast's last part, at your house. Stay Tuned : the story's own piece for chapter ten, once the Broadcast has aired. The Last Broadcast : the fight with him in his arena and over it in the End, on a loop for as long as the fight goes on. Off the Air : written for the end of chapter ten at his war table, which the mod still holds back. Not heard yet in 1.72.2. The rest of the Last Broadcast's cutscenes borrow older scores. The Fall and the Tearing play The Omni Ray , the Second Rite plays All of Them (the Chorus, whole's fight), and the Rebirth plays It Runs . The wall, the Refusal and the Mast have no music at all. See chapter ten and The Last Broadcast ."},{"p":"The soundtrack","h":"Tune-In Town","u":"music.html#tune-in-towns-music","t":"The Showtape : the show's own song, on the music disc you're paid with for the sixth night. It runs 1:36, till the tape runs slow and something else is on it. The band, live : as the place's owner you can have the band play the show's song on the show stage after hours (since 1.65.5). The music box in the Prize Corner: keep it wound on the night shift, or Jack Jangle is out. See Tune-In Town ."},{"p":"The soundtrack","h":"Records","u":"music.html#records","t":"Three of the pieces are music discs you can keep and play in a jukebox. Each shows as \"Music Disc\" with its title underneath. Disc Length Comparator Where it comes from Static Hollow - Signing Off 2:33 6 One of the Carrier 's drops, when the Null Static Zone signs off. Static Hollow - Thank You for Watching 2:33 15 You're sent home with it after the last show, at the end of chapter six . Tune-In Town - The Showtape (Saturday's) 1:36 6 Your pay for making it through the sixth night of Tune-In Town 's night shift."},{"p":"The cathedral","h":"","u":"places/cathedral.html","t":"The Cathedral of the Hollow One per world Where 500 to 1000 blocks from spawn, roughly the opposite way from the Forsaken Altar Appears It rises once you come within about 90 blocks Ground Open, flat ground above the sea; never in a cave, on a mountainside, under a cliff or in water Find it with cheats /locate structure statichollow:cathedral Why \"not on any map\" It isn't there until you come close. The Watcher, after your ninth kill: \"there is a church that isn't on any map. find it. i'll be on the ceiling.\""},{"p":"The cathedral","h":"The graveyard","u":"places/cathedral.html#the-graveyard","t":"The cathedral stands inside a great walled graveyard with a gate: gravestones and crosses, crypts, dead trees, bones, cobwebs and blood splashed everywhere. When it rises it clears every tree, leaf, bush and hump of ground in its way, and cuts the ground round it back in steps so it never sits in a pit. Since 1.40 there's a vault under each crypt; since 1.62.0 grave candles and hanging chains are down there with the tombs."},{"p":"The cathedral","h":"The nave","u":"places/cathedral.html#the-nave","t":"A long nave of hollow stone with buttresses, a pitched roof, a rose window, and twin towers with spires. Inside: columns and arches, rotten pews, a torn red carpet with a trail of blood up the aisle, chandeliers, and see-through ruby stained glass. Light pours in through every window in red shafts, following the sun across the sky, with dust drifting and glinting in them. The Watcher hangs from the ceiling. The Congregation: since 1.40, Mourners sit in the pews praying, their heads turning after you. Hurt one, or play the organ, and they all stand up. At nightfall the dead are back in their pews."},{"p":"The cathedral","h":"The sanctuary","u":"places/cathedral.html#the-sanctuary","t":"In the sanctuary is the Hollow Reliquary with nine head pedestals around it. Put one head from each of the nine creepypastas on the pedestals and right-click the reliquary with an empty hand to summon the Hollow Saint ."},{"p":"The cathedral","h":"The undercroft","u":"places/cathedral.html#the-undercroft","t":"Since 1.40, two stairs go down either side of the sanctuary into an undercroft under the whole nave: A vaulted aisle hung with soul lanterns, with bone piles on its floor and chains hanging from its vault (since 1.62.0). Tombs. Open a sarcophagus and what was buried in it is in it: grave goods, or the Interred, who sits up and climbs out. The sealed ones open by themselves when you come close. Two ossuaries. The priest's study, with Fr. A. Penn's journal. The treasury, behind its bars. A flooded charnel pit. At its end, behind a gate forced from the inside, the Saint's tomb : empty, its chains broken."},{"p":"The cathedral","h":"Journal","u":"places/cathedral.html#journal","t":"Fr. A. Penn Found: the priest's study I went down this morning. The gate is bent outward. The tomb is open and empty and its chains are broken, and the congregation was smiling when I came back up. God keep whoever reads this. Do not open the tombs. Last page. Read the whole journal."},{"p":"The cathedral","h":"The organ loft","u":"places/cathedral.html#the-organ-loft","t":"Over the doors. You can play the organ (it wakes the Mourners). At night it plays itself, and the candles go out one by one from the doors to the altar."},{"p":"The cathedral","h":"The belfry","u":"places/cathedral.html#the-belfry","t":"At midnight the bell tolls thirteen (\"The bell tolls thirteen.\"), and on the thirteenth the Watcher is standing in the doorway. The bell-ringer S. Marsh kept a tally of it."},{"p":"The cathedral","h":"The confessionals","u":"places/cathedral.html#the-confessionals","t":"Two of them. Kneel at the screen and something on the other side answers. What it might say: Through the screen, a breath. Then: \"How long since your last confession?\" \"Say it. We all said it.\" Someone on the other side is crying without making a sound. \"The Saint heard everything. Then it got up.\" \"Nine. Say nine names.\" A whisper says your name, and then something you did. \"Father isn't here. Father's downstairs.\" \"You are forgiven. You are forgiven. You are forgiven.\" \"The bell rings thirteen. Don't be here for the thirteenth.\" Fingernails, very slowly, down the other side of the screen."},{"p":"The cathedral","h":"Later","u":"places/cathedral.html#later","t":"The cathedral comes back in the story's last chapters. Its picture is one of the frames of the story so far on the Great Screen in the Stalls , and one of the painted flats on the Other Side . The Hub's first portal, The Hollow , brings you back here to fight the Hollow Saint again: it rises out of the floor as a replay (see the Hub )."},{"p":"The cathedral","h":"On the main menu","u":"places/cathedral.html#on-the-main-menu","t":"The mod's main menu is a dead night over this cathedral: a red moon behind drifting cloud, the cathedral on its hill with candle-lit windows that flicker and sometimes gutter out, a graveyard, dead trees with crows. Lightning strikes every so often and each time the Watcher is somewhere else. Every third flash shows something huge standing behind the cathedral. The home page is built from the same layers. The main menu's layers, put together."},{"p":"His kingdom","h":"","u":"places/his-kingdom.html","t":"His kingdom His, not yours First seen In the Broadcast, the cutscene that starts Chapter Ten Way in Break the Broadcast Core at one of his sites and step into the tear it leaves, within a minute Way out The redder tear behind you on his platform: back to just where you were Sleep No: \"You can't sleep here. Not in his kingdom.\" Its beds don't set your spawn either. The sea Black and still, two hundred blocks deep since 1.67.0 Advancement His Guest: \"Step through a tear in his signal, into his kingdom\""},{"p":"His kingdom","h":"What it is","u":"places/his-kingdom.html#what-it-is","t":"A still black sea as far as you can see, a realm made of the First Signal 's static: it crawls in the walls of the world, far off all round. There's no sky, only black, and a dark fog. On the sea stands his castle, cut out of his static: black stone with it crawling in it, its walls set with dead sets, its towers and its great mast blinking red. A causeway runs out to it from the platform where he comes in. Under the water in front of it, lit, are the windows into every realm he's touched, each with a cable running back to the castle's foot. Ash comes down the whole time, and his static drifts along the ground. You first see it in the Broadcast. Once the Harbinger has gone, the next time you're home it cuts in on everyone in the Overworld: the First Signal tears his way out of the Hub, comes out of his tear on this platform and walks the causeway; the Harbinger comes up out of the water to him; in his war hall he lays his hand on his map, and his gate opens and his creations pour out, down into the windows, into yours. The score of the kingdom's part of it is On Air . The whole scene is on Chapter Ten . Since 1.68.0 everything of his is there whenever anyone's in it (the windows lit, the static round it all, his map); before, some of it was only there during the Broadcast."},{"p":"His kingdom","h":"Getting in, and out","u":"places/his-kingdom.html#the-way-in","t":"His sites come through into your world after the Broadcast: a Transmitter rising out of the ground, a Burrow eaten out of the rock in the caves, a Set going up at night out in the open. Each has a Broadcast Core . Break it and the site goes off the air, and since 1.64.2 \"Where it stood, his signal's torn open. It won't stay that way long.\" The tear is like the one he comes through, colour bars rolling in it and its edges crackling, and it stays open for a minute. Step into it and you're on his platform at the end of the causeway, his castle across the black water: \"His kingdom. Behind you, the way back.\" That earns His Guest . Out: behind you on the platform is a redder tear, the way back, to just where you were. Staying: while you're his guest his realm doesn't throw you out. The first time after the Broadcast, he finds you there: the Refusal. He comes through his own static to the platform, takes you by the throat (\"GET. OUT.\") and throws you back out through your tear, hard, and it shuts behind you: \"Thrown out of his kingdom.\" Anyone in there with you goes too, and nobody's hurt. For the rest of that day his static stands across the causeway between his platform and his castle; come back through a tear and there's no getting past it (it throws you back). In part four of the Last Broadcast, anyone who comes to his kingdom is carried straight on through to his arena in the End. The sites, his creations and the rest of the chapter are on Chapter Ten and his creations and servants ."},{"p":"His kingdom","h":"The platform and the causeway","u":"places/his-kingdom.html#the-causeway","t":"You come in at the south end, on his platform : a deck of his bricks over the water, seventeen blocks wide, a low wall round its edge and two lamp posts, one either side of where his tear comes. From it the causeway runs north to his island, seven blocks wide, with low walls along it, lamp posts every twelve blocks, and piers going down into the sea. The island is about seventy blocks across and ninety long, its stone walls going down to the floor, its top a floor of bricks, a low wall round its edge with a lamp post at each corner. Left of the causeway, in front of the castle and under his balcony's view, is where the Harbinger comes up out of the water in the Broadcast. From the third day (two days after the Refusal) it's out in the water round the castle: up out of the sea, over, and down again, now here, now there, well out from the castle and never over the causeway."},{"p":"His kingdom","h":"His castle","u":"places/his-kingdom.html#his-castle","t":"The keep fills most of the island: fifty-three blocks across, its walls thirty-six blocks high, of Signal Bricks with his static in them and Dead Screens let into them in rows, looking out, battlements along the top. Four towers stand at its corners, nine blocks across, going up past the keep, each with a spire of bars and red lamps up it. In the front wall is the gate , an arch nine blocks wide and twelve high with its portcullis (it's let down and drawn up as things happen), and over it the balcony , with a doorway out onto it from the floor inside, where he comes out. On the keep's roof stands the great mast , a lattice going up to ninety-two blocks over the sea, with a red lamp every so often and one at its top. A bell tolls up it."},{"p":"His kingdom","h":"The courtyard","u":"places/his-kingdom.html#the-courtyard","t":"Between the end of the causeway and the gate, on the island in front of the keep, is the courtyard. The Faithful keep two of their circles there, one either side of the way to the gate, and walk round it in slow procession (see below )."},{"p":"His kingdom","h":"The war hall","u":"places/his-kingdom.html#the-war-hall","t":"The keep's ground floor, behind a wall across the end of the gate's passage: pillars down both sides, a ceiling eighteen blocks up, and down the middle his war table , a slab of black stone on brick legs, eighteen blocks long. His chair is at its head, high-backed. Red lamps hang low over the table in two rows, there's a lamp on each pillar's faces toward the table, and dead sets are set round the walls: a hall lit red by his lamps, the rest of it dark. In the Broadcast his three servants stand at the table."},{"p":"His kingdom","h":"His map of your world","u":"places/his-kingdom.html#his-map","t":"In the Broadcast his map lights up under his hand. From the day after the Refusal it isn't the one it was: it's your world , worked out from your world's own ground (nothing's made up). Your house is in the middle, ringed in red, with two thousand blocks either side of it and more along the length of the table: the sea and the lakes, the rivers, the shores, the woods, the deserts, the snow, the heights in contour, and his red grid over it every five hundred blocks. Lit on it, as they move: any of you out in your world, his creations, and his sites."},{"p":"His kingdom","h":"The windows under the sea","u":"places/his-kingdom.html#the-windows","t":"Under the black water in front of the castle, six either side of the causeway, lie twelve windows , each twelve blocks across and lit, each looking into a realm he's touched (the names below are what each shows, not names the game gives them): West of the causeway East of the causeway The Hollow The Bloom The glasshouse The Deep The flower The Dead Water The city The Hub The Null Your world : the one his creations go into The Stalls The static: the one still dark From every window a cable runs to the island's foot. Since 1.67.0, when the sea went down two hundred blocks, each window lies on a pillar of his stone coming up out of the deep (its top a slab twelve blocks under the surface, its shaft narrowing down into the dark and flaring out at its foot), and the cables run between them at that depth, held up on posts every ten blocks. You can still see them, lit, under the water. A kingdom made before 1.67.0 is made again, with his castle and his Faithful set down in it again. The old one is kept as a folder, the_kingdom-before-1.67 , in your world's dimensions/statichollow ."},{"p":"His kingdom","h":"The Faithful at their rites","u":"places/his-kingdom.html#the-faithful","t":"Since 1.64.2 his congregation is in his castle: the Faithful , tall, in hooded robes of a red so dark it's nearly black, a little red light hung at the breast, and under the hood a black hole where a face goes. They keep his rites : in circles of red and black candles round a lamp set in the floor, kneeling, rocking, chanting; praising on their knees, arms up, swaying; bowed flat, arms out along the floor, bowing again and again: two circles in the courtyard , four in the war hall's aisles behind the pillars; kneeling by his war table, facing it: eight , four a side, back from it behind his servants; in slow procession, hands clasped, hoods bowed: three walking the causeway from his platform to the gate and back, three round the courtyard. They don't stop for you, but their hoods turn after you wherever you go. Come right up to one and the whole circle stops, every hood on you, till you go. Hurt one and every one of them for twenty-four blocks turns on you, the chant breaking into a scream. Get far enough away and they go back to their places and kneel again. Killed, the robe falls empty, and those killed stay dead. Now and then (one in five, since 1.69.0) one drops the dagger he made them: Faithful's Dagger . More on them in his creations and servants ."},{"p":"His kingdom","h":"Nothing's quiet there","u":"places/his-kingdom.html#what-you-hear","t":"Its sound is his static, with the chant far off in it, and the voices through the windows. And now and then, from somewhere: whispering, just behind you (nobody there); footsteps behind you, coming up, and stopping; chanting, far off across the water; a bell tolling up his mast; iron groaning: his gate on its hinges; a music box somewhere, winding down in the middle of its tune; someone crying, inside, through the walls."},{"p":"His kingdom","h":"His arena","u":"places/his-kingdom.html#his-arena","t":"In the Coronation ( the Last Broadcast , part two) his arena comes up out of the sea off his island's east side. A round floor about forty blocks across, a wall round it, seven tiers of seats for his Faithful round that, his own box high on its north side with a throne in it, an outer wall going down into the sea, and lamps round its top. Its gate is on its west side, with a bridge from it to his island. The Watcher stands inside by the gate. Step down onto its floor and he comes down off his box at you; stay off it long enough and he's back in his box, whole. It stays there whenever you come back, until part four. In the Tearing (part four) the whole of it is torn up out of his sea into the sky, and you with it."},{"p":"His kingdom","h":"His arena in the End","u":"places/his-kingdom.html#the-arena-in-the-end","t":"It comes down in the End: hanging out over the void north of the End's island, a ragged cone of the rock it was torn out of under it, its bridge snapped off short, pieces of it hanging loose in the air round it. While all this is going on the End lets you in to it; the rest of the time the End still sends you home. Fall off its edge into the void and his static catches you and puts you back on the floor (it hurts). The fights in it are on the Last Broadcast ."},{"p":"His kingdom","h":"SENTINEL's wreck","u":"places/his-kingdom.html#sentinels-wreck","t":"In the Fall (part three) the sky over his castle rips open right across the north and SENTINEL comes through it, the whole station. He tears its right side off. That half comes down burning into his sea far out and lies there with its broken end up out of the water; one module of it comes down near, east of his arena. That module stays, real blocks: lying tilted in the sea, its hatch end up out of the water and its far end torn open, scorched, the parasites' resin in it; its windows, its deck, its lamps (some out); bits of its solar wing and a girder round it; fires on its back. Its crew's chest is still in it, with SENTINEL - Crew Log among what's in there. What's left of SENTINEL hangs dark in the rip over it all. Since 1.70.0 his kingdom's wall of static stands further out, past where the wreck came down."},{"p":"His kingdom","h":"What's there after each part","u":"places/his-kingdom.html#part-by-part","t":"The kingdom keeps what each part of the story leaves in it: After What you find The Broadcast His castle, the windows, the Faithful at their rites (from 1.64.2); him at his war table The Refusal (part one) That day, his static across the causeway. From the next day his static's gone, he isn't at his table, and his map is of your world; the Faithful at their rites as they were The third day The Harbinger in the water round the castle. Walk up the causeway (or wait) and the Coronation plays The Call (part two) His arena off the island's east side. Him on his roof at his mast, the Watcher knelt in the arena with the Omni up at him, the tear in the sky over it all The Forge (part three) Him in his box, mended, enchanted, alight with SENTINEL's power; what's left of SENTINEL dark in the rip; the Watcher knelt by the gate with the Omni; the wreck in the sea The Rebirth (part four) His arena gone from his sea; only SENTINEL's wreck and what's left of SENTINEL, dark in the rip. And he's gone"},{"p":"His kingdom","h":"Its blocks","u":"places/his-kingdom.html#its-blocks","t":"Signal Stone : his static, cut into stone (the sea's floor, the island, the windows' pillars) Signal Bricks , with their wall, slab and stairs Dead Screen : the dead sets in his walls Signal Lamp : his red lamps"},{"p":"Every location","h":"","u":"places/index.html","t":"Static Hollow's places don't generate with the world the normal way. Most rise out of nothing the first time someone comes near: on flat open ground, trees and hills cleared out of the way, in old worlds too. Later places only exist once the story wakes them, and the Watcher hands everyone a needle that points there."},{"p":"Every location","h":"Finding places","u":"places/index.html#finding-places","t":"Needles. When a place wakes, the Watcher gives each player a Watcher's Needle, a compass that only ever points there. Since 1.72.3 you start with three: the first time you join a world the Altar Needle, the Cathedral Needle and the Gardens Needle go into your inventory (a world you've already played gives them to you the next time you join, once only). Since 1.63.4 the Altar, Mansion and Gardens compasses find their places from anywhere. See Compasses and needles . /statichollow locate [place] tells you where each place is (how far, which way, and coordinates you can click to fill in a teleport), or when it will come if it isn't there yet. It knows gardens, mansion, breach_altar, cathedral, altar, rosemont, laboratory, shelter, nests, great_bloom, arena and stomach, and later uplink, capacitor_works, soul_well, ashford_plant, meridian_lab, blackwater_station, relay, drive_in and hive, and since 1.66.7 tune_in_town and flyer_tv. Since 1.66.7 you can click any place it lists to go there, and /statichollow goto [place] does the same: it puts you on the ground there, with room to stand. /locate structure statichollow:<id> works for the structures listed below with their id, once they exist. Both need cheats on. Since 1.63.2, clicking the coordinates it gives you puts you standing beside the structure, not under the ground or high in the air. Since 1.63.4 it finds the Botanic Gardens, the Murder Mansion, the Breach Altar, the cathedral and the Forsaken Altar from anywhere (where the place stands, or will rise the first time you come near), not only within a hundred chunks. In the Dead Water it finds each of the sea's places from anywhere and sets you down in the water beside it."},{"p":"Every location","h":"The realms","u":"places/index.html#dimensions","t":"Besides the Overworld, the Nether and the End, the story takes you to ten places of its own, each a separate dimension, and Tune-In Town's secret has one more. You can't sleep in any of them. Realm Id Chapter Way in The Void statichollow:the_void 2 The Breach, where the Hollow Saint fell The Bloom statichollow:the_bloom 3 The green rift over the Gardener's dead flower The Null Static Zone statichollow:the_null 5 The Last Reel held over the tear at the drive-in The Deep statichollow:the_deep 5 The Throat at the bottom of the Sinkhole The Stalls statichollow:the_stalls 6 The Door at the End of the World The Watcher's Vault statichollow:the_vault 6 The seam in the Great Screen The Other Side statichollow:the_other_side 6 The Door, once its static has gone black The Hub statichollow:the_hub 7 After the credits; then the Remote The Dead Water statichollow:dead_water 8 Off the Hub's edge, through his portal His kingdom statichollow:the_kingdom 10 The tear left where you broke one of his sites' Broadcast Cores Tune-In Town (Studio B) statichollow:tune_in_town 10 The STAFF ONLY door at the back of the old place (a secret)"},{"p":"Every location","h":"Chapter one","u":"places/index.html#chapter-one","t":""},{"p":"Every location","h":"The Forsaken Altar","u":"places/index.html#forsaken-altar","t":"Every world has one, 500 to 1000 blocks from spawn, on open, flat, dry ground on the far side of spawn from the cathedral. A ruined shrine with broken pillars, skulls, candles and a soul campfire (follow the blue smoke) rises round it within about 90 blocks. Its grounds have nine pilgrim stones, the pilgrims' abandoned camp, and a catacomb under a sealing stone that opens when the altar wakes. Since 1.62.0 the pilgrims have left offerings at the foot of the stones and stacked cairns behind them. The Watcher later works at Forsaken Altars: it infuses the Orbital Core and builds the Device and the Ray Gun there. statichollow:forsaken_altar"},{"p":"Every location","h":"The Cathedral of the Hollow","u":"places/index.html#cathedral","t":"The church that isn't on any map. One per world, 500 to 1000 blocks from spawn, roughly opposite the altar, inside a walled graveyard. The Hollow Saint is summoned at its reliquary. statichollow:cathedral"},{"p":"Every location","h":"Chapter two","u":"places/index.html#chapter-two","t":""},{"p":"Every location","h":"The Void","u":"places/index.html#the-void","t":"A dimension through the Breach: black all round, a fog the colour of a bruise, and the Breach Altar's island hanging in it. Round it, the Drift: the Torn Room, the Fallen Graves, the Mast and the Nest. Fall off and the Hand catches you. Since the altar wakes, the rift closes for good. See chapter two ."},{"p":"Every location","h":"The Breach Altar","u":"places/index.html#breach-altar","t":"The Forsaken Altar's other half: pale rose stone, spires of pink crystal and a pink altar with a torn eye carved in it, on top of the Void's island. In worlds from before 1.25 it stands in the Overworld. statichollow:breach_altar"},{"p":"Every location","h":"The Murder Mansion","u":"places/index.html#murder-mansion","t":"Hale House: a three-storey Second Empire house under a black mansard roof, with a turret and a spire, a widow's walk, a columned porch and a chimney still smoking, in its own railed yard with a fountain of blood (since 1.26.2, a weathered statue of the Mended with blood pouring from its mouth), dead hedges, lamp posts, things hanging from dead trees, and the family plot. Inside: a two-storey foyer, parlour, dining hall laid for guests who are only skulls, butcher's kitchen, library, master bedroom, nursery, a bathtub full of blood, servants' rooms, the red room, the attic, and through the Harvest Doors the Trophy Hall with the Mending Altar. Every chest is filled and the house's papers are where they were left. statichollow:murder_mansion"},{"p":"Every location","h":"Chapter three","u":"places/index.html#chapter-three","t":""},{"p":"Every location","h":"The Botanic Gardens","u":"places/index.html#botanic-gardens","t":"A Victorian glasshouse with a great glass dome, locked until the Mended's key. Inside: the great flower, the Head Gardener's office, a propagation house, a pond, a potting shed, an orchid house of iron lattice at the back, and the Seed Vault under a hatch. Once the Great Bloom rises, the glasshouse comes down round it and the Bloom takes its place for good. statichollow:botanic_gardens"},{"p":"Every location","h":"The Bloom","u":"places/index.html#the-bloom","t":"The teeth pit with floating islands. A dimension down the root: islands of what the flower ate over green fog, and the Great Bloom's mouth at the bottom."},{"p":"Every location","h":"The Great Bloom's stomach","u":"places/index.html#the-stomach","t":"Wet red folds lit faintly from inside, a knee-deep pool of green acid, and on the ledges round it what's left of the ones it ate before you. Cut the wall ten times to be thrown back up. See the Bloom ."},{"p":"Every location","h":"Chapter four","u":"places/index.html#chapter-four","t":""},{"p":"Every location","h":"The Flesh's land","u":"places/index.html#the-flesh","t":"The red fog. Everywhere the Flesh has taken: meat for grass, veined stone, sinew trees, and fog the colour of meat."},{"p":"Every location","h":"Rosemont","u":"places/index.html#rosemont","t":"The broken city, a few hundred blocks from the gardens on the flattest open ground there is: six streets of cracked asphalt and abandoned cars, the police precinct, the corner pharmacy, the bus station, an eight-floor apartment block with its floors rotted through, offices, shops and houses, a sinkhole forty blocks deep, and in the middle the army's evacuation checkpoint with the truck and the Military Cradle. The Congregation sleeps in the road. Its own music: a broken loop of car doors and struck pipes, a PA chime that has lost a note. statichollow:rosemont , once the Flesh has woken"},{"p":"Every location","h":"The Rosemont Botanical Research Laboratory","u":"places/index.html#laboratory","t":"A white building above ground (reception, two labs, offices, the director's office, a greenhouse wing where the Bloom and the Flesh fight over the beds) and two sublevels: decontamination, the control room with its glass floor over the reactor, the containment lab, the cold store, the server room, and the reactor hall behind blast doors, where Specimen Zero sleeps in the pool against the Core. statichollow:laboratory"},{"p":"Every location","h":"Shelter No. 4","u":"places/index.html#shelter-no-4","t":"Rosemont's Civil Defence shelter in Victoria Park: a blockhouse with its blast door jammed half open, a mess hall, bunk halls, the radio room with the generators, and Bunker B, a two-storey hall where the squad holds the dais and the Warden sleeps in the north wall. Roots hang out of the ceilings. Its own music below ground: Shelter Dark. statichollow:shelter"},{"p":"Every location","h":"Nests","u":"places/index.html#nests","t":"Where the Flesh has had the land long enough, the ground sinks into a bowl, ribs of bone arching over it, with the Broodmother at the bottom and rows of brood sacs round her. At most four at once, never within 160 blocks of another, cleared out to 23 blocks and ringed with standing bones. You hear one form: a long, deep, wet groan out of the ground."},{"p":"Every location","h":"The Uplink Station","u":"places/index.html#uplink-station","t":"Where the garrison talked to SENTINEL: a fenced compound, a great dish tipped at the sky still transmitting, the control bunker (the Targeting Array is in the locker by the consoles), a generator shed, a watchtower, sandbags, the truck that never got out, and the soldiers who stayed. statichollow:uplink , once the Bloom has changed"},{"p":"Every location","h":"The Capacitor Works","u":"places/index.html#capacitor-works","t":"The live banks. A brick hall of capacitor banks still holding its charge, arcs jumping between the lightning rods. The Capacitor Cell is in the test cage at the back. statichollow:capacitor_works , once the Bloom has changed"},{"p":"Every location","h":"The Soul Well","u":"places/index.html#soul-well","t":"Black obelisks burning with soul fire round a plaza of black brick, graves and pilgrims' stones round it; the well, a stair cut round and round its shaft thirty blocks down, souls going up past you and a wail coming up; at the bottom, its keepers kneeling round the altar, and the Bound Soul. Come to the altar and they get up. statichollow:soul_well , once the Bloom has changed"},{"p":"Every location","h":"Ashford Nuclear Plant","u":"places/index.html#ashford-nuclear-plant","t":"Cooling towers and a reactor that never went cold. The Nuclear Reactor Core is in the fuel pool. Decon lockers hold a hazmat suit and a Bloom Serum. Its hazmat teams and workers are still there. statichollow:ashford_plant , once the Orbital Railgun is built"},{"p":"Every location","h":"Meridian Laboratory","u":"places/index.html#meridian-laboratory","t":"Arcs jumping, capacitor banks humming, a test hall that lost its roof on run 47. The Discharge Destabilizer is in its core. Its researchers and spitters are still there. statichollow:meridian_lab , once the Orbital Railgun is built"},{"p":"Every location","h":"Blackwater Station","u":"places/index.html#blackwater-station","t":"An island research lab out at sea: its dock, its lighthouse, its foghorn, and the tank they built the station round. Something got loose in it. The Vial of Dark Matter Blood is in the sample freezer. Parasites, Parasite Hosts, xeno resin and pods. The Watcher gives you a boat. statichollow:blackwater_station , once the Orbital Railgun is built"},{"p":"Every location","h":"Chapter five","u":"places/index.html#chapter-five","t":""},{"p":"Every location","h":"Relay 6","u":"places/index.html#relay-6","t":"The relay. The county's emergency-broadcast relay on Hollow Ridge, with a guyed mast forty blocks high and the Amalgam at its foot. /statichollow locate relay , once the Bloom is dead"},{"p":"Every location","h":"The Starlite Drive-In","u":"places/index.html#starlite-drive-in","t":"Where the last of their static runs down. A screen twenty-five blocks across showing nothing, and a tear in the ground at its foot. /statichollow locate drive_in , once the relay is off the air"},{"p":"Every location","h":"The Null Static Zone","u":"places/index.html#null-static-zone","t":"Where everything that went into the static ran down to. A dimension: a grey plain under no sky, the Carrier's crater in the middle, and the Ancient Null Ruins out on the plain. statichollow:null_hush , statichollow:null_listening_stones , statichollow:null_sunken_choir , inside the Zone"},{"p":"Every location","h":"The Hive","u":"places/index.html#the-hive","t":"Where the parasite is growing itself a mind. A hamlet it took whole, gone under violet creep and black chitin, its hands standing round a pit with the Chorus in it and four nerve nodes on their stalks. statichollow:hive , or /statichollow locate hive , once the static has signed off"},{"p":"Every location","h":"The Sinkhole","u":"places/index.html#the-sinkhole","t":"Halloway's Low Field , pulled down from underneath: a crater thirty-odd yards across, a surveyor's camp on its rim, and a burrow winding down six turns to the Throat. statichollow:sinkhole , once the Chorus has run"},{"p":"Every location","h":"The Deep","u":"places/index.html#the-deep","t":"Where the Chorus went. A dimension of huge warm caverns with seas of blood in them: the Gullet, Low Marrow, the way-stones, the Old Halls and the Deaf King, the Listeners' nests, and the Warm Heart."},{"p":"Every location","h":"Chapter six","u":"places/index.html#chapter-six","t":""},{"p":"Every location","h":"The Door at the End of the World","u":"places/index.html#the-door","t":"Out past the obsidian in the End. A causeway of the Watcher's black seal-stone to an island, and on it a Door full of static. It's there once the Last Voice has broken his seal on the End."},{"p":"Every location","h":"The Stalls","u":"places/index.html#the-stalls","t":"An endless picture house in the dark , row on row of seats facing the Great Screen, the Audience in some of them and the Ushers walking the aisles."},{"p":"Every location","h":"The Watcher's Vault","u":"places/index.html#the-watchers-vault","t":"Behind the picture. His archive of film and tape, the Tuned standing in the stacks, three keeps off the nave, and the Watch."},{"p":"Every location","h":"The Other Side","u":"places/index.html#the-other-side","t":"A stage behind the screen your world is on. Painted flats, footlights, his last projector, and past the edge, the dark and what sits in it."},{"p":"Every location","h":"Chapter seven","u":"places/index.html#chapter-seven","t":""},{"p":"Every location","h":"The Hub","u":"places/index.html#the-hub","t":"A realm he made , floating in static: a plaza of hub stone, a gallery of six portals back to each chapter's last fight, and the edge."},{"p":"Every location","h":"Chapter eight","u":"places/index.html#chapter-eight","t":""},{"p":"Every location","h":"The Dead Water and the rig","u":"places/index.html#the-dead-water","t":"A dead green sea that goes on forever , laid out as one sea since 1.63.5: the oil rig he built in it long ago in the middle of the Grey Shelf, the sub bay and the submarine Orpheus, a ring of five shallow waters round it, a ring of five deeper ones round that, and past about 3,000 blocks the void. Since 1.63.6 each water has one place of its own, rebuilt bigger, and since 1.63.7 most of them have their own crews: Water Its place Id The Grey Shelf The Lifeboat Graveyard statichollow:sea_lifeboats The Haemal Reach The Drowned Heart statichollow:sea_drowned_heart Haemal Research Station statichollow:sea_enzyme_lab The Wireweed The Wireweed Mast statichollow:sea_radio_tower The Lantern Fields Lantern Station statichollow:sea_habitat_dome The Ossuary Flats The Leviathan Fall statichollow:sea_whalefall The Brine Sink Sink Station statichollow:sea_sink_station The Molar Reef The Jaw statichollow:sea_the_jaw The Drowned Mycelia The Drowned Grove (and the Grove Heart under it) statichollow:sea_drowned_mushrooms The Rime Shelf The Rime Outpost statichollow:sea_frozen_outpost The Rime Spires statichollow:sea_rime_spire The Ember Vents Ember Pumping Station statichollow:sea_pump_ruin The Carrier Wave The Wreck Field statichollow:sea_wreck_field The Black Below The Canticle's Anchor statichollow:sea_the_anchor Where each one lies from the rig is on the Dead Water's page . The ids are the old ones, kept."},{"p":"Every location","h":"Chapter nine","u":"places/index.html#chapter-nine","t":""},{"p":"Every location","h":"The Dead Water, after the Turning","u":"places/index.html#the-dead-water-after-the-turning","t":"No new place: the Undertow goes through the Dead Water's two hearts and comes back to lie in the sea north-east of the rig for three days, until the Harbinger rises out of it and tears its way out. See the Dead Water and Chapter Nine ."},{"p":"Every location","h":"Chapter ten","u":"places/index.html#chapter-ten","t":""},{"p":"Every location","h":"His sites","u":"places/index.html#his-sites","t":"After the Broadcast his sites come through into your world, each kept by one of his three servants and each with a Broadcast Core : break it and the site goes off the air, and its chests hold the best of what he brought. A keeper you've killed doesn't come back. See Chapter Ten . The Transmitter rises up out of the ground every ten-odd minutes, a long way off, its mast's red lamps on the skyline at night; the first one comes up right in front of you the first time you step out of doors by day. His creations come out of it at night. The Announcer keeps it. The Burrow is eaten out of the rock near you in the caves (the first the first time you're down in one): Hangers on its roof, blackout ore in its walls, lockers in it, and a tunnel from it to where you were. The Cameraman keeps it. The Set goes up at night out in the open: the front of a house and nothing behind it, studio lights, a camera (its core is the camera's eye), Lookalikes standing about being people. Since 1.72.2 the first one goes up in front of you on the third night. The Stagehand keeps it."},{"p":"Every location","h":"His kingdom","u":"places/index.html#his-kingdom","t":"A still black sea made of his static , his castle on it, the windows into every realm under it, and the tear you come in by from one of his broken sites. His arena comes up out of its sea in the Last Broadcast and is torn up into the End."},{"p":"Every location","h":"Tune-In Town Pizza & Playhouse","u":"places/index.html#tune-in-town","t":"A secret night shift (flashing lights and jumpscares: read the warning first). The HELP WANTED flyer on an Old Set leads you to the old place in your world, and its STAFF ONLY door to Studio B. The flyer can come any time after your first day. statichollow:tune_in_town (the old place), statichollow:flyer_tv (the set showing the flyer), or /statichollow locate tune_in_town and flyer_tv"},{"p":"Every location","h":"The Hollow's own country","u":"places/index.html#the-hollows-own-country","t":"Biomes of its own : five in the Overworld since 1.62.0 (the Hollow Moor, the Blightwood, the Weeping Fen, the Antler Woods and the Signal Flats), and since 1.66.0 to 1.66.3 thirteen more on the Overworld's surface, three under the ground, four in the Nether and three in the End. Since 1.66.7 they come in whole stretches of the world, not strips. New ground only: land you've already explored keeps what it has. And in worlds made since 1.62.0, oceans that go down about 2,000 blocks, in three depths: the Sunless Drop, the Hadal Dark and the Trench."},{"p":"The Null Static Zone","h":"","u":"places/null-static-zone.html","t":"The Null Static Zone Nulled Way in Hold the Last Reel over the tear at the Starlite Drive-In Way out The rift at the landing, any time While you're here Nulled the whole time; you can't sleep (\"Nothing here sleeps.\") In the middle The crater and the Carrier"},{"p":"The Null Static Zone","h":"The plain","u":"places/null-static-zone.html#the-plain","t":"A grey plain under no sky at all, grey fog, ash and static on the wind, voices a long way off. \"Everything that ever went into the static came here. It's very quiet.\" You come out on a landing among the things it took (cars, television sets, a radio mast bent double), and the rift there takes you home whenever you like."},{"p":"The Null Static Zone","h":"The dread","u":"places/null-static-zone.html#the-dread","t":"Wherever the static is (all over the Zone, while you're Nulled, near its creatures, and more of it at night) it closes in: a drone and a slow pulse under you, two notes grinding a half step apart, the static breathing, a crowd mumbling a long way off and echoing back and forth, metal groaning, a heartbeat, something enormous breathing. Far off: a scream through a radio, a scream run backwards, a steel door slammed, the dial turned through the stations, a music box running down, a laugh, knocking, feedback howling, a siren, some of them answered from the other side of you. Whispering close by your ear. And now and then the static shrieks at you. It eases while the Carrier's music plays."},{"p":"The Null Static Zone","h":"The crater","u":"places/null-static-zone.html#the-crater","t":"In the middle of the Zone is a crater, and in it the Carrier, coiled in its own pale body. Four black spires stand round the crater's rim, each with a ladder up its outer side and a knot on top where one of the Carrier's threads is tied off. See the Carrier ."},{"p":"The Null Static Zone","h":"The Ancient Null Ruins","u":"places/null-static-zone.html#the-ancient-null-ruins","t":"The static came once before, long ago, and the people who were here then built against it. It took what they built, whole, down with them. The ruins are out on the grey plain, 160 blocks or more from the crater, and nowhere else. Each has lamps, supplies and notes on lecterns: the field notes of the surveyors who came looking (the relay men had written about voices in the dead air), rubbings of what the old ones carved, and what the last of them scratched into a Hush's bench."},{"p":"The Null Static Zone","h":"The Listening Stones","u":"places/null-static-zone.html#the-listening-stones","t":"statichollow:null_listening_stones A round floor laid in a spiral like the inside of an ear, six dark stones leaning in round an obelisk, an ear cut into each. Put your ear to one (use it) and hear what the stone heard, and for a little while it hears you (you're Nulled). A stair goes down to a room with a wall of ears, and a camp left down there. Listening earns Put Your Ear to It . ...a crowd, very far down, all of them talking at once... ...someone says your name. Then someone else does... ...a dog whining, and the whine going to static... ...\"it's warm down here,\" says a man. \"nobody's alone\"... ...breathing, enormous and slow, under everything... ...a woman reading the same line over and over: \"stay inside until it forgets your name\"... ...nothing. Then, right at your ear, something listening back... A second set, kept apart in the mod's files, also uses the \"it's warm down here\" and \"breathing, enormous and slow\" lines from the first: ...the threads humming, all the way up into the dark... ...your own voice, a moment before you speak... ...\"whatever sounds like me at the door,\" a man says, very close, \"it isn't me\"..."},{"p":"The Null Static Zone","h":"The Sunken Choir","u":"places/null-static-zone.html#the-sunken-choir","t":"statichollow:null_sunken_choir A pit stepped down in rings, every ring lined with stone figures with open mouths, all facing in. In the middle, the throat: a ladder down a shaft to a room under it all, with ears in all four walls, facing in. \"The figures up top aren't singing. They're the audience.\""},{"p":"The Null Static Zone","h":"The Hush","u":"places/null-static-zone.html#the-hush","t":"statichollow:null_hush One room of a pale, dead stone, one door, and a seal in the middle of its floor. Nothing of the static's own can live in it. Come in over the line and the static stops: no Nulling, and the static's sounds cut off. \"It goes quiet - not quiet: stopped.\" A parasite on your neck comes apart at the line. One growing in you dies there; grown, it tears out of your back as it does, which hurts. A hound after you runs at the door and leaps, and comes apart in the air in the doorway (advancement Unmade ). The Hollowed, the Afterimages, the parasites and their hosts come up to the door, stop out past its two pillars and stare in at you. Then they go. Then, after a while, they come back. Stepping into one earns The Hush ."},{"p":"The Null Static Zone","h":"Rubbing: the Lintel","u":"places/null-static-zone.html#rubbing-the-lintel","t":"Dr. R. Calloway Found: a Hush (the carving over the door, as near as I can make it) THIS IS A HUSH. THE STONE IS DEAD. NOTHING OF THE MANY CAN LIVE IN IT. WHAT THEY PUT IN YOU WILL DIE AT THE LINE. THEY WILL COME TO THE DOOR. THEY WILL LOOK AT YOU. DO NOT GO OUT TO THEM. THEY KNOW YOUR VOICE. THEY CANNOT USE IT IN HERE. WE BUILT THESE TOO LATE. THE MANY TOOK THE REST OF US DOWN WITH THE STATIC. IF YOU ARE READING THIS, THEY ARE COMING BACK UP. The rest of the ruins' notes are on the lore page ."},{"p":"The relay and the live banks","h":"","u":"places/relay-6.html","t":"Two places in Static Hollow are all live current and dead air. Relay 6 carries the parasites' static in Chapter Five. The Capacitor Works, with its notice reading DANGER - LIVE BANKS, holds the charge SENTINEL needs in chapter four."},{"p":"The relay and the live banks","h":"Relay 6, Hollow Ridge","u":"places/relay-6.html#relay-6","t":"County Emergency Broadcast, Relay 6 On the air Wakes Once the Bloom is dead, 300 to 1000 blocks out Find it The Watcher's Needle (Relay 6), or /statichollow locate relay While on the air Hound packs come twice as often within 700 blocks Boss The Amalgam , at the mast's foot A fenced yard on open ground. In the middle, the mast : a steel lattice forty blocks up, held by guy wires, with a ladder up its south face and rest platforms at 12, 22 and 32. Round it are the transmitter hut (the operator's log on his desk, his locker by the racks), the generator shed, and his truck run into the fence. The parasite's resin creeps out from the mast's foot and its pods sit in the yard. Lashed to the mast on each platform is a tether , a knot of sinew, its veins lit, with a cable of sinew running down to what lies at the mast's foot. While it's on the air, static pours off the top of the mast, and it hums. Arriving: \"The air up here crackles. Something on the mast is still transmitting.\""},{"p":"The relay and the live banks","h":"What to do","u":"places/relay-6.html#what-to-do","t":"Read the operator's log. His locker has a Surgical Kit, food, iron, flashbangs, a lantern and shears. Climb the mast and cut the three tethers. Kill the Amalgam. The relay goes off the air. Take the Relay Core it leaves. You'll need it at the drive-in."},{"p":"The relay and the live banks","h":"Notice","u":"places/relay-6.html#notice","t":"County Emergency Broadcast Found: Relay 6 RELAY 6 - HOLLOW RIDGE. Authorized personnel only. This station relays the county emergency broadcast. Do not interfere with its operation. Climbing the mast: harness at all times. Rest platforms at 12, 22 and 32 metres. (scratched into the cover, underneath:) THEY'RE ON EVERY PLATFORM Advancements here: Dead Air (find the relay), Cut the Cord (cut the last tether while the Amalgam lives), Off the Air (kill it) and Tuned In (use the Relay Core)."},{"p":"The relay and the live banks","h":"The live banks: the Capacitor Works","u":"places/relay-6.html#the-live-banks","t":"Capacitor Works Live Wakes When the Bloom changes, 300 to 1000 blocks from the gardens Find it The Watcher's Needle (Capacitor Works), or /locate structure statichollow:capacitor_works What you need there The Capacitor Cell, one of the three power source parts Who's still there Its workers, infected Still holding its charge. A brick hall of capacitor banks with the roof half fallen in, catwalks, a gantry crane, the transformer yard, a pylon and the chimney, and arcs jumping between the lightning rods : anything standing in the way of one is burnt. The Capacitor Cell is in the test cage at the back, with Works Order 117, some redstone, copper and food. The safety notice is on a lectern beside it."},{"p":"The relay and the live banks","h":"Notice","u":"places/relay-6.html#notice-2","t":"Works Safety Officer Found: the test cage DANGER - LIVE BANKS. Do not stand between rods. Do not touch the bus bars. If it starts to crackle, get down and get out. Arc burns are not covered. (underneath, in pencil:) neither is whatever is in the cage."},{"p":"The relay and the live banks","h":"Works Order 117","u":"places/relay-6.html#works-order-117","t":"Capacitor Works Found: the test cage chest Cell 9 to be charged to full and held in the test cage for collection by Uplink. No collection came. Cell 9 is holding. We can't bleed it off, and we can't leave it. The arcs have started jumping the rods by themselves. Two men burnt. The rest of us sleep in the yard."},{"p":"The relay and the live banks","h":"Getting the cell out","u":"places/relay-6.html#getting-the-cell","t":"Watch the rods. Don't stand between them, and don't cross while one is crackling. Five infected workers wait inside. The cell's item text: \"Works cell 9, fully charged. Nobody came to collect it. It holds what the gun needs to fire.\" Take the cell with the Targeting Array and the Bound Soul to make the Orbital Core. See the power source parts ."},{"p":"The Starlite Drive-In","h":"","u":"places/starlite-drive-in.html","t":"The Starlite Drive-In Late show Wakes Once Relay 6 is off the air, 300 to 1000 blocks out Find it The Watcher's Needle (the Starlite), or /statichollow locate drive_in The screen Twenty-five blocks across Within 40 blocks of the tear You're Nulled Afterwards The screen shows one line: SIGNING OFF"},{"p":"The Starlite Drive-In","h":"The lot","u":"places/starlite-drive-in.html#the-lot","t":"A lot of cracked asphalt behind a chain-link fence, rows of speaker posts with the cars still parked at them, the snack bar, and the screen . Up the stairs is the projection booth with the projector at its window, the manager's note on a lectern, and his locker of reels (food, torches, arrows, flashbangs, iron, golden carrots). Since 1.47.1 the screen is dark until somebody comes into the lot. No static, nothing out of the tear, nobody Nulled."},{"p":"The Starlite Drive-In","h":"The late show","u":"places/starlite-drive-in.html#the-late-show","t":"The first step anyone takes inside the fence, the camera is taken for everyone nearby. The lot in the dark, the screen dead at the end of it. Somewhere a relay slams home, the lamp strikes, the screen flickers, and the static comes on all at once and pours off its face into the ground. From close at its foot, looking up: five of them peel off the picture, one after another, sink down out of it, and come up the lot for you. The Watcher is beside you. they came out of the picture. they always do, when somebody's watching. you can't hurt them yet. they're not all the way here. the core. hold it to your ear - tuned in, they're as real as you are. or let one reach for you. when it does, it's all the way here. hit it then. kill one and it leaves a frame of the picture behind. four frames. the projector's up in the booth. run the reel. see what's under all of it. ??? during the late show Then it's gone, and they're loose. A world whose last reel has already been shown doesn't play it again."},{"p":"The Starlite Drive-In","h":"The Null","u":"places/starlite-drive-in.html#the-null","t":"At the screen's foot is a tear in the ground, the Null , the static running down into it like water. Anywhere within forty blocks of it you're Nulled : the colour goes out of everything, static creeps in at the edges of your sight, the fog closes in grey, and you go hungry faster. Arriving: \"The colour goes out of everything. The screen ahead shows static - and the static is coming off it.\" The ground of the lot has gone to null static ."},{"p":"The Starlite Drive-In","h":"The Afterimages","u":"places/starlite-drive-in.html#the-afterimages","t":"What's left of the people who stayed in their cars after the late show's last reel: grey figures made of scan lines and static, see-through, flickering between frames, smeared off sideways, their faces only dark gaps. They don't walk. They drift, through cars and walls, and leave themselves behind for a moment as they go. They blink out and back nearer. They're mostly not all the way here: hit one and you go straight through it (\"Straight through it. It isn't all the way here.\"). You can hurt them when: you're Tuned In with the Relay Core, one is reaching for you (it's all the way here then, and its touch is Nulled II), or the last reel is running. They can't leave the Null: get far enough away and they let you go. Each one killed leaves a Frame of the Last Reel . Killing one earns Signal Lost . Death by them: \"went to static\"."},{"p":"The Starlite Drive-In","h":"The last reel","u":"places/starlite-drive-in.html#the-last-reel","t":"Load the projector in the booth with four frames , with the Relay Core on you to tune it (\"The lamp won't catch. It wants tuning - something on their frequency.\"). It runs the last reel: seventy seconds, five parts, on the screen. They come out of the picture for the booth: three, then four, then five, more with more of you there. While it runs they're all the way here, so anyone can hurt them. One that reaches the projector jumps the film back ten seconds. Leave the booth and the reel runs out, and your frames fall back out of the gate. Hold them off to the end and the last frame burns on the screen: what's under all of it, where they come from. The reel is yours. Keep it. This earns The Last Reel ."},{"p":"The Starlite Drive-In","h":"The way down","u":"places/starlite-drive-in.html#the-way-down","t":"Hold the Last Reel up over the tear. The static runs backwards off it into the tear, and the tear's bottom goes to a pool of static: a rift into the Null Static Zone ."},{"p":"The Starlite Drive-In","h":"The manager's note","u":"places/starlite-drive-in.html#the-managers-note","t":""},{"p":"The Starlite Drive-In","h":"To Whoever Runs Booth 1","u":"places/starlite-drive-in.html#to-whoever-runs-booth-1","t":"Starlite Drive-In Found: the projection booth p. 1 Ray - the late show's reel came in with no label and no distributor. Ran it anyway. Half the lot left before the end. The other half stayed in their cars after it finished. They're still out there. p. 2 I took the reel off. The screen kept showing it. Then the screen kept showing static, and the static kept coming off it like smoke off a fire. The things in it don't walk. They drift. p. 3 You can't hit them most of the time. They're not all the way here. Something on the right frequency might put them all the way here. When they come apart, they leave bits of the picture behind. p. 4 If you have to see the rest of the reel, load the projector with what's left of them and stay with it till the end. Don't let them at the booth. Whatever it shows you - it's where they come from. I'm not going."},{"p":"The Starlite Drive-In","h":"Signing off","u":"places/starlite-drive-in.html#signing-off","t":"When the Carrier dies, the screen goes black for the first time, and then shows one line: SIGNING OFF . The Null goes out of the lot and the Afterimages with it. The drive-in turns up again in Chapter Six: its picture is one of the frames of the story so far on the Great Screen in the Stalls , and one of the painted flats on the Other Side . NO SIGNAL"},{"p":"The Bloom (the teeth pit)","h":"","u":"places/the-bloom-realm.html","t":"The Bloom, down the root No ground, no sky Way in The green rift over the Gardener's dead flower, three days after he dies Way out The same rift, until the Binding breaks The air Eats you without the full Gardener's Weeds Sleep \"You can't sleep here. It would have you before you woke.\""},{"p":"The Bloom (the teeth pit)","h":"What it is","u":"places/the-bloom-realm.html#what-it-is","t":"A realm with no ground and no sky: green fog all the way down, spores and flies in the air, a wet drone and things far off (a groan, something chewing, a scream cut short). Hanging in it is everything the great flower has eaten, overgrown with its flesh, dripping vines and glowing pustules. Since 1.27.2 the fog thins out to 240 blocks, so you can see a long way, and from any edge you look straight down into the Great Bloom's throat. Far off in the green you might hear a child laughing (and then again, slowed, wrong), someone sobbing, a music box running down, a radio, knocking from inside something, a scream played backwards. Out on the islands you sometimes hear the Bloom calling from far, far down under you."},{"p":"The Bloom (the teeth pit)","h":"The islands","u":"places/the-bloom-realm.html#the-islands","t":"Each has a chest and a lectern with its story."},{"p":"The Bloom (the teeth pit)","h":"The Binding's island","u":"places/the-bloom-realm.html#the-bindings-island","t":"Where you come out. The stone in the middle is the Binding , chained, its sigil and the cracks in it glowing. The plaque on the lectern beside it is from the Laboratory. See below ."},{"p":"The Bloom (the teeth pit)","h":"A street of Rosemont","u":"places/the-bloom-realm.html#a-street-of-rosemont","t":"A torn-open pharmacy, wrecked cars, a bus stop, a traffic light, and a road bridge snapped off over nothing. Its lectern holds the Rosemont Courier, four issues folded together."},{"p":"The Bloom (the teeth pit)","h":"The research station","u":"places/the-bloom-realm.html#the-research-station","t":"The research station (Dr. Marsh's log says the flower ate the Laboratory's east wing): its lab, the burst specimen tank, benches of specimen jars, and a copper duct for a bridge. Its lectern holds Dr. Marsh's research log on Specimen 0."},{"p":"The Bloom (the teeth pit)","h":"Shelter No. 4","u":"places/the-bloom-realm.html#shelter-no-4","t":"A concrete bunker full of bunks, sunk in its island with roots through the roof. Its lectern holds the shelter warden's log. All four papers are on the lore page ."},{"p":"The Bloom (the teeth pit)","h":"The pit","u":"places/the-bloom-realm.html#the-pit","t":"Below everything is the Great Bloom . Its mouth is wider than all the islands together, and every island hangs over it. A lip of flesh, then a throat ringed with ring after ring of hooked teeth that turn against each other as it chews, a sick light far down in it, and at the very bottom a pool of its acid. Its throat has faces in it, pressed out through the flesh, mouths open. Round it rise eight tentacles like towers. Don't fall. A tentacle twenty blocks thick comes straight up out of its throat under you, coils round you and drags you down into its mouth. Since 1.38 you go down alive, into its stomach ."},{"p":"The Bloom (the teeth pit)","h":"The air","u":"places/the-bloom-realm.html#the-air","t":"Without the Gardener's Weeds (the full set) you're infected the moment you arrive, and after twenty seconds it starts eating you, slowly and then faster (\"The air in here is eating you. Without the Gardener's clothes you are rotting.\"). The edges of your sight go green-black and veined, the veins pulsing with its heart and creeping further in the longer you stay. Something whispers just behind you, wherever you turn. Now and then, for a blink, you see its mouth. In his clothes, the flies settle and lift off again. you're not wearing his clothes. it can smell you. it's eating you already - be quick. breathe through your sleeve. it's in the air. ??? in the Bloom without the Weeds"},{"p":"The Bloom (the teeth pit)","h":"The Binding","u":"places/the-bloom-realm.html#the-binding","t":""},{"p":"The Bloom (the teeth pit)","h":"The Binding","u":"places/the-bloom-realm.html#the-binding-2","t":"Rosemont Botanical Research Laboratory Plaque, the Binding's island THE BINDING Site 0: the root's end This stone holds the root down. While it holds, the flower cannot climb the root into Rosemont. DO NOT TOUCH THE STONE. DO NOT LOOSEN THE CHAINS. DO NOT LOOK DOWN. (scratched under it, in another hand) it doesn't hold it. it only keeps it asleep. wake it and you'll have ten seconds before it pulls this whole island down its throat. run for the tear in the air. don't look back. Touch the stone with an empty hand: \"The chains strain. Far below, something stops moving. Touch it again to break the Binding.\" Touch it again and it breaks. The Great Bloom goes mad, the ground quakes, a choir of screams swells up backwards, your heart pounds faster with the countdown, and its tentacles come up round the island and take hold. Ten seconds (\"THE RIFT! 10\") to get back through. Then the island's edges break away and it pulls the whole island into its mouth, rift and all (\"The rift is gone. There is no way back now.\"). When you come out, the Great Bloom comes up the root and through the glasshouse. See chapter three ."},{"p":"The Bloom (the teeth pit)","h":"The ledge","u":"places/the-bloom-realm.html#the-ledge","t":"In chapter four the Watcher tears the risen Bloom open and the rift comes out on what's left of the Binding's island: a torn slab of its ring hanging over the colossal Bloom's mouth, its tentacles hanging over it. At the far end is the Launch Mark, where the Rosemont Device goes. See the launch ."},{"p":"The Dead Water","h":"","u":"places/the-dead-water.html","t":"The Dead Water The sea won't let you Way in Off the Hub's edge, through the Watcher's portal, onto the rig's helipad Way out The Remote, once it's mended (or the Remote (Mutated) after Chapter Nine): to the Hub, and from there home Coming back Crouch and press the mended Remote Sleep No: \"You can't sleep here. The sea won't let you.\" The rig's beds still set your spawn. The sea The Grey Shelf round the rig, a ring of five shallow waters, a ring of five deeper ones, and past about 3,000 blocks the void: the Black Below Map The Watcher's Chart: the whole sea, out past the edge, every place marked"},{"p":"The Dead Water","h":"What it is","u":"places/the-dead-water.html#what-it-is","t":"A dead green sea that goes on forever, a grey sky and a grey fog over it, and a black sea under that. Standing alone in it is the rig the Watcher built long ago \"for when i needed somewhere to hide\". You come down onto its helipad out of the portal he tore open as you fell from the Hub . That earns Dead Water , and the title reads CHAPTER EIGHT / DEAD WATER / the deep is listening . ...we're out. it's awake now. the first signal. it'll come for me - then for you. but it can't hear us here. not through all this water. take this. it'll get you back - to the hub, and home. ...no. nothing of mine works right here. then you stay. there's food. beds. i built this place a long time ago - for when i needed somewhere to hide. fix it. the big ones down there sing on its frequency - cut out what they sing with. ??? on the rig's helipad Then he goes over the rail. The whole arrival is on Chapter Eight ; what the sea does after that is Chapter Nine ."},{"p":"The Dead Water","h":"Stranded: the Broken Remote","u":"places/the-dead-water.html#the-broken-remote","t":"The Remote he gives you cracks in your hand: the Broken Remote . \"Chapter Eight: Dead Water. The Remote's broken - mend it with a Static Leviathan's Signal Organ and a copper ingot. They live deep.\" Until it's mended you're held here. Die and \"The sea brings you back. Nothing leaves the Dead Water while the Remote's broken.\" Without one of the rig's beds you wake in its quarters. You can't lose the Broken Remote either: \"The Broken Remote's still in your pocket.\" Mending it: the Broken Remote, a Signal Organ from a Static Leviathan, and a copper ingot. Go more than forty blocks down in the water (anywhere but the Black Below) and now and then one of them comes up out of the dark after you, singing. Mending it earns Back On Air . Mended: \"The Remote works again. Press it: the Hub (and in the Hub, home). Crouch and press it: back to the rig.\" Mutated: at the end of Chapter Nine the Static Heart (Mutated) goes into the Remote, broken or mended, and makes the Remote (Mutated) . It goes to the same places, and it has the Undertow's roar in it. See Chapter Nine . The Watcher also presses his chart into your hands when you come down. Held, it shows the stretch of sea you're in, a thousand blocks to a square, with you, the others down there with you, and the rig. Use it to unroll the whole chart: since 1.63.5 the whole sea, out past the edge, every water in its own colour and named, the floor's depths shaded, and the Black Below hatched out in red as THE DEAD ZONE. Since 1.63.6 every place in it has a red cross and its name. Point at a water and you read his note on it. Scroll to zoom, drag to look round, R to come back to you."},{"p":"The Dead Water","h":"One sea: how it's laid out","u":"places/the-dead-water.html#the-map","t":"Since 1.63.5 the Dead Water is one sea, laid out the same way in every world. The rig stands in the middle of the Grey Shelf , about 420 blocks of it all round. Round that lies a ring of the five shallow waters , out to about 1,500 blocks, one of each; round that a ring of the five deeper waters , set between them, out to about 2,950. Their edges wander, and the floor slopes from one water to the next. About 3,000 blocks out the floor slopes down to the edge of everything and falls away: the Black Below , the void, all the way round, for ever. Since 1.63.6 each water has one place of its own, rebuilt bigger, to go into (they used to come up all over their waters, again and again). Each stands in the middle of its own water's stretch of the map: Water Which way from the rig Its place About how far Id The Grey Shelf All round it The Lifeboat Graveyard (west-north-west) 270 statichollow:sea_lifeboats The Lantern Fields East Lantern Station 950 statichollow:sea_habitat_dome The Molar Reef South-south-east The Jaw 950 statichollow:sea_the_jaw The Haemal Reach South-west Haemal Research Station, at the Reach's near edge 640 statichollow:sea_enzyme_lab The Drowned Heart 950 statichollow:sea_drowned_heart The Drowned Mycelia North-west The Drowned Grove 950 statichollow:sea_drowned_mushrooms The Rime Shelf North-north-east The Rime Outpost (north) 820 statichollow:sea_frozen_outpost The Rime Spires (north-north-east) 1,180 statichollow:sea_rime_spire The Wireweed South-east The Wireweed Mast 2,200 statichollow:sea_radio_tower The Brine Sink South-south-west Sink Station 2,200 statichollow:sea_sink_station The Ember Vents West Ember Pumping Station 2,200 statichollow:sea_pump_ruin The Carrier Wave North-north-west The Wreck Field 2,200 statichollow:sea_wreck_field The Ossuary Flats North-east The Leviathan Fall 2,200 statichollow:sea_whalefall The Black Below Everywhere past the edge The Canticle's Anchor (west-south-west) 3,330 statichollow:sea_the_anchor \"Which way\" is the middle of each water; the distances are to where each place is meant to stand. A place takes the flattest floor near its spot that's all its own water, so in your world it may stand a little off. The first ids are the old ones, kept: the habitat dome is Lantern Station now, the radio tower the Wireweed Mast, and so on. The Drowned Heart is about four hundred blocks west of the Haemal Research Sta"},{"p":"The Dead Water","h":"The rig","u":"places/the-dead-water.html#the-rig","t":"An oil platform on four great legs of rusted steel lattice that go down into the black to the sea floor, braced every fourteen blocks. It was waiting with its lights on and its larders full. The derrick stands in the middle, a lattice tower with red lights at its crown and its drill string going down into the moon pool's dark (since 1.63.22 its ladder has every rung, so you can climb it). There are two cranes, the flare stack out over the sea on the north that never goes out, and lifeboats on the west. Railings run round everything and stairs go between the decks. On the rig the music is The Rig ."},{"p":"The Dead Water","h":"The cellar deck","u":"places/the-dead-water.html#the-cellar-deck","t":"Eight blocks over the sea. The moon pool : a square of open water in the middle, a ladder down into it and a winch over it, a heavy weight on its chain. The dive locker (north-west): racks of gear, a shower and chests with Air Tanks, Marine Flares, Harpoon Bolts, a Harpoon Gun, a turtle shell and potions. The pumps (north-east). The pens (south-west): chickens, sheep, cows and a pig, let out when you arrive, with feed. Since 1.63.25 the hay and the trough are in the middle of each pen, so nothing steps over the fence. The boat dock below it on the south, with two boats."},{"p":"The Dead Water","h":"The main deck","u":"places/the-dead-water.html#the-main-deck","t":"The quarters : eight beds, and chests with rations, a clock, a compass, candles and some leather clothes. If you die without a bed of your own while the Remote's broken, this is where the sea brings you back. The mess and its kitchen: cooked fish, bread, stew, pie and Rig Rations. The infirmary (west): golden apples, potions, milk and honey, syringes and pill bottles. The workshop (east): copper, iron, glass, gunpowder, pistons and redstone; and a tool chest with iron tools, a fishing rod, shears, a shield and a spyglass. The stores (east): food, coal, torches, string, leads, ladders, planks and wool, and a boat. The greenhouse (east): crops growing under glass, water channels between the rows, a composter, and a chest of seeds and bone meal."},{"p":"The Dead Water","h":"The upper deck","u":"places/the-dead-water.html#the-upper-deck","t":"The control room (north): consoles, windows all round, and a chest with a map, a compass, a recovery compass and flares. The radio room (middle): the set, its mast up through the roof. The armoury (south): Harpoon Guns and their bolts, iron armour, a sword, a bow and crossbow, a shield, flares and flashbangs. The helipad , over the east side: where you come down. Every door's buttons are on the wall beside it (since 1.63.2), the cranes' hooks are iron blocks that stay on their chains, and the greenhouse's channels have a bottom (1.63.22-24). A rig set down before each fix mends itself the next time you're on it, without touching anything you built."},{"p":"The Dead Water","h":"Under the rig: the Watcher, asleep","u":"places/the-dead-water.html#the-watcher-asleep","t":"Since 1.63.21, straight down from where he went into the sea off the rig, the Watcher is there at the bottom: curled up, asleep, floating in a bubble of his own static with a faint light round him in the dark. Nothing gets into the bubble (it gives a little, then pushes you back out), and nothing you swing, throw or fire at it gets through. He doesn't wake, until the Turning breaks his bubble and he comes up onto the helipad. See the Watcher ."},{"p":"The Dead Water","h":"The sub bay and Orpheus","u":"places/the-dead-water.html#the-sub-bay","t":"Off the south end of the dock is the sub bay : a berth of open water between two steel catwalks, open to the sea on the south. The docking clamps are on a cradle under its water, with a gantry and lamps over it and a barrel of spares (copper, iron, glass, redstone, an Air Tank) by the way in. Since 1.63.8 a parts crate stands on the catwalk too, with a Depth Module in it, iron and a block of redstone. In its clamps lies the submarine Orpheus , and its clamp charges her power and mends her hull. Rigs already standing before 1.63.0 get the bay added. Orpheus at 43 metres, lamps on, sonar up. Orpheus is thirteen blocks long with a cabin you walk about in: the helm, floodlights and sonar at the bow, and the chart table, bunks, lockers, workbench, galley, battery bank, repair board and motor down her length. Since 1.63.22 her cabin is dry, clear air, with the sea starting at her glass. Come down through her hatch, or crouch and use her, to climb in; hold crouch to climb out, onto the catwalk in the bay or into the water at sea. How to drive her is on the items page ."},{"p":"The Dead Water","h":"Her upgrade bay","u":"places/the-dead-water.html#orpheus-upgrade-bay","t":"Use her motor (aft, in the engine room) and her upgrade bay opens: five mounts for modules, to fit, swap and take out as you like. What's in it is what she has, and the motor tells you her rating. Nothing fitted : she's rated for 183 metres (down to y -120). Past that the hull creaks and gives, the dome cracks, and at nothing she implodes. The Depth Module (280 m) : rated to 280 metres. One is in the parts crate, and it can be made from iron blocks, copper blocks, tinted glass and a block of redstone. Pressure Plating : no crush depth at all. The UV Field : her floodlights burn violet and keep Enzyme 1-2418 off her, and burn it out of her crew. Once she has all three of those modules in her bay, the Turning plays ( Chapter Nine )."},{"p":"The Dead Water","h":"The bay's console","u":"places/the-dead-water.html#sub-bay-console","t":"Since 1.63.21 the console on the catwalk by her berth tells you where she is: in her clamps (her hull and her power), out at sea (where she was last heard from, and how far), or nothing heard from her at all. Crushed, eaten or sunk, the bay's welders build her again in her clamps: a minute's work, nothing asked of you. Lost out of reach (stuck somewhere, sunk too deep)? Use the console crouching: she's scrapped where she lies and built again. Its screen shows her sonar, the welders at work, or red, NO SIGNAL."},{"p":"The Dead Water","h":"Her emergency locker","u":"places/the-dead-water.html#emergency-locker","t":"Since 1.66.6, when she's lost (crushed, swallowed, gone to flesh, or scrapped from the console) her emergency locker blows free with everything that was in her lockers and the modules out of her bay. It shoots up to the top of the sea (to the nearest open water if she went down under ice or rock) and floats there, its lamp blinking and a flare going up now and then. Her crew, and anyone else in the sea, are told where it came up and how far off it is, and it's on your locator bar as a little yellow locker however far away you are. Use it to open it (36 slots); empty it and it sinks away."},{"p":"The Dead Water","h":"Who lives down there","u":"places/the-dead-water.html#the-crews","t":"Since 1.63.7 the places have people of their own: the Deep Hands , who still live and work down there in the old diving dress (a round copper helmet with a face behind its lit glass, a brass corselet, lead boots, an air hose, a big spanner). Each working place has its own crew in its own colours. They walk from job to job, look round at you, wave when you first come near, and never go for you (the Salvagers aside). Right-click one and it talks to you (each crew has eight things to say). Hurt one and it backs off, and so does the rest of its crew. They don't drown, and the vents and the brine don't hurt them. Crew Where One of the things they say The Ember Crew Ember Pumping Station: the pump house, the pipeline, the wellhead, the gantry \"The portal's plugged. Bolted. Welded. If you hear knocking from the other side of the bulkhead, it's the lava. It's the lava.\" Lantern Station's Keepers The mess hall, the lab, the moon pool, the tower; two out at the lamp posts and the airlock \"We keep the lamps lit out on the fields. Something out there steers by them.\" Sink Station's Researchers The lab, the catwalk, the winch; one down on the brine by the cage \"We lower the cage, we bring it up, we write down what's in it. Lately it comes up empty. Lately it comes up heavier.\" The Signal Keepers The Wireweed Mast: its foot, the operator's hut, the dish's platform \"Keep your voice down near the wireweed. It picks things up.\" The Salvagers The Wreck Field, cutting up the containers, the hulls and the plane. Hit one and all of them come for you with their spanners. \"Cut the hull in the wrong place and she comes down on you. Seen it happen.\" The Castaways The Lifeboat Graveyard, round their boats, the raft and the buoy \"We waited for rescue up top. Then we waited down here. It's quieter down here.\" The Rime Crew (1.63.11) The Rime Outpost's divers, in frosted helmets, at their camp (a tent, a lantern post, a harpoon rack, a drying frame). They hunt frostjaws and the like with harpoon guns, and turn them on you if you turn on them. \"Frostjaws. They come up out of the white with their lights off. Watch the ice, not the water.\" Two places have lost their crews to what they found. The Drowned went down to see what the Heart was, and stayed: their dress split, the Flesh coming out through it, their glass cracked and full of red, two lights in it. Five walk the Heart's floor and o"},{"p":"The Dead Water","h":"The deep crushes you","u":"places/the-dead-water.html#the-deep-crushes","t":"Since 1.63.10, below about y -100 in the Dead Water the sea crushes you, more the deeper you go: you hear yourself creak, you slow down, and deeper still the world swims. Each piece of the Ember Deep Suit keeps a quarter of it off, and Orpheus keeps it off her crew. See survival ."},{"p":"The Dead Water","h":"The twelve waters","u":"places/the-dead-water.html#the-twelve-waters","t":"Each water has its own colour and murk, its own floor, plants, life, light, sound and music, and its own fish (since 1.63.11). Glowing plankton drifts in every one in its colour, flaring up in your wake. The sea's sound changes as you swim from one to the next, and the reverb follows the water: longer and darker the deeper you go. Drowned and glow squid turn up in most of them. From 1.63.12 to 1.63.17 nine of the waters (all but the Haemal Reach, the Ember Vents and the Black Below) were filled in with new growth, new creatures, an event of its own that comes now and then, and things to make; in an older world they grow in a little at a time, out past where you can see. \"His note\" is what the Watcher wrote of each water on his chart. The creatures are in the bestiary and the things made from them on the items page ."},{"p":"The Dead Water","h":"The Grey Shelf","u":"places/the-dead-water.html#the-grey-shelf","t":"His note: \"Grey water over grey silt. The rig stands in it. Nothing here is in a hurry - mostly.\" The rig's own grey-green water, over ash silt . Grey kelp and a few glow anemones grow here. Gentle Pipeyes, Lanternlets, Hum Skates, Stiltfins and Hymnbacks live here, with Hookjaws, Siphons and Needlemaws among them, and the Mouth of the Floor lies buried in the silt. Its fish is the Staticfin . You hear something groan, far off. Since 1.63.17 ghost nets stand up off the floor in great curtains, held up by floats and pinned down by sunk girders, with bones and skulls still hanging in them (swim into the mesh and it holds you). Between them grow drowned hair that tangles you, oil seeps that blind you, net floats on their tethers, and girders hung with rusticles. Since 1.63.18 all of it comes in to the feet of the rig's legs, the ghost nets to sixty blocks off. The Catch rolls over the floor (a ball of net with the drowned rolled up in it, groping), and crowds of little Buoylings live under the net floats. The Diving Bell : now and then a ship's horn sounds somewhere up above and a chain runs out. An old diving bell comes down out of the murk near you, its hatch swings open, and its supplies are set out beside it in a chest (sometimes the diver's still down there with it). After a while it's hauled back up. Its place: the Lifeboat Graveyard . The rig's launching davit has fallen over, one boat still hanging off it in its falls, with lifeboats strewn round it: one upright you can climb into (its benches, its flare locker), one split open, one on its back, one nose-down in the silt; a raft; a buoy on its chain, its lamp still lit. The Castaways live round it."},{"p":"The Dead Water","h":"The Haemal Reach","u":"places/the-dead-water.html#the-haemal-reach","t":"His note: \"The water's thick with blood. Clotfish come in swarms; the Siphons wait for them to pass.\" Blood-red water, thick as soup and lit red, over clot silt . Vein kelp (it glows), artery anemones and clot coral grow here. Pipeyes, Grinners, Puffbloats, Clotfish and Siphons live here, and its fish is the Bloodlet , which smells blood a long way off. Enzyme 1-2418 is in all of its water (since 1.63.9). Go in without the UV dress and it gets into you, out of a hundred. At 35 what you're wearing grows into you and won't come off; at 50 it wants to go home, pulling you toward the Drowned Heart; at 100 (or 80 near the Heart) it takes you there, into itself. A UV Lamp flash burns a fifth of it out, an Enzyme Inhibitor half, and the whole UV Dive Suit keeps it out. Orpheus without her UV Field goes to flesh in it. The detail is on survival . The Drowned Heart: a heart the size of a church. Its four chambers are hollow and joined by their open valves: swim in by the wound in its side or down its torn aorta, the veins glowing in its walls, its arteries branching away over the floor. Something is kept in its right atrium. Since 1.63.18 it beats once every forty seconds, a slow double thump you can hear a long way off and follow; dark blood shakes off it with each beat, and up close the water shoves at you. The Drowned keep it. Haemal Research Station At the Reach's near edge, a quick swim from the Grey Shelf: the lab where Enzyme 1-2418 was made, and where it got out. White modules round a domed hub, the dome caved in. The specimen lab's containment vat has burst and the flesh has poured out of it, up every wall, through the hub and out of a breach in its side. The office has the station's last log book, Research Log, HRS-3 (\"Haemal Research Station's last log book, in its sealed sleeve\"), and the inhibitors. The decontamination room, its UV strips still lit, is where the flesh never got in (it's burnt black in the doorway), and in its lockers is the UV Dive Suit . The station's divers lie where it left them, stretched out long. Some of them are only lying: the Stretched , who unfold when you come near and come fast when you look away."},{"p":"The Dead Water","h":"The Wireweed","u":"places/the-dead-water.html#the-wireweed","t":"His note: \"Weed like wire, and it sings. The Choir Eels nest in it. Don't touch the bright ones.\" Dark green water over rust silt , a forest of wireweed and signal bulbs. Choir Eels, Hookjaws, Pipeyes, Lanternlets, Hum Skates and Grinners live here, and the wires sing. Its fish is the Wirewhip , an eel of old cable with a plug for a head. Since 1.63.15 it's a forest of cable trees (black cable braided thick, hanging wire coming down off their limbs) and toppled pylons of rusted girder, with copper moss, insulator clusters and fuse pods (touch one and it blows) on the floor. Wirecutters wait in the roots; Coilbacks graze the copper moss. The Power Surge : now and then a hum, sparks running along the cable, and then the current comes, shocking anything touching the cable, the wire, the moss or the insulators until it's over. Its place: the Wireweed Mast , a lattice mast fifty blocks high with a ladder up one leg, two rest platforms, its dish and its red light blinking at the top; the operator's hut at its foot (his radios, his bunk, his logs); a second mast fallen across the floor, its guy wires, and the weed grown up through all of it. The Signal Keepers work it."},{"p":"The Dead Water","h":"The Lantern Fields","u":"places/the-dead-water.html#the-lantern-fields","t":"His note: \"Lights in the dark as far as you can see. Most of them are bulbs. Some of them aren't.\" Black-blue, clear water lit blue by its plants, over glow sand . Glow anemones and lantern bulbs grow here. Lanternlets, Thimble Jellies and Hymnbacks live here, and so do Gulpers with their lures. Glass chimes. Its fish is the Wickling , a stub of wax with a flame on its wick. Since 1.63.15 lantern trees of white wax coral stand here, hung with old iron lanterns on ropes, candle coral burning round their feet; rows of lantern buoys float up off the floor; lure stalks, glow moss and drowned lanterns, still lit, stand about. Lantern Moths go about in clouds and come to any light, and rarely one grows into a Lampmother , a moth the size of a boat. The Blackout : now and then the lanterns all round you flicker and go out at once, and in the dark something comes looking for you. After a while they come back on, one by one. Its place: Lantern Station , a seabase. Its glass-domed mess hall; a corridor west to its lab (benches, the specimen tanks still glowing); a corridor east to its moon pool (lockers, the pool down through its floor); a corridor north to its tower, a ladder up to the lookout bubble; lamp posts out over the fields. Its Keepers live there."},{"p":"The Dead Water","h":"The Ossuary Flats","u":"places/the-dead-water.html#the-ossuary-flats","t":"His note: \"A plain of bone. Whatever died here, died big. The Stiltfins pick it clean.\" Milky water over a floor of bone sand , with bone coral, bone fans and marrow sponge. Stiltfins, Pipeyes, Hum Skates, Hookjaws and Gulpers live here, the Mouth of the Floor lies buried here too, and bones knock. Its fish is the Marrowpike , which lies among the bones as if it's one of them. Since 1.63.16 whale falls lie half sunk in the sand, red bone worms all over them and carcass mat spread round them, with vertebrae and ribs standing up between. The Sleeper , a blind shark as long as a boat, smells you when you're hurt and comes slowly, and doesn't stop; colonies of Skullkeeps (crabs in human skulls) pick over the falls. The Fall : now and then a groan far up, a darkness coming down, and a dead whale lands not far off in a cloud of bone sand, its flesh rotting off a piece at a time. The Sleeper and the skullkeeps come to it. Its place: the Leviathan Fall , the skeleton of something ninety blocks long: its ribs arching up into a hall to swim the length of, its skull a cave with its eye sockets open (something left inside), its jaw fallen open in front. Hookjaws pick over it and mantlecrabs sit on its bones."},{"p":"The Dead Water","h":"The Brine Sink","u":"places/the-dead-water.html#the-brine-sink","t":"His note: \"The brine pools eat what falls in. The water's sour, and the Puffbloats like it.\" Sick yellow-green water over brine crust , with sulfur tubes. Puffbloats, Thimble Jellies, Clotfish and Siphons live here, and the brine fizzes. Its fish is the Brinecrust , buried in the floor until you step on it. Since 1.63.14 its brine pools are lakes on the sea floor with a surface of their own: what swims into them is eaten. Round their shores are lips of salt crust, mussel beds packed black, pink halite spires, cold seeps breathing methane, and fish pickled where they fell. Slimehags tangle where things are dead, and colonies of Wavers (white yeti crabs) all stop, face you and wave, in step. The Brine Surge : the floor rumbles and a pool, or the floor, erupts in a boiling torrent of bubbles and brine. Its place: Sink Station , two huts on stilts over the brine lake joined by a catwalk (the lab and the winch house), its crane out over the lake, its sampling cage still down in the brine, and the frame of a third hut, gone. Its Researchers work there."},{"p":"The Dead Water","h":"The Molar Reef","u":"places/the-dead-water.html#the-molar-reef","t":"His note: \"Teeth, grown into a reef. The Grinners live in it. They smile at you.\" Teal and pink water over gum silt : a reef of enamel coral, tooth fans, gum sponge and nerve anemones. Grinners, Puffbloats, Lanternlets, Clotfish and Hookjaws live here, the Mouth of the Floor lies buried here too, and teeth chatter. Its fish is the Gumnibbler , which nibbles at you if you keep still. Since 1.63.17 giant teeth as tall as towers stand up out of mounds of gum flesh. Some have gone bad, black decay eating down one side and a cavity big enough to swim into, with something left at the back. Milk teeth, tongue weed, plaque and gum blisters (they burst in a sour cloud and leave Reef Gum) are on the floor. The Tooth Fairy takes something off your hotbar and leaves a gold nugget; the Gnasher grinds your armour down. The Eruption : a toothache (your head throbs, your hands go slow), then the reef teethes, new teeth pushing up through the gum a layer at a time. Chew Reef Gum and the ache goes. Its place: the Jaw , a vault of gum and teeth to swim through: incisors and canines hanging over the way in, molars at the back, teeth standing along the floor, a tongue; a canine fallen outside; and a rotten molar with something hidden in its hollow."},{"p":"The Dead Water","h":"The Drowned Mycelia","u":"places/the-dead-water.html#the-drowned-mycelia","t":"His note: \"Mushrooms the size of towers, drowned. Their spores burst if you brush them.\" Violet water with spores in it, over spore silt . Gill glow and spore puffs grow here (they burst in your face). Pipeyes, Thimble Jellies, Gulpers and Siphons live here, and the drowned whisper. Its fish is the Sporegill . Since 1.63.12 giant drowned mushrooms stand all over its floor (parasols, bulbs, clusters, old ones fallen), their gills glowing, hyphae hanging down out of them in long strands that cling to you, shelf fungus up their stems to stand on. On the floor: hyphae mats, lantern caps, dead man's fingers, and ear fungus that whispers. Spore Drifters drift in shoals, and a Gillmaw is a mushroom on the floor until its cap splits open with teeth in it. Now and then one of the rooted dead lies grown over on the floor, until strings come down out of the dark and haul it up. Sporefall : every so often the whole Mycelia lets its spores go at once, and for a minute they come down like snow. Spore sickness (1.63.13): breathe its water and its spores build up in you. At 50 they've taken root and won't fade by themselves down here; at 100 the Grove has you. A sealed helmet keeps most of it out, Orpheus all of it, and a Spore Tonic burns sixty of it out of you. Milk does nothing. See survival . Its caves and the Gillmaws' nests Sinkholes in its floor, their rims matted and hyphae hanging down into them, open into winding fungal tunnels: glowing gills and shelf fungus on the walls, hyphae curtains, the rooted dead lying in them. Some come back up to the floor somewhere else. Some open into a Gillmaw nest , a wider hollow floored with bones and skulls, Gillmaws waiting in it, and a drowned diver's barrel. Its place: the Drowned Grove , a mushroom forty blocks high. Go in at its foot and climb the ladder up inside its stem to the camp someone made under its glowing cap; a grove of smaller ones stands round it, one fallen. The Sporeborn walk it, more hang under its caps on their strings (swim under one and it drops on you), and a gulper waits in the canopy. The Grove Heart Since 1.63.13 the great mushroom is hollow, and its hollow goes on down, through the floor, twenty blocks, into a hollow in the dark: roots as thick as a man in out of its walls, curtains of hyphae, the rooted dead on its floor, and in the middle, on its root mass, the Grove Heart . A mass of fungal flesh t"},{"p":"The Dead Water","h":"The Rime Shelf","u":"places/the-dead-water.html#the-rime-shelf","t":"His note: \"Ice under the sea. Things are frozen in it. Some of them wake up.\" Cold, clear water under a roof of rime ice , over rime silt , with frost anemones and frozen corpses. Packs of Frostjaws hunt here, and Stiltfins and Hymnbacks live here too. The ice groans. Its fish is the Rime Smelt , clear ice with a little red heart showing through. Since 1.63.14 sunken floes the size of a house lie tilted on the floor, fish (and now and then someone) frozen in them, anchor ice grown under their edges, and brinicles stand round them. Rime Striders wade the floor and Rimebacks call in long electric trills. Brinicles growing : a crackling above you, and a thread of ice comes down to the floor; when it touches, the cold spreads out and freezes whatever's caught in it nearly still. Its places: the Rime Outpost , its cabin and store shed locked in ice (bunks, stove, stores), its radio mast, a sledge still loaded, its fire out, its people; the Rime Crew have their camp by it. And the Rime Spires , a cluster of spires round a great one fifty blocks high, veined with blue ice, an arch of ice between two, and sealed in clear ice at the great one's heart, lit, someone, and what they had with them."},{"p":"The Dead Water","h":"The Ember Vents","u":"places/the-dead-water.html#the-ember-vents","t":"His note: \"Vents roaring up from below. Warm. The Mantlecrabs crowd round them - mind your power.\" Rust-orange water lit orange, over ember crust , with smoking vent chimneys and tube worms. Mantlecrabs (their pulse kills every light near them, the submarine's too), Choir Eels, Hum Skates, Stiltfins and Needlemaws live here, and the vents roar. Its fish is the Cinderling , a live coal that burns you. Ember Pumping Station Its place , rebuilt in 1.63.10. The portal hall: a Nether portal in the sea floor, sealed under an iron bulkhead, the lava main coming up out of it into the pumps, and a conveyor carrying the netherite debris it brings up to a hopper and a chest. The pump house: its engine, its great flywheel, its control board, two lava tanks glowing. The intakes drawing the sea in; the outflow pipe dumping the spent lava in a heap of obsidian and basalt; the workshop; the pipeline out on its supports to the wellhead capping the great vent, its stack; a gantry crane over the vent field. The Ember Crew work all of it. Its trade: right-click one of the Ember Crew (crouch to just talk) and they trade iron, copper and gold for Ember Plating , Heat Coils , Pressure Seals and Vent Glass (and ancient debris, now and then). They buy Needle Teeth, Shroud Hide, Photophores and Signal Organs, and restock every half day. What they trade makes the Ember Deep Suit , the strongest suit there is: see the items page ."},{"p":"The Dead Water","h":"The Carrier Wave","u":"places/the-dead-water.html#the-carrier-wave","t":"His note: \"The static's loudest here. The water hums. Your instruments won't like it.\" Blue-grey water with static shimmering through it, over static sand . Static coral, antenna weed and signal bulbs grow here, and drowned television sets hiss on the floor. Choir Eels, Mantlecrabs, Pipeyes, Lanternlets and Hum Skates live here, and there's a voice in the static. Its fish is the Dialfin , old bakelite with a lit radio dial on each flank. Since 1.63.16 great listening dishes stand on their pedestals tilted up at a surface nobody can see, and old loudspeaker horns hiss on posts. Tape weed, tuning fork coral, speaker anemones and valve bulbs grow between. The Handset lies on the floor ringing, an old telephone handset for its lure; Echo Jellies play back what they've heard. The Broadcast : a music-box tune out of every horn in the water at once, then a voice reading out three numbers, twice. They're a place, and someone's left a dead drop there on the floor, a chest of supplies with a horn on a post beside it. (The numbers show over your hotbar; a Receiver keeps them.) Its place: the Wreck Field , a cargo ship broken in two. Its stern half sits upright with its bridge house standing (three decks: its bridge, its cabins, its funnel and mast light); its bow half lies off on its own, its hold open; its containers are spilled, one full of televisions still showing static; and a plane is nose-down in the floor. The Salvagers are cutting it all up."},{"p":"The Dead Water","h":"The Black Below","u":"places/the-dead-water.html#the-black-below","t":"His note: \"THE DEAD ZONE. Past the edge of all this the floor drops away and doesn't stop. Something lives out there that's bigger than the sea. Don't.\" Past the edge, all the way round: the void. Near-black water, barely any light, over abyss silt with void moss and eye pods on it (shut until you come near; then the eye opens and follows you). The chart's tooltip says it plainly: \"The black hatched in red is the dead zone. Don't take the sub over it.\" There's no music here, only the sound of the ocean. Its fish is the Omenfry : black specks with human eyes, lit, in clouds, that trail you at the edge of your light and stare. The void is the Undertow 's. Go out over it at all (swimming, in Orpheus, in a boat on top of it) and stay, and it comes, sooner the deeper you are. Get back over the edge and it lets you go. Nothing else comes up out of the Black Below. Within ten seconds or so of you going out over it a lost whale comes out of the dark ahead of you, singing, its back glowing warm, and when the Undertow comes it goes for the whale first. The Canticle's Anchor Its place , out past the edge (rebuilt in 1.63.8): the anchor of the SS Canticle , a hundred blocks of it on the floor of the abyss. Its shank; its stock lying across its head; its crown, hollow (go in on its west side); one arm reaching up into the dark with its fluke and the other driven down into the silt; its ring standing up off the floor; and its chain rising two hundred blocks out of the dark, broken off, a length of it coiled on the floor. Beside it lies the Canticle herself: her bow half sunk, her name on her side, her decks open where she broke (cabins, a lamp still lit), her hawse pipe torn, her funnel fallen beside her. All round are the bones of what the Undertow has eaten: whales, a leviathan's skull with its jaws open, fish, divers. In the hollow of the anchor's crown is the Static Heart : \"Warm, and beating - to no rhythm of its own. There's a picture in it, of nothing, always moving\". \"Keep it. Something is going to be made with it\"."},{"p":"The Dead Water","h":"After the Turning","u":"places/the-dead-water.html#after-the-turning","t":"When the Turning plays ( Chapter Nine ), the Undertow comes up out of the sea by the rig, goes to the Drowned Mycelia and eats the Grove Heart, goes through the Drowned Heart in the Haemal Reach, and comes back with both in it. Its last time down it lies in the sea north-east of the rig (\"on your left, looking out to sea from the helipad\"), its jaws a hundred blocks off the rig: the husk, its eyes shut, spores steaming off one side and blood off the other, its heart heard from the rig, beating faster as the days go. For the three days it lies there nothing comes up out of the Black Below, the Grove's Heart doesn't grow back, and the Drowned Heart doesn't beat. The Watcher keeps watch at the helipad's rail. When the Harbinger has risen out of it and gone, the husk goes down into the sea."},{"p":"The Dead Water","h":"What's down there to take","u":"places/the-dead-water.html#loot-down-there","t":"Each place keeps its own chests, and the sea's events leave some of their own: Where What you can find The Lifeboat Graveyard Bread, dried kelp, honey, Air Tanks, flint and steel, a compass, iron, copper, string Lantern Station A heart of the sea, sea lanterns, prismarine, glass, iron, redstone, Air Tanks, Needle Teeth, Shroud Hide The Jaw Bone, bone meal, emeralds, gold nuggets, Needle Teeth, diamonds, a nautilus shell, a heart of the sea The Molar Reef's rotten teeth Milk Teeth, Enamel Shards, Reef Gum, gold, emeralds, diamonds The Drowned Heart Redstone, nether wart, rotten flesh, Needle Teeth, gold, Air Tanks, crying obsidian, a heart of the sea, diamonds Haemal Research Station The office: Research Log, HRS-3, Enzyme Inhibitors, UV Emitters, Photophores, Glow Gel, books, amethyst, Rig Rations, flares. The decon lockers: the UV Dive Suit, a UV Lamp, an inhibitor, Air Tanks The Drowned Grove Mushrooms, shroomlight, glowstone, bread, an Air Tank, a golden apple, diamonds A Gillmaw nest's barrel Gillmaw Teeth, a Spore Tonic, Spore Pouches, Drifter Jelly, Harpoon Bolts, flares, Lantern Caps, an Air Tank, now and then a Gillmaw-Tooth Spear or a Lantern-Cap Lamp The Rime Outpost Diamonds, blue ice, iron, coal, leather, a spyglass, cooked cod, torches, Shroud Hide The Wireweed Mast Redstone, copper, iron, glowstone, a compass, a spyglass, a map, Pressure Plating, diamonds Sink Station Diamonds, iron, redstone, glowstone, sugar, fermented spider eyes, Needle Teeth, Pressure Plating Ember Pumping Station Coal, iron, copper, magma cream, blaze powder, Ember Plating, Heat Coils, Pressure Seals, Pressure Plating, diamonds, netherite scrap; its conveyor's chest, ancient debris The Wreck Field Diamonds, emeralds, gold, iron, copper, redstone, a nautilus shell, a map, Pressure Plating The Leviathan Fall Bone blocks, bone, prismarine, a nautilus shell, gold, Needle Teeth, a heart of the sea, diamonds The Canticle's Anchor The Static Heart, iron blocks, chain, gold, iron, emeralds, diamonds, Pressure Plating, a heart of the sea, netherite scrap The diving bell's chest Salted Fish, Cured Sleeper, Sea Candles, Lumen Lures, Copper Wire, Rusticles, Crew Tags, a Receiver, a Crab Pot, a turtle helmet, now and then a heart of the sea A dead drop Vacuum Tubes, Copper Wire, Magnetic Tape, Lumen Lures, Arc Charges, food, ender pearls, a Receiver, gold, emeralds, diamonds, now and "},{"p":"The Sinkhole and the Deep","h":"","u":"places/the-deep.html","t":"The Deep Something is always listening Wakes Once the Chorus has run from its pit Way in The Throat at the bottom of the Sinkhole's burrow Way out The Throat in the floor of the Gullet Sleep No: \"You can't sleep down here. Something is always listening.\" Beds don't set your spawn either. Biomes The Warm Dark, the Root Hollows, the Old Halls Music The Deep"},{"p":"The Sinkhole and the Deep","h":"Finding it: the fragment","u":"places/the-deep.html#the-hunt","t":"When the Chorus runs from the Hive , it leaves a Chorus Fragment on the floor of its pit, and the fragment still hears the rest of it. Hold it to your ear and turn round. Facing the right way it whispers clearly, and what it says tells you how far. Side on it's faint and broken; facing away there's only static. Up in the world, leading you to the Sinkhole: down. a long way down. far from here - that way. that way. under the hills. we can feel you coming. closer. we can hear you walking. we can hear your heart. here. right under you. come down. it's warm. Down in the Deep, leading you to the Warm Heart: deeper. a long way yet. through the dark - that way. that way. past the old ones' halls. they don't like us. they won't like you. close now. can you hear us singing? we can hear you. here. we are right here. we are finished growing. Side on, and facing away: ...colder... no... turn... (nothing but static)"},{"p":"The Sinkhole and the Deep","h":"The Sinkhole","u":"places/the-deep.html#the-sinkhole","t":"statichollow:sinkhole , once the Chorus has run Halloway's Low Field , where a farm's field was pulled down from underneath. It's out in the world like the Hive: a crater thirty-odd yards across, its rim a cliff of torn turf and soil with cracks running out from it into the grass. The field's fences are snapped off at the edge, the barn has tipped over the brink and lies half down the slope, and the cart it was loading lies on its side at the bottom. Veins of hive flesh run down the walls with ribs of chitin sticking out of them. Steam comes up off its floor, and now and then the whole hole breathes out, deep. The first time someone comes up to it: this is where it went down. the ground didn't fall in. it was pulled. someone measured it before you. he went down after it. the piece of it you've got will tell you how far down it goes. ??? at the Sinkhole The surveyor's camp is on the north rim: E. Calder's notes on a lectern ( Subsidence, Halloway's Low Field ) and his chest of kit: two lanterns, sixteen torches, two leads, a spyglass, an iron pickaxe, bread, cooked beef and a Surgical Kit. Reaching the Sinkhole earns Warmer ."},{"p":"The Sinkhole and the Deep","h":"The burrow","u":"places/the-deep.html#the-burrow","t":"In the bottom of the hole, round a knot of flesh ringed with teeth, is the way the Chorus tore down: a tunnel round as a pipe, lined with hive flesh and ribs of chitin, winding down in six turns like a corkscrew, sixty blocks down from the floor of the hole. Halfway down, on a landing, is the surveyor's last page. At the bottom is a small domed chamber."},{"p":"The Sinkhole and the Deep","h":"The Throat","u":"places/the-deep.html#the-throat","t":"In the middle of the chamber's floor, three blocks across: the Throat , a ring of hive flesh puckered shut. Stand on it and it feels you (\"It feels you standing on it.\"). It stirs, it opens, and after a couple of seconds it takes you down into the Deep. That earns Down Where It Is Warm ."},{"p":"The Sinkhole and the Deep","h":"While it lives: it comes back up","u":"places/the-deep.html#it-comes-back-up","t":"Until the Chorus is dead, the world up top feels it: Tremors under you every so often: a low rumble and dust off the roof, without your view shaking. The ground gives way near you (natural ground only, never your builds): a pit lined with its flesh, its things climbing out of it. The pit heals over after five minutes. Flesh blisters swell up out of the ground: \"Something is swelling up out of the ground. Break it before it bursts.\" If it bursts, its forms come out. The Reach , every few nights where you live: three tremors, closer and closer, the ground splits, and one of the Chorus's hands tears up out of it with its things climbing out after it (\"IT COMES UP\"). Kill it for It Came Up ; leave it and after four minutes it sinks back down. See the Chorus ."},{"p":"The Sinkhole and the Deep","h":"The Deep","u":"places/the-deep.html#the-deep","t":"Huge warm caverns under the hills, older than anything over them, with seas of blood in their bottoms and a rock roof over everything. The Bloom's roots hang down through the roofs, gone deeper than anyone ever dug. Ember caps glow like coals on the floors. Ash and spores drift in the air, there's a warm drone and a heartbeat a long way off, and its own music plays. Coming down: \"It's warm down here. It's always been warm down here.\" If you carry the fragment, a moment later it whispers: \"home. we are home. come and find us. we are deeper.\""},{"p":"The Sinkhole and the Deep","h":"The Warm Dark","u":"places/the-deep.html#the-warm-dark","t":"Where the hive's flesh has grown over the rock: veins of flesh, chitin and bone through the stone, springs of blood, nerve stalks, pustules and ember caps, red spores in the air."},{"p":"The Sinkhole and the Deep","h":"The Root Hollows","u":"places/the-deep.html#the-root-hollows","t":"Where the Bloom's roots come down: great Bloom Roots up from the floor and down from the roof, and pale Root Tendrils hanging everywhere, their ends glowing. Fewer ember caps. The Listeners nest here."},{"p":"The Sinkhole and the Deep","h":"The Old Halls","u":"places/the-deep.html#the-old-halls-biome","t":"The pale worked stone of whoever was down here first: old stone through the rock, bones, skulls, candles, a few ember caps, and ash in the air."},{"p":"The Sinkhole and the Deep","h":"The Gullet","u":"places/the-deep.html#the-gullet","t":"Where you come out: a domed chamber of hive flesh shut in the rock, near the middle of the Deep and up near its roof, lit by nerve stalks round its wall and ember caps on its floor. A Throat is set in its floor: stand on it to go back up to the Sinkhole's chamber. Three tunnels run out of the Gullet and down through the rock until they come out into the caverns."},{"p":"The Sinkhole and the Deep","h":"Low Marrow","u":"places/the-deep.html#low-marrow","t":"About a hundred blocks from the Gullet: a hamlet the ground opened under one night, pulled down whole into a cavern of its own. Five cottages lie where they came to rest, tipped over and half sunk in a lake that isn't water any more, full of it inside. In the middle of the lake its church stands upended, its bell still in its tower. The Bloom's roots hang through the cavern's roof and ember caps burn on what dry ground there is. Two Listeners are still there. Nobody's left. The reeve wrote down why ( Low Marrow , T. Ashby, on the lectern in his cottage), and so did the priest ( the last sermon , Rev. J. Fairley). Both are on the lore page . The reeve's last page:"},{"p":"The Sinkhole and the Deep","h":"Low Marrow","u":"places/the-deep.html#low-marrow-2","t":"T. Ashby, Reeve Found: Low Marrow He said: follow the stones with the ears cut in them. A cap burns on every one. If you find this, go quiet. Go in your stockings. Follow the stones."},{"p":"The Sinkhole and the Deep","h":"The way-stones","u":"places/the-deep.html#the-way-stones","t":"The old ones' road-markers: squat columns with a spiral cut in each like an ear and an ember cap burning on top. They stand every thirty-odd blocks from the Gullet to the Old Halls. Follow them."},{"p":"The Sinkhole and the Deep","h":"The Old Halls","u":"places/the-deep.html#the-old-halls","t":"About 230 blocks from the Gullet, the far end of the way-stones: the older ones' hall, cut out of the rock before anything walked up top. A passage leads straight in to its door. Inside is a long nave of their pale stone, fifty-odd blocks long under a stepped vault, two rows of pillars carved with their spirals, ember caps along the walls and root tendrils hanging down through the vault. Two alcoves hold what they cut in the wall (on lecterns), and the third holds their things. At the far end is a dais, two steps up, with candles on it and a seat at the back. On the seat is the Deaf King , where he's sat ever since the singing came down. He can't hear you and can't see you. He feels the floor."},{"p":"The Sinkhole and the Deep","h":"(cut in the wall by the dais)","u":"places/the-deep.html#cut-in-the-wall-by-the-dais","t":"the old ones Found: the Old Halls p. 1 The king does not hear. The king does not see. The king feels the floor. When you come before him, be still. p. 2 If you would have what he put in his ears, you must take it out of him. He will not give it. With it in your own, the singing is only singing. Killing him earns Stand Still , and he leaves the King's Ear-Stones . Carry them into the Warm Heart and the Chorus's song can't get into you."},{"p":"The Sinkhole and the Deep","h":"The Listeners' nests","u":"places/the-deep.html#the-nests","t":"In the Root Hollows, one to each stretch of the Deep: a hollow where the Listeners (see the Deaf King ) take what they take. Bones, the clothes of the people they were, a barrel of their things, and a low wall of bone round it. The Listeners hunt the Chorus's forms just as they hunt you."},{"p":"The Sinkhole and the Deep","h":"The Warm Heart","u":"places/the-deep.html#the-warm-heart","t":"Where the Chorus went to ground, about 420 blocks out from the Gullet, the way the fragment points. It's a great round chamber in the rock, some seventy-five blocks across. Its floor is hive flesh running down on every side to a lake of blood, with a vault of chitin ribs over it. Four stalks of chitin stand round the lake with its nerve nodes on them, where they were round its pit, and there are three ways in. Come down into it and the Chorus rises: \"Up out of the blood it comes - whole again, and every voice in it singing.\" When it's down to two thirds of its health, the walls crack open (\"The walls crack open. Something's coming through them: the older ones. They've heard it.\") and the Listeners pour in. At a third it tears itself up out of its lake. See the Chorus . When it dies: \"Far below, the singing stops. It doesn't start again.\" Everything of its in the chamber falls apart, the world above stops feeling it, and it leaves the Last Voice (advancement The Last Voice ). That leads on to Chapter Six ."},{"p":"The Sinkhole and the Deep","h":"Its blocks","u":"places/the-deep.html#its-blocks","t":"Block What it is The Throat The way in and out, in the Sinkhole's chamber and the Gullet Deep Rock The Deep's own stone Old Stone, Old Stone Bricks, Carved Old Stone The older ones' pale worked stone Bloom Root, Root Tendril The Bloom's roots; the tendrils' ends glow Ember Cap Glows like a coal on the floors Hive Flesh, Hive Chitin, Nerve Node The Hive's own, in the Warm Dark, the Gullet and the Warm Heart All of them have HD textures and LabPBR maps."},{"p":"The red fog (the Flesh)","h":"","u":"places/the-flesh.html","t":"The Flesh's land Spreading Starts Ten seconds after the Great Bloom rises, east of the Botanic Gardens Reach About 1000 blocks round where it came up; 2000 once the Bloom has changed Ends Dies back once the Bloom is dead, except in the places it built itself into Music Its own, and Rosemont's, the Laboratory's and the shelter's"},{"p":"The red fog (the Flesh)","h":"The waking","u":"places/the-flesh.html#the-waking","t":"Ten seconds after the Great Bloom rises through the glasshouse, the ground east of the Botanic Gardens shakes and splits, and a column of raw muscle forty blocks high punches up out of it, sheds its skin, and opens a slit of teeth down its front. Veins race out from it across the ground. A title card: THE FLESH WAKES , the flower made it . The first of them get up out of the ground and come for you. Flesh and stone, with the HD world pack."},{"p":"The red fog (the Flesh)","h":"How it spreads","u":"places/the-flesh.html#how-it-spreads","t":"Outward from where it came up, further every day: a slow start, then faster. Near you it creeps from block to block. What was there What it becomes Grass and soil Flesh turf and flesh soil: meat Stone and brick Veined stone and veined masonry, lit red from inside Trees Sinew logs and hanging tissue Glass Stretched membrane Sand Rot sand Flowers Withered black stubs Deeper in it grows flesh pustules (tread on one, hit it or shoot it and it bursts over you), mouths in the ground that breathe red mist and let the infected climb out, nerve stalks lit from within, and pools of the Flesh that drag at your feet. Where it touches the Bloom's flesh and the gardens' flowers, they char, and the flowers fight back, killing what of it touches them."},{"p":"The red fog (the Flesh)","h":"The red fog","u":"places/the-flesh.html#the-red-fog","t":"Where it has taken the land, the fog goes the colour of meat and it breathes all round you, with things far off in it: screams, tearing, a heartbeat, a radio, gunfire. Every sound of it is new. With Sound Physics, the Flesh swallows sound like mud and resin do."},{"p":"The red fog (the Flesh)","h":"The infection","u":"places/the-flesh.html#the-infection","t":"Their hits, their bites, a pustule bursting: the Flesh gets into you (\"Something is in the wound. It's warm, and it's moving.\"). A vein beside your hotbar fills red with how much of you it has, and red veins creep in from the edges of your sight. Past halfway you're turning: hungry, slower, your heart pounding in your ears, your sight flushing red with every beat. \"You're turning. Find Bloom Serum.\" At the top, your Last Breath: thirty seconds, your sight closing to a tunnel and your heart slowing. Drink a Bloom Serum, or die and get up again as one of them, with your name (\"Infected Steve\"). Bloom Serum (a glass bottle, a Bloom pustule and sugar; or a ghost orchid, a whispering lily and sugar) drives it back and keeps it off you for twenty seconds. Tainted meat fills you, and infects you. The Gardener's clothes keep half of it off; the full hazmat suit halves the bile, gas and spores."},{"p":"The red fog (the Flesh)","h":"What lives in it","u":"places/the-flesh.html#what-lives-in-it","t":"The Flesh's infected, the things they mutate into after ten minutes on its ground, the Broodmother's nests, and on some nights a horde walking behind a Bellwether. All of them are in the bestiary . Since 1.43.3 parasites get into the infected too. Flower Ash Bombs (a garden flower, a burnt petal and gunpowder make two) burn it back: where one bursts the Flesh's growth dies back to what it was, and anything infected in it burns. Under the Flesh."},{"p":"The red fog (the Flesh)","h":"The places it built itself into","u":"places/the-flesh.html#the-places-it-built","t":"Rosemont , the broken city The Laboratory Shelter No. 4 The nests (while their Broodmother lives) The places the Bloom and the railgun woke, and the column it came up out of"},{"p":"The red fog (the Flesh)","h":"Dying back","u":"places/the-flesh.html#dying-back","t":"With the Bloom dead (since 1.43.5), the Flesh has nothing to grow from. It stops spreading and dies back: wherever you go, the ground it took comes back as it was, grass, earth, stone and trees. Its vents and hordes stop with it. The places it built itself into keep it, and what's in them stays there. it's dying. with the flower dead it's got nothing to grow from - the ground's coming back. not in the places it built itself into, though. those it keeps. ??? as the Flesh dies back"},{"p":"The Hive","h":"","u":"places/the-hive.html","t":"The Hive It's growing a mind Wakes Once the Carrier is dead and the static has signed off, 300 to 1000 blocks out Find it The Watcher's Needle (The Hive), handed out after It Speaks , or /statichollow locate hive Size About seventy blocks across; the pit in the middle is twelve deep In the pit The Chorus Arriving \"The ground here is warm, and soft, and it gives under you. Something under it is breathing.\""},{"p":"The Hive","h":"What it is","u":"places/the-hive.html#what-it-is","t":"With the Carrier dead, the parasite can't hear itself in the static any more. So it grows itself a mind instead, out in the world, in a hamlet it took whole. For about thirty blocks round, everything has gone under its creep : violet Hive Flesh , roots of black Hive Chitin running out over the ground from the middle, and ribs of chitin arched over the ground on the east, south and west. The way in is from the north, through the hamlet's gate. The first time someone comes near, the Watcher says: it took them whole. the people, the houses. everything they knew is in that pit now. it thinks with those, on the stalks round the pit. cut them and it can't think straight. there was a priest here. read him. ??? at the Hive The Hive's black hands standing round the pit, with the Chorus's bar already up."},{"p":"The Hive","h":"The hamlet it took","u":"places/the-hive.html#the-hamlet","t":"Three cottages and a bell tower, half swallowed by the creep. The lane runs in past them from the gate, between fence posts that have mostly fallen. The roofs have fallen in at one end and the creep grows up the walls and in through the doors. The bell tower has a ladder up inside it. In the first cottage is a lectern with the priest's journal, The Book of the Hollow Lane by Fr. Aldous Mercer, and his chest beside it with what he brought for the fire: a Surgical Kit flint and steel, and six fire charges a lantern, four bread, two golden apples and five iron ingots His last page says what to do: \"It thinks with the four bulbs on the black stalks. Burn what you can. Cut what you can't.\""},{"p":"The Hive","h":"The Hive Hands","u":"places/the-hive.html#the-hands","t":"The black spires round the pit are alive (since 1.53.0): seven Hive Hands , each an arm as tall as a tree coming up out of a mound of hive flesh, braided chitin round a core of flesh, a palm with eyes and a mouth at the top and three long hooked fingers. They never stop moving, and they turn to follow you. Come within reach and they slam down on you (the ground lights up violet where it's going to land), sweep low across their own foot, or grab you, lift you high over the hive, squeeze, and throw you. They can be killed; fire hurts them more. A dead one withers and goes down into its mound, and drops hive chitin and flesh. While the Chorus is still in its pit, the hive grows a dead hand back after five minutes. In a hive grown before 1.53.0, the old spires come down and the hands come up the first time you're there. More on the Chorus's page ."},{"p":"The Hive","h":"The nerve nodes","u":"places/the-hive.html#the-nerve-nodes","t":"Round the pit stand four stalks of chitin, nine blocks high, with steps of chitin wound round each one. On top of each is a Nerve Node , glowing and pulsing, joined to the Chorus by a cord with its light running along it. This is what it thinks with. Climb the steps and tear the nodes open: each one you break makes it scream and makes it easier to hurt. Break all four and everything gets through (advancement Senseless )."},{"p":"The Hive","h":"The pit","u":"places/the-hive.html#the-pit","t":"In the middle, the pit: about twenty-two blocks across at the rim, twelve deep, a ridge of flesh round its lip and black ribs of chitin up its walls. A ledge winds down its wall from the rim on the north side to the floor. The floor is heaped and wet, and in its middle is the socket where the Chorus is rooted. The first time anyone comes to the edge of the pit, the Chorus comes up out of it (the cutscene The Mind ) and the fight starts. It never leaves its pit. See the Chorus for the fight. When it's brought down to a quarter it tears itself down into the ground and runs, leaving a Chorus Fragment behind on the floor of the pit. That fragment leads you to the Sinkhole and the Deep ."},{"p":"The Hive","h":"Biomass, pods and bones","u":"places/the-hive.html#the-biomass","t":"Heaps of biomass lie about the place, violet flesh with chitin forced out through it. They aren't dead: with anyone about, they heave themselves up into the parasite's pure forms (see the turned ). Torn husks show where some already got up. Its pods sit in the creep, and the bones of what it took lie here and there."},{"p":"The Hive","h":"Advancements here","u":"places/the-hive.html#advancements","t":"The Hive : Come to where the parasite is growing itself a mind Senseless : Tear open all four of the Chorus's nerve nodes It Ran : Drive the Chorus down out of its pit The rest of Chapter Five's are on the advancements page ."},{"p":"The Hollow's own country","h":"","u":"places/the-hollows-country.html","t":"The Hollow's own country New ground only Since 1.62.0 (five places); 1.66.0 to 1.66.3 (twenty-three more); 1.66.7 (in whole stretches) Where Big stretches of the Overworld, under it, the Nether and the End, among the game's biomes and Biomes O' Plenty's Places Eighteen on the Overworld's surface, three under the ground, four in the Nether, three in the End And under the sea Oceans about 2,000 blocks deep, in three depths (new worlds only) Old worlds Land you've already been through stays as it was. New ground in an old world is laid out the new way, so there'll be a seam where they meet; a new world has it all the new way."},{"p":"The Hollow's own country","h":"The land itself","u":"places/the-hollows-country.html#the-land","t":"Static Hollow has its own country: places of its own, each with its own ground, trees, plants and stone, its own sky, fog and water, its own sounds and its own lullaby. Each one takes the place of one of the game's biomes, the other side of a kind of place you know, as the Moor is to the plains. Their terrain is the game's own, in the same climate. Everything that hunts the Hollow hunts there too. They sit alongside Biomes O' Plenty , which is in the modpack since 1.62.0 (with TerraBlender and GlitchCore), and Static Hollow's structures, fog and music are made to fit Biomes O' Plenty's biomes too. Out on the moor."},{"p":"The Hollow's own country","h":"How it comes: in whole stretches","u":"places/the-hollows-country.html#whole-stretches","t":"Up to 1.66.6 the Hollow's places were laid down on one side of the world's \"weirdness\", a noise that turns over every hundred blocks or so, so each came in strips and scraps, cut off short where it turned. Since 1.66.7 the Hollow has its own country: big stretches of the world, hundreds of blocks to over a thousand across (its rises and hollows some 600 to 1,500 blocks across), each world's own. Inside them, every one of the game's biomes the Hollow has its own for is the Hollow's, all of each one; outside them the world is the game's (and Biomes O' Plenty's). It's the same in the Nether, and in the End, where one of its three takes a whole stretch of islands rather than a different one on each island's top, slopes and edges. The big things only go down where all of one stands in its own biome, none half in the next one over: the ribcages, the radio masts, the frozen figures, the stone faces, the scarecrows, the crop rings, the grave rows, the choir, the heart, the gallows, the husks, the dead stars and the rest."},{"p":"The Hollow's own country","h":"Lighter places","u":"places/the-hollows-country.html#lighter-places","t":"In 1.66.4 the twenty-three places from 1.66.0 to 1.66.3 were thinned to about half as much decoration, to go easier on memory: half the trees, plant patches, bones, figures, husks, hearts, furnace stacks, watchers, dead stars and the rest, each kept or dropped on its own so the places stay even. In 1.66.5 the older places had the same: the Antler Woods, the Blightwood, the Hollow Moor, the Weeping Fen, the Signal Flats, the deep water's places (and the abyss under every ocean: its bone heaps, vents, spires and lights) and the deep's caves (the Old Halls, the Root Hollows, the Warm Dark). Their ground, ore veins, fog, light, sounds and music are unchanged. New ground only: chunks you've already explored keep what they have."},{"p":"The Hollow's own country","h":"The Overworld","u":"places/the-hollows-country.html#the-overworld","t":"Biome In place of Since The Hollow Moor Plains and meadows in a cool band 1.62.0 The Blightwood Dark forests 1.62.0 The Weeping Fen Swamps 1.62.0 The Antler Woods Snowy taiga, the wetter kind 1.62.0 The Signal Flats Dry savanna 1.62.0 The Hanging Wood Forests, birch forests, old growth birch, dappled forests 1.66.0 The Bone Dunes Deserts 1.66.0 The Rust Mesa Badlands (all three) 1.66.0 The Choke Jungle Jungles (all three) 1.66.0 The White Silence Snowy plains, ice spikes 1.66.0 The Watching Peaks Frozen and stony peaks 1.66.0 The Withered Fields The other plains, sunflower plains 1.66.1 The Mourning Garden Flower forests 1.66.1 The Tall Dark Taiga, old growth pine and spruce taiga 1.66.1 The Drowned Roots Mangrove swamps 1.66.1 Petal Rot Cherry groves 1.66.1 The Pale Caps Mushroom fields 1.66.1 The Ashen Shore Beaches 1.66.1 Each has its own lullaby. The first five's are Hollow Fields, Under the Boughs, Still Water, Pine Needles and Dry Bones; the further the story has got, the more often the chapter's own music plays instead (see the soundtrack ). With Serene Seasons, the fog also changes colour with the season."},{"p":"The Hollow's own country","h":"The Hollow Moor","u":"places/the-hollows-country.html#the-hollow-moor","t":"Open, misty heath under a grey-blue mist: dead heather, peat, old graves under the turf (grave soil), mossy boulders, fallen deadwood, and here and there a gallows-tree of deadwood with chains hanging from it. On the ground you find grave candles, cairn stones and bone piles. White ash drifts in the air. Wind crosses the moor, and a far bell tolls. (The plains and meadows outside its cool band are the Withered Fields' or the game's.)"},{"p":"The Hollow's own country","h":"The Blightwood","u":"places/the-hollows-country.html#the-blightwood","t":"Sick trees with grey-violet leaves, in a close fog the colour of a bruise: Blightwood , some of them great and dark-oak shaped, with Hanging Rot dripping from their leaves and shelf fungus on them. Huge brown mushrooms grow among them, and Rotgrass underneath. Rot caps and bone piles lie on the ground, and spores and carrion flies drift in the air. The wood creaks, and something breathes in the trees."},{"p":"The Hollow's own country","h":"The Weeping Fen","u":"places/the-hollows-country.html#the-weeping-fen","t":"Drowned Fen Willows trail Willow Strands into black water, over peat and mud and sparse rotgrass, a green murk coming off the water. Lights drift over it (lantern motes), carrion flies with them. You find ritual offerings, rot caps and cairn stones. Frogs and the bogged live here. Water laps, and someone weeps, far off."},{"p":"The Hollow's own country","h":"The Antler Woods","u":"places/the-hollows-country.html#the-antler-woods","t":"Bone-white Bonewood trees with dark red Bonewood Needles in a pale, cold fog, some of them tall spires, and antler-snags of fallen deadwood among them, with a little dead heather. Bone piles and cairn stones lie about and bone ash drifts in the air. Wolves and foxes live here. Wind whistles through bone, and something bellows, far off."},{"p":"The Hollow's own country","h":"The Signal Flats","u":"places/the-hollows-country.html#the-signal-flats","t":"Dead grey flats under a flat grey haze: Wire Grass , gravel, snags of deadwood, and outcrops of Static Stone , which hums. Bone piles and cairn stones lie about, and sparks of static and white ash drift on the wind. Static on the wind, and tones through the static."},{"p":"The Hollow's own country","h":"The Hanging Wood","u":"places/the-hollows-country.html#the-hanging-wood","t":"Pale birches and Hangwood under a pale haze, and from their boughs Nooses , Straw Effigies and Bone Chimes that clink in the wind. Ghostfern grows under them. A rope creaks under weight; bones clatter on strings."},{"p":"The Hollow's own country","h":"The Bone Dunes","u":"places/the-hollows-country.html#the-bone-dunes","t":"Drifts of Bone Sand , bleached bushes, Finger Cactus (a hand of a cactus: it pricks), and whole ribcages of things half out of the sand with a skull at the end. Bones shift under the sand; wind moans through bone."},{"p":"The Hollow's own country","h":"The Rust Mesa","u":"places/the-hollows-country.html#the-rust-mesa","t":"Blood-red cliffs with rust in the bands of the rock, Rust Silt , Rust Thorn (it cuts), and dust the colour of it in the air. Dead radio masts stand on it, some snapped, their lamps still blinking red. A voice in the static; metal groans."},{"p":"The Hollow's own country","h":"The Choke Jungle","u":"places/the-hollows-country.html#the-choke-jungle","t":"Every tree being strangled: red Throttle Vine up the trunks, Choke Vine hanging down from the leaves, and Meat Flowers that draw flies, in a close green fog. Vines tighten; something wet moves."},{"p":"The Hollow's own country","h":"The White Silence","u":"places/the-hollows-country.html#the-white-silence","t":"No wind and almost no sound. Rime Stalks , spikes of ice, and Haunted Ice with something in it (a hand, a face, someone a long way down). People stand frozen where they stood, two blocks high: Frozen Figures . Someone breathes out; ice cracks."},{"p":"The Hollow's own country","h":"The Watching Peaks","u":"places/the-hollows-country.html#the-watching-peaks","t":"Faces carved in the cliffs, nine stones each ( Cliff Face ), eyes open, mouths open; at night something glints in the eyes. Watching Stones sit on the rock, one eye each. The mountain rumbles; stone grinds."},{"p":"The Hollow's own country","h":"The Withered Fields","u":"places/the-hollows-country.html#the-withered-fields","t":"Dead fields: Blighted Wheat with black in its ears, and Withered Sunflowers that turn their heads to follow you while you're near. Scarecrows stand in them, a stitched sack for a head, and it turns too. Now and then a ring is flattened into the crops with a sunflower in the middle of it. Something moves in the wheat; crows call."},{"p":"The Hollow's own country","h":"The Mourning Garden","u":"places/the-hollows-country.html#the-mourning-garden","t":"Dark Yews over rows of old graves: Headstones , their mounds, Black Roses and Mourning Lilies left on them, a candle or two still burning, and Weeping Bells . Funeral bells toll on their own in the dark. Someone weeps."},{"p":"The Hollow's own country","h":"The Tall Dark","u":"places/the-hollows-country.html#the-tall-dark","t":"Nightspruce so tall and close it's dusk at noon. Someone has cut eyes into the trunks at head height; Dead Lanterns hang guttering from the branches; Gloomcaps glow faintly underneath. Something walks; something knocks."},{"p":"The Hollow's own country","h":"The Drowned Roots","u":"places/the-hollows-country.html#the-drowned-roots","t":"Grey Drowned Mangroves trailing vines, Root Hands reaching up out of the shallows and the mud, and Bloated Lilies with gas bubbling up round them. Something breathes under the water."},{"p":"The Hollow's own country","h":"Petal Rot","u":"places/the-hollows-country.html#petal-rot","t":"The blossom rotting on the trees ( Rotblossom ), brown-pink petals on the ground, flies, and Flesh Blossoms that bleed. Something wet moves; flies buzz."},{"p":"The Hollow's own country","h":"The Pale Caps","u":"places/the-hollows-country.html#the-pale-caps","t":"Pale Mycelium , giant pale mushrooms, Pale Caps , and Puffballs : walk into one and it bursts in your face (sick and blind for a moment). Unlike the game's mushroom fields, monsters walk here. Something breathes; spores burst."},{"p":"The Hollow's own country","h":"The Ashen Shore","u":"places/the-hollows-country.html#the-ashen-shore","t":"Grey Ash Sand , Driftwood , Ash Grass , and the rotting carcasses of huge things the sea gave up: mounds of Rotting Blubber (soft, slow to cross, stinking) with their ribs through them. Something moans out at sea."},{"p":"The Hollow's own country","h":"Under the ground","u":"places/the-hollows-country.html#under-the-ground","t":""},{"p":"The Hollow's own country","h":"The Flesh Throat","u":"places/the-hollows-country.html#the-flesh-throat","t":"In place of the lush caves (1.66.0). The rock is lined with Throat Flesh that slows you, Throat Fangs point up from the floor and down from the roof (falling on one hurts), and Sinew Strands and glowing Gut Pods hang down. It breathes, it has a heart, and now and then it swallows. The cave squelches."},{"p":"The Hollow's own country","h":"The Echo Hollows","u":"places/the-hollows-country.html#the-echo-hollows","t":"In place of the dripstone caves (1.66.0): Echo Stone and Echo Crystals that give back what was said here, a long time ago. Footsteps echo back; crystals ring."},{"p":"The Hollow's own country","h":"The Webbed Dark","u":"places/the-hollows-country.html#the-webbed-dark","t":"Its own place (1.66.0), deep under dry land inland. Webs in every corner and Web Mass on the roofs, Silk Cocoons hanging (break one for what it caught), and Egg Sacs : break one and the spiders come out. Spiders and cave spiders spawn there far more. Chittering; legs skitter."},{"p":"The Hollow's own country","h":"The Nether","u":"places/the-hollows-country.html#the-nether","t":"Since 1.66.2, four places of the Hollow's in the Nether, each with its own ground, growth and walls, its own fog (closer than the rest of the Nether), particles, sounds and lullaby. Since 1.66.7 each takes the whole of one of the game's own, in the Hollow's country. Biome In place of The Cinder Choir Soul sand valleys The Bleeding Wastes Crimson forests The Static Furnace Basalt deltas The Gallows Grove Warped forests"},{"p":"The Hollow's own country","h":"The Cinder Choir","u":"places/the-hollows-country.html#the-cinder-choir","t":"An ash plain, Charstone over it with embers still in its veins ( Ember Charstone ), Ash Reeds and Smoulder Bushes . Charred Figures stand in curved rows in the ash, all turned to the one in front of them, mouths open and the coal still burning in them. Come near and each hums its own note, so walking among them you hear the chord. The choir sings; embers crackle."},{"p":"The Hollow's own country","h":"The Bleeding Wastes","u":"places/the-hollows-country.html#the-bleeding-wastes","t":"Scab under foot, and the netherrack overhead bleeds: it drips. Artery Vines hang from the roof; Vein Roots and Bloodcaps grow, and there are hollows full of blood. Somewhere in it, under its ribs, is a heart in a mound of Heart Muscle , beating: you hear it a long way off, and it beats faster the closer you come."},{"p":"The Hollow's own country","h":"The Static Furnace","u":"places/the-hollows-country.html#the-static-furnace","t":"Slag and Clinker , old Cable strung across the caverns and hanging from the roof, furnace stacks with the fire behind a grate at the foot (hot to stand on), Static Vents breathing blue sparks (stand on one and it bites), Wire Tufts and Spark Bulbs . The air hums, and now and then the light dips, as if the power did. Machinery groans; static crackles."},{"p":"The Hollow's own country","h":"The Gallows Grove","u":"places/the-hollows-country.html#the-gallows-grove","t":"Grave Nylium , black Gallowwood trees with their arms out level, nooses from them, and iron Gibbets on chains (some with bones still in), Rope Grass , Gallows Blooms , and here and there a gallows. A Gallowwood Sprout grows into a gallows tree. Something swings; a rope creaks."},{"p":"The Hollow's own country","h":"The End","u":"places/the-hollows-country.html#the-end","t":"Since 1.66.3, out past the End's middle island, three places of the Hollow's, each with its own ground, growth, light and fog, sounds and lullaby. Each took the place of half of one of the game's own (its highlands, midlands or barrens); since 1.66.7, in the Hollow's country, one of the three takes a whole stretch of islands, highlands, midlands and barrens alike (the middle island and the small islands stay the game's)."},{"p":"The Hollow's own country","h":"The Pale Reaches","u":"places/the-hollows-country.html#the-pale-reaches","t":"Up to 1.66.6, in place of half the highlands. The End gone white as bone: Pale End Stone , Pale Chorus , Pale Moss , Pale Blooms . At the islands' edges stand Pale Watchers , too tall and too thin, looking out at the void. Don't look at one too long: your ears start to ring, and then the light goes out of your eyes."},{"p":"The Hollow's own country","h":"The Husk Fields","u":"places/the-hollows-country.html#the-husk-fields","t":"Up to 1.66.6, in place of half the midlands. The shed skins of huge, long, many-legged things lie on the slopes ( Husk , Carapace ), hollow, torn, split down the back where whatever wore them climbed out; Husk Flakes everywhere. Void Eggs lie about: break them and what's in them comes out, and when you're near, now and then one hatches by itself. Endermites live here. Many legs skitter; something rattles."},{"p":"The Hollow's own country","h":"The Starless Barrens","u":"places/the-hollows-country.html#the-starless-barrens","t":"Up to 1.66.6, in place of half the barrens. Black ground ( Starless Stone ), the light low, cracks down into the void with something whispering in them, and Dead Stars lying in their craters, a little light still in them, with Star Ash round them. They go out as you come near, and glow again once you've gone. The 1.66 blocks are all placeable and in the creative tab, and a few make things: planks from the new logs (crimson planks from gallowwood), dyes from black roses, lilies and pale blooms, tinted glass from ash sand, string from rope grass, chain from cable, glowstone dust from star ash, paper from husk, bone meal from carapace, end stone from starless stone. See the items page ."},{"p":"The Hollow's own country","h":"Small things sharing one space","u":"places/the-hollows-country.html#small-things","t":"Since 1.62.0 there are seven sets of little things that share a single block space, one to four of a set in it, each turned to face whoever put it down. Place one on another to add a piece; break it and one piece comes off. Set What's in it Where you find it Grave Candles Tallow candles, a stub, a skull. Light them, put them out. The Hollow Moor; the vaults under the cathedral's crypts Bone Pile A skull, its jaw, bones The Moor, the Blightwood, the Antler Woods, the Signal Flats; the cathedral's undercroft; the deep ocean floors and the Dead Water's Rot Caps The Blightwood's fungi. They glow a little, and puff spores. The Blightwood, the Weeping Fen Hanging Chains Chains, a hook, a shackle, a weight, hung from a ceiling. They creak. The cathedral's undercroft and crypt vaults; the rig's dive locker and workshop Rig Clutter A tin, an oil can, a wrench, bolts The rig in the Dead Water Cairn Stones Flat stones stacked by pilgrims, the top one carved. At night something whispers from them. The Moor, the Fen, the Antler Woods, the Signal Flats; behind the Forsaken Altar's pilgrim stones Ritual Offerings A bowl of ash, a straw doll, a red candle, dried herbs The Weeping Fen; at the foot of the Forsaken Altar's pilgrim stones The idea of small blocks sharing a space is from Olaf's Relatively Placed Blocks. Nothing of it is used; these are Static Hollow's own."},{"p":"The Hollow's own country","h":"The deep oceans","u":"places/the-hollows-country.html#the-deep-oceans","t":"In new worlds (made since 1.62.0) the oceans go down. Past the shelf the sea floor falls away to about 2,000 blocks below the waves : a black drop with the ocean monuments standing on its floor and lava glowing at the very bottom. The deep is the game's own terrain, stretched. (The idea is Tectonic's, MIT; nothing of its code is used.) Under an ocean the water is laid out in three depths, each its own place with its own dark, its own sounds and its own life: Depth From What's there What lives there The Sunless Drop below y -128 The last of the light goes and the slope falls away into nothing; bone-white snow drifting down through the black Shroud Rays, Needlemaws, drowned, glow squid The Hadal Dark below y -700 Pressure, cold, and things that make their own light Shroud Rays, Needlemaws, the Static Leviathan, glow squid The Trench below y -1400 The floor of the world's sea: vents breathing heat, the bones of very big things, and what made them bones Needlemaws, the Static Leviathan On the deep floors lie heaps of bone, spires of bone and calcite, and vents of basalt and blackstone with crying obsidian in them. Sea pickles glow in the dark and bone piles lie about. All the way down, the deep water groans and something passes in the dark. The Shroud Ray leaves you be, until you hit it. Then it wraps you. It drops Shroud Hide . The Needlemaw is dark until your light finds it. It lunges, and recoils from the light. It drops Needle Teeth . The Static Leviathan is a boss with its own bar. It charges, it swallows you whole, and it sings on the Remote's frequency. It drops its Signal Organ , which mends the Remote in the Dead Water . More on all three in the bestiary and on the Undertow's page ."},{"p":"The Hub","h":"","u":"places/the-hub.html","t":"The Hub A realm he made First time After the last show's credits, his hand comes up through them and takes you there After that Use the Remote; use it again in the Hub to go home Way out The Remote, or the edge (home to your bed or the world's spawn, no harm in the fall) Sleep No: \"Not here. Not with it out there, past the wall.\" Music The Hub"},{"p":"The Hub","h":"What it is","u":"places/the-hub.html#what-it-is","t":"A realm the Watcher made, floating in a sky of drifting static with a pale fog over everything. The middle of it is a round plaza of pale Hub Stone , about thirty-three blocks across, with his marks lit in it as Hub Glyphs in two rings and a cross in the middle. Underneath, the stone tapers away to a point, the way an island would if it had been torn up out of something. A few smaller pieces of it hang in the static round about. Being taken there earns The Hub . The gallery, during his speech."},{"p":"The Hub","h":"His speech","u":"places/the-hub.html#his-speech","t":"The first time, he's there with you (the cutscene The Hub ): this is the hub. i made it. a realm. it isn't mine - nothing is - but i made it. through these, you can go back. every chapter. play it again. or jump off the edge. it'll take you home, and you can carry on. ??? in the Hub He doesn't get to finish. A voice tears the sky over the gallery open (\"ENOUGH.\"), and the First Signal comes through. The whole scene is on Chapter Seven ."},{"p":"The Hub","h":"The gallery and its replay portals","u":"places/the-hub.html#the-gallery","t":"Along the north side of the plaza runs the gallery , a walk with six Replay Portals standing on it, one for each chapter, each with its chapter playing in it like a picture on an old set. Walk into one and you're back at that chapter's place in your world. A moment later its last fight comes back for another go: a replay . The replay portals, with the HD world pack. Portal Takes you to What comes back The Hollow The Cathedral of the Hollow The Hollow Saint , rising out of the floor Act Two The Botanic Gardens' glasshouse The Gardener The Bloom The Great Bloom's arena The Gardener, Reborn The Flesh The Laboratory Specimen Zero The Static The Deep The Deaf King The Door The Stalls The Crowd , getting up out of the heap of them Going through one earns Previously On... . The story stays told: whoever comes back is marked as a replay, and beating it again sets nothing off (no new act, no lockdown, no tickets). It fights the way it did and goes down the way it did, and then \"(The Remote takes you back to the Hub.)\" Beating a replay also leaves three or four Rerun Reels , which Chapter Seven's gear is made from (see gear for every chapter ). A replay ends if you go more than 160 blocks from it, leave, die, log out, or take longer than twenty minutes: \"The replay's over - it's gone back into the static.\" If a chapter's place isn't in your world, the portal says \"there's nothing there to go back to in this world.\""},{"p":"The Hub","h":"The edge","u":"places/the-hub.html#the-edge","t":"On the south side of the plaza a walk goes out over nothing: the edge . Jump off and you fall, the Hub going away above you, and come down at home (your bed, or the world's spawn) with no harm done. Since 1.62.0 there's one exception. If you've never been down in the Dead Water, the Watcher is there as you fall, and he tears a portal open under you. You come down on the rig in the Dead Water instead ( Chapter Eight ). The first time, at the end of his speech, that's where the jump goes. Worlds that had their landing at home before 1.62.0 get there by taking the Remote to the Hub and jumping off."},{"p":"The Hub","h":"The wall, and what's past it","u":"places/the-hub.html#the-wall","t":"When you both went off the edge the first time, he shut the realm behind you with a wall of static. Back in the Hub, the First Signal is still there, past that faint wall, standing and watching you. Now and then you hear it. Not for ever. When the Broadcast cuts in ( Chapter Ten ), it opens on the Hub: the First Signal at his wall, both hands flat on the static. He stops, and his head tilts. Then the rage: a scream of many voices through a dead channel, the wall bulging, his fists on it. He turns his back on it, lifts a hand, tears his own way open (colour bars, black) and walks into it. He comes out on his platform in his kingdom ."},{"p":"The Hub","h":"The Remote","u":"places/the-hub.html#the-remote","t":"The Remote is an old television's remote whose blank button is warm (being given it earns Channel Changer ). Use it at home and it takes you to the Hub; use it in the Hub and it takes you home. Since 1.62.0 he hands it to you on the rig in the Dead Water, and it breaks in your hand there. Mended, it works again, and crouching as you press it takes you back to the rig. See the Dead Water ."},{"p":"The Hub","h":"Its blocks","u":"places/the-hub.html#its-blocks","t":"Hub Stone and Hub Stone Slab Hub Glyph : his marks, lit Replay Portal Since 1.59.1 the mod's own copies of the Photon, Insanity and Hysteria shaders draw the Hub with their Nether programs: lit evenly by its own pale fog, with no sun, clouds or light shafts."},{"p":"The Hub","h":"Advancements here","u":"places/the-hub.html#advancements","t":"The Hub : Be taken into the realm he made, after the credits ENOUGH : Hear the First Signal - and jump Previously On... : Go back to a chapter through one of the Hub's portals"},{"p":"The Other Side","h":"","u":"places/the-other-side.html","t":"The Other Side Stay out of its eye Way in The Door at the End of the World, once its static has gone black Way out The seam in the screen's back, out into the End beside the Door Sleep No: \"Not here. Not with it out there.\" Past the edge The Viewer Music The Other Side; the Viewer's fight has its own (What He Kept Out) Arriving \"The other side. A stage, behind the screen your world's on - and past its edge, nothing. Something's sat out there in it.\""},{"p":"The Other Side","h":"The black door","u":"places/the-other-side.html#the-black-door","t":"When the Watcher has run his first reel in the Vault , the static in the Door at the End of the World goes black: the dark on the far side of it, looking out. It hums and the air is drawn into it. Walk into it. Going through earns The Other Side ."},{"p":"The Other Side","h":"The stage","u":"places/the-other-side.html#the-stage","t":"You come out through a seam of Black Static in the back of a screen as big as a cliff, ninety-six blocks wide and forty-eight high. Your world plays across it the wrong way round, its light coming through the cloth backwards. In front of you is a stage of pale boards about sixty-five blocks wide. On either side are the wings , black curtains with gaps in them, and over it stands a proscenium arch. Footlights run along the front edge. The Watcher's last projector is at the back of the stage, with him beside it."},{"p":"The Other Side","h":"The painted flats","u":"places/the-other-side.html#the-flats","t":"Nine flats of scenery stand about on the boards, each one a picture of somewhere from your story in a scene painter's broad strokes, on the side that faces out: the Cathedral Rosemont the Glasshouse the Drive-in the Bloom the Deep a house the woods the Stalls A flat between you and the Viewer's eye hides you from it. Its hands smash the flats they hit to splinters, so the cover doesn't last."},{"p":"The Other Side","h":"The edge","u":"places/the-other-side.html#the-edge","t":"Past the front of the stage there's nothing, only a dark so big it has a shape. Fall off and \"The dark doesn't keep you. You're back on the boards - it hurt.\""},{"p":"The Other Side","h":"Curtain Up","u":"places/the-other-side.html#curtain-up","t":"The first time anyone comes through, the camera is taken. Out past the edge there are knees like hills, shoulders up in the black, and hands on the stage's edge with fingers like felled trees. Then an eye opens. you came through. good. it hasn't looked this way. not yet. this is the other side. it's watched your world since the first picture. everything that ever happened to you - it watched. now it wants to see you up close. stay out of its eye. get behind the scenery. when it leans in - hit it. i'll run the projector. ??? Curtain Up \"Keep out of its light - get behind the scenery. When it leans in, hit its eye. Its hands feel it too.\" Then the fight with the Viewer begins. Cut-out Stand-Ins hop out of the gaps in the wings and point you out to it."},{"p":"The Other Side","h":"His Last Projector","u":"places/the-other-side.html#his-last-projector","t":"The projector at the back of the stage is his: \"His. He'll run it.\" Twice during the fight he loads it. At two thirds of the Viewer's health he puts the Omni's Heart in its lamp and throws every colour at once into its eye (advancement Every Colour at Once ). At a third, he puts in what's left of the Carrier: your world, carried out on the beam. After that the Viewer reaches for the projector with both hands, and you have to beat them back. At the end he threads his first reel and runs it for the Viewer, and it sits back to watch itself. When the last show is over, the credits roll and you're sent home with a record, Thank You for Watching . \"You're home. Somewhere past the end of the world, a projector's running, and something's watching itself, and will be for ever.\" The Door's static is static again."},{"p":"The Other Side","h":"Its blocks","u":"places/the-other-side.html#its-blocks","t":"Black Static : the Door's opening once it's gone black, and the seam home Stage Boards , Stage Flat , Painted Flat and Footlight The Screen's Back His Last Projector"},{"p":"The Other Side","h":"Advancements here","u":"places/the-other-side.html#advancements","t":"The Other Side : Go through the Door at the End of the World, its static gone black Out of Sight : Get through the first third of the Viewer without it ever seeing you right through Every Colour at Once : See the Omni's heart put into his last projector's lamp It Gets Up : Be there when what he kept out stands up Thank You for Watching : See the last show"},{"p":"The Door and the Stalls","h":"","u":"places/the-stalls.html","t":"The Stalls Quiet, please Way in The Door at the End of the World, out in the End Way out The Door behind you: home to your bed, or the world's spawn Sleep No: \"Not here. Not with them watching.\" Who's here Forty of the Audience in the seats, four Ushers in the aisles Music The Stalls; the Crowd's fight has its own The screen Sixty-four blocks across, about two hundred feet"},{"p":"The Door and the Stalls","h":"The seal on the End","u":"places/the-stalls.html#the-seal","t":"After signing off, the Watcher shut the End: anyone who goes through an End portal in survival is sent straight back out to their bed or the world's spawn. He can't keep you out if you carry the Last Voice in, the one voice the Chorus couldn't swallow (since 1.60.1 it works however you came by it). It speaks: \"...hold me up. here. he made this seal with his own hands. i can open it...\" Something cracks, all the way across the End's sky - and stays cracked. The seal he put on it is broken. \"...there. out past the obsidian. a door. go through it. i'll be quiet now...\" And the Watcher says one word: \"...don't.\" From then on the End is open to everyone, as it was. This earns The Door at the End of the World . (The dragon you'll meet there is the Infested Ender Dragon .)"},{"p":"The Door and the Stalls","h":"The Door at the End of the World","u":"places/the-stalls.html#the-door","t":"Out past the obsidian platform you arrive on, a causeway of seal-stone runs east over the void. Seal-stone is black with the Watcher's glyphs cut in it, and posts along the causeway each carry one of his glyphs, still faintly lit. At its end an island of the same stone hangs in nothing, with a long root of it going down underneath. On the island, facing back the way you came, stands the Door : a frame of seal-stone nine blocks wide and thirteen high, his glyphs cut all round it, and in its opening nothing but static , upright, crawling and humming. Walk into it. The Door stands about 28 blocks east of the obsidian, at the End's 128, 49, 0. Since 1.60.2 the End's island ground is cleared off it, with a way along the causeway and a bowl round the island so the Door stands in the open. The first time anyone is in the End, the ground over the obsidian also gives way into a shaft open to the sky, so you don't arrive shut in end stone. Later the Door changes. Once the Watcher has run his first reel in the Vault , its static goes black : the dark on the far side of it, looking out. It hums, the air is drawn into it, and walking in takes you to the Other Side . After the last show it's static again."},{"p":"The Door and the Stalls","h":"The Stalls","u":"places/the-stalls.html#the-stalls","t":"\"Rows and rows of seats in the dark, every one of them facing a screen. Some of them are taken.\" It's a picture house with no walls and no roof, going on further than you can see. The floor is black Stalls Asphalt , and on it row after row of Picture House Seats curve round in long arcs to face the screen, with two aisles running down through them. Black sky, dark fog, dust and ash in the air, its own air and its own music. Arriving earns Take Your Seat . Behind the last row are the cars of every drive-in that ever closed, wrecked, still facing the screen, with speaker posts among them. Behind those is the projection booth, up on its tower, with its beam going out over everything. And behind that is the way you came in: a Door of seal-stone, its opening full of static. Step back through it and you're home."},{"p":"The Door and the Stalls","h":"The Great Screen","u":"places/the-stalls.html#the-great-screen","t":"At the front stands the Great Screen , sixty-four blocks across in a black proscenium, its red curtains drawn back to either side and a low stage at its foot. Its picture flickers: static, and between the static the story so far, frame after frame, grey and grainy. The altar, the cathedral, the glasshouse, the Bloom, the city, the drive-in, the hive, the Deep."},{"p":"The Door and the Stalls","h":"The Audience in the seats","u":"places/the-stalls.html#the-audience-in-the-seats","t":"Forty of the seats are taken by the Audience : grey people in grey clothes, faces turned up to the screen, a ticket in one hand in their laps. They don't look round, but they hear you. A step near them, a block broken or a door, and they get up slowly with a finger to their lips, come for you and hold you where you are. Sneak and they don't hear you walk. Lose them and they go back and sit down. Some of them carry a Ticket Stub . Four Ushers walk the aisles with their lamps. Sneaking doesn't help against a lamp: it sees, it doesn't hear. If one finds you (\"The Usher's lamp is on you.\"), the SHHH goes through the house and everyone sat near you gets up. Show an Usher a Ticket Stub and it looks away for a minute. All three of them are on the Crowd's page ."},{"p":"The Door and the Stalls","h":"The front aisle","u":"places/the-stalls.html#the-front-aisle","t":"Between the stage and the front row runs the front aisle . Step out onto it and \"The picture on the screen is you.\" Every one of the Audience gets up and comes down to the front, and they go into a heap that stands up as the Crowd . It doesn't leave the front."},{"p":"The Door and the Stalls","h":"The front row","u":"places/the-stalls.html#the-front-row","t":"One seat in the front row, straight back from the middle of the screen, is always taken. When the Crowd has come apart and the screen has gone dark, you see who's in it (the cutscene Front Row ). He tears the screen open and goes through, and it closes up behind him to a seam of light down the middle of the screen: \"There's a seam of light down the middle of the screen where he went through. It won't stay shut forever.\" The Crowd leaves the Last Ticket behind. Hold it up to the seam and it tears in two in your hand, and the seam opens wide, light pouring out of it down to the stage. It stays open for everyone. That's the way into the Watcher's Vault . Coming back out of the Vault puts you on the stage in front of the screen."},{"p":"The Door and the Stalls","h":"Its blocks","u":"places/the-stalls.html#its-blocks","t":"Seal-Stone and Seal-Stone Glyph : the Door, its frame and the causeway The Door's Static : the Door's opening Stalls Asphalt , Picture House Seat , Screen Cloth and The Great Screen"},{"p":"The Door and the Stalls","h":"Advancements here","u":"places/the-stalls.html#advancements","t":"The Door at the End of the World : Carry the Last Voice into the End, and break his seal Take Your Seat : Go through the Door into the Stalls Quiet, Please : Keep perfectly still through the Crowd's Hush Standing Ovation : Bring the Crowd down Front Row : See who was sitting in the front row Admit One : Hold the Last Ticket up to the seam in the screen"},{"p":"The Watcher's Vault","h":"","u":"places/the-watchers-vault.html","t":"The Watcher's Vault Behind the picture Way in The seam in the Stalls' Great Screen, opened with the Last Ticket Way out The tear you came out of, onto the stage in the Stalls Sleep No: \"Not here. Not with them standing out there in the stacks.\" Who's here Sixteen Tuned in the stacks and two in each keep Music Behind the Picture; the Projectionist's fight has its own Arriving \"Behind the picture. Shelves going up into the dark, cans of film and boxes of tape on every one, and old sets among them - some still on.\""},{"p":"The Watcher's Vault","h":"Behind the picture","u":"places/the-watchers-vault.html#behind-the-picture","t":"You come out through the seam into his archive, on the back of the picture: a wall of grey canvas with the picture's light coming through it backwards. Going in earns Behind the Picture . Ahead, the nave runs north: a long walk of dark Vault Terrazzo , cable over the floor, bulbs in cages hanging on chains out of the black, and walls of the Watcher's own concrete. On either side are the stacks , row after row of steel Archive Shelves nine blocks high with a cross-aisle through them. There are cans of film on their edges and boxes of tape on every shelf, labels in his hand, and Old Sets among them, some still on, static crawling on their screens."},{"p":"The Watcher's Vault","h":"The Tuned","u":"places/the-watchers-vault.html#the-tuned","t":"Standing in the aisles are the Tuned : people from the neck down (a cardigan, a shirt done up to the collar, slippers) with an old television set where the head should be. They only move while you're looking at them. Look at one and it comes for you in jerks, like a picture with frames missing, with your face on its screen. Look away and it stops dead. Close, and watched, it takes your head in its hands and tunes you. In the dark, or in the Projectionist's light, they move whether you look or not. Flash an Usher's Lamp at one and it can't move for four seconds. Some drop a Vacuum Tube . More on the Projectionist's page ."},{"p":"The Watcher's Vault","h":"The keeps","u":"places/the-watchers-vault.html#the-keeps","t":"Three keeps open off the nave behind round steel Keep Doors : two facing each other near the seam, and one further in on the west side. Use a door or its wheel and \"The wheel turns. Somewhere in the door, bolts draw back, one after another.\" The door swings in. Two Tuned wait in each keep. On a plinth in each is what he kept: What he kept Taking it The Omni's Heart \"The Omni's heart: every colour at once, turning. It's lighter than it looks, and warm.\" What's Left of the Carrier \"What's left of the Carrier comes off its plinth beating - and the static pours out of it.\" Every Tuned near you is loose for a few seconds. His First Reel \"His first reel. On the lid, in his hand: THE OTHER SIDE. FIRST. DO NOT RUN.\" It's kept in a glass case. All three together: \"That's all three of them. Back to the Watch.\" That earns What He Kept ."},{"p":"The Watcher's Vault","h":"The Watch","u":"places/the-watchers-vault.html#the-watch","t":"At the north end of the nave is the Watch : his desk, his chair, and in front of them the Watch Wall , old sets stacked thirty-seven across and sixteen high, all showing one picture. The first time you come, he's there (the cutscene The Watch ): this is where i watch from. they watch the picture. i watch them. your world's a show to them. the worse it gets, the more of them come. they left you a ticket. it admits one. not you. something came in behind you. it's come for what i kept. the omni. the carrier. my first reel. get to them before it does. bring them here. ??? in the Watch Bring all three things back to the Watch and every set on the wall goes to one picture, and the Projectionist steps down out of them. In the last third of the fight comes the intermission: every set and every bulb goes out, there's only its lens, and \"Please remain seated.\" Burning it through earns The Final Reel . Afterwards he runs his first reel on the projector on his desk (the cutscene The First Reel ), and the Wall shows the first thing anyone ever saw on the other side. When it's over: \"Every set on the Watch Wall shows the Door at the End of the World. The static in it has gone black.\" That earns What He Kept Out and leads on to the Other Side ."},{"p":"The Watcher's Vault","h":"Its blocks","u":"places/the-watchers-vault.html#its-blocks","t":"Vault Terrazzo and The Watcher's Concrete Archive Shelf , Old Set (two Vacuum Tubes with glass, iron and redstone make two of your own, which switch on and off) and Cable Keep Door , Keep Wheel and What He Kept (the plinths) The Watch Wall"},{"p":"The Watcher's Vault","h":"Advancements here","u":"places/the-watchers-vault.html#advancements","t":"Behind the Picture : Go through the seam, into the Watcher's Vault What He Kept : Take all three things out of his keeps The Final Reel : Burn the Projectionist through What He Kept Out : See his first reel"},{"p":"Tune-In Town","h":"","u":"places/tune-in-town.html","t":"Photosensitivity warning Tune-In Town's night shift has flashing lights, flickering screens, loud noises and jumpscares. The game warns you before it starts, and once you say yes it keeps you there until you've survived five nights. If flashing images affect you, don't take the job. See also the warning on the install page . Tune-In Town Pizza & Playhouse A secret Since 1.65.0 (furnished in 1.71.1) Way in The HELP WANTED flyer, shown on an Old Set; the old place in your world; the STAFF ONLY door at its back Way out Studio B's front doors, back into the old place (once you're hired, not till you've survived five nights) Sleep No: \"You're on the clock - no sleeping on the job.\" Size One floor, about 120 blocks across The shift 12 AM to 6 AM; an hour is seventy seconds"},{"p":"Tune-In Town","h":"What it is","u":"places/tune-in-town.html#what-it-is","t":"Tune-In Town's show went out live on Channel 6 every Saturday from its own stage, its cast of animatronics running off reel-to-reel showtapes, till the Saturday the tape played HIM ( the First Signal ). It shut. Now he's opening it again. It's a secret Easter egg: a night shift in a pizza place, with twelve animatronics of its own coming for your office. The cast are on Tune-In Town's cast ."},{"p":"Tune-In Town","h":"The HELP WANTED flyer and the Old Set","u":"places/tune-in-town.html#the-flyer","t":"Since 1.65.3 the flyer is on the television, and it doesn't wait for the story: it can come any time after your first day. An Old Set that's on , one you've crafted and put down anywhere in your world, once in a long while stops showing static and shows the flyer, held up close to the camera: \"The set's stopped showing static. A flyer, held up close to the camera - yellowed, creased: HELP WANTED. TUNE-IN TOWN PIZZA & PLAYHOUSE. Then it clicks off - and the flyer's in your hand. Read it: the address.\" One dark night , out in the open, you come on a set someone's left switched on in the grass a little way in front of you, showing it. Look at it (or use it) and the set clicks off and the flyer's in your hand. On Chapter Ten's third day , while you're home, three knocks come at your door: someone's left a set on your step, facing in, on, showing static till the door's opened. Then it's the flyer. Since 1.72.2 it comes even if you've already seen the flyer or found the old place (a world past its third day gets it the next time you're home by day). The HELP WANTED Flyer reads \"Tune-In Town Pizza & Playhouse: Night Security, 12AM-6AM. Apply within. (It was on the television.)\" Use it to read the address, which way and how far: \"TUNE-IN TOWN PIZZA & PLAYHOUSE - so many blocks, that way \". When the flyer comes, the old place is there, a little way off: \"Somewhere close, the old place is there now - TUNE-IN TOWN. Read the flyer for the way.\" If there's nowhere for it yet (out at sea, up in the mountains), \"The address is nowhere near here yet - try somewhere open and dry, out of the water and off the mountains.\" It comes the moment you're somewhere open and dry."},{"p":"Tune-In Town","h":"The old place","u":"places/tune-in-town.html#the-old-place","t":"What's left of Tune-In Town in your world: shut years ago, a building about twenty-three blocks wide on a checker-tiled floor, the windows boarded, the dining room's tables and chairs where they were left, the little stage with its curtain in rags, the arcade dead, the sign over the door. Read the flyer when you get there: \"This is the place. STAFF ONLY - at the back, by the stage.\" At the back, by the stage, is a steel door that isn't rotten at all: STAFF ONLY . Through it is Studio B. Since 1.65.3 it's shut, not fallen: its roof and walls are whole, its floor level with the ground round it, nothing of the world comes through inside (no dirt, moss, gravel, rubble or cobwebs), and the trees, hillside or pond where it stands are cleared right up past its roof. Nothing of it breaks, by hand or by any blast: \"It won't break. Nothing of this place will.\" If the door won't open: \"STAFF ONLY. It won't open yet - something's moving about behind it. Try again in a moment.\""},{"p":"Tune-In Town","h":"Studio B","u":"places/tune-in-town.html#studio-b","t":"Through the STAFF ONLY door is the place as it was on television, all of it, lit and empty: \"TUNE-IN TOWN - Studio B. The real one.\" Going through earns Now Hiring . You come in at the lobby, at the front (the south). Since 1.71.1 it's furnished as a real restaurant, and since 1.65.3 it's darker: the dining hall a gloom under its high roof, the rooms off it dim, the halls near black. The front doors bring you back out into the old place. You're staff there, not a builder: you can't break or place anything (in creative you can, but not while a shift's on: \"You're on the clock - no building, no breaking.\"). Whatever was built or broken is put right when the next night starts, and anything dropped is cleared. Room Where What's there Camera The lobby The front The ticket booth; the front doors, glass either side, a doormat, EXIT over them; one of Mister Channel's TVs; benches, posters; gumball machines by the doors, the menu on the wall, balloons either side of the way in 11 The dining hall The middle, open to the roof Party tables in rows, gingham cloths, red chairs all round, and pizza, soda, balloons and the odd cake on them; diner booths in pairs along the walls; the party counter under the menus and the soda counter; gumball machines; bunting strung right across; hanging lights; posters; Mister Channel's TV on the east wall 2 The show stage The dining hall's north end Raised two blocks, its front skirted in red, steps up at each end; the curtain behind the band, the TUNE-IN TOWN sign over it, stage lights on their truss; Tempo's drums on a riser, Lulu's keyboard, Bucky's amplifier, speakers either side 1 Studio B Behind the stage, three steps down Where the show was filmed: the wall of televisions, the anchor desk, the studio cameras and lights 9 Rover's Raceway West A go-kart track painted on the floor (white lines, red and white kerbs, a grey infield with yellow chevrons), a few go-karts left where they stopped; the Pit Stop, curtained off at its north end: OUT OF ORDER 3 The arcade and the Prize Corner East Cabinets all along both walls (put a Tune-In Token in one for its little game and a prize out of the tray); the prize counter and its shelves of prizes; Jack's box in its corner, the music box on its stand, gift boxes heaped round 8 The Kids' Cove The front, south-east A real ball pit: sunk, padded round, netted over, two deep in coloured balls, an op"},{"p":"Tune-In Town","h":"After hours","u":"places/tune-in-town.html#after-hours","t":"Off the clock the cast stand at their places (on the stage, in the kitchen, behind the curtain, in the box, in the ball pit) switched on, their heads following you round the room. Come too near, make a noise or hit one, and it's awake and hunting you; lose it and it goes back to its place; kill it and it's off a few minutes, then back, rebooted. Now and then, after hours, the band on the stage go into each other and come for you as the Mended Band : \"On the stage, the band have gone into each other. There's only one of them now - and it can see you.\" All of it is on Tune-In Town's cast ."},{"p":"Tune-In Town","h":"The secret: kept till five nights","u":"places/tune-in-town.html#the-secret","t":"Since 1.65.2 the night shift is only played one way. Walk into the security office the first time and a WARNING comes up: This secret contains FLASHING LIGHTS, FLICKERING SCREENS, LOUD NOISES and JUMPSCARES. If you continue, you won't be able to play the story or the regular game until you beat this secret Easter egg: survive 5 nights on the Tune-In Town night shift. You'll be kept here - the doors won't let you out, and if you die, you'll wake up here. If you're not sure, go back. WARNING in the security office: CONTINUE / GO BACK GO BACK (or Esc): \"You back out of the office, to the lobby.\" You can look round Studio B as much as you like; the time clock won't take your card till you've said yes. CONTINUE : \"You've taken the job. Nobody goes home till they've worked 5 nights. Punch the time clock on the office wall.\" Kept: the front doors won't let you out (\"Not yet. You're staff now - so many more nights before you can go.\"), you wake up in the lobby if you die, and anything that puts you somewhere else puts you straight back. Free: 6 AM on the fifth night. \"FIVE NIGHTS. You did it - the doors are open, you're free to go. (The night shift's yours whenever you want it.)\" After that it's yours to play whenever you like, with no warning and no keeping. Anyone who'd already made it through five nights is free already."},{"p":"Tune-In Town","h":"The night shift","u":"places/tune-in-town.html#the-night-shift","t":"Punch the time clock in the security office: \"CLOCKED IN - Night 1. It's 12 AM. Your shift ends at 6.\" ( Clocked In .) The cast come for the office, each its own way, and the office TV plays Hal's orientation tape for the night: Hey, hey! Welcome to Tune-In Town - and welcome to the night shift. This is Hal. I manage the place. Managed. You'll see. Hal , on the first night's tape In the office What it does The doors and the vent Steel shutters on the west door, the east door and the vent behind you. The red DOOR button by each shuts it. The lights The white LIGHT button by each way in lights the hall outside for a few seconds a press. \"The lights are how you see who's there.\" The monitor Fifteen cameras you really look through: click the map (a small panel in the corner, with a dot for you) or press 1-9, 0 or the arrow keys. FLASH Since 1.71.1, the button or F: lights up the room the camera's on for a moment, for half a percent of your power. REBOOT The button or R on the monitor. From the third night (the second, before 1.71.1) HIS static is in one of tonight's cast, and nothing tells you which: it twitches, its eyes go red, its camera stutters, the office lights go when it's near, you hear it breathing behind the door. Reboot the right one (five seconds of static on the cameras) and \"HIS STATIC'S GONE OUT OF\" it; the wrong one costs 5% of your power and locks the system for twenty seconds. A door Chef Pete jams open, and Mister Channel's static on the cameras, are rebooted the same way. The music box In the Prize Corner: hold the button on camera 8 to wind it. Let it run down and Jack's out. The office TV Hal's tape each night (spoken since 1.71.2; switch it off and he's cut off mid-word). If Mister Channel's face comes up on it, switch it off, quick. Power A battery that drains cell by cell, amber then red. Doors shut, lights on and the cameras cost it, and the place itself more each night. At 0% the doors open, the lights go, and someone comes to the door, singing. Leaving the office: since 1.72.1, out of it more than three seconds and tonight's cast are off the show and after you, anywhere in the building (\"You left the office. They're off the show - and coming for you. Get back, shut the doors, make it to 6 AM.\"). Get back in and shut the doors on them, or keep ahead of them; make it to 6 AM and the night's still yours. While they're loose nothing you "},{"p":"Tune-In Town","h":"Who comes, and what stops them","u":"places/tune-in-town.html#who-comes","t":"Who What to watch for Tony Tune Moves only while nobody's watching him (he comes east) Bucky Beaver Gnaws the west door, and your power goes Lulu Lark Comes the long way round, through the kitchen, and knocks on the west door when she isn't there Tempo the Tortoise Beats his drum a step at a time: count them Rusty Rover Watch him on camera 3, or he comes out from behind the curtain and runs for the west door (shut it; he bangs) Mister Channel Hops from screen to screen (the cameras go to static), then his face is on your TV: switch it off Jack Jangle Keep the music box wound Spare Parts Crawls the vent: the vent light sends it back Chef Pete Light him and he goes back to the kitchen; shut the door on him and he jams it open The Employee of the Month Never shows on the cameras, only static where he is: listen for him (\"Hello?\") Tix Leave a door open and he steals your power and your monitor; the third time, it's you The Encore The sixth night only: the screen glitches, red on the side it's coming from. Shut that way, now HIS static's one ignores all of that: the doors, the lights and the cameras don't send it back, the music box won't wind with HIM in Jack, and the TV won't stay off with HIM in Mister Channel."},{"p":"Tune-In Town","h":"The nights and the Custom Night","u":"places/tune-in-town.html#the-nights","t":"Nights one to five get harder: since 1.71.1 the first is three of them, gently, the second five, and the rest ramp up to the sixth. None of them stirs for the first moments of a night, longest on the first two. Beating the fifth is beating the secret. The sixth night is the Encore's, there for the brave once you've lasted five ( Overtime : \"Make it through the sixth night - and the Encore\"). Picking a night: sneak and use the time clock to pick which unlocked night your next shift is (\"Next shift: Night 3 (sneak + use the clock to change - Night 4 is the newest)\"); after the newest it goes back round to Night 1. After 6 AM it's the newest again. The Custom Night , once the sixth is beaten: sneak and use the clock till it says CUSTOM NIGHT, then use it. Set how hard each of the twelve comes, from 0 (not at all) to 20 (shift-click goes by 5; ALL 0, ALL 20), and START. It's paid by how hard it was. Beating it with every one on 20 earns Twenty Twenty ."},{"p":"Tune-In Town","h":"On a server","u":"places/tune-in-town.html#on-servers","t":"Since 1.66.6 the night shift is everyone's. The time clock won't punch till everyone on the server is in the security office and has taken the job (\"Everyone clocks in together - waiting on them to come to the security office.\"), and those it's waiting on are told they're wanted. Then you're all on the clock together, on the night the furthest behind of you is up to: one power, one set of doors and lights, one music box, and each of you your own monitor (any of you can wind the box or run a REBOOT). Whoever gets in gets the one of you nearest it: they're out, thrown out to the lobby, and the rest keep going. It's only lost if it gets all of you, or the power goes. Make it to 6 AM and the night is everyone's who clocked in, caught or not: all paid, all on to the next night together. Walk off the job and you're off the shift (if you were the last, they come after you). Picking a night goes as far as the whole server has unlocked; the Custom Night once everyone's beaten the sixth."},{"p":"Tune-In Town","h":"What it pays","u":"places/tune-in-town.html#rewards","t":"For You get Every night Emeralds and Tune-In Tokens (for the arcade's cabinets) Nights one to five A plush each: Tony Tune, Bucky Beaver, Lulu Lark, Tempo the Tortoise, Rusty Rover. Put them on a shelf; give one a squeeze The fifth night The Employee Badge ; the Security Card (after hours the cast take no notice of you; swipe it to go to Studio B from anywhere, and back; hostile eyes show red through the dark); the Security Flashlight ; a gold star on the time clock The sixth night The Encore plush; the Showtape , a music disc (\"Tune-In Town - The Showtape (Saturday's)\"); the Night Guard's Cap and Jacket ; a gold star Each Custom Night beaten One of the other plushes; with every one of them on 20, Tony in gold, and the third gold star All three stars \"★★★ ALL THREE STARS. Tune-In Town is yours.\" The Showstopper , Golden Tony's Music Box and the Owner's Key ; the cast wave and say \"Hi, boss!\", the Mended Band never comes for you, and the band will play the show live for you (use the stage's curtain after hours) The Owner's Key also takes you into Studio B from anywhere, makes Studio B where you wake up (use it there again to undo it), and used on the time clock lists everyone online who isn't there: click one and they're asked in. What each reward does is on the items page ."},{"p":"Tune-In Town","h":"Commands","u":"places/tune-in-town.html#commands","t":"/statichollow locate tune_in_town and /statichollow locate flyer_tv (since 1.66.7): where the old place is, and the Old Set that last showed the flyer. Click the answer to go there. If the old place isn't anywhere yet, asking from the Overworld sets it down near you; if no set's showing the flyer, one's left on near you. /statichollow goto tune_in_town (or flyer_tv ): takes you there, onto the ground (in front of the Old Set, looking at it). /locate structure statichollow:tune_in_town and statichollow:flyer_tv find them too. /statichollow tunein release <players> (for server operators): lets someone out without beating it. /statichollow tunein skipnights [players] (with cheats on, since 1.72.1): all six nights behind you and straight to the Custom Night, with what the nights would have given you: \"All six nights, behind you. The Custom Night's open - pick it on the clock.\""},{"p":"Tune-In Town","h":"Advancements here","u":"places/tune-in-town.html#advancements","t":"Now Hiring : Go through the STAFF ONLY door into Studio B Clocked In : Start a night shift at Tune-In Town 6 AM : Make it through a night shift You're Fired : Get jumpscared on the night shift Have You Tried Turning It Off? : On the night shift, reboot the one HIS static's in Overtime : Make it through the sixth night - and the Encore Disbanded : Take apart the Mended Band Twenty Twenty : Beat a Custom Night with every one of them on 20 The Owner : Win all three gold stars on Tune-In Town's time clock Encore for One : Have the band play the whole show, just for you"},{"p":"Chapter one: The Nine","h":"","u":"story/chapter-1.html","t":"You find a ruined shrine with a soul campfire burning at it, and you touch the altar. From then on, nine creepypastas hunt everyone in the world, mostly in the dark, and something tall stands at the edge of your sight and watches you kill them."},{"p":"Chapter one: The Nine","h":"The Forsaken Altar","u":"story/chapter-1.html#the-forsaken-altar","t":"Every world has a Forsaken Altar, 500 to 1000 blocks from the world spawn. It always stands on open, flat, dry ground, never underground, in water or on a mountainside, and on the far side of spawn from the cathedral. Follow the blue smoke from its soul campfire. The ruin rises around the altar once you come within about 90 blocks: broken pillars, skulls, candles, graves and splashes of blood, built from the mod's own hollow stone, ossuary bricks of bone and rotten planks. It clears every tree, bush and bump of ground in its way as it goes up. Around it (since 1.40) stand nine pilgrim stones , each carved with the sign of one of the Nine. The pilgrims' camp is abandoned nearby, with one of their diaries, and a sealing stone by the shrine covers a stair down to the catacomb where the first pilgrims lie. It stays shut until the altar wakes. At night pilgrims kneel round the altar; come close and they fade away, and sometimes leave something behind. Right-click the altar with an empty hand to wake it. There is no going back after that. Read the pilgrim's diary on the lore page . Find the altar with /locate structure statichollow:forsaken_altar if you're testing with cheats on."},{"p":"Chapter one: The Nine","h":"The nine creepypastas","u":"story/chapter-1.html#the-nine","t":"Once the altar is awake the nine hunt everyone, mostly in the dark. Each one fights its own way, has its own sounds and its own death, and drops its own material, which is what the chapter's weapons and armour are made from. Creepypasta What to know Drops Hollow Neighbor Hostile to players only. Stalks you, knocks on doors, messages you in chat pretending to be a friend, and rises up behind your window to say it to your face. Hollow Knuckle Stitchjaw Hostile to everything. Crawls flat and climbs walls. Every bite opens the wound further (Bleeding I, II, III). Stitched Sinew Weeping Shepherd Neutral, but fights back. Weeps, stares if you stare, hunts the undead. Shepherd's Tear Lullaby Mother Neutral by day, hostile at night. Steals villagers. Her hits can drag you into the Hollow, a sealed black room under the world, for 15 seconds. Rusted Lullaby Key Broadcast A man with a CRT television for a head. Don't look at it (it burns) and don't touch it (it shocks). Its antennae glow green once it has seen you. Static Shard Little Lamb A crying child that follows you. Hit it and it shows its real face. Bloodied Wool The Hymnal Floats. Its song slows and weakens you and heals the other creepypastas. Hymnal Page The Underneath Waits buried with only its hands showing, and breathes under your bed. Grave Claw Antlerkin Imitates cows, pigs and sheep to lure prey, and at night it calls and runs its prey down. Antler Shard Heads. The first time you kill each one, it always drops its head. After that it's a 10% chance, plus 5% a level of Looting (25% with Looting III). Only a kill by a player counts, an arrow from your bow included, and in multiplayer each player gets their own first head. You need one head from each of the nine."},{"p":"Chapter one: The Nine","h":"Under the bed","u":"story/chapter-1.html#under-the-bed","t":"The Underneath deserves its own warning. Once the altar is awake, about four times in ten that you lie down, and always the next time after you've heard it breathing, it comes up under your bed: three knocks under the floor, then its hands feel for the edge of the mattress. The night won't pass while it's there. Get out of bed within about four seconds (Leave Bed) and it bursts up out of the floor to fight you. Stay, and its arms come up over you and it drags you down through the bed and eats you. In the dark you may see it waiting under a bed: two pale eyes and long fingers creeping out. It never comes in Creative or on Peaceful."},{"p":"Chapter one: The Nine","h":"The Watcher","u":"story/chapter-1.html#the-watcher","t":"The Watcher never attacks. It stares, waves, points, peeks round things, crouches, and sometimes stands right behind you. It speaks after your first kill, your fifth and your ninth, and again when the Saint rises and when it falls. you shouldn't have done that, [your name]. it was only watching you. like i do. i'll remember this. ??? after your first kill five. you're counting too, aren't you [your name]? i know where you sleep. i've known for a while. ??? after your fifth kill nine. do you know what nine heads are for? there is a church that isn't on any map. find it. i'll be on the ceiling. ??? after your ninth kill"},{"p":"Chapter one: The Nine","h":"The church that isn't on any map","u":"story/chapter-1.html#the-church","t":"The church is the Cathedral of the Hollow : one per world, 500 to 1000 blocks from spawn, roughly the opposite way from the altar. It rises out of nothing once you come within about 90 blocks of where it stands, inside a walled graveyard. The Watcher hangs from the ceiling of the nave, as it said it would. In the sanctuary is the Hollow Reliquary with nine head pedestals around it. Since 1.40 there is much more underneath: an undercroft of tombs, the priest's study, a flooded charnel pit and, at its end, the Saint's tomb, empty, its chains broken."},{"p":"Chapter one: The Nine","h":"The Hollow Saint","u":"story/chapter-1.html#the-hollow-saint","t":"Put one head from each of the nine different creepypastas on the pedestals, then right-click the reliquary with an empty hand. The summoning takes about ten seconds: a circle of runes burns open in the floor, a beam of light streams out of every head into an orb over the reliquary, and the Saint rises up out of the ground and roars with many dead voices at once. look up. i told you i'd be here. this is what they were all pieces of. ??? as the Saint rises The full fight, its dark form and Abyssal Rupture are on the Hollow Saint's page . When it dies, the Watcher won't let it stay: its beam burns a portal to hell open under the Saint, and a huge burning hand drags it down. you did it. do you understand what you've done? they were keeping it in. it was the only thing in this world bigger than me. thank you. i'll be seeing you. all of you. i always have. ??? after \"The Hollow Saint has fallen.\""},{"p":"Chapter one: The Nine","h":"What you can make","u":"story/chapter-1.html#what-you-can-make","t":"The nine's drops make the chapter's weapons and three armour sets. The Saint's own drops finish the job: its heart goes into the Saint's Requiem, and its shrouds upgrade the last armour set. Recipes are in the items section . Weapons: the Sinew Cleaver (Rend), the Antler Scythe (Reap), the Static Blade (Dead Air) and the Saint's Requiem (Last Rites), which needs the Saint's Heart. Armour: Stitchskin (Sewn Shut), Antlerbone (Night Hunter) and Static Mail (Dead Channel). Upgrade each Static Mail piece at a smithing table with a Saint's Shroud and a Hymnal Page to make the Saint's Vestments (Hollow Grace)."},{"p":"Chapter one: The Nine","h":"What comes next","u":"story/chapter-1.html#what-comes-next","t":"Where the Saint fell, the floor tears open into a red wound standing up out of the ground. That is the Breach ."},{"p":"Chapter ten: Stay Tuned","h":"","u":"story/chapter-10.html","t":"You come home, and it cuts in on you: a tone, static, black. In the Hub, the First Signal takes his hands off the wall. He doesn't need it any more. He has a kingdom of his own, and a map of your world on his table. Chapter Ten arrived in 1.64.0, and 1.64.1, 1.64.2 and 1.67.0 made it worse. The title card reads CHAPTER TEN , STAY TUNED , they're coming , and the chapter's own music is Stay Tuned . From 1.68.0 its story goes on in The Last Broadcast ."},{"p":"Chapter ten: Stay Tuned","h":"The Broadcast","u":"story/chapter-10.html#the-broadcast","t":"Once the Harbinger has gone through its way out, the next time you're home (back at your bed or your spawn in the Overworld, or home by the Remote), it cuts in on you, for everyone in the Overworld: a tone, static, black. A cutscene in three parts, with its own score ( On Air and Get Ready )."},{"p":"Chapter ten: Stay Tuned","h":"The wall","u":"story/chapter-10.html#the-wall","t":"In the Hub , the First Signal is at the wall the Watcher shut on him, both hands flat on the static. He stops. His head tilts. Then the rage: a scream of many voices through a dead channel, the wall bulging, his fists on it. He turns his back on it, lifts a hand, tears his own way open, colour bars and black, and walks into it."},{"p":"Chapter ten: Stay Tuned","h":"His kingdom","u":"story/chapter-10.html#his-kingdom","t":"A still black sea, in a realm made of his static: it crawls in the walls of the world, far off all round. On the sea stands his castle of black static-stone, dead television sets in its walls, red lamps up its towers and its mast. Under the water, all round, are the windows : every realm he's touched, each one lit, a cable running from each to his castle. He comes out of his tear on the platform and walks the causeway, and his Faithful go down on their faces as he goes by. The water heaves, and the Harbinger comes up out of it, hung on its strings. He speaks to it: The First Signal, to the Harbinger look at you. you went down an animal. you came up mine. stronger. so much stronger. It lowers its skull to his hand. In his war hall his servants stand round his table, a map of your world on it. He puts his hand on it, and its lights spring up all over it. The First Signal, at his war table it's time. find them. both of them. take them off the air. His gate opens, and his creations pour out, down the causeway and into the windows. Into yours. The whole place is on his kingdom ; everything he says is on The First Signal speaks ."},{"p":"Chapter ten: Stay Tuned","h":"Your house","u":"story/chapter-10.html#your-house","t":"Your door bangs open (the nearest door to where you are; with none near, he's simply there, since 1.72.1 somewhere he can actually stand): the Watcher, out of breath. do you feel that? it's everywhere. all over the world, all at once. that much signal - all of it his. get ready. ??? at your door CHAPTER TEN , STAY TUNED , they're coming . That's Stay Tuned (\"See what he did after the Hub - and what he let out\"), and the chat says: \"Chapter Ten: Stay Tuned. His creations are out - they see you, they hear you. Hide: lockers, under beds, crouched in the tall grass.\""},{"p":"Chapter ten: Stay Tuned","h":"The invasion","u":"story/chapter-10.html#the-invasion","t":"The first of them come for you a few seconds after, near home. Every night after (and any time you're down in the caves) the broadcast goes out round you, a tone far off (\"...the broadcast goes out.\"), and they come: more each night you've lived through, up to ten, out of the dark and out of your sight. By day there are Lookalikes, near villages and herds. They're his own, nobody else's: the Longplay , a person drawn out like a chewed-up tape, eleven feet tall, that pauses when you watch it; the Hanger , folded the wrong way, up walls and over roofs; the Lookalike , a villager, a cow, a pig, a sheep, a chicken or the Watcher, a few moments behind itself; and ERR , the broken script, a body in slices with errors in your chat. Over them are his three servants, bosses each: the Announcer , the Cameraman and the Stagehand . Since 1.64.1 they hunt together: one sees you, its head snaps round, it shrieks, and every one of his for thirty blocks comes. All of them are on his creations and servants . They see you and they hear you. Each has a cone of sight, shorter in the dark, much shorter if you're crouched, and crouched in tall plants it can't make you out past a few blocks. They hear you sprint, jump and land, break and place blocks, open doors, fight and eat, and come to look. The nearer one is to finding you, the faster and louder your heartbeat, and his static creeps in at the edges of your eyes. Since 1.67.0 they climb walls after you if you're above them (not his servants), and stuck, they claw through wood, glass, earth, leaves or wool (stone and iron hold them)."},{"p":"Chapter ten: Stay Tuned","h":"Tonight on Channel Zero","u":"story/chapter-10.html#tonight-on-channel-zero","t":"Since 1.67.0 each night of Chapter Ten has its own programme, never last night's again, told as the night comes in: TONIGHT ON CHANNEL ZERO . Programme What it says What it means THE SIEGE \"They know where you live. They're gathering out there - and they'll come all at once.\" More of them, gathering out of sight. Once enough are out there (or a minute into the night), every one comes at once, from every side: \"Every one of them, all at once - from every side.\" THE STALKING \"Quiet tonight. Don't look back - and if you do, it won't be there.\" Fewer, and quiet: no shriek when one sees you. Look at one and it's gone behind something; look away and it's nearer. THE CHASE \"Tonight they run. And they don't give up.\" More of them, a quarter faster, and they keep after you three times as long once they've lost you. THE AMBUSH \"They're already here. Waiting in the dark for you to come to them.\" Already close, stock still in the dark, facing your way, till you're on top of them. THE IMPOSTORS \"Trust nothing out there tonight. Not even a knock at the door.\" Mostly Lookalikes, throwing their voices to make you look the wrong way, and something knocks at your door wearing the Watcher."},{"p":"Chapter ten: Stay Tuned","h":"The first days","u":"story/chapter-10.html#the-first-days","t":"Since 1.67.0 he doesn't leave the first ones to chance: The first time you step out of doors by day after the Broadcast, his transmitter comes up out of the ground right in front of you: \"Out there the ground splits open - and something comes up out of it, red lamps climbing its mast. His.\" The first time you're down in a cave , his burrow is eaten out of the rock near you: \"Somewhere in the rock near you, something is eating its way through. You can hear it chewing toward you.\" On the third night (two of his nights lived through), the first time you're out of doors in the dark, his first set goes up out there in front of you (always, since 1.72.2): \"Out there in the dark, studio lights come on, one after another. Someone's built a set - and there are people standing about on it, waiting.\" On the third day , while you're home, three knocks at your door. Someone's left a set on your step, facing in, switched on, showing static till the door's opened. Then it's the flyer: see Tune-In Town ."},{"p":"Chapter ten: Stay Tuned","h":"His sites","u":"story/chapter-10.html#his-sites","t":"His sites come through into your world after it, each kept by one of his servants, and each with a Broadcast Core . Break the core and the site goes off the air (\"...and off the air.\"): its lamps go out, it calls nothing more, and the core gives up what it was burning. Their chests hold the best of what he brought. A keeper you've killed doesn't come back. Site Where and when Its keeper A transmitter Rises up out of the ground every ten-odd minutes, a long way off: its mast's red lamps on the skyline at night, its hum. His creations come out of it at night. \"Something's started broadcasting, out there.\" The Announcer A burrow Eaten out of the rock near you down in the caves: Hangers on its roof, blackout ore in its walls, lockers in it, a tunnel from it into your caves (since 1.72.1 all the way to where you were). \"Something's eating its way through the rock near you.\" The Cameraman A set At night, out in the open: the front of a house and nothing behind it, studio lights, a camera (its core is the camera's eye), Lookalikes standing about being people. \"Somewhere out there, someone's building a set.\" The Stagehand Breaking a core is Pulled the Plug ; killing a keeper is Off His Air ."},{"p":"Chapter ten: Stay Tuned","h":"Hiding","u":"story/chapter-10.html#hiding","t":"The chat told you how: lockers, under beds, crouched in the tall grass. The Steel Locker (iron and bars): get in and pull the door to. You see out through its vents and nothing sees in. Under a bed: crouch and use any bed. Crouched in tall plants (grass, ferns, bushes, leaves, crops): they can't make you out past a few blocks. One that's searching may come and stand at your hiding place, listening, sniffing. If it heard you in there, or saw you go in, it tears it open and drags you out; make a sound and it has you. Blackout is what you fight him with, the strongest gear there is: Signal Fragments from his creations, Blackout Shards from his servants, his cores and the blackout ore his static seeps into deep down. The Blackout Blade's Signal Cut tears at everything of his in front of you; its tools are silent; each piece of its armour makes you quieter, and the whole set is silent, with Lights Out (tap sneak twice) to throw everything hunting you down and vanish for ten seconds. See Gear for every chapter ."},{"p":"Chapter ten: Stay Tuned","h":"The Watcher at your house","u":"story/chapter-10.html#the-watcher-at-your-house","t":"He stays. Anything of the First Signal's that comes near your house, the Watcher strikes down. He can be fooled by a Lookalike, though, and on THE IMPOSTORS something else comes knocking wearing him."},{"p":"Chapter ten: Stay Tuned","h":"A way in","u":"story/chapter-10.html#a-way-in","t":"Since 1.64.2 there's a way into his kingdom . Break the Broadcast Core in one of his sites and his signal's torn open where it stood, a tear like the one he comes through, colour bars rolling in it, its edges crackling, for a minute: \"Where it stood, his signal's torn open. It won't stay that way long.\" Step into it and you're on his platform at the end of the causeway, his castle across the black water: \"His kingdom. Behind you, the way back.\" Behind you is a redder tear, the way back to just where you were. While you're his guest his realm doesn't throw you out ( His Guest ), but \"You can't sleep here. Not in his kingdom.\" Nothing's quiet there. His Faithful, his congregation in robes of a red so dark it's nearly black, keep his rites in circles of candles; their hoods turn after you, and hurt one and every one of them for 24 blocks runs at you. Whispering just behind you, footsteps coming up behind you and stopping, a music box winding down, someone crying through the walls. Since 1.67.0 his sea goes down two hundred blocks, and the windows stand on rock pillars up out of the deep. The first time you go through, he notices. That's where The Last Broadcast begins."},{"p":"Chapter ten: Stay Tuned","h":"Tune-In Town","u":"story/chapter-10.html#tune-in-town","t":"Tune-In Town Pizza & Playhouse's show went out live on Channel 6 every Saturday from its own stage, its cast of animatronics running off reel-to-reel showtapes, till the Saturday the tape played him . It shut. Now he's opening it again. It's a secret, an Easter egg (1.65.0 to 1.65.5, furnished and voiced in 1.71), and it doesn't wait for this chapter: since 1.65.3 it can turn up any time after your first day. Once in a long while an Old Set that's switched on stops showing static and shows a yellowed HELP WANTED flyer held up close to the camera, or one dark night you'll come on a set left on in the grass a little way in front of you, showing it. In Chapter Ten it also comes to your door on the third day. Look at the set and it clicks off, and the flyer's in your hand: it gives you the address. What's left of the old place has a steel door at the back by the stage that isn't rotten at all: STAFF ONLY. Through it is Studio B , the place as it was on television, and right at the back, the security office. The first time you walk in there, a WARNING comes up (read the photosensitivity warning before you go): flashing lights, flickering screens, loud noises and jumpscares, and if you go on, you're kept there and can't play the story or the rest of the game until you've survived five nights of the night shift. Twelve of the cast come for the office, each its own way, and from the third night (since 1.71.1; it was the second) his static is in one of them. Hal, the old manager, talks you through it on the office TV: his tapes are word for word on Tapes and broadcasts. The place is on Tune-In Town , and the twelve on Tune-In Town's cast ."},{"p":"Chapter ten: Stay Tuned","h":"What comes next","u":"story/chapter-10.html#what-comes-next","t":"\"find them. both of them.\" He has his map, his creations are out, and you've found the way into his house. He doesn't want you there: The Last Broadcast ."},{"p":"Chapter two: The Breach","h":"","u":"story/chapter-2.html","t":"When the Hollow Saint falls, the floor where it fell tears open. The creepypastas were keeping something in; now there's a hole, and it's been widening ever since. you didn't think that was the end of it, did you. when the saint fell it left a hole. it's been widening ever since. ??? after the Saint falls"},{"p":"Chapter two: The Breach","h":"The Breach","u":"story/chapter-2.html#the-breach","t":"A red wound stands up out of the ground: black inside, its edges burning, red lightning crawling off it, ash drifting round it and the air pulling in. In a world where the Saint already fell before this was added, one tears open near you soon after you play. Walk into it."},{"p":"Chapter two: The Breach","h":"The Void","u":"story/chapter-2.html#the-void","t":"Since 1.25 the Breach lets out into its own dimension: black all round, no ground and no sky, a fog the colour of a bruise, ash and embers drifting, a drone that never stops, and things moving out in the dark. Now and then, far out, two great red eyes open and look at you. You can't sleep out here. You come out on one torn-off island: pale dead moss over an upturned crag of earth and rose stone, crystals and roots hanging off it, dead trees leaning over the edge, and the Breach Altar's shrine on top. Four more pieces of the Hollow hang in the dark round it, the Drift , each with a chest and a page, all reachable on foot: The Torn Room (east, over a sagging rope bridge): the corner of a house ripped off at the floor, the bed unmade, a table laid for two, a music box playing somewhere. The Fallen Graves (west, over stepping stones): a lump of graveyard and a little mausoleum, its coffins sticking out of the earth underneath. The Mast (south): the Broadcast's radio mast, a red aviation light blinking on top that you can see from all over the Void, and a shed with a TV still on. The Nest (north): the carcass of something huge, a ring of standing stones round a black pool, sculk over everything. The lampreys come up out of the pool. If you fall, your fall slows as if the dark thickened, and a hand bigger than a man comes up out of it, closes round you (it hurts), and sets you back down on the island you fell from. Out here you'll also meet Driftlights , harmless jellyfish of pale flesh that light the islands, and Lampreys , eyeless eels with a glowing lure that bite and try to drag you out over the dark. careful. there's no ground out here but this. this is where they came up from. the breach tore this bit off with it. and don't look too long at the dark. it looks back. ??? in the Void"},{"p":"Chapter two: The Breach","h":"The Breach Altar","u":"story/chapter-2.html#the-breach-altar","t":"The Breach Altar is the Forsaken Altar's other half: a platform of pale rose stone, spires of pink crystal, pink candles round a pink altar with a torn eye carved in it. Wake it with an empty hand and everything turns purple: every crystal, every flame, every vein in the stone. Every creepypasta in the world is dragged back down where it came from, each one sinking into a red portal, fighting. The old haunting stops. The Watcher comes to stand behind the altar and tells you what comes up in their place, in its own way: a rabbit with an axe. a hook on the roof of your car. a butcher in a pig's face. a doll that moves when nobody looks. a scarecrow that wasn't there yesterday. red eyes on a bridge. the thirteenth child. something on two legs that should be on four. a tall glowing thing in the hills. ??? at the Breach Altar (paraphrased from the README) Once the altar is awake and you come back through, the rift turns, shudders and zips itself shut behind you for good. Anyone still out in the Void is brought home."},{"p":"Chapter two: The Breach","h":"The killers and the things from the woods","u":"story/chapter-2.html#the-killers-and-the-things-from-the-woods","t":"The new nine are five killers and four cryptids. Like the creepypastas they stalk first, at the treeline, across the water, overhead, and only come for you once they've watched long enough or you hit them. Each drops its own item and its head (always on the first kill, then 10% plus Looting). The Watcher has something to say the first time you kill each. Creature How it hunts Drops The Bunnyman A tall man in a filthy rabbit suit with a fire axe. Catch him watching and he waves. Chops through wooden doors. Anywhere in the dark, most of all near water. Bloodied Stuffing The Hookman Flings a meat hook on a chain and reels you in; pulls riders off horses, boats and carts. Rusted Hook The Hogshead A butcher in a rotting pig's head. Charges; sidestep and he stuns himself on the wall. 90 health. Flayed Hide The Porcelain Man Only moves while nobody is looking. Can only be hurt from behind. Porcelain Shards The Harvestman A scarecrow on a post in a field at night. Look away for long and the post is empty. Blighted Straw Mothman Red eyes circling in the night sky. Screeches, dives, and sometimes carries you up and lets go. Bring a bow. Moth Scales The Jersey Devil Screams, springs into the air and glides down onto you. Pine forests and woods at night. Devil's Horn Dogman Runs on all fours, stands up to howl (it roots you), pounces and mauls. Dogman's Fang The Flatwoods Monster Glides at you in a spade-shaped hood with a glowing red face, leaving a burning mist. Braxton Residue"},{"p":"Chapter two: The Breach","h":"The Murder Mansion","u":"story/chapter-2.html#the-murder-mansion","t":"The Watcher tells you where they live. The Murder Mansion is a three-storey Second Empire house under a black mansard roof, with a turret, a widow's walk and a chimney still smoking, in its own railed yard: a fountain of blood, dead hedges, things hanging from dead trees, the family plot. Inside are a foyer with twin staircases, a dining hall laid for guests who are only skulls now, a butcher's kitchen, a nursery, a bathtub full of blood, the red room and the attic. The house's papers are where they were left. Read them in order and you learn what the Hale family did: the housekeeper's accounts, the butcher's order book, a letter never sent, a nursery rhyme that counts the nine, the guest list, a surveyor's notes, a note from the glasshouse, the red room's instructions, and the Watcher's own pages on the mending, open on the library desk. They're all on the lore page . Through the Harvest Doors is the Trophy Hall : chains and hooks out of the dark, trophies on every wall, and the Mending Altar inside a horseshoe of nine trophy pedestals."},{"p":"Chapter two: The Breach","h":"The Mended","u":"story/chapter-2.html#the-mended","t":"Put one head from each of the new nine on the trophy pedestals and right-click the Mending Altar with an empty hand. The Watcher comes down from the ceiling and sews. It takes about thirty seconds, and nothing can hurt the result until it stands and roars with all nine voices. The Mended is four blocks tall, 750 health, with three phases: Agony, Aggression and Iron Will. When it dies it comes apart and the nine go up out of it. It leaves the Mended Heart and the Rusted Garden Key , with iron, chains and one of each of the nine's drops."},{"p":"Chapter two: The Breach","h":"What you can make","u":"story/chapter-2.html#what-you-can-make","t":"Six weapons: the Bunnyman's Fire Axe (Bridge Toll), Hook and Chain (Reel), the Hogshead's Tenderizer (Tenderize), the Porcelain Needle (Unseen), the Devil's Glaive (Hellfire) and the Rending Claws (Frenzy). Three armour sets: Butcher's Garb (Slaughterhouse), Mothwing (Night Flight) and Braxton Shell (Braxton Mist). Recipes and powers are on the items page ."},{"p":"Chapter two: The Breach","h":"What comes next","u":"story/chapter-2.html#what-comes-next","t":"The Mended's key fits the gate of the Botanic Gardens, a Victorian glasshouse that has been locked and sealed the whole time, with the jungle inside pressed up against the glass and something glowing in the middle of it. When the Mended dies, the Watcher has something to say about the glass house. Chapter three ."},{"p":"Chapter three: The Glasshouse","h":"","u":"story/chapter-3.html","t":"The Head Gardener tended the great flower under the dome for so long that it grew into him. Now he kneels at it with a root running from its heart into his face, and the flower is only a finger of something far, far bigger."},{"p":"Chapter three: The Glasshouse","h":"The Botanic Gardens","u":"story/chapter-3.html#the-botanic-gardens","t":"The Botanic Gardens are a Victorian glasshouse under a great glass dome, locked and sealed since chapter two. Bring the Mended's Rusted Garden Key to the glass doors and it turns all the way at last: the key goes in, turns hard, the padlock springs, the chain slides off and the gate swings in screaming on its hinges. The whole glasshouse breathes out spores, petals and warm air. Inside, the jungle has grown wild. Every flower does something when you brush it: the Whispering Lily says your name and the dark comes in, the Ghost Orchid fades you out, the Watching Fern's eyes open and everything sees you, the Lantern Pod lights up your eyes, the Weeping Bell weeps on you. Giant Venus flytraps grow in the beds and snatch you up and chew (mash E to force the jaws open). Burstpods go off in clouds of choking spores, and Clutchvines close on you and hold. While you walk it the place plays with you: lilies say your name, specimen jars topple off their barrels and smash, rusted sprinklers cough and spray, glass cracks overhead, a Rootling darts across the path and is gone into the ground. And while the Gardener still kneels, sometimes he isn't at his flower at all, but standing among the trees watching you, and gone when you look again."},{"p":"Chapter three: The Glasshouse","h":"What to find first","u":"story/chapter-3.html#what-to-find-first","t":"The Head Gardener's office: his journal on the lectern and a chest with his coat and breeches . The potting shed: a chest with his straw hat and boots . The Seed Vault: under a hatch at the back of the hall, with the under-gardener's ledger and the best chest in the place. A propagation house, and a pond with something at the bottom of it. Together the four pieces are the Gardener's Weeds . You will need the full set for what comes after him. If a chest was already opened, craft the set instead from Knotted Roots, which the Rootlings drop."},{"p":"Chapter three: The Glasshouse","h":"The Gardener","u":"story/chapter-3.html#the-gardener","t":"He kneels at the great flower and doesn't notice you at first. Walk softly. Go too close to him or to the flower, or strike him, and he tears loose and stands, and the gates slam shut behind you. He is slow and huge, with hedge shears as long as a man held in both hands. Keep out of reach of the shears but not so far that he lashes you in with his root arm, and step off the ground wherever earth bubbles, because thorns come up there. At half his health he drives his hands into the ground, the glasshouse answers him, and he can't be hurt while it does. After that, stay out of the pollen, kill the Rootlings he calls up, and keep moving across the lines of thorns. Full details are on the Gardener's page . When he dies he drops his shears, goes down on his knees, bows and goes down into the ground, and the great flower drags him in and eats him. He leaves the Gardener's Shears (Prune) and the Heartbloom , all that was left of the flower's heart, still beating. If everyone inside leaves or dies, he goes back to his flower healed and the gates open again."},{"p":"Chapter three: The Glasshouse","h":"The green rift","u":"story/chapter-3.html#the-green-rift","t":"Three days after the Gardener dies , by the world's clock (nights you sleep through count), a green tear opens over his withered flower under the dome. You need to be at the glasshouse, within about 80 blocks of the flower, for it to open. It looks like the Breach, but sick green, with carrion flies boiling out of it. the flower isn't dead. that thing under the glass was only a finger of it. it's opened a way down to the rest. his clothes. wear his clothes in there, or it'll be eating you before you've taken ten steps. ??? when the green rift opens"},{"p":"Chapter three: The Glasshouse","h":"The Bloom","u":"story/chapter-3.html#the-bloom","t":"Through the rift is the Bloom : a realm with no ground and no sky, green fog all the way down, and hanging in it, everything the flower has eaten. A street of Rosemont. The research station that studied it. Shelter No. 4, sunk in its island with roots through the roof. Each has a chest and a lectern with its story. The air eats you. Without the full Gardener's Weeds you're infected the moment you arrive, and after twenty seconds it starts eating you, slowly and then faster. In his clothes the flies settle and lift off again. Don't fall. Far down under the islands is the Great Bloom itself, its mouth wider than all the islands together, ring after ring of teeth turning against each other in its throat. Fall and a tentacle twenty blocks thick comes straight up after you and drags you into its mouth. this is what it ate. a street. the laboratory that studied it. a shelter full of people. it keeps them up here like a larder. and it's down there. look down. no - don't. if you fall, it catches you. it doesn't let go. ??? in the Bloom"},{"p":"Chapter three: The Glasshouse","h":"The Binding","u":"story/chapter-3.html#the-binding","t":"The stone on the island you arrive on is the Binding , and it holds the flower down. Read the plaque on the lectern beside it first. Touch the stone with an empty hand and the chains strain and it warns you. Touch it again and it breaks. The Great Bloom goes mad, thrashing and shrieking, and its tentacles come up out of the green round the island and take hold. You have ten seconds , counted down on your screen, to get back through the rift before the island's edges break away and it pulls the whole island into its mouth, rift and all. Anyone left out there is taken, one by one. the stone in the middle is what holds it down. leave it. please. no. NO - that was holding it down- the rift. RUN. ??? at the Binding"},{"p":"Chapter three: The Glasshouse","h":"It comes up the root","u":"story/chapter-3.html#it-comes-up-the-root","t":"You come out in front of the glasshouse. The ground shakes, the dome's glass starts to go, and the mound bursts. The Great Bloom rises up out of the ground as a closed bud and opens, while the whole glasshouse comes down round it, dome first, in a storm of glass and iron. It takes the gardens' place for good. Its tentacles reach for anything within about 26 blocks, players first, and its flies infect anyone near it who isn't wearing the Gardener's clothes. Since 1.38, what it swallows goes down alive into its stomach . you broke it. it's coming up the root. get away from the glass house. get AWAY. that's it. that's the real one. ??? as the Great Bloom rises"},{"p":"Chapter three: The Glasshouse","h":"What comes next","u":"story/chapter-3.html#what-comes-next","t":"Ten seconds after the Great Bloom rises through the glasshouse, the ground east of the gardens shakes and splits. Chapter four ."},{"p":"Chapter four: The Flesh","h":"","u":"story/chapter-4.html","t":"Ten seconds after the Great Bloom rises, a column of raw muscle forty blocks high punches up out of the ground east of the gardens, sheds its skin, and opens a slit of teeth down its front. It is what the great flower was holding down. It is also the flower's own doing. This chapter is the longest. The mod calls its first half \"Phase Two\" and its second half \"the end of it\"."},{"p":"Chapter four: The Flesh","h":"The Flesh wakes","u":"story/chapter-4.html#the-flesh-wakes","t":"A title card reads THE FLESH WAKES , and under it, the flower made it . The red Flesh is the rot the great flower's carrion flies carry, grown in the dark under Rosemont until the Great Bloom rose and let it up. It hates what made it all the same. that's not the flower. that's what the flower made. it came out of the flower's rot - and it hates what made it. it'll eat this whole world to get at them. and it's coming out of the ground. run. ??? as the Flesh wakes It spreads outward from where it came up, further every day: grass and soil turn to meat, stone and brick go veined and lit red from inside, trees to sinew, glass to membrane. Where it has taken the land the fog goes the colour of meat. That land, its infection and Bloom Serum are covered on the red fog page . It holds about 1000 blocks round where it came up, and 2000 once the Bloom has changed."},{"p":"Chapter four: The Flesh","h":"Three pieces of a reactor","u":"story/chapter-4.html#three-pieces","t":"Once Rosemont stands, the Watcher tells you there's a way to kill the big one: the Laboratory's reactor, in three pieces. A tracker at the top of your screen counts them (0/3). Each part is the only one there is: lose it and it goes back where you found it (the Rear Assembly a minute later). The Rear and Front Assemblies won't go into anything but the Assembly Cradle. there's a way to kill the big one. the laboratory's reactor. three pieces. the laboratory, the shelter, and a truck in the city. ??? once Rosemont is built"},{"p":"Chapter four: The Flesh","h":"Rosemont: the Rear Assembly","u":"story/chapter-4.html#rosemont","t":"Rosemont, the broken city , goes down a few hundred blocks from the gardens: six streets of cracked asphalt and abandoned cars, the police precinct, the corner pharmacy, the bus station, an eight-floor apartment block with its floors rotted through, a sinkhole forty blocks deep where the Bloom bit the street off, and in the middle the plaza the army turned into an evacuation checkpoint. The Rear Assembly sits in the army's Military Cradle on the back of the truck in the plaza, under a lock that takes an axe: three blows, each one setting the mechanism winding for ten seconds and each one bringing more of them over the sandbags. Car alarms call every infected within 48 blocks, rotten floors give way a second after they creak, and pools of the Flesh drag at your feet. The commuters on the crashed bus are fused into one thing that wears the bus as a shell. The Congregation (400 health) sleeps in the road until something hits it."},{"p":"Chapter four: The Flesh","h":"The Laboratory: the Reactor Core","u":"story/chapter-4.html#the-laboratory","t":"The Rosemont Botanical Research Laboratory goes down on the other side of the gardens: a white building above ground and two sublevels under it. You need a Level 2 Keycard (the director kept one in his locked desk: three good blows split the drawer). The airlock's lockers hold hazmat suits. Six tapes tell you what happened, what is in the pool and what it hates. The director's last tape gives the order of the three coolant levers , which is different in every world. In the reactor hall the Reactor Core sits in its rack over the pool. Hold use on the rack for three seconds and it's yours, and the pool turns to blood and Specimen Zero wakes (350 health): the night technician who cut a sample from the root's end. Burn the staff's bodies first, because it eats them to heal. When it dies the Laboratory locks itself down: ninety seconds to get out of the sublevels. The tapes are transcribed on Tapes and broadcasts ."},{"p":"Chapter four: The Flesh","h":"Shelter No. 4: the Front Assembly","u":"story/chapter-4.html#shelter-no-4","t":"Rosemont's Civil Defence shelter goes down south of the gardens where the ground allows: a fenced park, a blockhouse with its blast door jammed half open, and stairs down into the dark. There's no power. The fuel for the two generators in the radio room is wedged in the back of one of the shelter's lockers, a different one in every world, and most of the residents are hiding in those lockers, sobbing. With both generators running, the radio's evacuation notice turns into Control's emergency broadcast and Bunker B 's blast door opens. The special forces squad sent to hold it is still holding it, their guns grown into their arms. The Front Assembly is on the dais at the far end. Lift it, and the north wall tears itself out: the Warden of Shelter No. 4 . Kill the Warden and the Watcher leaves you a Civil Defence Compass on the dais, its needle set on Rosemont."},{"p":"Chapter four: The Flesh","h":"The Rosemont Device","u":"story/chapter-4.html#the-rosemont-device","t":"With the Rear Assembly, the Core and the Front Assembly clamped into the Assembly Cradle (in that order), hold use on the cradle with an empty hand for five seconds. The harness goes on, the wiring runs from rear to front, the Core lights blue-white and the strapped-on Geiger counter starts to tick. It is the Rosemont Device now, and there is only one. Since 1.43.1 there's another way: bring all three parts to a Forsaken Altar and the Watcher takes you to your cradle, puts a bubble of cold light round you, and builds the Device in front of you. that's it. that's a bomb. the flesh knows what it's for. it'll let you through while you carry it. take it to the bloom. to what's left of the glass house. ??? once the Device is wired Carrying it gives you Slowness II, no running and no gliding. While you carry it the Flesh lets you through: its infected stop, turn to watch you pass and step out of your way (hit one and the truce is off for fifteen seconds). The Bloom's things come for you instead. Within 200 blocks of the risen Bloom its roots crack up out of the ground after you, and its music, The Approach, comes up under everything."},{"p":"Chapter four: The Flesh","h":"The Gardener, reborn twice","u":"story/chapter-4.html#the-gardener-reborn","t":"Within 32 blocks, the Bloom goes still and turns every petal on the Device. Then it gags, heaves and spits the Gardener back up in a gush of nectar, his body knitting itself together with vines. It folds its petals shut and a ring of thorned roots six blocks high comes up round the arena. The Gardener, Reborn has 600 health, three phases and the Bloomshears. Since 1.40 he comes back once more: kill him and the Bloom grows him back as the Gardener, Reborn Again , faster and harder. Kill him the second time and the Watcher rips the portal into the Bloom open."},{"p":"Chapter four: The Flesh","h":"The launch","u":"story/chapter-4.html#the-launch","t":"Every sound drops out except footsteps. The Watcher steps out from right behind you, walks to the shut Bloom, pushes its fingers between two petals and pulls until they tear away and the green rift flares open, wider than before. Then it looks straight at you, and it's gone. The rift comes out on a ledge, what's left of the Binding's island, hanging over the colossal Bloom's mouth, its tentacles hanging over it, held back. At the far end is the Launch Mark , and the Device goes nowhere else (set it down anywhere else and you're told \"Not here. The edge.\"). On the mark it unfolds into a missile. Hold use on it for three seconds to arm it, then run: ten seconds to get back through the rift. take it through. put it down past the edge. then run. don't look at them. i've got them. i can't hold them long. and then you run. you don't stop, and you don't look back. ??? on the ledge Putting the Device into the Great Bloom earns Not Collected : \"It's still beating.\""},{"p":"Chapter four: The Flesh","h":"It changed","u":"story/chapter-4.html#it-changed","t":"Since 1.40, the camera is taken the moment nobody is left in the Bloom. You watch the Device burst up out of the rift and climb over the Bloom, the Bloom catch it with a tentacle and drag it down its throat, and the Watcher on the crater's rim pour its darkness into a beam. The Device goes off inside it. Everything goes white. Out of the white the sky opens, a column of light comes down on the Bloom, and it changes. A title card reads IT CHANGED : and its roar went all the way round the world . i knew it would do that. the bomb was never going to kill it. i needed it to change. bigger. a soul that size is worth something. but my darkness isn't enough for it now. i need a stronger soul to pour it through. ??? after the Bloom changes The changed Bloom is ten times bigger, its flesh gone blue, its acid purple, its teeth green, sunk in a pit it tears out of the ground. It reaches for anything within ninety blocks, and its roar can be heard from anywhere in the world. Over three days its blight grows out from it: blue flesh where the grass was, blisters of acid, green teeth up out of the ground, a violet haze over all of it. Since 1.42 it grows on what it eats, up to three times the size it changed to, and gets worse the longer it goes without. See the Bloom's page ."},{"p":"Chapter four: The Flesh","h":"The end of it","u":"story/chapter-4.html#the-end-of-it","t":""},{"p":"Chapter four: The Flesh","h":"A gun above the sky","u":"story/chapter-4.html#the-power-source","t":"there's a gun up above the sky. they built it before the city fell. they never got to fire it. it needs a power source. three places woke up when the bloom changed. what you need is in them. build the core. bring it to the forsaken altar, and i'll put my magic into it. then we kill it. ??? after the Bloom changes Three places wake 300 to 1000 blocks from the gardens, and the Watcher gives everyone a needle for each. A tracker counts THE POWER SOURCE (0/3) : The Uplink Station , where the garrison talked to the gun over the sky: the Targeting Array is in the locker by the consoles. The Capacitor Works , still holding its charge, with arcs jumping between the lightning rods and a notice that says DANGER - LIVE BANKS : the Capacitor Cell is in the test cage at the back. The Soul Well , a shaft thirty blocks down with its keepers kneeling round the altar at the bottom: the Bound Soul . Make the Orbital Core from the three, iron and redstone, and set it on a Forsaken Altar. The Watcher pours itself into it and gives it back infused . Build the Orbital Railgun round it. Its strikes call down a slug from SENTINEL, the gun above the sky: sixty damage, fire and a shockwave out to twelve blocks. See the power source parts ."},{"p":"Chapter four: The Flesh","h":"The Ray Gun and the Omni","u":"story/chapter-4.html#the-ray-gun","t":"The railgun's strikes make the changed Bloom scream, but it heals as fast as you tear it. Building the railgun wakes three more places: ...did you hear that. it's calling something up out of the ground. the gun can hurt it. it can't end it. what can end it is in what it's calling up. ??? once the railgun is built Ashford Nuclear Plant , its reactor never gone cold: the Nuclear Reactor Core , in the fuel pool (don't go in the water without a suit). Meridian Laboratory , its arcs jumping: the Discharge Destabilizer , in the glass cell in the middle of the ring. Blackwater Station , an island lab out at sea where something got loose: the Vial of Dark Matter Blood , and the parasites . Craft the Ray Gun round the railgun and the three parts, or bring them all to a Forsaken Altar and the Watcher builds it. Either way the Watcher wants it (\"give it here\"). Drop it near him or use it on him, and he gives you back the Omni Orbital Railgun ."},{"p":"Chapter four: The Flesh","h":"The Omni Ray","u":"story/chapter-4.html#the-omni-ray","t":"Stand fifty blocks or more off the changed Bloom's mouth, aim the Omni at the flower and fire. The camera is taken: SENTINEL comes down out of its orbit, a star that moves, then a fireball, then a sonic boom and retro thrusters. Five rings of glyphs close in round the line down to its mouth, TARGET LOCKED, and it fires. The Bloom fires back. If it has eaten too much, the Watcher gives the beam all of its own power. A title card reads THE OMNI RAY : the bloom is dead. the watcher rests. What's left is a husk. The blight dies back, and so does the Flesh, everywhere but the places it built itself into. i need time to rest. this took too much power. but when i come back with our work, i'll be ten times stronger. thanks to you. i will repay you. but for now, i must rest. ??? after the Omni Ray"},{"p":"Chapter four: The Flesh","h":"Not so fast","u":"story/chapter-4.html#not-so-fast","t":"The first time you carry the Omni off the Bloom's blight, the Watcher is in your way. It pulls the gun out of your hands, tears open a rift into its own realm, and throws the gun in. The first time anyone puts a Ray Gun together in a crafting grid afterwards, it's there at the table and burns the recipe out of every recipe book. The Mended guns, which are the Bloom's flesh, rot and jam once it's dead. wait. not so fast. it wouldn't be fair to let you take such a destructive toy with you, to use on everything. from what i see, i see great power. great potential. but zero responsibility for life. i can see the thoughts in your head, you know. ??? taking the Omni back"},{"p":"Chapter four: The Flesh","h":"Ten days later","u":"story/chapter-4.html#ten-days-later","t":"Ten days later by the world's clock, the Watcher comes back, rested, and finds you wherever you are. In your house it bangs on the window and then comes in, by the door, which creaks open on its own, or through the wall where the glass is. Down a mine it folds itself down the tunnel, and anything there trying to kill you bursts into ink. In the woods its head leans out from behind a tree. Anywhere else, it's right behind you, breathing, until you turn round. This earns the advancement Ten Days Later . ten days. i'm rested now - stronger, like i said i'd be. but i didn't come to talk about me. it's the parasites. the infection in those new places - blackwater - it isn't from here. it came into this realm from another one. the null static zone. the flesh is dying back. with the flower dead it's got nothing to grow from. they don't need the flower. they'll get into anything with blood in it - a cow, a horse, a villager. you won't see it often. but if something you know starts acting wrong, don't let it near you. keep your eyes open. ??? ten days later"},{"p":"Chapter four: The Flesh","h":"While the Flesh spreads","u":"story/chapter-4.html#while-the-flesh-spreads","t":"Through all of this chapter, the Flesh keeps making things worse: Mutations. Left alive on its ground for ten minutes (five on the thickest of it), one of the infected changes into a Stalker, a Bloater, a Screamer, a Brute, a Splitter or a Hive, depending on what it was. The nests. Where the Flesh has had the land long enough, the ground sinks into a bowl and grows the Flesh's own great flower, the Broodmother (340 health), with rows of brood sacs round her. The horde. Some nights, ten to eighteen of its dead climb out of the ground together and walk to you behind a Bellwether ringing its bell. Kill the Bellwether and the horde loses its way. Sapromyiophilous. The flower's flies can lay in you. At level III you turn, and what gets up where you fell is you , wearing your armour and carrying everything you had. Kill it to get it all back. Swallowed alive. What the Great Bloom eats goes down alive into its stomach. Cut the stomach wall ten times and it throws you back up. Every one of these is in the bestiary ."},{"p":"Chapter four: The Flesh","h":"What comes next","u":"story/chapter-4.html#what-comes-next","t":"With the Bloom dead, the Flesh has nothing to grow from and dies back. But the parasites don't need the flower, and the static isn't noise. Chapter five ."},{"p":"Chapter five: The Static","h":"","u":"story/chapter-5.html","t":"The Bloom is dead and the Flesh dies back with it. But the parasites came into this realm from another one, and they're still out there. When they talk to each other, it sounds like static. Chapter Five arrived in six parts, from 1.44.0 to 1.54.0: The Static , The Relay , The Null , The Null Static Zone (1.47.1 added the late show), The Hive and The Deep . It starts once the Bloom is dead and ends when the Chorus, whole, dies in the Warm Heart. Between the parts, 1.48.0 to 1.52.0 turned the parasite into an outbreak: from Chapter Five on, anything at all can carry one."},{"p":"Chapter five: The Static","h":"Part one: the static","u":"story/chapter-5.html#the-static","t":""},{"p":"Chapter five: The Static","h":"Static Hounds","u":"story/chapter-5.html#static-hounds","t":"What the parasites made of the wolves: starved to a frame, mangy, black chitin up through the spine, two violet pinpricks for eyes, and a muzzle that splits open into petals round a throat of teeth. At night, now and then, a pack of three to five comes out of the dark behind a Pack Leader with a brood sac on its back. The leader comes at you head on while the rest go wide and come in from your sides and behind. Seeing you, the leader howls , a wolf's howl breaking up into radio static, and the pack runs faster and bites harder for a while (and you're weak for a few seconds). Any of them lunges the last few blocks, and their bites make you bleed. Kill the leader and its sac tears open, one of them comes out, and the pack breaks and scatters, yelping."},{"p":"Chapter five: The Static","h":"One of them in you","u":"story/chapter-5.html#one-of-them-in-you","t":"A Parasite that holds on at the back of your neck for the whole four seconds gets in. Crouch, or get hit, to tear it off before then. If it gets in, its brood grows in you over about three days of play, and a meter beside your hotbar fills: How far grown What happens From the start You get hungrier. A quarter You can feel the others. Parasites, hounds, the Hollowed and anything with a brood in it show through walls to you, violet, and static comes off you. Two fifths You're stronger and faster. And starving. Half The sac shows on your back, and it has fits: you can hardly move for a second or two. Three quarters It's too big to burn out. Full It bursts out of your back: 7 hearts, bleeding, and two of them come out. Get it out first. A Surgical Kit cuts it out of you (or out of someone else, or an animal). Or burn it out : stand in fire long enough to be hurt, before it's three quarters grown. A Hush kills one outright."},{"p":"Chapter five: The Static","h":"The Hollowed","u":"story/chapter-5.html#the-hollowed","t":"In every village, one villager isn't one any more. Its eyes are two violet pinpricks; it mutters, and what comes out is static; it watches you. Wear the Dead Channel Helm , or have a brood in you a quarter grown, and you can see the static coming off it. At night, alone with it, no other villager near, it turns: it shakes, straightens up taller than it was, its folded arms come apart and hang to its knees, and its head splits open into four, like the parasite's mouth. Hurt it and it turns there and then. Turned, it comes for you and the rest of its village: it shrieks (the noise roots you to the spot), rakes and grabs, and sometimes puts one in you. Killed, a parasite crawls out of its throat, unless it burnt."},{"p":"Chapter five: The Static","h":"The outbreak","u":"story/chapter-5.html#the-outbreak","t":"Since 1.48.0 the parasite doesn't just brood in what it gets into and burst out. It takes it over , slowly, and then the creature is theirs. Any creature can carry it: the game's own animals, villagers and monsters, the golems, the warden, the Hollow's own things (but not the parasite's own, not the Flesh's, and not you; for you there's the brood above). It takes two days of the world's clock for an ordinary creature and three for the hard ones. You can watch it happen: a twitch now and then, violet veins under the skin, the first blisters, shaking fits, growths and chitin forcing out through its back, its head hanging to one side. Nearly gone, it stands and stares at you, and goes for you if you're close in the dark. Then the turn : five seconds of it seizing up and screaming, and it tears open into one of theirs. Turned, it hunts everything that isn't one of them, and what it hits it might put a parasite into. Killed, it bursts and its parasites come out, unless it burnt. A Surgical Kit cuts one out of anything before it turns. The parasite comes in kinds now too, each born of where it was (in the water, deep underground, out of anything with wings, in the Nether, in the End), and it leaves heaps of biomass that get up again as its pure forms . The Hollow's own creatures, bosses included, each turn into something new. All of it is on the turned and the Parasite ."},{"p":"Chapter five: The Static","h":"Part two: the relay","u":"story/chapter-5.html#the-relay","t":"do you hear it. under the static. it isn't noise. they're talking to each other. something's carrying it. this points to where. ??? handing out a needle to Relay 6 What one of them hears, all of them hear, and something is carrying it: Relay 6 on Hollow Ridge , the county's emergency-broadcast relay, 300 to 1000 blocks out. While it's on the air, static pours off the top of its forty-block mast and hound packs come twice as often within 700 blocks of it. At the mast's foot is the Amalgam : everyone who came to the relay, the operator, his dog and the people from the valley, grown together into one heap. Lashed to the mast on each rest platform is a tether , a knot of sinew with a cable running down to it. Climb the ladder and cut all three, then kill it. The relay goes off the air , the hounds near it lose the signal and run, and from then on packs come less often everywhere. It leaves the Relay Core . Hold it to your ear and you're Tuned In for thirty seconds. Keep it: it'll be wanted."},{"p":"Chapter five: The Static","h":"Part three: the Null","u":"story/chapter-5.html#the-null","t":"the relay's quiet. the static isn't gone. it's going somewhere. there's a place it all runs down into. like water. this points to it. ??? once the relay is off the air With the relay quiet, the last of their static runs down into the Starlite Drive-In , 300 to 1000 blocks out. Its screen is dark until somebody steps inside the fence. Then the late show plays: a relay slams home somewhere, the lamp strikes, the screen floods with static that pours off its face into a tear in the ground, and five figures peel off the picture and come up the lot for you. they came out of the picture. they always do, when somebody's watching. you can't hurt them yet. they're not all the way here. the core. hold it to your ear - tuned in, they're as real as you are. or let one reach for you. when it does, it's all the way here. hit it then. kill one and it leaves a frame of the picture behind. four frames. the projector's up in the booth. run the reel. see what's under all of it. ??? during the late show Within forty blocks of the tear you're Nulled : the colour goes out of everything, static creeps in at the edges of your sight, the fog closes in grey, and you go hungry faster. The figures are Afterimages , what's left of the people who stayed in their cars after the reel. Each one you kill leaves a Frame of the Last Reel . The last reel: load four frames into the projector in the booth, with the Relay Core on you to tune it. It runs seventy seconds in five parts. Afterimages come out of the picture for the booth (more of them with more of you there), and while the reel runs anyone can hurt them. One that reaches the projector jumps the film back ten seconds; leave the booth and the reel runs out. Hold them off to the end and the last frame burns on the screen, what's under all of it, and the reel is yours. you saw it. that's what's under all of it. that's where they come from. it was carrying them. the way the relay was. only it's alive. keep the reel. ??? after the last reel"},{"p":"Chapter five: The Static","h":"Part four: the Null Static Zone","u":"story/chapter-5.html#the-null-static-zone","t":"Hold the Last Reel up over the tear at the drive-in. The static runs backwards off it into the tear, and its bottom goes to a pool of static: a rift. Step in. The Null Static Zone is where everything that ever went into the static ran down to: a grey plain under no sky, grey fog, ash and static on the wind, voices a long way off. You come out on a landing among the things it took, cars, television sets, a radio mast bent double, and the rift there takes you home whenever you like. You're Nulled the whole time, and you can't sleep there. Out on the plain are the Ancient Null Ruins : the Listening Stones, the Sunken Choir and the Hush, built by the people who were here the last time the static came. the null static zone. everything that went into the static came here. it's in the middle. its threads go up to every mast you ever saw. cut them. ??? in the Null Static Zone"},{"p":"Chapter five: The Static","h":"The Carrier","u":"story/chapter-5.html#the-carrier","t":"In the crater in the middle of the Zone is what carried them all: the Carrier , a head the size of a house with one eye in it, on a neck up out of a coil of its own pale body. Its threads go up off the coil into the dark, and four of them run to the four black spires round the crater's rim, tied off in a knot on top of each. While a thread holds, it shrugs off most of what you do to it. Climb the spires, break the knots, and it's cut loose: furious, and far easier to hurt."},{"p":"Chapter five: The Static","h":"Signing off","u":"story/chapter-5.html#signing-off","t":"Kill it and it goes down across its coil, its threads coming down out of the dark one by one. Then the Watcher comes for its eye, tears a rift of its own and sends everyone home. Six seconds after you're back, the title card: CHAPTER FIVE , with SIGNING OFF under it. it's dead. good. it wasn't theirs, you know. it was a carrier. it carried whatever was put on it. the static was a door. and this was holding it open. this, i'll keep. for the future. go home. there's nothing on the air now. ??? signing off At the drive-in the screen goes black for the first time, and then shows one line: SIGNING OFF. The Null goes out of the lot, and the static is gone: no more hound packs at night, and the Hollowed in the villages are only villagers again. The Carrier leaves 6 to 10 Carrier Threads, some of its flesh, and a record, Signing Off . SIGNING OFF"},{"p":"Chapter five: The Static","h":"After signing off","u":"story/chapter-5.html#after-signing-off","t":"The title card reads CHAPTER FIVE over SIGNING OFF . Half a minute after you're home from the Null Static Zone, the Watcher comes to wherever you're standing, and he isn't pleased. ...this was unexpected. but we can work with it. we'll make do. it seems the carrier did what it was supposed to do. it carried them - all the way out. the parasites are increasing. every one of them hostile. the numbers are going off the charts. in your world. it's dangerous out there. more than ever, now. there's nothing we can do about it for now. just try not to die. for me. in the meantime. and i suggest you don't go to the end. ...actually. i'll make sure you can't go there. it's dangerous for you, player. you know i can see you right now, right, [your name]? remember who you work for. ??? half a minute after signing off From then on the outbreak is worse: the parasite gets into things half again as often, and more of its kinds turn up round you, more of them at once. And the End is shut . Anyone who goes through an End portal in Survival is sent straight back out of it to their bed or the world's spawn (\"The way's shut. He shut it.\"), and he has a word for you: \"no. i said not there.\" the first time, and \"not there. i told you.\" after that."},{"p":"Chapter five: The Static","h":"Part five: the Hive","u":"story/chapter-5.html#the-hive","t":"The static is gone, and the parasite, which used to hear itself in the static, all of it at once, has gone deaf. So it's growing itself a mind. Somewhere 300 to 1000 blocks from the gardens, it takes a hamlet whole and grows the Hive out of it: a crater of violet flesh, the cottages and their bell tower grown over, ribs arching over everything, and a pit in the middle with four stalks round it, a nerve node on top of each."},{"p":"Chapter five: The Static","h":"It Speaks","u":"story/chapter-5.html#it-speaks","t":"The first night after the Hive has grown, wherever you are out under the open sky, the camera is taken. The ground heaves round you, five of the parasite's pure forms stand up out of it in a ring, turn their heads to you all together, and it speaks through all of them at once, its voices out of step: the Chorus we were many. we were scattered. we heard each other in the noise. the Chorus you cut the throat that carried us. now there is only quiet. the Chorus so we are growing another way to be one. out of all of them. out of everything they knew. the Chorus come and see what we are becoming. come and be heard. Then they fold back into the ground, and the Watcher is beside you. it lost its voice when the carrier died. so it's growing itself a mind instead. out of everything it took. every body. every face. everything any of them ever knew. when it's finished it won't need the static to talk to them. it'll just be all of them. this points to where it's growing. go before it wakes up all the way. ??? handing out a needle to the Hive"},{"p":"Chapter five: The Static","h":"The Hive","u":"story/chapter-5.html#the-hive-itself","t":"The ground at the Hive is \"warm, and soft, and it gives under you. Something under it is breathing.\" Somebody got there first: Fr. Aldous Mercer's journal is on a lectern by what's left of a cottage, with his chest beside it (what he brought for the fire). Seven Hive Hands stand round the pit: arms as tall as trees, a palm with eyes and a mouth at the top and three hooked fingers. Get within reach and they slam down where the ground lights up violet, sweep you aside, or grab you, lift you over the Hive and throw you. They can be killed (fire hurts them more), but while the Chorus is in its pit the Hive grows a dead hand back after five minutes. it took them whole. the people, the houses. everything they knew is in that pit now. it thinks with those, on the stalks round the pit. cut them and it can't think straight. there was a priest here. read him. ??? the first time anyone reaches the Hive"},{"p":"Chapter five: The Static","h":"The Mind","u":"story/chapter-5.html#the-mind","t":"Go to the edge of the pit and its floor splits. The Chorus comes up out of it: a mound of everything it took, a great head with a split maw down the middle, faces all over it, arms ending in hooks. Its faces open their eyes, and it knows you: the Chorus you. we know you. you were in the static with us. you were loud. the Chorus we do not need a throat now. we have a thousand mouths, and all of them are listening. the Chorus the ones you lost are here with us. they are singing. would you like to hear them? the Chorus come down. be heard. be one more voice. The Hive The Chorus's bar is up; its black Hive Hands stand round the pit. The fight (900 health, its own bar and music) never leaves the pit. It sends tendrils up under you (the ground churns first: move), lets out clouds of spores, gives birth to pure forms, slams an arm down, sings in three swells, each worse than the last, and draws through the cords to its nodes to heal. It's hard to hurt unless its maw is open or you've torn its nerve nodes open. Climb the steps round the four stalks and break the glowing nodes: each one makes it scream and makes it easier to hurt (\"It screams - and it can't think straight any more. Everything gets through now.\" once all four are gone). Fire hurts it more. If nobody's near and it hasn't been hurt for half a minute, it mends."},{"p":"Chapter five: The Static","h":"It Runs","u":"story/chapter-5.html#it-runs","t":"Bring it down to a quarter and it won't die. It screams and tears itself down through the floor of its pit, deep, and its nodes burst. the Chorus no. no - not yet. we are not finished. it ran. it can do that now. it's got enough of a mind to be afraid. it's gone down. deep. where everything went before the static was ever a noise. that's a piece of it. it still talks. keep it - listen to it. it'll tell you where it went. it'll come back up. bigger. and next time it won't be half finished. ??? on the rim of the empty pit It leaves pieces of itself on the floor of the pit: Chorus Fragments , one for each of you. They still talk. Hold one to your ear. Four advancements come out of this part: It Speaks , The Hive , Senseless (all four nodes) and It Ran ."},{"p":"Chapter five: The Static","h":"Part six: the Deep","u":"story/chapter-5.html#the-deep","t":"It isn't dead. It went down, and now you go after it."},{"p":"Chapter five: The Static","h":"The hunt","u":"story/chapter-5.html#the-hunt","t":"The Chorus Fragment still hears the rest of it. Hold it to your ear and turn round: facing the right way it whispers clearly, and what it says tells you how far (\"down. a long way down. far from here - that way.\" when it's more than 600 blocks off, then \"that way. under the hills. we can feel you coming.\", \"closer. we can hear you walking. we can hear your heart.\" and finally \"here. right under you. come down. it's warm.\"). Side on, it's faint and broken (\"...colder... no... turn...\"). Facing away, only static."},{"p":"Chapter five: The Static","h":"The Sinkhole","u":"story/chapter-5.html#the-sinkhole","t":"It leads you to the Sinkhole , 300 to 1000 blocks from the gardens: a farm's low field pulled down from underneath into a crater thirty-odd yards across, steam coming off its floor, the barn tipped over the edge, the fences snapped at the rim. The county surveyor's camp is on the north rim (his notes, his kit), and his last page is halfway down. In the floor is the Burrow , a tunnel round as a pipe and lined with the Hive's flesh, going down in six turns like a corkscrew to a chamber at the bottom. In that chamber's floor is the Throat , a puckered ring of flesh. Stand on it: it stirs (\"It feels you standing on it.\"), opens, and takes you down. That's Warmer for finding the Sinkhole and Down Where It Is Warm for going down. this is where it went down. the ground didn't fall in. it was pulled. someone measured it before you. he went down after it. the piece of it you've got will tell you how far down it goes. ??? the first time anyone reaches the Sinkhole"},{"p":"Chapter five: The Static","h":"It comes back up","u":"story/chapter-5.html#it-comes-back-up","t":"Until it's dead, the world up top feels it. Tremors go under you every so often. The ground gives way near you (natural ground only, never your builds): a pit lined with its flesh with its things climbing out, which heals over after five minutes. Flesh blisters swell up out of the ground; break one before it bursts or its forms come out. And every few nights, where you live, comes the Reach : three tremors, each closer, then the ground splits and one of the Chorus's hands tears up out of it, half again as big as the Hive's, with waves of its things climbing out after it (\"IT COMES UP\", its own bar and music). Kill it for It Came Up . Leave it, and after four minutes it sinks back down."},{"p":"Chapter five: The Static","h":"Down in the Deep","u":"story/chapter-5.html#down-in-the-deep","t":"You come out in the Gullet , a chamber of flesh with a Throat in its floor that takes you back up. \"It's warm down here. It's always been warm down here.\" The Deep is a dimension of its own: huge warm caverns under everything, with seas of blood at the bottom. The Warm Dark is the Hive's flesh grown over the rock. In the Root Hollows the Bloom's roots hang down through the roofs. The Old Halls are the pale worked stone of whoever was down there first. You can't sleep there (\"You can't sleep down here. Something is always listening.\"). If you're carrying a fragment, it whispers: \"home. we are home. come and find us. we are deeper.\" Two places to look for: Low Marrow , a hamlet the ground opened under one night, pulled down whole into a cavern of its own, its cottages tipped over and half sunk in a lake that isn't water any more and its church upended in the middle (the reeve and the priest both wrote down why); and the Old Halls, at the end of a road of way-stones (squat columns with a spiral cut in them like an ear and an ember cap burning on top) that starts at the Gullet."},{"p":"Chapter five: The Static","h":"The older ones","u":"story/chapter-5.html#the-older-ones","t":"Something was down there first, and it hates the Chorus as much as it hates you. The Listeners can't see you. They hear you: every step, every block broken or set, every door, every mouthful. A Listener goes to the sound fast and rakes whatever's there. Sneak and it can't hear you walk; throw something and it goes to where it lands. They nest in the root hollows and hunt the Chorus's forms too. Stitch two of their ears over leather boots (with string) for Hushed Boots and walk as quietly as sneaking ( Not a Sound ). The Deaf King is the oldest thing in the Deep, the one that carved the Old Halls. Long ago it drove a plug of stone into each ear so it wouldn't hear the Chorus singing. It can't hear or see you; it feels you through the floor. Stand still and you aren't there. It sits on its dais at the end of the Old Halls. Kill it ( Stand Still ) and its crown cracks off and leaves the King's Ear-Stones . Carry them into the last fight."},{"p":"Chapter five: The Static","h":"The Warm Heart","u":"story/chapter-5.html#the-warm-heart","t":"Follow the fragment to where the Chorus went to ground (\"here. we are right here. we are finished growing.\"): a great round chamber, its floor of flesh running down to a lake of blood under a vault of chitin ribs, with four nerve nodes on their stalks round the shore. Come down into it and the Chorus, whole rises out of the blood, made again from everything it took, with a second pair of arms and the Bloom's roots run all through it. \"Up out of the blood it comes - whole again, and every voice in it singing.\" It fights in three parts. First as it did in its pit, harder, with its nodes and its hands round the shore. At two thirds the walls crack and the older ones break in : the Listeners come through for it, its things and you, and its song gets worse (carry the King's Ear-Stones and the song can't get into you at all). With a third left it tears itself up out of its lake , ripping out its cords as it goes: no nodes any more, everything it has, as fast as it can. Then it dies. Really, this time: every voice in it goes quiet one after another and it sinks into the blood. \"Far below, the singing stops. It doesn't start again.\" Everything of its in the chamber falls apart and the world above stops feeling it. See the Chorus for the whole fight. Out of it comes the Last Voice , the one voice it couldn't swallow, still trying to tell you something ( The Last Voice ). A while later, someone else has something to say to whoever was there: it's quiet down there now. i can hear you breathing. you've got something of it. one voice it couldn't swallow. keep it. there's a door at the end of the world with a seal on it. i made that seal. i can't open it. that voice can. when you're ready, take it to the end. ??? after the Chorus, whole, is dead Hold the Last Voice up and it talks too: \"...there's a door. at the end. he sealed it...\", \"...take me to the end of the world. i'll open it for you...\", \"...the one in the black coat knows. ask him what he locked up...\". Its lines are collected on Tapes and broadcasts ."},{"p":"Chapter five: The Static","h":"What comes next","u":"story/chapter-5.html#what-comes-next","t":"The story's music changes to Quiet Now , the Lullaby's tune in a major key. But the Watcher has just told you he sealed something, and the Last Voice wants to be carried to it. Take it into the End: that's Chapter Six: The Door at the End of the World ."},{"p":"Chapter six: The Door at the End of the World","h":"","u":"story/chapter-6.html","t":"He shut the End after the Carrier died. Now you know why he'd want to. Out past the obsidian there's a door he made, and a seal he put on it with his own hands, and the one voice the Chorus couldn't swallow knows how to open it. Chapter Six came in three parts, 1.56.0 to 1.58.0. The mod's title cards call them The Door at the End of the World - Part One: The Audience , Part Two: The Watcher's Vault and Part Three: What He Kept Out . It starts once the Chorus, whole, is dead and you're holding the Last Voice ."},{"p":"Chapter six: The Door at the End of the World","h":"The seal","u":"story/chapter-6.html#the-seal","t":"Carry the Last Voice into the End. The Watcher can't keep you out of it any more. The voice talks first (\"...here. it's here. can you feel it? something on the other side is listening...\" and then \"...hold me up. here. he made this seal with his own hands. i can open it...\"), and something cracks all the way across the End's sky and stays cracked: \"Something cracks, all the way across the End's sky - and stays cracked. The seal he put on it is broken.\" He says one word. ...don't. ??? as the seal breaks That's The Door at the End of the World . From then on the End is open to everyone, as it was. Since 1.61.1 the dragon waiting there is always the Infested Ender Dragon , so come ready for it. Since 1.60.2, the first time anyone's in the End the island's ground over the obsidian platform gives way into a shaft up to the sky, so you don't arrive shut in end stone. Out past the obsidian, a causeway of seal-stone (black, his glyphs cut into it, a few still faintly lit) runs east over the void to an island. On the island is the Door : a frame of seal-stone taller than a house with nothing in it but humming static. The voice tells you where: \"...there. out past the obsidian. a door. go through it. i'll be quiet now...\""},{"p":"Chapter six: The Door at the End of the World","h":"Part one: the Audience","u":"story/chapter-6.html#part-one-the-audience","t":"Walk into the static. It takes you to the Stalls : an old picture house's seats out in the open in the dark, row after row of them in long curves, every one facing the Great Screen. The screen is two hundred feet wide, its curtains drawn back, and between the static it plays the story so far, frame by frame. Behind the seats are the lot, wrecked cars, speaker posts and the projection booth on its tower. \"Rows and rows of seats in the dark, every one of them facing a screen. Some of them are taken.\" You can't sleep there (\"Not here. Not with them watching.\"), and the way home is the Door behind you. That's Take Your Seat . If you're still carrying the Last Voice, it has one more thing to say as you come in: \"...shh. don't wake them. they're watching...\""},{"p":"Chapter six: The Door at the End of the World","h":"Keep quiet","u":"story/chapter-6.html#the-audience","t":"The Audience. Forty of the seats are taken by grey people in grey clothes, faces turned up to the screen, a ticket in their laps. They don't look round, but they hear you: a step near them, a block broken, a door. Then they get up, slowly, a finger to their lips, and come and hold you where you are. Sneak and they can't hear you walk. Lose them and they go back and sit down. Some of them have a Ticket Stub . The Ushers. Four of them walk the aisles with lamps, tall, too thin, maroon uniforms, white gloves and no face. An Usher sees, it doesn't hear, so sneaking won't help. If its lamp finds you (\"The Usher's lamp is on you.\") it puts a finger to where its lips should be, the SHHH goes through the house, and everyone sitting near you gets up. Then it comes for you, bashing you with the lamp, and if it gets hold of your collar it walks you back up the aisle toward the Door. Show one a Ticket Stub (use it on the Usher) and it tears it in two and looks away: for a minute its lamp doesn't see you. Now and then one drops its lamp. The Usher's Lamp. Held, it lights the dark round you. Use it and it flashes: Audience and Ushers caught in the flash reel with their hands over their faces for a few seconds. It needs eight seconds to warm again."},{"p":"Chapter six: The Door at the End of the World","h":"The Crowd","u":"story/chapter-6.html#the-crowd","t":"Step out onto the front aisle under the screen and \"The picture on the screen is you.\" Every one of the Audience gets up (the Last Voice, if you have it: \"...they're getting up. all of them...\") and comes down to the front, into one heap, and it stands up: the Crowd , three men high, two great arms made of people and a knot of faces on top, every one of them looking at you. It doesn't leave the front. It reaches across the front rows, slams both arms down (jump the ring), applauds (each clap a wall of air) and sheds people who get up and come for you. From two thirds down comes the Hush (\"Quiet, please.\"): for four seconds anyone who moves or strikes is grabbed by hands up out of the floor. Stand still ( Quiet, Please ), or flash an Usher's Lamp at it to break the Hush. In its last third it roars with every mouth at once. Dead, it comes apart into the people it was, they come apart into static, and the screen goes dark ( Standing Ovation ). \"Something's left in the middle of where it stood: a ticket. It's warm.\" That's the Last Ticket , one for everyone who was there."},{"p":"Chapter six: The Door at the End of the World","h":"Front Row","u":"story/chapter-6.html#front-row","t":"The screen is dark and the house is empty, but one seat in the front row is still taken. It's the Watcher. it was a good show. you weren't meant to see the end of it. you want to know what i locked up. come and see, then. ??? in the front row He gets up, goes to the screen, puts his hand on it and tears it open, and goes through. It closes behind him to a seam of light down the middle: \"There's a seam of light down the middle of the screen where he went through. It won't stay shut forever.\" That's Front Row , and the title card: Chapter Six , The Door at the End of the World - Part One: The Audience ."},{"p":"Chapter six: The Door at the End of the World","h":"Part two: the Watcher's Vault","u":"story/chapter-6.html#part-two-the-watchers-vault","t":"Hold the Last Ticket (\"ADMIT ONE - THE VAULT\") up to the seam. The ticket tears in two in your hand and the seam opens wide, from the top of the screen down to the stage, light pouring out, and stays open for everyone ( Admit One ). Walk into it. You come out of a tear in a great dark canvas into the Watcher's Vault , his archive behind the picture: the stacks, steel shelving going up into the dark with cans of film and boxes of tape on every shelf, labelled in his hand, and old television sets among them, some still on. Down the middle runs a long nave. You can't sleep there (\"Not here. Not with them standing out there in the stacks.\"), and the way back is the tear you came through ( Behind the Picture ). ...in here. all the way up. don't look at them. ??? as you come into the Vault"},{"p":"Chapter six: The Door at the End of the World","h":"The Tuned","u":"story/chapter-6.html#the-tuned","t":"Standing in the aisles are people from the neck down, an old television set where the head should be. Unlike most things, the Tuned only move while you're looking at them : watch one and it comes for you in jerks, your face on its screen; look away and it stops dead. Close and watched, it takes your head in its hands and tunes you. Flash an Usher's Lamp at one and it can't move for four seconds, watched or not. In the dark, or in the Projectionist's light, they move whether you look or not. Some drop a Vacuum Tube."},{"p":"Chapter six: The Door at the End of the World","h":"The Watch","u":"story/chapter-6.html#the-watch","t":"At the far end of the nave is his desk, his chair, and a wall of sets thirty-seven across and sixteen high, all showing one picture. The first time anyone comes in: this is where i watch from. they watch the picture. i watch them. your world's a show to them. the worse it gets, the more of them come. they left you a ticket. it admits one. not you. something came in behind you. it's come for what i kept. the omni. the carrier. my first reel. get to them before it does. bring them here. ??? at the Watch"},{"p":"Chapter six: The Door at the End of the World","h":"The keeps","u":"story/chapter-6.html#the-keeps","t":"\"Three keeps off the nave, behind round steel doors: the Omni's heart, what's left of the Carrier, his first reel. Bring them to the Watch.\" Use a door or its wheel and the bolts draw back one after another. On a plinth in each is what he kept: The Omni's Heart : \"every colour at once, turning. It's lighter than it looks, and warm.\" What's Left of the Carrier : a knot of it, still beating. Take it and its static pours out, and every Tuned near you is loose for a few seconds (\"...quick. they can all move while it's loose like that.\"). His First Reel , in a glass case: \"On the lid, in his hand: THE OTHER SIDE. FIRST. DO NOT RUN.\" All three is What He Kept ."},{"p":"Chapter six: The Door at the End of the World","h":"The Projectionist","u":"story/chapter-6.html#the-projectionist","t":"Bring all three to the Watch and every set on the wall goes to it (\"...it's here. it's in the wall.\"). Then it steps down out of them: the Projectionist , twice a man's height, a long coat made of film, and a cinema projector for a head with a lens you can't look into. It sweeps its beam across the Watch (while you're in it, the Tuned can move), projects reruns of old bosses' best moves onto the air, lashes film round you, splices itself behind you, and changes its reels at each third (hit it then). In the last third comes Intermission : every set and bulb goes out and there's only its lens (\"Please remain seated.\"). Dead, it burns through from the middle like film stuck in the gate and leaves the Projectionist's Lens ( The Final Reel )."},{"p":"Chapter six: The Door at the End of the World","h":"The First Reel","u":"story/chapter-6.html#the-first-reel","t":"He runs it. The projector on his desk clatters into life: this is the first thing anyone ever saw on the other side. i kept it so i'd never forget what it looks like. that's what i kept out. it's all for that one. the whole show. and now it's seen you. it's coming through. ??? running his first reel On the wall: a dark so big it has a shape, sitting, with an eye in it, opening. The eye turns to look at you. Then the wall shows the Door at the End of the World. \"Every set on the Watch Wall shows the Door at the End of the World. The static in it has gone black.\" That's What He Kept Out , and the title card for Part Two. He keeps his three things now."},{"p":"Chapter six: The Door at the End of the World","h":"Part three: what he kept out","u":"story/chapter-6.html#part-three-what-he-kept-out","t":"The Door's static has gone black : the dark on the far side of it, looking out. It hums, and the air is drawn into it. Walk into it. The other side is a stage behind the screen your world is shown on: the back of the screen behind you, as big as a cliff, with your world playing across it the wrong way round; the wings either side; painted flats of places from your story; footlights along the front; and past the edge, nothing. \"The other side. A stage, behind the screen your world's on - and past its edge, nothing. Something's sat out there in it.\" You can't sleep there (\"Not here. Not with it out there.\"). Fall off the edge and the dark puts you back on the boards, which hurts. The way home is the seam in the back of the screen ( The Other Side )."},{"p":"Chapter six: The Door at the End of the World","h":"Curtain Up","u":"story/chapter-6.html#curtain-up","t":"The first time anyone comes through, the Watcher is at a projector at the back of the stage. you came through. good. it hasn't looked this way. not yet. this is the other side. it's watched your world since the first picture. everything that ever happened to you - it watched. now it wants to see you up close. stay out of its eye. get behind the scenery. when it leans in - hit it. i'll run the projector. ??? Curtain Up"},{"p":"Chapter six: The Door at the End of the World","h":"The Viewer","u":"story/chapter-6.html#the-viewer","t":"Out in the dark, knees like hills, hands on the stage's edge with fingers like felled trees, and an eye opening: the Viewer , the last boss. It's so big you only ever fight its eye and its hands. Its gaze wanders the stage; stand in its light with the eye in sight of you and you're Seen , more and more, until it reaches for you. A flat between you and the eye hides you. When it leans in , its eye right at the stage's edge, hit it. With its eye shut nothing hurts it. Plywood stand-ins hop out of the wings and point at you to bring its eye straight to you; knock them over. His last projector does the rest. At two thirds he loads it with the Omni's Heart (\"...its eye's shut. now - the heart.\" then \"every colour at once. it's never seen that.\"), and it reels, blinded ( Every Colour at Once ). At one third he loads the Carrier (\"...the carrier. it carries whatever's put on it.\" then \"your world. all of it. out onto it.\"): the stand-ins burn and it gets up (\"it's getting up. keep its hands off the projector.\"). Standing, it comes faster, the footlights go out, and it reaches for the projector from both sides; beat its hands back ( It Gets Up ). Get through the first third without it ever seeing you right through for Out of Sight ."},{"p":"Chapter six: The Door at the End of the World","h":"The last show","u":"story/chapter-6.html#the-last-show","t":"It can't be killed. At the last it's held (\"...now. give it the reel.\"), and he threads his first reel and runs it, for it. everyone's always watched it. nobody ever showed it to itself. there. something to watch. it'll watch that forever. it won't look at your world again. somebody has to run the projector. go home. ...thank you for watching. ??? the last show Its own eye goes up on it. It goes still and sits back into the dark, watching itself. He sits down by the projector. Then black, and the credits: STATIC HOLLOW made by Death with the Hollow Saint · the Gardener, Reborn · the Great Bloom · the Flesh · the Carrier · the Chorus, whole · the Deaf King · the Crowd · the Projectionist and the Watcher (he's still running the projector) and you (who watched) THANK YOU FOR WATCHING Everyone who was there gets Thank You for Watching and the record Thank You for Watching . The Omni's Heart, what's left of the Carrier and his first reel are his again, and the Door's static goes back from black to grey. The story's music becomes The Show Goes On , the music box warm and in a major key at last, a projector still running somewhere and slowing. Chapter Six is done."},{"p":"Chapter six: The Door at the End of the World","h":"...not yet","u":"story/chapter-6.html#not-yet","t":"Since 1.59.0 the credits don't end there. They stop on THANK YOU FOR WATCHING, and he speaks: ...not yet. ??? over the last line of the credits His hand comes up through the picture, filling it, and closes round you. That's Chapter Seven: The First Signal . A world whose last show was over before 1.59.0 gets the same moment, the \"encore\", the next time anyone's at home."},{"p":"Chapter seven: The First Signal","h":"","u":"story/chapter-7.html","t":"The credits roll to their last line, THANK YOU FOR WATCHING, and stop. \"...not yet.\" His hand comes up through the picture and closes round you, and you're somewhere he made. Chapter Seven arrived in 1.59.0, and the mod calls it CHAPTER SEVEN - THE FIRST SIGNAL , \"to be continued\". Since 1.62.0 it runs straight on into Chapter Eight : the jump at its end no longer brings you home. See the landing below."},{"p":"Chapter seven: The First Signal","h":"The Hub","u":"story/chapter-7.html#the-hub","t":"Everyone who saw the last show is brought to the Hub ( The Hub ): a floating plaza of pale Hub Stone with his marks lit in it, in a sky of drifting static, pieces of realm hanging out in it every way. Along its north side is a gallery of six replay portals , one for each chapter, each playing its chapter on an old set. On its south side is the edge , a walk out over nothing. You can't sleep there. The Hub His speech, at the gallery of replay portals."},{"p":"Chapter seven: The First Signal","h":"His speech","u":"story/chapter-7.html#his-speech","t":"He turns round to you, and for once he talks for a long time: this is the hub. i made it. a realm. it isn't mine - nothing is - but i made it. through these, you can go back. every chapter. play it again. or jump off the edge. it'll take you home, and you can carry on. this was only the beginning. thank you. ...i could wipe you from existence, you know. find another one of you. but you passed the first trials. all of them. every one made me stronger. whatever held me back - it's gone. i can make realms now. make things you wouldn't dare believe could exist. all thanks to you. i think we'll be fighting forever. until one day i'm strong enough to bring you up to my level. what do you- ??? in the Hub As he says he can make realms now, he lifts a hand, and out in the static a new piece of realm comes together."},{"p":"Chapter seven: The First Signal","h":"ENOUGH","u":"story/chapter-7.html#enough","t":"The picture breaks up. The sky over the gallery tears open, and a voice comes out of it, low, huge, more than one voice at once: ENOUGH. He goes at the rift with both hands, pushing it shut, and a hand comes out of it and stops him. It tears the rift wide and comes through. The First Signal is your shape and your size. Its skin is crawling static. It wears a long charcoal studio coat, old broadcast headphones round its neck and a little red ON AIR lamp on its chest, lit, and a plain white mask with an eye in the dark behind each eye-hole, always on you. It never hurries. When it moves fast it skips like a signal, frames of it missing and its colours coming apart. It comes for you both. He turns to run, and it shakes its head: no. He stops, turns back, and shoves it with everything he has. It's thrown five hundred blocks out over the static, tumbling. It catches itself with a hand dug into the static, tears a piece of his realm loose, stamps it to rubble, and comes back in jumps, landing on the pieces of his realm one after another as each crumbles behind it. jump. ??? at the edge You go off the edge together. Falling, he shuts the realm behind you: a wall of static , slammed down. It stops at the wall with its hand flat against it. That's ENOUGH . The First Signal \"the first signal. it was here before me. before the first picture.\""},{"p":"Chapter seven: The First Signal","h":"The landing","u":"story/chapter-7.html#the-landing","t":"Where the fall takes you depends on when your world got here. Since 1.62.0 (any world that reaches the Hub from then on): falling, he tears a blue portal of signs open under you both, and you come down through it onto an oil rig in the Dead Water. What he says there, and the Remote breaking in your hand, are on Chapter Eight . You still get The First Signal and Channel Changer . In 1.59.0 to 1.61.1 the fall brought you home instead. He came down crouched beside you, wherever you landed: ...it's awake. the first signal. it was here before me. before the first picture. every bit of static you ever heard - that was it. asleep. i made a realm out of its static. and it noticed. i shut the realm behind us. it'll hold. for now. it'll come for me. then for you. ...we're going to need more than i've got. take this. if you need to go back - it's still there. ??? the landing (worlds that came down before 1.62.0) He looks up at a hairline tear across the sky, gives you the Remote and goes. The title card reads CHAPTER SEVEN , THE FIRST SIGNAL , to be continued , and the chat says: \"Somewhere past the static, the First Signal is awake - and it knows your name. Chapter Seven: The First Signal.\" Those worlds get Chapter Eight the next time someone takes the Remote to the Hub and jumps off its edge: he's there, falling beside you (\"not that way. not this time.\" \"hold on.\"), and tears the portal open under you."},{"p":"Chapter seven: The First Signal","h":"The Remote","u":"story/chapter-7.html#the-remote","t":"An old television's remote; its blank button is warm. Use it and you go into the Hub; use it in the Hub and you go home. The edge takes you home too, with no harm from the fall (but since 1.62.0, if you've never been down to the Dead Water, going off the edge takes you there instead: see Chapter Eight ). In the Hub the First Signal is still there, past the faint wall he shut, standing, watching you. Now and then you hear it. You can't sleep in the Hub (\"Not here. Not with it out there, past the wall.\"). Since 1.62.0 the Remote breaks in the Dead Water and has to be mended before it works again. Mended, crouch and press it to go back to the rig. See getting home ."},{"p":"Chapter seven: The First Signal","h":"Replays","u":"story/chapter-7.html#replays","t":"Walk into one of the gallery's portals and you're back at that chapter's place in your world. A moment later its last fight comes back for another go: Portal Where it takes you Who comes back The Hollow The Hollow Cathedral The Hollow Saint , rising out of the floor Act Two The Botanic Gardens' glasshouse The Gardener The Bloom The Great Bloom's arena The Gardener, Reborn The Flesh The Laboratory Specimen Zero The Static The Deep The Deaf King The Door The Stalls The Crowd , getting up out of the heap of them The story stays told: beating a replay sets nothing off (no new act, no lockdown, no tickets). Go far from it, leave, die or take too long, and the replay is over: \"The replay's over - it's gone back into the static.\" Your first one is Previously On... . When you've beaten it (\"beaten again\"), the Remote takes you back to the Hub."},{"p":"Chapter seven: The First Signal","h":"Rerun Reels","u":"story/chapter-7.html#rerun-reels","t":"Since 1.60.0 a replay beaten again leaves three or four Rerun Reels behind (\"AS SEEN BEFORE\"; Rerun ). Chapter Seven's gear, the On Air armour, the Antenna Glaive, the On Air Mace and the Hub-Stone tools, is made with them. See Gear for every chapter ."},{"p":"Chapter seven: The First Signal","h":"What comes next","u":"story/chapter-7.html#what-comes-next","t":"The story's music for this chapter is The First Signal : glass over a bowed bass, static under it all, a skip now and then, and its four notes, low. \"...we're going to need more than i've got.\" In worlds since 1.62.0 the next thing that happens is the Dead Water: Chapter Eight . Through Chapters Eight and Nine the First Signal is still there, past the wall in the Hub. In Chapter Ten he gives up on it, tears his own way out of the Hub to a kingdom of his own, and lets his creations out into your world. What he does after that is The Last Broadcast ."},{"p":"Chapter eight: The Dead Water","h":"","u":"story/chapter-8.html","t":"Off the edge of the Hub, with the First Signal behind a wall of static, the fall goes somewhere else. The Watcher tears a portal open under you both, and you come down onto an oil rig in a dead green sea that goes on until it doesn't. Chapter Eight arrived in 1.62.0, and 1.63.0 to 1.63.22 filled its sea. Since 1.63.5 it's one map , the same in every world, and since 1.63.6 each of its places stands there once, rebuilt bigger, and since 1.63.7 with people in it. The title card reads CHAPTER EIGHT , DEAD WATER , the deep is listening . Its realm is the Dead Water , a dimension of its own. When Orpheus has all three of her modules, it goes on into Chapter Nine ."},{"p":"Chapter eight: The Dead Water","h":"Getting there","u":"story/chapter-8.html#getting-there","t":"In a world that reaches the Hub in 1.62.0 or later, it follows straight on from ENOUGH : you jump, and falling, he tears a blue portal of signs open under you. A world that already had Chapter Seven's landing at home gets here the next time someone takes the Remote to the Hub and goes off its edge. He's there, falling beside you: not that way. not this time. hold on. ??? off the Hub's edge, in a world that landed before 1.62.0 Either way you come out over the rig's helipad and land, and he lands after you, crouched ( Dead Water ). ...we're out. it's awake now. the first signal. it'll come for me - then for you. but it can't hear us here. not through all this water. take this. it'll get you back - to the hub, and home. ...no. nothing of mine works right here. then you stay. there's food. beds. i built this place a long time ago - for when i needed somewhere to hide. fix it. the big ones down there sing on its frequency - cut out what they sing with. ??? on the rig's helipad He gives you the Remote , and it breaks in your hand, turning into the Broken Remote (press it and \"It sparks. The warm button's cold. Nothing.\"). Then he goes over the rail into the sea. The chat says what you need: \"Chapter Eight: Dead Water. The Remote's broken - mend it with a Static Leviathan's Signal Organ and a copper ingot. They live deep.\""},{"p":"Chapter eight: The Dead Water","h":"The rig","u":"story/chapter-8.html#the-rig","t":"An oil platform standing alone in the Dead Water, four great legs of rusted steel going down into the black. He built it a long time ago, he says, and it's been waiting with its lights on and its larders full: The cellar deck: the moon pool (a square of open water with a ladder down into it), the dive locker, the pumps, the pens (chickens, sheep, cows and a pig, let out when you arrive), the boat dock below it with two boats, and since 1.63.0 the sub bay off the dock, where the submarine Orpheus lies in its clamps, with its console on the catwalk beside her berth. The main deck: the quarters (eight beds), the mess and its kitchen, the infirmary, the workshop, the stores and the greenhouse (crops under glass, water channels, a composter). The upper deck: the control room, the radio room, the armoury, and the helipad you came down on. The derrick in the middle with red lights at its crown, two cranes, the flare stack out over the sea that never goes out, and the lifeboats. You're stranded until the Remote is mended. The rig's beds set your spawn but you can't sleep in them (\"You can't sleep here. The sea won't let you.\"). Die out here and the sea brings you back to the quarters: \"The sea brings you back. Nothing leaves the Dead Water while the Remote's broken.\" You can't lose the Broken Remote either; it's always still in your pocket. The rig's chests (the armoury, the dive locker, the mess, the stores, the sub bay) have what you'll need for the sea: the Harpoon Gun (hold to pump, let go to fire, in water or out; it reels you to the catch or the catch to you) and Harpoon Bolts, Marine Flares (a minute of red light, even underwater), Rig Rations and Air Tanks (a dozen breaths). Thirst and the cold (also new in 1.62.0) follow you here, so keep a canteen filled too. All of it is on Every item and block ."},{"p":"Chapter eight: The Dead Water","h":"The Watcher's chart","u":"story/chapter-8.html#the-watchers-chart","t":"A little after you come down, the Watcher presses a rolled chart into your hands: here. the sea, as far as i ever charted it. every water has its own colour. the black, hatched in red - that's the dead zone. the black below. nothing down there is small. don't take the little boat over it. ??? handing you his chart The Watcher's Chart shows every water in its own colour and named, the floor's depths shaded and contoured, and the Black Below hatched in red as THE DEAD ZONE. Since 1.63.5 it covers the whole sea, out past the edge all round, and since 1.63.6 every one of the sea's places is on it as a red cross with its name. Held, it's a map of the stretch you're in (a thousand blocks a square), with you as an arrow, the others down there with you, and the rig. Use it to unroll the whole chart: scroll to zoom, drag to look round, R to come back to you. Point at a water and you get his note on it. A Map, a Glow Ink Sac and a Prismarine Shard make another."},{"p":"Chapter eight: The Dead Water","h":"One sea","u":"story/chapter-8.html#one-sea","t":"Since 1.63.5 the Dead Water is laid out like one sea, the same in every world. The rig stands in the middle of the Grey Shelf. Round it is a ring of the shallow waters, one of each: the Lantern Fields, the Molar Reef, the Haemal Reach, the Drowned Mycelia and the Rime Shelf. Round that is a ring of the deeper ones: the Wireweed, the Brine Sink, the Ember Vents, the Carrier Wave and the Ossuary Flats. Their edges wander, and the floor slopes from one to the next. About three thousand blocks out the floor slopes down to the edge of everything and falls away: the Black Below , the void, all the way round, for ever. (A world that had already been to the Dead Water keeps the sea it had where it had been; the new map is where its sea is still new.)"},{"p":"Chapter eight: The Dead Water","h":"The twelve waters","u":"story/chapter-8.html#the-twelve-waters","t":"Each of the twelve waters has its own colour and murk, its own floor, plants, life, sound, music and light, and since 1.63.11 a fish of its own. The notes are his, from the chart. Water What it's like His note The Grey Shelf The rig's own grey-green, in the middle of the map. \"Grey water over grey silt. The rig stands in it. Nothing here is in a hurry - mostly.\" The Haemal Reach Blood-red water, thick as soup. Since 1.63.9 the Enzyme is in all of it. \"The water's thick with blood. Clotfish come in swarms; the Siphons wait for them to pass.\" The Wireweed Dark green, a forest of singing wire. \"Weed like wire, and it sings. The Choir Eels nest in it. Don't touch the bright ones.\" The Lantern Fields Black-blue and clear, lit by its plants. \"Lights in the dark as far as you can see. Most of them are bulbs. Some of them aren't.\" The Ossuary Flats Milky, a floor of bone sand. \"A plain of bone. Whatever died here, died big. The Stiltfins pick it clean.\" The Brine Sink Sick yellow-green, with lakes of brine that eat you. \"The brine pools eat what falls in. The water's sour, and the Puffbloats like it.\" The Molar Reef Teal and pink, a reef of teeth and gum. \"Teeth, grown into a reef. The Grinners live in it. They smile at you.\" The Drowned Mycelia Violet, spores in the water. Breathe it and the spores grow in you. \"Mushrooms the size of towers, drowned. Their spores burst if you brush them.\" The Rime Shelf Cold and clear under a roof of ice. \"Ice under the sea. Things are frozen in it. Some of them wake up.\" The Ember Vents Rust-orange, smoking vents. \"Vents roaring up from below. Warm. The Mantlecrabs crowd round them - mind your power.\" The Carrier Wave Blue-grey, static shimmering through it. \"The static's loudest here. The water hums. Your instruments won't like it.\" The Black Below The void past the edge, all the way round: the floor falls away and doesn't stop. Lost whales and the Omenfry are out there, and the Undertow. \"THE DEAD ZONE. Past the edge of all this the floor drops away and doesn't stop. Something lives out there that's bigger than the sea. Don't.\" What lives in them runs from cute to eldritch: gentle things like the one-eyed Pipeye and the singing Hymnback whales, hunters like the Clotfish, the Hookjaw (which steals your metal) and the Mantlecrab (its pulse kills every light near it, the submarine's too), and the Mouth of the Floor , buried in the "},{"p":"Chapter eight: The Dead Water","h":"Its places","u":"story/chapter-8.html#its-places","t":"Since 1.63.6 there's one of each of the sea's places, standing in its own water's own stretch of the map, every one of them rebuilt bigger, to go into. /locate structure finds each one from anywhere in the Dead Water (since 1.63.18 it sets you down in the water right beside it), and the Watcher's chart marks every one. Since 1.63.21 the floor round each is levelled to its own, so none stands in a pit or on a plinth. Place Water What's there The Lifeboat Graveyard The Grey Shelf The rig's fallen launching davit, lifeboats strewn round it, a raft, a buoy with its lamp still lit. The Drowned Heart The Haemal Reach A heart the size of a church, its four chambers hollow and joined. Something is kept in its right atrium. Since 1.63.18 it beats, once every forty seconds: swim toward the sound. The Haemal Research Station The Haemal Reach's near edge The lab where Enzyme 1-2418 was made, and got out (1.63.9). Its last log book, and the UV Dive Suit in the lockers. The Wireweed Mast The Wireweed A lattice mast fifty blocks high, its dish and red light, the operator's hut at its foot. Lantern Station The Lantern Fields A seabase: a glass-domed mess hall, a lab, a moon pool and a tower with a lookout bubble. The Leviathan Fall The Ossuary Flats The skeleton of something ninety blocks long, its ribs a hall, its skull a cave. Sink Station The Brine Sink Two huts on stilts over the brine lake, a crane and a sampling cage still down in the brine. The Jaw The Molar Reef A vault of gum and teeth to swim through, and a rotten molar with something hidden in it. The Drowned Grove The Drowned Mycelia A mushroom forty blocks high with a camp under its cap. Since 1.63.13 its hollow goes on down to the Grove Heart. The Rime Outpost and the Rime Spires The Rime Shelf A cabin and store shed locked in ice, and a great spire with someone sealed in clear ice at its heart. Ember Pumping Station The Ember Vents The pump house, the pipeline to the great vent and, since 1.63.10, a Nether portal sealed in the sea floor. The Wreck Field The Carrier Wave A cargo ship broken in two, its containers spilled (one full of televisions still showing static), a plane nose-down in the floor. The Canticle's Anchor The void, past the edge The anchor of the SS Canticle , a hundred blocks of it, and the Static Heart . Every place, inside and out, is on the Dead Water ."},{"p":"Chapter eight: The Dead Water","h":"The crews","u":"story/chapter-8.html#the-crews","t":"Since 1.63.7 the places have their own people. The Deep Hands still live and work down there in the old diving dress: the round copper helmet with a face behind its lit front glass, the brass corselet, lead on their boots, a big spanner. Each working place has its own crew in its own colours: the Ember Crew at the pumping station, Lantern Station's Keepers, Sink Station's Researchers, the Signal Keepers at the mast, the Salvagers in the Wreck Field and the Castaways at the Lifeboat Graveyard (and since 1.63.11 the Rime Crew, who hunt the frostjaws near their camp with harpoon guns). They walk from job to job, wave when you first come near and never go for you, except the Salvagers: hit one and the lot of them come for you with their spanners. Right-click one and it talks to you. Since 1.63.10 the Ember Crew trade, too. Not everyone who went down stayed themselves. The Drowned keep the Drowned Heart: the crew that went down to see what it was, their dress split and the Flesh coming out through it. The Sporeborn hang on their strings under the Drowned Grove's caps, and the Grove talks to you through them. The Stretched lie round the research station, the lab's divers as the Enzyme left them, until you come near. See the bestiary ."},{"p":"Chapter eight: The Dead Water","h":"What the water does to you","u":"story/chapter-8.html#what-the-water-does","t":"The Haemal Reach (1.63.9): Enzyme 1-2418 is in all of its water, and without the UV dress it gets into you. At 50 \"You want to go to the Heart. You don't know why.\", and it pulls you there. A flash of the UV Lamp burns a fifth of it out of you and the lab's Enzyme Inhibitor half; the UV Dive Suit keeps it out. The Drowned Mycelia (1.63.13): breathe its water and its spores build up in you, until \"The Grove has you.\" A sealed helmet keeps most of it out, Orpheus all of it, and a Spore Tonic burns sixty of it out of you. The deep (1.63.10): below about y -100 the sea crushes you, more the deeper you go. The Ember Deep Suit, made from what the pumping station's crew trade, keeps it off, and so does Orpheus. What the Grove, the Grove Heart, the Enzyme and Orpheus say to you down there is on Tapes and broadcasts ."},{"p":"Chapter eight: The Dead Water","h":"Orpheus","u":"story/chapter-8.html#orpheus","t":"The submarine Orpheus waits in its own sub bay off the rig's dock (1.63.0; it's added to rigs that were already up). Since 1.63.2 it's a real submarine thirteen blocks long, with a cabin you walk about in, for up to four people. Climb in by its hatch and down the ladder (\"The helm is up in the bow, under the dome; the bunks, lockers, galley and battery are aft. Walk about her, and use whatever you're looking at.\"). Climbing out (hold crouch) puts you down off her side; since 1.63.22 her cabin is dry air, and the sea starts at her glass. At the bow, under the dome: the helm (take it and drive; crouch to step away), the floodlight switches and the sonar console. Down its length: the chart table (the Watcher's chart), two bunks (lie down to heal, once every two minutes), lockers (27 slots, kept with the sub), a workbench, the galley (its hot plate cooks what you hold), the battery bank (charged with copper ingots, redstone or a block of redstone), the repair board (iron ingots patch the hull and the dome's cracks) and the motor. Driving: W/S thrust, A/D turn, jump to rise, sprint to dive. Use switches the floodlights (they light the water ahead, and draw things that love light, and things that hunt it), attack works its claw, and swap-hands pings the sonar. A submarine's sonar shows where a Mouth of the Floor lies. Depth: it's rated to 183 m down. Past that the hull creaks and the glass cracks, and at nothing it implodes."},{"p":"Chapter eight: The Dead Water","h":"Her upgrade bay","u":"story/chapter-8.html#her-upgrade-bay","t":"Since 1.63.8, use her motor (aft, in the engine room) and her upgrade bay opens: five mounts for modules, to fit, swap and take out as you like. What's in it is what she has, and the motor tells you her rating. Three modules matter for the story: Pressure Plating (iron blocks, Needle Teeth, Shroud Hide and obsidian, or found down there): no crush depth at all. She can go as deep as the sea goes. The Depth Module (280 m) : she's rated to 280 m with it. There's one in the parts crate on the sub bay's catwalk, and it can be made from iron blocks, copper blocks, tinted glass and a block of redstone. The UV Field Module (1.63.9; four UV Emitters, copper, glowstone and redstone): her floodlights burn violet and keep the Enzyme off her, and burn it out of her crew. Without it, in the Haemal Reach, she goes to flesh: her hull warm, then veined, then all of it, eyes and mouths, breathing. She talks to you, and begs. All the way, and she keeps you. Fit all three and the sea answers: see what comes next . Lost her? Since 1.63.21 the sub bay's console, on the catwalk by her berth, tells you where she is: in her clamps (her hull and power), out at sea (where she was last heard from, and how far), or nothing heard from her at all, and then the bay's welders build her again in her clamps, a minute's work, nothing asked of you. Use it crouching and she's scrapped where she lies and built again. Since 1.66.6, when she's lost her emergency locker blows free with everything that was in her lockers and the modules out of her bay, and floats at the top of the sea with its lamp blinking until someone empties it. Orpheus Its instruments: depth, hull, power, lamps and sonar."},{"p":"Chapter eight: The Dead Water","h":"The Static Heart","u":"story/chapter-8.html#the-static-heart","t":"Out past the edge, on the floor of the abyss, lies the Canticle's anchor (rebuilt in 1.63.8): a hundred blocks of it, its chain rising two hundred blocks out of the dark and broken off, and beside it the Canticle herself, her bow half sunk, her name on her side, a lamp still lit in her cabins. All round are the bones of what the Undertow has eaten: whales, a leviathan's skull with its jaws open, fish, divers. Its crown is hollow (go in on its west side), and in the hollow is the Static Heart : \"Warm, and beating - to no rhythm of its own. There's a picture in it, of nothing, always moving\". \"Keep it. Something is going to be made with it\"."},{"p":"Chapter eight: The Dead Water","h":"The Watcher, asleep","u":"story/chapter-8.html#the-watcher-asleep","t":"He went over the rail when you came down. Since 1.63.21 you can find where he went: straight down from where he went into the sea off the rig, he's there at the bottom, curled up, asleep, floating in a bubble of his own static with a faint light round him in the dark. Nothing gets into the bubble, and nothing you swing at it, throw at it or fire at it gets through: \"The bubble gives a little - then pushes you back out. He doesn't stir.\" He doesn't wake until the Turning ."},{"p":"Chapter eight: The Dead Water","h":"The Static Leviathan","u":"story/chapter-8.html#the-static-leviathan","t":"What you need lives deep. The Signal Organ comes from the Static Leviathan , a boss with its own bar, forty-five blocks long since 1.63.2, with fangs, tusks and its ribs showing through its rotted hide. It charges, it swallows you whole, and it sings on the Remote's frequency. Go more than forty blocks under the surface, anywhere but the Black Below, and now and then one comes up out of the dark after you. (Back home they live in the Overworld's new deep oceans too, down in the Hadal Dark and the Trench.)"},{"p":"Chapter eight: The Dead Water","h":"The Black Below","u":"story/chapter-8.html#the-black-below","t":"Don't take the little boat over it. Since 1.63.5 the void past the edge is the Undertow 's: go out over it at all, swimming, in Orpheus or in a boat on top of it, and stay, and something notices (sooner the deeper you are). A rumble from below, and it comes up out of the dark, a thing three thousand blocks long whose head is a flower of jaws. Get back over the edge and it lets you go. You can see it in the dark now, shaders or not: lines of cold light run the length of its body, a chevron of light over its back every twenty blocks, and its eyes glow, ringed in cold light, and stay on you. It doesn't come straight at you. It stalks you (\"Something vast is keeping pace with you, out in the dark.\"), off one shoulder; every half minute or so it slides up into the corner of your eye and holds there, and soon after it finds you it makes a pass right under you. It learns you (since 1.63.3), and tells you so: It has learned how you move. It saw you run for the surface. It will be waiting under you. It has learned your light. It keeps out of it. It knows you now. What it learns, it keeps. It eats when it's hungry (\"It is hungry.\"). Only when it's starving does it roar and come for you; before that, if a lost whale is near, it eats the whale instead (\"It has fed. For now.\"). Since 1.63.5 there's always a whale about: one comes out of the dark ahead of you within seconds of you going out over the void, the reef on its back glowing warm, and keeps near you, singing. When the Undertow comes, it roars (a submarine's glass cracks and its power dies), lunges and swallows you whole. Run for the surface and it breaches after you, hundreds of blocks into the sky."},{"p":"Chapter eight: The Dead Water","h":"Getting home","u":"story/chapter-8.html#getting-home","t":"Craft the Broken Remote, the Static Leviathan's Signal Organ and a copper ingot together ( Back On Air ): \"The Remote works again. Press it: the Hub (and in the Hub, home). Crouch and press it: back to the rig.\" The Dead Water stays yours to come back to. The rig and each of the twelve waters have music of their own."},{"p":"Chapter eight: The Dead Water","h":"What comes next","u":"story/chapter-8.html#what-comes-next","t":"The First Signal is still awake, past the wall in the Hub. \"it'll come for me - then for you.\" But the next thing to come up isn't him. Once Orpheus has all three of her modules in her bay, the pressure plating, the depth module and the UV field module, the Undertow comes up out of the sea by the rig, and the Watcher wakes: Chapter Nine: The Harbinger ."},{"p":"Chapter nine: The Harbinger","h":"","u":"story/chapter-9.html","t":"Orpheus has all three of her modules, and the sea goes wrong. The Undertow comes up out of the water by the rig and roars, goes down through the Grove and through the Drowned Heart, and comes back as something its maker never made. Chapter Nine arrived in 1.63.23, and 1.63.24 and 1.63.25 mended it. The title card reads CHAPTER NINE , THE HARBINGER , three days . It happens in the Dead Water , round the rig, and it has two pieces of music of its own, The Turning and The Harbinger . What it makes is the Harbinger ."},{"p":"Chapter nine: The Harbinger","h":"The Turning","u":"story/chapter-9.html#the-turning","t":"Once Orpheus has all three of her modules in her bay (the pressure plating, the depth module and the UV field module), it plays, for everyone in the Dead Water: off whatever you're in (she's put back in her clamps), out of any screen, up onto the rig's helipad. A full cutscene, with its own score. The Undertow comes up out of the sea by the rig and roars . Then it goes. To the Drowned Mycelia, down through the roof of the Grove's hollow, and it eats the Grove Heart, which has one thing left to say, in a voice that isn't anyone's: \"...no. not you. not you.\" To the Haemal Reach, and through the Drowned Heart. With both in it, it turns: the Grove's fungus up its left side, pale, gilled, caps growing out of it; the Reach's flesh up its right, raw and veined, its light gone red. It comes back mad, up out of the sea hundreds of blocks and down, again and again round the rig, and the last time it comes down by the rig, and lies there. Down under where he went in, the sleeping Watcher wakes. His bubble breaks, and he comes up out of the sea and onto the helipad beside you. After his first words, you point at it. ...what the hell is happening? ...what is that? i never made that. i made this place. every wreck, every fish in it. not that - i don't know how it got in here. and the grove's fungus is in it now. the virus - in my safe world. and the divers. what the enzyme made of them. i should have told you. it ate both hearts. they're in it now. one thing. it isn't dead. it's sleeping. whatever it is - we have to kill it. if we do - its static's still in there. we put it in your remote. something stronger than it ever was. then we go back to the hub. ??? on the helipad, looking at it That's CHAPTER NINE , and The Turning (\"Watch the Undertow eat both hearts - and come down by the rig\"). The chat says: \"Chapter Nine: The Harbinger. It lies in the sea by the rig, both infections all over it - he says it's sleeping. Three days.\""},{"p":"Chapter nine: The Harbinger","h":"Three days","u":"story/chapter-9.html#three-days","t":"It lies in the sea north-east of the rig, its jaws about a hundred blocks off (on your left, looking out to sea from the helipad): the husk, its eyes shut, both infections all over it, spores steaming off one side and blood off the other. From the rig you can hear its heart, beating faster as the days go. There's no fight. It just lies there. And with it lying there, nothing comes up out of the Black Below, the Grove's Heart doesn't grow back, and the Drowned Heart doesn't beat. The Watcher keeps watch at the helipad's rail, and has something to say each day when you come near him: The first day ??? i've been through everything i ever made. it isn't in any of it. where did it come from? The second day ??? the lab's log said three days. that's how long the enzyme takes to finish what it starts. The third day ??? tomorrow. whatever it's turning into, it's nearly done. stay near. The three days are 72,000 ticks. The Dead Water's sky never moves and nobody sleeps there, so they count by the Overworld's clock (since 1.63.24): nights slept through at home, or /time add , bring the Harbinger on."},{"p":"Chapter nine: The Harbinger","h":"The Harbinger","u":"story/chapter-9.html#the-harbinger","t":"Three days on, the next time you're in the Dead Water, it happens. Its bones come out through its mouth: a skull, a spine and its ribs, strung all through with the Grove's strings out of the heart in its ribs, where the Grove's heart and the Reach's are going into one (\"Two hearts become one\"). It rises over the sea, hung on its strings, and brings up the static heart at your feet, one for each of you. Then the heart speaks to you both, in two voices whispering as one: The Grove's voice and the Reach's, together thank you for making us one. this gift will not be wasted. we would want you to join us. to be stronger. both of you. but we have more important work to do. It tears a way out of the Dead Water, half the Grove's and half the Reach's, and goes through it. The husk goes down into the sea. ...it's gone. pick it up. put it in your remote. i'll meet you at the hub. ??? after it's gone through That's This Gift Will Not Be Wasted (\"See what came out of it after three days\"). The chat says: \"It's gone through. The static heart it brought up is on the helipad - put it in the Remote (craft them together).\""},{"p":"Chapter nine: The Harbinger","h":"The Remote (Mutated)","u":"story/chapter-9.html#the-remote-mutated","t":"What it brought up is the Static Heart (Mutated) , \"Thrown up by the Harbinger\": \"The Undertow's static, grown through with the Grove's threads and the Reach's flesh. It still beats - a little faster than yours.\" Craft it with the Broken Remote (or the mended one) and you have the Remote (Mutated) : \"It works again - and it roars\". Press it: the Hub (and in the Hub, home). Crouch and press it: the Dead Water. Hold it, then let go: the Undertow's roar comes out of your hand. Everything near you that isn't with you is thrown back, torn at and slowed (half as far again under water), and its echo makes everything alive for 48 blocks round glow. Then it's spent for fifteen seconds. The first time is Its Roar, In Your Hand . So you're not stranded any more, whether or not you ever mended the Remote with a Signal Organ. See Every item and block ."},{"p":"Chapter nine: The Harbinger","h":"What comes next","u":"story/chapter-9.html#what-comes-next","t":"\"i'll meet you at the hub.\" The Harbinger has gone through its way out, and nobody has said where it goes. The next time you're home, back at your bed or your spawn in the Overworld, or home by the Remote, something cuts in on you: Chapter Ten: Stay Tuned ."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"","u":"story/index.html","t":"Static Hollow tells one story across ten chapters, and the tenth goes on in The Last Broadcast. You don't need to read anything to follow it: the Watcher tells you where to go, the needles it hands you point there, and the papers left on lecterns fill in what happened before you arrived. This page is the whole path in order, for when you've lost the thread."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"How the story is told","u":"story/index.html#how-the-story-is-told","t":"The Watcher. A tall black figure with glowing eyes, named only \"???\" in the game. It never attacks. It turns up at each turning point, says a few words in chat, and points. Everything it says is collected on its own page. The First Signal. From Chapter Seven on, the thing that was here before him. Its words come with no name on them, in a cutscene or in dark red in chat. Everything it says has a page too. Title cards. The big moments put words across your screen, like THE FLESH WAKES / the flower made it and CHAPTER FIVE . Trackers and needles. When you need to collect parts, a tracker along the top of the screen counts them. When a new place wakes, the Watcher hands everyone a needle: a compass that only ever points there. Papers and tapes. Almost every place has a journal, a log or a notice on a lectern or in a chest. The Laboratory's tapes are voiced. All of them are on the lore pages . Cutscenes. The biggest moments take the camera: the Device's last flight, the Omni Ray, the Watcher taking the Omni back, the late show at the drive-in, signing off, the Chorus speaking ( It Speaks , The Mind , It Runs ), Front Row, the Watch, the First Reel, Curtain Up, the last show and its credits, the Hub and ENOUGH, the rig, the Turning and the Harbinger, the Broadcast, and every part of The Last Broadcast. In the modpack they play since 1.47.1 (Entity Culling used to stop them). Music. Since 1.55.0 none of Minecraft's music plays. The world keeps track of how far its story has got, and its music follows: the further along, the more often it's the chapter's own piece. See the soundtrack ."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"The whole path, in order","u":"story/index.html#the-whole-path","t":""},{"p":"Story overview","h":"Wake the Forsaken Altar","u":"story/index.html#wake-the-forsaken-altar","t":"Chapter one Every world has one, 500 to 1000 blocks from spawn. Follow the blue smoke, then right-click the altar with an empty hand. The nine creepypastas start hunting everyone in the world."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"Take nine heads","u":"story/index.html#take-nine-heads","t":"Each creepypasta always drops its head the first time you kill one. After your ninth kill the Watcher tells you about a church that isn't on any map."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"Raise the Hollow Saint","u":"story/index.html#raise-the-hollow-saint","t":"In the cathedral, put one head of each of the nine on the pedestals round the Hollow Reliquary and right-click it. Kill the Saint and the Watcher's beam drags it down to hell."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"Go through the Breach","u":"story/index.html#go-through-the-breach","t":"Chapter two Where the Saint fell, a red wound tears open in the ground. It leads into the Void, to the Breach Altar on a floating island."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"Wake the Breach Altar","u":"story/index.html#wake-the-breach-altar","t":"Every creepypasta is dragged back down. In their place come five killers and four things from the woods. The Watcher tells you where they live: the Murder Mansion."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"Feed the Mending Altar","u":"story/index.html#feed-the-mending-altar","t":"One head from each of the new nine on the trophy pedestals. The Watcher sews them into the Mended . Kill it for the Rusted Garden Key."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"Open the glasshouse","u":"story/index.html#open-the-glasshouse","t":"Chapter three The key opens the Botanic Gardens. Find the Gardener's clothes before you wake him, then kill the Gardener at his flower."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"Go down the root","u":"story/index.html#go-down-the-root","t":"Three days later a green rift opens over the dead flower. Wear the Gardener's Weeds and go through into the Bloom . Break the Binding and run: ten seconds."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"The Great Bloom rises","u":"story/index.html#the-great-bloom-rises","t":"It comes up the root and through the glasshouse, and takes the gardens' place for good."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"The Flesh wakes","u":"story/index.html#the-flesh-wakes","t":"Chapter four Ten seconds later, what the flower was holding down punches up out of the ground east of the gardens, and starts to spread."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"Collect the reactor's three parts","u":"story/index.html#collect-the-reactors-three-parts","t":"The Rear Assembly from a truck in Rosemont, the Core from the Laboratory's pool, the Front Assembly from Shelter No. 4, past its Warden ."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"Build the Rosemont Device","u":"story/index.html#build-the-rosemont-device","t":"Wire the three parts in the Assembly Cradle, or bring them to a Forsaken Altar and let the Watcher build it. Carry it to the Bloom. The Flesh lets you pass."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"Kill the Gardener twice more","u":"story/index.html#kill-the-gardener-twice-more","t":"The Bloom spits the Gardener, Reborn back up at you, and when he dies it grows him back again."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"Launch the Device","u":"story/index.html#launch-the-device","t":"The Watcher tears the Bloom open. Set the Device on the launch mark, arm it, run. It goes off inside the Bloom, and the Bloom changes."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"Build a gun that talks to the sky","u":"story/index.html#build-a-gun-that-talks-to-the-sky","t":"Three places wake. Bring back the power source parts, have the Watcher infuse the core, and build the Orbital Railgun. Three more places wake for the Ray Gun's parts."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"Call down the Omni","u":"story/index.html#call-down-the-omni","t":"The Watcher turns the Ray Gun into the Omni . Fire it at the changed Bloom and SENTINEL comes down out of orbit. Then the Watcher takes the gun back and goes to rest."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"Ten days later","u":"story/index.html#ten-days-later","t":"The Watcher finds you wherever you are, with a warning: the parasites came from somewhere else."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"The static comes","u":"story/index.html#the-static-comes","t":"Chapter five Static Hound packs at night. One villager in every village hollowed out. Parasites that get into you and grow."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"Take Relay 6 off the air","u":"story/index.html#take-relay-6-off-the-air","t":"Climb the mast, cut the tethers, and kill the Amalgam at its foot. It leaves the Relay Core."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"Run the last reel","u":"story/index.html#run-the-last-reel","t":"At the Starlite Drive-In , kill Afterimages for four frames and hold them off the projector to the end."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"Signing off","u":"story/index.html#signing-off","t":"Hold the reel over the tear and go down into the Null Static Zone . Cut the Carrier loose and kill it. The screen at the drive-in shows one line: SIGNING OFF."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"The outbreak, and the End shut","u":"story/index.html#the-outbreak-and-the-end-shut","t":"The Carrier carried them all the way out. The Watcher comes to tell you the parasite's numbers are going off the charts, and shuts the End. From now on the outbreak is worse."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"The Hive","u":"story/index.html#the-hive","t":"It speaks through five of its pure forms, and the Watcher hands you a needle to the Hive . Tear open the four nerve nodes and bring the Chorus down to a quarter. It runs, deep, and leaves a fragment of itself."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"Down into the Deep","u":"story/index.html#down-into-the-deep","t":"Follow the fragment's whispers to the Sinkhole , down the Burrow to the Throat, and into the Deep. Kill the Deaf King for his ear-stones."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"The Chorus, whole","u":"story/index.html#the-chorus-whole","t":"In the Warm Heart it rises out of the blood. Kill it for good. It leaves the Last Voice, and the Watcher tells you about a seal he made."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"Break the seal","u":"story/index.html#break-the-seal","t":"Chapter six Carry the Last Voice into the End. The seal breaks (\"...don't.\"), and out past the obsidian stands the Door at the End of the World."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"The Stalls","u":"story/index.html#the-stalls","t":"Sneak past the Audience and the Ushers' lamps in the Stalls , step onto the front aisle and bring down the Crowd . The Watcher was in the front row. He goes through the screen."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"The Watcher's Vault","u":"story/index.html#the-watchers-vault","t":"The Last Ticket opens the seam. In the Vault , take his three kept things to the Watch, kill the Projectionist , and see his first reel."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"What he kept out","u":"story/index.html#what-he-kept-out","t":"Through the black door to the other side . Stay out of the Viewer 's eye while he runs the projector, until it's held and shown itself. The credits roll."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"The Hub","u":"story/index.html#the-hub","t":"Chapter seven \"...not yet.\" His hand takes you to the Hub . His speech is cut short: ENOUGH. The First Signal breaks in. Jump."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"The Dead Water","u":"story/index.html#the-dead-water","t":"Chapter eight Falling, he tears a portal open under you, onto a rig in the Dead Water . The Remote breaks in your hand. Mend it with a Static Leviathan's Signal Organ, and keep out of the Black Below, where the Undertow is."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"Fit out Orpheus","u":"story/index.html#fit-out-orpheus","t":"The sea's places each stand once, with their crews, from the Drowned Heart to the Canticle's anchor out past the edge. Put all three modules in the submarine's upgrade bay: the pressure plating, the depth module and the UV field module."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"The Turning","u":"story/index.html#the-turning","t":"Chapter nine The Undertow comes up by the rig, eats the Grove Heart and the Drowned Heart, and turns. The Watcher wakes out of his bubble: it isn't dead, it's sleeping."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"Three days","u":"story/index.html#three-days","t":"It lies in the sea by the rig, its heart beating faster. Three days on, the Harbinger comes out of it, leaves you the Static Heart (Mutated) and goes through a way out. Craft the heart into the Remote. \"i'll meet you at the hub.\""},{"p":"Story overview","h":"The Broadcast","u":"story/index.html#the-broadcast","t":"Chapter ten Next time you're home it cuts in: the First Signal leaves the Hub's wall for a kingdom of his own , takes the Harbinger for his, and lets his creations out into your world. The Watcher comes to your door: \"get ready.\""},{"p":"Story overview","h":"Stay tuned","u":"story/index.html#stay-tuned","t":"They come every night, more each time, a different programme every night on Channel Zero. Hide in lockers, under beds and in the tall grass. Break the Broadcast Cores in his transmitters, burrows and sets, and make Blackout from what they leave."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"A way in","u":"story/index.html#a-way-in","t":"Where a core stood, his signal's torn open for a minute. Step through into his kingdom, and he throws you out of it: the Refusal."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"The Coronation","u":"story/index.html#the-coronation","t":"The Last Broadcast Two days later he's crowned, with a blade drawn out of the Harbinger, in an arena raised out of his sea. Fight him on its floor with the Watcher's gifts, until he takes his towers' power and the Watcher calls down SENTINEL."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"The Fall and the Forge","u":"story/index.html#the-fall-and-the-forge","t":"He tears SENTINEL in half. Its wreck brings the hive back, into the Harbinger. Bring him to half with the Omni's help: his Faithful forge him, and he drains SENTINEL's light into himself."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"The Tearing and the Second Rite","u":"story/index.html#the-tearing-and-the-second-rite","t":"He tears his arena up into the End, where the hive has the dragon. At a fifth of him he takes its head, wings and heart, and fights you on its wings. Bring him down, and the Watcher gets up and fights him; his Faithful take him, and the Harbinger is reborn. To be continued. Tune-In Town A secret that can turn up any time after your first day: a HELP WANTED flyer on an old television, for the night shift at Tune-In Town Pizza & Playhouse. It has flashing lights, loud noises and jumpscares, and once you take the job you're kept there for five nights. Read the photosensitivity warning first. See Tune-In Town ."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"The chapters","u":"story/index.html#the-chapters","t":"1. The Nine The altar, the nine creepypastas, the cathedral and the Hollow Saint. 2. The Breach The Void, the killers and cryptids, the Murder Mansion and the Mended. 3. The Glasshouse The Gardener, the green rift and the Great Bloom. 4. The Flesh Rosemont, the Device, the changed Bloom and the Omni. 5. The Static Hounds, the relay, the drive-in, the Carrier, the outbreak, the Hive and the Deep. 6. The Door at the End of the World The seal, the Stalls, the Watcher's Vault, the other side and the last show. 7. The First Signal After the credits: the Hub, ENOUGH, the Remote and the replays. 8. The Dead Water The rig, the twelve waters and their places, Orpheus and the Undertow. 9. The Harbinger The Turning, three days, the Harbinger and the mutated Remote. 10. Stay Tuned The Broadcast, his creations, Channel Zero, his sites, hiding and a way in. The Last Broadcast The Refusal, the Coronation, the Fall, the Forge, the Tearing and the Second Rite."},{"p":"The Last Broadcast","h":"","u":"story/the-last-broadcast.html","t":"You came into his house. He throws you out of it. Two days later he crowns himself, pulls a blade out of the Harbinger, and lifts an arena up out of his sea to fight you in. The Watcher calls down the biggest thing he can, and the First Signal takes it. The Last Broadcast is the rest of Chapter Ten , in four parts: part one, the Refusal (1.68.0); part two, the Coronation, his arena and the Call (1.69.0); part three, the Fall, the second quarter and the Forge (1.70.0); and part four, the Tearing, the End's guardian, the Second Rite and the Rebirth (1.71.0), with the fight on the dragon's wings added in 1.72.0. From part two on, each part runs straight on into the next, and it ends, for now, on to be continued . It all happens in his kingdom , and at the end in the End. Nobody is hurt by any of its cutscenes, and anyone else there sees them too. Its fight has its own music, The Last Broadcast ."},{"p":"The Last Broadcast","h":"Part one: the Refusal","u":"story/the-last-broadcast.html#part-one-the-refusal","t":""},{"p":"The Last Broadcast","h":"The Refusal","u":"story/the-last-broadcast.html#the-refusal","t":"The first time you come through one of his tears into his kingdom after the Broadcast (or if you're there already), it's a cutscene. His castle, across the black water. In his hall he's at his war table, his hands flat on his map, and he goes still. His head comes up. The First Signal, at his table ...you. The scream; his fists down on his table three times, his map's lights jumping you came into MY house? His static comes up out of the sea between his platform and his castle, and the castle's gone behind it. He's there, through it, on the platform in front of you, his hand at your throat GET. OUT. He holds you out at arm's length, your toes just off the floor (since 1.72.1), and throws you back out of the tear you came in by, hard, the way the Watcher threw him out of the Hub. It shuts behind you, and in chat, in dark red: \"and STAY out.\" Anyone else in his kingdom with you is thrown out with you (\"Thrown out of his kingdom.\")."},{"p":"The Last Broadcast","h":"His static","u":"story/the-last-broadcast.html#his-static","t":"For the rest of that day his static stands across his causeway. Come back through a tear and there's no getting past it; it throws you back: \"His static stands across his causeway. He's shut you out - for today.\""},{"p":"The Last Broadcast","h":"His map of your world","u":"story/the-last-broadcast.html#his-map","t":"The next day his static's gone, and he isn't at his table. His war map isn't the one it was any more: it's your world, your house in the middle of it ringed in red, two thousand blocks either side of it and more along the length of his table, worked out from your world's own ground (the sea and the lakes, the rivers, the woods, the deserts, the snow, the heights in contour), his red grid over it every five hundred blocks. And lit on it as they move: any of you out in your world, his creations, his sites. Your house. On his map. His war map isn't the one it was. It's your world - your house in the middle of it, two thousand blocks all round it - lit wherever any of you are, wherever his creations are, wherever his sites stand. And he isn't at his table. His Faithful are at their rites as they were (and can be killed)."},{"p":"The Last Broadcast","h":"Part two: the Coronation","u":"story/the-last-broadcast.html#part-two-the-coronation","t":""},{"p":"The Last Broadcast","h":"The third day","u":"story/the-last-broadcast.html#the-third-day","t":"Two days after the Refusal, come through to his kingdom and something enormous is in the black water round his castle: \"Something enormous is moving in the water round his castle.\" It's the Harbinger , the Undertow taken by his static, up out of the sea, over and down again, now here, now there, well out from his castle and never over his causeway."},{"p":"The Last Broadcast","h":"The Coronation","u":"story/the-last-broadcast.html#the-coronation","t":"Walk up his causeway (or wait long enough) and it's a cutscene. The Watcher tears his way through after you: \"i couldn't let you come here alone.\" The two of you walk up to him together. The First Signal ...both of you. good. you'll want to see this. His Faithful stand round him in a ring and lift the daggers he made them, and give themselves to him with them. What they were streams into him: his armour forms out of them, piece by piece, and their daggers come together over his head as his crown. The Harbinger comes up out of the sea behind him, and out of it he draws his blade : huge, black and alive, the Undertow's own teeth set along its edge as fangs, and an eye in it near the hilt that blinks and looks about. Then he speaks, to the Watcher first and then to you: The First Signal, crowned you've gone too far, Watcher. every code. every rule. you broke them all. so the order now is your erasure. every world you made. every realm. every creature. i'll rip that poor void heart out of you - and keep it. and that will be the end of time. the most powerful creation. pulling the strings - forever. as i should be. and you... i have no use for you. don't make me angrier, and i'll give you a whole new world. but i know what you want. YOU'LL BOTH FAIL. stay behind me. i've nothing left to fight him with - but what i have is yours. ??? to you, after his speech His arena comes up out of the sea off his island's east side: its floor, tier on tier of seats, his Faithful flashing into them, his own box high on its north side. He goes up to his box. \"He's crowned. His arena's up out of the sea - step down onto its floor and he'll come down to you.\""},{"p":"The Last Broadcast","h":"His arena","u":"story/the-last-broadcast.html#his-arena","t":"It's over the bridge from his island's east side. Step down onto its floor and he comes down off his box at you (\"COME, THEN.\"), crowned, with his blade, under a bar of his own: The First Signal, Crowned . He sweeps it round in front of him and lunges straight through you; there's his hand, his skips, his static on the floor, his scream, and his creations called in (\"STAY TUNED.\"). Since 1.71.2 the blade winds back with a whine, static crawling up it, before it comes round in great cuts that tear up the floor. The Watcher stands by the gate with no power left of his own, but every so often he gives each of you on the floor what he has: thirty seconds of something at its strongest, level V (Strength, Speed, Regeneration, Haste, Absorption, Health Boost, Jump Boost or Fire Resistance). \"The Watcher gives you [it] V - for thirty seconds.\" here. take it. it's all i have. use it. go on - while it lasts. for thirty seconds, you're more than him. take it. don't waste it. ??? one of these, with each gift Stay off its floor long enough and he's back up in his box, whole. His arena stays: it's there whenever you come back. His Faithful sometimes drop the daggers he made them (one in five), a quick blade. The fight itself is on the First Signal ."},{"p":"The Last Broadcast","h":"The Mast","u":"story/the-last-broadcast.html#the-mast","t":"Take a quarter of him and it's a cutscene. \"...enough.\" He's gone from the floor to his castle's roof, his hand on his mast, and every lamp on his towers goes dark, into him. The Watcher's on his knees: \"no... he's taking it. all of it. mine too.\" His laugh: \"ha. ha ha. HA HA HA HA.\" And the Watcher takes out the Omni . then i'll call down something bigger. ??? with the Omni in his hands He fires it up into the sky, the call, and the sky over the castle tears open. (In 1.69.0 it stopped there, on a card: THE LAST BROADCAST , THE CALL , to be continued . Since 1.70.0 there's no card: the Fall goes straight on from it.)"},{"p":"The Last Broadcast","h":"Part three: the Fall","u":"story/the-last-broadcast.html#part-three-the-fall","t":""},{"p":"The Last Broadcast","h":"The Fall","u":"story/the-last-broadcast.html#the-fall","t":"The call goes straight on into the Fall (in a world where the call was already made, it plays the next time any of you is in his kingdom). THE LAST BROADCAST , THE FALL , part three . The sky over his castle rips open right across the north, black in it and his colour bars round its edge, and through it comes SENTINEL . All of it this time, not just its gun: three thousand blocks of station, its hub, its gun under it, two habitat rings on their spokes, its truss out to its wingtips, its solar wings, radiators and modules, a docking spine with ships on it, its windows lit and its lamps blinking. It stops over his castle, and its gun charges at him, its read-out counting up along the top of the picture: \"SENTINEL // MAIN GUN CHARGING\". The First Signal you called THAT down on me? The Watcher: \"...come on. come on.\" At half its charge, he puts everything he took from his towers up through his blade then watch it fall. His blast tears SENTINEL's right side off: \"HULL BREACH // SECTIONS 4-9 // CONTAINMENT LOST // HOLD B OPEN\". \"no. no, no, no -\", says the Watcher. That half comes down burning into his sea far out (the sea goes up where it hits, and it lies there after, its broken end up out of the water), and a module of it comes down near, east of his arena."},{"p":"The Last Broadcast","h":"SENTINEL's wreck and crew","u":"story/the-last-broadcast.html#sentinels-wreck","t":"The module stays: real blocks, lying tilted in the sea, its hatch end up out of the water and its far end torn open, scorched, the parasites' resin in it, its windows, deck and lamps (some out), bits of its solar wing and a girder round it, fires on its back. Its crew's chest is still in it, with SENTINEL's crew log among what's in there. Its crew, the SENTINEL Crew , astronauts in their white suits and gold visors, climb out of its hatch onto its hull, their radio breaking up: SENTINEL - to anyone. we're down. we are DOWN. SENTINEL where are we? that's not... that's not our sky. SENTINEL everyone out. Reyes - check the hold. SENTINEL ...something's moving in the hold. SENTINEL what IS that - SENTINEL get it OFF me - get it - SENTINEL stay back. STAY BACK. SENTINEL brought Blackwater's parasites up with it, and they're out of the hold and onto the crew, one after another. The last of them backs off to the end of the hull, and the parasites stop, and the Chorus 's last voice speaks through them: \"...one voice left.\" \"it will do.\" They pour into him, and the hive comes up through him: \"we hear you, signal.\" The Harbinger comes up out of the sea beside the wreck and swallows him whole, and the hive gets into it (its bones go violet). \"what... what was THAT?\", says the Watcher. A door of the hive's chitin opens on the air out past the wreck, and it goes out through it and is gone. And from his roof: The First Signal ...your toy brought guests. NOW. WHERE WERE WE."},{"p":"The Last Broadcast","h":"The second quarter","u":"story/the-last-broadcast.html#the-second-quarter","t":"Straight after, he's on his arena's floor again with three-quarters of him left, and the fight goes on to half of him: \"SENTINEL's down - and so's what was in it. He's on his arena's floor again, three-quarters of him left. The Watcher has the Omni: when he fires it, hit him.\" Every half-minute or so the Watcher fires it into him and puts him down on one knee, his armour cracking and burning at the seams, and while he's down everything hurts him half again as much (\"The Omni! He's down - hit him now!\"). New, too: he puts his blade up at the rip, and bolts of his static come down where each of you is standing (red rings on the floor first: get out of them)."},{"p":"The Last Broadcast","h":"The Forge","u":"story/the-last-broadcast.html#the-forge","t":"Take half of him and it's a cutscene. The Omni puts him on his knee. \"...my Faithful.\" They come down out of their seats to him in flashes of his static, lay their hands on his armour and close its cracks, and chant their glyphs into it: his armour and his blade enchanted, glyphs crawling over them. He gets up and tells you what it was all for. The First Signal, mended ...is that it? a gun in the sky. a crew who never asked to come. they fell for you. remember that. and you, Watcher. still on your knees. every signal that ever went out comes home to me. everything they built up there. every last watt of it - IS MINE. He puts his blade up at what's left of SENTINEL and tears every bit of its light out of it, down into him, till it's dark (\"he's draining it. all of it.\", says the Watcher). (In 1.70.0 it stopped there, on a card: THE LAST BROADCAST , THE FORGE , to be continued . Since 1.71.0 there's no card: the Tearing goes straight on from it.) His kingdom's wall of static stands further out now, past where the wreck came down."},{"p":"The Last Broadcast","h":"Part four: the Tearing","u":"story/the-last-broadcast.html#part-four-the-tearing","t":""},{"p":"The Last Broadcast","h":"The Tearing","u":"story/the-last-broadcast.html#the-tearing","t":"The Forge goes straight on into the Tearing (in a world where it was forged already, it plays a few seconds after any of you is in his kingdom). THE LAST BROADCAST , THE TEARING , part four . \"this sea's too small for me now.\" He puts his blade straight up, and the sky over his arena tears open, flat across it, as wide as the arena, colour bars round its edge. The Watcher: \"...what is he doing?\" His sea pours off it, its walls groan, its bridge breaks, and the whole of it is torn up out of his sea (\"HOLD ON TO SOMETHING.\"), and you with it, up into the tear."},{"p":"The Last Broadcast","h":"The End's guardian","u":"story/the-last-broadcast.html#the-ends-guardian","t":"His arena hangs out over the void north of the End's island, a ragged cone of the rock it was torn out of under it, its bridge snapped off short, pieces of it hanging loose in the air round it. \"...the End. he's brought it all to the End.\", says the Watcher. Up out of the dark comes the End's guardian : the Ender Dragon, taken, its back split open, the parasite all through it and the hive's growths on it. It circles. The First Signal the last thing your world kept for itself. and look what's kept it all this time. He comes down off his box. The dragon circles his arena; now and then it comes round at one of you and strafes you (its fireballs burst into its breath on the floor), or dives at you, low and fast. It can't be brought down. Only he can do that."},{"p":"The Last Broadcast","h":"The fight in the End","u":"story/the-last-broadcast.html#the-fight-in-the-end","t":"Half of him is gone already, and this time he fights to a fifth of him (15%). He's forged now, enchanted and alight with SENTINEL's power, and the Watcher still has the Omni and still fires it into him every half-minute or so. Step down onto the floor and he leaps down to you (\"AGAIN.\"). Fall off the edge into the void and his static catches you and puts you back on the floor, and it hurts (\"Caught by his static - and put back.\"). Anyone who comes to his kingdom now is carried on through to his arena in the End (\"Carried through to the End - to his arena.\"), and the End lets you in to it while all this is going on."},{"p":"The Last Broadcast","h":"The Second Rite","u":"story/the-last-broadcast.html#the-second-rite","t":"At 15% it's a cutscene. \"...not like this.\" Then \"YOU. you'll do.\" He's up onto the dragon's neck as it comes down at him, his blade in it, riding it round over his arena, and it comes down on the floor. He takes its head off; tears its wings off; reaches into its chest and pulls out its heart. His Faithful come down to him and sing the second rite round him, their glyphs lit in a ring on the floor: The Faithful, chanting \"head to crown him. wings to bear him.\" \"heart to keep him. ours, for ever.\" Its head over his is his helm: since 1.72.2 its skull forms over his piece by piece, out of nothing, red-hot, its eye sockets lit violet and two pairs of horns swept back between his crown's daggers. Its wings go onto his back; its heart into his chest. \"NOW. I AM THE END.\" His wings open."},{"p":"The Last Broadcast","h":"On its wings","u":"story/the-last-broadcast.html#on-its-wings","t":"Since 1.72.0 he takes off on the dragon's wings, and you fight him again in the air over his arena, under a whole new bar: The First Signal, The End (lighter-armoured in the air). He circles over you, then: A dive: reared up, his blade over his head, and down on you head first. The floor bursts where he hits it, and he's down on it for a few seconds, getting up: hit him then. A gust: three great beats of his wings (\"DOWN.\") and everything in front of him is thrown back across the floor. Mind the edge. Its breath: down low, the dragon's head on him breathes its fire in a sweep across the floor, and it burns there a while. A volley: balls of its fire spat down at you one after another. Seized (once he's lost a third): he swoops down and carries you up in his hand, crushing you (\"UP.\"), and throws you down. Hurt him enough while he's got you and he lets go. His static (once he's lost two-thirds): bolts down out of the sky where you stand. The Watcher's Omni still knocks him out of the sky now and then, down on the floor and wide open. A bow, a crossbow or a trident helps. Brought down to nothing (\"NO -\"), he falls out of the air, turning over and over, onto where the rite was, and the Watcher gets up."},{"p":"The Last Broadcast","h":"The Watcher fights","u":"story/the-last-broadcast.html#the-watcher-fights","t":"The Watcher lets the Omni fall and gets up off his knees: \"the End was never yours.\" The First Signal's static throws him back. He catches the blade, and puts his beam, a real beam of shadow out of his hands, into the First Signal's heart: \"i've watched you since the first night. i know what you are.\" Then the Faithful seize the First Signal. A seal opens behind him, black, ringed in their glyphs, and \"this isn't over. THIS ISN'T OVER -\", and they're gone into it with him, and it's shut. ...they took him. somewhere even i can't see. go home. while there's still a home to go to. ??? on one knee"},{"p":"The Last Broadcast","h":"The Rebirth","u":"story/the-last-broadcast.html#the-rebirth","t":"Straight after: far out in the dark, the Harbinger's bones. Its skin grows back over them from its skull to its tail, all three of them in it, grown over each other: the Grove's, the Reach's and the hive's. Its eye opens, and a voice that isn't anyone's says: \"...again.\" A door of the hive's, and it goes through; out of another, far off; and into another. THE LAST BROADCAST , THE SECOND RITE , to be continued . The Watcher sends you home: \"The Watcher sent you home. THE LAST BROADCAST goes on in its next part (a coming update).\""},{"p":"The Last Broadcast","h":"After it","u":"story/the-last-broadcast.html#after-it","t":"His arena's gone from his sea, and so is he: only SENTINEL's wreck, and what's left of SENTINEL dark in the rip. \"His arena's gone from his sea - and so is he. THE LAST BROADCAST goes on in its next part.\" The End goes back to sending you home. Every word he says is on The First Signal speaks , and every word of the Watcher's on The Watcher speaks ."},{"p":"The Last Broadcast","h":"What comes next","u":"story/the-last-broadcast.html#what-comes-next","t":"\"this isn't over.\" The mod says so too: to be continued . The Faithful have him somewhere even the Watcher can't see, and the Harbinger is going from door to door."},{"p":"Cold, thirst and the world","h":"","u":"survival.html","t":"Since 1.62.0 staying alive takes more than outrunning what hunts you. You get cold, you get thirsty, the seasons turn, and the world itself moves: rain leaves puddles, rivers flood and running water eats at the land. None of it touches the story's own places. Most of this is built into the mod. The puddles, the erosion, the streams, the seasons and the workstation scenes come from other people's mods that the modpack brings in; they're credited on the credits page ."},{"p":"Cold, thirst and the world","h":"Warmth","u":"survival.html#warmth","t":"A little dial sits over the middle of your hotbar, its needle swinging from frost-blue to red, with a chevron over it while you're warming up or cooling down. Your warmth eases toward what's round you: Where you are: the biome, the season, the sun and the night, rain and snow, how high up you are, and deep water. What's near you: fires, lava, campfires, furnaces, torches and lanterns warm you; ice and snow chill you. What you wear: leather keeps the cold out; any armour helps a little. Every piece of the UV Dive Suit keeps the cold out like leather (since 1.63.9). The whole Ember Deep Suit \"has its own air, its own warmth\" (1.63.10): in it you stay comfortable, whatever's outside it. What you eat: Blubber , from the Rimebacks, is \"Not much of a meal, but it keeps the cold off you for a long while\". The haunting: the air goes cold round the things that walk in the dark, and colder round the Watcher . The Flesh in you is a fever. What happens, getting worse Cold Your breath shows (a mist on your screen, and puffs that everyone else sees), you shiver and your teeth chatter, then you're slowed, then frost creeps in over your sight, and then it freezes you. Heat You sweat and pant, and you get thirsty faster. Then you weaken, a red haze wavers at the edges of your sight, and heatstroke strikes you down (\"collapsed in the heat\")."},{"p":"Cold, thirst and the world","h":"Thirst","u":"survival.html#thirst","t":"A row of drops sits over your food bar. It drains a little all the time and more as you work (sprinting, fighting, digging), and faster in the heat. You go parched , then dehydrated , and then it kills you the way hunger does: on Easy it stops at five hearts, on Normal at half a heart."},{"p":"Cold, thirst and the world","h":"Drinking","u":"survival.html#drinking","t":"Water bottles, milk, honey, stews, melon, berries and apples. Look straight up into the rain. Crouch at the water's edge with empty hands and hold use: you drink from your cupped hands."},{"p":"Cold, thirst and the world","h":"Tainted water","u":"survival.html#tainted","t":"Water that isn't clean may leave you Tainted : you get thirsty faster and feel queasy (without the nausea effect's swimming screen), and your drops go murky."},{"p":"Cold, thirst and the world","h":"Salt","u":"survival.html#salt","t":"Since 1.63.14 salt makes you thirstier at once. Salted Fish (raw cod or salmon and brine salt) is \"Filling - but it's salt all through. You'll be thirsty after\", and keeps forever. The Brine Sink's brine surge salts you too, if you're caught in it. Cupped hands at the sea's edge (or anywhere in the Dead Water) give you half what fresh water does, and are likelier to leave you Tainted. River water is the safest to drink that way; swamps and the Hollow's own places are as chancy as the sea."},{"p":"Cold, thirst and the world","h":"The Canteen","u":"survival.html#the-canteen","t":"Item How In game Canteen String on top, leather either side of an iron ingot, leather below. \"A dented tin flask in a stitched leather sleeve.\" Use it on water to fill it, or hold it out in the rain: rainwater's clean. Murky Canteen Filled from water. Five sips. It may leave you Tainted. \"Pond water. Things move in it if you hold it to the light.\" Clean Canteen Filled in the rain, or a murky one boiled in a furnace, a smoker or on a campfire. Five sips of good water: more thirst back, and it cools you. \"Good water's worth more than it used to be.\""},{"p":"Cold, thirst and the world","h":"When it's off, and turning it off","u":"survival.html#turning-it-off","t":"Nothing about warmth or thirst changes in Creative, in Spectator, on Peaceful, during a cutscene, or in the story's own places ( the Hub , the Stalls , the Vault , the Other Side , his kingdom and Tune-In Town ). While a workstation scene plays, the gauges step aside with the rest of the screen. The settings are in config/statichollow-vitals.properties , made the first time a world starts: # Static Hollow - the cold and the thirst # thirst: true/false - the thirst bar, drinking, Tainted water thirst=true # temperature: true/false - warmth, cold and heat temperature=true # thirst_drain: how fast you get thirsty (1.0 as made; 0.5 half as fast) thirst_drain=1.0 # damage: how hard thirst, freezing and heatstroke hurt (1.0 as made; 0 never) damage=1.0 On a server it's the server's config folder that counts. The idea comes from Tough As Nails; none of its code is used."},{"p":"Cold, thirst and the world","h":"The seasons","u":"survival.html#the-seasons","t":"The modpack has Serene Seasons (unmodified, with Static Hollow's own settings in config/sereneseasons ), and the mod fits itself to it: Summer days are hot and winter is bitter; the tropics have their wet and dry seasons. The hound packs come more often through the winter dark, and the things in the woods walk more in autumn. The fog closes in and goes the colour of frost in winter, amber in autumn and a pale haze in summer. The Watcher notices each season turn."},{"p":"Cold, thirst and the world","h":"Every sound, where it is","u":"survival.html#every-sound-where-it-is","t":"Since 1.61.1 every sound in the world sounds like the place you're in. A few times a second the mod feels out what's round you: how far away the walls are, how much is open to the sky, and what it's all made of. Stone, metal and glass throw sound back; wood less; earth and sand less again; snow, wool, leaves, moss and the Flesh hardly at all. A cave rings and booms for a second or two. A great cavern's tail runs on for seconds and sound comes back off its far walls as an echo. A stone cellar is short and hard, a wooden room warmer, a wool one dead, a forest a soft close wash, open ground almost nothing. Walk from one into another and it changes smoothly with you. The further off a sound is, the more of it reaches you as the place's echo. Through walls it's muffled, more so the more there is between you; far off, the air takes the top off it. Under water everything is heavy, dull and boomy, and a sound from under the water is muffled the same when you hear it from above. In the Dead Water the echo follows the water: longer and darker the deeper you go. Music and the menus' sounds are left alone. It works the same on Forge and Fabric, with or without shaders. Sound Physics Remastered is still in the modpack but switched off in its settings, since it would do it all a second time. To use it instead, set enabled=true in config/sound_physics_remastered/soundphysics.properties ; the mod's own then steps aside."},{"p":"Cold, thirst and the world","h":"Puddles and floods","u":"survival.html#puddles-and-floods","t":"Puddles & Floods (PigCart's) leaves puddles in the rain, under drips and where water runs, and rivers flood their banks. Static Hollow's own water stays on top of it. It also has to be on a server, so the puddles that water, drips and potions leave work there too. Forge has no build of it for 26.3, so the Forge pack carries a port made for it."},{"p":"Cold, thirst and the world","h":"Water that wears the world away","u":"survival.html#erosion","t":"Water Erosion (13rac1's, ported to 26.3 for this pack) lets running water dig creeks deeper, cut banks back and dig in under waterfalls. Earth crumbles down to gravel and sand, and stone by running water goes mossy. Only running water erodes, so still water and the deep oceans cost nothing. The pack's settings keep buildings standing and leave the story's places alone ( config/water-erosion.properties )."},{"p":"Cold, thirst and the world","h":"Streams (Fabric)","u":"survival.html#streams","t":"The Fabric modpack has Streams: Reflowing (NiceJohn's, unmodified): streams that follow the land down to lakes, rivers and the sea, with whitewater and drifting leaves. It makes its own settings in the config folder the first time; if new chunks are slow to appear, pick a lower quality preset there."},{"p":"Cold, thirst and the world","h":"Workstations as scenes","u":"survival.html#workstations-as-scenes","t":"Cinematic Interactions (Southware's, in a build made for this pack) turns crafting tables, furnaces, anvils, grindstones, stonecutters, looms, enchanting tables, brewing stands, lecterns, bookshelves, jukeboxes, campfires and beacons into first-person scenes: you lay the ingredients on the table, load the furnace by hand and hammer at the anvil. Its pages, chimes, hums, the beacon's tuning and the hammer sound like an old house and a dying radio, and its film bars come in with an edge of static. With the First-person Model mod in as well, your own body's arm used to be drawn beside the two the scene reaches in with. Since 1.63.25 it holds off while one of the scenes is on (or one of the mod's cutscenes)."},{"p":"Cold, thirst and the world","h":"Falling stars and Channel Zero","u":"survival.html#falling-stars","t":"At night shooting stars streak over the sky, and now and then a small one comes down somewhere near you. Mine the Fallen Star it leaves for Star Static : \"A splinter of the dead channel over the world. It's still warm. It crackles if you hold it to your ear.\" The first one earns Fallout . Channel Zero is a remote that calls things down out of the sky. It's Creative-only for now, with no recipe yet. Point it at the ground and press it; crouch and press it for the next channel: Channel What comes down CH 1 Falling Star : a crater lined with static stone, and a Fallen Star left glowing in it. CH 2 Starfall : nine small stars over four seconds. CH 3 Dead Satellite : it falls burning for five seconds and leaves a wreck, and a satellite core's chest. CH 4 Test Card : colour bars thrown over the ground, and each bar burns in turn. It makes craters only where the TNT game rule lets things blow up. If it isn't pointed at a block it says \"No signal. (Point it at the ground.)\", and too near your own feet, \"Too close - you'd be under it.\""},{"p":"Cold, thirst and the world","h":"Small things that share a space","u":"survival.html#small-things","t":"Seven sets of little things that fit one to four to a block space, each piece turned to face whoever put it down. Place one on another to add a piece; break it and one piece comes off. You'll find them out in the Hollow's own country , on the deep sea floors, on the rig, in the cathedral's crypts and at the altar's pilgrim stones. Set In game Grave Candles \"Tallow candles, a stub, a skull. Up to four in one space; light them.\" Light them and put them out. Bone Pile \"A skull, its jaw, bones. Up to four in one space.\" Rot Caps \"The Blightwood's fungi. They glow a little, and breathe out spores.\" Hanging Chains \"Hung from a ceiling: chains, a hook, a shackle, a weight.\" They creak. Rig Clutter \"What's left lying about on the rig: a tin, an oil can, a wrench, bolts.\" Cairn Stones \"Flat stones, stacked by pilgrims. The top one is carved.\" At night something whispers from the cairn. Ritual Offerings \"A bowl of ash, a straw doll, a red candle, dried herbs.\" The idea of small blocks sharing a space comes from Olaf's Relatively Placed Blocks; nothing of it is used."},{"p":"Cold, thirst and the world","h":"Wearing heads","u":"survival.html#wearing-heads","t":"Since 1.60.0 every creature head can go on your head. It goes on over your own (yours is hidden under it), the edges of the screen darken as you look out of it, and its own kind notice you from only half as far off."},{"p":"Cold, thirst and the world","h":"The elements leave the Hollow's own alone","u":"survival.html#the-elements","t":"Since 1.64.1 \"none of the mod's creatures drown, dry out, freeze, starve, go thirsty, burn on hot floors or get crushed by the deep's pressure\" (the Rime Charge still slows them). Of the Dead Water's creatures only the Undertow gets hungry now; the sea's hunters prowl now and then instead, and the grazers pick at the floor."},{"p":"Cold, thirst and the world","h":"Blood on the ground","u":"survival.html#blood-on-the-ground","t":"When something bleeds out, its pool used to be laid flat wherever it was: up a wall with a spider, in the air, in the water, out over a drop. Since 1.66.7 blood lies on the ground under whatever bled, and only as far as the ground stays level round it: not over an edge, up a step or into a wall. There's none if there's no ground close under it, or it's in the water."},{"p":"Cold, thirst and the world","h":"Finding the story's places","u":"survival.html#finding-places","t":"From anywhere (since 1.63.4): /locate structure statichollow:botanic_gardens (and the Murder Mansion, the Breach Altar, the cathedral and the Forsaken Altar) used to give up when you were more than 100 chunks off. It finds them from anywhere now, where the place stands or will rise, and so do the Altar, Mansion and Gardens needles (see compasses and needles ). In the Dead Water , /locate for any of its places sets you down in the water right beside it, a third of the way up it, where you can see it. Click to go (since 1.66.7): every place /statichollow locate lists can be clicked to go there, and /statichollow goto [place] does the same: onto the ground there, with room to stand. The way to Tune-In Town: /statichollow locate tune_in_town (the old place) and /statichollow locate flyer_tv (the Old Set that last showed the flyer). If the old place isn't anywhere yet, asking for it from the Overworld sets it down near you; if no set's showing the flyer, one's left on near you. See Tune-In Town , and read the warning there first. Needles to start with (1.72.3): you're given the Altar, Cathedral and Gardens needles the first time you join a world, and the Cathedral Needle has a recipe: a compass, a purple stained glass pane and a candle."},{"p":"Cold, thirst and the world","h":"Going easier on your machine","u":"survival.html#performance","t":"Random ticking (1.63.20): the game looks for blocks to tick at random (grass, leaves, crops, ice) in every section of every chunk near you, every tick, and the deep Overworld is 147 sections tall. Now each chunk keeps a list of the sections with anything in them that ticks, and only those are looked through. Crops grow as before. \"Standing about in the Overworld, the server's time per tick fell by about two fifths in testing.\" To go back to the game's own way, add -Dstatichollow.vanillaRandomTicks=true to the Java arguments. The sea's big ones check the water down their middle, not through their whole box, and the places that build themselves (the cathedral, the altar's grounds and the rest) go up only as much as fits in a hundredth of a second each tick, so a slower machine isn't held still for seconds. Lighter places (1.66.4 and 1.66.5): the Hollow's places have about half as much decoration as they did (trees, plant patches, bones, figures and the rest), to go easier on memory. Their ground, fog, light, sounds and music are unchanged. New ground only: chunks you've already explored keep what they have. In the Fabric modpack (since 1.63.20): FerriteCore (\"less memory for the game's blocks and models\") and ImmediatelyFast (\"the HUD, text and entities drawn in fewer, bigger batches\"). See what's in the Fabric modpack ."},{"p":"Cold, thirst and the world","h":"Max, in the modpack","u":"survival.html#max","t":"The Fabric modpack comes with Max Companion (since 1.63.22), made for the pack by Death. \"Max, the AI, plays with you: the first time you join a world you're given his core (use it on the ground and he boots up beside you); say \"max help\" in chat for what he can do.\" He follows you, fights for you, gathers, farms, builds, lights the place up, keeps your stuff when you die, and talks the whole way, all built in, with no internet and no keys. He keeps to the Overworld: into the Hollow's other worlds (the Hub, the Dead Water and the rest) he doesn't follow; he waits for you."},{"p":"Cold, thirst and the world","h":"The rest of the world","u":"survival.html#the-rest-of-the-world","t":"The oceans go down to about 2,000 blocks below the waves. The Hollow has had its own country since 1.62.0; since 1.66 it comes in big stretches of the Overworld, and has places in the Nether and the End too. See the Hollow's own country . The Ender Dragon is always the Infested Ender Dragon since 1.61.1: see the turned . The music is all the mod's own: see the soundtrack ."}];
